{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition","id":1050476,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get a Simple Answer: Changeling Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-17T07:14:44-08:00","id":1050476,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get a Simple Answer: Changeling Edition","content":"Saw that this is one of the few boards that didn't have one of these. And since Changeling is only rivaled by Mage in the &quot;you will encounter loopholes, fringe circumstances and weirdness&quot; category, I'm thinking it could definitely use one of these.<br /> <br /> I'll probably be asking more questions than I ever get the knowledge to answer, personally, but there are a lot of smart, informed people on this board who can contribute, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>, etc.<br /> <br /> So, to start off the board, here's my first question.<br /> <br /> A mortal in the Hedge is in a bad way, but what happens to them if a Changeling with a Mien that is easily hideable even when exposed follows them through a hedge gate right into their Hollow? Depending on the Hollow, could they not even realize they're somewhere magical? Or does the Hedge call to them still?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:22:48-08:00","id":1050514,"title":"","content":"I would say that it would be possible, but unlikely, unless of course it is important to the story. I'd say that regardless of what the changeling and Hollow looked like, the poor mortal would feel strange. No matter how normal it looked, something just wouldn't seem right. Everything would seem off, and while the mortal might be able to rationalize some of it away, deep down they'd know that their world no longer made sense.<br /> <br /> And thank you for the compliment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:32:57-08:00","id":1050515,"title":"","content":"Welp, guess my secret Hedge dance club isn't going to be very popular. Hard to get that Desire Glamour flowing if everyone's distracted like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T15:06:45-08:00","id":1050741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050515#post1050515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, guess my secret Hedge dance club isn't going to be very popular. Hard to get that Desire Glamour flowing if everyone's distracted like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in that case what you would want to do is open a club in Ironside which housed Doors to a communal Hollow, and make the Hollow the VIP section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T04:20:43-08:00","id":1050942,"title":"","content":"How about this one? I'm fairly sure the answer is no, but can you use Shatter the Mask in Hedge-side? What about if you Shatter, then walk into the Hedge - do you lose the benefits when you cross the barrier, or do they remain? Does the beacon effect from Shattering the Mask cross over into the Hedge from Ironside? You are opening all the doors into the Hedge, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T04:28:08-08:00","id":1050944,"title":"","content":"And here's a second question - lots of people have been saying that pledges have been ruined, they're weak, etc. But then, I look at Goblin Vows and see all the merit-granting and abilities right there, the stuff that used to be in the old pledges.<br /> <br /> So, here's my question. Can we tie others into a Goblin Vow through use of Bargains? This would allow us to have the old deal-with-the-devil type of pledges we had before, making bargains for wealth or beauty, with the changeling as a middlewoman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T04:53:54-08:00","id":1050949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050944#post1050944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's a second question - lots of people have been saying that pledges have been ruined, they're weak, etc. But then, I look at Goblin Vows and see all the merit-granting and abilities right there, the stuff that used to be in the old pledges.<br /> <br /> So, here's my question. Can we tie others into a Goblin Vow through use of Bargains? This would allow us to have the old deal-with-the-devil type of pledges we had before, making bargains for wealth or beauty, with the changeling as a middlewoman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we can already do that. Bargains involve the changeling doing something for the human, right? The changeling can just use Goblin Vows and Contracts to give the human those things. No need for extra mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:14:44-08:00","id":1050959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050949#post1050949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we can already do that. Bargains involve the changeling doing something for the human, right? The changeling can just use Goblin Vows and Contracts to give the human those things. No need for extra mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where does it say you can do that, though? I don't see it. I'm not asking for extra mechanics, I'm asking where it says its possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-18-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:28:21-08:00","id":1050963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050959#post1050959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where does it say you can do that, though? I don't see it. I'm not asking for extra mechanics, I'm asking where it says its possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order to make a bargain with a person, the changeling has to reveal her true nature. She<br /> <br /> doesn\u2019t have to be honest with the mortal about the particulars of her situation, but she<br /> <br /> has to appear to the person without her Mask and propose the terms of the agreement.<br /> <br /> She can promise anything she wants to the person, but in order to gain the benefits of the<br /> <br /> bargain, she has to be capable of making good on her promise. Changelings should<br /> <br /> therefore take care to bargain for services they have the Skills or Contracts to provide, </div> </div> </div>From the open development on Pledges. If a changeling can use both mundane abilities (Skills) or magic (Contracts) to provide for his end of the Bargain, then why not Merits like Goblin Vows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:37:02-08:00","id":1050969,"title":"","content":"Can Huntsmen, Hobs and Gentry see through the Mask when they're on Ironside? And on a related note, can the Mien be seen in photos and videos? How about in paintings? If a mortal artist paints a Changeling, would mortals see the Mask and Changelings see the Mien?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:50:51-08:00","id":1050972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050969#post1050969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Huntsmen, Hobs and Gentry see through the Mask when they're on Ironside? And on a related note, can the Mien be seen in photos and videos? How about in paintings? If a mortal artist paints a Changeling, would mortals see the Mask and Changelings see the Mien?</div> </div> </div> </div>A changeling's shadow reveals his Mien, unless he strengthens his Mask. Changelings see through each others' Masks unless strengthened. Everybody can see through the Mask in the Hedge. Mortals won't see a changeling's Mien, unless the changeling decides to take off the Mask in front of them, or the human catches a glimpse of the changeling in the Hedge, or the human somehow figures out that the girl over there casts a shadow that looks like a huge songbird or something.<br /> <br /> While the whole 2e mechanics aren't revealed yet, I suspect that Huntsmen and Gentry will be able to see through the Masks of changelings belonging to freeholds whose Bulwark has fallen. No idea on hobs, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T07:35:28-08:00","id":1050990,"title":"","content":"But only if the Bulwark has fallen?<br /> <br /> And I thought the shadow thing only happened -when- you strengthened the Mask","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T09:35:58-08:00","id":1051025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050990#post1050990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But only if the Bulwark has fallen?<br /> <br /> And I thought the shadow thing only happened -when- you strengthened the Mask</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under that impression as well: Strengthening the Mask hides you from fae beings, but it has the drawback of potentially alerting mortals to your weirdness via your shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T10:17:21-08:00","id":1051046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050963#post1050963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the open development on Pledges. If a changeling can use both mundane abilities (Skills) or magic (Contracts) to provide for his end of the Bargain, then why not Merits like Goblin Vows?</div> </div> </div> </div> So, by your reasoning, I can give someone access to a Contract I have already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:43:07-08:00","id":1051243,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to grant the ability of ... true sight (the ability to see the fae mien) to another supernatural in some way? 1e says they can't take the oath or whatever, but I'm wondering if it might be possible to craft a magical item, or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:46:57-08:00","id":1051278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051046#post1051046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, by your reasoning, I can give someone access to a Contract I have already?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so was your question about granting magic ability itself to the human, not doing things for the human using magic? If so, then I misunderstood, and changelings probably can't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:31:54-08:00","id":1051310,"title":"","content":"What would be a good example of an Icon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:50:34-08:00","id":1051322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051310#post1051310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be a good example of an Icon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Icons are one of the few things about Changeling 2e we don't actually have much information about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:34:57-08:00","id":1051487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051243#post1051243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to grant the ability of ... true sight (the ability to see the fae mien) to another supernatural in some way? 1e says they can't take the oath or whatever, but I'm wondering if it might be possible to craft a magical item, or something else.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's hints that Ensorcellement is around, but we have no rules for it at the moment. I assume this would do what you ask.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051310#post1051310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be a good example of an Icon?</div> </div> </div> </div> Blood and flesh, literally torn by the Thorns, or dropped clothing / items from your escape including tools, clothes, broken chains, perhaps some food. <br /> <br /> Here's the way I see it - you have your soul shredded as you are taken into the Hedge. Now, when you flee Faerie through the Hedge, your signs of captivity are being torn away as you flee to Ironside. So, if you were forced into a collar and treated as a pet, your collar and pet toys would be Icons. If you were turned into a lamp flame, bits of the lamp, oil, etc would be Icons. At least, that's my impression. Icons form the spoor that Huntsmen use to track you down. Hide the spoor, and they can't track you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:25:45-08:00","id":1051512,"title":"","content":"I think it's supposed to at least metaphorically be the part of your heart you left behind. So, it could be the teddy bear that a captive cried himself to sleep with when they let him sleep, which he left behind with the part of his heart that carried his emotional pain when he became an Ogre","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T18:25:04-08:00","id":1051793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1050942#post1050942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this one? I'm fairly sure the answer is no, but can you use Shatter the Mask in Hedge-side? What about if you Shatter, then walk into the Hedge - do you lose the benefits when you cross the barrier, or do they remain? Does the beacon effect from Shattering the Mask cross over into the Hedge from Ironside? You are opening all the doors into the Hedge, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is an excellent question!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:49:46-08:00","id":1051838,"title":"","content":"Do Changelings age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:54:17-08:00","id":1051839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051838#post1051838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Changelings age?</div> </div> </div> </div>At a decelerated rate and occasionally backwards for a bit, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T21:00:38-08:00","id":1051841,"title":"","content":"Though changelings do have options like certain merits which do stop their aging all together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T22:57:27-08:00","id":1051868,"title":"","content":"Is that for &quot;always looks like a kid&quot; or classic 20 yr old immortal look?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:16:35-08:00","id":1051872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051868#post1051868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that for &quot;always looks like a kid&quot; or classic 20 yr old immortal look?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take your pick. I'd angle for the apparent age of the character at abduction or escape if you want thematic grounding, but the Merit just works by doubling the rate at which your Wyrd extends your life until at Wyrd 5 you've got the Wyrd 10 &quot;immortal&quot; bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bonuses to lifespan granted by Wyrd slow the changeling\u2019s aging, so that she remains proportionately aged for her total lifespan. Additionally, increases in Wyrd and the concomitant lifespan extension are retroactive, which can sometimes age a changeling backwards. For example, if a changeling is weathered and elderly at 80 years old, and her Wyrd rises so that her lifespan grows by another 75 years, she will gradually \u201cde-age\u201d so that she only looks middleaged. Changelings age well regardless of their total lifespan and suffer few, if any, effects of age until their time is up. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T02:14:49-08:00","id":1051901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051872#post1051872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the Merit just works by doubling the rate at which your Wyrd extends your life until at Wyrd 5 you've got the Wyrd 10 &quot;immortal&quot; bonus.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually was referring to the 2 dot merit which makes you immortal regardless of Wyrd. But yeah, whatever appearance is most thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:34:06-08:00","id":1051975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1051901#post1051901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually was referring to the 2 dot merit which makes you immortal regardless of Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long of Days just makes you immune to age-based infirmity and gives you Informed once a chapter. It doesn't actually remove or upshift your expiration date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:37:03-08:00","id":1051976,"title":"","content":"And there's a one dot merit that doubles your Wyrd for purposes of aging, letting you become immortal at Wyrd 5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:56:46-08:00","id":1051985,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing &quot;eternal child&quot; without the immortal part is more of a persistent condition anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:09:19-08:00","id":1053362,"title":"","content":"whats the maximum number of individuals who can participate in a single pledge? example; I'm planning on having my CofD setting to have a strong alliance between changeling and vampire communities where part of it acts like a mass ensorcelment for all the vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:55:57-08:00","id":1053481,"title":"","content":"Well, there's no ensorcelment rules. If its anything like last time, it'd be one permanent glamour per participant. I think that's the only requirement at this point. You'd probably need to initate everyone individually into said pledge, but theoretically doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:49:16-08:00","id":1053568,"title":"","content":"The Toronto Freehold document does not actually tell me what specific Goblin Vow each court has. Does any one know? Like, does the Brass Court have Goblin Vow (Sacred Ground) or even Goblin Vow (Faith)?<br /> <br /> And any word on whether the Seasonal Courts now get the appropriate Goblin Vow Merit at Mantle 2 in 2ND edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:17:35-08:00","id":1053802,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure goblin vow at 2 dots is universal. <br /> <br /> We know Honshu courts have Begging Bowl (Skeptism), Fire Rats (Rebellion), Dragon's Jewel (Tradition) for goblin vows, so perhaps it's possible to extrapolate what the Toronto Court Goblin Vows would be. <br /> <br /> I think it would be Brass (Religion), Silver (Hunt), Jade (Success or Perfection), Ruby (Authority or Secrets), Ivory (Cults or Wealth) for goblin vows, but I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:12:28-08:00","id":1053863,"title":"","content":"Considering that the write-up says that Brass Courtiers can have faith in scientific progress, free trade, democracy, humanity in general, etc., Religion seems too narrow. How about Goblin Vow (Hope) or Goblin Vow (Loyalty)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: what do you think the Seasonal Court Vows should be? Here's my ideas:<br /> <br /> Summer: Strife<br /> Autumn: Knowledge <br /> Winter: Blindness/Lies or Darkness<br /> Spring: Growth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-23-2017, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T08:16:09-07:00","id":1092334,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this has been asked or not, but how do Loyalists work if they still serve the True Fae? Last time I checked, your Seeming in 2E is based on how you chose to rebel and free yourself, instead of being determined by your Keeper. So does that mean if you keep working for them, you never develop one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-08-2017, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:18:22-07:00","id":1092389,"title":"","content":"Yes, they have no Seeming. However, Seeming is not a well-known phenomenon in-universe I think, so it's not as bad a handicap to infiltration as it sounds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:39:27-07:00","id":1092402,"title":"","content":"Actually, David Hill previously talked about Loyalists as a Seeming* defined by the choice to serve the True Fae as a method of escape. I don't know if the material still holds in the current version, but it made sense at the time.<br /> <br /> *An uncounted one that was not considered a standard choice for PCs, mind. And still required a <i>choice</i>, so it didn't exclude the possibility of loyalists without Seeming. They could presumably be changeling antagonists serving a Gentry who just didn't get a say in the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-14-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T16:16:07-07:00","id":1093884,"title":"","content":"Do Changelings have any easy way to contact Spirits from the Shadow? Is there any group of Changelings that do that regularly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T18:12:56-07:00","id":1093928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1093884#post1093884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Changelings have any easy way to contact Spirits from the Shadow? Is there any group of Changelings that do that regularly?</div> </div> </div> </div>None that aren't equally available to mortals. The Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches are a noble order that subdivides loosely by specialty; they could conceivably have a few members who know some generally useful Shadow-lore, but that's a bit closer to &quot;consult a specialist&quot; than &quot;any one of the Lost can do this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T18:42:02-07:00","id":1093939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1093884#post1093884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Changelings have any easy way to contact Spirits from the Shadow? Is there any group of Changelings that do that regularly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the kith rules stay the same (including the rules for altering kiths to meet specific needs), you'd be allowed to take the kith which allows changelings to interact with Ghosts and swap the word Ghost to Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:05:09-07:00","id":1100239,"title":"","content":"This one's more of an opinion poll than a question, but who thinks that clothing alterations needed to accommodate certain features of the Mien should be hidden by the Mask, such as back slits in shirts for wings? I think that asking the Mask to cover non-magical clothing alterations is too much and Changelings should always be a little strange in some way to Mortals even through the Mask, but what do you all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T15:13:27-07:00","id":1101384,"title":"","content":"If I recall, one can strengthen their mask to make other people see their mask rather than their mien. So my question is... can you do this in the hedge? Potentially as a way of performing an act that you would otherwise not your fae identity known for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:21:52-07:00","id":1101419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1101384#post1101384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall, one can strengthen their mask to make other people see their mask rather than their mien. So my question is... can you do this in the hedge? Potentially as a way of performing an act that you would otherwise not your fae identity known for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno the rules, but since nothing has a Mask in the Hedge, I'd say no","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T19:07:05-07:00","id":1101828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1101419#post1101419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I dunno the rules, but since nothing has a Mask in the Hedge, I'd say no</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah I found it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's official, no masks in hedge even if you spend wp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T20:35:39-07:00","id":1101852,"title":"","content":"That said, nothing says you can't bring in some really good mundane disguise kits... Perhaps a contract or token to assist...<br /> <br /> As far as I know, Supernatural powers do jack shit on mundane disguises unless they're looking for liars, or know who to look for","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:20:29-07:00","id":1102552,"title":"","content":"In 2e, if a changeling seals another changelings words (as per the pledge rules), the changeling allowing their words to be sealed gets a beat. What I'm asking is, if a non-changeling (mortal, vampire, werewolf, etc), had their words sealed, would the non-changeling get a beat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T07:27:52-07:00","id":1103123,"title":"","content":"Probably not. That rule exists to give an incentive for changelings to accept a sealing on their words, since its trivially easy to not be bound (1 glamour). Others don't have that defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T09:59:43-07:00","id":1103536,"title":"","content":"Do we have any sources on changeling-specific conditions for 2e? The playtest material mentioned Acuity, Warped, and Delusional.<br /> <br /> EDIT: pffft, I somehow glossed over Acuity and Delusional in the playtest compilation. There is no Condition written up for Warped, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","user":"Lackey Man Ren","date":".  found the answer myself, ignore me 06-14-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T19:11:21-07:00","id":1103688,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm making a Dual Kithed Brollachan/Snowskin and I have to ask, should I get Potent Kith or Killer Instinct?, I have three free dots, the others are Fighting Finesse (Gantlets) for Dex 4 and Brawl 3, Interdisciplinary Specialty and Area of Expertise (Shadows) for Stealth 4, and the mantle of the Autumn Court. He also has Intimidation 4.<br /> <br /> So I guess the question is, should I go all out on Boogeyman with Potent Kith, or get more combat ability with Killer Instinct or a combination of the two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T19:11:27-07:00","id":1114358,"title":"","content":"Are there guidelines for 2E Token design? I've gotten in my head an interesting idea for a token, but searching what is known so far hasn't really gotten me a lot of stuff to go on other than the obvious Drawback/Catch stuff and some vague guidelines as to how many dots a token of a certain ability should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T07:59:36-07:00","id":1128045,"title":"","content":"May I ask a question as well? It's been a long time since I read the books, do pledges and other supernatural agreement between the Lost need to be spoken ones? Or could someone agree to a written Pledge (and not read the fine print)? Or a better option would be to the character make a spoken agreement to uphold the written one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13992-lady-platypus","name":"Lady Platypus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T09:36:29-07:00","id":1128074,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting idea for a thread, but until 2e is released perhaps premature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T10:01:48-07:00","id":1128082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1128074#post1128074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting idea for a thread, but until 2e is released perhaps premature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As the creator of this thread, I would like to say that this was created a few months back, and 1st Edition with or without the previewed material and/or GMC updates will still see a lot of play till 2e comes out who knows when.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:34:31-07:00","id":1128162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Platypus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1128045#post1128045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask a question as well? It's been a long time since I read the books, do pledges and other supernatural agreement between the Lost need to be spoken ones? Or could someone agree to a written Pledge (and not read the fine print)? Or a better option would be to the character make a spoken agreement to uphold the written one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If we're going by the proverb of &quot;my word is my bond&quot; (which is often quite prevalent in fantasy) then a verbal agreement could be just as legally binding as a sheet of parchment signed in your own blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:12:05-07:00","id":1128178,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there something about needing a physical symbol to swear on? A contract could be one way to do that. Though tricking people like that for anything other than true desperate needs would get you kicked into the Hedge by most Courts for Gentry-like behavior<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, I was thinking of corporals, which are only one type of pledge. Pledges in 1e at least seem to be verbal agreements, but more binding than any mortal contract due to the enforcement from the Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-12-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T18:02:49-07:00","id":1128277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1128162#post1128162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If we're going by the proverb of &quot;my word is my bond&quot; (which is often quite prevalent in fantasy) then a verbal agreement could be just as legally binding as a sheet of parchment signed in your own blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that I understand. The question is that I want to make character that will sign agreements with random customers, with fine print giving him a lot of supernatural blessings, because no one ever read the block of text.<br /> <br /> Edit: Thanks for the response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13992-lady-platypus","user":"Lady Platypus","date":". 08-13-2017, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13992-lady-platypus","name":"Lady Platypus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T18:53:06-07:00","id":1128292,"title":"","content":"You can hide parts behind confusing language, but I don't think you can outright omit parts of the agreement or hide them in the fine print","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T20:42:07-07:00","id":1128323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1128292#post1128292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can hide parts behind confusing language, but I don't think you can outright omit parts of the agreement or hide them in the fine print</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, isn't there a rule stating the person has to <b>knowingly</b> agree to the pledge?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Which actually gives me a fiendishly clever idea for a story hook: If somebody agrees to a pledge while possessing another's body (and pretending to be them), who's responsible for upholding the pledge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-12-2017, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T04:45:36-07:00","id":1128388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1128323#post1128323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, isn't there a rule stating the person has to <b>knowingly</b> agree to the pledge?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Which actually gives me a fiendishly clever idea for a story hook: If somebody agrees to a pledge while possessing another's body (and pretending to be them), who's responsible for upholding the pledge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The intelligence making the agreement. Forms are transient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T05:10:46-07:00","id":1128391,"title":"","content":"But do they have to know it's supernaturally enforced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T08:49:57-07:00","id":1128470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1128388#post1128388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The intelligence making the agreement. Forms are transient.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my assumption.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What a twist!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T04:52:21-07:00","id":1131670,"title":"","content":"Something I've been wondering is when would the dawn or dusk courts hold power? I'm working on a freehold where the dawn court is going to be one of the most powerful, but I can't think of when they would actually hold the freeholds throne in comparison to the seasonal courts. Can anyone help me out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:20:44-07:00","id":1131682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1131670#post1131670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been wondering is when would the dawn or dusk courts hold power? I'm working on a freehold where the dawn court is going to be one of the most powerful, but I can't think of when they would actually hold the freeholds throne in comparison to the seasonal courts. Can anyone help me out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed Dusk ruled the second half of the &quot;day&quot; (the half with dusk in it) while Dawn ruled the first half. Not sure what you mean by &quot;in comparison to the seasonal courts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:39:27-07:00","id":1131732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1131670#post1131670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been wondering is when would the dawn or dusk courts hold power? I'm working on a freehold where the dawn court is going to be one of the most powerful, but I can't think of when they would actually hold the freeholds throne in comparison to the seasonal courts. Can anyone help me out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always saw the Dawn and Dusk courts as supplementary courts which were not meant to actually hold power as the governing monarch of a territory, usually. This might not be true (in fact the following is entirely my interpretation of the subject matter), but while the Dusk and Dawn courts contrast, they also do not need each other - as represented by the fact that they are both in two separate books. They usually exist in a city with another governing body - the Seasonal Courts, the Diurnal Courts, etc - and represent very fate-bound elements. A powerful Dawn Court is, in essence, a Court that embodies <i>revolution</i>. It's the call to arms, the banner of people rushing together to say something needs to <i>change</i>. Sometimes, this is the current structure - and for dedicated Dawn Courtiers, this is the <i>very way our world works. </i>Either way, a Dawn Courtier is someone who by their very nature will shake the Status Quo. It is not impossible for a Dawn Courtier to take up Monarchy - but remember that they are agents of change and their monarchy is likely to reflect that. This might in theory allow for a long reigning king, because the Keepers do not in fact like to deal with change... but of course, the risks with that are also evident. One of their tools, if I recall, is actually a tool to remove the crown from a monarch. The cost is that they themselves can never then be monarch... So even if they themselves work supplementary as a Court, they can have a -lot- of power over the political structure of any freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:32:03-07:00","id":1131776,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of different ways you could do it: They could split the year in half, with Dawn taking either the longer days from vernal to autumnal equinox (ruling Spring and Summer while Dusk rules Autumn and Winter) or taking the lengthening days from the Winter Solstice the Summer Solstice. <br /> <br /> You could cut each day in half, but that's more the Diurnal Courts' thing.<br /> <br /> You could have rule change based on the mood of the local populace, with some kind of mystic barometer measuring whether people are more hopeful or pessimistic, like a doomsday clock or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:12:58-07:00","id":1131825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1131682#post1131682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed Dusk ruled the second half of the &quot;day&quot; (the half with dusk in it) while Dawn ruled the first half. Not sure what you mean by &quot;in comparison to the seasonal courts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess wasn't clear, my apologies. I wanted the dawn court to be a court that would be a part of the seasonal court structure, meaning that along with the seasonal courts taking power at different times of year, dawn would be somewhere in the mix as well, sorry for not making that simpler.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> that's a really interesting point, and it makes me kind of rethink what I had in mind. I was envisioning a dawn court that had grown complacent from prosperity. They fought their battles and made their sacrifices and believe that they've made a place that's as good and safe for changelings as it can get. Basically trying to have them reflect what happens when the revolution works out, as it were.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5328\" data-vbnamecard=\"5328\">HelmsDerp</a> those are really good ideas, and I think I may adapt the doomsday clock idea in some fashion somewhere down the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T16:33:04-07:00","id":1131940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1131670#post1131670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been wondering is when would the dawn or dusk courts hold power? I'm working on a freehold where the dawn court is going to be one of the most powerful, but I can't think of when they would actually hold the freeholds throne in comparison to the seasonal courts. Can anyone help me out?</div> </div> </div> </div>WARNING: TOTALLY NOT A SIMPLE ANSWER<br /> <br /> there is no indication in either &quot;dancers in the dusk&quot; or &quot;swords at dawn&quot; that the dusk and dawn courts exist in a power sharing structure similar to that of the great courts. the virtue of them being detailed in two separate books would indicate that they aren't meant to be dualistic courts. even at the end of each writeup, opinions were only given on courtiers from the seasons instead of the other transitional court.<br /> <br /> the dawn court seems to be set up in a way that reminds me of ecclesiastical organizations like the salvation army or the jesuits, what with the titles like &quot;saints&quot; and &quot;martyrs.&quot; they don't really seem heavy into &quot;ruling&quot; anything, but they probably would have lotsa influence amongst charity organizations and non-profits based on social justice.<br /> <br /> the dusk court seems more like a state of mind than a real organization. it is basically what happens when a changeling starts getting into sartre, nietzche and metal. in fact, the write up of the dusk court indicated that membership waxes and wanes depending on how nihilistic the mood of the scene be and that folks sometimes drop out of the seasonal system to join the court of dooms and vice versa. they also don't really seem to be about &quot;ruling anything&quot; as their court motto is *&quot;dgaf yolo.&quot;<br /> <br /> my completely non-official opinion on a question that wasn't asked but is still pertinent to the original question would be to say that dawn court freeholds defies fairy attention because the keepers just can't understand why anyone in a position of &quot;power&quot; would choose to dedicate themselves to the service of less fortunate. while i could never imagine there being enough dusk courtiers around with the compunction to set up a freehold (&quot;society is a comforting lie for those who are too cowardly to accept their own impending doom!&quot;), i imagine that the court allegiance creates a shroud made of their own indifference that obfuscates them from the fair folk.<br /> <br /> <br /> *this is not their official motto but it totally should be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:46:32-07:00","id":1133931,"title":"","content":"How might you justify a Changeling going past the Dream Layer of the Astral on their own? A Goblin Contract? Entitlement? Would their Oneiromancy still work on the deeper layers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T05:25:53-07:00","id":1134806,"title":"","content":"Were the rules for Keening prewied and if so, where can I look them up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T22:45:50-07:00","id":1135076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1133931#post1133931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might you justify a Changeling going past the Dream Layer of the Astral on their own? A Goblin Contract? Entitlement? Would their Oneiromancy still work on the deeper layers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should ask...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Stranger Paths<br /> The edges of a Dreaming Road are unusual opportunities for the Storyteller to introduce crossovers into realms associated with other game lines, anywhere that an unrestrained dream path might intrude. Some potential destinations include the wild corners of Old Arcadia, where the Fae have no purchase; a clockwork nightmare of the God-Machine\u2019s occult industry, where flesh-and-metal angels guard enormous gears lubricated by the blood of the poor; the hidden chambers of the Primordial Dream, wherein dwell terrible and ancient things; the astral realm of the Temenos or the Anima Mundi, where archetypical deities and ideals given flesh inhabit cyclopean structures and mystical landscapes; the depths of a mythical Underworld, where the dead walk and the susurrus of ocean waves beckons around every corner; or even stranger places. A changeling may even be able to reach an Oneiros \u2014 the astral realm that resides within a person\u2019s soul \u2014 if the circumstances are right; but it is not a dream, and fae oneiromancy doesn\u2019t work there, despite the name.</div> </div> </div> </div> How to get there varies, but one way could be failing to escape a Bastion before the dreamer wakes. Fae oneiromancy only works in dreams, not in the Astral proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T10:52:33-07:00","id":1141126,"title":"","content":"So i am looking at the merit Harvest.<br /> <br /> Which gives you a bonus dice equal to its rating for a form of getting glamour. Whoever how does that applies to pledges? (which is one of the examples of the merit) as they dont have a dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:06:01-07:00","id":1141570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141126#post1141126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am looking at the merit Harvest.<br /> <br /> Which gives you a bonus dice equal to its rating for a form of getting glamour. Whoever how does that applies to pledges? (which is one of the examples of the merit) as they dont have a dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the moment, there are no rules for getting glamour from a pledge. Without those rules, we can't say.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:15:44-07:00","id":1141575,"title":"","content":"So, about the new material.... I just noticed with the new Autumn stuff, but what's with the big difference between Common and Royal Contracts going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:22:05-07:00","id":1141579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141570#post1141570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At the moment, there are no rules for getting glamour from a pledge. Without those rules, we can't say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am talking about 1st edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T18:06:06-07:00","id":1141606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141575#post1141575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, about the new material.... I just noticed with the new Autumn stuff, but what's with the big difference between Common and Royal Contracts going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this not adequately explained in the primer at the start of the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">initial preview</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:14:01-07:00","id":1141696,"title":"","content":"No. If it was, I wouldn't ask. &quot;For servants or royals&quot; makes zero sense in a Court, for instance. Why are Autumn Contracts divided thus? There has to be more going on, unless it's just a thin justification for raising a cost. Or an attempt to classify subtle v. Obvious magic and what will attract a huntsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-19-2017, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T04:23:47-07:00","id":1141706,"title":"","content":"Courts are absolutely divided into commoners and royalty. Autumn literally has a monarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T05:22:57-07:00","id":1141713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141696#post1141696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. If it was, I wouldn't ask. &quot;For servants or royals&quot; makes zero sense in a Court, for instance. Why are Autumn Contracts divided thus? There has to be more going on, unless it's just a thin justification for raising a cost. Or an attempt to classify subtle v. Obvious magic and what will attract a huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for Arcadian Contracts, it's said that Royal Contracts are ones that the Gentry forged for themselves. So the Gentry probably struck a deal with Autumn and other &quot;Court patrons&quot; somewhere in history, just as how they struck deals with almost everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:25:02-07:00","id":1141757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141696#post1141696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. If it was, I wouldn't ask. &quot;For servants or royals&quot; makes zero sense in a Court, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i>that</i> was answered back in the thread discussing the initial preview:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121479#post1121479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Court Contracts also come in Common and Royal categories. In this case \u201croyalty,\u201d rather than being those who rise to the levels of the Others, are those who rise to the levels of the Court founders.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:25:30-07:00","id":1141758,"title":"","content":"Court Contracts were struck by changelings, for changelings and by changelings. Not the Gentry. So, I don't think that quite makes sense either. Why would they create an exclusive tier like such? This is not making sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:49:09-07:00","id":1141767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141758#post1141758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Court Contracts were struck by changelings, for changelings and by changelings. Not the Gentry. So, I don't think that quite makes sense either. Why would they create an exclusive tier like such? This is not making sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not actually exclusive and there is zero reason to conclude that changelings devised the mechanical structure of Court Contracts just because they formed Courts. &quot;Some of the things your patron grants your Court are common tricks while others are more strongly associated with legendary figures like its founder&quot; is a simple division that can be seen as baked into the way the Wyrd does formal Contracts.<br /> <br /> This is fae magic to swear a notionally-aboveboard supernatural pact; the lack of direct involvement by the Gentry is why Court Contracts aren't divided into Regalia, but Goblin Contracts are the place to look if you're expecting Contracts sorted into a whole sort of general mishmash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-19-2017, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T13:34:44-07:00","id":1141875,"title":"","content":"Its exclusive. That's pretty much the definition of Royal Contracts being made to kept with the intent to the Gentry specifically. Long story short, there doesn't seem to be a reason other than just copying what others did for no strong reason, but it happened anyways. Got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:15:39-07:00","id":1141941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141875#post1141875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its exclusive. That's pretty much the definition of Royal Contracts being made to kept with the intent to the Gentry specifically. Long story short, there doesn't seem to be a reason other than just copying what others did for no strong reason, but it happened anyways. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of it was that when changelings struck those bargains, they were treated as though they were Gentry. The founders of the Courts gained their new Contracts, with some that would be easily obtained by lesser members of the Court and others that were the special prize of the founders for striking the bargains in the first place. The fact that they'd be willing to share those with the others would be immaterial. The Contracts are Royal because they were bestowed in the same manner that the Royal Contracts of the Gentry were bestowed, and share the same mystical potency. They are the Contracts that the Gentry would have considered worth obtaining and holding for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:17:36-07:00","id":1141942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141875#post1141875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its exclusive. That's pretty much the definition of Royal Contracts being made to kept with the intent to the Gentry specifically. Long story short, there doesn't seem to be a reason other than just copying what others did for no strong reason, but it happened anyways. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Royal Contracts used to be exclusive to the Gentry... until changelings figured out how to claim them as their own. What's more, they're now forging new Royal Contracts, without the intercession of the Gentry. I find it kinda awesome, and in-theme with all the &quot;use the enemy's tools against them&quot; kind of motifs we've seen in how Seemings and Kiths now work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T20:36:05-07:00","id":1142020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1141875#post1141875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its exclusive. That's pretty much the definition of Royal Contracts being made to kept with the intent to the Gentry specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>really not</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121366#post1121366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In designing new Contracts, you use the power level to determine the origin. If it works with existing resources, the Others would have willingly let their servants have it. If it's more overtly creative (or so transformative as to essentially be creative), it's the kind of thing they would have kept to themselves.<br /> <br /> (There are exceptions, of course, where Keepers might have added changelings as beneficiaries of Royal Contracts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The selfish conquering Lords and Ladies of Faerie would have kept this ability to themselves if not compelled otherwise&quot; is not &quot;This ability can only be learned and used by the Gentry,&quot; &quot;This ability can only be used by the character who bargained for it,&quot; &quot;This ability can only be gained by characters above a certain threshold of Mantle,&quot; &quot;This ability cannot be shared,&quot; or any other meaningful extrapolation of the word &quot;exclusive&quot; into this conceptual space.<br /> <br /> A Royal Contract is a Contract that makes a character capable of things that a Common Contract does not enable, and is accordingly more costly to become a beneficiary of. That's it. That's the whole distinction \u2014 it's a major power rather than a moderate power and therefore the egomaniacs who made you fae wouldn't have wanted to share it if they were in the position of the Court Founder who litigated for it in the first place, but nothing about that separation compels the establishment of a more involved barrier to learning it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Long story short, there doesn't seem to be a reason other than just copying what others did for no strong reason, but it happened anyways. Got it. </div> </div> </div>No, <i>long story short</i>, the mythology that builds up around the founder of a Court in relation to the patron of its Contracts is usually about what that individual did or got from the bargain, and does not frame those benefits as being <i>for the sake of empowering a Court.</i> The powers a legendary figure's followers pick up through their association with her come <i>after</i> the powers she gets by becoming a legendary figure who pacts with elements of the universe for hidden opportunities to exploit.<br /> <br /> Having swindled the North Wind into lending you his coat and hound lends you a stature that anyone who you might wish to empower as an associate does not have in the eyes of that phenomenon, and so it's logically going to take more investment on their part to receive the same gifts than it would to get, say, an ear for who and what has the scorn of the blizzard and the ability to steer the ire of unhappy travelers. Common and Royal Contracts have different thresholds for what they can accomplish and those thresholds are the difference between metalworking and turning straw into gold. A distinction still ought to exist between a character who can shift the manifestations of a force and someone who can generate that force outright \u2014 these powers are not equivalent.<br /> <br /> Regardless of any aspersion you may wish to cast about Court Founders, a Court is a hierarchical structure. &quot;The Courts are just Arcadia in miniature!&quot; has been a common in-universe grumble since First Edition and an inbuilt systemic inequality drives conflict in a way that &quot;The powers of the founding nobility of a Court are no harder to access than those of its common membership, because Courtly power structures are completely level except for whoever is currently Sovereign&quot; does not. It is a distinction worth having even without the need to mechanically distinguish Contracts that are extremely potent and overt from Contracts that are subtle to use and easy to come by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-21-2017, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:10:29-07:00","id":1144909,"title":"","content":"This is probably due to unseen changes in 2 edition rules, but I need to make sure that this isn't just me being out of the loop.<br /> True Fae blog post mentions that each Title has Seeming mostly in that it impacts their appearance, determines one Regalia they must have, and lets them benefit from its blessing. The last one doesn't compute, since as far as I checked and understood Seeming blessing only offered free Clarity dots; What possible use could Storyteller/Gentry have from that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:07:34-07:00","id":1144938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1144909#post1144909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably due to unseen changes in 2 edition rules, but I need to make sure that this isn't just me being out of the loop.<br /> True Fae blog post mentions that each Title has Seeming mostly in that it impacts their appearance, determines one Regalia they must have, and lets them benefit from its blessing. The last one doesn't compute, since as far as I checked and understood Seeming blessing only offered free Clarity dots; What possible use could Storyteller/Gentry have from that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here are the blessing/curse for Darklings, by way of example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 1: The Fair and the Foul</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Blessing:</b> Gain an additional dot of one Finesse Attribute at character creation. If you spend a point of Willpower, your character may touch something insubstantial and become part of it for three consecutive turns, transubstantiating into smoke, shadow, a sunbeam \u2014 whatever\u2019s handy. This ability costs a point of Glamour if anyone is looking directly at her at the time.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> In addition to your character\u2019s other breaking points, she risks Clarity damage with a dice pool equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up) whenever a secret she knows turns out to be false.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:23:39-07:00","id":1144951,"title":"","content":"Thank you for swift answer! This makes total sense now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:25:34-07:00","id":1144953,"title":"","content":"Wait, Clarity <i>damage?</i><br /> <br /> Does that mean it heals, and if so, does that mean it's not an Integrity dot scale any more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:27:28-07:00","id":1144955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1144938#post1144938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here are the blessing/curse for Darklings, by way of example:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes. yes. so much yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:30:30-07:00","id":1144959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1144953#post1144953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, Clarity <i>damage?</i><br /> <br /> Does that mean it heals, and if so, does that mean it's not an Integrity dot scale any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch, I completely missed that. Clarity as different type of health sounds very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:23:06-07:00","id":1145023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1144938#post1144938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here are the blessing/curse for Darklings, by way of example:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, so now the Darklings are the nimble ones instead of the Wizened. And with abilities like this, it would be easier in-universe to classify Seemings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:24:29-07:00","id":1145024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1144959#post1144959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good catch, I completely missed that. Clarity as different type of health sounds very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kinda hope that's not how it turns out. Reminds me too much of my least favorite part of my favorite system (FATE Dice and mental damage tracks to be specific)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:27:47-07:00","id":1145026,"title":"","content":"Well, there are two other types besides Finesse in that particular attribute axis and at least six seemings, so its possible there's more than one that gets that bonus. (Though they could also just switch to the other axis).<br /> <br /> My inference of what has been shown thusfar is that Clarity is still their effective integrity trait. It just goes up and and down far more freely than most other equivalents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:31:20-07:00","id":1145028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1145026#post1145026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are two other types besides Finesse in that particular attribute axis and at least six seemings, so its possible there's more than one that gets that bonus. (Though they could also just switch to the other axis).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, when I said nimble, I equally meant quick-thinking (mentally nimble) and good at reading people quickly (socially nimble)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:31:21-07:00","id":1145029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1144938#post1144938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here are the blessing/curse for Darklings, by way of example:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I love this! Are Darklings able to move in their intangible state? Could one turn into smoke and pour themselves through a keyhole, or become shadow to slip under a door? Could one in the form of a sunbeam go directly through a window without breaking it? This has a lot of potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:33:26-07:00","id":1145032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1145029#post1145029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I love this! Are Darklings able to move in their intangible state? Could one turn into smoke and pour themselves through a keyhole, or become shadow to slip under a door? Could one in the form of a sunbeam go directly through a window without breaking it? This has a lot of potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I should hope so. Otherwise, it wouldn't be very useful except for quickly hiding or delaying getting shanked for a few seconds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T03:04:43-07:00","id":1145147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1145032#post1145032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> delaying getting shanked for a few seconds</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Great, now we've got Obito style Darklings....<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> What's the general etiquette for slapping the reigning King / Queen of the Freehold in the face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T12:33:33-07:00","id":1145328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1145029#post1145029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I love this! Are Darklings able to move in their intangible state? Could one turn into smoke and pour themselves through a keyhole, or become shadow to slip under a door? Could one in the form of a sunbeam go directly through a window without breaking it? This has a lot of potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, all of the above. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Glad you like it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T12:41:59-07:00","id":1145329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1145328#post1145328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, all of the above. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Glad you like it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent! I can do so much with that in my games. Thank you for letting us know. I can't wait to see the rest of the Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T13:07:16-07:00","id":1145876,"title":"","content":"Can True Fae drop their Masks while on Earth to benefit from automatic Exceptional Successes on all their Contract rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  And in either case: What's stopping them? 10-01-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T14:04:21-07:00","id":1149234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1145876#post1145876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can True Fae drop their Masks while on Earth to benefit from automatic Exceptional Successes on all their Contract rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would hate this thread go dead until actual release of 2e, so I am gonna rubber tape answer my own question until rules confirm or deny it:<br /> Because opening Hedge Gates, alerting Huntsmen, and driving humans into Delirium is also bonus to Other, they have to pay additional price to drop the Mask. In order to drop the Mask Kindly Cousin must give up one piece of its Regalia, which instantly reforms in Hedge in form of collectible Token, that must be collected by Title in question to restore. Since losing Regalia makes Titles more vulnerable, it should be good deterrent.<br /> <br /> Another question: Do we know how True Fae &quot;earn&quot; Titles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T13:47:55-07:00","id":1150199,"title":"","content":"I don't think we don't mention this directly in the book, but True Fae get Titles the same way they get anything else -- by bargaining for them. And yes, that means that they can use one Title as collateral for another... the pacts the Others make with each other and external cosmic forces get positively Byzantine.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: There's also inheriting Titles or taking them as tokens of surrender, but those are both forms of bargain, as far as the Wyrd is concerned.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 10-16-2017, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T17:04:11-07:00","id":1150237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1150199#post1150199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we don't mention this directly in the book, but True Fae get Titles the same way they get anything else -- by bargaining for them. And yes, that means that they can use one Title as collateral for another... the pacts the Others make with each other and external cosmic forces get positively Byzantine.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: There's also inheriting Titles or taking them as tokens of surrender, but those are both forms of bargain, as far as the Wyrd is concerned.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So if some Title is the collateral for another Title, what happens when they lose the collateral? Could you trigger a domino effect of default and render a True Fae &quot;naked&quot; by taking out the right Title?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T20:55:24-07:00","id":1150263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1150237#post1150237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if some Title is the collateral for another Title, what happens when they lose the collateral? Could you trigger a domino effect of default and render a True Fae &quot;naked&quot; by taking out the right Title?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems totally viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:07:47-07:00","id":1150357,"title":"","content":"These probably won't come up in regular play but in case Storyteller decides to throw other splat at players: <br /> <br /> Can Changelings harvest Glamour from other splats? Would such Glamour be any different from regular one? <br /> <br /> Do other Templates of World of Darkness have any means to back out when their words get sealed into pledge by fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T19:48:55-07:00","id":1150531,"title":"","content":"Something that <i>will </i>come up a lot:<br /> <br /> How does Clarity work now? Clarity &quot;damage&quot; implies a health track, but that, as mentioned, rubs some people the wrong way. Not me, but clarification?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T00:22:43-07:00","id":1150561,"title":"","content":"Yeah, surprising no one, I'm not a fan of this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T01:06:49-07:00","id":1150568,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Clarity damage takes bits from that alternate integrity system from Hurt Locker where it piles up damage as you take trauma, if you fill up the thing with damage then you lose a dot of clarity and all your current clarity damage is healed. Just a theory though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T01:13:46-07:00","id":1150570,"title":"","content":"I think Clarity &quot;damage&quot; might just be a shorthand for how many dots you lose in a given instance. It was mentioned that Clarity loss and gain was swingier now, if I recall correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T02:13:49-07:00","id":1150581,"title":"","content":"While I am also very curious about new Clarity rules I have gnawing suspicion that we aren't going to get any further sneak peeks into rules and systems until Kickstarter starts (so, even in best case scenario not until weekend).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T06:49:07-07:00","id":1151633,"title":"","content":"Okay so meanwhile, on Mask and how deep it goes: Do cameras only capture Changeling's Mask, or is Mask rather obscuring photography's content from mortal viewers? What happens when entity incapable of looking through the Mask dips into Changeling's memories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T07:43:47-07:00","id":1151638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1150357#post1150357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These probably won't come up in regular play but in case Storyteller decides to throw other splat at players:<br /> <br /> Can Changelings harvest Glamour from other splats? Would such Glamour be any different from regular one?<br /> <br /> Do other Templates of World of Darkness have any means to back out when their words get sealed into pledge by fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Earlier playtests had a reference to the Exotic Airs merit, but it was never included. I'm assuming it would work like the other supernaturals' versions, where each dot would be a specific supernatural to feed on. So first dot you might pick vampires, second you might grab prometheans, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:26:33-07:00","id":1151657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icefyer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1151638#post1151638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Earlier playtests had a reference to the Exotic Airs merit, but it was never included. I'm assuming it would work like the other supernaturals' versions, where each dot would be a specific supernatural to feed on. So first dot you might pick vampires, second you might grab prometheans, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Changelings still feed on Willpower dots or would they be draining the other being's Glamour equivalent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:43:54-07:00","id":1151737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1151657#post1151657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would Changelings still feed on Willpower dots or would they be draining the other being's Glamour equivalent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea. I'm not a developer, but I think it could go either way. Would be interesting to siphon a vampire and drain their vitae through their emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T08:41:47-07:00","id":1153184,"title":"","content":"Changelings can absorb Glamour from any sophont with emotions. Vampires count. Ghosts count. No special effects for taking energy from specific other monsters... we've been trying to cut down on those in second edition, because it means making up a wide variety of special effects and if every one is just a different flavor of magic potion, the fun gets lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T09:31:05-07:00","id":1153198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1153184#post1153184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings can absorb Glamour from any sophont with emotions. Vampires count. Ghosts count. No special effects for taking energy from specific other monsters... we've been trying to cut down on those in second edition, because it means making up a wide variety of special effects and if every one is just a different flavor of magic potion, the fun gets lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic! Thank you so much, Rose!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T15:57:04-07:00","id":1153305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1153184#post1153184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings can absorb Glamour from any sophont with emotions. Vampires count. Ghosts count. No special effects for taking energy from specific other monsters... we've been trying to cut down on those in second edition, because it means making up a wide variety of special effects and if every one is just a different flavor of magic potion, the fun gets lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I personally found the fact changeling blood was like the mother of all acid trips to vampires to be hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T07:52:22-08:00","id":1158166,"title":"","content":"Do (Hob)goblins have a Wyrd score? In 1st edition some did, some didn't and some where straight up changelings who joined a Market.<br /> <br /> Likewise, do they get a Glamour pool? They get a Turn, a single contract they can use for free (though sometimes only once per day). So they have no need to spend Glamour, but when accepting it as payment they would need to store it somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 11-13-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T14:20:42-08:00","id":1159180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1158166#post1158166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do (Hob)goblins have a Wyrd score? In 1st edition some did, some didn't and some where straight up changelings who joined a Market.</div> </div> </div> </div> In 2e? I don't think we have any information about how to stat non-ling, non-Gentry fae things up. <br /> <br /> There are hedge ghosts, who likely will use Rank and Essence, but do fae-like things. There's the oneroi who will do their dream stuff. There's random non-hedge fae besides the huntsmen. Huntsmen might remain close to the same, if they do, there's no Wyrd or glamour there.<br /> <br /> So, hobs? Could be anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T19:11:24-08:00","id":1159298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1159180#post1159180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In 2e? I don't think we have any information about how to stat non-ling, non-Gentry fae things up.<br /> <br /> There are hedge ghosts, who likely will use Rank and Essence, but do fae-like things. There's the oneroi who will do their dream stuff. There's random non-hedge fae besides the huntsmen. Huntsmen might remain close to the same, if they do, there's no Wyrd or glamour there.<br /> <br /> So, hobs? Could be anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge ghosts, hobgoblins, and Huntsmen all have Wyrd and use Glamour. The difference is that Hedge ghosts (mostly) use the rules for ephemeral beings and have Numina and Influences, while hobgoblins and Huntsmen (mostly) use the rules for Horrors and have Dread Powers. All three have some exceptions, because they're uniquely fae. (For instance, hobgoblins can also have Contracts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T23:16:33-08:00","id":1159356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1159298#post1159298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge ghosts, hobgoblins, and Huntsmen all have Wyrd and use Glamour. The difference is that Hedge ghosts (mostly) use the rules for ephemeral beings and have Numina and Influences, while hobgoblins and Huntsmen (mostly) use the rules for Horrors and have Dread Powers. All three have some exceptions, because they're uniquely fae. (For instance, hobgoblins can also have Contracts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen have Wyrd scores now? Interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T12:35:33-08:00","id":1160603,"title":"","content":"I've missed what happened with Changeling 2.0. I understand we had a Hill (Underhill?) version but thats been cancelled? And now Rose is working on the version on Kickstarter?<br /> <br /> What information is there for the Kickstarter version of Changeling 2.0? I'm backing so I have:<br /> &quot;Changeling the Lost Second Edition Preview - Part 1 (Introduction, Chaper 1, Chapter 2)&quot;<br /> and I found &quot;Goblin Contracts Preview (public)&quot; on these forums. Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T14:05:36-08:00","id":1160644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1160603#post1160603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've missed what happened with Changeling 2.0. I understand we had a Hill (Underhill?) version but thats been cancelled? And now Rose is working on the version on Kickstarter?<br /> <br /> What information is there for the Kickstarter version of Changeling 2.0? I'm backing so I have:<br /> &amp;quot;Changeling the Lost Second Edition Preview - Part 1 (Introduction, Chaper 1, Chapter 2)&amp;quot;<br /> and I found &amp;quot;Goblin Contracts Preview (public)&amp;quot; on these forums. Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything posted by Rose on Onyx Path blog is from this version. Most of the playtest stuff that came before has been &quot;polished&quot; or removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T04:55:09-08:00","id":1160811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1160603#post1160603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I understand we had a Hill (Underhill?) version but thats been cancelled? And now Rose is working on the version on Kickstarter?...</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose <i>and</i> Meghan. <br /> <br /> but yeah you've got it about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T20:44:28-08:00","id":1161067,"title":"","content":"How many humans can a True Fae take to Arcadia at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T04:57:40-08:00","id":1161125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1161067#post1161067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many humans can a True Fae take to Arcadia at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that the number would vary based on the situation and the people involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T19:08:06-08:00","id":1161383,"title":"","content":"What are the differences between the Kith Book &amp; Companion Book? I'm assuming that the Kith Book has more material on The Kith's Legends &amp; Backstory and that's the reason they got separated into 2 different books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T08:26:14-08:00","id":1161525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1161383#post1161383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the differences between the Kith Book &amp; Companion Book? I'm assuming that the Kith Book has more material on The Kith's Legends &amp; Backstory and that's the reason they got separated into 2 different books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kith book's real name is &quot;Kith &amp; Kin&quot;. We don't know a lot about it but from what we can figure, it will likely be a book focused around characters and character options with a large (seemingly) focus on Kiths and more example Kiths. (I hypothesize that it will be like a more focused version of a Player's Guide).<br /> <br /> The Companion book, we have even less info on other than the things that will be inside. From what I can tell, the Companion book might be a collection of additions and detail that couldn't make it into the Core book due to word count limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T10:18:18-08:00","id":1161548,"title":"","content":"A few questions, two of them are cross posts from the kickstarter topic (since this is the more appropriate place to put questions.)<br /> <br /> 1. Can a Mage accidentally exit from one's oneiros into a Dreaming Rode in the Hedge?<br /> <br /> 2. Can the Dreaming roads enter into a Beasts labrynth/soul stuff (not sure where the Beast's 'Soul' lies but I hear it has something to do with a Dreamscape.<br /> <br /> 3. Another quick question, but this time on Court Crowns.<br /> <br /> So each Crown is displayed differently and as different objects but only one explicitely says that it is located on the head. See below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Spring]<br /> The Crown wreathes around the queen's head, cascading down her shoulders to a resplendent robe of young blooms.<br /> <br /> [Summer]<br /> Mahogany branches and emerald leaves braid together in the Crown, wrapping down into a magnificent breastplate.<br /> <br /> [Autumn]<br /> Red and yellow leaves crown the queen, fanning out behind her like great wings.<br /> <br /> [Winter]<br /> Frozen ashes make the Crown, flowing down into a shimmering mantle of gray and silver. </div> </div> </div><br /> - Spring's Crown specifically mentions that it rests on the head before bustling into a robe.<br /> - Summer's Crown says that it rests where a normal breastplate would, but it words it as &quot;wrapping down into...&quot; which makes it ambiguous if the crown is also on the head or not.<br /> - Autumn's Crown says that it is on the back, but the wording before it is &quot;leaves crown the queen&quot;. The wording of 'crown' as a lowercase verb would indicate it resting on the head as well but again: ambiguous.<br /> - Winter's Crown says that it is a mantle (a cloak/cape mantle) and so would indicate it rests on the shoulders but again the wording of &quot;flowing down into a...&quot; is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Spring's is not ambiguous at all, Winter's is less ambiguous than the others (as the cape can be the one 'flowing down') but it is still not clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> 4. tl;dr: Two Assumptions:<br /> - The element associated with an Elemental who wasn't made an Elemental is the element most closely associated to the expression of what the Changeling is an Elemental in the first place.<br /> - The Seeming changes the Mein regardless of how the changeling obtained that Seeming.<br /> <br /> Are these assumptions correct?<br /> <br /> <br /> (in more detail)<br /> The Elemental Blessing uses a specific elemental medium to do stuffs at range. What if the Elemental isn't an Elemental because the changeling was made into that element during the Durance?<br /> <br /> My assumption would be that each elemental is associated even with the (quasi-personality) traits of a specific element then it's that element that the Elemental has affinity in.<br /> (for example, a Changeling is remade into a Satyr to continually groom her keepers wild lawn. However the changeling could not give up on leaving and very slowly but very surely whittled down the defenses, inch by inch, of her keepers demesne till she escaped back (as in: she gained her Seeming of Elemental w/ a Water association through her means of escape (elemental due to the sheer force of will and water because it's expressed in a way similar to water eroding anything and everything in its path)).<br /> <br /> My other assumption is that, regardless of how a Changeling obtains their Seeming, the Seeming changes the Mein in related ways.<br /> <br /> This all is due to how Seemings are no longer literal and more broad archetypes due to the examples below but yet the Elemental blessing asks for a specific element:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL2e 2nd Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character's seeming <b>forms from what happened to her in Arcadia, how she escaped it, <u>or</u> how<br /> she approaches the world now.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And for what the archetypes are (note how elemental are not literally the elements):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast: Savage survivalists, passionate and deadly.<br /> Darkling: Lurkers hiding in the shadows, silent but ever watchful.<br /> Elemental: Unbridled and unchained, the true forces of nature.<br /> Fairest: Stately and elegant, forever loved and craving true connection.<br /> Ogre: Warriors and brutes, blunt and to the point.<br /> Wizened: Crafters and builders, weary but not jaded. </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the long post ^.^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 11-22-2017, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T12:09:48-08:00","id":1161580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1161548#post1161548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few questions, two of them are cross posts from the kickstarter topic (since this is the more appropriate place to put questions.)<br /> <br /> 1. Can a Mage accidentally exit from one's oneiros into a Dreaming Rode in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div> Unlikely, but anything is possible. I would also argue that such a gateway would trigger Passive Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can the Dreaming roads enter into a Beasts labrynth/soul stuff (not sure where the Beast's 'Soul' lies but I hear it has something to do with a Dreamscape. </div> </div> </div> The Beast stuff lies in the Primordial Dream which, despite the name, isn't a dream but part of the barrier between the Temenos and the Anima Mundi. You can enter into either the Temenos or Anima Mundi, so the Primordial Dream is likely included there as well. All else fails, you get to the Primordial Dream by entering the Temenos and walking a bit until the PD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Another quick question, but this time on Court Crowns.<br /> <br /> So each Crown is displayed differently and as different objects but only one explicitely says that it is located on the head. See below:<br /> <br /> - Spring's Crown specifically mentions that it rests on the head before bustling into a robe.<br /> - Summer's Crown says that it rests where a normal breastplate would, but it words it as &quot;wrapping down into...&quot; which makes it ambiguous if the crown is also on the head or not.<br /> - Autumn's Crown says that it is on the back, but the wording before it is &quot;leaves crown the queen&quot;. The wording of 'crown' as a lowercase verb would indicate it resting on the head as well but again: ambiguous.<br /> - Winter's Crown says that it is a mantle (a cloak/cape mantle) and so would indicate it rests on the shoulders but again the wording of &quot;flowing down into a...&quot; is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Spring's is not ambiguous at all, Winter's is less ambiguous than the others (as the cape can be the one 'flowing down') but it is still not clear. </div> </div> </div> There's part of the chapter that talks about how you can just absorb the &quot;crown&quot; into the Mantle / Mein, or physically manifest it, or turn it into a token. In fact, you can actually change all three states during the course of your season.<br /> <br /> All in all, I wouldn't peg on any one manifestation for any season, and just go by what seems to be appropriate for each person in question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T12:35:35-08:00","id":1161586,"title":"","content":"A few of the contracts in the preview require an element from the Changeling for the Elemental Seeming Bonus. While this is obviously not a problem if the Changeling is an Elemental, it does make things difficult if the Changeling is a Beast, or a Fairest, or really anything other than an Elemental. How would you guys rule that, if such a case were to come up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T13:09:17-08:00","id":1161593,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> , Thanks! I didn't know too much about really anything Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T01:23:54-08:00","id":1161786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1161586#post1161586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few of the contracts in the preview require an element from the Changeling for the Elemental Seeming Bonus. While this is obviously not a problem if the Changeling is an Elemental, it does make things difficult if the Changeling is a Beast, or a Fairest, or really anything other than an Elemental. How would you guys rule that, if such a case were to come up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Player picks 1 element that character is associated with and it applies to all Elemental clauses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T16:13:23-08:00","id":1162277,"title":"","content":"So, here's a question; up until now, I'd presumed that acts like creative writing, singing and even acts like song writing would be under the Expression tab. However, the Artist Kith works based on Crafts rolls, and has noted that Song Writing is indeed a Crafts roll. What would Creative Writing fall under, then? I ask, because this relates rather heavily to a character I'm very interested in playing when the game comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-24-2017, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:10:06-08:00","id":1162300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1162277#post1162277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a question; up until now, I'd presumed that acts like creative writing, singing and even acts like song writing would be under the Expression tab. However, the Artist Kith works based on Crafts rolls, and has noted that Song Writing is indeed a Crafts roll. What would Creative Writing fall under, then? I ask, because this relates rather heavily to a character I'm very interested in playing when the game comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it fits under Expression. For my games, I'd allow them to exchange Expression for Crafts in their blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:12:57-08:00","id":1162302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1162277#post1162277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a question; up until now, I'd presumed that acts like creative writing, singing and even acts like song writing would be under the Expression tab. However, the Artist Kith works based on Crafts rolls, and has noted that Song Writing is indeed a Crafts roll. What would Creative Writing fall under, then? I ask, because this relates rather heavily to a character I'm very interested in playing when the game comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> which would you like it to be? as expression and crafts are both attempts to quantify creativity, i can see a justification for either stat being used. maybe even academics. yeah, it doesn't make a ton of sense for someone skilled at poetry also be bomb at general contracting. but it also doesn't make sense for a brilliant, yet otherwise mousey, author to be a badass operatic singer either. for the sake of character building efficiency, just go with crafts. changelings are all about magical items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:37:32-08:00","id":1162313,"title":"","content":"I think a new version of this thread should made, too many of the questions are for David Hill's Changeling, not Meghan/Rose's Changeling, so a lot of people could read this thread and get confused. <br /> <br /> Example there is a question on Goblin Vows, which Rose/Meghan's version doesn't even have (no Goblin Vows merit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T06:58:29-08:00","id":1162452,"title":"","content":"Ok, make it so, then","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T09:48:46-08:00","id":1162493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1162277#post1162277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a question; up until now, I'd presumed that acts like creative writing, singing and even acts like song writing would be under the Expression tab. However, the Artist Kith works based on Crafts rolls, and has noted that Song Writing is indeed a Crafts roll. What would Creative Writing fall under, then? I ask, because this relates rather heavily to a character I'm very interested in playing when the game comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see anything about song composition in the artist write up? Painting, sure. There's an offhand mention of composers, but that doesn't say anything about Song Writing = Crafts roll. <br /> <br /> Expression and Crafts do have overlap, but its the difference between technical perfection and emotional pleas. I can see where writing music could be a Crafts roll, because a lot of music is actually very mathematical in its approach. And the Gentry aren't exactly human who understand human emotions being conveyed. So, they would want technical perfection rather than an emotional appeal. <br /> <br /> Which is rather fitting for what we're dealing with here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T15:42:22-08:00","id":1162563,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> That makes sense. It could tie into his character too - great at writing works like bibliographies and dictation, but not creative stories or poetry. It definitely gives an avenue for growth throughout the game...<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think that we need a second thread for answering questions regarding Changeling's second edition Omegaphallic. We didn't make a second edition for the David Hill version, in spite of its differences from the first edition of the game, and once the second edition is released after the kickstarter, it'll be released to a much wider audience, so the thread will be populated by more people wise to its contents. It's early days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-25-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:56:34-08:00","id":1165396,"title":"","content":"What are the Patrons of the Seasonal courts? They sound like Spirits but also kinda sound like insanely power True Fae. What could possibly uphold their end of the Bargain (give them access to Contracts, causing a Give&amp;Take with the Fae, ETC)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:13:56-08:00","id":1165401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165396#post1165396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the Patrons of the Seasonal courts? They sound like Spirits but also kinda sound like insanely power True Fae. What could possibly uphold their end of the Bargain (give them access to Contracts, causing a Give&amp;Take with the Fae, ETC)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's the same, and I think you could make an argument it is, they're basically Arcadian/Wyrd-interpretations of the Seasons (or really, any court patron). They can be interacted with because the Wyrd is a power of give and take, contracts, and stories. It's about interaction, so IN THEORY, you can make a deal with them. In a real way, they're the same KIND of thing as the patrons of the Arcadian/Regalia Contracts. The difference is in who made a deal with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:27:03-08:00","id":1165405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165401#post1165401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's the same, and I think you could make an argument it is, they're basically Arcadian/Wyrd-interpretations of the Seasons (or really, any court patron). They can be interacted with because the Wyrd is a power of give and take, contracts, and stories. It's about interaction, so IN THEORY, you can make a deal with them. In a real way, they're the same KIND of thing as the patrons of the Arcadian/Regalia Contracts. The difference is in who made a deal with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So essentially, if I'm getting this right, they're things that exist in the Hedge/Arcadia (somewhere, maybe Old Arcadia?) that aren't goblins, True Fae, or Huntsman. They're Wyrd infused 'Concepts' similar to Spirits but possibly a bit more physical.<br /> <br /> Is that about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:55:36-08:00","id":1165415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165405#post1165405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So essentially, if I'm getting this right, they're things that exist in the Hedge/Arcadia (somewhere, maybe Old Arcadia?) that aren't goblins, True Fae, or Huntsman. They're Wyrd infused 'Concepts' similar to Spirits but possibly a bit more physical.<br /> <br /> Is that about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that seems about right. The thing you might notice from all the stories is often you first had to FIND them to make the deal. Which probably is a worthy Story of its own ending in however they made the pact, but not whole Campaign either.<br /> <br /> Edit: And the reasons they can hold the True Fae to rules is probably because of the very Contracts the True Fae made to rule Arcadia and be as they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:10:57-08:00","id":1165455,"title":"","content":"The entities which are patrons for a court apparently don't need to be very powerful themselves &quot;it just has to be able and powerful enough to make and uphold a deal with True Fae or changelings.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:27:00-08:00","id":1165459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165455#post1165455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entities which are patrons for a court apparently don't need to be very powerful themselves &quot;it just has to be able and powerful enough to make and uphold a deal with True Fae or changelings.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, I assume, they'd have to be powerful enough to create contracts if you wanted Court Contracts for that Court. I don't really expect a court with a Patron of an Elder Invictus vamp to have the connection to the wyrd to create Court Contracts for its courtiers. <br /> <br /> Or maybe the Wyrd makes it happen anyways. Maybe changelings can utilize contracts based off of the Patrons disceplines and innate abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:44:44-08:00","id":1165463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165459#post1165459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I assume, they'd have to be powerful enough to create contracts if you wanted Court Contracts for that Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were true, then it would have said that rather than &quot;it can be anything as long as it can do x&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or maybe the Wyrd makes it happen anyways. Maybe changelings can utilize contracts based off of the Patrons disceplines and innate abilities? </div> </div> </div>I can easily see a court which has had an ancient vampire in it's basement generations locked in torpor until the agreed upon date, with their bargain requiring the changelings to use oneiromancy to eternally protect the kindred from the horrific dreamscapes which normally plague a vampire, and in return the court gains protection against their own nightmares allowing them to ward areas from the gentry by spilling their own blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T13:38:27-08:00","id":1165659,"title":"","content":"So, about the Elemental Weapon Contract, would you rule that these are unmasked items that last forever and can be used by anyone? The manuscript doesn't seem to address these points but it seems unbalanced under these assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T14:23:13-08:00","id":1165672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165659#post1165659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, about the Elemental Weapon Contract, would you rule that these are unmasked items that last forever and can be used by anyone? The manuscript doesn't seem to address these points but it seems unbalanced under these assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless otherwise specified, Contracts last a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T14:33:45-08:00","id":1165674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165672#post1165672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless otherwise specified, Contracts last a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel stupid for missing this. Thank you so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T14:38:15-08:00","id":1165675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165674#post1165674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel stupid for missing this. Thank you so much!</div> </div> </div> </div>We all miss something like this somewhere. Nothing to feel stupid about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:43:34-08:00","id":1165848,"title":"","content":"If I'd like to run a character or NPC as a satyr inspired by Greek mythology, what kind of kith would be adviced for that? I look through but didn't find anything I really liked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:50:36-08:00","id":1165853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165848#post1165848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'd like to run a character or NPC as a satyr inspired by Greek mythology, what kind of kith would be adviced for that? I look through but didn't find anything I really liked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What aspect of satyrs do you wish to focus on? Also, which version and have you looked through the homebrew kiths on here and 1d4chan, depending on the version. Plus, kiths are only one part of the Changeling. You could add more satyr-like traits with tailored starting contracts, aspirations, anchors and even just their Skills and Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:13:52-08:00","id":1165861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165848#post1165848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'd like to run a character or NPC as a satyr inspired by Greek mythology, what kind of kith would be adviced for that? I look through but didn't find anything I really liked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's many routes you could go for that. The simplest would be a Beast Seeming with whichever kith most accents the aspect of satyrs that you favor. A Runnerswift or Steepscrambler could both work if you're looking for athletic ability. If you want them to have an enchanting song, you could re-skin the Nightsinger to use pipes rather than singing. A Brewer could offer anyone the finest wine around. Those are just a few thoughts off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:22:01-08:00","id":1165864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165853#post1165853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What aspect of satyrs do you wish to focus on? Also, which version and have you looked through the homebrew kiths on here and 1d4chan, depending on the version. Plus, kiths are only one part of the Changeling. You could add more satyr-like traits with tailored starting contracts, aspirations, anchors and even just their Skills and Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm a 1st edition person so, thus I'm not sure what aspirations and anchors does. But no, I haven't checked for homebrew yet as I wouldn't know where to find them and a quick search on the forum don't seem to have conjured up anything. If anyone sits on a good kith I'm totally open to take a look at it.<br /> <br /> The aspect of the satyr I was thinking about was essentially the satyr as part of Dionysios' train of partygoers. So less &quot;I'll fuck anything that moves!&quot; and more on the side of the ecstatic force of life that just keeps going and won't ever take a break, ever. Kind of thing. I don't know how clear that came across but I hope I made some sense. If not feel free to ask for more clarifications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:35:58-08:00","id":1165867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165864#post1165864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm a 1st edition person so, thus I'm not sure what aspirations and anchors does. But no, I haven't checked for homebrew yet as I wouldn't know where to find them and a quick search on the forum don't seem to have conjured up anything. If anyone sits on a good kith I'm totally open to take a look at it.<br /> <br /> The aspect of the satyr I was thinking about was essentially the satyr as part of Dionysios' train of partygoers. So less &amp;quot;I'll fuck anything that moves!&amp;quot; and more on the side of the ecstatic force of life that just keeps going and won't ever take a break, ever. Kind of thing. I don't know how clear that came across but I hope I made some sense. If not feel free to ask for more clarifications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>First, Spring Court would be the obvious choice, as that gives you the passion and revelry right out of the gate. With 1E, I'd say Beast would be best for Seeming. Are you using Dual Kith? If so, I'd recommend going with Steepscrambler or Runnerswift, and possibly linking one of those with Minstrel or Nightsinger for the musical talent. I could also see Hunterheart to reflect the &quot;chasing nymphs&quot; aspect, with the natural weaponry referring to the hooves and horns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:45:39-08:00","id":1165870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165867#post1165867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, Spring Court would be the obvious choice, as that gives you the passion and revelry right out of the gate. With 1E, I'd say Beast would be best for Seeming. Are you using Dual Kith? If so, I'd recommend going with Steepscrambler or Runnerswift, and possibly linking one of those with Minstrel or Nightsinger for the musical talent. I could also see Hunterheart to reflect the &quot;chasing nymphs&quot; aspect, with the natural weaponry referring to the hooves and horns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Spring Court is a given. No dual kiths I'm afraid. But Steepscrambler or Runnerswift are interesting. I'll take a closer look at those.<br /> <br /> Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:57:01-08:00","id":1165871,"title":"","content":"Do Seeming bonuses for Contracts come with the contract always? I was a little unclear on when a contract has a Seeming bonus. I seem to remember the bonuses having a cost of one dot higher during purchasing? Can you buy the contract and then purchase the seeming bonus later? Do seeming bonuses need to be taught? Or are seeming bonuses just ingrained into every contract?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165864#post1165864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm a 1st edition person so, thus I'm not sure what aspirations and anchors does. But no,<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The aspect of the satyr I was thinking about was essentially the satyr as part of Dionysios' train of partygoers. So less &quot;I'll fuck anything that moves!&quot; and more on the side of the ecstatic force of life that just keeps going and won't ever take a break, ever. Kind of thing. I don't know how clear that came across but I hope I made some sense. If not feel free to ask for more clarifications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For 1st Ed, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> 's post as that is pretty much what you described. <br /> <br /> If you were interested in 2nd Ed I would go for an Elemental Steepscrambler (would have write up the Kith stuff to make it 2nd Edition friendly) of the Spring Court. Not sure on contracts at the moment but definitely an Elemental. Your description of &quot;the ecstatic force of life that just keeps going and won't ever take a break, ever.&quot; is very very 2nd ed elemental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 12-07-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T08:05:42-08:00","id":1165873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165871#post1165871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Seeming bonuses for Contracts come with the contract always? I was a little unclear on when a contract has a Seeming bonus. I seem to remember the bonuses having a cost of one dot higher during purchasing? Can you buy the contract and then purchase the seeming bonus later? Do seeming bonuses need to be taught? Or are seeming bonuses just ingrained into every contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Contract has a bonus effect for your Seeming, you get it free. If you want a bonus effect for a different Seeming, you need to find a changeling of the right Seeming who knows the Contract, swear an oath and learn it from them for one experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T08:06:33-08:00","id":1165874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1165871#post1165871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Seeming bonuses for Contracts come with the contract always? I was a little unclear on when a contract has a Seeming bonus. I seem to remember the bonuses having a cost of one dot higher during purchasing? Can you buy the contract and then purchase the seeming bonus later? Do seeming bonuses need to be taught? Or are seeming bonuses just ingrained into every contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're the correct Seeming, you get those bonuses for free. If you want one you don't normally get you need to find a teacher of the correct Seeming, swear an oath to them in return for them teaching you, then you get any Contracts their Seeming favors as if you favored it and for 1 xp, you can learn their Seeming benefit for any Contract (with it feeling like they're teaching you it perhaps... or maybe that's part of the personal oath).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T08:10:28-08:00","id":1165875,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar378_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"378\" data-vbnamecard=\"378\">haren</a> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T14:08:15-08:00","id":1166530,"title":"","content":"So, I finished the last preview of the 2nd edition, and I'm a little confused about the character creation of the Fae-Touched:<br /> - do they have Virtue/Vice or Needle/Tread?<br /> - do they use Touchstones?<br /> - do they begin with seven or ten dots in Merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T14:38:14-08:00","id":1166538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1166530#post1166530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I finished the last preview of the 2nd edition, and I'm a little confused about the character creation of the Fae-Touched:<br /> - do they have Virtue/Vice or Needle/Tread?<br /> - do they use Touchstones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Needle/Thread is part of the Lost Template, as are Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T14:56:45-08:00","id":1166540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1166538#post1166538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Needle/Thread is part of the Lost Template, as are Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but it's the part about them having Integrity instead of Clarity that makes me question the possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T19:26:27-08:00","id":1166580,"title":"","content":"&quot;Note that the Avowed share many traits with changelings, but they are not changelings. Some<br /> traits are completely unique to changelings. If an advantage or trait is not listed below, do not<br /> assume fae-touched characters gain it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right before that it says that you should follow regular character creation <i>except</i> adding the Lost template (i.e. step 5) which is were both Needle/Thread and Touchstones are added to changelings. The only reason Clarity is mentioned is because it's added in a later step 7 rather than step 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: However, they seem to have omitted that they should have Virtue/Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-10-2017, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:50:42-08:00","id":1168238,"title":"","content":"So, this may seem like a dumb question, but is ensorcelment (allowing a mortal to see past the mask of not just yourself but all Changelings) still a thing for Changelings in second edition? I've not found any reference to it, and people have suggested that it can be made as a benefit of the bargain, but I'm not entirely sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T14:55:00-08:00","id":1168254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1168238#post1168238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this may seem like a dumb question, but is ensorcelment (allowing a mortal to see past the mask of not just yourself but all Changelings) still a thing for Changelings in second edition? I've not found any reference to it, and people have suggested that it can be made as a benefit of the bargain, but I'm not entirely sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not a thing in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T03:58:34-08:00","id":1168498,"title":"","content":"With traveling the Hedge acting like a chase, how exactly are certain abilities that involve learning the direction or location of certain places supposed to work? Hedgespinnig for example, gives suggestions regarding learning the direction to go to find a location, but it doesn't say how that's meant to manifest because according to the rules, you just declare a goal and roll to find your way..One of the examples given by the book of this is declaring you want to find an icon, something which I get the sense should be an extremely big thing in and out of game, potentially even the center of its own story-not something that should be accomplished in just one chase. Does the book specify that you need to already know certain things before you can declare them goals and I just missed it? Or if not, can anyone suggest ideas on how to integrate those ideas. Currently I'm thinking just a die bonus, or in the case of certain hedgespinning rolls, even automatic successes. I just wanted to pull from further knowledge before I make that definitive, because it still feels like for certain things, the system doesn't have the necessary gravitas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T06:04:41-08:00","id":1168511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1168498#post1168498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With traveling the Hedge acting like a chase, how exactly are certain abilities that involve learning the direction or location of certain places supposed to work? Hedgespinnig for example, gives suggestions regarding learning the direction to go to find a location, but it doesn't say how that's meant to manifest because according to the rules, you just declare a goal and roll to find your way..One of the examples given by the book of this is declaring you want to find an icon, something which I get the sense should be an extremely big thing in and out of game, potentially even the center of its own story-not something that should be accomplished in just one chase. Does the book specify that you need to already know certain things before you can declare them goals and I just missed it? Or if not, can anyone suggest ideas on how to integrate those ideas. Currently I'm thinking just a die bonus, or in the case of certain hedgespinning rolls, even automatic successes. I just wanted to pull from further knowledge before I make that definitive, because it still feels like for certain things, the system doesn't have the necessary gravitas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, don't forget that you can hedgespin with a Wits + Investigation roll (and, if you're a hunterheart, get an exceptional on three successes). That's the kind of thing that would give you the direction or location. You're using tracking skills (Investigation, Streetwise, Survival) to follow signs and portents within the Hedge to your destination.<br /> <br /> How this manifests? The same exact way you'd expect spoor in any tracking roll to manifests. Game trails, scent paths, torn clothing, hints of civilization in a forest, crumbs from bread, and more.<br /> <br /> There's not a lot of detail given, simply because the number of things you can do at this point is frankly outragously huge. Combat is hedgeshaping. Tracking is shaping. Jogging is shaping. Dancing is shaping. Actual shaping with gardening or blacksmith tools is hedgespinning.<br /> <br /> As an ST, you have the job to make sure that the right bonus is resulting from the right action. I wouldn't give the direction or location benefit from a non-perception roll, for instance, or the weapon benefit from dancing the polka.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, in the case of finding an Icon? I imagine that would be a situation of trying to rely on your memory and retrace your steps during your capture and/or escape (I forget which, if not both, icons come from). The Hedge does react to your intentions, yes, but you still have to act out those intentions. You'll be faced with chasing against not only the hedge, but also with trying to outrun some hobs, or a huntsman following you; you might need to stop the chase and fight off some attackers, perhaps.<br /> <br /> And, when you get to the site the icon was at, you might find that it was taken by some hob merchants, so you'll need to continue tracking to get to a Market and barter for it, etc. Lots of potential complications beyond just rolling for a chase that will drag out the difficulty.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you need to know &quot;certain things&quot; before you start rolling, since looking for signs of those &quot;certain things&quot; is, itself, a hedge spinning roll and the start of a chase. And the hedge will respond to your searching (assuming you win) and give you those signs and knowledge you need as the first step in the chase.<br /> <br /> EDIT - or you can use an Investigation subsystem thing, and get Clues, which in turn can be used as equipment dice on the Chase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-18-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T06:21:13-08:00","id":1168515,"title":"","content":"Do True Fae have Mask? Can they scour it for benefits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T07:09:56-08:00","id":1168520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1168515#post1168515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do True Fae have Mask? Can they scour it for benefits?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. But only in the form of an individual Title, and there's always a Tell of some kind that leeks through. <br /> <br /> And I'm fairly sure it can be scoured on Earth just like any changeling ( I think this is true of hobs and all other critters with a Mask as well? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T19:25:05-08:00","id":1168978,"title":"","content":"Would a mortal or non-changeling that has the hedge denizen condition be altered physically as well and in that way gain a mask and a mein? Of course, referring to the Kickstarter documents. Then, for the goblin contracts they gain, are they able to get glamour in any way or are they restricted to using the loophole only? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T02:39:14-08:00","id":1169034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1168978#post1168978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a mortal or non-changeling that has the hedge denizen condition be altered physically as well and in that way gain a mask and a mein? Of course, referring to the Kickstarter documents. Then, for the goblin contracts they gain, are they able to get glamour in any way or are they restricted to using the loophole only?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I would say no to Mask/Mien, barring picking up something like Riddle-kith*. Or some other kind of goblin deal to get them. Or just ST ruling, but given the below, I'd say the default is no. It appears that we can get Wyrd and glamour, though.<br /> <br /> Looking at the sample antagonist Liza Cantwell, Age 9, Goblin Queen... the poor girl picked up Wyrd and a glamour pool, but the description seems to be human still, and there is no seeming or kith. Mien is the result of having a Seeming and/or Kith's blessings (as per pdf 2) that reshapes your appearance, and without a faerie appearance, I'd say no Mask. So, as items exposed to the magic of the Hedge eventually become tokens, it appears that non-fae exposed to the hedge long term pick up Wyrd and glamour. <br /> <br /> * Riddle-kith, when used on yourself with the darkling and elemental clauses, basically lets you transform your seeming and kith indefinitely. I'd say that could give a non-changeling such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T05:58:38-08:00","id":1169061,"title":"","content":"@MCN but don't hobgoblins benifit from a mask ironside? I could have sworn I'd seen that. In part it's wondering just how much of a hob hedge denizen makes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T18:36:55-08:00","id":1169244,"title":"","content":"Sure they do... IF they have an appearance that doesn't match up to something common in Ironside. The Mask is designed to hide the mien, aka fae features (which generally are the result of Seeming and Kith, as per pdf) from mortal view. If there are no fae featuers, then there's no Mask. And there are hobs that look entirely like creatures found Ironside. <br /> <br /> Hedge Denizen and Goblin Queen aren't adding a mien to a character by default; they're deliberately just Conditions, not a new template. That's why we can have changelings with those Conditions and have no issues in game play.<br /> <br /> If the ST wants there to be mutation and adopt a mien? That's cool, I'm all for that. But its not a requirement, and I consider that more of the exception than the rule. <br /> <br /> Now, items and animals left in the Hedge DO mutate into full hobgoblins if left unattended over time. You make tokens by marinating items of worth. The Thorns leech away part of a being and warp them into &quot;weirder, truer versions of their old selves.&quot; But that's a function of the Thorns themselves, rather than the Hedge Denizen / Goblin Queen Contracts, and is entirely in the STs's hand on how that happens. If a Hedge Denizen sticks to the trods, they might never undergo said warping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T07:52:34-08:00","id":1169353,"title":"","content":"I kinda figured that their features did warp, if even slightly, by virtue of automatically obtaining contracts and contracts change the mien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T08:46:08-08:00","id":1169365,"title":"","content":"i think the way contracts affects a changeling mien is different then how it would effect someone else. people who have souls (Integrity) may just be more stable in their own sanctity of form than one of the Lost, whose soul was shredded when they were dragged through the thorns and then patched up with fairy magic and moonbeams by capricious, all powerful otherworldly entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T05:41:30-08:00","id":1169601,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Hi guys,<br /> <br /> Does a changeling, when he takes a comatose condition, really falls asleep or does he sleepwalk?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T10:43:41-08:00","id":1169679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1169601#post1169601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Hi guys,<br /> <br /> Does a changeling, when he takes a comatose condition, really falls asleep or does he sleepwalk?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basrring ST fiat and the needs of a Story, the default is that they lit fall asleep per the wording:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Comatose</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She believes she is awake, living her life perfectly normally, but <b>is instead <u><i>lying</i></u> in a coma</b>. She cannot roll to enter the Gate of Ivory (p. XX) and dream lucidly without help.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording indicates that the character is perceiving her own comatose dream as real and interacts with props and eidolons without knowing that she is actually asleep. To the waking world, she's just in a deep coma in a bed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T06:33:35-08:00","id":1170662,"title":"","content":"Is the mechanism described in the early 2016 doc for a Changeling returning to human still a thing? (Reduce Glamour to zero, kill fetch.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T09:40:05-08:00","id":1170707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1170662#post1170662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the mechanism described in the early 2016 doc for a Changeling returning to human still a thing? (Reduce Glamour to zero, kill fetch.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from what I've read. <br /> <br /> Reducing Glamour to zero has the chance of becoming Glamour Starved then Glamour Addicted if left too long. And the book had many different ways of dealing with a fetch that served whichever purpose the story and character have such as killing the fetch, reconciling with (or allying with) the fetch, and even hints you might be able to merge with the fetch and treat that like an obtaining one of your Icons.<br /> <br /> So while the book didn't discuss a way to change back to a human, I'd imagine that it wouldn't be hard to make such a ritual work for your chronicle if you're interested in exploring that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T09:51:08-08:00","id":1170714,"title":"","content":"The effect was to reduce Wyrd to 0, not Glamour, but the answer remains the same. It isn\u2019t in the books as per raw, but it could work as per ST fiat. Still, given Clarity is described as your mind being torn by the thorns, to the point you don\u2019t use Vice or Virtue anymore, it would probably need something potent to ensure you aren\u2019t an insane human by the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T17:21:05-08:00","id":1170810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1170714#post1170714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effect was to reduce Wyrd to 0, not Glamour, but the answer remains the same. It isn\u2019t in the books as per raw, but it could work as per ST fiat. Still, given Clarity is described as your mind being torn by the thorns, to the point you don\u2019t use Vice or Virtue anymore, it would probably need something potent to ensure you aren\u2019t an insane human by the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, yeah. Wyrd not Glamour. In addition the draft called for using Glamour as little as possible to simply sustain oneself. If that sidebar didn't make the final version them sure, it could be a plot mechanism.<br /> <br /> Thanks folks.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T20:00:26-08:00","id":1170842,"title":"","content":"Is there still a way to bestow the ability to see through the Mask to mortals or are the Ensorcelled gone as a concept in this version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T20:44:11-08:00","id":1170849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1170842#post1170842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there still a way to bestow the ability to see through the Mask to mortals or are the Ensorcelled gone as a concept in this version?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as it requires a judgement call for what does and doesn't count?<br /> <br /> Dream Assailant's active resolution mechanic includes the option of bestowing a dot of a Supernatural Merit upon a qualified target for the rest of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T17:11:44-08:00","id":1171104,"title":"","content":"I believe this would qualify as a &quot;Simple questions/Simple Answer&quot; in that I don't think it needs a full new topic.<br /> <br /> But, is anyone here planning on updating the<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/ChangelingTheLost\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling: The Lost TVTropes page</a>? It's currently frightfully out of date (still saying that there <i>will</i> be about 100 kiths in the core and other such things). <br /> <br /> It's just, I don't know how to update TVTropes and it's been one of the best resources for showing new people the basics beforehand (when it's up to date that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T05:41:51-08:00","id":1171209,"title":"","content":"Hi guys<br /> <br /> I was thinking about the comatose condition, and one way to end it is to convince the dreamer that he is dreaming, a easy way to do it is to kill him. <br /> <br /> I know that it would be a break point for the person who will do it, but i still thinking that is a easy and fast way.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T06:05:50-08:00","id":1171213,"title":"","content":"&quot;Its only a flesh wound.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T10:27:36-08:00","id":1171260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1171104#post1171104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe this would qualify as a &quot;Simple questions/Simple Answer&quot; in that I don't think it needs a full new topic.<br /> <br /> But, is anyone here planning on updating the<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/ChangelingTheLost\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling: The Lost TVTropes page</a>? It's currently frightfully out of date (still saying that there <i>will</i> be about 100 kiths in the core and other such things).<br /> <br /> It's just, I don't know how to update TVTropes and it's been one of the best resources for showing new people the basics beforehand (when it's up to date that is).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd thought someone would, since the Characters page has been updated pretty well, but I think I can do some clean-up.<br /> <br /> Edit: And updated. May not be entirely correct, but it's more accurate to the current product than before. However, I have noticed that the Seemings need some more updates in the Characters page; it's mostly summary, fortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-28-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:48:06-08:00","id":1171283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1170842#post1170842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there still a way to bestow the ability to see through the Mask to mortals or are the Ensorcelled gone as a concept in this version?</div> </div> </div> </div> Ensorcellment isn't a thing this time, which I find odd honestly. <br /> <br /> But you can sort of grant a human the ability to sense the fae by using dreamweaving dream condition to grant them the unseen sense merit. <br /> <br /> A Telepath might be able to sense the fae as well as I don't think the mask extends to Supernatural senses or it might prevoke a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:59:23-08:00","id":1171290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1171283#post1171283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ensorcellment isn't a thing this time, which I find odd honestly.<br /> <br /> But you can sort of grant a human the ability to sense the fae by using dreamweaving dream condition to grant them the unseen sense merit.<br /> <br /> A Telepath might be able to sense the fae as well as I don't think the mask extends to Supernatural senses or it might prevoke a clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd honestly grant something more akin to a condition than a true merit. Merits are meant to last, whereas conditions can be shed either over time or from particular circumstances. I don't know if I'd make Unseen Sense grant the ability to see through the Mask either - the merit's closer to simply knowing they're around rather than actually seeing things as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T02:31:09-08:00","id":1173184,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, this may be a bit overpowered, but could a Changeling use Props And Scenary to transform into a working motorcycle, if they have the Ogre's seeming bonus? If so, could they use the motorcycle's speed rating, or would they be restricted to their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:42:46-08:00","id":1173351,"title":"","content":"I am considering nerfing Field of Regret so that it only can affect one target. It seems to me so strangely stronger than its Summer counterpart that I even suspect that it can be an artifact of some former versions. (essentially it is an attack with a decent dice pool with no reliable way of protecting against it, at arbtitrary distance at which you see a target, against an unbounded number of targets, at the cost of essentially 1 wp, since its Loophole is extremely easy to meet).<br /> <br /> Do I miss something? In particular, is there any drawback to this contract which would make it weaker than it appears to be? Or is there any particular reason why it shouldn't be nerfed despite being so strong?<br /> <br /> I am primarly concerned with its balance against the other Contracts: as a pure offensive power, it seems outright better than others with no obvious downsides (Helios Judement's relative downsides being the necessity to use it outdoors and an actual Glamour cost, the fact that it is an actual attack which seems to be resolved normally, with Defense and armor, and the fact that it affects one target only).<br /> <br /> As an aside which could partly explain my doubts: is the dice pool listed in Helios Judgement the final dice pool or it resolved normally like a throwing attack? I.e., is Defense subtracted? Or is it just a dicepool to invoke the beam which then works normally as a thrown weapon? Is Mantle calculated into every subsequent attack? The wording somewhat suggests that it works just like a normal Thrown weapon with a very decent Damage rating.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-04-2018, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:06:51-08:00","id":1173357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1173351#post1173351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I miss something? In particular, is there any drawback to this contract which would make it weaker than it appears to be? Or is there any particular reason why it shouldn't be nerfed despite being so strong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering it's a multi-target resisted roll, I'm reasonably certain that with or without errata each use of Field of Regret is supposed to be a single invocation, which stands in stark contrast with Helios' Judgement's roll-once-get-a-new-attack-for-the-scene arrangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T07:33:48-08:00","id":1173486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1173357#post1173357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering it's a multi-target resisted roll, I'm reasonably certain that with or without errata each use of Field of Regret is supposed to be a single invocation, which stands in stark contrast with Helios' Judgement's roll-once-get-a-new-attack-for-the-scene arrangement.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand the dicepool granted by Helios' Judgement is Dexterity + Athletics - Defense (as it works like a thrown weapon), subject to further modifications by cover against one target.<br /> <br /> Field of Regret is a multitarget attack, essentially for 1 wp, at essentially arbitrary distance, with dicepool given by Empathy + Presence + Mantle - Resolve which actually seems undetectable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T10:37:52-08:00","id":1173525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1173486#post1173486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand the dicepool granted by Helios' Judgement is Dexterity + Athletics - Defense (as it works like a thrown weapon), subject to further modifications by cover against one target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the nature of Royal Court Contract prerequisites is such that it's doing at least four lethal damage on every successful hit, with no Willpower cost save the one that makes that aggravated damage. Unsurprisingly, the Summer Contract works better in open conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T12:54:22-08:00","id":1173553,"title":"","content":"With Tatterdemalion's Workshop, does the item created with help from the contract have the Fragile or Volatile condition? It says that it works as a jury rigging Build Equipment action, but it says the device will function as its normal version would as well. I suppose it'd be a moot point for an exceptional success, but what of a normal success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T13:41:53-08:00","id":1173566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1173553#post1173553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Tatterdemalion's Workshop, does the item created with help from the contract have the Fragile or Volatile condition? It says that it works as a jury rigging Build Equipment action, but it says the device will function as its normal version would as well. I suppose it'd be a moot point for an exceptional success, but what of a normal success?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the general themes of fae magic I would say the answer to this question is &quot;yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Are fetches subject to the bane of iron?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T15:54:31-08:00","id":1173604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1173566#post1173566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are fetches subject to the bane of iron?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no; unlike Changelings, a Fetch is designed to be human even in a place such as the Hedge, where a Changeling's mask is eschewed. The Fetch is meant to replicate the person the Fae has taken, and though they are based on Fae magic the piece of shadow/soul they have anchors them pretty dang well.<br /> <br /> At worst, I'd say they'd develop an allergy to iron like some people have to nickel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T15:06:44-08:00","id":1173850,"title":"","content":"Does a condition such as Too Solid Flesh enable application a supernatural banes to the sleeping victim? Silver? Fire? Staking?<br /> <br /> What about un-staking? How might the dream effects carry over?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  Fixing autocorrect... 01-10-2018, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T10:08:15-08:00","id":1174574,"title":"","content":"Are Fae-touched still around in the latest draft?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T10:32:14-08:00","id":1174580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1174574#post1174574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Fae-touched still around in the latest draft?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. They are peeps that made promises to folks who got done took by the fairies and were compelled to enter the hedge in order to find them. They emerge from this ordeal with some ability to use fairy magic and an addiction to the fairy world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T16:19:55-08:00","id":1176405,"title":"","content":"Here's a question; can Changelings still take Eidetic Memory in second edition? I don't see it in the available merits in the Changeling materials, but it could simply have been neglected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T16:26:50-08:00","id":1176406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1176405#post1176405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question; can Changelings still take Eidetic Memory in second edition? I don't see it in the available merits in the Changeling materials, but it could simply have been neglected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: the Lost Second Edition preview, Character Creation Step Six: Merits</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lost may possess any of the Merits from the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook, except for those on the Supernatural Merits list, Vice-Ridden, and Virtuous (since changelings do not have Virtue and Vice traits).</div> </div> </div> </div>The list of Human Merits is likely abridged for limited space in the book to the ones the author felt most relevant to Changeling games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T16:44:08-08:00","id":1176412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1176406#post1176406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The list of Human Merits is likely abridged for limited space in the book to the ones the author felt most relevant to Changeling games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I missed that annotation. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T17:57:03-08:00","id":1176426,"title":"","content":"Slightly dumb question but:<br /> <br /> Can mortals still perceive and interact with goblin fruit? Even if a mortal either mostly or completely can't take advantage of a goblin fruits' benefits?<br /> <br /> (like, obviously regaining a point of Glamour doesn't mean anything since regular mortals don't have a Glamour pool to replenish)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T18:20:08-08:00","id":1176431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1176426#post1176426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly dumb question but:<br /> <br /> Can mortals still perceive and interact with goblin fruit? Even if a mortal either mostly or completely can't take advantage of a goblin fruits' benefits?<br /> <br /> (like, obviously regaining a point of Glamour doesn't mean anything since regular mortals don't have a Glamour pool to replenish)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fair question; in Underhill's materials, a mortal eating a goblin fruit was poisoned by it unless they were encorcelled. There was also a condition/tilt where they'd be able to see past the mask but it would instead warp the mien into something terrifying, and one of the sources was eating a goblin fruit. I don't remember seeing anything equivocal in the Kickstarter materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T12:41:16-08:00","id":1176570,"title":"","content":"What I'm about to say is no where in the 2nd manuscript as far as what I remember. <br /> <br /> But I'd add little odds and ends ST-fiat rulings to that. I'd say they see the fruit as something mundane/close but the fruit does something similar but odd to mortals. Like simple glamour fruit gives them a a kind of emotional high as it were. But not something that could easily be traced or defined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T11:40:47-08:00","id":1176809,"title":"","content":"So, I'm planning on running a one-shot for a group of CtL first-timers using the 2e Kickstarter preview rules, and something I'm struggling to find is the starting Glamour in 2e for new character. Can't seem to find a trace of it in either character creation or Advantages sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T12:35:20-08:00","id":1176816,"title":"","content":"I hadn't realized that was an issue until now. Fair point. The first edition has a player start with half their maximum glamour pool, so I'd go on that for now, though if this is a single session thing you may be justified in letting them run with a full pool. It depends on how much power you want them to have access to - not all contracts are easy to fulfill the loopholes for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:32:09-08:00","id":1178072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1173850#post1173850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a condition such as Too Solid Flesh enable application a supernatural banes to the sleeping victim? Silver? Fire? Staking?<br /> <br /> What about un-staking? How might the dream effects carry over?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hate bumping my question, but I thought it was fairly straightforward. Any ideas, folks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:14:40-08:00","id":1178079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1178072#post1178072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate bumping my question, but I thought it was fairly straightforward. Any ideas, folks?</div> </div> </div> </div> The only thing the Too Solid Flesh (or Flesh Too Sold, if Rose version) Tilt does is take any injuries you suffer in the dream and inflict them on the normal body as well. By a strict reading of the rules, even healing the dream form can't affect the physical body of injuries. So, strictly speaking, removing a stake in a dream would have no bearing on the stake in reality. That said, ask your ST, because they might have different ideas on how things work. <br /> <br /> I don't see anything about dream forms not taking the usual bashing/lethal/aggravated damage, so I assume banes apply as normal. Its another question, however, if &quot;Dream fire&quot; or &quot;dream silver / iron / salt&quot; should count as a bane, while I don't think anyone will argue that elemental Contracts that use fire would count as a bane for vamps, prommies and mummies, and I don't feel that dream-iron should count as actual iron. <br /> <br /> All in all, I think this is going to be a case where you have to ask your ST, since this kind of extrapolation is going to depend on the stories the ST is telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:53:10-08:00","id":1178107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1178079#post1178079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only thing the Too Solid Flesh (or Flesh Too Sold, if Rose version) Tilt does is take any injuries you suffer in the dream and inflict them on the normal body as well. By a strict reading of the rules, even healing the dream form can't affect the physical body of injuries. So, strictly speaking, removing a stake in a dream would have no bearing on the stake in reality. That said, ask your ST, because they might have different ideas on how things work.<br /> <br /> I don't see anything about dream forms not taking the usual bashing/lethal/aggravated damage, so I assume banes apply as normal. Its another question, however, if &quot;Dream fire&quot; or &quot;dream silver / iron / salt&quot; should count as a bane, while I don't think anyone will argue that elemental Contracts that use fire would count as a bane for vamps, prommies and mummies, and I don't feel that dream-iron should count as actual iron.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think this is going to be a case where you have to ask your ST, since this kind of extrapolation is going to depend on the stories the ST is telling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bThanks for the response, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>, I'm likely to be the ST being asked, and as I've missed the playtest doc/Kickstarter I'm trying to get my head around the core ideas as far as I can. Plotting, yaknow.<br /> <br /> So essentially the point is: Flesh Too Solid (preferring Rose's version) is harmful tilt and not something that could bend a dream to benefit the dreamer (healing). That, conceptually, opens up the door for a Contract that does the reverse, empowering fantastic dream-healing to be reflected in reality.<br /> <br /> I'll have to see what to what extent dreamweaving skills enable creation of things within dreams, but if the Changeling weilds a bane-creating Contract then yeah--it should definitely convey damage... if not aggravated, then lethal. And absolutely: no iron! At least, not that actually damages as cold iron does. I can imagine that forcefully presented iron, by the dreamer, might cause fae in their dream to step back and take pause simply because that is the normal course of their relationship (contract) with iron....<br /> <br /> Actually just thought of how to handle &quot;unstaking&quot;--the stake is part of the dreaming, torpic vampire's body, and thus sympathetically vulnerable to damage in the form of accelerated wood decay/insects. So though it could not be physically removed (pulled), it might be reduced to dust...?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:00:06-08:00","id":1178108,"title":"","content":"My question:<br /> Goblin contracts have a double price: standard glamour cost AND debt points. Having low debt accumulated may give the GM chances to subtract dices from the player, and having too much may risk having the character to become a hob.<br /> On top of that, In order to remove debt points the character has to complete difficult quest like: guessing the goblin\u00b4s true name, finding his missing heart in the Hedge, etc...<br /> <br /> Isn\u00b4t... well, a bit too much compared with standard contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T13:30:43-08:00","id":1178177,"title":"","content":"The upside is supposed to be that they either do things outside the theme of any contract or noticably more powerful than a contract with similar EXP costs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T13:47:43-08:00","id":1178179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1178108#post1178108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn\u00b4t... well, a bit too much compared with standard contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, that seems thematically on-point for Goblin Contracts to be convoluted messes in compared to the more well known and well-worn Arcadian and Court contracts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T14:52:04-08:00","id":1178216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1178108#post1178108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, In order to remove debt points the character has to complete difficult quest like: guessing the goblin\u00b4s true name, finding his missing heart in the Hedge, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for mortals. Changelings vent Debt through the aforementioned penalties much more easily, and there's a core Merit whose entire mechanical function is reducing your Goblin Debt without harm on a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:28:45-08:00","id":1178232,"title":"","content":"The Autumn court also have a way to vent their Goblin Debt via their mantle, though it's once per story as opposed to the merit's more regular means.<br /> <br /> Goblin Debt is a way for reigning in what are otherwise potent, and cheap, contracts. The ability to permanently erase memories, to make someone believe a lie made so long as it isn't demonstrably false, or to bolster the power of Kenning should not be underestimated and can break a game without something to give a person pause for their use. Of course, Goblin Debt isn't designed to be a noose, simply a stopgap. If the ST is using it as a looming threat...well, suffice to say, it's not really being used as designed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:23:24-08:00","id":1178385,"title":"","content":"I hate to double post, but the Autumn Mantle's fifth dot effect confuses me; by paying two glamour, a Changeling can exactly replicate a magical effect that has affected them during the scene and choose a new target. Does that mean they can exactly replicate the end result (the amount of damage or conditions), the casting roll (the die pool of the power used) or they use their own equivalent minus other requirements (Wyrd instead of a Vampire's Blood Potency and their own Wits + Expression rating)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T09:30:15-08:00","id":1178457,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. It says &quot;exactly&quot; so I would treat it as achieving the same number of successes as the original roll, although if it's a contested power the target rolls their own pool normally, which might alter the final result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T13:55:09-08:00","id":1178538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1178107#post1178107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So essentially the point is: Flesh Too Solid (preferring Rose's version) is harmful tilt and not something that could bend a dream to benefit the dreamer (healing). That, conceptually, opens up the door for a Contract that does the reverse, empowering fantastic dream-healing to be reflected in reality.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely be interested in such a dream-healing contract if anyone was willing to create one, since my character concept relies on the old Oneirophysic ability to heal people through dreams, and it's a shame if there's no way to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T08:42:32-08:00","id":1180730,"title":"","content":"Ok, iron/cold iron questions for a 5th-century DE use: (working from v6 compiled obsolete playtest document, mind you)<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Iron that is at least half pure ignores fae-born defenses and magic. ... Iron is difficult to find in the modern day, outside of antique shops, old estates surrounded by wrought-iron fences, special order, and so on.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> 1. So this sounds like &quot;iron&quot; is being treated as specifically iron and not steel, yes? But! Even highly engineered iron (cast iron types) are at most perhaps 6-7% carbon and silicon. You only get serious mixtures of something else (such as nickle) if you're alloying in other ferrous elements for specific purposes; these are referred to as &quot;ferroalloys&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;To qualify as \u201ccold iron,\u201d the metal cannot have been shaped or transformed by magic. It must have been forged by hand, not mass-produced, cast, or created by a machine.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> 2. Ok... so this is not generally what we would call cold-working. Hot-working iron involves smelting it, generally, and is used for all ironworking beyond very early phases--which were also periods when meteoric iron was the most common type (and still very rare and valuable, roughly 40x silver of same weight). Early iron smelting involved some form of a bloomery and produced metallic iron at temperatures below its melting point with very low carbon content; it would be further worked (&quot;wrought&quot;) to force out slag and compress an otherwise porous structure. Obviously, this is done by hand, using simple tools (hammer, tongs) and structures (bloomery, forge, optional coolant for tempering). <br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Subtract a changeling\u2019s Wyrd from all dice pools while she touches cold iron.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> 3. Sure thing. What qualifies as &quot;touching&quot; in this case? Is wearing a cold iron item sufficient? Is skin contact necessary? How about carrying something through gloves?<br /> <br /> Summary: so basically I'm trying to understand if a DE setting prior to the industrial production of iron (or, to be generous, late middle-ages advances beyond bloomery smelting) means that for all intents and purposes Changelings are utterly surrounded by a world of &quot;cold-iron&quot; at worst and &quot;iron&quot; at best.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, cold iron remains rare, meteoric iron pure enough to be hammered without heating (and potentially other natural ingots of the stuff). <br /> <br /> Any advice?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:25:49-08:00","id":1180957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cold Iron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is iron? Does steel count? Conceptually, iron is what most people consider iron. Your average person would perceive most swords, for example, as steel, but an iron gate as definitely iron.<br /> <br /> So-called &quot;cold iron&quot; acts as a frailty bane for changelings and True Fae. To qualify as &quot;cold iron,&quot; the metal must be mostly pure iron and magic cannot play a role in its creation in any way. It must be hand-forged, not mass-produced, cast, or created by a machine. Touching this iron inflicts aggravated damage on the Gentry and changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frailties</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banes cut instantly through all forms of armor and protective magics, and damage suffered from a bane cannot be healed until the bane is removed from the changeling's presence. Even acting against the source of a bane is difficult: Doing so requires spending a point of Willpower per action, which does not add dice to the pool. Additionally, the character suffers a three-die penalty on all rolls related to acting against the cause of a minor frailty. This penalty increases to -5 when acting against a major frailty.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;For all intents and purposes,&quot; yes, in a world where iron is common changelings are going to have trouble stretching their legs, but metal in general is a commodity and to my understanding most places in the fifth century weren't operating on a saturation level even approaching &quot;utterly surrounded.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T00:53:40-08:00","id":1181036,"title":"","content":"Re: iron vs. carbon steel:<br /> <br /> Yes, chemically the two are just different ranges on the same spectrum. There are a LOT of very important reasons why people don't usually think of it that way, though, and those reasons (together with the &quot;people not thinking of it that way&quot; part itself) are what informs steel not being a bane to the fae.<br /> <br /> IMO the more interesting question is, is a hand-forged wrought iron sword still cold iron if the wrought iron ingot the smith started with was made from pig iron? The answer to that is actually quite important in the event that there's ever a Changeling Dark Era set in certain parts of Asia that adopted the blast furnace early; China actually <i>started</i> with it, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:37:59-08:00","id":1181095,"title":"","content":"Huntsman questions: Do Huntsmen just harvest glamour normally, or can they eat Goblin Fruits, reap glamour, or do other special stuff? <br /> <br /> And Also, do they all have the same array of Huntsmen Dread Powers? <br /> <br /> On a related note, does Hunter's Panoply do anything other than giving them signature weapons and tells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T09:12:51-08:00","id":1181152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1180957#post1180957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;For all intents and purposes,&quot; yes, in a world where iron is common changelings are going to have trouble stretching their legs, but metal in general is a commodity and to my understanding most places in the fifth century weren't operating on a saturation level even approaching &quot;utterly surrounded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well by the late Roman period (3rd century) on virtually every tool had an iron component or version available, making copper and bronze optional and utilized only when cost, availability or fashion dictated them. Normally you'd find copper, bronze, and lead in alloys (e.g. pewter) for casting, while iron was refined to a usable form and hammered out into the desired implements--even iron-shod tools such as spades and hoes have been found, wool combs, and the like. Iron fittings for harness, clothing and other such were also common.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing though: production was never high and recycling of older/worn iron items was the norm as far as we can tell. Also, while earlier Roman military equipment was what we would call &quot;cold iron&quot; (even swords), later Roman and Anglo-Saxon weapons tended toward a core of iron surrounded by steel. I'll just assume here that armor likewise benefited from a shift/focus toward steel facing if not production solely of steel items. <br /> <br /> So.. from a setting standpoint, you're looking at a lot of &quot;cold iron&quot; items floating around--things that were crafted at the most basic, hand-driven model of iron production you can get shy of hammering off meteorite bits. BUT! As ST I would NOT call recycled iron items &quot;cold iron&quot; any longer. Nor would steel count as iron, since it's thought of differently by human perception. <br /> <br /> Cold Iron is:<br /> 1. Meteoric pure iron worked without significant temperature.<br /> 2. Bloomery-refined iron worked below melting point with hand-tools once only into a finished item.<br /> <br /> Iron is:<br /> 3. Bloomery-refined iron scrap that has been reheated and re-combined to form a new item.<br /> <br /> Not Iron is:<br /> 4. Iron alloyed to steel.<br /> 5. Iron heated to its melting point, whether for casting or other circumstances.<br /> <br /> By the way, there is a Changeling DE in China of similar nature, so blast-furnace invention there is kinda important. That's Three Kingdoms of Darkness, and I didn't note any comments on iron use/proliferation in that DE.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T17:59:15-08:00","id":1181292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181152#post1181152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.. from a setting standpoint, you're looking at a lot of &quot;cold iron&quot; items floating around--things that were crafted at the most basic, hand-driven model of iron production you can get shy of hammering off meteorite bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I'm saying that regardless of how prolific cold iron might have been in the realm of tools and weaponry, an iron cage or gate was a discrete inconvenience rather than the stuff of universal construction \u2014 this is one of many splats whose powers and thematics allow them to live in the woods on the edges of civilization in comparative comfort, and changelings in particular are very much oriented toward avoiding harm by not being there for the downswing of an irritable farmer's spade.<br /> <br /> &quot;For all intents and purposes&quot; a lot of the Lost have a decent reason not to live too deep in civilization if they intend to avail themselves of the advantages of their magic, which frankly sounds like it would track in a pre-industrial Dark Era that close to the fall of Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T07:04:13-08:00","id":1181385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181292#post1181292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. I'm saying that regardless of how prolific cold iron might have been in the realm of tools and weaponry, an iron cage or gate was a discrete inconvenience rather than the stuff of universal construction \u2014 this is one of many splats whose powers and thematics allow them to live in the woods on the edges of civilization in comparative comfort, and changelings in particular are very much oriented toward avoiding harm by not being there for the downswing of an irritable farmer's spade.<br /> <br /> &quot;For all intents and purposes&quot; a lot of the Lost have a decent reason not to live too deep in civilization if they intend to avail themselves of the advantages of their magic, which frankly sounds like it would track in a pre-industrial Dark Era that close to the fall of Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again, right. You're looking at, as a Changeling, interacting with a world of civilization that takes on a distinctively hostile tone when you realize that every half-successful farmer with iron clothing loops is carrying at best easy kryptonite to your glamour-bourne magic and at worst weaponizable assets. There's a reason why the peasantfolk go first to touch an bit of iron whenever magic, curses, and the fae come up.<br /> <br /> And they come up quite a bit (Western Europe, again, here) in reference to the woods. Following the tropes, the uncivilized woods is where humans atavistically go to return to hunting, where they go to respectfully obtain the produce of the forest (wood included) and where the lords direct their iron axes to clear more land for cultivation. It's where storied characters find adventure, where wild beasts live, and where people regularly do not come back from.<br /> <br /> The Fae live there, along with under/within other natural places. Finding fae in your house means you need to immediately either 1. get a priest, 2. put out offerings/payment, 3. ward it with iron. Two of these three things are likely to work.<br /> <br /> Living as a Changeling in this iron-sprinkled world means being unable to trust the efficacy of your magic most the time, in trade for being surrounded by crap the Huntsmen won't like either and you know exactly how to use.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T07:25:41-08:00","id":1181390,"title":"","content":"New question, separate post:<br /> <br /> [Older playtest doc, again.] There is some mention of &quot;bargains&quot; being used to shield Changelings from Huntsman detection, effectively integrating them into human society by giving them responsibilities so long as their human partner keeps their end of the agreement.<br /> <br /> Ok, this works great for spinning wool and cobbling shoes, etc.<br /> <br /> What about bargains that provide what would effectively be status (dots?) within human society? For example, legal adoption of the Changeling (or of the Changeling of a human child). Employment at a workplace? Or, bestowment of a title or office? Or degree? Marriage?<br /> <br /> Now the mentioned bargains are special because they require the Changeling to show their true form (scouring the Mask away, I assume, unless other merits permit dropping it more gently). You're not going to walk across the stage for your masters as a flaming-winged creature of shadow and light, so a few of these examples may be way out. What about others, where you can secure the &quot;meat&quot; of the bargain through a more private understanding between characters?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T14:59:10-08:00","id":1181499,"title":"","content":"What about them? What differs about changelings making deals for jobs or offices compared to regular talented humans making those deals? Not every bargain is a Bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T21:22:33-08:00","id":1181567,"title":"","content":"My reading of the Obliged condition (which is how the protection against Huntsmen is operationalized) is that a Bargain has to be a specific, discrete, repeated action on the Changeling's end. It's underpinned by the Wyrd's this-for-that nature, so both the Changeling and the human have to do a specific thing on a schedule for the Bargain to still be in force. Things like marriage, or getting a degree, are more like a change of state than a series of this-for-that exchanges. You could model those as an oath, but they wouldn't grant Obliged.<br /> <br /> Certain jobs might take the form of a Bargain, but it would be less &quot;Hire Johnny as your new IT guy&quot; and more &quot;If you leave an old laptop and an envelope full of cash on your windowsill, Johnny will sneak into you office at night and upgrade you to Windows 10.&quot; (Maybe that resembles your IT department, I don't know.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T06:47:13-08:00","id":1181637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181567#post1181567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading of the Obliged condition (which is how the protection against Huntsmen is operationalized) is that a Bargain has to be a specific, discrete, repeated action on the Changeling's end. It's underpinned by the Wyrd's this-for-that nature, so both the Changeling and the human have to do a specific thing on a schedule for the Bargain to still be in force. Things like marriage, or getting a degree, are more like a change of state than a series of this-for-that exchanges. You could model those as an oath, but they wouldn't grant Obliged.<br /> <br /> Certain jobs might take the form of a Bargain, but it would be less &quot;Hire Johnny as your new IT guy&quot; and more &quot;If you leave an old laptop and an envelope full of cash on your windowsill, Johnny will sneak into you office at night and upgrade you to Windows 10.&quot; (Maybe that resembles your IT department, I don't know.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First: LOL. Having very nearly <i>been</i> that IT department, nicely done. (Except: no cash involved.)<br /> <br /> Ok, so I can see the difference. I think part of my confusion is thinking that a Bargain and the Obliged condition are in some way analogous to a Demon's Cover, essentially establishing an innocuous role for the Changeling in human society such that the Huntsman overlooks him. <br /> <br /> On this topic I'm a bit surprised as well that the Bargain hinges on the Changeling revealing their true nature to the person with whom they are making the agreement. This, as I remember plenty of fairy tale stories had faeries who struck bargains with unsuspecting mortals--who later had the terms of their agreement brought up to their detriment. Further, Celtic mythology in particular is rife with tales of fae-wives who laid on conditions which when inevitably broken destroyed the family by revealing their nature/demanding their departure.<br /> <br /> I had thought the Bargain mechanism was intended to model these sorts of stories, but may be mistaken.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:30:54-08:00","id":1181653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181637#post1181637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, so I can see the difference. I think part of my confusion is thinking that a Bargain and the Obliged condition are in some way analogous to a Demon's Cover, essentially establishing an innocuous role for the Changeling in human society such that the Huntsman overlooks him. <br /> <br /> On this topic I'm a bit surprised as well that the Bargain hinges on the Changeling revealing their true nature to the person with whom they are making the agreement. This, as I remember plenty of fairy tale stories had faeries who struck bargains with unsuspecting mortals--who later had the terms of their agreement brought up to their detriment. Further, Celtic mythology in particular is rife with tales of fae-wives who laid on conditions which when inevitably broken destroyed the family by revealing their nature/demanding their departure.<br /> <br /> I had thought the Bargain mechanism was intended to model these sorts of stories, but may be mistaken.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Bargain is intended to hide a changeling in an innocuous fae role, rather than a human one. The Huntsman sees them and thinks, &quot;Wait, that's not the changeling I'm looking for. Look at how he's cleaning that house in exchange for a bowl of milk left on a hollow log... That's nothing more than a common house brownie. Boy, would I have looked stupid coming back with that!&quot; <br /> <br /> That said, I agree that it seems odd that they must reveal their nature, especially when the Bargain is something where the changeling can fulfill their end in an entirely mundane manner. I suppose that the &quot;deal with a secret faery&quot; trope is intended to be covered by the Gentry themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:36:37-08:00","id":1181654,"title":"","content":"Can Huntsmen see past the Mask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:06:02-08:00","id":1181661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181654#post1181654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Huntsmen see past the Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div> Rule of thumb is that if it has any amount of faerie magic, it can see through the Mask, from Gentry to Hobs to Fae Touched, and everything in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T10:14:28-08:00","id":1181699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181653#post1181653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the Bargain is intended to hide a changeling in an innocuous fae role, rather than a human one. The Huntsman sees them and thinks, &quot;Wait, that's not the changeling I'm looking for. Look at how he's cleaning that house in exchange for a bowl of milk left on a hollow log... That's nothing more than a common house brownie. Boy, would I have looked stupid coming back with that!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'd like to hear the whole story from the Huntsman's side!<br /> <br /> 8:01 am - arrive at work; park flaming horse. Queen of Air and Darkness yells at me for being late. Can't I just quit? Flipping burgers sounding pretty good! I like milk.<br /> 8:23 am - coffee machine is out of order. I kick it until it screams for mercy and spits grounds all over my best pants. Fine. Not like I have any meetings today.<br /> 8:45 am - all-hands meeting. &quot;Go around the table and share...&quot;<br /> 1:47 pm - lunch interrupted. Sandwich wasn't weeping much anyway. &quot;Go to Toronto they say! It'll be fine they say!&quot; Check weather. Snowing.<br /> ...<br /> 9:33 pm - leave diner. Horse won't start. Stupid snow!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181653#post1181653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I agree that it seems odd that they must reveal their nature, especially when the Bargain is something where the changeling can fulfill their end in an entirely mundane manner. I suppose that the &quot;deal with a secret faery&quot; trope is intended to be covered by the Gentry themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the secret faerie trope could be easily satisfied by a Gentry, but pity the poor human who hid the shawl of the Queen of Air and Darkness for twenty years to make her keep house! He'd better <i><b>never</b></i> go into the woods again!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:51:11-08:00","id":1181740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181653#post1181653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I agree that it seems odd that they must reveal their nature</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: They don't.<br /> <br /> Specific wording of the section's opening line notwithstanding, the requirement is that the changeling appear to the mortal in question without their Mask and make an offer \u2014 they explicitly don't have to give any details about why they have burning hair or extra digits or cloven hooves, or even reveal their mundane identity.<br /> <br /> What this produces is an identifiable narrative and role for a character who can otherwise have at least one entity sharing their Mask at any given time, as well as a relationship that can be entirely confined to &quot;the woman with obsidian teeth and a nacreous throat helps me get rid of the dead bodies that keep turning up behind my butcher shop twice a week in exchange for her pick of the choice cuts.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like it's notable that one of the main benefits of Obliged is shared with Goblin Queen, which itself shares Hedge Denizen's specification of &quot;you look very different from how people might have otherwise known you, but you have a tell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T00:55:53-08:00","id":1181935,"title":"","content":"Regarding cold iron and using Contracts: if a changeling is in contact with cold iron does it impede their ability to use Contracts, even if the Contract isn't specifically targeting the iron?<br /> <br /> For instance, if a changeling was imprisoned by cold iron chains and wanted to use Unravel the Tapestry to jump back in time to before he got the chains slapped on him and then try to stop that from happening on his second chance. Would the Contract still work as intended, or would it not on the basis of the changeling being in contact with cold iron while invoking the Contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T14:40:08-08:00","id":1182071,"title":"","content":"From the second preview doc: <span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">When in doubt, Storytellers should always favor iron piercing fae magic, or otherwise being immune to it. This limitation even applies to the basic advantages changeling characters possess; for example, iron restraints make a changeling unable to escape automatically with Glamour. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T15:35:55-08:00","id":1182095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181935#post1181935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding cold iron and using Contracts: if a changeling is in contact with cold iron does it impede their ability to use Contracts, even if the Contract isn't specifically targeting the iron?<br /> <br /> For instance, if a changeling was imprisoned by cold iron chains and wanted to use Unravel the Tapestry to jump back in time to before he got the chains slapped on him and then try to stop that from happening on his second chance. Would the Contract still work as intended, or would it not on the basis of the changeling being in contact with cold iron while invoking the Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Changeling could do that, what would be the danger of being trapped in iron, especially if they were a Darkling and hid in the shadows, or used any number of other contracts to simply slip through the walls or become invisible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T17:52:35-08:00","id":1182129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182071#post1182071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the second preview doc: <span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">When in doubt, Storytellers should always favor iron piercing fae magic, or otherwise being immune to it. This limitation even applies to the basic advantages changeling characters possess; for example, iron restraints make a changeling unable to escape automatically with Glamour. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182095#post1182095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Changeling could do that, what would be the danger of being trapped in iron, especially if they were a Darkling and hid in the shadows, or used any number of other contracts to simply slip through the walls or become invisible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:37:50-08:00","id":1182594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181740#post1181740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: They don't.<br /> <br /> Specific wording of the section's opening line notwithstanding, the requirement is that the changeling appear to the mortal in question without their Mask and make an offer \u2014 they explicitly don't have to give any details about why they have burning hair or extra digits or cloven hooves, or even reveal their mundane identity.<br /> <br /> What this produces is an identifiable narrative and role for a character who can otherwise have at least one entity sharing their Mask at any given time, as well as a relationship that can be entirely confined to &quot;the woman with obsidian teeth and a nacreous throat helps me get rid of the dead bodies that keep turning up behind my butcher shop twice a week in exchange for her pick of the choice cuts.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting thought just occurred: so could you, as a Changeling, invade a given person's dream, up the intensity such that they'll remember (lucid dreaming), and then reveal your form without Mask and bargain with them? Or, does it have to accomplished entirely Ironside?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1181740#post1181740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's notable that one of the main benefits of Obliged is shared with Goblin Queen, which itself shares Hedge Denizen's specification of &quot;you look very different from how people might have otherwise known you, but you have a tell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to follow. And will take a dramatic failure to ask for clarification. Are you hinting at the increased difficulty of Huntsmen to find the character as being similar between Obliged and Goblin Queen?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:42:57-08:00","id":1182597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182095#post1182095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Changeling could do that, what would be the danger of being trapped in iron, especially if they were a Darkling and hid in the shadows, or used any number of other contracts to simply slip through the walls or become invisible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and once of the biggest dangers to a Changeling in a DE is that they will be caught by the local authorities and hammered into iron manacles as a matter of course. Escaping from a prison cell with iron bars won't be hard, however, unless they are also chained up with the stuff, since there is likely a stone or wooden wall/floor/ceiling to work with. Modern steel handcuffs, however, are <b><i>not</i></b> iron, and therefore easy to escape from.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder if there's a Changeling industrialist who labored hard in the 1800s to perfect widespread steel manufacturing....<br /> <br /> Note again that iron in this case doesn't have to be <b><i>cold iron</i></b> just regular iron would be disruptive enough to prevent easy escape.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:44:13-08:00","id":1182598,"title":"","content":"New question. Easy one I promise?<br /> <br /> How would a Changeling draw multiple sleepers (lowercase &quot;s&quot;) into the same dream? Is that feasible? The character is basically merging Bastions in that case, no?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T08:56:56-08:00","id":1182620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182598#post1182598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would a Changeling draw multiple sleepers (lowercase &quot;s&quot;) into the same dream? Is that feasible? The character is basically merging Bastions in that case, no?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you're trying to do. A whole motley can enter the same dream at once just by falling asleep while in physical contact with one another. (The intended image is probably &quot;laying on the floor, holding hands&quot; but I am also in favor of the &quot;sleeping in a big ol' puppy pile&quot; interpretation.) One member of the group then rolls to pass through the Gate of Ivory and onto the Dreaming Roads, and she can bring the rest with her unless they spend Glamour to resist. Non-Changelings, including other supernaturals, can be brought along the same way.<br /> <br /> If your questions is, &quot;How can this changeling gather the motley (or group otherwise specified) together in a dream if they're not together in the waking world?&quot; there doesn't seem to be any way to do this in the RAW. Changelings would have to separately enter the Dreaming Roads and meet up there. The text implies that mortals can end up on the Dreaming Roads by accident, so maaaybe you can bring a dreamer out of their Bastion without waking them -- but there's no indication of whether the Bastion would remain, like an empty set, or would crumble as soon as the dreamer leaves. And you'd still need to conduct each dreamer along the Dreaming Roads to whatever Bastion you wanted to gather them into, and then get them in...<br /> <br /> All that said, I'd say the best way to achieve this effect would be to create a set of Tokens with the explicit power of &quot;draws sleeping owners into a common Bastion when activated.&quot; A set of chessmen, for instance, which can be activated by whoever possesses the king. Then your problem is distributing the rest of the pieces to the intended targets, and making sure they keep them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T09:10:18-08:00","id":1182625,"title":"","content":"Gonna repost these and one more unrelated question to see if they get answered this time<br /> <br /> Huntsman questions: Do Huntsmen just harvest glamour normally, or can they eat Goblin Fruits, reap glamour, or do other special stuff? <br /> <br /> And Also, do they all have the same array of Huntsmen Dread Powers? <br /> <br /> On a related note, does Hunter's Panoply do anything other than giving them signature weapons and tells?<br /> <br /> Would the classic iron horseshoe hung over the door be enough to stop Contracts that affect the house and those currently inside its walls? Would an iron good-luck charm, as rare as that is, protect against stuff like the Fleeting Seasonal Contracts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T10:30:51-08:00","id":1182644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182620#post1182620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on what you're trying to do. A whole motley can enter the same dream at once just by falling asleep while in physical contact with one another. (The intended image is probably &quot;laying on the floor, holding hands&quot; but I am also in favor of the &quot;sleeping in a big ol' puppy pile&quot; interpretation.) One member of the group then rolls to pass through the Gate of Ivory and onto the Dreaming Roads, and she can bring the rest with her unless they spend Glamour to resist. Non-Changelings, including other supernaturals, can be brought along the same way.<br /> <br /> If your questions is, &quot;How can this changeling gather the motley (or group otherwise specified) together in a dream if they're not together in the waking world?&quot; there doesn't seem to be any way to do this in the RAW. Changelings would have to separately enter the Dreaming Roads and meet up there. The text implies that mortals can end up on the Dreaming Roads by accident, so maaaybe you can bring a dreamer out of their Bastion without waking them -- but there's no indication of whether the Bastion would remain, like an empty set, or would crumble as soon as the dreamer leaves. And you'd still need to conduct each dreamer along the Dreaming Roads to whatever Bastion you wanted to gather them into, and then get them in...<br /> <br /> All that said, I'd say the best way to achieve this effect would be to create a set of Tokens with the explicit power of &quot;draws sleeping owners into a common Bastion when activated.&quot; A set of chessmen, for instance, which can be activated by whoever possesses the king. Then your problem is distributing the rest of the pieces to the intended targets, and making sure they keep them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent and useful response, calling up several possibilities. I had in mind specifically things like &quot;several sleepers are in a general area (e.g. town)--how to get them to the shared experience of a dream?&quot; Going in and taking them on a trip, one by one, sounds like a good adventure.<br /> <br /> Then the shortcut (Token) could work but I also recall a (ancient playtest) Contract (?I think?) that had the Changeling craft a small item and leave it within the target's dream-self... after which they would be favorably inclined to the Changeling so long as the object remained in their Bastion. A Contract that involved giving a token (small &quot;t&quot;) to the target, and then drew their dreaming self either to the Changeling's Bastion or a third location could work, no?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:46:39-08:00","id":1182670,"title":"","content":"1) Is there a way for mortal occultists to cause Glamour loss (especially in Gentry)?<br /> <br /> 1) a) What're the effects of new new Bane of Iron?<br /> <br /> 2) What's the tl;dr version of the new new fluff of core Seemings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T12:46:12-08:00","id":1182682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182625#post1182625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsman questions: Do Huntsmen just harvest glamour normally, or can they eat Goblin Fruits, reap glamour, or do other special stuff?<br /> <br /> And Also, do they all have the same array of Huntsmen Dread Powers?<br /> <br /> On a related note, does Hunter's Panoply do anything other than giving them signature weapons and tells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsmen recover Glamour by reaping and eating goblin fruit. They cannot harvest Glamour.<br /> <br /> There are four Dread Powers shared by all Huntsmen. Each Huntsman then has other Dread Powers selected from the general Horror list, or from a provided list of six more Dread Powers which are unique to Huntsmen, but not shared by all of them.<br /> <br /> The Hunter's Panoply Dread Power confers certain benefits to using the Huntsman's signature weapons and tools, and allows them to recall their panoply with Glamour when lost, but imposes a penalty when they attempt an action they would normally use their tool for without first recovering it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182670#post1182670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is there a way for mortal occultists to cause Glamour loss (especially in Gentry)?<br /> <br /> 1) a) What're the effects of new new Bane of Iron?<br /> <br /> 2) What's the tl;dr version of the new new fluff of core Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no provided method by which a mortal occultist would sap Glamour from the fae. That's not to say it couldn't somehow be done, but there's no relevant core mechanic.<br /> <br /> Iron bypasses magical fae defenses and resists magical fae manipulation, and changelings bound by iron can't portal out of it. Hand-forged iron inflicts aggravated damage to changelings and the True Fae.<br /> <br /> The fluff identity of the core Seemings is largely in keeping with the first edition Seemings. The writeups emphasize agency and the &quot;now&quot; of the Seemings somewhat more than first edition, which largely emphasized the &quot;then&quot; of the Durance more, but this is a difference of degree, not kind. Ogres gain a bit more of painting as defenders of the things they care about once they escape the Durance, and the element of spite doesn't drive the Wizened as much, who are instead largely restless and in need of control, driven to plan and labor because it's empowering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 02-05-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T17:16:35-08:00","id":1182750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1182594#post1182594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting thought just occurred: so could you, as a Changeling, invade a given person's dream, up the intensity such that they'll remember (lucid dreaming), and then reveal your form without Mask and bargain with them? Or, does it have to accomplished entirely Ironside?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dream Intensity no longer being a thing notwithstanding, that is in fact a thing that I have previously leaned on in prior discussions where &quot;the target has to see you with your Mask is a huge risk&quot; was presented as an argument against bargains' utility \u2014 the most basic long-term oneiromancy effect allows you to give someone information that they will remember in content without remembering its source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fail to follow. And will take a dramatic failure to ask for clarification. Are you hinting at the increased difficulty of Huntsmen to find the character as being similar between Obliged and Goblin Queen?<br /> --Khanwulf </div> </div> </div>Increased difficulty of <i>any</i> fae to track the character, but yes.<br /> <br /> The evolutionary pressures of the Wyrd make &quot;magical subcontractor&quot; a natural role for changelings to fall into, and that manifests in a lot of different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-05-2018, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T18:59:46-08:00","id":1182775,"title":"","content":"Doesn't a Changeling appear as her true self while in a dream anyways, be it in her own dreams or of those she visits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T08:16:06-08:00","id":1184403,"title":"","content":"I'm quite sure this has been already discussed somewhere.<br /> <br /> How does Mask interact with recording devices? Essentially, there apper to be two reasonable rulings:<br /> (i) Since Mask is an illusion, a photo of a changeling records only Mien, but the photo itself is only subject to a Mask. In particular, other changelings can just look at a picture of a large group and immediately tell whether some changelings or other Fae creatures are present there.<br /> (ii) Mask is not only an illusion, it actually interacts with recording devices so as to produce the image of the Mask. No one can ever tell, whether you are a Changeling or not just by looking at some pictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:29:58-08:00","id":1185165,"title":"","content":"Is Wyrd pronounced &quot;word&quot; or &quot;weird&quot;? It has been bugging me for a while now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:36:24-08:00","id":1185167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1185165#post1185165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Wyrd pronounced &amp;quot;word&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;weird&amp;quot;? It has been bugging me for a while now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its pronounced Weird","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:42:07-08:00","id":1185170,"title":"","content":"I think its pronounced in-between word and weird. I've always leaned closer to word tho. (keep in mind tho i'm not an english native speaker so that might influence a bit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T07:46:13-08:00","id":1185173,"title":"","content":"What we need is a native German speaker, as i believe thats the origin of the word","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:19:13-08:00","id":1185193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1185165#post1185165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Wyrd pronounced &quot;word&quot; or &quot;weird&quot;? It has been bugging me for a while now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are correct! Although, I prefer &quot;weird&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re-pyNX78I\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re-pyNX78I\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re-pyNX78I\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9re-pyNX78I </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T15:08:29-08:00","id":1187356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1184403#post1184403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite sure this has been already discussed somewhere.<br /> <br /> How does Mask interact with recording devices? Essentially, there apper to be two reasonable rulings:<br /> (i) Since Mask is an illusion, a photo of a changeling records only Mien, but the photo itself is only subject to a Mask. In particular, other changelings can just look at a picture of a large group and immediately tell whether some changelings or other Fae creatures are present there.<br /> (ii) Mask is not only an illusion, it actually interacts with recording devices so as to produce the image of the Mask. No one can ever tell, whether you are a Changeling or not just by looking at some pictures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In a similar vein, if a changeling has antlers, does he fit through a door? Does he shuffle in sideways? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We've house ruled that the antlers are only &quot;there&quot; when the Wyrd finds it thematically relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T18:34:02-08:00","id":1187422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1187356#post1187356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In a similar vein, if a changeling has antlers, does he fit through a door? Does he shuffle in sideways? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We've house ruled that the antlers are only &quot;there&quot; when the Wyrd finds it thematically relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To maintain the theme of &quot;you can't go back&quot; and lasting marks, I would actually suggest that yeah, if you've got antlers, you might have to shuffle through doors sideways. The Mask might alter how ordinary humans perceive this: they might see you as taller and having to duck down, or a little clumsy and trip-prone, or something. Small everyday inconveniences are pretty appropriate for certain miens.<br /> <br /> Bigger inconveniences than that ought to be opt-in from player-side or handwaved. The character's consent isn't necessarily, but the player's is, if you're going to have stuff like a headless horseman who actually has to carry around his head (likely a Persistent Condition that can award beats), and a lightning elemental should be able to get into a pool without shocking everyone who's swimming. But if it comes down to something flavorful that doesn't have be narratively labored over all the time, something where you can just say &quot;yeah he doesn't like doors anymore because it's awkward getting in,&quot; I think that's a comfortable space to express the reality of the mien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T20:31:33-08:00","id":1187444,"title":"","content":"I honestly love those little super-minor Frailties. The kind of things that won't make most people suspicious, but still make you look weird. I honestly don't want them covered by the Mask personally. If a Windwing has to wear loose or backless clothing to accomodate their wings, people should wonder why she's wearing that stuff in Winter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T09:36:05-08:00","id":1187580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1187422#post1187422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you're going to have stuff like a headless horseman who actually has to carry around his head (likely a Persistent Condition that can award beats), and a lightning elemental should be able to get into a pool without shocking everyone who's swimming. But if it comes down to something flavorful that doesn't have be narratively labored over all the time, something where you can just say &quot;yeah he doesn't like doors anymore because it's awkward getting in,&quot; I think that's a comfortable space to express the reality of the mien.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just as quickly, she rushes back into the cafe: 'sorry!' she smiles weakly, 'forgot my bag!' before scurrying after her companions.<br /> You swear, that girl would forget her head if it wasn't attached.<br /> The coffee could use a bit more cream, and while rummaging through the bin the idle thought lingers: why does she always pick up that old thing by the sides--it has a handle after all....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 02-19-2018, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T13:59:49-08:00","id":1187963,"title":"","content":"Could someone tell me how you Calculate how many Clarity Boxes you have, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T14:20:00-08:00","id":1187971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1187963#post1187963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone tell me how you Calculate how many Clarity Boxes you have, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wits + Composure + incorporated Icons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:40:30-08:00","id":1190221,"title":"","content":"Do tokens lose their Mask once activated in either 1e or 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T09:09:32-08:00","id":1190300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1190221#post1190221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do tokens lose their Mask once activated in either 1e or 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, &quot;a token reveals (only to changelings)&quot; its mien (page 201); in 2e, activated tokens &quot;[reveal] their true fae natures to anyone who can see through the Mask.&quot; So in either edition, I interpret this as meaning a mortal still wouldn't see through the active token's Mask, but changelings, fae-touched, etc. would.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T02:21:03-07:00","id":1196421,"title":"","content":"This may be a bit of a silly question, but is a Hollow linked to ironside via a permanently open hedgegate (so anyone could wander in if they opened the right door) or is it simply a hedgegate that leades from a particular door to the Hollow? I'm in a game and have a dot of Hollow, but one of the motley is concerned with putting the Hollow entrance inside of the Safehouse we have, as it could be a way someone could reliably invade from the Hedge. We haven't quite settled where the entrance is as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:20:56-07:00","id":1196523,"title":"","content":"Reading the Hollow Merit description: yes, the Hollow has a permanent entrance in the real world, unless you buy the Easy Access enhancement at Hollow 3. But anyone attempting to invade a Hollow a) has to have a Wyrd higher than the Hollow's rating and b) has to beat you in a Clash of Wills. Which isn't much comfort if you're starting characters, I know, but it's not like any hob can just walk in while you're not there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T18:34:53-07:00","id":1196672,"title":"","content":"Not permanently <i>open</i>, but the entrance to a Hollow is definitely consistently accessible by the changeling barring particular examples and the space itself is specifically secure against intrusion under normal circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T06:23:50-07:00","id":1198307,"title":"","content":"If a Changeling with an active Mask is subjected to shape-changing magic (regardless of type), does their Mask reshape itself to accommodate their physical form?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of things such as taking animal forms or the like, stemming from crossover applications (Life magic, etc.). My assumption is that *if* there are Changeling-centered shapeshifting powers the Mask would of course accommodate.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:28:41-07:00","id":1201756,"title":"","content":"From what I understand about the Mask, it works to hide the existence of fairy magic from the mortal world. If the shapeshifting affect alters the changeling's physical form so that it it is no longer possesses Wyrd tainted abnormalities, what does the Mask have to hide?<br /> <br /> I guess the real question is: Can magical effects that operate outside of the Wyrd erase the mutations inflicted upon a changeling's body by the Gentry? Like, if a mage uses their magic to a transform a changeling with stone skin into a fox ... does the changeling become a normal fox, or does he become a fox with stone fur that just looks like a fox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T00:47:59-07:00","id":1201870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1198307#post1198307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Changeling with an active Mask is subjected to shape-changing magic (regardless of type), does their Mask reshape itself to accommodate their physical form?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of things such as taking animal forms or the like, stemming from crossover applications (Life magic, etc.). My assumption is that *if* there are Changeling-centered shapeshifting powers the Mask would of course accommodate.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Mask changes to accomodate - it's why powers such as Chrysalis or Props And Scenary, which change a Changeling into an animal or an object respectively, hide them away from people who can't see past the Mask. Otherwise, they would see normal people acting like animals or standing awkwardly. This would also apply to transformations forced upon a Changeling by another being.<br /> <br /> Rule of thumb is, unless it specifies a Changeling's Mien or Mask, presume a transformation affects both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1201756#post1201756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand about the Mask, it works to hide the existence of fairy magic from the mortal world. If the shapeshifting affect alters the changeling's physical form so that it it is no longer possesses Wyrd tainted abnormalities, what does the Mask have to hide?<br /> <br /> I guess the real question is: Can magical effects that operate outside of the Wyrd erase the mutations inflicted upon a changeling's body by the Gentry? Like, if a mage uses their magic to a transform a changeling with stone skin into a fox ... does the changeling become a normal fox, or does he become a fox with stone fur that just looks like a fox?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Changeling's transformation is complete and total - from their blood to their bones to their very soul, they are considered fae, otherwise iron would not affect them as it does. The closest that a fae would have to &quot;Wyrd tained abnormalities&quot; would be a Fae-Touched, that being a person who has made a significant promise to someone who became a Changeling, journeyed into the Hedge and absorbed some of its ambient magic, and managed to escape in turn. Even in that case, the &quot;abnormalities&quot; would be that fae magic itself, and a Fae-Touched is still changed so innately they are harmed by iron like a Changeling is. A Mage cannot change a Changeling back into a human anymore than they could turn a normal mortal into a Changeling, unless they were an Archmage and even then that change could be dispelled. As noted above, even if a Mage transforms a Changeling so they are a fox, they will look like a fox both to Mask and Mien...but as for whether their Mien would lack their stone fur depends on the Storyteller, and or if the spell specifically was to change a Changeling into a fox or a normal person into a fox. If it was for just a normal person, I'd rule no because it wasn't specifically meant to affect the fae nature of the person. If it was for a Changeling...well that'd still be quite a feat, and they'd still have a Changeling on their hands, not just a fox.<br /> <br /> Even if someone could change a Changeling's Mien so it no longer looks fae, that doesn't mean that they aren't. The Mask serves not only to keep other people from realizing a Changeling is anything but human, but also serves to keep other fae from tracking a Changeling down easily. Without their Mask, a Changeling leaves a trail that any fae can follow, which is why journeying through the Hedge (where their Mask is innately down) is a risky prospect for them. The Mask suppresses their fae nature, to the point that when a Changeling eschews it when it's normally up their contracts are innately more potent (as in they always result in an Exceptional Success).<br /> <br /> One final note on the subject. Given a Changeling's durance was so horrific that they were changed innately, their mien itself being changed by an outside force would probably be an attack on their clarity and thus sanity, since yet another being is transforming them outside of their control. If anything, it being a non-fae source would probably be worse, since it'd be from a power they wouldn't have an innate understanding unlike the Wyrd. If they willingly consented or even asked for it, it may not be as bad but it is a significant transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T12:24:48-07:00","id":1201985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1201870#post1201870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the Mask changes to accomodate - it's why powers such as Chrysalis or Props And Scenary, which change a Changeling into an animal or an object respectively, hide them away from people who can't see past the Mask. Otherwise, they would see normal people acting like animals or standing awkwardly. This would also apply to transformations forced upon a Changeling by another being.<br /> <br /> Rule of thumb is, unless it specifies a Changeling's Mien or Mask, presume a transformation affects both.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A Changeling's transformation is complete and total - from their blood to their bones to their very soul, they are considered fae, otherwise iron would not affect them as it does. The closest that a fae would have to &quot;Wyrd tained abnormalities&quot; would be a Fae-Touched, that being a person who has made a significant promise to someone who became a Changeling, journeyed into the Hedge and absorbed some of its ambient magic, and managed to escape in turn. Even in that case, the &quot;abnormalities&quot; would be that fae magic itself, and a Fae-Touched is still changed so innately they are harmed by iron like a Changeling is. A Mage cannot change a Changeling back into a human anymore than they could turn a normal mortal into a Changeling, unless they were an Archmage and even then that change could be dispelled. As noted above, even if a Mage transforms a Changeling so they are a fox, they will look like a fox both to Mask and Mien...but as for whether their Mien would lack their stone fur depends on the Storyteller, and or if the spell specifically was to change a Changeling into a fox or a normal person into a fox. If it was for just a normal person, I'd rule no because it wasn't specifically meant to affect the fae nature of the person. If it was for a Changeling...well that'd still be quite a feat, and they'd still have a Changeling on their hands, not just a fox.<br /> <br /> Even if someone could change a Changeling's Mien so it no longer looks fae, that doesn't mean that they aren't. The Mask serves not only to keep other people from realizing a Changeling is anything but human, but also serves to keep other fae from tracking a Changeling down easily. Without their Mask, a Changeling leaves a trail that any fae can follow, which is why journeying through the Hedge (where their Mask is innately down) is a risky prospect for them. The Mask suppresses their fae nature, to the point that when a Changeling eschews it when it's normally up their contracts are innately more potent (as in they always result in an Exceptional Success).<br /> <br /> One final note on the subject. Given a Changeling's durance was so horrific that they were changed innately, their mien itself being changed by an outside force would probably be an attack on their clarity and thus sanity, since yet another being is transforming them outside of their control. If anything, it being a non-fae source would probably be worse, since it'd be from a power they wouldn't have an innate understanding unlike the Wyrd. If they willingly consented or even asked for it, it may not be as bad but it is a significant transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What I mean by &quot;abnornormality&quot; is a feature that deviates from the normal form associated with humanity. Horns are an abnormality for a human. Changelings, before their durance, were humans. So any changes made to their form from Arcadia can be considered an abnormality (or mutation, as it were). <br /> <br /> Personally, I am of the mind that if it were so easy to transform the physicality of a changeling, finding a mage would be one of the first things that most changelings would do upon finding out about their existence. I am with you about the depth of the changes made to Changeling's being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T12:49:23-07:00","id":1201992,"title":"","content":"Only problem is that Changelings don't automatically know mages are even a possibility. And those who hear about them are likely to hear horror stories about them wanting to cut you up for magical experiments if you give them the chance. Plus, I feel like most Changelings would be a bit scared of getting bound by the Wyrd to a debt that great.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus, this also assumes the Awakened exist in your setting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:17:54-07:00","id":1201997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1201985#post1201985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean by &quot;abnornormality&quot; is a feature that deviates from the normal form associated with humanity. Horns are an abnormality for a human. Changelings, before their durance, were humans. So any changes made to their form from Arcadia can be considered an abnormality (or mutation, as it were).<br /> <br /> Personally, I am of the mind that if it were so easy to transform the physicality of a changeling, finding a mage would be one of the first things that most changelings would do upon finding out about their existence. I am with you about the depth of the changes made to Changeling's being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize if I came (and come) across as lecturing, but your definitions are a little...odd, considering that by that meaning every single supernatural creature a player can play has &quot;abnormalities&quot;. From a Vampire's fangs and requirements for Vitae, to a Werewolf's rage and otherworldly forms, to a Mage's ability to affect the universe with their magic, anything that a player can play that isn't mundane human is abnormal and mutated. &quot;Normal&quot; is a <i>very</i> subjective term in real life, and in a world where someone can meet or become virtually anything they can imagine it becomes even more flexible.<br /> <br /> A Changeling's physicality isn't any easier to change than most mortals. Changelings are humans who were taken to Arcadia and forced to become the property of a True Fae, allowing said True Fae to basically alter them as they please. The True Fae, Gentry, Keepers or however you want to refer to them are practically gods in their domain, and can change their surroundings and property to fit their whims. They possess a level of power not even obtainable by a Changeling at Wyrd 10, even when compared to a Gentry who is effectively at Wyrd 6. Even taking out the factor of the Gentry, the Hedge by its very nature turns people into &quot;stranger, truer versions of themselves&quot;, meaning any normal mortal (or potentially any other supernatural) who wanders the Hedge long enough becomes a Hobgoblin that in some way represents who and what they were in reality. Everything involved here is not only on a scale of power practically no playable supernatural can achieve, it is a process that is practically part of the laws of physics for the realm the Hedge and Arcadia inhabit. Just as everything degrades on the molecular level in the normal realm, so does everything change in the Hedge until it fits that particular system, and once it fits then that form becomes all but permanent for them. In exchange for these transformations, these beings become tied to the Wyrd and gain power through it.<br /> <br /> This isn't like being tainted by the Abyss and transformed in ways that don't make logistical sense - the Hedge and Gentry have a logic to their transformations, but it's not a human logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:16:06-07:00","id":1202066,"title":"","content":"Oh, threads like this have a tendancy to make people sound pedantic. No worries. It seems like we are debating semantics. I view all the above examples as abnormalities (fangs, blah blah), and I wasn't using the term to refer to a specific in-game system definition but rather a change that physically/metaphysical altered a once &quot;normal&quot; human into something else. Yanno, the definition being the deviation from the &quot;normal&quot; (like, yanno, a changeling being just a normal human before they had horns / wings / preternatural beauty etc etc).<br /> <br /> I don't know what the Abyss is. The only game from WW/OP that I have ever played and continue to play is Changeling (all the various iterations since '96), so I am not sure about the other cosmologies that you speak of. Please excuse my ignorance on those specific topics. I have downloaded the Chronicles of Darkness bundle reward on my backer kit, but have yet to read any of the other games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1201992#post1201992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only problem is that Changelings don't automatically know mages are even a possibility. And those who hear about them are likely to hear horror stories about them wanting to cut you up for magical experiments if you give them the chance. Plus, I feel like most Changelings would be a bit scared of getting bound by the Wyrd to a debt that great.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus, this also assumes the Awakened exist in your setting</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm feeling you. I'm just wondering now how sacrosanct a changeling's physicality is when being forced to transform into something beyond what their Keeper intended by an outside, non Wyrd aligned force. Would their fairy traits carry on over to the new form, pushing its way past cosmetic alterations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:43:29-07:00","id":1202092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202066#post1202066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm feeling you. I'm just wondering now how sacrosanct a changeling's physicality is when being forced to transform into something beyond what their Keeper intended by an outside, non Wyrd aligned force. Would their fairy traits carry on over to the new form, pushing its way past cosmetic alterations?</div> </div> </div> </div>First: oh boy, sorry for lighting a fire.<br /> <br /> Second: the above is my exact point to the question. And it seems like a reasonably answer is &quot;you can change (regardless of method) your physical form but will retain a the soul-deep nature of your mien despite doing so, which is not a new issue since your mask will warp to continue to make you look 'mundane'&quot;. Am I wrong?<br /> <br /> Noted is the Clarity hit potential for undergoing form-warping magics outside the Wyrd. Good call!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:46:38-07:00","id":1202093,"title":"","content":"New question, triggered from one of the recent posts. Please keep in mind that I haven't played Changeling 1e and don't have the backer pdf....<br /> <br /> So, the Mask is strong enough that unless dropped somehow even other Changelings cannot see through it?<br /> <br /> How do they spot each other, then? How do the Keepers/Huntsmen spot them?<br /> <br /> I'm starting to modify my tone expectations from &quot;on the lam and coping&quot; to &quot;fae cloak and daggers&quot;--a bit....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:15:51-07:00","id":1202101,"title":"","content":"Other Changelings, as well as Fae-touched, Hobgoblins and probably some sentient Tokens (though those might just be weird Hobgoblins) can see through The Mask. The general rule seems to be if it has a Mask itself, it can see through it too. I'm not sure if True Fae can see through it (I think in 2e they have more raw power than the Mask can contain), but it's not a big issue as being Ironside is taxing for them and not something they do when they have other choices. Huntsmen can see through the Mask, but making pledges with humans (standard house fairy stuff like protecting someone's herd in exchange for food left on the doorstep or protecting their dreams from nightmares and supernatural intrusions) gives you a sort of disguise as a natural supernatural element of Ironside instead of a Changeling.<br /> <br /> The Mask, however, does not conceal obvious shows of fae magic. So you may not see a clockwork man suddenly become surrounded by a whirlwind of scrap metal, but you'll still see a pale guy with slightly stiff movements suddenly conjure up a whirlwind of scrap metal out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> You can Strengthen the Mask for a scene for a point of Glamour to have it appear to other Changelings, but in exchange, your shadow will show the shape of your Mien to not only Changelings, but everyone who sees it.<br /> <br /> The Mask does not work in the Hedge or Arcadia, so anyone who winds up there sees the Mien of any Fairy or fae-made magical object (Tokens and Hedge-spun items).<br /> <br /> The way other monsters' powers affect the Mask is weird, as its considered an innate feature rather than an active power. I'll let someone else explain this part.<br /> <br /> Dropping the Mask, which can only be done Ironside, trades the obvious downsides of revealing your true nature for some sort of boost to Contracts. It is also a prerequisite for making the kind of pledges that mask you from the Huntsmen, as they must be made with full knowledge on the mortal's part of the nature and terms of the bargain from what I gather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:16:08-07:00","id":1202102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202093#post1202093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question, triggered from one of the recent posts. Please keep in mind that I haven't played Changeling 1e and don't have the backer pdf....<br /> <br /> So, the Mask is strong enough that unless dropped somehow even other Changelings cannot see through it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. Fae beings, which includes fellow changelings, see through a changeling's Mask by default. It's possible to strengthen your Mask to shield your mien from changeling eyes, but this takes effort and does not last forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:18:20-07:00","id":1202104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202102#post1202102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect. Fae beings, which includes fellow changelings, see through a changeling's Mask by default. It's possible to strengthen your Mask to shield your mien from changeling eyes, but this takes effort and does not last forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is the cost a Glamour or a Willpower? I can't remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T20:38:24-07:00","id":1202117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202101#post1202101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but in exchange, your shadow will show the shape of your Mien to not only Changelings, but everyone who sees it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shadow betrays the changeling's nature specifically to other fae, unlike the baseline Mask, which is permeable to other fae as well as other supernatural beings with mystical senses. Regular mortals don't get the tip-off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T04:22:09-07:00","id":1202193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202117#post1202117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shadow betrays the changeling's nature specifically to other fae, unlike the baseline Mask, which is permeable to other fae as well as other supernatural beings with mystical senses. Regular mortals don't get the tip-off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a new thing in 2e, or was I misinterpreting 1e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:39:57-07:00","id":1202208,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks. I was confused by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>'s comment earlier: <i>&quot;The Mask serves not only to keep other people from realizing a Changeling is anything but human, but also serves to keep other fae from tracking a Changeling down easily. Without their Mask, a Changeling leaves a trail that any fae can follow, which is why journeying through the Hedge (where their Mask is innately down) is a risky prospect for them.&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I conflated &quot;seeing the Changeling as what it is&quot; with &quot;tracking a Changeling down easily&quot;--in careful reflection they do not have to be the same thing, I suppose. Taidragon refers in the remainder of this quote to the &quot;trail any fae can follow&quot;, which gets at tracking and chase and the like, not staring one in the face....<br /> <br /> Ok, so in summary (because others with this question will read the thread):<br /> <br /> 1. The Mask covers the appearance of the Changeling and her abnormalities to non-Glamour-wielding creatures. <br /> 2. Supernatural creatures of all stripes may be able to pierce the Mask and perceive her as she really is using their supernatural abilities. (Clash of Wills I assume.)<br /> 3. When in the Hedge, the Mask slips. Everything in the Hedge is more True to itself, and that definitely includes a Changeling's appearance!<br /> 4. Changelings may drop their Mask for benefits. This could be done by scouring it (which is... unsubtle) or through certain Contracts.<br /> 5. The Mask carries even through supernatural transformations to other physical forms--especially those triggered by Contracts, but also (keeping in theme) other splat powers. <br /> <br /> Bonus question, then: since dream bastions are in the Hedge, does that mean that when the Changeling appears in a dream she manifests without her Mask? I presume that dream-shaping abilities would enable her to cover up, so to speak, but does she have no automatic concealment? Is it any different if she appears in the dreams of another supernatural creature?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:45:38-07:00","id":1202211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202193#post1202193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a new thing in 2e, or was I misinterpreting 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the first paragraph of &quot;Affecting the Mask&quot; on 1e Core p172 as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:50:45-07:00","id":1202212,"title":"","content":"New Question:<br /> <br /> Since a Changeling's soul is partially shredded by the Thorns and &quot;filled in&quot; with the stuff of Glamour during her transformation, what happens to the Changeling if she:<br /> <br /> 1. Has her soul removed (soul loss) through some supernatural power (i.e. from a Horror, say); and then<br /> 2. Has a replacement soul not her original found and inserted to stave off Willpower degradation?<br /> <br /> In other words, how important is the actual soul to the Changeling, after they've passed through their Durance and received a Mask and Mien?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T10:00:29-07:00","id":1202249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202208#post1202208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus question, then: since dream bastions are in the Hedge, does that mean that when the Changeling appears in a dream she manifests without her Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Dream Form lacks a Mask, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I presume that dream-shaping abilities would enable her to cover up, so to speak, but does she have no automatic concealment? Is it any different if she appears in the dreams of another supernatural creature?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf </div> </div> </div>There is no automatic concealment, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202212#post1202212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Question:<br /> <br /> Since a Changeling's soul is partially shredded by the Thorns and &quot;filled in&quot; with the stuff of Glamour during her transformation, what happens to the Changeling if she:<br /> <br /> 1. Has her soul removed (soul loss) through some supernatural power (i.e. from a Horror, say); and then<br /> 2. Has a replacement soul not her original found and inserted to stave off Willpower degradation?<br /> <br /> In other words, how important is the actual soul to the Changeling, after they've passed through their Durance and received a Mask and Mien?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>You're describing a situation that is pretty far from simple, given the assumptions it relies upon. As a comparable translation, though, probably the changeling would gradually lose the ability to recover Willpower through their Needle and treat recovering Willpower through their Thread as a breaking point with a hefty bonus to the Clarity attack roll until they'd marked every box with severe damage but one, at which point they'd start losing Willpower dots. <i>Maybe</i> they'd de-integrate any Icons they had along with the Willpower dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T11:15:06-07:00","id":1202266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202249#post1202249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Dream Form lacks a Mask, yes.<br /> <br /> There is no automatic concealment, no.<br /> <br /> You're describing a situation that is pretty far from simple, given the assumptions it relies upon. As a comparable translation, though, probably the changeling would gradually lose the ability to recover Willpower through their Needle and treat recovering Willpower through their Thread as a breaking point with a hefty bonus to the Clarity attack roll until they'd marked every box with severe damage but one, at which point they'd start losing Willpower dots. <i>Maybe</i> they'd de-integrate any Icons they had along with the Willpower dots?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lol ok. I was keying onto the common CofD mechanics for Soul Loss, which usually treat souls as interchangeable--but all right. My assumption is that those mechanics would apply while sans-soul, but after? I don't know. Depends on how important it is to the Changeling's condition and &quot;magic&quot; that their soul be cobbled together?<br /> <br /> Thanks on all points.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T11:23:50-07:00","id":1202269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202266#post1202266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lol ok. I was keying onto the common CofD mechanics for Soul Loss, which usually treat souls as interchangeable--but all right.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of historical material has generally treated the souls of supernatural creatures as more difficult if not outright impossible to affect with the same magic as used for mortal humans. Step 2 of the process you're talking about relies on the uncertain notion that Step 1 is even possible for changelings in the same way as it is for mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My assumption is that those mechanics would apply while sans-soul, but after? I don't know. Depends on how important it is to the Changeling's condition and &quot;magic&quot; that their soul be cobbled together? </div> </div> </div>The thing that the most dangerous parts of the Hedge shred off is not interchangeable on a one-to-one level with the occult facet of being that keeps human Integrity and Willpower stable. Finding a thing that undoes whatever replicates the effects of soul loss on a changeling without giving them back the exact thing they lost would probably undo the effects of soul loss, but &quot;changelings can suffer soul loss and fix it with other people's souls and this isn't a specifically-built plot device&quot; is firmly in the realm of figure-it-out-for-your-table at the time of this writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:56:01-07:00","id":1205293,"title":"","content":"I'd guess its the same as for a mage. Gnosis/Wyrd recovers slowly as the Supernal/Wyrd changes the Sleeper soul back into an Awakened/Changeling soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:49:53-07:00","id":1210260,"title":"","content":"Okay simple question that eludes me. If two changelings eat the same goblin fruit at the same time, who gets the glamour? Or do both get the glamour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:14:00-07:00","id":1210268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1210260#post1210260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay simple question that eludes me. If two changelings eat the same goblin fruit at the same time, who gets the glamour? Or do both get the glamour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flip a coin or assume a character needs to eat most if not all of the fruit in question to get its benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T00:36:34-07:00","id":1210855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1202249#post1202249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're describing a situation that is pretty far from simple, given the assumptions it relies upon. As a comparable translation, though, probably the changeling would gradually lose the ability to recover Willpower through their Needle and treat recovering Willpower through their Thread as a breaking point with a hefty bonus to the Clarity attack roll until they'd marked every box with severe damage but one, at which point they'd start losing Willpower dots. <i>Maybe</i> they'd de-integrate any Icons they had along with the Willpower dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap I am so lost now. What is this Needle and Thread, and why do we suddenly have a Clarity attack roll? And now there's damage to clarity instead of levels of clarity? Where and when was this introduced? I think I may need to wait for the book to come out before browsing this forum again. So many new mechanics. I did see a mention of a 'Thread' in the Hedgespinning thing that was posted a while back but it didn't exactly say what it was. I also don't know what this Icon is.<br /> <br /> Found something else to ask, too. Just on the last page was 'The Mask carries even through supernatural transformations to other physical forms--especially those triggered by Contracts, but also (keeping in theme) other splat powers.' Does that mean my Mirrorskin can't disguise their mask, can only disguise their mask, or do the disguises work on both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4558-silvermistshadow","user":"silvermistshadow","date":". 04-24-2018, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4558-silvermistshadow","name":"silvermistshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T03:50:57-07:00","id":1210887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silvermistshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1210855#post1210855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy crap I am so lost now. What is this Needle and Thread, and why do we suddenly have a Clarity attack roll? And now there's damage to clarity instead of levels of clarity? Where and when was this introduced? I think I may need to wait for the book to come out before browsing this forum again. So many new mechanics. I did see a mention of a 'Thread' in the Hedgespinning thing that was posted a while back but it didn't exactly say what it was. I also don't know what this Icon is.<br /> <br /> Found something else to ask, too. Just on the last page was 'The Mask carries even through supernatural transformations to other physical forms--especially those triggered by Contracts, but also (keeping in theme) other splat powers.' Does that mean my Mirrorskin can't disguise their mask, can only disguise their mask, or do the disguises work on both?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's described in the previews sent out to backers of the kickstarter. Due to reasons much (most? all?) of the work on the book was redone. Hence why the open previews you've probably seen aren't relevant anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T09:17:36-07:00","id":1210980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silvermistshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1210855#post1210855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy crap I am so lost now. What is this Needle and Thread, and why do we suddenly have a Clarity attack roll? And now there's damage to clarity instead of levels of clarity? Where and when was this introduced? I think I may need to wait for the book to come out before browsing this forum again. So many new mechanics. I did see a mention of a 'Thread' in the Hedgespinning thing that was posted a while back but it didn't exactly say what it was. I also don't know what this Icon is.</div> </div> </div> </div>David Hill, who developed and oversaw the various preview chapters and open development, chose to withdraw his development work for various reasons. Changeling 2e was then co-developed by Rose Bailey and Meghan Fitzgerald, and the manuscript of this different Changeling 2e was made available to backers of the Changeling 2e Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Clarity works differently now and resembles a Health track. Needle and Thread are the new edition's Anchors, rather than Virtue and Vice or Mask and Mien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T09:29:28-07:00","id":1210985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>silvermistshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1210855#post1210855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy crap I am so lost now. What is this Needle and Thread, and why do we suddenly have a Clarity attack roll? And now there's damage to clarity instead of levels of clarity? Where and when was this introduced? I think I may need to wait for the book to come out before browsing this forum again. So many new mechanics. I did see a mention of a 'Thread' in the Hedgespinning thing that was posted a while back but it didn't exactly say what it was. I also don't know what this Icon is.<br /> <br /> Found something else to ask, too. Just on the last page was 'The Mask carries even through supernatural transformations to other physical forms--especially those triggered by Contracts, but also (keeping in theme) other splat powers.' Does that mean my Mirrorskin can't disguise their mask, can only disguise their mask, or do the disguises work on both?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lots to go over but here's the skinny (in brief):<br /> <br /> 1. Needle &amp; Thread: They are the replacement to Virtue/Vice. They work (kinda) similarly to Vampire's equivalents. We can go into specifics but suffice to say they're just the words that define behaviours that can get the character willpower back.<br /> <br /> 2. Clarity has been reworked into a health track rather than a strict morality equivalent. I mean really that says it all, certain things can damage clarity in the same way that they used to cause &quot;Breaking Points&quot;. But now clarity can go down and up depending on actions and can be healed. Calling it a health track, I feel, says it all. Certain things can cause damage to it.<br /> <br /> 3. This is all in the preview (plus a few other places beforehand) from the Kickstarter. At some point, the development changed due to a dev changeup.<br /> <br /> 4. You don't have to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> honestly I think most of us are willing to give you the skinny on the changes in aggregate and answer what questions we can w/o further dev input.<br /> <br /> 5. An Icon is basically the piece of your Shadow (your soul) that got ripped off you when you traveled through the hedge on your way to Arcadia the first time (and/or on your way back). Essentially it's just a thing with a piece of your soul in it that you can reabsorb for Clarity and other benefits. It's the kind of thing to put on the goals for your character and other related story hooks.<br /> <br /> 6. Someone else may have to answer your Mirror skin question. But to my knowledge, you can still change your Mien...but the mask will still apply (it may change with the Mien but it still hides the supernatural features.)<br /> <br /> <b>EDITE:</b> Just ask questions if you see an unfamiliar term <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:57:08-07:00","id":1211169,"title":"","content":"(cross-posted from Beast simple Q&amp;A thread)<br /> <br /> ...possibly a dumb question but:<br /> <br /> So if through happenstance a Beast gets kidnapped by the Gentry and they attempt to turn them into a changeling...nothing happens, due to their soul being so irreversibly altered that they can't be fae'd, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:54:03-07:00","id":1211191,"title":"","content":"Ain't no official answer to that I know of. Whatever it is, it's probably not just &quot;stack the changeling template onto the Beast template,&quot; but &quot;something weird and unfamiliar happens&quot; is a pretty valid development, whether transformative or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:18:13-07:00","id":1211229,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4558-silvermistshadow\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4558\" data-vbnamecard=\"4558\">silvermistshadow</a> Mirrorskin in 2e explicitly changes both Mask and Mien, so those who attempt to see past the Mask only see another disguise. Powers that would pierce the deception evoke a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> Edit: here's a question I forgot to post earlier, and didn't want to double post. What is the benefit of a Fae Mount scouring their Mask (if they have Actormask that is)? The only one I can think of is if they use it to frighten someone with their otherworldly appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-24-2018, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T02:08:30-07:00","id":1211327,"title":"","content":"Alright, good to know. By the time I saw the Kickstarter, it was beyond too late. I'll just pre order it when I can. At least that way I'll get it when it does come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4558-silvermistshadow","name":"silvermistshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T05:18:25-07:00","id":1211372,"title":"","content":"So, like which kind of Fae is actually most likely to be the one who personally kidnapped a Changeling that didn't just wander into the Hedge as a human and get captured there? In both editions. Do True Fae now use Huntsmen to do this in 2e? Ive been seeing that used in a few places. Or is it just so varied that there's no clear answer?<br /> <br /> Also, how do you run those True Fae with Titles that manifest as groups (I think the official term is Ensemble Title)? Brief Nightmares? Less Simplified stat blocks? Do they lose Attributes if they're not all interacting at once? Or are their numbers more of an in-universe narrative abstraction like &quot;we are legion&quot; or &quot;A small forest council&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:57:00-07:00","id":1213211,"title":"","content":"So, Primal Glory vs. weapons. Does &quot;immune to damage from the element&quot; apply (e.g.- wood armor vs. wooden club, metal armor vs. knives and bullets) or just the 1/1 armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T18:10:49-07:00","id":1213248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1213211#post1213211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Primal Glory vs. weapons. Does &quot;immune to damage from the element&quot; apply (e.g.- wood armor vs. wooden club, metal armor vs. knives and bullets) or just the 1/1 armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>The equivalent didn't in 1e and I can't see much reason for the context of the new use-method to change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T18:50:11-07:00","id":1213258,"title":"","content":"Is there a benefit to a Fae Mount scouring their Mask when they have Actormask? As far as I know they don't have contracts, which is what scouring the Mask usually benefits in practically every way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:55:13-07:00","id":1213315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1213258#post1213258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a benefit to a Fae Mount scouring their Mask when they have Actormask? As far as I know they don't have contracts, which is what scouring the Mask usually benefits in practically every way.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The character</i> can scour away or reinforce their Mount's Mask as well as their own, which is mostly a matter of aesthetics but does maybe serve to help steer the outcome of mortal onlookers getting Spooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T10:29:26-07:00","id":1217043,"title":"","content":"So. Through Dream Antagonist (at least in previous versions of 2nd ed.) a Changeling can instill a supernatural merit into their victim, right?<br /> <br /> We know this could create wolf-blooded, because they have a Merit that determines whether they are one or not, very effectively. (Merit: Tell)<br /> <br /> What about other minor splats? I'm thinking especially Proximi, but Fae-touched? Dhampyr? <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T10:58:54-07:00","id":1217052,"title":"","content":"The rules might not say it, but I would rule that granting minor splats, maybe even certain merit templates too tied to other gamelines, should be out of the Fae wheelhouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T13:45:48-07:00","id":1217103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1217043#post1217043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Through Dream Antagonist (at least in previous versions of 2nd ed.) a Changeling can instill a supernatural merit into their victim, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Single dots for the length of a story and it requires you to do the narrative legwork in the dream and the subject to actually qualify for the Merit. This is very much not a &quot;make anyone into anything&quot; option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:12:21-07:00","id":1217359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1217103#post1217103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Single dots for the length of a story and it requires you to do the narrative legwork in the dream and the subject to actually qualify for the Merit. This is very much not a &quot;make anyone into anything&quot; option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh <i>good! </i>Thanks! Because the abuse-train looked a couple miles long on this one....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Also thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a>. The underlying jab is the idea of whether or not the Fae influence (even through Changelings) is so potent that it can rewrite [mortals?] into unrelated supernatural denizens via dreams. That seemed a stretch, but yaknow, not all splats have equal influence in the World....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T11:25:19-07:00","id":1217728,"title":"","content":"Regarding the entry of a Bastion, the manuscript says this &quot;A Bastion always allows an oneiropomp inside if she has an active invitation, which takes the<br /> form of a pledge (p. XX).&quot;<br /> <br /> However, there doesn't seem to be any mention of that mechanic in the Pledges section. Did I miss something, or has it been clarified since then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T17:30:17-07:00","id":1217833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1217728#post1217728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the entry of a Bastion, the manuscript says this &quot;A Bastion always allows an oneiropomp inside if she has an active invitation, which takes the<br /> form of a pledge (p. XX).&quot;<br /> <br /> However, there doesn't seem to be any mention of that mechanic in the Pledges section. Did I miss something, or has it been clarified since then?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're allowed in if you have a pledge whose terms allow you in. That's the entirety of the mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T11:21:44-07:00","id":1218023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1217833#post1217833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're allowed in if you have a pledge whose terms allow you in. That's the entirety of the mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. So with a human that'd have to be either as part of a bargain or sealing some kind of statement along the lines of 'I promise you'll be welcome in my dreams' ? Maybe I'm overthinking this but it seems so far removed from the other 2e pledge mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:17:45-07:00","id":1218643,"title":"","content":"Hoi!<br /> <br /> I have three questions, more academic and less about mechanics, so both 1e/2e answers are fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (if they are not simple enough I happily move them to a thread)<br /> <br /> <b>1. Clarity and Breaking Points</b><br /> In 1e the rules say that a Lost, reaching a BP by acting in a way that threatens her Clarity endangering the delicate balance between her Mortal and Fae sides.<br /> That's nice and breezy, but the Breaking Points are really messed up in the text, without proper balance mixing up holier-than-thou moralizing with understandable border lines.<br /> <br /> If you strictly adhere to the rules 7-to-2 downfall is probably a month after escaping.<br /> <br /> 10-9-8 is fine and dandy; 7 is the base, what you can easily loose w/o ID and money (even fare dodging is a form of petty theft after all) and don't forget that the escaping alone is a &quot;serious unexpected life change&quot;, seeing a mirror at the first time counts as well; after a PTSD I bet that you can easily go without human contact while try to realize WTF is happening with you, so that's a 6; 5 is fine, obviously; 4 is common if you have a Fetch, more common if you get rid of it; 3 is baffling because Dreamwalking and plundering is supposed to be the THING to the escapee from Nightmareland; 2 is another interesting one, &quot;serial murder&quot; is pretty straightforward but I still don't know after all these years what &quot;Casual / callous crime&quot; means. If my Mortal/Fae balance is on the stake, why should I bother with casual crimes against &quot;subhumans/abmortals/things&quot;? and finally the 1 one: &quot;perversion&quot; oh, please someone define it - one mans's perversion is the other man's mere pleasure (or in this case the &quot;doing it with one feather is kinky / with a whole chicken is perversion&quot; rule plays?)<br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> In a dangerous environment almost everyone should be counted as Clarity 4 at most or precise conditioning/brainwashing/training shifts the moral standing points of the BPs?<br /> (e.g. trained soldiers, street raised thugs, professional crime syndicate members, conmen, cultist, etc.) / Will it be addressed or changed in 2e?<br /> <br /> <b>2. Durance</b><br /> 1e states that <i>&quot;Changelings who were taken as infants or very young children, and those who were abducted more than 50 years ago, don\u2019t have a strong enough memory of their homes to find their way through the Thorns.&quot;</i> what is a bit shortsighted, I think. A hundred years is more plausible, probably. Since it's 2018 it means that not a single boheme from the roaring 20's, a strong-willed partisan from the WW2 not even a revolutionary student or hippie from the 60's could escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> What do you think? / Will it be addressed or changed in 2e?<br /> <br /> <b>3. Parenting</b><br /> Someone wrote in the other thread that Rose doesn't want to exclude parenting from the 2e (please direct me to the proper thread with the whole explanation, thank you).<br /> In one hand it is a nice touch, on the other hand\u2026 Look, this is a horror game after all and I like to hurt my Players a bit once in a while, but I don't want to beat them to pulp.<br /> Pregnancy is already a heavy burden to a Mortal woman (bless them all!) but a devastating experience to a Changeling in my opinion: my body is changing; something growing inside me; my feelings, cravings and needs are not mine; constant adult fears, paranoia and overprotecting - no matters if the offspring is a Mortal or a Changeling: what does she see and experience; what does she tells to anyone; why doesn't she hold or go to a sleepover; why doesn't she checked in; why doesn't she came home in the proper time, and the list goes on.<br /> It's a much more heavier responsibility to bring a child to life, THIS life what is full of dangers than to a Mortal. They just suspecting that danger lurks in every shadows, but you know it exactly.<br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> What do you think? Is it really a good idea? / How exactly will it be addressed or changed in 2e?<br /> <br /> Thank you and sorry for the tl;dr <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u041f\u0438\u0444-\u043f\u0430\u0444 \u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439 / \u0423\u043c\u0438\u0440\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0437\u0430\u0439\u0447\u0438\u043a \u043c\u043e\u0439 </span></span>","edited":{"userid":24224,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","user":"Insane\u2022kismanO","date":". 05-14-2018, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","name":"Insane\u2022kismanO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T12:41:20-07:00","id":1218650,"title":"","content":"Don't know about the rest, but it's NWoD tradition as I understand it to use utter perversion as a euphemism and collective shorthand for rape, pedophilia, bestiality, maybe cannibalism if its not listed somewhere else, feeding someone their own fingers one by one and even grosser stuff that I can easily imagine but would hesitate to list outside of PM. Basically, it's, it's most sex-related felonies and any non-sexual act that no one but the most jaded, twisted sicko would hesitate to call evil, or at least gross and excessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 06-27-2019, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T17:49:02-07:00","id":1218746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Insane\u2022kismanO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1218643#post1218643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">holier-than-thou moralizing</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally never going to be a useful thing to claim about 1e's Morality stats and the sooner you can disabuse yourself of the idea that it's worth holding onto the less trouble you're going to encounter with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you strictly adhere to the rules 7-to-2 downfall is probably a month after escaping. </div> </div> </div>This suggests quite strongly that your definition of &quot;strictly adhere to the rules&quot; is out of line with the intent of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7 is the base, what you can easily loose w/o ID and money (even fare dodging is a form of petty theft after all) and don't forget that the escaping alone is a &quot;serious unexpected life change&quot;, seeing a mirror at the first time counts as well; after a PTSD I bet that you can easily go without human contact while try to realize WTF is happening with you, so that's a 6; </div> </div> </div>Case in point: <i>Every changeling already knows they are no longer human by the time of character creation. Many of them escaped to try and reunite with loved ones. Breaking points are not automatically failed upon rolling.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 is baffling because Dreamwalking and plundering is supposed to be the THING to the escapee from Nightmareland; </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how &quot;doing the exact sort of thing the Fae do on the regular is highly damaging to a changeling's ability to remind themselves that they aren't still along for the ride with a fairytale godmonster that owns their soul&quot; is supposed to be confusing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 is another interesting one, &quot;serial murder&quot; is pretty straightforward but I still don't know after all these years what &quot;Casual / callous crime&quot; means. </div> </div> </div>Doing crimes to people with no regard for their personhood? &quot;People don't usually thieve and maim with inhuman indifference in most Earthly societies&quot; is another one of those lines keeping your experience in Arcadia firmly in the realm of fuzzy memory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and finally the 1 one: &quot;perversion&quot; oh, please someone define it - one mans's perversion is the other man's mere pleasure (or in this case the &quot;doing it with one feather is kinky / with a whole chicken is perversion&quot; rule plays?) </div> </div> </div>It's part of a larger sentence, dude \u2014 <i>Heinous acts of torture, depravity, and perversion</i> paints a much more drastic picture of the implied activities than a night at the fetish club, particularly when &quot;perversion&quot; as a word is not purely a sex thing; there's an angle on <i>corruption</i> present in the set of definitions of that word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Question:</b> In a dangerous environment almost everyone should be counted as Clarity 4 at most or precise conditioning/brainwashing/training shifts the moral standing points of the BPs? </div> </div> </div>This is generally why most changelings are not going to be too keen on staying in dangerous environments unless they're well and truly stuck in the mindset of &quot;I'm still in Arcadia, so I might as well act like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2. Durance</b><br /> 1e states that <i>&quot;Changelings who were taken as infants or very young children, and those who were abducted more than 50 years ago, don\u2019t have a strong enough memory of their homes to find their way through the Thorns.&quot;</i> what is a bit shortsighted, I think. A hundred years is more plausible, probably. Since it's 2018 it means that not a single boheme from the roaring 20's, a strong-willed partisan from the WW2 not even a revolutionary student or hippie from the 60's could escape. </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of escape. It's a matter of still having a recognizable personal point of reference on Earth to get back to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T09:47:17-07:00","id":1218949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1218650#post1218650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know about the rest, but it's NWoD tradition as I understand it to use utter perversion as a euphemism and collective shorthand for rape, pedophilia, bestiality, maybe cannibalism if its not listed somewhere else, feeding someone their own fingers one by one and even grosser stuff that I can easily imagine but would hesitate to list outside of PM. Basically, it's, it's most sex-related felonies and any non-sexual act that no one but the most jaded, twisted sicko would call evil, or at least gross and excessive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! It seems like a case of sentence comprehension mistake in my side.<br /> <br /> I've read <i>&quot;</i><i>Heinous acts of torture, depravity or perversion.&quot;</i><br /> as <i>&quot;Heinous acts: torture / depravity / perversion&quot;</i><br /> not as <i>&quot;Classified acts of graphic torture, absolute depravity and utterly heinous perversion&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u041f\u0438\u0444-\u043f\u0430\u0444 \u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439 / \u0423\u043c\u0438\u0440\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0437\u0430\u0439\u0447\u0438\u043a \u043c\u043e\u0439 </span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","name":"Insane\u2022kismanO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T10:24:14-07:00","id":1218955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Insane\u2022kismanO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1218643#post1218643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hoi!<br /> <br /> I have three questions, more academic and less about mechanics, so both 1e/2e answers are fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (if they are not simple enough I happily move them to a thread)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3. Parenting</b><br /> Someone wrote in the other thread that Rose doesn't want to exclude parenting from the 2e (please direct me to the proper thread with the whole explanation, thank you).<br /> In one hand it is a nice touch, on the other hand\u2026 Look, this is a horror game after all and I like to hurt my Players a bit once in a while, but I don't want to beat them to pulp.<br /> Pregnancy is already a heavy burden to a Mortal woman (bless them all!) but a devastating experience to a Changeling in my opinion: my body is changing; something growing inside me; my feelings, cravings and needs are not mine; constant adult fears, paranoia and overprotecting - no matters if the offspring is a Mortal or a Changeling: what does she see and experience; what does she tells to anyone; why doesn't she hold or go to a sleepover; why doesn't she checked in; why doesn't she came home in the proper time, and the list goes on.<br /> It's a much more heavier responsibility to bring a child to life, THIS life what is full of dangers than to a Mortal. They just suspecting that danger lurks in every shadows, but you know it exactly.<br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> What do you think? Is it really a good idea? / How exactly will it be addressed or changed in 2e?<br /> <br /> Thank you and sorry for the tl;dr <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that making it possible for changelings to have children is a great idea. Whether individual characters think it\u2019s a good thing doesn\u2019t matter, at least from a game perspective. First edition pretty much said that it couldn\u2019t happen, which eliminated a lot of potential stories. It was one of the things that we house ruled away for our games, and I\u2019m glad to see that it isn\u2019t returning for second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T10:49:30-07:00","id":1218964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1218746#post1218746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally never going to be a useful thing to claim about 1e's Morality stats and the sooner you can disabuse yourself of the idea that it's worth holding onto the less trouble you're going to encounter with them.<br /> <br /> This suggests quite strongly that your definition of &quot;strictly adhere to the rules&quot; is out of line with the intent of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I disagree with you in some points, but the different PoV gave some food to my brain to chew on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Case in point: <i>Every changeling already knows they are no longer human by the time of character creation. Many of them escaped to try and reunite with loved ones. Breaking points are not automatically failed upon rolling.</i> </div> </div> </div>Knowing something is different from &quot;seriously shocked by something&quot;.<br /> In my teenage years I've had an accident and woke up in the hospital.<br /> I <u>knew</u> that something is wrong, I <u>felt</u> that it hurt and many things changed, but <u>facing with it</u> the first time and seeing my broken face, scars and bruises all together was a <i>Breaking Point</i> for me IRL.<br /> <br /> I meant that a Changeling is foredoomed to loose most of her Clarity in a relatively short period, facing with all of the changes (pun not intended) at the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure how &quot;doing the exact sort of thing the Fae do on the regular is highly damaging to a changeling's ability to remind themselves that they aren't still along for the ride with a fairytale godmonster that owns their soul&quot; is supposed to be confusing. </div> </div> </div>I thought that <i>&quot;Actively harming a mortal by ravaging their dreams.&quot;</i> is a Changeling thing, but nowadays it's more a Beast territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doing crimes to people with no regard for their personhood? &quot;People don't usually thieve and maim with inhuman indifference in most Earthly societies&quot; is another one of those lines keeping your experience in Arcadia firmly in the realm of fuzzy memory. </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood me: crimes against Mortals are higher BPs and it's absolutely logical to me (while a Lost tries to balance her humanity with the miraculous side) but the <i>&quot;Casual/callous crime against other supernaturals (serial murder).&quot;</i> makes me confused. Not the serial murder part, obviously.<br /> Why is it more serious to raid an Egyptian tomb than a burglary / to join a Hunter group and decimate the local Kindred than manslaughter / to rob the Magi in a Ponzi-scheme than raid the local elderly home?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's part of a larger sentence, dude \u2014 <i>Heinous acts of torture, depravity, and perversion</i> paints a much more drastic picture of the implied activities than a night at the fetish club, particularly when &quot;perversion&quot; as a word is not purely a sex thing; there's an angle on <i>corruption</i> present in the set of definitions of that word. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my bad, got it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is generally why most changelings are not going to be too keen on staying in dangerous environments unless they're well and truly stuck in the mindset of &quot;I'm still in Arcadia, so I might as well act like it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So, you suggest that previously trained / conditioned criminals, members of the law enforcement and military, even member of some religious orders with strict rules should avoid their former life to hold on their Clarity because they were strong and agile enough to escape the magical nightmares but soft and fragile enough to live by the slightly different mindset they were taught to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not a matter of escape. It's a matter of still having a recognizable personal point of reference on Earth to get back to. </div> </div> </div>This point I strongly disagree.<br /> I believe that for example my Mum has more emotional anchors to the people and places in the 60's than to the 90's.<br /> If the quoted sentence would have been written about the time period of the Durance then I would agree. Fifty years in Faerie makes every memories more than a little bit fuzzy. But it was about IRL time and I still think that 50 years are too rigorous.<br /> I think that a veteran of Normandy, abducted in the fifties could have more recognizable point of references than me, abducted ten years before.<br /> <br /> Anyways, using most of the text as guidelines rather than irreconcilable rules is a good advice - so I will reshape my Clarity ladder to better fit to the setting and social environment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u041f\u0438\u0444-\u043f\u0430\u0444 \u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439 / \u0423\u043c\u0438\u0440\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0437\u0430\u0439\u0447\u0438\u043a \u043c\u043e\u0439 </span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","name":"Insane\u2022kismanO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:50:29-07:00","id":1219128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Insane\u2022kismanO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1218964#post1218964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing something is different from &quot;seriously shocked by something&quot;.<br /> In my teenage years I've had an accident and woke up in the hospital.<br /> I <u>knew</u> that something is wrong, I <u>felt</u> that it hurt and many things changed, but <u>facing with it</u> the first time and seeing my broken face, scars and bruises all together was a <i>Breaking Point</i> for me IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings at character creation have had time to get to grips with their altered state even if they weren't already aware that they'd been through an ordeal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant that a Changeling is foredoomed to loose most of her Clarity in a relatively short period, facing with all of the changes (pun not intended) at the beginning. </div> </div> </div>You meant that if you treat a character from character creation as though they were fresh out of the woods and had no idea how being a changeling worked then they would get plinked down the scale immediately, despite basic common sense indicating that that's not how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought that <i>&quot;Actively harming a mortal by ravaging their dreams.&quot;</i> is a Changeling thing, but nowadays it's more a Beast territory. </div> </div> </div>It has literally never been presented as a particularly common activity for changelings to do in Lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is it more serious to raid an Egyptian tomb than a burglary / to join a Hunter group and decimate the local Kindred than manslaughter / to rob the Magi in a Ponzi-scheme than raid the local elderly home? </div> </div> </div>&quot;We're breaking down the magical door of a vampire's mausoleum stronghold. Is this Faerie? I can't really tell because we seem to be fucking around with a lot more monsters than is usual for Earth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, you suggest that previously trained / conditioned criminals, members of the law enforcement and military, even member of some religious orders with strict rules should avoid their former life to hold on their Clarity because they were strong and agile enough to escape the magical nightmares but soft and fragile enough to live by the slightly different mindset they were taught to. </div> </div> </div>I suggest that being stuck with PTSD's horrible magically-backed second-cousin due to an extended stay in a plastic reality at the whim of capricious angel-fiends means these characters are going to be a lot better off not being in places where their agency is in question and their fundamental routines are disturbed on the regular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This point I strongly disagree. </div> </div> </div>The main street intersection of my hometown has changed so drastically in the last ten years that I would not be able to tell you what it looked like when I was in kindergarten. If I were taken as a child and had only a strong memory of the bakery that used to be there to go off of to find my way back I would not be able to find my way back, because my reference point no longer exists. You cannot seriously claim that this interpretation did not occur to you, because it is explicitly stated in the very next sentence after the one you quoted:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the former case [infants and very young children], they can\u2019t recall enough details; in the latter [abducted more than fifty years ago], <b>the details of their homes have almost indubitably changed beyond recognition.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T18:14:15-07:00","id":1219134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1219128#post1219128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You meant that if you treat a character from character creation as though they were fresh out of the woods and had no idea how being a changeling worked then they would get plinked down the scale immediately, despite basic common sense indicating that that's not how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to emphasize this, especially because I've seen it come up, occasionally, in other gamelines, too.<br /> Starting splat characters are not day one changelings/vampires/werewolves etc any more than a starting mortal is necessarily an infant.<br /> <br /> We don't know how the splats look in those formative days/weeks/months/years.<br /> For all we know, Changelings don't even form Clarity until <i>after</i> that initial acclimation period has passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T12:09:35-07:00","id":1219338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1219128#post1219128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings at character creation have had time to get to grips with their altered state even if they weren't already aware that they'd been through an ordeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>o.O Please add a reference, where was it stated like you suggest. In that spirit, there are no &quot;last day of durance&quot; and escape stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You meant that if you treat a character from character creation as though they were fresh out of the woods and had no idea how being a changeling worked then they would get plinked down the scale immediately, despite basic common sense indicating that that's not how it works. </div> </div> </div>Reference again, please. Citing &quot;common sense&quot; is a bit condescending while you present an opinion.<br /> Playing &quot;fresh out of the woods&quot; characters is supposed to be the basic thing but you are strongly suggesting that the mere idea is preposterous.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the other thing - it is my bad that I haven't stated explicitly that &quot;the continuous shocks of the brand new experiences if played truthfully to the rules resulting so many Braking Points that the victim statistically predestined to lose a handful of Clarity points in the first half year&quot; and you continuously implying that I meant that it is absolutely automatic.<br /> I don't know if it's really my bad or am I bothering you or what...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has literally never been presented as a particularly common activity for changelings to do in Lost. </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i> p. 14-49 somehow suggesting otherwise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;We're breaking down the magical door of a vampire's mausoleum stronghold. Is this Faerie? I can't really tell because we seem to be fucking around with a lot more monsters than is usual for Earth.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Instead of coping with the facts that the world is full of nightmares, the Lost continuously in doubt about their own sanity. I pretty much like this approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suggest that being stuck with PTSD's horrible magically-backed second-cousin due to an extended stay in a plastic reality at the whim of capricious angel-fiends means these characters are going to be a lot better off not being in places where their agency is in question and their fundamental routines are disturbed on the regular. </div> </div> </div>That's not an answer to my question. There are people who were conditioned to act outside the simpleton way of life. Trained to be violent, dishonest, hurt or even kill other people when it is necessary. The &quot;returning to the NORMAL life&quot; to them, applying the well-know routines and acts to regain the stability of the previously known life with all of its rules - it requires a Clarity scale what is different from what was presented in the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main street intersection of my hometown has changed so drastically in the last ten years that I would not be able to tell you what it looked like when I was in kindergarten. If I were taken as a child and had only a strong memory of the bakery that used to be there to go off of to find my way back I would not be able to find my way back, because my reference point no longer exists. You cannot seriously claim that this interpretation did not occur to you, because it is explicitly stated in the very next sentence after the one you quoted: </div> </div> </div>Deliberate misinterpretation again. I was bothered by the 50 years rule, you are talking about the other side of the spectrum.<br /> <br /> I don't know about the rest of the world but in Europe things tend to be a little bit more lasting. Not everything, of course, but enough things remains the same to provide an emotional anchor.<br /> Just for the record, I've asked my Mum about the most important of emotional anchors from the 60's and checked them online / personally today:<ul><li>her grandparent's home and the department store next to it \u2013 the home is renovated / the store is refurbished but the place of the old neon lights are still visible on the frontage</li> <li>the doorway of the same house, where she was first kissed \u2013 safe and sound (doesn't looks to be changed too much since then, shame to the owners)</li> <li>the square and a statue where she met with her friends for chat and booze \u2013 still intact</li> <li>the field and viewpoint where they played \u2013 still there</li> <li>the outdoor concert place they visited frequently \u2013 renovated and reopened after some thirty years of neglect</li> <li>her elementary school and the lime trees in the garden \u2013 never better</li> </ul>So, I really think that she might escape clinging to these reference points.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it seems like <i>Rites of Spring</i> changed the rules, so our debate is a little bit pointless: <i>&quot;It is all but unheard of for changelings who have spent more than 100 years in Arcadia to return. Most Anachronistic Lost will have come from no later than the early 1900s, but even a century provides plenty of challenges for a returning fae.&quot;</i><br /> 100 years are just fine, as I've stated at the beginning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u041f\u0438\u0444-\u043f\u0430\u0444 \u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439 / \u0423\u043c\u0438\u0440\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0437\u0430\u0439\u0447\u0438\u043a \u043c\u043e\u0439 </span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","name":"Insane\u2022kismanO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:05:00-07:00","id":1219368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Insane\u2022kismanO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1219338#post1219338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">o.O Please add a reference, where was it stated like you suggest. In that spirit, there are no &quot;last day of durance&quot; and escape stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storytelling the Prelude and the fact that you can start the game as part of a Court with no special consideration.<br /> <br /> The game is built on the assumption that your character doesn't need the basics of their condition explained to them just like your Medicine 3 doctor doesn't need to be walked through how to use a first-aid kid.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a game <i>about</i> those first-day-back experiences, that is a decision you have made as a Storyteller; as presented, the books are written for starting characters to be at least minimally established in their placement within the setting and able to do the things that their positions imply without difficulty outside of dramatic circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A special note should be made regarding two specific instances: Combat <b>and Clarity loss.</b> In both cases, consider very carefully whether you want to allow the dice to determine the outcomes. No one wants to invest time and thought in creating a character only to have him die before the game starts, and <b>a player may not want to begin the game at a Clarity deficit.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reference again, please. Citing &quot;common sense&quot; is a bit condescending while you present an opinion.<br /> Playing &quot;fresh out of the woods&quot; characters is supposed to be the basic thing but you are strongly suggesting that the mere idea is preposterous. </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the mere idea is preposterous, I'm saying that the game is not written for that to be &quot;the basic thing,&quot; else the game would not have Court mechanics baked into the character generation quick-reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and the other thing - it is my bad that I haven't stated explicitly that &quot;the continuous shocks of the brand new experiences if played truthfully to the rules resulting so many Braking Points that the victim statistically predestined to lose a handful of Clarity points in the first half year&quot; and you continuously implying that I meant that it is absolutely automatic. </div> </div> </div>Breaking points in 1e get no better pool than six dice at the absolute best and the higher pools fall out of consideration entirely as your Clarity drops.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if it's really my bad or am I bothering you or what... </div> </div> </div>It is extremely difficult to believe you are approaching the rules in good faith when you've read Rites of Spring, the book that <i>goes into greater detail on the rationale behind each and every one of the corebook's Clarity breaking points</i>, and think that a changeling character is statistically likely to undergo &quot;continuous shocks of brand new experiences&quot; after returning to Earth within their first six months back and that prompting degeneration rolls for these things is &quot;playing truthfully to the rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i> p. 14-49 somehow suggesting otherwise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Dancers in the Dusk is the book I most recently finished rereading. It does not present &quot;Actively harming a mortal by ravaging their dreams&quot; \u2014 a process which most closely fits the oneiromancy section's use of dreamscaping to craft nightmares and/or inflicting derangements through extreme damage in oneiromachy \u2014 as a common behavior for changelings, whose interaction with dreams is highly dependent upon the promises they use to get there in the first palce. You appear to think that the breaking point in question refers to <i>any dreamwalking whatsoever</i>, judging from your reaction, and you would be incorrect to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not an answer to my question. There are people who were conditioned to act outside the simpleton way of life. Trained to be violent, dishonest, hurt or even kill other people when it is necessary. The &quot;returning to the NORMAL life&quot; to them, applying the well-know routines and acts to regain the stability of the previously known life with all of its rules - it requires a Clarity scale what is different from what was presented in the core book. </div> </div> </div>It does not, in fact, <i>require</i> a completely different Clarity scale just because living in the manner to which they were once accustomed is now associated with their time in Faerie. A character is allowed to stabilize at a lower rating, but the way Clarity works privileges characters who can keep their word and hold onto a stable lifestyle by design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deliberate misinterpretation again. I was bothered by the 50 years rule, you are talking about the other side of the spectrum. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The 50 years rule&quot; is &quot;Characters who were taken more than fifty years ago in Earth years likely have few strong personal anchors that would not have changed their tenor significantly in that time, such that their memories are unlikely to match up with the current reality.&quot; That's a statement of <i>general likelihood </i>based on <i>factors external to the character</i>. What even is &quot;the other side of the spectrum&quot; in that scenario?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I really think that she might escape clinging to these reference points. </div> </div> </div>Your rationale here is that because <i>isolated pictures of the places</i> \u2014 and in some cases <i>pictures of isolated parts of those places</i> \u2014 are the same, the emotional connection your mother holds to those locations \u2014 as a person who has not been <i>mutated out of her human body and frame of reference</i> by fifty years in a place that can reasonably be liked to the experience of a <i>psychotropic drug trip</i> \u2014 is comparable to the core shreds of memory a changeling would hold onto about a place that is important to them at the level of <i>I broke out of God's dollhouse for this</i> and leads back to a place that is, in the grand scheme of things, fundamentally and thematically <i>almost the same place</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't know how else to tell you that renovations are a meaningful and substantial degree of change in a setting where the supernatural is pervasive and anachronistic by inclination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:14:49-07:00","id":1219371,"title":"","content":"Although I still disagree with you in some points, all of your replies gave me interesting points of view and an impulsion to thoroughly read again each and every books (and make notes\u2026 sooo many notes). So, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u041f\u0438\u0444-\u043f\u0430\u0444 \u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439 / \u0423\u043c\u0438\u0440\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0437\u0430\u0439\u0447\u0438\u043a \u043c\u043e\u0439 </span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","name":"Insane\u2022kismanO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T10:30:53-07:00","id":1219697,"title":"","content":"Related to some points raised in the recent exchanges:<br /> <br /> Is there a representation in the published books of the experience for Changelings who have freshly escaped? Perhaps some of the story beats they should pass through to arrive at &quot;starting character&quot; situation? <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T14:28:29-07:00","id":1221544,"title":"","content":"Does the benefit of the Stable Trod Merit also raise the Hollow's effective rating for the purposes of effects that reference it, like Hob Alarm, Luxury Goods, Home Turf, or the Merit's universal security features?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T21:08:29-07:00","id":1221612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221544#post1221544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the benefit of the Stable Trod Merit also raise the Hollow's effective rating for the purposes of effects that reference it, like Hob Alarm, Luxury Goods, Home Turf, or the Merit's universal security features?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no; it specifically states that the trod grants an extra one-dot enhancement, not an additional dot of Hollow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T05:38:19-07:00","id":1221665,"title":"","content":"Is there a mechanical consequence if a changeling avoids anything fae and supernatural and tries to live a normal life without using contracts, pledges and having glamour 0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:04:12-07:00","id":1221712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pluvinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221665#post1221665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a mechanical consequence if a changeling avoids anything fae and supernatural and tries to live a normal life without using contracts, pledges and having glamour 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having no Glamour in your system means you will starve in relatively short order, as well as being nearly incapable of avoiding the notice of any fae that come your way. It's theoretically possible for you to coast by at Wyrd 1 with a single point of Glamour in this manner without running into any other fae, but the nature of the game makes that incredibly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Also, depending on how you read some of the breaking points, it's possible that simply venting all the Glamour you have on hand in short bursts and not being able to talk about your experiences or have contact with other changelings is going to gradually wear on your Clarity as readily as lies and rejection do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:11:24-07:00","id":1221789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221712#post1221712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no Glamour in your system means you will starve in relatively short order, as well as being nearly incapable of avoiding the notice of any fae that come your way. It's theoretically possible for you to coast by at Wyrd 1 with a single point of Glamour in this manner without running into any other fae, but the nature of the game makes that incredibly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Also, depending on how you read some of the breaking points, it's possible that simply venting all the Glamour you have on hand in short bursts and not being able to talk about your experiences or have contact with other changelings is going to gradually wear on your Clarity as readily as lies and rejection do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I now remember Rites of Spring having some optional rules for how the True Fae could notice you or not if you were filled or emptied of glamour.<br /> <br /> Another one: Is it possible to enter a True Fae's dream (maybe with skeinwalking or with some crazy Dream Pledge) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:38:38-07:00","id":1221798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221712#post1221712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no Glamour in your system means you will starve in relatively short order, as well as being nearly incapable of avoiding the notice of any fae that come your way. It's theoretically possible for you to coast by at Wyrd 1 with a single point of Glamour in this manner without running into any other fae, but the nature of the game makes that incredibly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Also, depending on how you read some of the breaking points, it's possible that simply venting all the Glamour you have on hand in short bursts and not being able to talk about your experiences or have contact with other changelings is going to gradually wear on your Clarity as readily as lies and rejection do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's all partly dependent on the activity cycles of the Huntsmen, how often they're in your area, and how often you're rubbing shoulders with Hedge-denizens and other Changelings. If you do so frequently then your efforts to be magically-minimal will suffer.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24237\" data-vbnamecard=\"24237\">Pluvinarch</a> to answer your question with an idea, it was proposed in ... an early 2e draft? I think? That a Changeling could maybe starve down her Wyrd to 1 and run on minimal Glamour in order to set up the possibility of destroying their fetch (and consuming it?) to become human again. I doubt that sort of edge-case text will make the final cut, however.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T16:54:55-07:00","id":1221881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221798#post1221798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that's all partly dependent on the activity cycles of the Huntsmen, how often they're in your area, and how often you're rubbing shoulders with Hedge-denizens and other Changelings. If you do so frequently then your efforts to be magically-minimal will suffer.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24237\" data-vbnamecard=\"24237\">Pluvinarch</a> to answer your question with an idea, it was proposed in ... an early 2e draft? I think? That a Changeling could maybe starve down her Wyrd to 1 and run on minimal Glamour in order to set up the possibility of destroying their fetch (and consuming it?) to become human again. I doubt that sort of edge-case text will make the final cut, however.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one reason it was cut was for a simple reason; the Wyrd in 2e is a cosmic balancing act. By being taken you gained phenomenal powers and magics as compensation. Abstaining from using that power at Wyrd 1, and then killing your Fetch once it had taken your magic...doesn't make sense in that context. Your very soul has been made Fae, and your mind has been stripped of human faculties to the point that your vices and virtues aren't how you regain will. It is acting true to yourself and to your image that you gain willpower back. How can you truly be &quot;human&quot; without any of fixing that? How <i>can</i> you fix any of that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T05:31:27-07:00","id":1221993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221881#post1221881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one reason it was cut was for a simple reason; the Wyrd in 2e is a cosmic balancing act. By being taken you gained phenomenal powers and magics as compensation. Abstaining from using that power at Wyrd 1, and then killing your Fetch once it had taken your magic...doesn't make sense in that context. Your very soul has been made Fae, and your mind has been stripped of human faculties to the point that your vices and virtues aren't how you regain will. It is acting true to yourself and to your image that you gain willpower back. How can you truly be &quot;human&quot; without any of fixing that? How <i>can</i> you fix any of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a dramatic perspective, I can see some changelings who just escaped their ordeal and trying to deny all that happened to them. They will fail, but it makes good stories.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T07:36:46-07:00","id":1222027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1221881#post1221881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one reason it was cut was for a simple reason; the Wyrd in 2e is a cosmic balancing act. By being taken you gained phenomenal powers and magics as compensation. Abstaining from using that power at Wyrd 1, and then killing your Fetch once it had taken your magic...doesn't make sense in that context. Your very soul has been made Fae, and your mind has been stripped of human faculties to the point that your vices and virtues aren't how you regain will. It is acting true to yourself and to your image that you gain willpower back. How can you truly be &quot;human&quot; without any of fixing that? How <i>can</i> you fix any of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you fix any of that? Dunno. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24237\" data-vbnamecard=\"24237\">Pluvinarch</a> alludes the effort makes a good story. After all, &quot;I wanna be a real boy!&quot; is a firm story trope. <br /> <br /> Part of me wants to believe that the struggle for Changelings to hope and adapt, <i>by itself </i>is valuable to the Keepers, in that it continues to generate &quot;story&quot; in ways that channel glamour back to Arcadia. If this surmise is even partially correct, it could explain why some Changelings and Holds are left more or less alone by the Huntsmen, or... just enough so to keep the inhabitants of the fishbowl properly terrified.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd also like to believe that it <i>is</i> possible to become human again--even if difficult--but that doing so never really sheds ties completely. There will always be something tugging at the back of the mind. Something... watching.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T21:23:21-07:00","id":1222163,"title":"","content":"Becoming human again, huh. I hear the 2E preview has the Comatose Condition, where the wounds on your psyche are so great you retreat into an unending, blissful dream... (evil giggle)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T22:11:00-07:00","id":1222168,"title":"","content":"A Gentry can have titles and for each title he can manifest as an actor, a prop, a realm or wisps. So I guess, for a Storyteller planning a long term campaign, maybe the actor can be defeated by an epic battle or a broken pledge, the prop can also be destroyed, the wisps can be killed... But what about the realm? How do players fight a realm? Do they have to burn it down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T22:51:25-07:00","id":1222171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1222027#post1222027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can you fix any of that? Dunno. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24237\" data-vbnamecard=\"24237\">Pluvinarch</a> alludes the effort makes a good story. After all, &quot;I wanna be a real boy!&quot; is a firm story trope.<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to believe that the struggle for Changelings to hope and adapt, <i>by itself </i>is valuable to the Keepers, in that it continues to generate &quot;story&quot; in ways that channel glamour back to Arcadia. If this surmise is even partially correct, it could explain why some Changelings and Holds are left more or less alone by the Huntsmen, or... just enough so to keep the inhabitants of the fishbowl properly terrified.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd also like to believe that it <i>is</i> possible to become human again--even if difficult--but that doing so never really sheds ties completely. There will always be something tugging at the back of the mind. Something... watching.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hate to pick nits here, but that concept of &quot;story&quot; generation is part of the reason I think that Hill's version of the Courts needed a lot of reworking. You haven't escaped the Gentry, you're just appeasing them so they don't come and stomp you dead. What's the point of leaving if you're just doing what they want, you are now exposed to something that hurts you and negates your powers, and you have <i>less</i> magical power in your day to day life?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pluvinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1222168#post1222168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Gentry can have titles and for each title he can manifest as an actor, a prop, a realm or wisps. So I guess, for a Storyteller planning a long term campaign, maybe the actor can be defeated by an epic battle or a broken pledge, the prop can also be destroyed, the wisps can be killed... But what about the realm? How do players fight a realm? Do they have to burn it down?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to kill the Realm, as it were - you need to go for the physical Title itself. Dispute the Gentry's claim to the Title and you dispute the abilities that come from it, as well as their manifested form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T09:24:54-07:00","id":1222272,"title":"","content":"Equinox Road has this to say about killing a Realm: <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">\u201cCrush the purple rose that grows on the tallest peak, for it contains her vital essence.\u201d He doesn\u2019t say that this is only true because his enemy\u2019s taken the form of a Realm, or that this particular weakness is driven by the Legend the enemy\u2019s playing out&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Now, this doesn't necessarily apply to all Realms, and certainly they don't all have purple flowers, but the implication seems to be that Realms have some kind of critical weakness that can be exploited the same way as an Actor's Banes. The thermal exhaust port on the Death Star, if you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:22:26-07:00","id":1223265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1222171#post1222171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hate to pick nits here, but that concept of &quot;story&quot; generation is part of the reason I think that Hill's version of the Courts needed a lot of reworking. You haven't escaped the Gentry, you're just appeasing them so they don't come and stomp you dead. What's the point of leaving if you're just doing what they want, you are now exposed to something that hurts you and negates your powers, and you have <i>less</i> magical power in your day to day life?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... and I'm not well-enough read in Changeling to take the thought further. Really looking for 2e to lay a firm foundation. That said, the view of &quot;Changelings as not-really escapees&quot; could <b><i>at least</i></b> be a flawed thought process a Privateer might use to justify their involvement.<br /> <br /> After all, if you've escaped your cell and are running around the prison yard pretending to be free, what's the real moral issue with putting a few actors back in their cage now and then? It's not like the warden's couldn't do it whenever, right? May as well get some brownie points and all....<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating this as a Truth (capital T), just pointing out that Courts or no, it looks like a potential conclusion a character could reach, given everything.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T18:09:44-07:00","id":1223454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1222171#post1222171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hate to pick nits here, but that concept of &quot;story&quot; generation is part of the reason I think that Hill's version of the Courts needed a lot of reworking. You haven't escaped the Gentry, you're just appeasing them so they don't come and stomp you dead. What's the point of leaving if you're just doing what they want, you are now exposed to something that hurts you and negates your powers, and you have <i>less</i> magical power in your day to day life?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of why I prefer the mercantile emphasis over the specifically-narrative angle \u2014 a political-economic magical context means it's very simple to illustrate &quot;Your Keeper's wants and resources do not exist in a vacuum and the things you do to get around them matter&quot; without reducing it to playing Scheherazade to keep the gods at bay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T18:22:25-07:00","id":1223461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1223454#post1223454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is part of why I prefer the mercantile emphasis over the specifically-narrative angle \u2014 a political-economic magical context means it's very simple to illustrate &amp;quot;Your Keeper's wants and resources do not exist in a vacuum and the things you do to get around them matter&amp;quot; without reducing it to playing Scheherazade to keep the gods at bay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm feeling dense and distracted. Might you expand a bit on your quoted paradigm--perhaps with an example?<br /> <br /> You are referring to the transactional nature or Arcadian &quot;magic&quot;, yes?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf the Tired","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T18:37:21-07:00","id":1223466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1223461#post1223461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm feeling dense and distracted. Might you expand a bit on your quoted paradigm--perhaps with an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fae don't approach the denizens of the Grey City Freehold without caution.<br /> <br /> This has basically nothing to do with its alignment with the story of the interplay between the Great Chicago Fire and the World's Columbian Exposition; it's just that the Bright Face and the Long Shadow that watch over the Courts of Dread and Defiance are infamously litigious forces squatting on a massive cache of dreams and debt, and the last thing any crusading Gentry want to countenance is the prospect of losing Their estate to a hobgoblin prince or an overgrown Bedlam-ghost.<br /> <br /> So they play it cool and wait for an opportune moment, which might not be on a straightforward timeline because their fellows are watching for the exact same chances and there's only so much room on the trods for fae agents on the ground, particularly in the case of the major investment a Huntsman represents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are referring to the transactional nature or Arcadian &quot;magic&quot;, yes? </div> </div> </div>The very same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":"05-30-2018, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:11:39-07:00","id":1223596,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, that's very helpful. Let me check myself....<br /> <br /> Ok, so essentially what will give the Gentry pause is the possibility that someone can use the same mechanisms as well as they can, to force the issues and exploit the loopholes that exist (because they have to exist). In other words, someone is as clever, as invested, or as resourced as they are. Natch. <br /> <br /> If you're a Freehold that doesn't have a &quot;\u043a\u0440\u044b\u0448\u0430&quot; (roof) to cover you, then you get huntsmen bi-weekly and twice on St. Patrick's Day? Obvious spur for Changelings to properly organize is obvious, no? So They play around the edges waiting for some Changelings (preferably &quot;Their&quot; Changeling) to go solo and try to live in the cracks, right? <br /> <br /> Which is once of the reasons the Changelings try to find a place in the world, no? It make it harder from a contractual standpoint to just scoop them up--because they have ties that have to be respected, even if you're an alien demigod. I suppose this makes some sense, since after all you can't just tie up a Changeling and expect them to stick around... have to use red tape to accomplish that--the Headless Horseman only can get you AND keep you if you do X and Y and don't Z.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T17:08:19-07:00","id":1223760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1223596#post1223596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so essentially what will give the Gentry pause is the possibility that someone can use the same mechanisms as well as they can, to force the issues and exploit the loopholes that exist (because they have to exist). In other words, someone is as clever, as invested, or as resourced as they are. Natch.<br /> <br /> If you're a Freehold that doesn't have a &quot;\u043a\u0440\u044b\u0448\u0430&quot; (roof) to cover you, then you get huntsmen bi-weekly and twice on St. Patrick's Day? Obvious spur for Changelings to properly organize is obvious, no? So They play around the edges waiting for some Changelings (preferably &quot;Their&quot; Changeling) to go solo and try to live in the cracks, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's all that and also the other side of the coin: Sometimes a Keeper just <i>doesn't see much worth</i> in dispatching agents to retrieve a wayward servant.<br /> <br /> This is the paradox of the Courts: they make it substantially harder for the Fae to go after a changeling, but they also foster <i>much greater returns</i> to a Stranger who's prepared to wait for their lost seed of fae magic to blossom into a little portfolio of connections and materiel and bargaining chips. Changelings with a Court to cover them have more opportunities to raise their Wyrd, which makes them easier to find as they become more powerful, and the next thing you know you're Wyrd 7 and running a hobgoblin commune to cover your debts because being hard to find and possessed of a shifting roster of abilities is more important than holding Courtly rank and power and <i>what was that at the window?</i> (Goblin Debt is a gift, as mechanics go.)<br /> <br /> This is a markedly different state of affairs than &quot;you exist at Our sufferance&quot; \u2014 a monstrous god being prideful enough to think He can leave you alone and wait for you to get stronger is more than just a narrative beat, it's a political gamble based in the Fae's greed and ego and drive for conquest, which nevertheless contains the possibility of failure (a possibility that other fae can influence). That you might sacrifice your childhood trumpet to the Thorns for a weapon against the Others and court the favor of long-hidden hobgoblin witnesses to oaths sworn by moonlight among the misty gardens of the Gentry only sweetens the pot \u2014 everything has a price, even if it's just in the form of lost opportunities, and if you can get someone else pay it for you then so much the better.<br /> <br /> The fae inhabit a world of gates and bridges, and negotiating either takes its toll with or without the framework of dreams and stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T06:36:34-07:00","id":1223899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1223760#post1223760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's all that and also the other side of the coin: Sometimes a Keeper just <i>doesn't see much worth</i> in dispatching agents to retrieve a wayward servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThank you again, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, this enriches the perspective greatly. And, for bringing up the above quote, which was also on mind: why bother if some other poor sot will do the trick and become a brand new shoe-polisher to break all over again? Old tools are old, and boring, after all! Leaving your escapee fallow to sprout new, useful crops may make him more valuable in the end. And... fun!<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Let me pivot to another question, spurred from reading bits of Equinox Road the other day.<br /> <br /> So in Arcadia items are either ephemeral, real (and thus intelligent) or Hedge-spun, right? Am I missing a category? I mean, what about the clothing your Changeling slaves wears? Do all escapees show up either naked or with Hedge-spun stuff on?<br /> <br /> What about taking other things out of Durance? Do they have to be Hedge-spun? You cannot have a mundane gold coin with your Keeper's likeness on it, for random example?<br /> <br /> Feel like I'm missing something here, as well.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T10:34:38-07:00","id":1223949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1223899#post1223899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in Arcadia items are either ephemeral, real (and thus intelligent) or Hedge-spun, right? Am I missing a category? I mean, what about the clothing your Changeling slaves wears? Do all escapees show up either naked or with Hedge-spun stuff on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either is a distinct possibility, but it's worth remembering that &quot;intelligent&quot; doesn't necessarily translate to &quot;active&quot; outside the context of fae magic \u2014a Wizened tailor might extract whispered promises from their handiwork, but it's just as possible for a changeling to escape with stolen kit from a new arrival or piece together a rough outfit in the Hedge on their way back to Earth.<br /> <br /> The thematic connection clothing and identity have and the fact that the Fae regularly have the ability to make their servants immune to things one might need particular clothes for (or force them through those things regardless) generally make an escape from the Durance rough and/or some level of supernatural theft/kidnapping \u2014 your own garments may have been shredded long ago by the Thorns or your Keeper's household, but if you escape with nothing more than the clothes on your back then they either were magical or belonged to somebody (or both).<br /> <br /> Other personal possessions fill the same niche, but in general there's a reason the Gentry still largely stuck to Arcadia even in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T08:05:16-07:00","id":1228299,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, it seems then that the Hedgespun Merit is the means the game intends players to use to represent &quot;stuff they liberated from Faerie&quot; on their way out. Broadly speaking. <br /> <br /> Additional question:<br /> <br /> Do Changelings mature after their return? If you, for example, spent a subjective eternity as a 9-y.o. playmate, would you remain so thereafter even as you age slowly?<br /> <br /> Or does maturation kick back in at a slowed rate in line with aging?<br /> <br /> Or is it pretty much normal up to physical maturity, and then you just live a long time (Wyrd permitting)?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T12:54:49-07:00","id":1228357,"title":"","content":"Your growth seems to continue like normal (if slowed), but aspects of it can be anchored by kith, like how many ogres tend to be large even if they use traditional weight-loss techniques. If you've ever seen Batman the Animated Series, you have the character Baby Doll, who is sort of stuck in a small, childish form even while she ages due to systemic hypoplasia, which kept her from growing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://3.bp.blogspot.com/-1VzgJ0eQ5H8/VvVriHLsIjI/AAAAAAAAtqQ/nErrdcxsutwXG2e7v9qUyupNjWrYn3gsg/s1600/vlcsnap-2016-03-23-23h15m11s704.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or I guess more fitting for your 9-month old example, Baby Herman from Roger Rabbit.<br /> <br /> Probably more suitable for NPCs, in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T10:28:20-07:00","id":1228892,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>. So... basically growth is slowed to a thematically appropriate rate for the story/character the player wants to tell. Cool. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T16:24:31-07:00","id":1229670,"title":"","content":"So, I'm scouring all the 2E books I can grasp at for anything that looks like an Ephemeral Entity rules for reasons. How do Hedge Ghosts work now again? Or more to the point, are they divergent enough from the standard Ephemeral Entity rules enough that it wouldn't be wise to benchmark them for homebrewing a different set of ephemeral entities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:10:03-07:00","id":1229675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1229670#post1229670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm scouring all the 2E books I can grasp at for anything that looks like an Ephemeral Entity rules for reasons. How do Hedge Ghosts work now again? Or more to the point, are they divergent enough from the standard Ephemeral Entity rules enough that it wouldn't be wise to benchmark them for homebrewing a different set of ephemeral entities?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're similar and different.<br /> <br /> At their foundation they do use the Ephemeral Entity rules. Differences (at least from the KS manuscript, and assuming the Proofing process since then hasn't drastically changed them) include:<ul><li>Having a Wyrd rating instead of Rank (so same Trait point allocation).</li> <li>Glamour instead of Essence</li> <li>Can enter and influence a target's dreams for the purposes of gaining Glamour.</li> <li>Frailties instead of bans and banes (amount determined by Wyrd).</li> <li>Common abilities including: being able to navigate through the Thorns in the Hedge, being able to Reach into the mortal world while on the other side of a Hedge gate, can sense Glamour, and the ability to know where the closest Goblin Market is.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:44:37-07:00","id":1229684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1229675#post1229675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're similar and different.<br /> <br /> At their foundation they do use the Ephemeral Entity rules. Differences (at least from the KS manuscript, and assuming the Proofing process since then hasn't drastically changed them) include:<ul><li>Having a Wyrd rating instead of Rank (so same Trait point allocation).</li> <li>Glamour instead of Essence</li> <li>Can enter and influence a target's dreams for the purposes of gaining Glamour.</li> <li>Frailties instead of bans and banes (amount determined by Wyrd).</li> <li>Common abilities including: being able to navigate through the Thorns in the Hedge, being able to Reach into the mortal world while on the other side of a Hedge gate, can sense Glamour, and the ability to know where the closest Goblin Market is.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks. <br /> <br /> Maybe I\u2019ll borrow some ideas from them for spirit-Liches in Mage...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:48:53-07:00","id":1229700,"title":"","content":"Hedge Ghosts are also not twilight entities, even in the mortal world they're not in twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T08:11:35-07:00","id":1230544,"title":"","content":"<b>What happens if a changeling invokes Contracts of Fang &amp; Talon (Insects) in the middle of winter?</b> Would the clause fail automatically because there are no living insects nearby to answer the call? Would dormant insects wake themselves up and crawl out of their hidey-holes, only to die of exposure within seconds? Or would the magic of the contract protect the insects from the cold until they fulfill their obligations to the Wyrd?<br /> <br /> The last option seems the most fair to the player, but it opens up avenues for abuse and manipulation. If the Wyrd protects the player's insect allies from cold until they fulfill their obligations, then why wouldn't the Wyrd also protect them from the heat and smoke of a fire, or a cloud of pesticide? And that doesn't even get into magically-created cold: what happens if that changeling summons their insect allies but then someone else invokes &quot;Riding the Devil's Jawbone&quot; to freeze the whole area? What if the changeling calls for his insect-allies' aid from inside a meat locker or a walk-in freezer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T00:50:00-07:00","id":1244749,"title":"","content":"So, this may be breaching the \u201cSimple Answer\u201d aspect of this thread, but I\u2019m really kind of confused here. Barring one contract (Pure Clarity), none of the healing contracts in second edition, nor the Playmate Kith, specify if a Changeling can target themselves with those healing options. With Shared Burden, it makes sense, since you\u2019re accepting another\u2019s wounds, but something like Gift Of Warm Breath makes sense...but doesn\u2019t specify if you could.<br /> <br /> This is kind of feeling like a doctor being unable to heal thyself, and I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s a good thing or not considering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T06:49:50-07:00","id":1244798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1244749#post1244749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kind of feeling like a doctor being unable to heal thyself, and I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s a good thing or not considering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that this is normally how that state of affairs works and that the fae ecology/economy of the Hedge provides a number of direct workarounds for this even if changelings weren't based on a type of supernatural creature that didn't commonly had access to personal self-healing.<br /> <br /> It follows that most changelings who find themselves needing to heal themselves quickly either get themselves to a doctor of some stripe or make use of external fae powers like goblin fruit or Arcadian Metabolism \u2014 the Lost's primary means of handling damage is to not take any and to lay low when they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T10:49:02-07:00","id":1244856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1244798#post1244798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that this is normally how that state of affairs works and that the fae ecology/economy of the Hedge provides a number of direct workarounds for this even if changelings weren't based on a type of supernatural creature that didn't commonly had access to personal self-healing.<br /> <br /> It follows that most changelings who find themselves needing to heal themselves quickly either get themselves to a doctor of some stripe or make use of external fae powers like goblin fruit or Arcadian Metabolism \u2014 the Lost's primary means of handling damage is to not take any and to lay low when they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, considering the game's themes of rebuilding trust in people as a cornerstone of rebuilding home and the import of relationships and how they affect you, it's doubly effective that the game does basically make all of it's physical healing options a mechanical extension of healing those personal, socio-psychological wounds at the risk of exploitation.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're bleeding, and you should trust this person to help you, but what will it actually cost?&quot; is a pretty potent question for this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T07:57:00-07:00","id":1245474,"title":"","content":"Contracts (p.95) states that you may learn favored Regalia and Court Contracts without a teacher, but all other Contracts require someone or something to teach you. Pupil's Devotion (p.129) states you may learn an Arcadian Contract more easily by seeking a teacher, offering a discount down to favored costs if you do and swear an oath. Is it intended that you can learn from a teacher without the oath, but gain the discount if you do swear? Or is p.95 off and you can learn any contract you have the xp to purchase, with pupil's devotion just granting an optional discount?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24499-yukidaore","name":"Yukidaore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:22:11-07:00","id":1245491,"title":"","content":"Page 95 says you need something to learn it from, but it doesn't have to be someone who's actively teaching you the contract. I think it would be possible to learn Contracts by just reading about them or possibly even studying someone who uses the Contract regardless if they intentionally shows it off or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:50:49-07:00","id":1245506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1245491#post1245491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 95 says you need something to learn it from, but it doesn't have to be someone who's actively teaching you the contract. I think it would be possible to learn Contracts by just reading about them or possibly even studying someone who uses the Contract regardless if they intentionally shows it off or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that lines up quite closely with my take on the intent, as well! I feel like the wording - specifically, using 'teach' on p.95, which implies deliberate effort to instruct another - is probably just an artifact of some older iteration that got missed. Wish I hadn't missed the errata thread with this one, but c'est la vie!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24499-yukidaore","name":"Yukidaore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:58:25-07:00","id":1245963,"title":"","content":"I have a few questions.<br /> <br /> In which order should Clarity damage be healed when resolving Clarity Conditions? Mild or severe first?<br /> <br /> What emotions are the Dragon Societies, Tide Courts and Traders' Courts tied to? Page 307 states that all courts are tied to an emotion for the purpose of inciting Bedlam. Does this also extend to the bonus Glamour gained from harvesting that emotion, or is that an advantage only the Seasonal Courts have?<br /> <br /> Court Contracts can substitute Goodwill for Mantle for the dice pool. Does this mean dot for dot, or does it refer to the effective Mantle dots that is Goodwill-2?<br /> Should Goodwill also substitute for Mantle in the Contract effects as well? Otherwise some Contracts will become completely useless because they scale with Mantle.<br /> <br /> How does the in-season/out-of-season benefits work?<br /> A member of an in-season court gains the Royal benefit, but does that benefit extend to all Royal Contracts of his court, all Royal Court Contracts regardless of court, or all Royal Contracts including Royal Arcadian Contracts?<br /> Similarly, a member of an out-of-season court gains the Common benefit, but does that benefit extend to all Common Contracts of the in-season court, all Common Contracts of her own court, all Common Court Contracts regardless of court, or all Common Contracts including Common Arcadian Contracts?<br /> <br /> Should non-cyclical court structures also receive a bonus to Contracts, or is it something about the cyclical structure that inherently empower Contracts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:15:44-07:00","id":1245975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1245963#post1245963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which order should Clarity damage be healed when resolving Clarity Conditions? Mild or severe first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably mild, because healing generally proceeds from right to left and severe damage specifically overlaps mild damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should non-cyclical court structures also receive a bonus to Contracts, or is it something about the cyclical structure that inherently empower Contracts? </div> </div> </div>Even the freehold structure that doesn't have more than one Court makes mention of cyclic power arrangements within that Court, so probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-14-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T17:58:32-07:00","id":1246135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1245963#post1245963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What emotions are the Dragon Societies, Tide Courts and Traders' Courts tied to? Page 307 states that all courts are tied to an emotion for the purpose of inciting Bedlam. Does this also extend to the bonus Glamour gained from harvesting that emotion, or is that an advantage only the Seasonal Courts have?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know. Just as with the court contracts, we kind of need to make that up ourselves. However, the means to get an extra glamour from doing a certain action is a pretty good way to extrapolate the emotions involved from the actions, and given how 1e courts all had an emotion involved with them I imagine that 2e ones do too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Court Contracts can substitute Goodwill for Mantle for the dice pool. Does this mean dot for dot, or does it refer to the effective Mantle dots that is Goodwill-2?<br /> Should Goodwill also substitute for Mantle in the Contract effects as well? Otherwise some Contracts will become completely useless because they scale with Mantle. </div> </div> </div>Yes, where it says Mantle, replace Court Goodwill that you have dot for dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does the in-season/out-of-season benefits work?<br /> A member of an in-season court gains the Royal benefit, but does that benefit extend to all Royal Contracts of his court, all Royal Court Contracts regardless of court, or all Royal Contracts including Royal Arcadian Contracts? </div> </div> </div>I believe that it refers to the court you have Court Goodwill in, not all Royal Court Contracts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, a member of an out-of-season court gains the Common benefit, but does that benefit extend to all Common Contracts of the in-season court, all Common Contracts of her own court, all Common Court Contracts regardless of court, or all Common Contracts including Common Arcadian Contracts? </div> </div> </div>I believe that refers to the in-season court. Considering the tone of the rest of the paragraph, I think that it only grants a bonus to seasonal contracts too. You're free to interpret this as you wish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should non-cyclical court structures also receive a bonus to Contracts, or is it something about the cyclical structure that inherently empower Contracts? </div> </div> </div>As with their emotions, this looks to be something that Storytellers and players should decide for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T18:56:24-07:00","id":1246150,"title":"","content":"How literally should I interpret light-shy's darkling clause of temporary erasure from existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:43:13-07:00","id":1246172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1246150#post1246150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How literally should I interpret light-shy's darkling clause of temporary erasure from existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you no longer register as a sensory phenomenon extends from a mental effect to something capable of fooling theoretically objective observers; change the &quot;and&quot; in that sentence out for a semicolon or an em-dash if necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T07:50:14-07:00","id":1246332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1246135#post1246135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that refers to the in-season court. Considering the tone of the rest of the paragraph, I think that it only grants a bonus to seasonal contracts too. You're free to interpret this as you wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers.<br /> This one seems a bit weird to me. It makes the out-of-season courtiers better at the in-season court's Common Contracts than members of the actual court. That's why I wondered if the Mantle/Goodwill for rolls might actually refer to the effective Mantle rating rather than straight translation as it says. In that case the Common Contract benefit would instead grant out-of-season courtiers equal footing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T10:18:45-07:00","id":1246373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1246332#post1246332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answers.<br /> This one seems a bit weird to me. It makes the out-of-season courtiers better at the in-season court's Common Contracts than members of the actual court. That's why I wondered if the Mantle/Goodwill for rolls might actually refer to the effective Mantle rating rather than straight translation as it says. In that case the Common Contract benefit would instead grant out-of-season courtiers equal footing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as a balancing act - common powers are given a bonus, but those in the court gain an exceptional on 3 successes for royal. Both sides gain something that lets them be effective and incentiveses buying the contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T12:30:20-07:00","id":1246410,"title":"","content":"No, I get why. Both gets bonuses. It just feels weird that the non-courtier bonus is something that the courtiers don't have any access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T17:08:40-07:00","id":1248901,"title":"","content":"Would a contract like 'shared burden' that heals a target's disease at the expense of the changeling taking on the disease themselves be too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T21:06:24-07:00","id":1248919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1248901#post1248901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a contract like 'shared burden' that heals a target's disease at the expense of the changeling taking on the disease themselves be too much?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You wouldn't even need a contract &quot;like&quot; Shared Burden, just make it a seeming benefit for whichever seeming makes the most sense to you. <br /> <br /> The ability to houserule minor variations on contracts with seeming benefits is one of my favorite parts of the redesign they got for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T22:27:45-07:00","id":1248924,"title":"","content":"A Fae Mount cannot leave the Hedge unless it has Actormask (which allows it to enter the mortal world). But, can a Fae Mount enter dreams? What about Arcadia, or other realms beyond the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T22:33:10-07:00","id":1248927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1248919#post1248919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You wouldn't even need a contract &quot;like&quot; Shared Burden, just make it a seeming benefit for whichever seeming makes the most sense to you.<br /> <br /> The ability to houserule minor variations on contracts with seeming benefits is one of my favorite parts of the redesign they got for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>A seeming benifit could be an interesting direction to take with that and it'd fit the theme still. Should it just be &quot;[Seeming]: Instead of damage you may take on a sickness and heal another suffering that sickness.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T11:01:06-07:00","id":1248980,"title":"","content":"What determines, in the Doylist sence, your second favored Regalia? Who you were before your Durance, who you were made into during it, or who you became during your escape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T01:32:42-07:00","id":1249079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1248980#post1248980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What determines, in the Doylist sence, your second favored Regalia? Who you were before your Durance, who you were made into during it, or who you became during your escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Changeling\u2019s second favored Regalia, outside of the one that their Seeming forms into, is really more like a talent in my eyes than anything else. Just as two kids in exactly the same living space and teaching methods may both be able to do math extremely well, one might have an increased ability in Gym class, whereas the other would have a greater aptitude for English class. It could also stem from the needs of their Keeper\u2019s realm and of their Keeper in turn, their desires and what magic they might tuck away or be exposed to.<br /> <br /> Really, the realms of the Gentry are practically infinite in their difference and complexity, and each one will have different circumstances on why a Fairest may have a favored Regalia in Shield and another would have a favored Regalia in Mirrors, even when they were doing the exact same job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T15:06:33-07:00","id":1249796,"title":"","content":"Should the 1e goblin market book still function for 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T13:23:47-07:00","id":1250042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1249796#post1249796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should the 1e goblin market book still function for 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>That book was mostly great for inspiration material so I don't see why not. <br /> <br /> Looking specifically at the book now. <br /> Chapter 1 should work (if you want it to) as written in 2nd Ed. <br /> <br /> Chapter 2 might need a bit of updating but not much. <br /> The things I see are:<br /> - Goblin Contract Price: basically the same but be aware that Goblin Debt should be a part of the process. <br /> - Actually Goblin Debt should be pretty much everywhere in this chapter (still a very minor update, just determine the Goblin Debt amount and who owns the debt (as an ST)<br /> - I'd include the merit &quot;Fae Mount&quot; in the &quot;Servants, Pets, and Slaves&quot; portion of the chapter as things you could potentially get.<br /> - Since Changelings don't use Virtue or Vice, the Vice portion could be adapted to things that have similar effects.<br /> - Pretty much all goblin contracts can prolly still work they just need a bit of updating (no dot rating, no catch, maybe someother stuff)<br /> <br /> Chapter 3 would need a tad bit of updating mostly for the kinds of contracts the sample characters have. But otherwise should be usable. The big part would be changing out their contracts me thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T03:58:34-07:00","id":1250220,"title":"","content":"In second edition, is there any material that explicitly supports or rejects the idea presented in Equinox Roads that high-Wyrd, low Clarity changelings can become Gentry? I have the preview but I haven't seen any references to this, so I'm wondering if it was removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T07:50:02-07:00","id":1250250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1250220#post1250220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In second edition, is there any material that explicitly supports or rejects the idea presented in Equinox Roads that high-Wyrd, low Clarity changelings can become Gentry? I have the preview but I haven't seen any references to this, so I'm wondering if it was removed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given that clarity has been overhauled into a mental damage track that renders you comatose when it's filled up, I'd say it's at least no longer automatic. That said, I vaguely remember something about unscrupulous and power-hungry Changelings trying to steal Titles from The Gentry to become Gentry themselves, so Changelings still can become True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T09:50:33-07:00","id":1250266,"title":"","content":"What happens to a weapon (or other piece of equipment)created via Oneiromancy if a changeling tries to carry it from a Bastion out into the Hedge?<br /> <br /> Does it persist as an object that's usable by physical beings in the Hedge?<br /> Does it persist as an object that's only usable by dream form beings in the Hedge?<br /> <br /> If the former, can it be physically carried <i>out</i> of the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T14:47:47-07:00","id":1250328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1250250#post1250250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that clarity has been overhauled into a mental damage track that renders you comatose when it's filled up, I'd say it's at least no longer automatic. That said, I vaguely remember something about unscrupulous and power-hungry Changelings trying to steal Titles from The Gentry to become Gentry themselves, so Changelings still can become True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, it's not automatic. And there isn't just one way to do it. Later books will go more into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1250266#post1250266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to a weapon (or other piece of equipment)created via Oneiromancy if a changeling tries to carry it from a Bastion out into the Hedge?<br /> <br /> Does it persist as an object that's usable by physical beings in the Hedge?<br /> Does it persist as an object that's only usable by dream form beings in the Hedge?<br /> <br /> If the former, can it be physically carried <i>out</i> of the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't persist beyond the Bastion and its immediate environs, barring something unusual happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T20:13:34-07:00","id":1250387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1250328#post1250328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't persist beyond the Bastion and its immediate environs, barring something unusual happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the same is not true of similar objects created via Hedgespinning? Or is there some special process outside of the Hedgespinning rules to create traditional Hedgespun clothing, objects, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T21:30:59-07:00","id":1250402,"title":"","content":"2e manuscript quiestion regarding true fey, are true fey immune to non-bane damage unless its true name is invoked or it breaks an oath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T20:05:11-07:00","id":1251268,"title":"","content":"I never considered this before but can hobgoblins preform Oneiromancy? If it works just like hedge-spinning as described in the section on subtle shifts that'd lead me to think a hobgoblin could. They just would be unable to do paradigm shifts just as they cannot during hedge-spinning","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T10:20:55-07:00","id":1252796,"title":"","content":"Does being Fae-Touched work more similarly to Ghouls, or to being Wolf-Blooded, with respect to gaining a supernatural template?<br /> <br /> Ghouls cannot also have a supernatural template, and (iirc) this is explicit. They lose all their Ghoul stuff if they gain one.<br /> Wolf-Blooded characters keep their Tells (their primary feature) if they become a supernatural template other than werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T11:38:23-07:00","id":1252814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1252796#post1252796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does being Fae-Touched work more similarly to Ghouls, or to being Wolf-Blooded, with respect to gaining a supernatural template?<br /> <br /> Ghouls cannot also have a supernatural template, and (iirc) this is explicit. They lose all their Ghoul stuff if they gain one.<br /> Wolf-Blooded characters keep their Tells (their primary feature) if they become a supernatural template other than werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think closer to Ghouls. Both are acquired and contingent upon circumstances to be maintained, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T11:47:43-07:00","id":1252816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1252814#post1252814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would think closer to Ghouls. Both are acquired and contingent upon circumstances to be maintained, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being Fae-Touched doesn't have to be maintained. Once you're Fae-Touched, that's just what you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T14:58:10-07:00","id":1252855,"title":"","content":"I remember seeing that the tagline was changed to &quot;A Storytelling Game of Beautiful Lies and Bittersweet Truths&quot; from the original one of &quot;A Storytelling Game of Beautiful Madness&quot;. Then, I saw a recent update on the Kickstarter page (well after the tagline change) with an image of the corebook's cover that had the original tagline.<br /> <br /> So my questions are: what's the situation behind the tagline (I know that the one who changed it had very personal reasons for it), and what's the official tagline now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T20:31:27-07:00","id":1253202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1250387#post1250387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the same is not true of similar objects created via Hedgespinning? Or is there some special process outside of the Hedgespinning rules to create traditional Hedgespun clothing, objects, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking something you made via Hedgespinning out of the Hedge makes it vanish unless you go through one of the processes it takes to make any other kind of token.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1250402#post1250402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e manuscript quiestion regarding true fey, are true fey immune to non-bane damage unless its true name is invoked or it breaks an oath?</div> </div> </div> </div>True Fae are immune to bashing damage except from banes; they're immune to lethal damage except from banes unless those things happen; the only thing that causes them aggravated damage is cold iron, which works no matter what (as it's a bane).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T20:33:04-07:00","id":1253204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1251268#post1251268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never considered this before but can hobgoblins preform Oneiromancy? If it works just like hedge-spinning as described in the section on subtle shifts that'd lead me to think a hobgoblin could. They just would be unable to do paradigm shifts just as they cannot during hedge-spinning</div> </div> </div> </div>Hobgoblins as a collective entity can't perform oneiromancy, but an individual hobgoblin's powers might let them screw around with dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T13:33:16-07:00","id":1253367,"title":"","content":"Hey i have 2 questions<br /> I'm writing my first campaign of Changeling: The Lost and i will be using the 2e, i'm planning to set a camapaign in London but i'm having diffcult in some aspects<br /> Like how much changelings should exist ? <br /> i imagine that british isles in general might be quite connected to the wyrd soo a big number might be needed <br /> <br /> And one more questions i should try to create in my first game my own courts or just stick with the Seasonal ones(that are quite fleshed out and very interesting in this edition) ? <br /> I wanted create more not only to represent the immigrant communities but also some based on great britain folklore like a court of the knights based on arthurian myths and maybe another freehold on Ireland who have some grudges against the British courts but i think this might be too much too deal for a first game what do you all think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T01:03:30-07:00","id":1253520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queer Snake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1253367#post1253367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one more questions i should try to create in my first game my own courts or just stick with the Seasonal ones(that are quite fleshed out and very interesting in this edition) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely up to you.<br /> <br /> Personally, if this is your first campaign, I'd say there's no shame in using the Seasonal Courts. They're ubiquitous enough to plug in, and all the big work is ready for you right out of the box. And it would give you a feel of a set of Courts already completed so you know what to do when making your own.<br /> <br /> However, if you're full to the brim on ideas for your own Courts and you feel you have a good grasp of your concepts and the systems of the game, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T10:55:26-07:00","id":1253649,"title":"","content":"Inception questions:<br /> <br /> - If a changelling dreams and meditates, he is lucid inside his dreams. If someone else dreams while touching him, his friend also goes to the changeling dream through the ivory gate. Does that invited person has a bastion of his own that he/she can later visit?<br /> <br /> - If a changeling is dreaming inside the Hedge, can he get out of his own bastion and meet his real body on his Hollow?<br /> <br /> - If a changeling enters another person dream through the horn gate and starts to dream inside someone\u00b4s else bastion, will his dreamning self be transported to his own bastion?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T16:04:54-07:00","id":1257272,"title":"","content":"How do Fetches regain Glamour? I probably missed something but I can't seem to find anything on that in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T16:26:11-07:00","id":1257274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pluvinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1253649#post1253649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that invited person has a bastion of his own that he/she can later visit?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - If a changeling is dreaming inside the Hedge, can he get out of his own bastion and meet his real body on his Hollow? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - If a changeling enters another person dream through the horn gate and starts to dream inside someone\u00b4s else bastion, will his dreamning self be transported to his own bastion? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1257272#post1257272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Fetches regain Glamour? I probably missed something but I can't seem to find anything on that in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably safe to assume that emotion-harvesting and Hedge bounty are fair game, at the bare minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T08:06:50-07:00","id":1257368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1257274#post1257274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably safe to assume that emotion-harvesting and Hedge bounty are fair game, at the bare minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetches however don't get hurt by staying with zero Glamour, do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T11:16:34-07:00","id":1257404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1257274#post1257274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably safe to assume that emotion-harvesting and Hedge bounty are fair game, at the bare minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. Although it would be nice to have some confirmation as it's pretty crucial to understanding the creature, at least when it leans more on the supernatural side.<br /> <br /> On a different note, how specifically would you rule the pledge to obtain an active invitation into a mortal's Bastion? Sealing? Bargain? Under what terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T01:09:41-07:00","id":1257731,"title":"","content":"This may be a weird question, but in second edition, can Wizened use their Blessing to change a substance into something edible? Use a hammer and anvil to shape metal into gingerbread, or a lathe to turn wood into cheese, or even something like inedible bark into flour using a mortar and pestle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T17:06:52-07:00","id":1257868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1257731#post1257731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a weird question, but in second edition, can Wizened use their Blessing to change a substance into something edible? Use a hammer and anvil to shape metal into gingerbread, or a lathe to turn wood into cheese, or even something like inedible bark into flour using a mortar and pestle?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW it's...a bit of a grey area.<br /> <br /> The Wizened Blessing is specifically based around the use of the Build Equipment action. And the type of Equipment listed as stuff you could build doesn't really list consumables, unless if you count the first aid kit. Just as is, there isn't any precedent to it, but IMO, there's really nothing holding you back for counting food as Building Equipment...it does kind of stretch things with what's in the text.<br /> <br /> That said, the idea of a Wizened as a cook/chef is a good concept and doesn't sound unreasonable. Probably better off making it as some kind of chef-kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T19:05:43-07:00","id":1257885,"title":"","content":"There's nothing stopping you from using the Build Equipment rules to cook food, it's just that in most circumstances food doesn't count as &quot;equipment&quot; because it doesn't grant bonuses to anything. And usually there's no reason to roll dice to cook something. So yeah, you could use the Wizened blessing to turn wood into cheese--it just introduces a roll to something that otherwise wouldn't bother with one (making cheese).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T19:16:27-07:00","id":1257889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1257868#post1257868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW it's...a bit of a grey area.<br /> <br /> The Wizened Blessing is specifically based around the use of the Build Equipment action. And the type of Equipment listed as stuff you could build doesn't really list consumables, unless if you count the first aid kit. Just as is, there isn't any precedent to it, but IMO, there's really nothing holding you back for counting food as Building Equipment...it does kind of stretch things with what's in the text.<br /> <br /> That said, the idea of a Wizened as a cook/chef is a good concept and doesn't sound unreasonable. Probably better off making it as some kind of chef-kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I get where you're coming from, the suggested equipment for the various skills in the Changeling book is pretty liberal in what is considered &quot;equipment&quot;, and the items suggested for what a Wizened can make (diamond and straws of gold) aren't exactly what you'd consider &quot;equipment&quot; either. Though some of that equipment does sound like it'd be hard for the average person to build themselves, I don't feel it'd be unreasonable for someone to use a Build Equipment action for those kinds of things.<br /> <br /> I'd bring up how Quality Food would be reasonable equipment for a Social action involving a party, but at this point it feels like I'm quibbling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T06:51:34-07:00","id":1258727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1257885#post1257885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing stopping you from using the Build Equipment rules to cook food, it's just that in most circumstances food doesn't count as &quot;equipment&quot; because it doesn't grant bonuses to anything. And usually there's no reason to roll dice to cook something. So yeah, you could use the Wizened blessing to turn wood into cheese--it just introduces a roll to something that otherwise wouldn't bother with one (making cheese).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd contest that a well put together meal might be a social bonus similar to nice clothes (ninja'd), and that some recipes could require a Skill roll. \u263a<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not sure if one would want to explore the Fragile or Volitile tags/Conditions for Jury-Rigging a meal...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Ninja'd 10-03-2018, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T11:00:46-07:00","id":1258755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1258727#post1258727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd contest that a well put together meal might be a social bonus similar to nice clothes (ninja'd), and that some recipes could require a Skill roll. \u263a<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not sure if one would want to explore the Fragile or Volitile tags/Conditions for Jury-Rigging a meal...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Thus, \u201cmost circumstances.\u201d As usual, CofD encourages you to be flexible about the rules when it suits your story and come up with your own ideas. We can\u2019t include literally every possible example in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T13:51:05-08:00","id":1264790,"title":"","content":"Small question; potentially simple:<br /> <br /> What happens to an otherwise mortal child born in Faerie? In the Hedge? Would the location of conception matter?<br /> <br /> Speculative answers welcomed if books do not directly comment.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T13:55:51-08:00","id":1264791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1264790#post1264790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small question; potentially simple:<br /> <br /> What happens to an otherwise mortal child born in Faerie? In the Hedge? Would the location of conception matter?<br /> <br /> Speculative answers welcomed if books do not directly comment.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the old rules, you needed an strong connection aka memories in order to get back to the mortal world. So newborns were trapped forever.<br /> No idea if that still applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T19:48:08-08:00","id":1264860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1264790#post1264790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small question; potentially simple:<br /> <br /> What happens to an otherwise mortal child born in Faerie? In the Hedge? Would the location of conception matter?<br /> <br /> Speculative answers welcomed if books do not directly comment.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd need Equinox Road to get a more solid answer, but by those rules, there's a gradiation of effect that would occur for the child based on time they were in the Hedge and just what had been eaten by the parent in the time they were there.<br /> <br /> Arcadia...changes some of those rules based on the rules that govern the Stranger and its' Domain(and Realm, should that apply), but by and large it's the same, just less of each needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T21:36:21-08:00","id":1264878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1264860#post1264860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd need Equinox Road to get a more solid answer, but by those rules, there's a gradiation of effect that would occur for the child based on time they were in the Hedge and just what had been eaten by the parent in the time they were there.<br /> <br /> Arcadia...changes some of those rules based on the rules that govern the Stranger and its' Domain(and Realm, should that apply), but by and large it's the same, just less of each needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks guys! So basically there is no inherent difference to origin, just a matter of associations and contamination--just as with other visitors?<br /> <br /> The child would presumably grow up as normally as the Keeper wished, then.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T23:16:39-08:00","id":1264892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1264878#post1264878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks guys! So basically there is no inherent difference to origin, just a matter of associations and contamination--just as with other visitors?<br /> <br /> The child would presumably grow up as normally as the Keeper wished, then.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is a difference, in that while things become mutable in the Hedge, they are hella mutable in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Also, it depends on if a Keeper gets to direct their life or if their presence merely affects it.<br /> <br /> The latter is unlikely, but not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T22:53:22-08:00","id":1265451,"title":"","content":"If a Fire themed Elemental Changeling has taken Lethal Mein and chosen for the lethal damage to come from small jets of flame from his knuckles, would you allow that to count as &quot;touching the element&quot; for the purposes of the Elemental's blessing? Would it count as &quot;purely elemental damage&quot; for the purposes of Elemental Warrior?<br /> <br /> Personally I'm tempted to just rule that it does for the former (and will continue to count for the latter) for the same reason Fire Benders in <i>Avatar: the Last Airbender</i> didn't have to be touching fire: it just looks silly for something like fire for the bender to have to grab a torch (or a Zippo).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I've been allowing the player to inflict the &quot;Burning&quot; tilt on the target on an exceptional success and having it deal an additional 1L/turn unless put out by a successful Dex+Athletics - Wyrd roll. Is this a balanced condition or does anyone have a better idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 11-08-2018, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T12:38:35-08:00","id":1265556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1265451#post1265451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Fire themed Elemental Changeling has taken Lethal Mein and chosen for the lethal damage to come from small jets of flame from his knuckles, would you allow that to count as &quot;touching the element&quot; for the purposes of the Elemental's blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't\u2013\u2013but I'd let him set objects aflame with his knuckles, and then let him use those growing flames he created to use the Elemental blessing. That way, he has easy (but not automatic) access to his blessing, but it takes a little bit of situational awareness and thought (&quot;What's flammable here? Am I willing to risk collateral damage?&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it count as &quot;purely elemental damage&quot; for the purposes of Elemental Warrior? </div> </div> </div>My gut says yes, but my head says &quot;not if other players are wanting to contribute in combat but are struggling to keep up.&quot; But if he uses Elemental Weapon or Hungry Leaping Flames? Definitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I've been allowing the player to inflict the &quot;Burning&quot; tilt on the target on an exceptional success and having it deal an additional 1L/turn unless put out by a successful Dex+Athletics - Wyrd roll. Is this a balanced condition or does anyone have a better idea? </div> </div> </div>Do you mean you're A) using a custom Burning Tilt (due to lack of access to the Hurt Locker) or that you're B) adding 1L to the Burning Tilt's damage (and a quicker escape clause)?<br /> <br /> A is fine (in my personal opinion), but not nearly as strong as the HL Burning Tilt, if your player is built to be &quot;the combat guy&quot; and is managing to fall behind somehow.<br /> <br /> In B's case, I'd say the Burning Tilt is strong enough as is; I'd use that, and use the Elemental's weapon modifier as the fire's heat level (or a minimum of 1 heat level, if the Elemental's weapon modifier is 0L)\u2013\u2013maybe allow further exceptional successes to amp up the heat level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22860-miirik","name":"Miirik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T15:16:20-08:00","id":1265595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miirik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1265556#post1265556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't\u2013\u2013but I'd let him set objects aflame with his knuckles, and then let him use those growing flames he created to use the Elemental blessing. That way, he has easy (but not automatic) access to his blessing, but it takes a little bit of situational awareness and thought (&quot;What's flammable here? Am I willing to risk collateral damage?&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, I'm just a little leery of him deciding to whip out a Bic or a Zippo and the silly image that creates. But I suppose I'll burn that bridge when I come to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My gut says yes, but my head says &quot;not if other players are wanting to contribute in combat but are struggling to keep up.&quot; But if he uses Elemental Weapon or Hungry Leaping Flames? Definitely. </div> </div> </div>Thankfully that's not a problem. The non-combat focused characters don't really expect to contribute significantly to combat, so it hasn't been a problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you mean you're A) using a custom Burning Tilt (due to lack of access to the Hurt Locker) or that you're B) adding 1L to the Burning Tilt's damage (and a quicker escape clause)?<br /> <br /> A is fine (in my personal opinion), but not nearly as strong as the HL Burning Tilt, if your player is built to be &quot;the combat guy&quot; and is managing to fall behind somehow.<br /> <br /> In B's case, I'd say the Burning Tilt is strong enough as is; I'd use that, and use the Elemental's weapon modifier as the fire's heat level (or a minimum of 1 heat level, if the Elemental's weapon modifier is 0L)\u2013\u2013maybe allow further exceptional successes to amp up the heat level? </div> </div> </div>I didn't even know that Hurt Locker <i>had</i> a Burning Tilt, thanks for letting me know! Definitely going to use that one from now on. I'll probably use your suggestion to take the weapon modifier as the heat level, but leave the minimum as heat level 0 since HL's burning tilt deals 1 + heat level damage each turn, it's already doing a minimum of one damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T07:47:48-08:00","id":1265821,"title":"","content":"Iron. We know the mechanical effects of it on Changelings and True Fae. But...<br /> <br /> 1. How sensitive are they to its presence? Could a Changeling or True Fae sense it much as werewolves smell silver? If so, would Changeling senses get dulled over time by the iron-rich environment of, um, Ironside?<br /> <br /> 2. It harms them, but does it affect them by touching it (nausea, hives, psychological aversions)? Or does the symbolic power of iron fade for Changelings in particular as the acclimate? <br /> <br /> 3. Are there Merits representing severe iron issues or the suppression of same?<br /> <br /> There were, I think, some 1e material about this, but it's unclear to me.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T10:52:56-08:00","id":1265872,"title":"","content":"Answering for second edition:<br /> <br /> 1. The fae have no special ability to sense the presence of iron. The environment is presumed not to be &quot;iron-rich&quot; in the modern day, as alloys conventionally thought of as their own material (i.e. steel) don't count.<br /> 2. Unspecified, except for hand-forged iron, which causes aggravated damage simply by touch. It would be reasonable to think that the touch of non-hand-forged iron might cause at least enough discomfort to recognize it for what it is.<br /> 3. No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T20:51:06-08:00","id":1266338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1265872#post1265872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answering for second edition:<br /> <br /> 1. The fae have no special ability to sense the presence of iron. The environment is presumed not to be &quot;iron-rich&quot; in the modern day, as alloys conventionally thought of as their own material (i.e. steel) don't count.<br /> 2. Unspecified, except for hand-forged iron, which causes aggravated damage simply by touch. It would be reasonable to think that the touch of non-hand-forged iron might cause at least enough discomfort to recognize it for what it is.<br /> 3. No.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, this is helpful: so basically iron showing up is a surprise unless it's obvious or actively assumed: e.g. you're in an iron-heavy environment, or dealing with a known iron-wielder. <br /> <br /> And sounds like there is literary license to describe the impact of iron without forcing characters to go through mechanical side-effects other than the damage. Cool.<br /> <br /> It's always good to sketch out the boundaries of design intent, with these things, thanks.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T07:46:17-08:00","id":1266411,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> there is <i>one</i> standout feature that might make changeling characters notice that they've touched iron. Iron ends all Contracts and fae magic without exception. Fae armour doesn't shield them, boosted Defense fail, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T12:47:18-08:00","id":1266475,"title":"","content":"So this has most likely been answered elsewhere but I can't find it<br /> <br /> I really like the dark eras contracts but how to I tell if they are royal or common and under which regalia <br /> <br /> My favorite is the contract of air and darkness but all of them are very cool and I would love to use them all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T14:16:19-08:00","id":1266494,"title":"","content":"The Changeling content in Dark Eras was written prior to an unanticipated shakeup in Changeling Second Edition development, where the developer left the project and declined to contribute her work to the final product. CTL 2e was then re-developed by a new pair of developers who contributed their own work, which did not take all of the same tacks as the previous working draft.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this leaves the Dark Eras content in an awkward limbo, having been written for an edition of the game that was never finished or published. The Contracts, then, are not under any Regalia because Regalia was a new idea brought in by the developers of the finalized Second Edition. It probably shouldn't be hard to assign the Contracts to Regalia using the rule of thumb on CTL 2e p. 127. (For example, the Contract of Air and Darkness is a good candidate for the Jewels, because its primary function is manipulation.) As a vague rule of thumb, look at one to three dot Contracts to become Common Contracts, and four or five dot Contracts to become Royal, but salt to taste.<br /> <br /> Some material will be harder to adapt, as some of these mechanics reference rules that do not exist in the finalized Second Edition, and Second Edition doesn't have dot ratings for Contracts. You might have to, for example, implement Air and Darkness as a Royal Contract of Jewels which gets to pick one of the dot-level effects for free, and which can take a die penalty to its roll for each effect used after the first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:23:20-08:00","id":1266503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1266411#post1266411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> there is <i>one</i> standout feature that might make changeling characters notice that they've touched iron. Iron ends all Contracts and fae magic without exception. Fae armour doesn't shield them, boosted Defense fail, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of the reasons Huntsmen are so damn scary is that they aren\u00b4t vulnerable to iron at all. In fact, they have no problem using it to neutralize and shackle changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:15:37-08:00","id":1266520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1266494#post1266494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changeling content in Dark Eras was written prior to an unanticipated shakeup in Changeling Second Edition development, where the developer left the project and declined to contribute her work to the final product. CTL 2e was then re-developed by a new pair of developers who contributed their own work, which did not take all of the same tacks as the previous working draft.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this leaves the Dark Eras content in an awkward limbo, having been written for an edition of the game that was never finished or published. The Contracts, then, are not under any Regalia because Regalia was a new idea brought in by the developers of the finalized Second Edition. It probably shouldn't be hard to assign the Contracts to Regalia using the rule of thumb on CTL 2e p. 127. (For example, the Contract of Air and Darkness is a good candidate for the Jewels, because its primary function is manipulation.) As a vague rule of thumb, look at one to three dot Contracts to become Common Contracts, and four or five dot Contracts to become Royal, but salt to taste.<br /> <br /> Some material will be harder to adapt, as some of these mechanics reference rules that do not exist in the finalized Second Edition, and Second Edition doesn't have dot ratings for Contracts. You might have to, for example, implement Air and Darkness as a Royal Contract of Jewels which gets to pick one of the dot-level effects for free, and which can take a die penalty to its roll for each effect used after the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the explanation.<br /> Does anyone know if there's any thought on an edit or patch in the future?<br /> <br /> My instinct is to make them all royal contracts.<br /> The contract of inspiration may be a common but I would change the yards affected to be wyrd x 10<br /> The contract of abjuration would keep all of its powers but the exceptional success would allow for shattered illusions instead of steadfast condition<br /> <br /> I love the contract of air and darkness I really would like to keep it as strong as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T18:20:12-08:00","id":1266559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1266520#post1266520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if there's any thought on an edit or patch in the future?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> As far as we know, OPP has no plans to officially update the older &quot;CtL2e&quot; material to the final 2e rules, or any of the 1e content in Dark Eras 1 or its Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T10:04:13-08:00","id":1267337,"title":"","content":"Are there any official rules or suggestions on the sort of powers even 5-dot Tokens don't usually possess? I mean, not in terms of raw power, but in terms of... i dunno... no direct damage buffs, no instant death, no polymorphing people unwillingly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T10:11:37-08:00","id":1267341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1267337#post1267337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any official rules or suggestions on the sort of powers even 5-dot Tokens don't usually possess? I mean, not in terms of raw power, but in terms of... i dunno... no direct damage buffs, no instant death, no polymorphing people unwillingly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the last stretch goal the Kickstarter got to was &quot;there'll be a section on tokens in the Companion,&quot; I'm pretty confident there <i>will</i> be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T15:43:49-08:00","id":1267434,"title":"","content":"Yep, the Companion will contain a section on how to design custom tokens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T02:17:26-08:00","id":1267523,"title":"","content":"Will Entitlements return? I was very found of Scarecrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:43:34-08:00","id":1267558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1267523#post1267523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Entitlements return? I was very found of Scarecrows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/changeling-the-lost-2nd-edition\" target=\"_blank\">stretch goal put it in the Companion</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:53:09-08:00","id":1267586,"title":"","content":"don't know if it's been answered already, but will kiths still be usable? I really want my first try at changeling to be with a ogre troll","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T09:25:54-08:00","id":1267594,"title":"","content":"Kiths are getting a major mechanical overhaul in their structure, becoming much more standardized and powerful, so you probably cant use 1E kiths unmodified. <br /> <br /> However, we are getting a new sourcebook just for new and updated Kiths after the Changeling corebook comes out, which will include rules and advice for making your own kiths and updating 1e kiths on your own. I believe its called Kith &amp; Kin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T09:34:55-08:00","id":1267596,"title":"","content":"that's very good to hear. while I doubt all kiths will be getting an official update, it's nice to hear they care about allowing the resources to update ones we want to<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> what do you mean by standardize exactly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 11-15-2018, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:26:07-08:00","id":1267610,"title":"","content":"Here's how the kiths seem to be standardized from the ones I've seen each with two specific types of benefits, one of each type:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1223967#post1223967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Skill Trick</u></b>: a way of using a certain Skill or Skills which the character is supernaturally good at, giving them an exceptional success on three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Trickery</u></b>: an overtly supernatural trick that costs a single Glamour per use. Should relate to the same overall concept, but generally not provide an advantage for the same action the skill trick covers.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:36:20-08:00","id":1267614,"title":"","content":"so it's kinda like giving a specialty? like a troll would only need 3 successes on social rolls like manipulation and subterfuge while a gargantuan would have good strength?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:58:53-08:00","id":1267622,"title":"","content":"Its a specialty, but not a Specialty as in the thing that adds a die to certain skill rolls.<br /> <br /> Also, it should be more focused than just extra strong or extra manipulative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here, why don't you take a look at this thread for examples<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew\"> [2E] Kith Conversion (Homebrew) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This is the first draft of my guide to kith creation. I hope that it will prove useful to someone. White Oak Dragon&rsquo;s Unofficial Guide to Kith Creation </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:57:14-08:00","id":1267641,"title":"","content":"thanks for the link man, and for dealing with my dumb questions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T23:29:09-08:00","id":1271712,"title":"","content":"The Fae Mount ability Actormask says it disguises the Fae Mount as a vehicle in the mortal world, but Fae Mounts are <i>significantly</i> slower than real world vehicles, even if the Mount has Manyleague.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm just treating it as a typical example of a vehicle of its type in the mortal world, but I'm curious what everyone else does or if we know designer intent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T07:54:45-08:00","id":1274362,"title":"","content":"Since &quot;all rules governing Mask apply&quot; to Trivial Reworking, am I correct in assuming that a changeling strengthening their Mask would also affect their target of this contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T19:47:41-08:00","id":1275224,"title":"","content":"In second edition when a changeling uses Chrysalis to transform into a creature with more health than the changeling, like an elephant for example, and takes damage in that form what happens when they transform back? Say the changeling has 8 health in normal form and 16 in animal. If the animal form takes 16 lethal damage and then the changeling transforms back would they have 16 lethal, and thus 8 aggravated damage with rollover, or would the 8 extra lethal disappear leaving the changeling form with 8 lethal marked, or would the base form have no damage marked at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T20:40:59-08:00","id":1275229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1275224#post1275224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In second edition when a changeling uses Chrysalis to transform into a creature with more health than the changeling, like an elephant for example, and takes damage in that form what happens when they transform back? Say the changeling has 8 health in normal form and 16 in animal. If the animal form takes 16 lethal damage and then the changeling transforms back would they have 16 lethal, and thus 8 aggravated damage with rollover, or would the 8 extra lethal disappear leaving the changeling form with 8 lethal marked, or would the base form have no damage marked at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of specific statement otherwise, I'd assume the 1e rule of &quot;damage persists even when temporary Health goes away&quot; holds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T12:00:00-08:00","id":1276100,"title":"","content":"Pathfinder (pg 144-145) : &quot;Effects: The changeling mingles some of his spit or blood with earth from the Hedge, and uses the mixture to draw a compass on his hand. He instinctively knows the distance and the direction of the nearest general Hedge feature of his choice \u2014 the nearest Goblin Market or Hollow, a patch of goblin fruit, or an entrance to Gthe ate of Horn, for instance. The Contract only reveals information about the Hedge itself, not about creatures lurking within.&quot;<br /> <br /> Good...but: stats wise... how it help?<br /> <br /> At page 200 is &quot; To do anything other than wander aimlessly, charactersmust make navigation rolls inside the Hedge. They begin by stating a goal, which could be a specific location\u2014 \u201cI want to take a shortcut to San Francisco\u201d or \u201cI want to find the nearest Goblin Market\u201d \u2014 or a more general objective, like \u201cI want to find an Icon\u201d or \u201cI want to get away from this loyalist.\u201d<br /> Navigation inside the Hedge works just like a chase, using the rules on p. 195. Even if the characters are unopposed, the Hedge itself works as an \u201copponent,\u201d representing the myriad dangers and temptations that face all travelers there.<br /> The characters must engage in a new chase whenever they have a new goal.<br /> <br /> Any hints?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 12-22-2018, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T01:15:50-08:00","id":1276192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1276100#post1276100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good...but: stats wise... how it help?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably use it as gaining the modifier &quot;Your character knows the territory intimately (-3)&quot; (CtL2e, p. 196)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T02:57:34-08:00","id":1276203,"title":"","content":"Excellent! Thanks You!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T08:29:31-08:00","id":1276798,"title":"","content":"Does permakilling a Huntsmen with their own Arcadian Weapons destroy the Title they have been controlled with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T14:43:21-08:00","id":1276875,"title":"","content":"I don't think Arcadian Weapons are a thing anymore, instead you have to locate the Huntsman's heart in a dream bastion and destroy it. They're a lot like liches that way.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly confident it does not destroy the Title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T17:50:08-08:00","id":1276905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1276875#post1276875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Arcadian Weapons are a thing anymore, instead you have to locate the Huntsman's heart in a dream bastion and destroy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each of the Huntsmen has a panoply that serves as part of its core identity \u2014 it has 8-Again on all relevant rolls with its tools and regains Willpower on every exceptional success with them, in addition to being able to recall them to its person with a point of Glamour and an instant action. Whatever the role Arcadian weapons fulfilled in 1.5, the Hunter's Panoply doesn't serve the same purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T14:33:21-08:00","id":1277082,"title":"","content":"Nevermind - found the answer to my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 12-27-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T11:43:52-08:00","id":1277236,"title":"","content":"Do Corgis have Anything to do with the True Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T12:37:14-08:00","id":1277241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1277236#post1277236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Corgis have Anything to do with the True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not officially.<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2952\" target=\"_blank\">This an SCP reference?</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:26:12-08:00","id":1277258,"title":"","content":"No But the SCP 2952 is a referenced to a welsh legend that Faeries rode Corgis as there battle steeds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:33:53-08:00","id":1277259,"title":"","content":"Was that a legend or an old joke?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:41:22-08:00","id":1277261,"title":"","content":"IDK <a href=\"https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/home/did-fairies-really-ride-corgis\" target=\"_blank\">https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/...ly-ride-corgis</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:48:59-08:00","id":1277265,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s actually quite a recent one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/home/did-fairies-really-ride-corgis\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://writinginmargins.weebly.com/uploads/4/7/0/0/47004293/published/846780908.JPG?1526916731\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/home/did-fairies-really-ride-corgis\" target=\"_blank\"> Did fairies really ride corgis? </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/home/did-fairies-really-ride-corgis\" target=\"_blank\"> https://writinginmargins.weebly.com/home/did-fairies-really-ride-corgis </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In Welsh legend, corgis were once the steeds of the fairy folk. \u200bYou can still see the faint markings of the fairy saddles across the Pembroke Welsh Corgi's shoulders and back... or so I've heard.... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T12:10:41-08:00","id":1278118,"title":"","content":"Trying to parse down the character creation rules and possibly a dumb question but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CtL2e p. 94<br /> <br /> &quot;Each character starts with four Contracts from Common Regalia, Common Court, or Goblin Contracts, at least two of which must be in favored Regalia. <b>Also choose two Royal Contracts from court or favored Regalia.</b>&quot; </div> </div> </div>...as in addition to the other four Contracts you picked, bringing the total up to six? Or are the two Royal Contracts part of the initial four you select?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T13:20:45-08:00","id":1278130,"title":"","content":"The way I parsed it, you have a total of 6 contracts. Four Common, Two Royal. Quite the power boost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T15:46:08-08:00","id":1278184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1278130#post1278130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I parsed it, you have a total of 6 contracts. Four Common, Two Royal. Quite the power boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct - four Common, two Royal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T11:18:29-08:00","id":1279261,"title":"","content":"Questions regarding &quot;cold iron&quot; --<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Page 102 - So-called \u201ccold iron\u201d acts as a frailty bane for changelings<br /> and True Fae. To qualify as \u201ccold iron,\u201d the metal<br /> must be mostly pure iron and magic cannot play a role<br /> in its creation in any way. It must be hand-forged, not<br /> mass-produced, cast, or created by a machine. Touching<br /> this iron inflicts aggravated damage on the Gentry and<br /> changelings. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Question 1: If Iron acts as bane (as defined several paragraphs earlier) for changelings, what severity is it? (I assume that since it inflicts Aggravated damage, that it is considered a major frailty.)<br /> <br /> Question 2: If it is considered a frailty as defined in the corebook, does it share all the same traits as a major frailty? IE: Willpower expenditure needed to act against cold iron? -5 penalty to all rolls when acting against it? unable to heal wounds inflicted by the weapon as long as they are in presence of the bane that damaged them? etc etc<br /> <br /> Question 3: Does intent matter when it comes to using Cold Iron as a weapon in terms of the vague term &quot;acting against&quot;? For ex: If August Montalvo, Summer Court thug, has a cold iron spike embedded into a baseball bat to use as a weapon in an upcoming conflict ... would his fairy enemies have to spend a Willpower point per turn to stand against him? And if they decided to spend the willpower, would their attacks against August suffer a -5 penalty?<br /> <br /> Or does intent not matter to Cold Iron? Is it automatically considered to be &quot;working&quot; against all things of Faerie whether or not it is being handled? In the above example, if August were to try and wield the aforementioned spike studded baseball bat, would he and his allies suffer the negative effects of being in the presence of Cold iron as well?<br /> <br /> If intent does matter, could the abjuring aura of Iron be used to hinder changelings even if the Iron-wielder isn't around? Like ... if I pound a cold iron spike into the wood of my front door, because of a superstition says that doing so will protect my home from fairies, would changelings suffer the bane's effects when trying to break in or scry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":".  spelling 01-07-2019, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T19:29:58-08:00","id":1280813,"title":"","content":"I guess the question was not simple enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T05:06:52-08:00","id":1280878,"title":"","content":"Damage wise I'd rule it as similar to silver for werewolves. Bashing (or lethal in some circumstances) from touching it, Agg if it is being used to harm. I would probably not give it a willpower to act against it as cold iron lacks intent. It is the antithesis of the fae and isn't bound by wordings and intents. It is painfully real and the epitome of cause and effect and it flat out cancels any fae magic it contacts. In regards to the area of effect of the cold iron in the door example I think it is largely up to the GM discretion. A changeling couldn't use magic against the door itself and would probably hurt themselves if they touched the iron directly, but it becomes a grey area if they want to break a window with a nearby rock and sneak in that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24608-dom2772","name":"Dom2772","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T01:14:05-08:00","id":1281059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1279261#post1279261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions regarding &quot;cold iron&quot; --<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Question 1: If Iron acts as bane (as defined several paragraphs earlier) for changelings, what severity is it? (I assume that since it inflicts Aggravated damage, that it is considered a major frailty.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Major frailty, so Aggravated Damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 2: If it is considered a frailty as defined in the corebook, does it share all the same traits as a major frailty? IE: Willpower expenditure needed to act against cold iron? -5 penalty to all rolls when acting against it? unable to heal wounds inflicted by the weapon as long as they are in presence of the bane that damaged them? etc etc </div> </div> </div>That's my reading, yes. Though, in many ways it's even stronger than that, as no faerie magic can affect any sort of iron (&quot;cold&quot; or otherwise).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 3: Does intent matter when it comes to using Cold Iron as a weapon in terms of the vague term &quot;acting against&quot;? For ex: If August Montalvo, Summer Court thug, has a cold iron spike embedded into a baseball bat to use as a weapon in an upcoming conflict ... would his fairy enemies have to spend a Willpower point per turn to stand against him? And if they decided to spend the willpower, would their attacks against August suffer a -5 penalty? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Acting against&quot; is &quot;acting against.&quot; If the Faerie wanted to attack the cold iron spike they'd have to spend the willpower and take the penalty, but attacking August wouldn't trigger that. And, again, the Faerie would be unable to use any Contracts or other powers against the cold iron spike, Willpower expenditure or no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or does intent not matter to Cold Iron? Is it automatically considered to be &quot;working&quot; against all things of Faerie whether or not it is being handled? In the above example, if August were to try and wield the aforementioned spike studded baseball bat, would he and his allies suffer the negative effects of being in the presence of Cold iron as well?<br /> <br /> <br /> If intent does matter, could the abjuring aura of Iron be used to hinder changelings even if the Iron-wielder isn't around? Like ... if I pound a cold iron spike into the wood of my front door, because of a superstition says that doing so will protect my home from fairies, would changelings suffer the bane's effects when trying to break in or scry? </div> </div> </div>It's not kryptonite. If you wanted to protect against scrying it'd have to be fully covered in iron, though it wouldn't have to be &quot;cold&quot; iron to block magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:03:03-08:00","id":1281122,"title":"","content":"Are there any kiths whose Trickery power does not require an activation roll or do the kith creation rules explicitly say that is a feature of all Trickeries?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:07:45-08:00","id":1281123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281122#post1281122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any kiths whose Trickery power does not require an activation roll or do the kith creation rules explicitly say that is a feature of all Trickeries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Build-a-Kith rules specifically say that it requires a &quot;conscious effort&quot; in order to use them. It does say that it only &quot;most commonly&quot; requires spending a Glamour point and using an Attribute + Skill roll,, if for some reason you wanted the Trickery to be activated by other means you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:34:54-08:00","id":1281127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281059#post1281059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Acting against&quot; is &quot;acting against.&quot; If the Faerie wanted to attack the cold iron spike they'd have to spend the willpower and take the penalty, but attacking August wouldn't trigger that. And, again, the Faerie would be unable to use any Contracts or other powers against the cold iron spike, Willpower expenditure or no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks so much for your answers. Got me thinking ...<br /> <br /> While I see the point of this, thematically, it doesn't seem really to jive with the idea of supernatural banes as described in folklore ... and also there is this passage from the text, page 102 under the Frailties heading ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even acting<br /> against the<i><b> source of a bane</b></i> is difficult: Doing so requires<br /> spending a point of Willpower per action, which does not<br /> add dice to the pool. Additionally, the character suffers<br /> a three-die <i><b>penalty on all rolls related to acting against<br /> the cause</b></i> of a minor frailty. This penalty increases to \u22125<br /> when acting against a major frailty. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Major banes<br /> are common substances or situations, and rapidly prove<br /> fatal to the changeling if touched or experienced. Examples<br /> include an inability to go outside while the moon<br /> (or sun) is in the sky, being forced to walk backwards<br /> or hop at all times, the sound of a child\u2019s laughter, or<br /> touching glass. </div> </div> </div>So, in this case ... let's say that the sound of Child's laughter is the Major Bane. The bolded wording in my above quote states that *acting* against the <i>source</i>of the frailty imparts a penalty. In example regarding children's laughter ... by using your interpretation, acting against the child (the source of the laughter) wouldn't be penalized because only actions taken against the substance of the bane (in this case the laughter) takes the hit. That really doesn't seem to jive with the feel of the game.<br /> <br /> What ya think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:57:32-08:00","id":1281226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281127#post1281127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks so much for your answers. Got me thinking ...<br /> <br /> While I see the point of this, thematically, it doesn't seem really to jive with the idea of supernatural banes as described in folklore ... and also there is this passage from the text, page 102 under the Frailties heading ...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, in this case ... let's say that the sound of Child's laughter is the Major Bane. The bolded wording in my above quote states that *acting* against the <i>source</i>of the frailty imparts a penalty. In example regarding children's laughter ... by using your interpretation, acting against the child (the source of the laughter) wouldn't be penalized because only actions taken against the substance of the bane (in this case the laughter) takes the hit. That really doesn't seem to jive with the feel of the game.<br /> <br /> What ya think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of faeries as a whole being loophole abusing assholes about things. &quot;The sound of a child's laughter&quot; and &quot;a child laughing&quot; should be significantly different: the former could be recorded; the latter doesn't even need to be heard, simply be present.<br /> <br /> And yes, in my opinion, the faerie could act against the source of the laughter unimpeded (in the case of the former), but would require the willpower expenditure to say, create a magical silence effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T13:23:22-08:00","id":1281357,"title":"","content":"So, to be clear, when a Title is empowering a huntsman, it's unavailable for the True Fae to manifest in, right? <br /> <br /> Could make life tricky for single-title keepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T16:56:26-08:00","id":1281394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281357#post1281357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to be clear, when a Title is empowering a huntsman, it's unavailable for the True Fae to manifest in, right?<br /> <br /> Could make life tricky for single-title keepers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Keeper empowers a huntsman by imbueing its heart with their Title. The Keeper's Title still belongs to the Fairy who controls the Huntsman, which allows the verderer to access some unique abilities that it wouldn't normally have access to. If the empowering Title is the only one that the fairy lays claim to, it can manifest through its Name. In a way, this is a great way to hide for a down on their luck fairy looking to defend themselves from their Arcadian Rivals. The Title is buried in a Huntsman heart, that is in turn hidden in some rando's dreams. In order to strip that Title, a rival first has to find the Huntsman in the real world and kill it so that the Title returns to its Keeper. If the said Impecunious Fairy wanted a good insurance plan against dissolution, it could train a changeling champion that is unusually suited to evading capture and then let the changeling &quot;escape&quot; so it can set a Huntsman after the &quot;wayward&quot; Lost. Of course, the Durance of this changeling should be particularly nightmarish to ensure that they would want to escape in the first place. ..<br /> <br /> But this sorta long game makes a lot of sense, in an insane way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T17:29:24-08:00","id":1281404,"title":"","content":"Yeah, except reading through again I realised that a keeper is now a <i>specific</i> title (they need an aspiration about being a keeper), and the huntsman section refers to the huntsman &quot;wear[ing] the livery of [their] queen&quot; which sounds like it's the same title that manifests as the keeper. <br /> <br /> So now I'm still confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T17:52:43-08:00","id":1281412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281404#post1281404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, except reading through again I realised that a keeper is now a <i>specific</i> title (they need an aspiration about being a keeper), and the huntsman section refers to the huntsman &quot;wear[ing] the livery of [their] queen&quot; which sounds like it's the same title that manifests as the keeper.<br /> <br /> So now I'm still confused.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not sure what you are confused about. A True Fae is a Name (the core of their being) wrapped in a number of Titles (from one to five). A Fairy can manifest its will through these Titles, with each one offering them nigh infinite power within a very specific poetic purview and possess a panoply of regalia as vessels of their dominion. Each Title has its own Aspirations, one of which may be &quot;Keep changelings and make their life hell for the lulz.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the embodiment of a particular Title in a fairy's portfolio doesn't *have* to be a person. The Title can manifest as a realm, or thing, or a pack of dogs with too-human eyes.<br /> <br /> The fairy's Name is aware of all the things going on in the &quot;lives&quot; of their Titles. If one of their changelings escape, the guiding intelligence of the fairy (it's Name), can decide to get the slave back by temporarily empowering a verderer with the specific Title that has the &quot;Keeper&quot; Aspiration. While the Huntsman is off Ironside hunting down the escaped Changeling, the fairy has to rely upon embodiment through their other Titles or (if they are desperate) their Name. The Title still belongs to the Fairy and it informs the desires of the Huntsman<br /> <br /> From what I can tell, there is nothing in 2e elaborating on the form that the Name takes when it is forced to become embodied. In First Edition;s &quot;Equinox Roads&quot; there was a whole section detailing the minutiae of fairy life in Arcadia, and how they constantly struggle and fight against each other not because they hate each other, but because they need conflict in order to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 01-17-2019, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T18:12:47-08:00","id":1281417,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm probably overthinking it. <br /> <br /> It was mostly situations where the keeper would need to be both in arcadia (like, if they had other changelings) and empowering a huntsman. But you could say that a Name can manifest as any of it's titles if it needs to or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T19:06:00-08:00","id":1281425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281417#post1281417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm probably overthinking it.<br /> <br /> It was mostly situations where the keeper would need to be both in arcadia (like, if they had other changelings) and empowering a huntsman. But you could say that a Name can manifest as any of it's titles if it needs to or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm feeling you. One of my criticisms of the book in general is how the overwrought nature of the prose can distract certain readers (like me) from properly grokking the rules. <br /> <br /> But yes, you are correct. The Name can Manifest as it any of its Titles whenever they like (unless, of course, the nature of the Title prevents it from doing so unless under special circumstances), even simultaneously. <br /> <br /> For Example: The Keeper known as the Smiling Lord rules over an unending bacchanal deep in The Bleeding Woods that hosts a diverse array of monsters, both beautiful and grotesque, united by their lustful appetites, their dedication to revelry and their inability to say goodbye. Fairy Lords from across Arcadia visit for a chance to win the favor of his twin daughters, Weeping Ingenue and Secret Coquette, who are alike only in their shared hatred of their father. While at first charmed by the rampant hedonism on display, changelings made captive for entertainment or drudgery rapidly grow to despise the party and many make plans to leave. Sometimes, an exceptional changeling manages to actually escape ... <br /> <br /> So, although it seems like there three different fairy lords here ... in truth, there is only one of the True Fae. The True Fae in the above example is manifesting itself, simultaneously, through four different Titles: The Smiling Lord, The Bleeding Woods, the Weeping Ingenue and Secret Coquette. Only one of them, the Smiling Lord, has the Keeper Aspiration ... so when it comes time to send out a Huntsman to bring back a changeling, the Smiling Lord &quot;leaves&quot; his unending party and the True Fae then stuffs that Title into the heart of a verderer. The Huntsman then takes on the Tell of the Title (a permenant wide, mirthful smile) and two Aspirations inspired by the animating Title (The Keeper Aspiration and the Craving Aspiration). While the Huntsman is off in the mortal world tracking down the lost changeling, the True Fae's will is still embodied by the Weeping Ingenue, Secret Coquette and the Bleeding Woods. <br /> <br /> does that help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 01-17-2019, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T22:05:38-08:00","id":1281452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281357#post1281357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to be clear, when a Title is empowering a huntsman, it's unavailable for the True Fae to manifest in, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>To all available evidence, no \u2014 the description of what happens when a Huntsman dies frames the Title as returning to a still-extant actor, and the Gentry's section describes them as sufficiently boundless that it's not difficult to imagine a Keeper's Title serving as both the principal and the source of its Huntsman agent's power, motifs, and agenda.<br /> <br /> The imposition is more like that of a vampire and ghoul than a body-thief and its host save for the implicit limit of one-Huntsman-at-a-time; the Keeper is staking its Title on the verderer's success, not outright possessing it through the shared desire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could make life tricky for single-title keepers. </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, if we're drawing from Equinox Roads, most Fae have at least two Titles and having less than that is generally dire straits regardless of what it hopes to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T02:09:28-08:00","id":1281760,"title":"","content":"Does a True Fae receive 1 free dot in each Attribute before assigning (Wyrd*5) dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T03:10:29-08:00","id":1281763,"title":"","content":"Browsing the new core book, I discovered that the old contract of Fang and Talon ability &quot;<b>Tongues of Birds and Words of Wolves</b>&quot; apparently did not make it over, was this an oversight? Pretty much any supernatural being has a low level power to speak with animals, so why don't Changelings anymore?<br /> Of course you can go straight to Pipes of the Beast Caller, but that seems a bit odd honestly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T05:19:49-08:00","id":1281765,"title":"","content":"My partner and I seem to have different interpretations of Whispers of Morning, so I'm hoping someone here can help. Does it make the changeling invisible as well as intangible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T06:02:42-08:00","id":1281769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281765#post1281765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My partner and I seem to have different interpretations of Whispers of Morning, so I'm hoping someone here can help. Does it make the changeling invisible as well as intangible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no, the changeling does not become invisible. Compare with the Helldiver's Kith Blessing, where it is stated that he fades &quot;into an incorporeal, invisible form&quot;. Light-Shy is the Contract allowing a changeling to become invisible to the mind (but not to recording devices unless the changeling invokes the Darkling benefit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T06:47:02-08:00","id":1281775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281765#post1281765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My partner and I seem to have different interpretations of Whispers of Morning, so I'm hoping someone here can help. Does it make the changeling invisible as well as intangible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enmai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281769#post1281769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no, the changeling does not become invisible. Compare with the Helldiver's Kith Blessing, where it is stated that he fades &quot;into an incorporeal, invisible form&quot;. Light-Shy is the Contract allowing a changeling to become invisible to the mind (but not to recording devices unless the changeling invokes the Darkling benefit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Light-Shy is a Common Contract of Jewels, whereas Whispers of Morning is a Royal Contract of the Shield that specifically references the intangibility of Hedge ghosts, which itself references the Dematerialize Numen, whose first effect-based descriptive phrase is &quot;the Hedge ghost fades from sight.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T07:23:46-08:00","id":1281777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281765#post1281765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My partner and I seem to have different interpretations of Whispers of Morning, so I'm hoping someone here can help. Does it make the changeling invisible as well as intangible?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281775#post1281775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light-Shy is a Common Contract of Jewels, whereas Whispers of Morning is a Royal Contract of the Shield that specifically references the intangibility of Hedge ghosts, which itself references the Dematerialize Numen, whose first effect-based descriptive phrase is &quot;the Hedge ghost fades from sight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The reference to Hedge Ghosts is in the description of the interaction between them and Whispers of Morning using changelings; not a direct reference to how Whispers of Morning works. There's not a single mention of Whispers of Morning hiding the user in addition to them becoming intangible. If invisibility was part of the effect Whispers of Morning would definitely have been a Jewel Contract since that's the Regalia that deals with outright invisibility (in addition to general ephemeral-ness).<br /> <br /> Invisibility (or at least a penalty to being seen) would be a great Darkling benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T07:52:12-08:00","id":1281780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281777#post1281777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If invisibility was part of the effect Whispers of Morning would definitely have been a Jewel Contract since that's the Regalia that deals with outright invisibility (in addition to general ephemeral-ness).</div> </div> </div> </div>The literal first Shield Contract in the book is a stealth-booster, with a &quot;hide this portal&quot; effect not much further down the list; neither of these needs the added justification of being a more powerful class of Contract for hiding to fall within the sphere of Shields.<br /> <br /> Regalia are not prescriptive sorting mechanisms, non-Goblin Contracts can specifically have multiple effects folded into one, and the nearest equivalent effect in both 1e and Underhill specifically references Twilight as an analogous state just as Whispers of Morning does. Which is more likely: that a Royal Contract which makes you intangible lets you see other things with the same type of intangibility (including other users of the Contract itself) for no real reason, or because the type of intangibility it grants normally comes with invisibility?<br /> <br /> The description uses &quot;cloak&quot; and &quot;forget&quot; as the operative verbs. What about that suggests people can still see you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T22:23:12-08:00","id":1281876,"title":"","content":"Those are basically the same considerations we came up with for and against invisibility. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> any chance you could clear this up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T00:50:03-08:00","id":1281894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281876#post1281876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are basically the same considerations we came up with for and against invisibility. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a> any chance you could clear this up?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make you invisible. I agree that it would make a good Darkling effect! It's Shield because the most obvious use of this power is to avoid getting hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T00:58:18-08:00","id":1281897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1281894#post1281894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't make you invisible. I agree that it would make a good Darkling effect! It's Shield because the most obvious use of this power is to avoid getting hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for clearing it up! We're loving the 2E book so far, and looking forward to starting up a game using it soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T19:43:22-08:00","id":1282373,"title":"","content":"Are there any limits on the choice of Tilts for Elemental Fury (aside from the ST being reasonable and saying &quot;no, you can't make a horde of zombies by screaming really loudly&quot;)? Normally I'm all for &quot;the ST is a reasonable arbiter&quot; but if there was ever a place for loophole abuse, it's Contract wording\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T23:10:57-08:00","id":1282391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282373#post1282373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any limits on the choice of Tilts for Elemental Fury (aside from the ST being reasonable and saying &quot;no, you can't make a horde of zombies by screaming really loudly&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The ones included in the book the Contract is printed in&quot; passes the basic sanity-check as readily as any other sensible application of &quot;don't expect every book to take every other possible book into account in an edition where the baseline system rules no longer require reference to a separate corebook as long as you have the starter book for the gameline.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but if there was ever a place for loophole abuse, it's Contract wording\u2026 </div> </div> </div>This has never been a very good joke, much less a serious interpretive standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T08:31:38-08:00","id":1282437,"title":"","content":"1. Are Changelings always originally humans or can they originate from animals or objects through some weirdness that become self aware?<br /> 2. Just in general, do/would a fae take an animal into the Hedge and would it likely affect it in a manner?<br /> <br /> Friend was asking and I know little about this splat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T08:46:13-08:00","id":1282439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282437#post1282437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are Changelings always originally humans or can they originate from animals or objects through some weirdness that become self aware?<br /> 2. Just in general, do/would a fae take an animal into the Hedge and would it likely affect it in a manner?<br /> <br /> Friend was asking and I know little about this splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook assumes that all changelings begin as humans. Objects taken into the Hedge or Arcadia usually turn into Tokens, while mortal animals left in the Hedge, if they survive, transform into hobgoblins (in first edition anyway; I don't recall seeing anything in the second edition rules on the subject).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T08:49:05-08:00","id":1282440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282437#post1282437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are Changelings always originally humans or can they originate from animals or objects through some weirdness that become self aware?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer: Yes, changelings are always humans. Animals and objects can be come &quot;self-aware&quot; through exposure to the Wyrd, but they become either Hobgoblins (for animals) or Tokens (objects).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282437#post1282437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2. Just in general, do/would a fae take an animal into the Hedge and would it likely affect it in a manner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer: It depends on the fairy, I guess. Hobgoblins, True Fae and Changelings often leave objects in the Hedge for an extended period of time so they can become tokens. Plenty of hobgoblins are descended from animals that have found themselves in the Hedge for some reason or another. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T09:37:49-08:00","id":1282446,"title":"","content":"I'm slightly confused by the wording of Seeming benefits and Pupil's Devotion. Is it that a changeling can either pay 1 Experience to obtain the benefit of a different Seeming, or she gets it for free via Pupil's Devotion? Or does a changeling have to swear the Oath in order to purchase the benefit in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:12:25-08:00","id":1282490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282391#post1282391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has never been a very good joke, much less a serious interpretive standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree with that: as an ST, I'm absolutely open to players using loopholes in the book's wording of Contracts. The book outright encourages it in some places, such as the loophole for <i>Glimpse of a Distant Mirror</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:14:58-08:00","id":1282492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282446#post1282446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm slightly confused by the wording of Seeming benefits and Pupil's Devotion. Is it that a changeling can either pay 1 Experience to obtain the benefit of a different Seeming, or she gets it for free via Pupil's Devotion? Or does a changeling have to swear the Oath in order to purchase the benefit in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pupil's Devotion is &quot;a changeling can swear a personal oath with another changeling to receive up to two benefits for an Arcadian Contract that changeling knows: the teacher's cost-break for affinity Regalia may be applied to the changeling learning the Contract even if it's not part of their own favored Regalia, and the changeling may spend an additional Experience to learn the teacher's seeming benefit for that Contract.&quot;<br /> <br /> Out-of-seeming benefits are effectively a surcharge even on your favored Regalia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:17:47-08:00","id":1282493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282490#post1282490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd disagree with that: as an ST, I'm absolutely open to players using loopholes in the book's wording of Contracts. The book outright encourages it in some places, such as the loophole for <i>Glimpse of a Distant Mirror</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a world of difference between &quot;I stole this thing and am not claiming it belongs to me, so I can save a single point of Glamour on this spying Contract&quot; and &quot;The book doesn't say that flesh and blood aren't 'elements,' therefore this fairy-tale power to invoke storms and fire and earthquakes can summon zombies or pull a bonesword out of a bystander's arm.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:26:01-08:00","id":1282494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282492#post1282492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pupil's Devotion is &quot;a changeling can swear a personal oath with another changeling to receive up to two benefits for an Arcadian Contract that changeling knows: the teacher's cost-break for affinity Regalia may be applied to the changeling learning the Contract even if it's not part of their own favored Regalia, and the changeling may spend an additional Experience to learn the teacher's seeming benefit for that Contract.&quot;<br /> <br /> Out-of-seeming benefits are effectively a surcharge even on your favored Regalia.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is to say also that if a changeling wants a certain Seeming benefit, they have to swear Pupil's Devotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:52:14-08:00","id":1282507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282494#post1282494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is to say also that if a changeling wants a certain Seeming benefit, they have to swear Pupil's Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Similar to learning other clans' signature Disciplines in Vampire, branching into &quot;proprietary&quot; powers comes with a cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T15:14:25-08:00","id":1282525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282507#post1282507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Similar to learning other clans' signature Disciplines in Vampire, branching into &quot;proprietary&quot; powers comes with a cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Thank you for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T12:26:44-08:00","id":1282698,"title":"","content":"If a contract activation costs Willpower in addition to Glamour, does the Loophole cover the Willpower cost as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T13:02:37-08:00","id":1282703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1282698#post1282698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a contract activation costs Willpower in addition to Glamour, does the Loophole cover the Willpower cost as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>No it does not.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CtL2e p.127<br /> <br /> Every Contract has a Loophole that lets the changeling invoke the Contract\u2019s basic effect at no Glamour cost <i><b>(though he must pay Willpower costs, and any cost associated with seeming benefits, as normal).</b></i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T13:17:45-08:00","id":1282709,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Also, does the Loophole of Unravel The Tapestry apply to the upon-death activation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T14:32:40-08:00","id":1283124,"title":"","content":"Also, just checking. Everyone else agrees that the combo of it not being mentioned in their Mantle writeup and the presence of the Fair Harvest, joining a Court no longer gives you a 1 Glamour bonus to all successful Harvest rolls for a specific emotion, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:59:16-08:00","id":1283134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1283124#post1283124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, just checking. Everyone else agrees that the combo of it not being mentioned in their Mantle writeup and the presence of the Fair Harvest, joining a Court no longer gives you a 1 Glamour bonus to all successful Harvest rolls for a specific emotion, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It still is. <br /> <br /> \u201cHarvesting the emotion favored by the changeling\u2019s court grants an additional point of Glamour on a successful roll.\u201d<br /> Changeling: The Lost Second Edition, Page 103","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:10:41-08:00","id":1283137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1283134#post1283134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still is.<br /> <br /> \u201cHarvesting the emotion favored by the changeling\u2019s court grants an additional point of Glamour on a successful roll.\u201d<br /> Changeling: The Lost Second Edition, Page 103</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work with the non-Seasonal courts in the back of the book? I don't see any listed emotions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T17:02:13-08:00","id":1283144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1283137#post1283137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does that work with the non-Seasonal courts in the back of the book? I don't see any listed emotions</div> </div> </div> </div>You're supposed to extrapolate emotions for them, I believe; it looks like the ever dreaded Word Count has sidelined any emotions, merits, contracts or even some logistics on how these courts are supposed to work. I still can't wrap my head around how the Hong Kong courts are supposed to work as well as the Seasonal Courts in spite of lacking the Bargain other courts have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T17:13:21-08:00","id":1283147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1283137#post1283137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that work with the non-Seasonal courts in the back of the book? I don't see any listed emotions</div> </div> </div> </div>Contextual inference is your friend here and the dividing line for Courts that aren't literally built around their emotional anchors is, in practical terms, &quot;does this harvest reinforce the tone of the Court?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:04:18-08:00","id":1283151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1283147#post1283147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contextual inference is your friend here and the dividing line for Courts that aren't literally built around their emotional anchors is, in practical terms, &quot;does this harvest reinforce the tone of the Court?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Mind if I post my inferences on appropriate emotions or circumstances for each Court once i do a second readthrough, see how other people differ?<br /> <br /> EDIT: moods instead of circumstances, as Arcane suggested","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-27-2019, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:21:09-08:00","id":1283154,"title":"","content":"Courts may not have emotions, but they def always have moods, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T21:40:57-08:00","id":1283189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1283151#post1283151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind if I post my inferences on appropriate emotions or circumstances for each Court once i do a second readthrough, see how other people differ?<br /> <br /> EDIT: moods instead of circumstances, as Arcane suggested</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be wise to make a separate thread, between higher future usability and the nature of potential discussion on the topic feeling forum-game-adjacent, but certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T11:46:50-08:00","id":1285615,"title":"","content":"So, I noticed that Changeling: the Lost, 2ed is finally out (added it to my Wishlist), but when I clicked on the live preview, I was surprised and confused by what I saw in the table of contents.<br /> <br /> Namely that most of the stuff I was lead to believe would be featured in 2e seems to have been gutted from this book.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, I didn't see any mention of the Grimm Seeming we were expected to get, and there is an extremely limited amount of Kiths to go around. Most of which aren't even useful for combat!<br /> <br /> Anyways, onto my question:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - Does this book feature rules / guidelines for home brewing Kiths?<br /> <br /> 2 - Are there supplement materials for this book that I should probably look into purchasing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:09:12-08:00","id":1285621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285615#post1285615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I noticed that Changeling: the Lost, 2ed is finally out (added it to my Wishlist), but when I clicked on the live preview, I was surprised and confused by what I saw in the table of contents.<br /> <br /> Namely that most of the stuff I was lead to believe would be featured in 2e seems to have been gutted from this book.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, I didn't see any mention of the Grimm Seeming we were expected to get,</div> </div> </div> </div>This was actually discussed a week or so back <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282195#post1282195\">in this forum post</a>. The Dev clarified it here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282195#post1282195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Grim&quot; is a casual nickname for the Beast seeming, as in church grim. The Grimm seeming (as in Brothers Grimm) wasn't &quot;left out,&quot; it exists in Dark Eras as an era-specific seeming relevant to that time and place, just like many of the other character options you find in Dark Eras. If you'd like to update the mechanics and use it at your table in a modern game, feel free; but note that the Wyrd doesn't work on narrative logic anymore in 2e, so you probably won't see canonical support for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285615#post1285615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and there is an extremely limited amount of Kiths to go around. Most of which aren't even useful for combat!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is mostly because Kiths are incredibly easy to create now and they aren't related (for the most part) to Seemings so you can essentially make a Kith out of anything. Think of a role a Keeper (or the environment) made/forced your character into: Make a new kith out of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285615#post1285615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Anyways, onto my question:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - Does this book feature rules / guidelines for home brewing Kiths?<br /> <br /> 2 - Are there supplement materials for this book that I should probably look into purchasing?</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Yuppers! It's pretty easy to be honest. Though I think we'll be getting more rules and ideas when the next supplement comes out titles &quot;Kith &amp; Kin&quot;</li> <li>CtL2e is the only (book) thing that's out but there are 2 supplements that in the works:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Kith &amp; Kin</li> <li>Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn</li> <li>The Hedge (although this may be the same as Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn)</li> </ol></li> </ol>Otherwise there's 1st Edition material that could be useful with some hacking, a Dark Eras, and a quickstart. Check out <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1048977-changeling-resources\">here</a>, they're updated often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 02-07-2019, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:23:08-08:00","id":1285631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285621#post1285621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was actually discussed a week or so back <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1282195#post1282195\">in this forum post</a>. The Dev clarified it here:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is mostly because Kiths are incredibly easy to create now and they aren't related (for the most part) to Seemings so you can essentially make a Kith out of anything. Think of a role a Keeper (or the environment) made/forced your character into: Make a new kith out of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Yuppers! It's pretty easy to be honest. Though I think we'll be getting more rules and ideas when the next supplement comes out titles &quot;Kith &amp; Kin&quot;</li> <li>CtL2e is the only (book) thing that's out but there are 2 supplements that in the works:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Kith &amp; Kin</li> <li>Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn</li> <li>The Hedge (although this may be the same as Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn)</li> </ol></li> </ol>Otherwise there's 1st Edition material that could be useful with some hacking, a Dark Eras, and a quickstart. Check out <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1048977-changeling-resources\">here</a>, they're updated often.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answers. I haven't been keeping up with the development news, so I'm pretty behind on this kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>One More Question:</b> What about the Contracts and their power scaling?<br /> <br /> I came across a fandom wiki that tries to explain the new setting's mechanics. But when you get to the contracts section, it only includes the 1st and 2nd dot levels of each contract. Granted, there seems to be a lot of them, but the fact they only go up to rank 2 has me confused, since the other books have generally gone from 1 to 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:36:55-08:00","id":1285639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285631#post1285631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>One More Question:</b> What about the Contracts and their power scaling?<br /> <br /> I came across a fandom wiki that tries to explain the new setting's mechanics. But when you get to the contracts section, it only includes the 1st and 2nd dot levels of each contract. Granted, there seems to be a lot of them, but the fact they only go up to rank 2 has me confused, since the other books have generally gone from 1 to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e Contracts don't use dot scaling any more.<br /> <br /> Now when it comes to power they're split into two categories; Common (rating 1-3) and Royal (rating 4-5). The rationale given by the devs was that in-story, it doesn't make sense for a <i>contract </i>to get more powerful the more you use it. So now, each individual contract only has the one power associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:38:33-08:00","id":1285640,"title":"","content":"2e is mostly getting away from the straight 1-5 scaling (which was taken from OWoD Vampire and applied to every line in NWoD 1e\u2014in 2e, only Vampire keeps it). Contracts don't have 1-5 dot levels any more: they're separated into &quot;Common&quot; and &quot;Royal&quot;, and each one has multiple effects depending on your Seeming (or the Seeming of the Changeling you learned it from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:44:53-08:00","id":1285644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285640#post1285640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and each one has multiple effects depending on your Seeming (or the Seeming of the Changeling you learned it from).</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Arcadian Contracts though.<br /> <br /> Court and Goblin Contracts don't have any special Seeming effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:51:29-08:00","id":1285647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285640#post1285640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e is mostly getting away from the straight 1-5 scaling (which was taken from OWoD Vampire and applied to every line in NWoD 1e\u2014in 2e, only Vampire keeps it). Contracts don't have 1-5 dot levels any more: they're separated into &quot;Common&quot; and &quot;Royal&quot;, and each one has multiple effects depending on your Seeming (or the Seeming of the Changeling you learned it from).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More like, you learn the extra contract effect of your Seeming by default. After that, you can swear pledges to gain a tutor from another Seeming to teach you their Seeming's benefit for a Contract you both know. Also, Contracts can have multiple Seeming benefits for each Seeming, with the question of which benefits are most common and easy to learn being up to your group. The book only shows two Seeming Benefits per Contract, each for a different Seeming<br /> <br /> Also, only basic contracts (Arcadian Contracts) have Seeming Benefits and fit neatly into the Contract families called Regalia. Contracts created by the Changeling Courts (Court Contracts or bargained for with Hobgoblins (Goblin Contracts) are still split into Common and Royal, but have no Seeming Benefits. In exchange, they provide powers not covered by the commonly-known Arcadian Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T15:37:11-08:00","id":1285705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285647#post1285647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> More like, you learn the extra contract effect of your Seeming by default. After that, you can swear pledges to gain a tutor from another Seeming to teach you their Seeming's benefit for a Contract you both know. Also, Contracts can have multiple Seeming benefits for each Seeming, with the question of which benefits are most common and easy to learn being up to your group. The book only shows two Seeming Benefits per Contract, each for a different Seeming<br /> <br /> Also, only basic contracts (Arcadian Contracts) have Seeming Benefits and fit neatly into the Contract families called Regalia. Contracts created by the Changeling Courts (Court Contracts or bargained for with Hobgoblins (Goblin Contracts) are still split into Common and Royal, but have no Seeming Benefits. In exchange, they provide powers not covered by the commonly-known Arcadian Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about anyone else, but I've basically considered every Arcadian Contract to have a seeming benefit for <b>every</b> seeming. It doesn't explicitly say so in the book but I kinda took the description to mean that the two seeming benefits listed were just <i>examples </i>and that it wants you to make the benefits for the other seemings if it applies. .<br /> <br /> Again though, that's just how I interpreted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:10:05-08:00","id":1285712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285705#post1285705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't explicitly say so in the book</div> </div> </div> </div>It kinda does:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>CtL2e, p. 128</i><br /> <br /> &quot;The Contracts below present two seeming benefits each, <i><b>but Storytellers are encouraged to add their own.'</b></i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:25:39-08:00","id":1285716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1285712#post1285712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It kinda does:</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh 0.0<br /> <br /> Well Yay!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:38:24-08:00","id":1285724,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Seemed obvious to me the other remaining 4 Seeming Benefits for each Arcadian Contract weren't added was due to the almighty Wordcount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:19:09-08:00","id":1285996,"title":"","content":"Now I am hoping we get to see additional Seeming benefits for Contracts in an upcoming supplement. that would be nifty af.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T06:07:13-08:00","id":1286159,"title":"","content":"- How should the Helios\u2019 Judgment Contract's damage be handled versus vampires? Should they take the attack's damage as aggravated damage or should they take normal damage and then use the sunlight damage rules from their corebook?<br /> <br /> - Someone asked this question but no one answered: Can the effects of dropping the Mask be applied somehow in the Hedge? If not, that means a changeling can be more powerful in the real world than in the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24457-draziel","name":"DRaziel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T09:22:42-08:00","id":1286207,"title":"","content":"Since sunlight is a bane for vampires, I would say something that specifically causes <i>damage from sunlight</i> (like Helios' Judgement) does its normal damage but aggravated. Like how silver doesn't agg werewolves on contact, but a successful attack with a silver weapon does its normal damage as aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T11:01:27-08:00","id":1286228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DRaziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1286159#post1286159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Someone asked this question but no one answered: Can the effects of dropping the Mask be applied somehow in the Hedge? If not, that means a changeling can be more powerful in the real world than in the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, I don't think dropping the Mask and its mechanics are intended to be used in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> The mechanical effects described are written with the assumption that you're doing this Ironside, considering the multiple references to being witnessed by mortals. And since while in the Hedge, a changeling's Mask isn't present at all, dropping the Mask wouldn't be a thing.<br /> <br /> And I don't think trying to do the inverse would work either: if anything, putting on the Mask could be seen as a DENIAL of your fae side. So no more liberal exceptional succeeded Contract rolls for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T04:12:25-08:00","id":1287016,"title":"","content":"With the Darkling Blessing, when you turn into something immaterial, what all turns immaterial with you? Do you drop clothes? Do you keep a pistol in your hand? a pistol in your holster? a big hulking backpack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25063-diabadass","name":"Diabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T06:36:16-08:00","id":1287037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diabadass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1287016#post1287016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Darkling Blessing, when you turn into something immaterial, what all turns immaterial with you? Do you drop clothes? Do you keep a pistol in your hand? a pistol in your holster? a big hulking backpack?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;Stuff you're wearing and stuff you're carrying that isn't too big to hold casually&quot; is a serviceable metric for &quot;what does ten seconds of insubstantial status apply to besides yourself?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T07:59:02-08:00","id":1287056,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my rule of thumb is &quot;anything you're wearing/carrying, not greater than your own Size&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:29:16-08:00","id":1288009,"title":"","content":"Do Fetches have a Mask &amp; Mein?<br /> <br /> If so, can Changelings see through them by default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:23:16-08:00","id":1288029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1288009#post1288009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Fetches have a Mask &amp; Mein?<br /> <br /> If so, can Changelings see through them by default?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think they do.<br /> <br /> The text makes multiple references to how, when a changeling comes back through the Hedge and check in on their previous life, they see someone that looks exactly like them in their place. So presumably can only see their &quot;Mask&quot; and not the detritus that is composed of their actual form. However, just by the fact that the Fetch is a doppelganger of them, the changeling should, in theory logically deduce what it actually is.<br /> <br /> So the notion of being able to see a Fetch's &quot;Mein&quot; is unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T13:42:28-08:00","id":1288058,"title":"","content":"The chapter fictions imply that fetches do have a Mask and Mien. <span style=\"color:#008000\"><span style=\"font-family:Broadsheet\">&quot;He sews his button eyes back on every morning, thinking they\u2019re eyeglasses, and kisses some other woman. She\u2019s cute, I guess, but doesn\u2019t seem like our type. Or maybe just not mine.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><span style=\"font-family:Broadsheet\">&quot;When I turned slightly past, I could see our reflections in the bathroom mirror. Mine looked the same \u2014 snub nosed, sleepy-eyed, blonde roots growing in under bottle red. His... blurred like someone had smeared a handful of Vaseline on the glass. There, his face was patchwork, and his flat, button eyes hung loose. When I turned back to James, his bright-blue eyes lit up, and his smile pulled up the rims of his glasses. In the mirror, cloth shuffled itself and formed a gap shaped like that smile. I didn\u2019t flinch when he rested his flesh (fabric) hand on her knee and leaned in for a kiss. His face felt warm and unshaven and familiar. But when I peeked through my lashes, the cloth face in the mirror was rubbing against hers.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Broadsheet\">The mechanics section does not specify, but there are a couple of points in favor. Fetches are built like Changelings, and the text says that the Adding Supernatural Template step &quot;varies a bit&quot;. It then lists five ways the fetch template is different from the changeling one, but I think we can reasonably assume that traits not specifically identified as different follow the same rules for Changelings.<br /> <br /> Second, the Normalcy Echo makes Fetches undetectable to Fae Magic, so by default it must be possible to identify them somehow. That could just mean kenning and the like, but given the above points I treat Fetches as being as visible to Changelings as Changelings are to them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:28:35-08:00","id":1288100,"title":"","content":"That conflict between rules and fluff implications is what brought up the question - since it seems like there isn't a Word of God on this, I'll do some house-ruling.<br /> <br /> Second Question:<br /> <br /> Does going into full Severe Clarity Damage cause permanent Clarity Loss?<br /> <br /> If not, is there anything that does cause permanent Clarity Loss, or is that mechanic gone entirely from their morality track?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T17:06:00-08:00","id":1288118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1288100#post1288100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does going into full Severe Clarity Damage cause permanent Clarity Loss?<br /> <br /> If not, is there anything that does cause permanent Clarity Loss, or is that mechanic gone entirely from their morality track?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Clarity loss&quot; is &quot;you have Clarity damage marked.&quot; Severe damage being harder to heal in bulk and causing the detachment of Touchstones means it falls closer to the traditional understanding of &quot;losing dots of Integrity-analogue,&quot; but generally speaking your max rating can only go up.<br /> <br /> I've got a homebrew Contract whose dramatic failure result shaves a dot off your maximum Clarity, but that's for a Contract that only works in the Hedge and produces a thing that leaves behind an Icon when it dies, so it's still something of an aberrant circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:31:26-08:00","id":1288417,"title":"","content":"What happens to a Huntsman whose Prey dies?<br /> <br /> Given that Huntsmen (as far as I know) have the goals of their Keeper instead of their own, do they even need a specific target anymore, or could a keeper send one out with the mission to &quot;bring as many back to me as you can&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T20:48:42-08:00","id":1288509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1288417#post1288417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to a Huntsman whose Prey dies?<br /> <br /> Given that Huntsmen (as far as I know) have the goals of their Keeper instead of their own, do they even need a specific target anymore, or could a keeper send one out with the mission to &quot;bring as many back to me as you can&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like it's a safe bet where fae magic is concerned that recovering an operable remnant will suffice in the rare circumstance that a verderer fails to intervene in its target's untimely demise despite its skillset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:34:27-08:00","id":1291991,"title":"","content":"Can you use Talon and Wing to gain the ability to fly?<br /> <br /> EDIT: how about a boost to swimming speed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T17:36:54-08:00","id":1292652,"title":"","content":"Me and my players have a question about iron/cold iron, the book says that an iron/prison cage makes the Changeling unable to use faerie Magic to escape.<br /> Some of us believe that by the idea of iron being a bane (cold iron) and how it is exposed in the book, being imprisioned by it wold invalidate all contracts and feeric powers the Changeling uses while they are being imprisioned by iron.<br /> Other players believe that only the powers that would help or make Changeling be able to escape would be nullified by iron imprisonment (example: they believe that a Changeling could use contracts to make rain or a contract that attacked someone, while they changeling using said contract where imprisioned by Iron).<br /> So the question is: Does Iron prevent Changeling from using any fey magic or only those that could be used by Changeling to escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25121-oniverse","name":"Oniverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T17:39:00-08:00","id":1292653,"title":"","content":"Sorry I posted twice still learning how to use the forum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25121-oniverse","user":"Oniverse","date":". 02-27-2019, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25121-oniverse","name":"Oniverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T15:16:33-08:00","id":1293356,"title":"","content":"is equinox road still a relevant book for changeling 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T15:29:54-08:00","id":1293359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1293356#post1293356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is equinox road still a relevant book for changeling 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> nope. It's outright contradicted in the new core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T16:36:40-08:00","id":1293367,"title":"","content":"what is it that 2md edition contradicts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T17:32:00-08:00","id":1293376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1293367#post1293367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what is it that 2md edition contradicts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From memory, the way True Fae work and the method of going from Changeling to True Fae, which is much harder now. As for anything else, I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T17:38:27-08:00","id":1293379,"title":"","content":"crap, so that means even the lands of Arcadia (since true fae basically are that) is pointless. well, Hope's to a new supplement in the same vein","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T17:51:26-08:00","id":1293384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1293379#post1293379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">crap, so that means even the lands of Arcadia (since true fae basically are that) is pointless. well, Hope's to a new supplement in the same vein</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, the True Fae are still their domains. There is also an Old Arcadia that existed before them that was mentioned as the home of the Huntsmen, but described sparsely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T17:54:31-08:00","id":1293385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1293376#post1293376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From memory, the way True Fae work</div> </div> </div> </div>Several mechanical conceits scan directly and at least one metaphysical explanation uses an identical example paragraph to the one found in Equinox Road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the method of going from Changeling to True Fae, which is much harder now. </div> </div> </div>Addressed not at all in 2e Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T18:51:04-08:00","id":1293399,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, are saying it is still relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T21:37:25-08:00","id":1293413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1293399#post1293399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, are saying it is still relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending future material to the contrary, all that 2e contradicts from the rough overview of Equinox Road has to do with elements of the setting that didn't exist before, like token Regalia or the mythic explanation for why Contracts exist or access to nested Hedgeways like the Dreaming Roads and the Hall of Mirrors; that and the firm changeover of implicit placement of Faerie relative to the Supernal Realms of Mage make some niche aspects of Equinox Road less viable, but most of the rest of it is no more irrelevant to people looking to 1e books for inspiration than <i>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i> is to people fishing for ideas to use for their city in Requiem 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T22:33:54-08:00","id":1293419,"title":"","content":"thank you for clarifying satchel, I'll be saving up for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T19:55:04-08:00","id":1294291,"title":"","content":"I had trouble finding this real quick, I used the search function but didn't find this question. I'm sure other people have asked and maybe it is in the books but I sort of had short notice.<br /> <br /> Is there a way for changelings to store glamour in an object? Something already designed in the books? I'm using a token impromptu for the purpose but, if there's a method already shown in second edition I'd love to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:08:05-08:00","id":1294313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1294291#post1294291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had trouble finding this real quick, I used the search function but didn't find this question. I'm sure other people have asked and maybe it is in the books but I sort of had short notice.<br /> <br /> Is there a way for changelings to store glamour in an object? Something already designed in the books? I'm using a token impromptu for the purpose but, if there's a method already shown in second edition I'd love to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for <i>storing</i> it in a fungible medium, but oath-forged tokens and goblin fruits both serve as portable sources of glamour, and there's a token in 1e that existed as a tool for collecting Glamour (the Hollow Heart from page 36 of Swords at Dawn), which I don't imagine would be terribly problematic to port over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:10:12-08:00","id":1294314,"title":"","content":"This may be weird to ask, but do Fae Touched have Iron as a bane? It affects their contracts, certainly, but would they take increased damage from it like a Changeling would? Someone brought this up and I'm having a hard time disputing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:25:10-08:00","id":1294317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1294314#post1294314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be weird to ask, but do Fae Touched have Iron as a bane? It affects their contracts, certainly, but would they take increased damage from it like a Changeling would? Someone brought this up and I'm having a hard time disputing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> They have a Drawbacks section (CtL2e p. 319) and the only thing listed is the &quot;Susceptible to Delirium&quot; bit. And, while not a concrete statement, the section does include this line of:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being fae-touched carries its own dangers and drawbacks, <b>uniquely separate from those changelings suffer.</b> </div> </div> </div>Which I believe was to imply: &quot;no, fae-touched don't have the exact same weaknesses as full changelings&quot;. My reading of them has always been that, while yes they now have access to some fae powers, at the end of the day fae-touched are predominantly human and immune to the usual changeling-specific weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-06-2019, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:30:26-08:00","id":1294320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1294314#post1294314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be weird to ask, but do Fae Touched have Iron as a bane? It affects their contracts, certainly, but would they take increased damage from it like a Changeling would? Someone brought this up and I'm having a hard time disputing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're Wyrd 0 and bound to considerably more forthright uses of fae magic by the nature of their relationship with Contracts and pledgecraft. Changelings of Wyrd 1 only have the bane of iron as a frailty, can initiate oaths, and have access to Loopholes.<br /> <br /> The most unusual thing about the Avowed constitution is their Glamour dependency, which is entirely separate from any of the reasons one might pick for why iron deals aggravated damage to fae formed after the rise of Faerie. I feel this is very much meant to be in the same vein as ghouls and fire \u2014 they're a mortal resource who doesn't have to deal with more severe banes as part and parcel of their more constrained abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T23:11:16-08:00","id":1294330,"title":"","content":"A question concerning Demon: the Descent, how do True Fae or a Huntsman know if their target is actually human or a Demon in Cover? What would happen if that True Fae/Huntsman tried to abduct said potential Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T03:40:05-08:00","id":1294354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1294330#post1294330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question concerning Demon: the Descent, how do True Fae or a Huntsman know if their target is actually human or a Demon in Cover? What would happen if that True Fae/Huntsman tried to abduct said potential Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can only know if they use some sort of power to search for a suitable human and the demon fails to Spoof that power.<br /> Most of the time they'll only know once they've attempted the abduction and found out that their victim is struggling back with inhuman powers. Depending on what the True Fae wants or what the Huntsman's orders are they might either just let the demon go, try to kill them for being a witness, or still try to carry out the attempt. If the attempt is successful and the demon hasn't gone Demonic Form yet I'd guess that their current Cover is shredded by the Thorns on the way to Arcadia.<br /> \u200bWhat happens after that is pure ST fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T04:24:31-08:00","id":1294363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1291991#post1291991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Talon and Wing to gain the ability to fly?<br /> <br /> EDIT: how about a boost to swimming speed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about reposting this. It just seemed to have been forgotten and unanswered","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:20:55-08:00","id":1294563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1294354#post1294354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can only know if they use some sort of power to search for a suitable human and the demon fails to Spoof that power.<br /> Most of the time they'll only know once they've attempted the abduction and found out that their victim is struggling back with inhuman powers. Depending on what the True Fae wants or what the Huntsman's orders are they might either just let the demon go, try to kill them for being a witness, or still try to carry out the attempt. If the attempt is successful and the demon hasn't gone Demonic Form yet I'd guess that their current Cover is shredded by the Thorns on the way to Arcadia.<br /> \u200bWhat happens after that is pure ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your time and knowledge, Tessie. Also this is pure hilarity, be sure to grab some popcorn if your ST allows this to happen during the Chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:49:02-08:00","id":1294841,"title":"","content":"Are characters who become a Goblin King / Queen still playable, or does the transformation make them too alien to function properly as a playable character, anymore?<br /> <br /> And if they can be, how does becoming a Hobgoblin affect their previous existence as a Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:35:39-08:00","id":1294864,"title":"","content":"I would expect Talon and Wing to apply to swimming speed. Growing webbed hands and feet or similar alterations seems far too easy and minor to not be possible for a royal contract.<br /> <br /> I'm less certain about giving characters a flight speed. That's a more dramatic shift, but it is a royal contract and that wouldn't be the most impressive thing one can accomplish. <br /> <br /> If you feel like flight should be allowed but unlimited flight at +10 speed is too much you could do what some similar powers have done and require the character to land and rest for a turn after a certain amount of time in flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:59:19-08:00","id":1294876,"title":"","content":"J assumed if flight was possible, it was flight at 10 Speed flat, as it adds to a starting flight Speed of 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-07-2019, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T14:41:15-08:00","id":1294886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1294841#post1294841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are characters who become a Goblin King / Queen still playable, or does the transformation make them too alien to function properly as a playable character, anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah they're still playable as PCs. Especially considering the result of the exit condition is turning back into a regular changeling.<br /> <br /> Continue being fabulous and dance the magic dance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T21:54:49-07:00","id":1295740,"title":"","content":"So if Bridge-burners are still a thing and they don't want anything to do with the Hedge and what not, wouldn't that make them hate Icons, thus turning them into Iconoclasts as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:33:34-07:00","id":1295789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1295740#post1295740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if Bridge-burners are still a thing and they don't want anything to do with the Hedge and what not, wouldn't that make them hate Icons, thus turning them into Iconoclasts as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not want to use their own Icons as to not get bad memories back, but only the most extreme would actively seek out and destory Icons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:15:10-07:00","id":1295827,"title":"","content":"As presented in the book, they tend to hypocritically use any form of fae magic that will help them with their main goal: destroying and suppressing both anything fae and anything that attracts the fae, including dreams, art, creativity, beauty and imagination<br /> <br /> As Icons give them more Clarity, strengthening their minds against the horrible things they do, i think they will pursue their icons just as much as any other Changeling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:14:18-07:00","id":1297065,"title":"","content":"Here's a simple question about the contents of a book.<br /> <br /> I already have Dark Eras and the Dark Eras Companion. I saw there is a Victorian Lost book, but Victorian Lost is also covered in Dark Eras. Does the separate Victorian Lost book contain any content that isn't in the Dark Eras book, or is it exactly the same content?<br /> <br /> Given that I already have Dark Eras, should I buy Victorian Lost or would that be a waste of money?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:41:32-07:00","id":1297071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1297065#post1297065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a simple question about the contents of a book.<br /> <br /> I already have Dark Eras and the Dark Eras Companion. I saw there is a Victorian Lost book, but Victorian Lost is also covered in Dark Eras. Does the separate Victorian Lost book contain any content that isn't in the Dark Eras book, or is it exactly the same content?<br /> <br /> Given that I already have Dark Eras, should I buy Victorian Lost or would that be a waste of money?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Victorian Lost is from 1st Edition Changeling, IIRC","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T16:39:25-07:00","id":1297111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1297071#post1297071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Victorian Lost is from 1st Edition Changeling, IIRC</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I misremembered. I thought Victorian Lost was in Dark Eras but what's in Dark Eras is the 'Grimm Dark Era', same time period, but covers 19th century Europe in general rather than focussed on Victorian England.<br /> I just bought the Victorian Lost PDF. I hope I won't regret my purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T08:46:36-07:00","id":1298337,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is answered somewhere already, but here's a question:<br /> <br /> Does the Changeling's Mask automatically (without strengthening it with Glamour) work towards creatures other than humans? For example vampires, werewolves, demons? Do they see the changeling's Mask by default or do they see his Mien by default?<br /> <br /> The book says <i>&quot;Fae beings and other supernatural creatures with mystical senses can see through the Mask.&quot;</i>, but I'm not sure if that means all vampires can automatically see changelings for what they really are, or only those using vampires using Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-21-2019, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T09:58:49-07:00","id":1298355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1298337#post1298337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is answered somewhere already, but here's a question:<br /> <br /> Does the Changeling's Mask automatically (without strengthening it with Glamour) work towards creatures other than humans? For example vampires, werewolves, demons? Do they see the changeling's Mask by default or do they see his Mien by default?<br /> <br /> The book says <i>&quot;Fae beings and other supernatural creatures with mystical senses can see through the Mask.&quot;</i>, but I'm not sure if that means all vampires can automatically see changelings for what they really are, or only those using vampires using Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's been some conversation on the topic but let me briefly summarize what has been logically concluded (whether to full satisfaction or not is another matter):<br /> <br /> 1. The Mask is in place for other supernaturals.<br /> 2. Other supernatural abilities that pierce deception do so normally.<br /> 3. A powerstat-contested roll may not apply unless the Changeling is using a specific ability (Glamour, Contract, etc.) to strengthen their Mask.<br /> <br /> So, Changeling X may look normal-ish, but they will smell off to a werewolf's supernatural senses, and &quot;ping&quot; as supernatural and whatever else to Auspex. <br /> <br /> My <b><i>impression</i></b> is that a Changeling really ought to think about how they're hiding from someone (their Keeper, and Huntsmen) and conduct themselves accordingly. Incidental to this point is that if the setting is crossover they are going to stand out to other supernaturals whe are looking for unusual things... and that can get bad in a hurry. A wise Changeling (one almost as paranoid as a Demon) would wander about with Contracts in place to disguise their, oh--briney scent and trailing tentacles or whatnot.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T13:33:25-07:00","id":1299026,"title":"","content":"Both 1e and 2e lost have contracts that allow changelings to become something inanimate (Chrysalis in 1e, Props and Scenery in 2e).<br /> <br /> 1e specifically states that the object has to be relatively simple (the most complex example given is a clock). 2e doesn't really specify.<br /> <br /> My question is:<br /> could one use these contracts to become a weapon like a large blade? A suit of armor around someone? A sniper rifle?<br /> <br /> Because the idea of making a pledge with someone and becoming weapon/wielder partners is something so fantastical that I desperately want to play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","user":"GourmetBrickWall","date":". 03-23-2019, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T17:34:26-07:00","id":1299081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GourmetBrickWall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1299026#post1299026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is:<br /> could one use these contracts to become a weapon like a large blade? A suit of armor around someone? A sniper rifle?<br /> <br /> Because the idea of making a pledge with someone and becoming weapon/wielder partners is something so fantastical that I desperately want to play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely in line with the fairy tale headspace of Contracts and the concept doesn't include any specifications that would disqualify it (though in action timing it might be a bit of a stretch to shortcut past needing to put on armor), so basically, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T20:21:45-07:00","id":1299120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1299081#post1299081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely in line with the fairy tale headspace of Contracts and the concept doesn't include any specifications that would disqualify it (though in action timing it might be a bit of a stretch to shortcut past needing to put on armor), so basically, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what makes the 2e version even more epic- with an exceptional, you can perma-buy the form and make it reflexive for a glamour. Not to mention you can get it at char. creation. I figured blades and armor would be allowed, but didn't know if guns like sniper rifles would be too advanced. <br /> <br /> It also brings several awesome roleplay capabilities. Since YOU aren't performing actions to attack/defend, your actions are free. A playmate could help their owner as a suit of protective armor, using their kith talent and contracts. A bright one could be a blazing sword. A leechfinger could turn into a suit of armor around an enemy and slowly drain the life from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:14:04-07:00","id":1299357,"title":"","content":"Can 2e Pledges/Oaths still grant Glamour as a reward for completing your task?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:05:59-07:00","id":1299384,"title":"","content":"Haven't read anything specifically mentioning glamour. There are a bunch of neat side effects that could be interpreted to give glamour; for example, making a bargain with a human is left ambiguous- the most clarifying statement being that a one-to-three dot merit is appropriate for a changeling to ask for in return. Some ling merits specify assisting in glamour (goblin bounty gives fruits which gives glamour); if it were my game, I'd certainly allow something like the 1e version. <br /> <br /> But no- just looked over it again. Nothing specific about glamour; the biggest mention is the ability to swap willpower and glamour once per chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:34:53-07:00","id":1299472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1299357#post1299357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can 2e Pledges/Oaths still grant Glamour as a reward for completing your task?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending further options in the Companion and future supplements, this is accomplished through oath-forged tokens, which essentially makes oaths that grant Glamour required to be what 1e called a Corporal pledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:36:06-07:00","id":1299592,"title":"","content":"How does dreaming work for abductees still in Arcadia? Are they able to lucid dream, and move from the Bastion out into the Hedge? <br /> Can someone <i>else</i> find their way into an abducted person's Bastion, even while their physical body is in Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T17:34:30-07:00","id":1300151,"title":"","content":"About the Cold Iron bane:<br /> <br /> The 2e book is incredibly vague about it to a unhelpful degree. When does something count as &quot;cold iron&quot;? The book says it has to be man-made, not factory-made or mass-produced. Okay, fair enough. That already narrows it down. It also says that the product has to be mostly iron. Okay, cool, so hand-forged steel swords and daggers count then, right?<br /> <br /> Except, maybe not... Because the book also says that only what people think is iron, counts as cold iron, and then points out that steel weapons might not count because people supposedly don't think steel is iron...<br /> <br /> Does that mean steel weapons never work against changelings, or does it only not work if the wielder does not understand that steel is an iron-carbon alloy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":".  Removed the part that could potentially be seen as insulting. 03-26-2019, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T17:54:07-07:00","id":1300155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300151#post1300151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me? Since when are people this stupid? Is there seriously anyone who doesn't know that steel is an iron-carbon alloy, perhaps with another metal mixed in, but always predominantly iron?</div> </div> </div> </div>People in general can understand that from a storytelling/symbolic perspective &quot;steel&quot; is a different thing from &quot;iron,&quot; particularly in a setting derived from the modern world where &quot;steel&quot; is a pervasive material and &quot;iron&quot; has fallen out of popular usage with advances in metallurgy and engineering.<br /> <br /> There are connotations to a thing being made of iron that things made of steel generally lack, and the express lack of a hard explanation for why the bane exists means the metal existing in unalloyed forms as an ugly, unrefined, fundamental substance with connotations of solidity, inflexibility, and eventual dissolution is, at best, a hint at why the metal occultists have identified with prisons and the body is proof against the powers of the ephemeral and mind-warping dream-creatures that promised to conquer Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sure, lets say for the sake of argument that a lot of people are stupid and don't know that steel is an iron-carbon alloy. Does that mean steel weapons never work against changelings, or does it only not work if the wielder is dumb enough to not understand that steel is an iron-carbon alloy? </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the way the bane of iron works means that steel weapons <i>won't work</i>. Aggravated damage and the ability to ignore fae defenses are not essential to the functioning of a weapon.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to get this confrontational and frustrated right out the gate over this, much less to the point of throwing insults around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T18:06:37-07:00","id":1300156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300155#post1300155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in general can understand that from a storytelling/symbolic perspective &quot;steel&quot; is a different thing from &quot;iron,&quot; particularly in a setting derived from the modern world where &quot;steel&quot; is a pervasive material and &quot;iron&quot; has fallen out of popular usage with advances in metallurgy and engineering.<br /> <br /> There are connotations to a thing being made of iron that things made of steel generally lack, and the express lack of a hard explanation for why the bane exists means the metal existing in unalloyed forms as an ugly, unrefined, fundamental substance with connotations of solidity, inflexibility, and eventual dissolution is, at best, a hint at why the metal occultists have identified with prisons and the body is proof against the powers of the ephemeral and mind-warping dream-creatures that promised to conquer Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Nothing about the way the bane of iron works means that steel weapons <i>won't work</i>. Aggravated damage and the ability to ignore fae defenses are not essential to the functioning of a weapon.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to get this confrontational and frustrated right out the gate over this, much less to the point of throwing insults around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not frustrated, just utterly confused.<br /> <br /> If what is physically iron is not a reliable way to determine what counts as &quot;cold iron&quot; and what doesn't count, then what is? How do I, as a Storyteller, decide what counts as &quot;cold iron&quot; and what doesn't?<br /> <br /> The fact that the book literally contradicts itself isn't helping. In the first paragraph, it mentions cast-iron as counting, but then in the next paragraph it says cast iron doesn't count. If cast iron doesn't count, then cast-iron shouldn't count, should it? I'm confused.<br /> <br /> If it's about people's belief, then I once again have to ask: What if the person in question knows that steel is iron (in fact, it's more pure iron than cast-iron, pig iron or meteoric iron)?<br /> Or what if a person believes that the pipe he's holding is made of iron, even though it's actually made of lead?<br /> What if the person wrongfully thinks the manacles he owns are steel, while in reality they're actually made of cast-iron?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> It also mentions that the reason &quot;cold iron&quot; might be the bane of fae is because it symbolizes &quot;the death blow to the age of superstition and legend&quot; as brought forth by the industrial revolution.<br /> <br /> Which again leaves me in confusion, because humans already stopped using cast-iron for most things and steel was the material of choice for most things well before the industrial revolution came along, and on top of that, the era of the industrial revolution, the 19th century, was actually one of the eras where people were <i>most</i> superstitious, even more so than the centuries before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":".  Removed the part that could potentially be seen as insulting. 03-26-2019, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T18:23:40-07:00","id":1300157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300151#post1300151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Cold Iron bane:<br /> <br /> The 2e book is incredibly vague about it to a unhelpful degree. When does something count as &quot;cold iron&quot;? The book says it has to be man-made, not factory-made or mass-produced. Okay, fair enough. That already narrows it down. It also says that the product has to be mostly iron. Okay, cool, so hand-forged steel swords and daggers count then, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not vague at all. &quot;Mostly pure and hand forged&quot; is pretty clear. Steel is not &quot;mostly pure&quot; iron, it is intentionally adulterated iron and was very much not hand-forged, the process for creating steel necessitates the use of machinery. So, no, there is absolutely no way to argue that a steel sword counts as &quot;mostly pure and hand forged&quot; iron, because it is not &quot;mostly pure&quot; and the steel itself is machine made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except, maybe not... Because the book also says that only what people think is iron, counts as cold iron, and then points out that steel weapons might not count because people supposedly don't think steel is iron... </div> </div> </div>No, it says that what most people consider iron is iron. Most people don't consider steel to be iron, they consider it to be steel. Just like most people don't consider brass to be copper or zinc, they consider it brass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Excuse me? Since when are people this stupid? Is there seriously anyone who doesn't know that steel is an iron-carbon alloy, perhaps with another metal mixed in, but always predominantly iron? </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure when you order a steak at a restaurant you'd be perfectly fine receiving ground beef in gravy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sure, lets say for the sake of argument that a lot of people are stupid and don't know that steel is an iron-carbon alloy. Does that mean steel weapons never work against changelings, or does it only not work if the wielder is dumb enough to not understand that steel is an iron-carbon alloy? </div> </div> </div>The weapons still work against fae, they just don't ignore magical defenses. It doesn't matter what one person believes, it's the general perception of iron and steel as fundamentally different products (which they very much are, there's a reason people differentiate) as well as the fact that steel must be created via mechanical process that prevents it from acting as iron.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300156#post1300156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not frustrated, just utterly confused. I also wasn't insulting anyone, if anything, I'm giving my fellow human's intelligence more credit than whoever wrote this Cold Iron section.<br /> <br /> If what is physically iron is not a reliable way to determine what counts as &quot;cold iron&quot; and what doesn't count, then what is? How do I, as a Storyteller, decide what counts as &quot;cold iron&quot; and what doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>What part of &quot;mostly pure and hand forged&quot; is confusing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that the book literally contradicts itself isn't helping. In the first paragraph, it mentions cast-iron as counting, but then in the next paragraph it says cast iron doesn't count. If cast iron doesn't count, then cast-iron shouldn't count, should it? I'm confused. </div> </div> </div>Cast iron counts as iron, cast iron does <i>not</i> count as <i>cold iron</i>. Before you start calling everyone in the world stupid, maybe you should calm down and reread the sections in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's about people's belief, then I once again have to ask: What if the person in question knows that steel is iron (in fact, it's more pure iron than cast-iron, pig iron or meteoric iron)? </div> </div> </div>Steel is not iron, it is an alloy of iron, carbon, and other stuff. It is <i>intentionally adulterated</i> and created by machine, not naturally occurring iron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or what if a person believes that the pipe he's holding is made of iron, even though it's actually made of lead? </div> </div> </div>They're probably in for a rude surprise when fae defenses continue to work against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the person wrongfully thinks the manacles he owns are steel, while in reality they're actually made of cast-iron? </div> </div> </div>Then they're in for a rude surprise when they can't easily escape from the bindings.<br /> <br /> Individual belief doesn't matter, it's the general perception and understanding of people as a whole that matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Edit:</b> It also mentions that the reason &quot;cold iron&quot; might be the bane of fae is because it symbolizes &quot;the death blow to the age of superstition and legend&quot; as brought forth by the industrial revolution.<br /> <br /> Which again leaves me in confusion, because humans already stopped using cast-iron for most things and steel was the material of choice for most things well before the industrial revolution came along, and on top of that, the era of the industrial revolution, the 19th century, was actually one of the eras where people were <i>most</i> superstitious, even more so than the centuries before. </div> </div> </div>It says that &quot;some changelings theorize,&quot; not that it is in any way substantiated. Nobody actually knows why iron is anathema to the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 03-26-2019, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T18:39:22-07:00","id":1300162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300156#post1300156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wasn't insulting anyone, if anything, I'm giving my fellow human's intelligence more credit than whoever wrote this Cold Iron section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't disrespect me with this halfhearted evasive nonsense. I am asking you to have the common decency to not toss unhelpful words like &quot;stupid&quot; and &quot;dumb&quot; around in the course of what you are claiming is just an earnest request for clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that the book literally contradicts itself isn't helping. In the first paragraph, it mentions cast-iron as counting, but then in the next paragraph it says cast iron doesn't count. If cast iron doesn't count, then cast-iron shouldn't count, should it? I'm confused. </div> </div> </div>You're looking at two different levels of bane, as evidenced by the fact that the type that deals aggravated damage specifies &quot;this iron.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Iron&quot; and &quot;cold iron&quot; in 2e are what 1e called &quot;cold iron&quot; and &quot;hand-forged iron,&quot; and the latter type of iron cannot be made by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casting_(metalworking)\" target=\"_blank\">casting</a>, which is a separate process from the substance known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cast_iron\" target=\"_blank\">cast-iron</a>. Normal &quot;iron&quot; just bypasses fae magic, and &quot;cold iron&quot; also deals aggravated damage. That's the distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T19:31:28-07:00","id":1300171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300157#post1300157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not vague at all. &quot;Mostly pure and hand forged&quot; is pretty clear. Steel is not &quot;mostly pure&quot; iron, it is intentionally adulterated iron and was very much not hand-forged, the process for creating steel necessitates the use of machinery. So, no, there is absolutely no way to argue that a steel sword counts as &quot;mostly pure and hand forged&quot; iron, because it is not &quot;mostly pure&quot; and the steel itself is machine made.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not correct. Steel is often more pure iron than any other kind of iron we use, with sometimes less than 0,002% carbon, where as iron ore naturally contains significantly more carbon, and sometimes nickel as well.<br /> <br /> You don't need a machine to make steel either, all you need is a high temperature to smelt the iron to create steel. People as far back as 1400 BCE already knew how to make steel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300157#post1300157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of &quot;mostly pure and hand forged&quot; is confusing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that steel is often the purest of all irons, and can be hand forged, yet steel doesn't count as &quot;cold iron&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300157#post1300157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cast iron counts as iron, cast iron does <i>not</i> count as <i>cold iron</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me get this straight. Cast iron manacles allow me to bind a changeling, cast iron weapons allow me to ignore a changeling's defenses and nullify his magic, but does <i>not</i> allow me to inflict aggravated damage on him because... reasons?<br /> <br /> What are the reasons? Another misconception that cast iron is machine-made? It isn't. Not necessarily. Cast iron can be hand forged, just like steel, and has been hand forged as far back as 5th century BCE.<br /> <br /> So okay, machine-made cast iron and steel don't inflict aggravated damage, fair enough. What about hand forged cast iron and steel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300157#post1300157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steel is not iron, it is an alloy of iron, carbon, and other stuff. It is <i>intentionally adulterated</i> and created by machine, not naturally occurring iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is quite simply not correct. You might want to look it up. it's not intentionally adulterated, it's actually intentionally purified. Steel is often purer iron than meteoric iron, pig iron, or cast iron, and about as pure as wrought iron, Unless chromium is used as an alloy, which isn't necessarily the case. Sometimes steel can be created by smelting cast iron with wrought iron, the resulting mixture becomes steel.<br /> <br /> &quot;Steel&quot; really just means the iron ore has been smelted into pig iron, and then has been smelted again to form an interstitial alloy bond with the carbon that is naturally already present in pig iron, and the process also removes excess carbon from the pig iron, turning it into steel.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, meteoric iron is a naturally occurring alloy of iron and nickel. Does that mean meteoric iron doesn't count as &quot;cold iron&quot;? Or does it count because it occurs naturally, even though it's an alloy?<br /> <br /> <br /> I just checked the Changeling 1e book, which is slightly more clear on this, but I'm still not sure if I get this correctly. So let me sum up what I understand now:<br /> <br /> Cold iron is iron that humans perceive as iron and is hand forged. Naturally-occurring alloys count, but man-made alloys do not, unless humanity at large refers to the alloy as iron. So wrought iron counts, because humans refer to it as iron, but steel does not count, because humans refer to it as steel, even though physically there is hardly any difference between wrought iron and steel.<br /> However, for wrought iron to count as &quot;cold iron&quot;, it has to be hand forged. But if it's not hand forged, it still might keep a changeling prisoner, it also nullifies his magic, and penetrates his defenses, but it does <i>not</i> do aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Do I understand it correctly now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-26-2019, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T19:39:19-07:00","id":1300175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300162#post1300162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't disrespect me with this halfhearted evasive nonsense. I am asking you to have the common decency to not toss unhelpful words like &quot;stupid&quot; and &quot;dumb&quot; around in the course of what you are claiming is just an earnest request for clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only person disrespecting anyone here is you with your passive-aggressive behavior and insinuations towards me. Why do you always try to gaslight me and start unproductive arguments with me? You think this is helpful?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>You know what? You're right. I do need to apologize. Not to you, but to the person who wrote the Cold Iron section. My post was definitely insulting towards him/her, and that's not cool. So I'm legit sorry, I did not mean to insult the Onyx Path writing team.<br /> I edited my previous posts to remove the parts that could potentially have been taken as an insult. Again, I'm sorry, in particular towards the writers of Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-26-2019, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T09:00:18-07:00","id":1300304,"title":"","content":"Now I'm confused again. From the Bridge-Burner part of the book:<br /> <br /> <i>the 20th century gave the Bridge-Burners far<br /> more weapons with which to fight the Arcadians. Even<br /> as belt-fed machine guns chattered and flung <b>iron</b> at<br /> a rate magic could never match,</i><br /> <br /> Iron? But bullets aren't made of iron, bullets are made of lead.<br /> <br /> So, does lead count towards the bane then? I would guess not.<br /> <br /> So I take it this piece of text is completely unrelated to the changeling cold iron bane? Or do bullets count because people often (wrongfully) refer to them as iron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-27-2019, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T09:02:17-07:00","id":1300307,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that they made their own special machine guns with iron bullets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T10:05:13-07:00","id":1300318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300307#post1300307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is that they made their own special machine guns with iron bullets</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, creating iron bullets for machine guns is a pretty bad idea, but somehow I get the feeling the Bridge-Burners don't really care about that. :')<br /> <br /> So yeah, you could be right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T10:35:30-07:00","id":1300324,"title":"","content":"They may be inferior to steel bullet machine guns in terms of reliability , but a badly-working iron bullet machine gun is still better at hurting the Gentry than any top shelf non-cold-iron weapon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T10:43:12-07:00","id":1300327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1299592#post1299592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does dreaming work for abductees still in Arcadia? Are they able to lucid dream, and move from the Bastion out into the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, the limits of a Dream Form indicate very few issues with the process being technically possible \u2014 even after the Glamour-intensive process of escaping a Bastion, the Dreaming Roads are behind Hedgeways themselves, which leaves would-be fugitives to tangle with the usual hazards of the Hedge at large and take risks with goblin fruit. On the other hand, a character's durance probably isn't meant to be represented with their having Clarity (and thus the question of how to calculate Dream Health arises) and the control a Keeper exercises over their captives feels germane to the Comatose Condition if they're even allowed to sleep \u2014 and relative time in Faerie is sufficiently wonky that I'm not sure there wouldn't just be an ample chance of the changeling in question getting woken up by external factors at an inopportune moment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can someone <i>else</i> find their way into an abducted person's Bastion, even while their physical body is in Arcadia? </div> </div> </div>Less issues than the above, but the way the Dreaming Roads work means I wouldn't be surprised if a captive changeling's Bastion manifested along a Road that led to their Keeper's domain in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> What it boils down to, though, is how much importance your chronicle places on changelings under their durance having access (mutual or otherwise) to the world outside of Faerie through their dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T11:17:52-07:00","id":1300335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300171#post1300171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold iron is iron that humans perceive as iron and is hand forged. Naturally-occurring alloys count, but man-made alloys do not, unless humanity at large refers to the alloy as iron. So wrought iron counts, because humans refer to it as iron, but steel does not count, because humans refer to it as steel, even though physically there is hardly any difference between wrought iron and steel.<br /> However, for wrought iron to count as &amp;quot;cold iron&amp;quot;, it has to be hand forged. But if it's not hand forged, it still might keep a changeling prisoner, it also nullifies his magic, and penetrates his defenses, but it does <i>not</i> do aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Do I understand it correctly now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold Iron is not meant to be found or worked easily, simply put. You can\u2019t buy it in bulk, or even all that easily from a lot of places, it isn\u2019t going to be as good as normal store bought iron and, simply put, iron isn\u2019t as good as steel. If it sounds like making Iron useful, or even keeping Cold Iron status, is byzantine, welcome to faerie law; even when it applies to things that break faeries down, it\u2019s still something that you have to wrap your head around.<br /> <br /> Another thing about the whole Iron/Steel thing is that, chemical understndings aside, Iron and Steel simply look and react different. Steel covers a wide range of different substances, looks nicer and is stronger. Iron rusts exceptionally easily unless alloyed (stainless steel) and has impurities in it that Steel does not. Iron has an identity that is different from Steel. Chemically they are similar, but the same can be said for water and hydrogen peroxide (they are just one element off), or how humanity shares most of its genes with primates like monkeys. The two are related, but on the whole are considered very different things by humanity even if chemically/scientifically they are very similar and one came from the other.<br /> <br /> TLDR: you\u2019re looking too deeply into game mechanics/lore meant to make scarcity out of a potent weapon against fae both friendly and otherwise. If it\u2019s ever up to question, the storyteller can make a decision on the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T11:55:32-07:00","id":1300347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300335#post1300335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cold Iron is not meant to be found or worked easily, simply put. You can\u2019t buy it in bulk, or even all that easily from a lot of places, it isn\u2019t going to be as good as normal store bought iron and, simply put, iron isn\u2019t as good as steel. If it sounds like making Iron useful, or even keeping Cold Iron status, is byzantine, welcome to faerie law; even when it applies to things that break faeries down, it\u2019s still something that you have to wrap your head around.<br /> <br /> Another thing about the whole Iron/Steel thing is that, chemical understndings aside, Iron and Steel simply look and react different. Steel covers a wide range of different substances, looks nicer and is stronger. Iron rusts exceptionally easily unless alloyed (stainless steel) and has impurities in it that Steel does not. Iron has an identity that is different from Steel. Chemically they are similar, but the same can be said for water and hydrogen peroxide (they are just one element off), or how humanity shares most of its genes with primates like monkeys. The two are related, but on the whole are considered very different things by humanity even if chemically/scientifically they are very similar and one came from the other.<br /> <br /> TLDR: you\u2019re looking too deeply into game mechanics/lore meant to make scarcity out of a potent weapon against fae both friendly and otherwise. If it\u2019s ever up to question, the storyteller can make a decision on the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty useful answer, thanks.<br /> <br /> I'm not used to making rulings based on &quot;feelings&quot; and &quot;concepts&quot; so this is foreign territory to me. My players are often rules lawyers and gamers, I know they are going to try to find the boundaries of this bane and experiment with it, hence I'm concerned about the exact definition of &quot;cold iron&quot;, which the book doesn't really give, and only now do I understand that this is probably on purpose.<br /> <br /> It's not super helpful to me that the book is intentionally vague and symbolic about it, but I understand why now. I guess I'll just have to make my own rulings on it when it comes down to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-27-2019, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:25:51-07:00","id":1300356,"title":"","content":"In 1E Changeling, Changelings could affect the way the Hedge manifested around them by virtue of high Wyrd (iirc).<br /> In Beast, Beasts have the exact same effect on the Hedge by virtue of high Lair.<br /> <br /> In 2E Changeling, the systems have been revised so that Changelings can perform Hedgespinning<br /> Does it follow for Beasts to be able to do Hedgespinning, given that when it was released, Beasts had the same impact on the Hedge that changelings did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T13:21:26-07:00","id":1300369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300356#post1300356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2E Changeling, the systems have been revised so that Changelings can perform Hedgespinning<br /> Does it follow for Beasts to be able to do Hedgespinning, given that when it was released, Beasts had the same impact on the Hedge that changelings did?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The 1e mechanics Beast is referencing are dramatically less versatile than Hedgespinning, and the deliberate options only cost Glamour when retrying a failed attempt at making the same change, whereas 2e Hedgespinning always costs Glamour and uses Traits other than Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> The scaling pseudo-chart preceding the rolled mechanic, which describes how dramatically the Hedge changes around a changeling and for how long (and how much these changes benefit attempts to track the character) is less germane to 2e changelings (who in various ways deal with those effects everywhere under normal circumstances), but the basic concept of &quot;you can tell that a Beast has been in a Hedge locale on an increasingly longer timetable as their Lair increases&quot; translates well enough narratively.<br /> <br /> For a cross-edition kludge, you might allow Beasts to attempt Hedgespinning in line with their Legends as though they were a True Fae Title by spending Satiety and rolling the same dicepool they would use for a Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T15:38:17-07:00","id":1300689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300304#post1300304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm confused again. From the Bridge-Burner part of the book:<br /> <br /> <i>the 20th century gave the Bridge-Burners far<br /> more weapons with which to fight the Arcadians. Even<br /> as belt-fed machine guns chattered and flung <b>iron</b> at<br /> a rate magic could never match,</i><br /> <br /> Iron? But bullets aren't made of iron, bullets are made of lead.<br /> <br /> So, does lead count towards the bane then? I would guess not.<br /> <br /> So I take it this piece of text is completely unrelated to the changeling cold iron bane? Or do bullets count because people often (wrongfully) refer to them as iron?</div> </div> </div> </div>On this note, because someone or their players are going to come up with it:<br /> <br /> Iron bullets are/<a href=\"https://www.americanrifleman.org/articles/2018/3/14/back-to-basics-pistol-bullets/\" target=\"_blank\">were used</a>, especially early on, but were generally supplanted by lead for most purposes (cannonballs remained iron). Modern steel and steel-core bullets are a thing, and you could use iron just as easily for them (though iron-core probably wouldn't have the desired result on Fae). The issue is that iron is less dense and loses velocity faster, but its greater hardness will help it penetrate better at close range. An additional drawback is that it will wear barrels much faster, though a high-grade steel bore will still hold up somewhat.<br /> <br /> If you're going Fae or Changeling-hunting, then you will bring the weapons that will help you hurt them better, regardless of long-term drawbacks. It's like casting silver bullets (a bitch to do casually, btw) or loading shotshells with silver scrap--you're going out loaded for Uratha and don't care about the difficulty and/or consequences.<br /> <br /> So, yes, bridgeburners leveraging easy access to suitable iron for their machinegun bullets would totally be a thing all the way to modern days. Just picture the fun of one with a fedora and cigar, rocking their 100-round drum in Chi-town Changeling Noir.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 03-29-2019, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T11:45:43-07:00","id":1300889,"title":"","content":"If we're still on the subject of Iron, &quot;Rites of Spring&quot; from Lost 1e lays it out pretty well. The 'why' of the matter is left ambiguous (though multiple potential origin stories for the reason are presented for an ST to use if they wish).<br /> <br /> The standard they set up is whether or not the iron has been melted (heated) in some way. So iron ore would deal aggravated, but pig iron would not. They also possess the means by which someone can &quot;Hand Forge&quot; Iron (quite literally bending the ore into shape with strength alone), though this requires blacksmithing tools and a minimum of 4 strength. <br /> <br /> It's on Page 86 for anyone who has the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T12:48:51-07:00","id":1301120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300689#post1300689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just picture the fun of one with a fedora and cigar, rocking their 100-round drum in Chi-town Changeling Noir.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Al Capone and his gang were secretly a hunter compact- gangsters sure, but also a secret compact. I'd run that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T12:52:32-07:00","id":1301122,"title":"","content":"What would the availability of a cold iron item be and would it be 'cheaper' during a Victorian era game?<br /> Though I do find it interesting that in changeling it doesn't play up the 'never touched by flame' side of the mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T13:08:34-07:00","id":1301127,"title":"","content":"If you mean that &quot;the ore can't even touch flame&quot; then yeah, ling doesn't say that. But if you mean the ore can't be heated, then Rites of Spring begs to differ. It lists iron ore as the thing that deals aggravated. Pig iron and other &quot;heated&quot; variants don't count.<br /> <br /> Though, it also includes several optional rules. One is that, if magic is used in the creation process, the iron is treated as &quot;cold&quot; regardless.<br /> <br /> Hm. Actually it's kinda ambiguous sometimes too. because it also gives the rule of thumb &quot;If it's usually called iron, it counts as cold iron.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","user":"GourmetBrickWall","date":". 03-30-2019, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:22:42-07:00","id":1301165,"title":"","content":"Remember that <i>Rites of Spring</i> is a 1e book. The 2e corebook updated the definition of &quot;cold iron&quot;:<br /> <br /> - If people usually call it iron (as opposed to steel etc), it's iron. Fae magic can't touch it in any way.<br /> - If it's iron by that definition, <i>and</i> it was shaped by human hands rather than by magic or a mass-production process, it's <i>cold</i> iron. It does agg to fae creatures on contact.<br /> <br /> That said, if a given ST wants to use the &quot;never heated&quot; definition, or the &quot;magic makes it cold&quot; definition, that's their prerogative. I personally like the 2e version better since it comes into play more often: according to RoS rules, Hunters with cold iron are practically impossible (since they'd either need magic or the ability to find and work meteoric iron without heat), and on the flipside any type of magic can turn iron &quot;cold&quot; trivially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:07:36-07:00","id":1301355,"title":"","content":"Dreamsteps describes physically stepping into someone else's dream, implying the Changeling would be physically present within.<br /> However, they pass through the Gate of Ivory to do so, which would normally imply they are in Dream Form, with their body unconscious in the physical world.<br /> <br /> Which is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:43:41-07:00","id":1301479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1301355#post1301355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreamsteps describes physically stepping into someone else's dream, implying the Changeling would be physically present within.<br /> However, they pass through the Gate of Ivory to do so, which would normally imply they are in Dream Form, with their body unconscious in the physical world.<br /> <br /> Which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dream form. The description is metaphorical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T18:37:50-07:00","id":1301488,"title":"","content":"Oh does humans who get the hedge denizen condition keep their integrity trait? I am asking because one of my players got turned into a hob","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T20:50:45-07:00","id":1301499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1301488#post1301488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh does humans who get the hedge denizen condition keep their integrity trait? I am asking because one of my players got turned into a hob</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:10:05-07:00","id":1301630,"title":"","content":"Court Bargains i have a question! Ignoring when the bargain is with a universal concept like a season, emotion or natural phenomenon.They also can bargain with a specific supernatural creature, like a vampire, spirit, qashmal, angel and so on right? Is there a rule for what kind of creature is vieable for such a bargain. Like a corporeal supernatural((vampires and so on)) needs to have blood potency 6+ and spirits and the like must rank 6+? Or is it more open ended than that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:18:20-07:00","id":1301634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1301630#post1301630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Court Bargains i have a question! Ignoring when the bargain is with a universal concept like a season, emotion or natural phenomenon.They also can bargain with a specific supernatural creature, like a vampire, spirit, qashmal, angel and so on right? Is there a rule for what kind of creature is vieable for such a bargain. Like a corporeal supernatural((vampires and so on)) needs to have blood potency 6+ and spirits and the like must rank 6+? Or is it more open ended than that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was under the impression that such bargains (where the changeling or Court gets a certain benefit or protection in return for a favor, service or certain restrictions imposed on the changeling/Court) can only be struck with the Wyrd itself, or with creatures that are somehow connected to the Wyrd, such as True Fae, Titles, spirits and other entities connected to Arcadia or the Hedge, perhaps even powerful changelings and goblins.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong though.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about the opposite (where the changeling provides a service to the person who wants to bargain with her, in return for camouflage from the Gentry and Huntsmen) I think the bargain has to be with a human mortal (mages count as both human and mortal, as do hunters of course, but other than that I don't think any of the other splats count as human nor mortal, based on the &quot;Mortals?&quot; section in Hunter: The Vigil 1e, found on page 159).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-01-2019, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:40:28-07:00","id":1301641,"title":"","content":"It says that non fae creatures also counts when it comes to bargaining..so it doesn't strictly have to be humans, look at page 215 if you want to check it out. I also know that court bargains with creatures not of the wyrd are possible, but i just wanted to have the rules for it clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T09:13:47-07:00","id":1301651,"title":"","content":"Do you have the book? I remember something similar but i think its a vague idea with no mechanics. Just a storyteller fiat thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:37:09-07:00","id":1301702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1301630#post1301630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a rule for what kind of creature is vieable for such a bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, anything, but since most participants in a Bargain are not going to have the kind of pull needed to force the Gentry into a pattern of behavior on their own, would-be Courts of discrete patrons hoping to last are advised to pick a partner who can keep up their end of the Bargain by intervention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T17:22:44-07:00","id":1301761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1301641#post1301641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says that non fae creatures also counts when it comes to bargaining..so it doesn't strictly have to be humans, look at page 215 if you want to check it out. I also know that court bargains with creatures not of the wyrd are possible, but i just wanted to have the rules for it clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you are right.<br /> <br /> Other than what's written on p. 307 in CTL 2e, I couldn't find anything about court bargains. Quite frankly, the paragraph kinda confuses me. It speaks of a bargain with a promethean who feeds his Disquiet to the astronomical clock in Prague, which the court turns into Glamour, but the section doesn't explain how that works, which leaved me quite puzzled. <br /> <br /> Which begs the question: do bargains in and of themselves have any power (other than concealing the changeling from the Gentry when bargaining with a human)? Or does the power gained through a bargain come from the participants?<br /> <br /> How does one go about turning Disquiet into Glamour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T18:01:28-07:00","id":1301769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1301761#post1301761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one go about turning Disquiet into Glamour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably by Harvesting the population-wide surges of strong emotions like Wrath, Fear and Desire generated by various forms of Disquiet. Perhaps as part of the Bargain, this emotional draining actually lessens the population-wide psychological effects of Disquiet.<br /> <br /> Actually, how does this sound as a house-rule: if a Changeling Harvests from someone with a Condition tied to an overpowering form of the emotion the Changeling is Harvesting, the Changeling can resolve the Condition and grant the person a Beat (or a Willpower for NPCs) in exchange for one bonus glamour?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:26:44-07:00","id":1302025,"title":"","content":"Oh i may have blinked and missed it, but what happens to mortals that end up in the hedge...and in the thorns but who are not avowed or taken by the gentry. LIke let's say a cell of hunters end up in the hedge and have to fight to survive it and get out, what happens to them? Like are they changed or do they manage to remain human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:38:47-07:00","id":1302030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1302025#post1302025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh i may have blinked and missed it, but what happens to mortals that end up in the hedge...and in the thorns but who are not avowed or taken by the gentry. LIke let's say a cell of hunters end up in the hedge and have to fight to survive it and get out, what happens to them? Like are they changed or do they manage to remain human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking? Their lack of ability to use Hedgespinning or process goblin fruit means they die, get roped into hobgoblin deals, or luck out and get found by something that can bring them back to the paths or the mortal world. They don't receive any special effects from having been in the Hedge other than what happened to them in there (and sometimes not even that) by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:59:52-07:00","id":1302033,"title":"","content":"Away from my book as well as lazy and have three Harvesting questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Are there any benefits to an Exceptional Success on a Harvest roll besides gaining 5 or more Glamour (which is pretty sweet already)?<br /> <br /> 2) If the former is true, can kith abilities (specifically the ones that modify ES) effect Harvest rolls?<br /> <br /> 3) Can you harvest emotions induced or strengthened by Contracts? Pretty sure the answer is a hard no to prevent possible massive glamour loops and weird fridge logic, but I just want to be sure.<br /> <br /> P.S. 3 likes on my previous post! Does that mean people like my proposed house-rule?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:49:34-07:00","id":1302051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1302033#post1302033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Away from my book as well as lazy and have three Harvesting questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Are there any benefits to an Exceptional Success on a Harvest roll besides gaining 5 or more Glamour (which is pretty sweet already)?<br /> <br /> 2) If the former is true, can kith abilities (specifically the ones that modify ES) effect Harvest rolls?<br /> <br /> 3) Can you harvest emotions induced or strengthened by Contracts? Pretty sure the answer is a hard no to prevent possible massive glamour loops and weird fridge logic, but I just want to be sure.<br /> <br /> P.S. 3 likes on my previous post! Does that mean people like my proposed house-rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though I recently read CTL 2e from cover to cover, I'm still coming to grips with this splat, so I don't know if I can answer your questions with any certainty. I will give it my best shot though:<br /> <br /> 1) There is nothing in CTL 2e about gaining an exceptional success on a harvest roll, so I'm going to assume nothing happens other than gaining more glamour.<br /> <br /> 2) I don't think there is a hard rule against using your Kith abilities in conjunction with harvesting, but what would be the point? Gaining an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5 isn't going to do anything for your harvest, unless you rule that gaining an exceptional success on 3 dice means the same as gaining 5 successes, thus giving you 5 Glamour for 3 successes.<br /> <br /> 3) The core CTL 2e book says nothing about this, but if you think it's safer to say &quot;no, you can't harvest emotions induced or strengthened by Contracts&quot; then go for it. With these sort of things I usually decide on a case by case basis. If I think it makes sense and doesn't break the game, I'll allow it. If I think my players are trying to game the system or gain an unfair advantage (unfair from a game perspective), I'll no longer allow it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, yes, I 'liked' your post because of the house-rule suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T04:29:04-07:00","id":1302159,"title":"","content":"The general rule for ES is to gain a relevant Condition (or impart one on another character, if it makes sense). Just do that whenever something doesn't list any Exceptional effects. Perhaps something to make it easier to manipulate the emotional state of those you harvested from, or a Condition on them giving them a harder time expressing the harvested feeling for some time because you gained so much Glamour from them.<br /> <br /> As for the third question, I would compare how much Glamour the Contract costs to use in that way with how many extra dice on the Harvest roll you can reliably get from using the Contract. If you can reliably gain more Glamour than it costs by using the Contract, I'd probably rule that it can't be used.<br /> Contracts that were to enforce a feeling rather than manipulating a character towards it might also be a no from me just because it's less the character and more the magic. It's their feelings, but not their <i>own</i> feelings, if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:22:06-07:00","id":1302172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1302159#post1302159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general rule for ES is to gain a relevant Condition (or impart one on another character, if it makes sense). Just do that whenever something doesn't list any Exceptional effects. Perhaps something to make it easier to manipulate the emotional state of those you harvested from, or a Condition on them giving them a harder time expressing the harvested feeling for some time because you gained so much Glamour from them.<br /> <br /> As for the third question, I would compare how much Glamour the Contract costs to use in that way with how many extra dice on the Harvest roll you can reliably get from using the Contract. If you can reliably gain more Glamour than it costs by using the Contract, I'd probably rule that it can't be used.<br /> Contracts that were to enforce a feeling rather than manipulating a character towards it might also be a no from me just because it's less the character and more the magic. It's their feelings, but not their <i>own</i> feelings, if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it. That was why i was pretty sure it was no. You should not be able to create a feeling almost entirely out of glamour and then get more glamour from it than you put in. I know that a lot of contracts probably already ignore conservation of mass and energy, but I see that as glamour filling in the gaps. And the Wyrd is the enforcer of equivalent exchange. So it would break at least my headcanon rules to put 1 glamour into a system and get out 3 glamour without any extra input<br /> <br /> EDIT: unless you see it as the magic opening a deeper and richer mine shaft of sorts. In which case, I would still rule the possible glampur-farming loops as too broken<br /> <br /> Although... What happens when you harvest someone with no Willpower left in their pool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-03-2019, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T05:06:08-07:00","id":1302524,"title":"","content":"How does dream form work?<br /> A changeling has 3 attributes: Power equal to presence , Finess equal to manipulation, Resistance equal to composure, and Dream Heath equal to Clarity+Max Wyrd attribute. <br /> But have skill or use spirit/ghost rules? And defense/initiative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T15:41:19-07:00","id":1302665,"title":"","content":"The listed stats for Dream Forms mentions which stats they replace. All other stats are intact, including Skills and all derived traits (except Health, of course). You might have to recalculate them, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T16:49:54-07:00","id":1302677,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so if you are in dream form and you happen to start a combat inside someone's dream, you basically roll Presence + Brawl or Presence + Weaponry or Manipulation + Firearms, instead of Strength + Brawl or Strength + Weaponry or Dexterity + Firearms.<br /> <br /> It basically means that Social primary characters will likely be the strongest in dream form. I find this a weird but interesting design choice personally. It means that your anti-social Ogre buddy who always reliably crushes skulls with his fists might suddenly find himself rather useless in dream combat, while the weak but socially savvy Fairest is potentially the heavy hitter in dream form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T18:07:26-07:00","id":1302698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1302677#post1302677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so if you are in dream form and you happen to start a combat inside someone's dream, you basically roll Presence + Brawl or Presence + Weaponry or Manipulation + Firearms, instead of Strength + Brawl or Strength + Weaponry or Dexterity + Firearms.<br /> <br /> It basically means that Social primary characters will likely be the strongest in dream form. I find this a weird but interesting design choice personally. It means that your anti-social Ogre buddy who always reliably crushes skulls with his fists might suddenly find himself rather useless in dream combat, while the weak but socially savvy Fairest is potentially the heavy hitter in dream form</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, it might be interesting to have a homebrew Merit that lets you use e.g. your Mental attributes instead of your Socials for calculating dream-form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T22:32:02-07:00","id":1302743,"title":"","content":"If a changeling enter in a dream through the gate of Horn, are in his physical form whit his normal health trait, and if are kill he dies (real death). Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9092,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","user":"Nesky","date":". 04-05-2019, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T02:37:57-07:00","id":1302766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1302743#post1302743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a changeling enter in a dream through the gate of Horn, are in his physical form whit his normal health trait, and if are kill he dies (real die). Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:57:47-07:00","id":1302960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1302743#post1302743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a changeling enter in a dream through the gate of Horn, are in his physical form whit his normal health trait, and if are kill he dies (real death). Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and also uses his normal Attributes rather than the simplified Attributes based on his Social Attributes. So a changeling who is physically present in someone's dream still uses Strength and Dexterity to attack, rather than Presence and Manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T19:17:47-07:00","id":1303691,"title":"","content":"When a character with a major template becomes a Hedge Denizen, or Goblin Queen, do they gain a Wyrd trait and Glamour pool?<br /> <br /> The sample Goblin Queen has Wyrd and Glamour despite being a mortal turned Goblin Queen, but that seems likely to be just an artifact of having been built directly via the Hobgoblin rules. The Conditions themselves don't mention this, except to state that <i>non-supernaturals</i> that retain Goblin Contracts after reverting to their true nature can fuel them by taking bashing damage in lieu of spending Glamour.<br /> <br /> They do explicitly state that non-mortal, non-changeling characters can gain the Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit for Extra Info: </b><br /> For some further Goblin Queen info, Rose mentioned that when a human takes the place of a Goblin Queen, they take on the seeming and kith of the prior Queen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 04-09-2019, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T07:49:27-07:00","id":1304189,"title":"","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>' question about Beasts using Family Resemblance, I've got a question about Chagelings making a bargain with other splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL2e Bargains - Systems</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings cannot swear bargains with other fae<br /> creatures, including changelings, and prefer to do so with<br /> human beings. Magical beings unaffiliated with the Wyrd<br /> can agree to bargains, but doing so sometimes has strange<br /> side effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are some potential side effects if a Changeling were to make a bargain with a Mage, a Vampire, or some other supernatural creature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T08:19:49-07:00","id":1304197,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it's meant to be Storyteller fiat. A thread for creating an optional homebrew mechanical system around it for fun could be nice thouch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:01:48-07:00","id":1304208,"title":"","content":"Well, if Bargains are intended to help you hide among humanity, I guess you hide better among whatever you dealt with, for starters.<br /> <br /> Mild and Twisted Kinship Merit-esque possibilities await.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T14:09:15-07:00","id":1304313,"title":"","content":"Fun and exciting things! Maybe a bargain with a vampire lets you fight back against the Predatory Aura with Attr + Wyrd, imposing Bedlam on a win, and/or gives you Blood Sympathy to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T12:17:50-07:00","id":1304660,"title":"","content":"Can Fetches reproduce or all of them are sterile? I wanted to plot twist with one of the Fetches having kids, but I don't really know if fetches can have kids<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25121-oniverse","name":"Oniverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T12:35:36-07:00","id":1304671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oniverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1304660#post1304660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Fetches reproduce or all of them are sterile? I wanted to plot twist with one of the Fetches having kids, but I don't really know if fetches can have kids</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can find there are no rules regarding this in the CtL2 book. In my game Fetches can reproduce, at least with humans, and those children are fully human. The decision was based solely on what I felt would make for the most compelling story for the character, I don't have any wider lore justification for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T12:58:21-07:00","id":1304678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oniverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1304660#post1304660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Fetches reproduce or all of them are sterile? I wanted to plot twist with one of the Fetches having kids, but I don't really know if fetches can have kids</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, fetches are sterile, except if you use the optional rules in Autumn Nightmares, pp. 104-106, which say it can happen in exceptional circumstances, and give rules for two potential outcomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T18:22:38-07:00","id":1304738,"title":"","content":"I think it would be extremely interesting if the child of a Fetch is automatically Fae-touched and linked to the changeling who the Fetch replaced. The child is not necessarily aware of this or even understand why he's different, but he'd probably dream about his changeling &quot;parent&quot; often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:21:27-07:00","id":1304979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oniverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1304660#post1304660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Fetches reproduce or all of them are sterile? I wanted to plot twist with one of the Fetches having kids, but I don't really know if fetches can have kids</div> </div> </div> </div>I know when I was writing my changeling based story the Fetch had a child, but that child was adopted, but loved no less than if she was his own. I think the real answer now is it varies fetch to fetch, and how much effort and/or thought the keeper put into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:33:41-07:00","id":1304985,"title":"","content":"I do have a question. In a character's background they are given an item crafted during a shared durance by another changeling. That item was made especially for them (in this chain armor made of links cast from the heart of a Glacier, the love of a Shield maiden, quenched in the blood of a wyrm.<br /> <br /> Of the 3 types of Token which would best represent this gift from a Shield Maiden to her Berserker Lover? I don't think it quite fits the stolen token, because the keeper didn't forge it (nor is it important to them) it was crafted by a slave for a slave not by their command. Nor was it made by leaving something in the thorns, it was crafted in arcadia from the stuff of Arcadia, and I'm not sure oath bound fits it either, maybe it might?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T22:40:42-07:00","id":1304993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1304985#post1304985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a question. In a character's background they are given an item crafted during a shared durance by another changeling. That item was made especially for them (in this chain armor made of links cast from the heart of a Glacier, the love of a Shield maiden, quenched in the blood of a wyrm.<br /> <br /> Of the 3 types of Token which would best represent this gift from a Shield Maiden to her Berserker Lover? I don't think it quite fits the stolen token, because the keeper didn't forge it (nor is it important to them) it was crafted by a slave for a slave not by their command. Nor was it made by leaving something in the thorns, it was crafted in arcadia from the stuff of Arcadia, and I'm not sure oath bound fits it either, maybe it might?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a special mechanic to it that's not part of the token's actual effect? If not, it's Hedge-forged. If so, it's oath-forged or stolen, depending.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that non-stolen tokens are just grouped the way they are as methods of <i>deliberate creation in the course of a game</i>. Tokens made by leaving something important to you in the darkest parts of the Hedge happen to be the standard from which the other varieties deviate, but it's in the text that tokens can form in less typical circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T04:55:18-07:00","id":1305237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1304993#post1304993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a special mechanic to it that's not part of the token's actual effect? If not, it's Hedge-forged. If so, it's oath-forged or stolen, depending.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that non-stolen tokens are just grouped the way they are as methods of <i>deliberate creation in the course of a game</i>. Tokens made by leaving something important to you in the darkest parts of the Hedge happen to be the standard from which the other varieties deviate, but it's in the text that tokens can form in less typical circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to figure out what sort of Token it would be before I started to think up powers, rather than fitting the power of the token to the effect, I wanted fit the token type to the narrative of token, and then using that info craft a power. My ST got back to me and pointed out that this token was crafted in the keepers Domain out of material from there, and was known to the keeper. As such they have a innate mystical connection to it and Stolen Token works for the narrative.<br /> <br /> So now I need to think of a good effect worthy of that armor, combat effects are harder to gauge in changeling right now. I was thinking about having it make use of the better of defense or wits and allowing the user to apply their defense to firearms based attacks? But that feels more like a 1 dot effect.<br /> <br /> Then I thought maybe adding a number of Automatic successes to strength rolls seeing it as making him into a powerful warrior so the keeper will leave him alone (at the cost of doing bashing damage if he fails to meet his mark as his muscles hyper extend joints or just rip himself apart) or something like upping defense by doing dex+wits+athletics would be good (plus ignoring all wound effects up to Aggravated damage) at the cost of needing to be humpty-dumpty'ied back together again (Double the difficulty to treat injuries) because you couldn't feel pain and kept fighting past the point most people would have passed out from pain impact trauma or blood loss because the armor numbed you to pain and kept splinting your wounds. Thus allowing you to fight beyond human capacity...but wrecking your body in the process (almost making it like guts Berserker Armor).<br /> <br /> But while I'm not sure the first effect is worthy of 3 dots seems a bit anemic. Second might be a bit too strong if the drawback isn't strong enough. Do we have a token help thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:28:29-07:00","id":1305381,"title":"","content":"Lost 2e provides two seemings to go with each kith. Does this mean that the kith is restricted to these seemings, or merely examples? <br /> <br /> Like, I can see an Elemental gristlegrinder meant to embody the swallowing sea, or a beast bright one embodying a firefly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:35:56-07:00","id":1305383,"title":"","content":"It's meant to be examples. Kiths can go with any Seeming, though some combinations are obviously more intuitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:47:21-07:00","id":1305384,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Yeah, see the page now. Could've sworn that was the way it was. Page 92.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25172-gourmetbrickwall","name":"GourmetBrickWall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:50:33-07:00","id":1305385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1305237#post1305237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was trying to figure out what sort of Token it would be before I started to think up powers, rather than fitting the power of the token to the effect, I wanted fit the token type to the narrative of token, and then using that info craft a power. My ST got back to me and pointed out that this token was crafted in the keepers Domain out of material from there, and was known to the keeper. As such they have a innate mystical connection to it and Stolen Token works for the narrative.<br /> <br /> So now I need to think of a good effect worthy of that armor, combat effects are harder to gauge in changeling right now. I was thinking about having it make use of the better of defense or wits and allowing the user to apply their defense to firearms based attacks? But that feels more like a 1 dot effect.<br /> <br /> Then I thought maybe adding a number of Automatic successes to strength rolls seeing it as making him into a powerful warrior so the keeper will leave him alone (at the cost of doing bashing damage if he fails to meet his mark as his muscles hyper extend joints or just rip himself apart) or something like upping defense by doing dex+wits+athletics would be good (plus ignoring all wound effects up to Aggravated damage) at the cost of needing to be humpty-dumpty'ied back together again (Double the difficulty to treat injuries) because you couldn't feel pain and kept fighting past the point most people would have passed out from pain impact trauma or blood loss because the armor numbed you to pain and kept splinting your wounds. Thus allowing you to fight beyond human capacity...but wrecking your body in the process (almost making it like guts Berserker Armor).<br /> <br /> But while I'm not sure the first effect is worthy of 3 dots seems a bit anemic. Second might be a bit too strong if the drawback isn't strong enough. Do we have a token help thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have access to Hurt Locker you might consider using the Punch Drunk merit as the basis for a berserker effect. It's a two dot merit that allows a character to spend a willpower point to upgrade damage instead of letting their last box fill and potentially knock them out. Ignoring wound penalties is also a reasonable effect, but to ignore them completely is already a three dot merit, per iron stamina in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Using the higher of wits or dex is one of those effects that's variable and potentially prone to abuse. For many characters it's only going to be a one point difference, but Changelings can pretty easily reach five in one or the other at character creation and have 10 defense without sacrificing much. Definitely don't add them both together, defense is already a hefty dice penalty in a system that normally caps at -5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T20:57:46-07:00","id":1305393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1305385#post1305385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you have access to Hurt Locker you might consider using the Punch Drunk merit as the basis for a berserker effect. It's a two dot merit that allows a character to spend a willpower point to upgrade damage instead of letting their last box fill and potentially knock them out. Ignoring wound penalties is also a reasonable effect, but to ignore them completely is already a three dot merit, per iron stamina in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Using the higher of wits or dex is one of those effects that's variable and potentially prone to abuse. For many characters it's only going to be a one point difference, but Changelings can pretty easily reach five in one or the other at character creation and have 10 defense without sacrificing much. Definitely don't add them both together, defense is already a hefty dice penalty in a system that normally caps at -5.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my case my wits and dex are both 2. So using the best of either is waisted on me. I thought about adding the effective background rating as an alternative. Though maybe just being able to ignore wound penalties and apply defense against all ranged attacks is good enough?<br /> <br /> Or going with the strength boost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 04-17-2019, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T02:53:09-07:00","id":1306786,"title":"","content":"Can I use Dreamsteps as consequences for a broken seal statement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T07:46:26-07:00","id":1306853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1306786#post1306786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use Dreamsteps as consequences for a broken seal statement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not in any meaningful sense, though a broken sealing might constitute an active invitation into the character's Bastion for the scene in which it's broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:49:02-07:00","id":1308379,"title":"","content":"Would the Seizing The Edge, Greyhound or Relentless merits affect chases through the Hedge in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-27-2019, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T14:31:52-07:00","id":1308789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1303691#post1303691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a character with a major template becomes a Hedge Denizen, or Goblin Queen, do they gain a Wyrd trait and Glamour pool?<br /> <br /> The sample Goblin Queen has Wyrd and Glamour despite being a mortal turned Goblin Queen, but that seems likely to be just an artifact of having been built directly via the Hobgoblin rules. The Conditions themselves don't mention this, except to state that <i>non-supernaturals</i> that retain Goblin Contracts after reverting to their true nature can fuel them by taking bashing damage in lieu of spending Glamour.<br /> <br /> They do explicitly state that non-mortal, non-changeling characters can gain the Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit for Extra Info: </b><br /> For some further Goblin Queen info, Rose mentioned that when a human takes the place of a Goblin Queen, they take on the seeming and kith of the prior Queen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone want to take a stab at this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1308379#post1308379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Seizing The Edge, Greyhound or Relentless merits affect chases through the Hedge in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I'd be inclined to say no, but the system is structured to take physical Speed and Initiative into account, even assigning placeholder values to the Hedge itself, so it seems like those merits may well be meant to apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Avoiding a double post. 04-29-2019, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T15:41:50-07:00","id":1309943,"title":"","content":"What's the point of blessing of spring if all damage and conditions return?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T16:53:58-07:00","id":1309950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1309943#post1309943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of blessing of spring if all damage and conditions return?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a temporary full-restore that can be used for other things as well, which is a different niche than Gift of Warm Blood fills.<br /> <br /> You want to help a devastated town rebuild from disaster? Wait for spring to arrive and bring adults back to the prime of their youth, help children be born in a fraction of the time it would normally take, raise certain crops to fruiting, and similarly make use of the capacity to briefly shunt a target to a beneficial time in their life-cycle. You want to heal somebody in a way that lasts? Use the Contract that asks you to bleed and drain yourself in return for salving even the most horrendous form of damage in the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T17:13:10-07:00","id":1309953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1309950#post1309950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a temporary full-restore that can be used for other things as well, which is a different niche than Gift of Warm Blood fills.<br /> <br /> You want to help a devastated town rebuild from disaster? Wait for spring to arrive and bring adults back to the prime of their youth, help children be born in a fraction of the time it would normally take, raise certain crops to fruiting, and similarly make use of the capacity to briefly shunt a target to a beneficial time in their life-cycle. You want to heal somebody in a way that lasts? Use the Contract that asks you to bleed and drain yourself in return for salving even the most horrendous form of damage in the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really doesn't help if all it does is make you worse off. It also only works on one person at a time, lasts one scene and takes a day to make the cordial. It seems like it'd be better as a permanent once per story use power than something that can be used over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T17:34:09-07:00","id":1309958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1309953#post1309953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really doesn't help if all it does is make you worse off.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes you potentially less than exactly as badly off as you were at the start, plus the need for a hunger binge to make up for missing time. There are worse surcharges to pay for being able to clear most things that aren't injury from your system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also only works on one person at a time, </div> </div> </div>This is irrelevant, seeing as none of the other restorative Contracts do any differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> lasts one scene </div> </div> </div>A unit of time which is explicitly divided by dramatic events, which means the duration of this temporary restoration is marked out as &quot;long enough to do something important.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and takes a day to make the cordial. </div> </div> </div>Which is a prerequisite activity rather than a part of the Contract. Nothing about the framing suggests that the cordial can't be prepared in advance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like it'd be better as a permanent once per story use power than something that can be used over and over again. </div> </div> </div>That's not what it's for. &quot;Clear temporary poisons and diseases from the target's system or make plants that aren't goblin fruits yield a bounty&quot; are still lasting results.<br /> <br /> You asked what the point of the Contract is. The simple answer is that it's a niche power. It's allowed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T18:08:23-07:00","id":1309962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1309958#post1309958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes you potentially less than exactly as badly off as you were at the start, plus the need for a hunger binge to make up for missing time. There are worse surcharges to pay for being able to clear most things that aren't injury from your system.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you revert to what you were before. You lose any health you might have healed and anything you cured. But now you are also hungry so yeah it's worse. I remember this power being a pretty decent healing ability in the previous edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You asked what the point of the Contract is. The simple answer is that it's a niche power. It's allowed to be. </div> </div> </div>I did but it doesn't really explain why have a power that does nothing. Actually it's one that could kill you if you get into a fight and take too much damage. And yes it does other things which makes it useful especially when it works on goblin fruit. However, I'm wondering why have a heal all that's not actually a heal all.<br /> <br /> Edit- I also don't know what this has to do with spring. Spring is a permanent change. having to lose one year of life for a healthy body makes sense. Having to lose one year then go back to what you were doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-04-2019, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T21:49:35-07:00","id":1309975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1309962#post1309962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you revert to what you were before. You lose any health you might have healed and anything you cured. But now you are also hungry so yeah it's worse. I remember this power being a pretty decent healing ability in the previous edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you remember it completely wrong, because Yesterday's Birth didn't have any healing effect at all, explicitly only moved the target's growth forward one season without exceptional success, and included a non-negotiable cost of three Glamour and a Willpower dot to use on humans on top of the follow-up need for feed. Its 2e inheritor is both more flexible and less expensive.<br /> <br /> You may be thinking, again, of Warmth of the Blood, the Contract expressly and solely for healing wounds which comes directly before Yesterday's Birth in the Eternal Spring list and exists in 2e with roughly the same basic effect except better and with a more onerous catch in the form of Gift of Warm Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did but it doesn't really explain why have a power that does nothing. Actually it's one that could kill you if you get into a fight and take too much damage. </div> </div> </div>Why do you imagine a power whose effects on plants and animals are expressly brought up and that has extra costs to use on people is supposed to be used for a violent encounter in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes it does other things which makes it useful especially when it works on goblin fruit. However, I'm wondering why have a heal all that's not actually a heal all. </div> </div> </div>Because it's not a healing power. This is there so you can let the livestock start replenishing their numbers despite poor health or bring in a seasonally-appropriate harvest, not so that you can press fast-forward on the growth of your community.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit- I also don't know what this has to do with spring. Spring is a permanent change. having to lose one year of life for a healthy body makes sense. Having to lose one year then go back to what you were doesn't. </div> </div> </div>You don't lose a year! If you're a pregnant human or animal your pregnancy gets advanced twelve months and if the kids are out then they're out to stay, but Spring is a temporary state and invoking it with magic for probably-agricultural reasons isn't something that exists to make people well on a permanent basis by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T22:36:09-07:00","id":1309983,"title":"","content":"If it's just plans and births why does it heal and then revert. It used to be a permanent growth and the text implies that only the healing goes way not the age that you lost for temporary healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T23:59:03-07:00","id":1309994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1309983#post1309983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's just plans and births why does it heal and then revert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's easier to do the things you'd use this Contract for when the target is not literally dying of poison and blunt force trauma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It used to be a permanent growth </div> </div> </div>Again, it also used to cost a permanent resource and required the extra nutrition immediately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the text implies that only the healing goes way not the age that you lost for temporary healing. </div> </div> </div>Literally the only thing implying this is that you're reading discussion of &quot;[time] worth of growth&quot; as if it took days off of an abstracted lifespan counter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:55:05-07:00","id":1310053,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest. The growth and healing seems like it should be permanent through the expenditure of a willpower dot. I just don't see the need for a temporary full heal that later gets completely undone but also inflicts you with an additional tilt. Either that or remove that aspect of the power because it could get someone killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T10:30:01-07:00","id":1310061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1310053#post1310053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest. The growth and healing seems like it should be permanent through the expenditure of a willpower dot. I just don't see the need for a temporary full heal that later gets completely undone but also inflicts you with an additional tilt. Either that or remove that aspect of the power because it could get someone killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're starting to become a repeating recrepeating recrepeating recrepeating recrepeating record.<br /> <br /> The logic of this has been explained-it's there for basically a magical moment in time where people have all the youth and health they need to do things that matter to them(and probably to the changeling)-,they aren't changing the power at this point, and if you object, you can houserule it, and it seems like you have a clear idea of what you want it to do.<br /> <br /> So what are you hoping to achieve here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T11:37:36-07:00","id":1310075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1310061#post1310061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're starting to become a repeating recrepeating recrepeating recrepeating recrepeating record.<br /> <br /> The logic of this has been explained-it's there for basically a magical moment in time where people have all the youth and health they need to do things that matter to them(and probably to the changeling)-,they aren't changing the power at this point, and if you object, you can houserule it, and it seems like you have a clear idea of what you want it to do.<br /> <br /> So what are you hoping to achieve here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I'm trying to ask what you can do with a power like that when it only lasts a scene. Outside of temporary goblin fruits and getting a pregnant woman to give birth in an instant. It only seems good for tricking someone into thinking they're healthy and then doing enough damage so that they die the next scene from over extending themselves.<br /> <br /> Edit- Also, the way birth works and how a scene works, it shouldn't actually be enough time to birth a child unless it's through a c-section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-05-2019, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T12:40:44-07:00","id":1310088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1310075#post1310075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I'm trying to ask what you can do with a power like that when it only lasts a scene. Outside of temporary goblin fruits and getting a pregnant woman to give birth in an instant. It only seems good for tricking someone into thinking they're healthy and then doing enough damage so that they die the next scene from over extending themselves.<br /> <br /> Edit- Also, the way birth works and how a scene works, it shouldn't actually be enough time to birth a child unless it's through a c-section.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the numerical measurement of a scene, then?<br /> <br /> Hint: There is none because it is a dramatic unit of time, and therefore covers the time needed for the drama to occur and achieve payout. A scene could be a couple of seconds or the payout of several years. This is film language, think of how films handle it, and how you have definitely seen scenes where years pass. What keeps this from being overpowered is that the nature of the genre provides a clear sense of what's going on-this is &quot;until the clock strikes twelve&quot; sort of stuff, Till the Moment Is Gone sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> As for the logistics and realities, dude, this is fairy magic going on. A few hours is a lifetime to the fae, and people who have only just met could have a household full of children before the sun is born again. The Contract is a momentary suspension of reality, a slice of time so infused with desire that, in this hour that goes on forever, <i>anything</i> could happen. The dream, of course, ends, and time and tide take what is owed-but what is left is promised and therefore kept.<br /> <br /> This is fairy magic. This is wishes and illusions and dreams and eternal moments and blinked forevers and things just working out. It's not hard when you let yourself surrender and join the dance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T13:14:37-07:00","id":1310096,"title":"","content":"I suppose my problem is that a scene's usually just been at most a few hours in the games I've played. Which is why it's not designated a day but if changeling's get scenes which are much longer than normal it would have more uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T16:00:33-07:00","id":1310124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1310088#post1310088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the numerical measurement of a scene, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it one hour?<br /> At least when a numerical measurement is sought. It was a while ago but I recall seeing the whole scene/chapter/story/chronicle terminology in a chart in some book. Even if I'm recalling it from first edition, I know that at least Mage still equates a scene with an hour when it comes to spell duration. And even in other games it tend to be turns &lt; scenes &lt; days in terms of supernatural power durations. Vampire has a few Disciplines where part of the effect can last beyond the scene to the end of the night, and at least one that is upgraded from a scene to a full night if rolling an ES.<br /> <br /> Edit: I was looking up blood bonds for another thread and found that a third stage blood bond upgrades the duration of Disciplines. The progression is one scene -&gt; night -&gt; week -&gt; month -&gt; year.<br /> Considering that it's the exact same progression as in Mage (except that it goes up to indefinite duration and uses &quot;day&quot; instead of &quot;night&quot;) I think it's safe to say that scenes aren't normally supposed to drag on for more than a couple of hours at most. When rushing through larger periods of time it shouldn't be considered a scene. It's called a time skip, and it is the progression between scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-06-2019, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T08:59:46-07:00","id":1310296,"title":"","content":"The chart of possible Breaking Points lists receiving a mind-altering Condition such as Lost or Spooked as a 2-die Clarity attack. The Contract Tumult can potentially inflict multiple such Conditions at the same time. How should one handle this situation? By rolling each Clarity attack separately? By combining the multiple attacks into a single, accumulated dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:06:38-07:00","id":1310323,"title":"","content":"As long as it's simultaneously and from a single source I'd say it's a single attack. More Conditions and more severe Conditions can definitely add dice, but not as much as one extra die per extra Condition. Perhaps every two Conditions grants a bonus die for a maximum bonus of +3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T17:34:35-07:00","id":1310432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1310124#post1310124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't it one hour?<br /> At least when a numerical measurement is sought. It was a while ago but I recall seeing the whole scene/chapter/story/chronicle terminology in a chart in some book. Even if I'm recalling it from first edition, I know that at least Mage still equates a scene with an hour when it comes to spell duration. And even in other games it tend to be turns &lt; scenes &lt; days in terms of supernatural power durations. Vampire has a few Disciplines where part of the effect can last beyond the scene to the end of the night, and at least one that is upgraded from a scene to a full night if rolling an ES.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Mage has hour-by-hour timekeeping built into other parts of its mechanics, uses a modular system for constructing the generalizable qualities of its core powers, determines whether a power is free at its baseline by criteria that are typically fixed parts of the character's splat or development, and has as part of its thematic focus the fact that it's often tempting to just re-cast the spell or push your limits at the risk of the thing being more likely to blow up in your face. Vampire similarly operates in a context where how rapidly you cycle your fuel says something about your character.<br /> <br /> Blessing of Spring has a prerequisite prep activity and a patron-appropriate Loophole, but does not occupy the framework of a game where its effect is expected to need reinforcing or strict timekeeping beyond the bounding box of &quot;a dramatic narrative beat is handled with the power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Arc is not proposing that the Contract last more than a day, but the existence of an equivalence between a scene and an hour in a game where cascade complication is an issue and how many hours a ritual will take is important doesn't mean the Antler Crown can't make an afternoon of seeing how Jimmy Short takes to a growth spurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T17:45:59-07:00","id":1310433,"title":"","content":"^Pretty much that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T16:02:43-07:00","id":1311299,"title":"","content":"Just wondering, what was the inspiration. Behind the Huntsman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T16:09:26-07:00","id":1311300,"title":"","content":"OOC? I think the idea was to make getting recaptured a legitimate threat. In 1e, all Changelings are terrified of being taken back to Arcadia, but it's not clear <i>how</i> they would be taken back (since they have ways of escaping pretty much anything). 2e provided an answer: the Huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T18:44:20-07:00","id":1311326,"title":"","content":"I'll be more clear (you response was excellent to why they were created though). What sorta stories and fairy tales inspired the creation of Huntsmen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T01:05:05-07:00","id":1311360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1311326#post1311326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be more clear (you response was excellent to why they were created though). What sorta stories and fairy tales inspired the creation of Huntsmen</div> </div> </div> </div>The huntsman of Snowhite comes to my mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T14:09:23-07:00","id":1312408,"title":"","content":"how much would a Hunter Cell by worth at the Goblin Market? My character Is Thinking about being a Slaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T14:16:49-07:00","id":1312409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1312408#post1312408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much would a Hunter Cell by worth at the Goblin Market? My character Is Thinking about being a Slaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) What.<br /> 2) Depends on the Hunter Cell.<br /> 3) What.<br /> 4) Consider buying the supplement Goblin Market.<br /> 5) What.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-15-2019, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T14:54:53-07:00","id":1312418,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a Tier one Hunter cell of four members Two of which have the Striking Looks merit. There all in there Early 20tes One is a physician in training ,Master Baker and Heiress to a Giant Company.<br /> <br /> Another is a Expert hacker that has a Ability to never by tracked by Supernatural mean. A mage can\u2019t cast a spell to find her, nor can a werewolf use One of her gifts.<br /> <br /> Another one At the peak of Human Potential and Knowledgeable About Philosophy. He has the striking looks merit.<br /> <br /> And the fourth is mostly Vampire Bait and is super Handsome .<br /> And what\u2019s with the two what\u2019s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T16:24:31-07:00","id":1312436,"title":"","content":"Um\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026I can imagine they'd be worth quite a lot. On the other hand, the local Changelings will <b>not</b> be happy with you selling people to the Fae.<br /> <br /> Prices at the Goblin Market are never just numbers (&quot;you'll get \u00a418.25 for this&quot;), though. The real question is, what do you want in return?<br /> <br /> I imagine first you'd want to get a letter of marque. OOC, that's where privateers came from: a letter of marque is a contract with the government that says &quot;this person can go out and basically be a pirate, and as long as they don't attack <i>our</i> ships, they're under our protection&quot;. So in the world of Changeling, I imagine a similar arrangement with the Gentry: &quot;I'll supply you with new Changelings in exchange for my own safety&quot;.<br /> <br /> But after that\u2026when you're working for <i>them</i>, the sky's the limit. There's no telling what any individual Gentry might desire, but if you can figure it out and offer them that, you can have pretty much anything you'd ever want. Want to have all memories and effects of your Durance erased, continue your life with your family from the moment before you were taken, live out a pleasant human lifespan and die surrounded by your loved ones? The Gentry can make it happen. It might not be &quot;real&quot;, it might all be a fantastic Arcadian dream, but if you can't tell the difference, does it really matter?<br /> <br /> (And after that dream ends, when you realize you're back in Arcadia under the control of the True Fae again\u2026well, you should have read the fine print.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T16:28:06-07:00","id":1312438,"title":"","content":"When its Goblin trading that stuff would be real. You dont have to go to an Arcadian realm and pretend. Goblins literally trade in bottled memories, solidified feelings, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108