lass=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1321214#post1321214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, that is quite useful. I suspected it was first edition they were referancing but wasnt sure. Should be easy enough to port to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looking at this system, I wonder if it would work for humans that find themselves in the Hedge as well - assuming they managed to survive for extended periods without getting eaten, killed, or captured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T18:50:51-07:00","id":1321448,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12034\" data-vbnamecard=\"12034\">jmkoontz1980</a> I could definitely see it. That would fit also some bits mentioning humans getting lost in the hedge and becoming hobgoblins I swear I remember reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T09:45:13-07:00","id":1323219,"title":"","content":"If an effect adds &quot;extra successes&quot; to a roll, can it upgrade the result of that roll from a standard success to an exceptional one? (Seeing as you only get the extra successes if you don't fail?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T11:14:57-07:00","id":1323236,"title":"","content":"What sort of effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T11:31:25-07:00","id":1323239,"title":"","content":"For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blessing of the Green (Spring)<br /> [fluff cut out]She may spend a point of Willpower to let one Lost<br /> (including herself) add her Mantle rating as bonus successes<br /> on a Glamour harvesting roll. [amount of times you can do this cut out] </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Extra Successes: Assuming your roll succeeds, you<br /> get a number of extra successes added to your total. </div> </div> </div>There's many effects that work like this, can get it on attacks etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T05:27:56-07:00","id":1324188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1323219#post1323219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an effect adds &quot;extra successes&quot; to a roll, can it upgrade the result of that roll from a standard success to an exceptional one? (Seeing as you only get the extra successes if you don't fail?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody? O.o I thought it was a simple enough question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, is Inciting Bedlam always going to incur the &quot;Using Glamour to force someone to change their behavior.&quot; Clarity Attack? (Well, not if you do it involuntarily I guess, since you use no Glamour then... Actually, if you use a Contract's Loophole, does that also mean it can't qualify for this?) Or is that only if you actively -force- them, rather than influencing their behaviour through their emotions? I'm leaning towards the latter, since people are not forced to behave a certain way if you change their emotions, they can still fully decide on their actions and ignore their emotions potentially?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T13:30:57-07:00","id":1324256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1323219#post1323219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an effect adds &amp;quot;extra successes&amp;quot; to a roll, can it upgrade the result of that roll from a standard success to an exceptional one? (Seeing as you only get the extra successes if you don't fail?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes, but i can t find a source to confirm it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T14:56:13-07:00","id":1324278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324256#post1324256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say yes, but i can t find a source to confirm it</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been looking, but can't find anything for or against it. :/<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, I found it. P. 176<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once you\u2019ve rolled all the dice, counted all your successes, <b>and finished any rerolls or other permutations, </b>it\u2019s time to see how your character fared. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Extra successes&quot; is listed under &quot;permutations on the same page:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Extra Successes: Assuming your roll succeeds, you<br /> get a number of extra successes added to your total.<br /> <b>This permutation</b> mostly applies to weapons, which<br /> add their damage bonus as extra successes on your<br /> attack roll </div> </div> </div>And as it points out, this means that a 4 or 5 damage weapon will always score an exceptional success on any hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-13-2019, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T00:09:25-07:00","id":1324372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324278#post1324278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been looking, but can't find anything for or against it. :/<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, I found it. P. 176<br /> <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Extra successes&amp;quot; is listed under &amp;quot;permutations on the same page:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And as it points out, this means that a 4 or 5 damage weapon will always score an exceptional success on any hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but no books list exeptional success option for weapon attack if i remember correctly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T03:21:21-07:00","id":1324395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324372#post1324372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but no books list exeptional success option for weapon attack if i remember correctly</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the default fall-back when no other option is listed is a Condition of the player's choice, with Inspired suggested as a default if you don't have a specific other idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T03:35:24-07:00","id":1324398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324395#post1324395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but the default fall-back when no other option is listed is a Condition of the player's choice, with Inspired suggested as a default if you don't have a specific other idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe a relevant tilt on the opponent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T03:40:00-07:00","id":1324401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324398#post1324398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe a relevant tilt on the opponent</div> </div> </div> </div>We're actually discussing that here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1320623-so-got-a-question-about-2e-and-attack-rolls\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...d-attack-rolls</a><br /> <br /> Guess it is better to not split the discussion if they're both sliding toward that anyway ^^ (TL;DR: I totally agree with you, Satchel thinks it is absurd.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T15:30:05-07:00","id":1324562,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that Extra Successes says <i>assuming your roll succeeds</i>, ie you check for success (and exceptional success) <i>before </i>you add those successes. This is a specific permutation overriding the general rule about resolving permutations before determining your result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T12:08:31-07:00","id":1324788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324562#post1324562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that Extra Successes says <i>assuming your roll succeeds</i>, ie you check for success (and exceptional success) <i>before </i>you add those successes. This is a specific permutation overriding the general rule about resolving permutations before determining your result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... it could have been spelled out more clearly if it was supposed to change the order in which you apply it. But this seems to be the most sensible option, so I will go with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T20:34:24-07:00","id":1326596,"title":"","content":"What resources are there for designing 2E friendly Keepers? I'm going to read some 1E books but I want to know if there's anything the designers have said/released/posted which indicate a change in Keeper powers or psychology. I understand 2E is more explicit about not all Gentry choosing to be Keepers and make Changelings, so I'm wondering what else I should be aware of. <br /> <br /> For starting material, I'm going to read through Autumn Nightmares and Grim Fears. Any other guides for making Keepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24098-maltschlitzmann","name":"MaltSchlitzmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T03:20:36-07:00","id":1326657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaltSchlitzmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1326596#post1326596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What resources are there for designing 2E friendly Keepers? I'm going to read some 1E books but I want to know if there's anything the designers have said/released/posted which indicate a change in Keeper powers or psychology. I understand 2E is more explicit about not all Gentry choosing to be Keepers and make Changelings, so I'm wondering what else I should be aware of. <br /> <br /> For starting material, I'm going to read through Autumn Nightmares and Grim Fears. Any other guides for making Keepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite honestly, the 2e core book does a marvellous job of showing how to make Gentry and what they can do, so I would check there first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T08:06:10-07:00","id":1326703,"title":"","content":"Only problem I ran into was how to run one with a Title that doesn't manifest as a singular entity, but instead as a group or a Realm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T18:45:07-07:00","id":1326849,"title":"","content":"Equinox road had the most comprehensive rules on how to build a Fae before second edition. Not surprisingly, second edition uses a fairly similar base.<br /> <br /> I will say that Autumn Nightmares and Grim Fears will give you *wildly* different perspectives on how powerful keepers are/are intended to be. Autumn Nightmares is written primarily as antagonists for starting characters, Grim Fears is decidedly about challenging even the most advanced Changelings. Like, some of the AN Fae are weaker than is even possible under the later Equinox/2e rules, and then GF throws a dragon with 40 health at you. Not a typo. 40 health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T22:57:54-07:00","id":1327360,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this isn't the thread for this but, is it possible to back any of the new supplements, or is that over, or it wasn't a different specific kickstarter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T23:22:29-07:00","id":1327364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1327360#post1327360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this isn't the thread for this but, is it possible to back any of the new supplements, or is that over, or it wasn't a different specific kickstarter?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the other 2e books?<br /> <br /> If so, then no. The ones announced and in development (the Companion and Kith and Kin) were Stretch Goal rewards for 2e corebook KS, and therefore not getting their own KS. And outside of that, typically gameline-exclusive supplements don't get their own KSs. Never say never, of course, but it's unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:50:04-07:00","id":1327408,"title":"","content":"Why does the &quot;Fae Cunning&quot; contract key off of Presence? Wits seems more logical for cunning, and Manipulation seems more logical for deceiving someone into hitting an ally. Especially with how incredibly common Presence is for contracts already, easily the #1 spot there. Also &quot;cunning&quot; is clearly more finesse than power.<br /> <br /> I am leaning towards manipulation, since Wits is already in defense and the contract feels more like a faerie trick than just dodging that way.<br /> <br /> Would you use Wits or Manipulation if you were to change it, or do you see a strong reason for keeping it Presence that I missed?<br /> <br /> Edit: actually, I counted how many contracts are associated with each attribute, and found pres is 20, manip is 15, while mental is only 22 in total and phys is 7, so I will likely move it to dex. And make using Presence a Fairest benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-25-2019, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T12:54:58-07:00","id":1327946,"title":"","content":"With Court Goodwill, if the benefit is dependant on the number of Mantle dots you have, is that also reduced by the -2 for accessing that benefit to begin with, or does it go by how many dots of Court Goodwill you have?<br /> <br /> For an example, if Mandy the Winter Courtier has Court Goodwill: Spring at 3 dots, does Mandy get +3 (her Court Goodwill amount) to rolls to seduce someone or +1 (her Court Goodwill after the -2)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T15:14:30-07:00","id":1327974,"title":"","content":"My assumption is that the numerical benefits are also reduced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T17:31:47-07:00","id":1327988,"title":"","content":"Court Goodwill providing anything beyond access to Court Contracts is news to me. Must be a 2e thing I missed in my readthrough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T19:51:15-07:00","id":1328009,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s part of the merit writeup - you can access the Mantle benefits of any court you get Court Goodwill in, but you will need Court Goodwill 3 to access Mantle 1 of that court. It also acts as a Status merit for that court and grants you a Mentor that teaches you the various aspects and contracts of that court. It\u2019s a potent merit.<br /> <br /> Also, another question. What sorts of buildings aren\u2019t affected by Hostile Takeover, outside of one owned/primarily resided in by a Changeling with Hostile Takeover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T08:17:43-07:00","id":1328096,"title":"","content":"How would carrying iron interact with a contract like Light-Shy? Let's say you're carrying an iron sword, for example; would the sword be hidden, or would the iron still be visible even with the contract active and just appear awkwardly floating in the air? Or would the contract not work at all, for that matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25525-breezysatina","name":"BreezySatina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25525_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T00:01:59-07:00","id":1328232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BreezySatina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1328096#post1328096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would carrying iron interact with a contract like Light-Shy? Let's say you're carrying an iron sword, for example; would the sword be hidden, or would the iron still be visible even with the contract active and just appear awkwardly floating in the air? Or would the contract not work at all, for that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe as a general rule, Contracts tend to get nullified in the presence of iron. Full-stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T10:53:48-07:00","id":1330083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1324188#post1324188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Inciting Bedlam always going to incur the &quot;Using Glamour to force someone to change their behavior.&quot; Clarity Attack? (Well, not if you do it involuntarily I guess, since you use no Glamour then... Actually, if you use a Contract's Loophole, does that also mean it can't qualify for this?) Or is that only if you actively -force- them, rather than influencing their behaviour through their emotions? I'm leaning towards the latter, since people are not forced to behave a certain way if you change their emotions, they can still fully decide on their actions and ignore their emotions potentially?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still hoping for a simple answer to this. :O Or is this complex enough to need its own thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T14:59:03-07:00","id":1330140,"title":"","content":"There's a sidebar on 105 that refers to changing people's desires as grounds for a breaking point. As opposed to the more strict reading of forcing them to act a certain way, it seems pretty clear that mucking around in someone's mind/emotions without their consent is going to lead to breaking points regardless of outcome. I'm also fairly certain that &quot;spending glamour&quot; is intended to mean &quot;using Changeling magic as opposed to normal social maneuvering&quot; and that loopholes don't protect you from the ethical or mental ramifications of abusing your powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T16:26:29-07:00","id":1330163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1330140#post1330140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a sidebar on 105 that refers to changing people's desires as grounds for a breaking point. As opposed to the more strict reading of forcing them to act a certain way, it seems pretty clear that mucking around in someone's mind/emotions without their consent is going to lead to breaking points regardless of outcome. I'm also fairly certain that &quot;spending glamour&quot; is intended to mean &quot;using Changeling magic as opposed to normal social maneuvering&quot; and that loopholes don't protect you from the ethical or mental ramifications of abusing your powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, good catch! &quot;wouldn't normally agree to&quot; is pretty vague though, I think whenever you're using one of these powers they wouldn't &quot;normally agree to it&quot;, else why use the power if they would otherwise just agree? :P<br /> A grand majority of Contracts inflict emotional Conditions on a target, so I don't think simply slapping one of those on is intended to virtually always be a breaking point. The &quot;forcing a desire on someone&quot; here sounds like a deeper change than just making them feel a certain emotion.<br /> <br /> It sounds like good rule of thumb is: If it is something the target could be made to feel with high enough mundane rolls, but the Contract simply takes a shortcut or enhances it, it is probably ok. So for instances, using a Contract to make someone Frightened of you is alright since it's &quot;just&quot; supercharged Intimidation skill, and you could supposedly achieve the same by having very high Intimidation skills and a good roll. But making an asexual person sleep with you by using Tumult on them to make them Wanton, Swooning and Obsessed with you is going against their fundamental nature, and no Persuasion roll would ever be enough, so it is a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> That's how I'm reading it right now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-09-2019, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T06:23:08-07:00","id":1330236,"title":"","content":"You could theoretically use Spring's Contracts to temporarily change an unhealthy desire into something the person wants to want. There have been times in my life where I would have gladly paid someone to magic an unreciprocated crush into a desire to do the yard work I was neglecting for lack of motivation, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T07:18:15-07:00","id":1330244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1330236#post1330236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could theoretically use Spring's Contracts to temporarily change an unhealthy desire into something the person wants to want. There have been times in my life where I would have gladly paid someone to magic an unreciprocated crush into a desire to do the yard work I was neglecting for lack of motivation, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that still falls under &quot;theoretically, mundane means could be used to make you feel/desire/do that.&quot;, and thus fits into that &quot;rule of thumb&quot;. If someone was a great motivationalist, they could talk you into it!<br /> <br /> I'd been trying to hit the gym for ages, never managed to get to that point. But someone finally told me a really inspiring story about their past, and just totally fired me up to finally make the change. Sort of like that. ^^<br /> <br /> But perhaps going by specific Contracts is more useful: Would you say that &quot;Overpowering Dread&quot; is pretty much always a Clarity attack? I would say not, because the Changeling is only being supernaturally scary. They're not rewriting the target's emotions in great detail or directly, and certainly not touching their desires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-10-2019, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T12:57:15-07:00","id":1330972,"title":"","content":"How do you go about finding a specific Bastion? A Dreaming Road is described as a trod, and trods only link a finite number of endpoints together, so how does that work? Do you need to go through the Gate of ivory, step out onto the Dreaming Road connected to your Bastion, then go through the Gate of Horn, traverse the Hedge, find the correct Dreaming Road and go through its Gate of Horn? But all of humanity is linked up through the Dreaming Roads, right, so shouldn't need to leave the Roads at all to find any dream... right? I'm confused. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T13:09:06-07:00","id":1330974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1330972#post1330972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you go about finding a specific Bastion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The established method, at least, is to use a Hedgespinning paradigm shift to learn the direction of a specific dreamer's Bastion and go from there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Dreaming Road is described as a trod, and trods only link a finite number of endpoints together, so how does that work? Do you need to go through the Gate of ivory, step out onto the Dreaming Road connected to your Bastion, then go through the Gate of Horn, traverse the Hedge, find the correct Dreaming Road and go through its Gate of Horn? But all of humanity is linked up through the Dreaming Roads, right, so shouldn't need to leave the Roads at all to find any dream... right? I'm confused. :P </div> </div> </div>&quot;Some Bastions have more than one exit, opening out onto different Dreaming Roads depending on how their dreams harmonize with the snatches of nightmare or reverie that lie along each.&quot;<br /> <br /> We will <i>probably</i> have more details in The Hedge or Oak, Ash, and Thorn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T15:14:46-07:00","id":1331001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1330974#post1330974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The established method, at least, is to use a Hedgespinning paradigm shift to learn the direction of a specific dreamer's Bastion and go from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you do that while on a Dreaming Road, or do you have to get off of it first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T15:21:46-07:00","id":1331002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1331001#post1331001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you do that while on a Dreaming Road, or do you have to get off of it first?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, since Hedgespinning doesn't work in the Dreaming Roads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T15:37:07-07:00","id":1331004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1331002#post1331002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter, since Hedgespinning doesn't work in the Dreaming Roads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very kindly for the answers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T04:20:14-07:00","id":1331752,"title":"","content":"Hi <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Do you guys draw(?) Hedge maps for the games? Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","name":"Dexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T09:03:30-07:00","id":1331780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dexter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1331752#post1331752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Do you guys draw(?) Hedge maps for the games? Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Nope. Hedge changes too much for that.<br /> 2) For a split second, I thought someone was using my account on here before I remembered I haven't used that avatar since 2010, so that's fun. Also, you have good taste in avatars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T02:28:03-07:00","id":1331929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1331780#post1331780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Nope. Hedge changes too much for that.<br /> 2) For a split second, I thought someone was using my account on here before I remembered I haven't used that avatar since 2010, so that's fun. Also, you have good taste in avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . So if a changeling enters the Hegde through a known entry the Hedge will looks like completely(?) different since the last time?<br /> 2) Thank you #2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Probably this is my favourite CtL picture ever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I'm using this picture as avatar many places since the CtL came out and lots of my friends thought this is a picture from me with a little bit of photoshop <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","name":"Dexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T07:07:58-07:00","id":1331953,"title":"","content":"I dunno about completely different but the way I would play it is that the Hedge<br /> <br /> 1) changes a little based on the thoughts you bring in with you<br /> <br /> 2) has distances expressed in non-linear terms. If you walked one mile in a direction on one trip and then somehow walked one mile in the same direction on a second trip, you would not pass the same places. The stable trod goes through the same points, but what's between the stable points shifts around to match the &quot;flow&quot; of the Hedge and keep connecting the shifting positions of those stable points. Or at least thats how it seems to people used to operating in a world where a straight line is always the fastest route between two points. Navigating a trod can look like a walking down a road, but it's at heart following the signs and omens that mark the trail so long as the trod exists. Also, something about trails being a series of events rather than a winding line of straight kilometers/miles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-21-2019, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:04:38-07:00","id":1331978,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that some consistent rules for the Hedge are A) Trods are fixed, and usually well known with a good number of locations along them, B) Fixed locations like Hollows and such don't nessecarily don't move, but there's not much reason to worry about them moving, C) There is always <i>a</i> way to reach to reach a set destination, and D) The rest by and large has to do with your state of mind and sense of focus, and otherwise everything covered in Hedge Travel rules.<br /> <br /> So as pertains maps, if I were going to draw something up, I'd start with Trods, create the islands of Fixed locations, and the rest would be thorn mess.<br /> <br /> Still, it can be worth mapping out a Trod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:11:15-07:00","id":1331989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1331978#post1331978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that some consistent rules for the Hedge are A) Trods are fixed, and usually well known with a good number of locations along them, B) Fixed locations like Hollows and such don't nessecarily don't move, but there's not much reason to worry about them moving, C) There is always <i>a</i> way to reach to reach a set destination, and D) The rest by and large has to do with your state of mind and sense of focus, and otherwise everything covered in Hedge Travel rules.<br /> <br /> So as pertains maps, if I were going to draw something up, I'd start with Trods, create the islands of Fixed locations, and the rest would be thorn mess.<br /> <br /> Still, it can be worth mapping out a Trod.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What she said. Major locations will always be somewhere along the trod between the same two other locations as long as the trod stays stable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:31:12-07:00","id":1331990,"title":"","content":"(Can't upload attachment or post links)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","user":"Dexter","date":". 08-21-2019, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","name":"Dexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:14:40-07:00","id":1332002,"title":"","content":"I have a couple of questions here.<br /> <br /> 1) What mechanical benefit does Pathfinder offer for navigating the Hedge, if any? It lets you know the direction something is, but what benefit that has for Hedge chases is something I am a little confused by.<br /> <br /> 2) If a Fairest uses their Blessing to spend a Willpower to bolster another\u2019s die pool, could the other person also spend a Willpower to do the same? That is, overall gaining 6 dice rather than being limited to 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T13:15:22-07:00","id":1332010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1332002#post1332002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a couple of questions here.<br /> <br /> 1) What mechanical benefit does Pathfinder offer for navigating the Hedge, if any? It lets you know the direction something is, but what benefit that has for Hedge chases is something I am a little confused by.<br /> <br /> 2) If a Fairest uses their Blessing to spend a Willpower to bolster another\u2019s die pool, could the other person also spend a Willpower to do the same? That is, overall gaining 6 dice rather than being limited to 3?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) By and large it depends on the Chase in question, but in the highly mutable Hedge, it pays to be the one who knows where they are going versus someone who doesn't. It doesn't directly translate into mechanical benefits on it's own, but I think it's a decent argument for inherent Edge and at least a +2 on any skill roll made with the idea of misdirecting the opponent in mind, since you know more about the general lay of the land than they do. When chasing against the Hedge itself vs getting to a location, it's much the same principle except it happens all the time-alternatively, it lets you skip over the Chase aspect for casual travel all together.<br /> <br /> 2) It doesn't specify that a person benefiting from the Fairest can't, and it fits the idea that a Fairest builds you up even more, so I don't see a reason you can't. You could also mix and match the benefits of Willpower expenditure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-21-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T22:54:14-07:00","id":1332778,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">How does breaking into bastions work?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It looks like you can observe the bastion defenses and roll Manipulation + Empathy, using successes to enact a paradigm shift. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is the usual way, as described on p.221.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">But what does &quot;old-fashioned way&quot; mean? How do you break through without a paradigm shift? Does it mean beating up eidolons? Or breaking through solid walls using various tools? Or do you just enter the dream, but all of your actions are contested by bastion fortifications?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25597-deniv","name":"DeniV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T23:50:03-07:00","id":1332782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeniV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1332778#post1332778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what does &quot;old-fashioned way&quot; mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Bastion is not just a word for an abstract dream-barrier - a Bastion is, well, a bastion. It's a physicalized structure in the Dreaming Roads that defends the dreamer's soul from tampering, and that literal metaphor is as subject to regular interactions as any real fortification.<br /> <br /> It will likely depend on the form it takes, but picking the lock on the gate of a Bastion is only distinguished from doing so to a similar gate in the real world by the fact that the dream gets to contest your attempts to break in normally, and involving an important eidolon in the process often makes it harder still thanks to the way their dicepools work. Getting in sans pledge or Key without disturbing the dream is generally the demesne of lower-Fortification dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T01:15:59-07:00","id":1333491,"title":"","content":"I have a Fae Mount. Will it exist on Dreaming Roads or Bastion? Are they part of the hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25597-deniv","name":"DeniV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T11:15:55-07:00","id":1333564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeniV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1333491#post1333491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a Fae Mount. Will it exist on Dreaming Roads or Bastion? Are they part of the hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on where you put it. If you don't leave them somewhere specific, they usually mill around in the Hedge until called(ST fiat goes a long way with this, but as a general rule the Mount should be available upon entering the Hedge and not killed or wounded unless there's an agreement between ST and player for story's sake, keeping in mind the Sanctity of Merits), but it's assumed that you would keep them in a Hollow. Since your Bastion falls apart when you wake, I wouldn't keep it there, and honestly I wouldn't be quick to let anything stay in a dreamscape.<br /> <br /> As a native of the Hedge, the Mount would be a part of the Hedge in the same way any other hobgoblin would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-01-2019, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T14:03:29-07:00","id":1333737,"title":"","content":"Considering that if a Earth Creature goes to the Hedge/Arcadia they become more Faerie-Like would a Hobgoblin that lived with A motley of Changelings on Earth yet more..Eathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T14:42:24-07:00","id":1333746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1333737#post1333737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that if a Earth Creature goes to the Hedge/Arcadia they become more Faerie-Like would a Hobgoblin that lived with A motley of Changelings on Earth yet more..Eathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely? Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T14:44:59-07:00","id":1333748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1333737#post1333737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that if a Earth Creature goes to the Hedge/Arcadia they become more Faerie-Like would a Hobgoblin that lived with A motley of Changelings on Earth yet more..Eathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>The relationship between worlds is unfortunately not quite so predictably two-way; there might be particular methods for fae creatures to naturalize themselves out of reliance on the Hedge, but the default state of affairs is generally that supernatural limitations are harder to shed than mundane ones.<br /> <br /> A hobgoblin who spends a lot of time around Earthly people and things might have a stronger understanding of how things work outside the Fae's backyard, but it's a bigger stretch for it to have lost its need for Hedge comforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T16:16:39-07:00","id":1333761,"title":"","content":"Yeah I said lived with. It wouldn\u2019t happen in a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T16:34:45-07:00","id":1333762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1333761#post1333761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I said lived with. It wouldn\u2019t happen in a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm saying it typically won't happen in a decade. Mere exposure isn't how these things work, especially not for creatures out of a place where the passage of time is as variable as the climate. Circumstances more special than changeling roommates will be called for for the mundane world to not give a hob a headache.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T17:21:12-07:00","id":1333765,"title":"","content":"Like what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T17:55:37-07:00","id":1333767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1333765#post1333765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what?</div> </div> </div> </div>To give some perspective, I\u2019m going to point something out; mundane reality is not like the Hedge.<br /> <br /> That sounds facetious but trust me, I\u2019m going somewhere with that.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is home to entities tied to the Wyrd, making deals, gathering energy and in general acting through and around it as an arbitrator for deals and fate. Everything in the Hedge gravitates towards the Wyrd, with people, animals and objects being permanently transformed by it into stranger, truer versions of themselves. The Hedge is strange, non-linear and psychoactive. The Hedge <i>changes</i> itself and the people within it based on the people and beings within it.<br /> <br /> Mundane reality is nothing like this. True, it\u2019s strange, it changes due to people within it and it is home to all kinds of supernaturals, but even in those similarities it\u2019s <i>extremely</i> different. Mundane reality is beholden to no one power, with laws and rules that few entities barring the God-Machine can entirely comprehend and make use of. The Wyrd exists there but it\u2019s not nearly the mover and shaker that it is in the Hedge. Indeed, there is no one real source of supernatural power in the mundane world, and as such it doesn\u2019t change beings to fit its norm - the Hedge is a specialty store, with items to fill any niche and all under one brand, whereas the mundane realm is Walmart, with everything and anything from multiple different brands. Humanity is extremely transmutable in the mundane realm, to the point that even the dead can become any number of things, whereas in the Hedge there are just a few routes humanity can take (even if in those routes the forms are infinitely varied).<br /> <br /> As such, a Hob spending any amount of time in the mundane realm is going to take a lot more than just exposure to its people and cultures to change their tune and acclimate like a person in the Hedge (becoming a Hob or a Changeling) does. The mundane realm simply doesn\u2019t <i>change</i> people and things like the Hedge does... and even in the mundane realm, those changes are sometimes not even consistent within one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T18:26:47-07:00","id":1333770,"title":"","content":"In short, the Wyrd inflicts as much as it connects. Mundane reality does not bear this consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T19:43:02-07:00","id":1334041,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain to me how Ride the Falling Leaves works?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25600-redtooth-redtooth","name":"Redtooth-Redtooth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T20:34:24-07:00","id":1337003,"title":"","content":"So the game introduces a few mechanics in 2e related to an elementals 'elemental' affinity. In 1e, your elemental was based on kith - but in 2e, since Kith is not bound, do you just... pick an element that is tied to the elemental that doesn't contrast with the kith you've chosen?<br /> <br /> What are the limits on the choices of elements? For instance, if your a Storm Elemental, is your element 'Wind, Water, and Lightning' or is it specific to storm clouds to work your seeming benefit? Can you manipulate all versions of your element in question (for instance, a water elemental manipulating ice and vice versa.)<br /> <br /> Following up on that question, there are three contracts whose elemental seeming bonus allows an individual to incorporate 'their elemental affinity'. If your not an elemental, do you just pick an element when you learn that seeming bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T03:19:13-07:00","id":1337052,"title":"","content":"In the Dark Eras book the Grimm Dark Era chapter talks about how human stories, fairy tales, and folklore can influence fae magic and even change how it works in a given area. Is that a thing in 2e? I know in the end it's up to the individual ST to determine whether this is the way it works, but I'm curious if this was ever part of the base setting or if it's only ever mentioned in that chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T07:04:50-07:00","id":1337083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1337052#post1337052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Dark Eras book the Grimm Dark Era chapter talks about how human stories, fairy tales, and folklore can influence fae magic and even change how it works in a given area. Is that a thing in 2e? I know in the end it's up to the individual ST to determine whether this is the way it works, but I'm curious if this was ever part of the base setting or if it's only ever mentioned in that chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was part of the original plan for 2e, but the game changed developers during development and went a different direction, so the Grimm Dark Era ends up being the only place it appears.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T09:31:18-07:00","id":1338639,"title":"","content":"Is there a homebrew Goblin Fruit thread yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T11:14:32-07:00","id":1339023,"title":"","content":"With discrete summons ability to summon an object of up to availability 3, would it fit for this ability to be used to summon drugs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T19:47:08-07:00","id":1339105,"title":"","content":"So, I just bought CtL 2e and I'm making my way through it. I have. . . questions. I'm coming back to WoD, or CoD now, after about 4 years of D&amp;D where every ability/effect/consequence is explained with almost airtight clarity (I suppose I can't expect any less from the pseudo-lawyers who make MtG, lol). To be clear, I LOVE WoD. I love the setting and loved the sandbox/toolbox approach of NWoD in 2004, but after reading clear, defined rules in D&amp;D for the last few years, I'm feeling frustrated at the ambiguity and, to be honest, ephemeral feel of a lot of CtL 2e's rules.<br /> <br /> I came across this question from a week or so ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1337003#post1337003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the game introduces a few mechanics in 2e related to an elementals 'elemental' affinity. In 1e, your elemental was based on kith - but in 2e, since Kith is not bound, do you just... pick an element that is tied to the elemental that doesn't contrast with the kith you've chosen?<br /> <br /> What are the limits on the choices of elements? For instance, if your a Storm Elemental, is your element 'Wind, Water, and Lightning' or is it specific to storm clouds to work your seeming benefit? Can you manipulate all versions of your element in question (for instance, a water elemental manipulating ice and vice versa.)<br /> <br /> Following up on that question, there are three contracts whose elemental seeming bonus allows an individual to incorporate 'their elemental affinity'. If your not an elemental, do you just pick an element when you learn that seeming bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the kind of stuff I'm talking about. Is it left ambiguous intentionally? If it's up to the ST to make the final arbitration, I feel like that's a lot of undue burden added to the STs responsibilities.<br /> <br /> Some more things I'm struggling with:<br /> <br /> - The Seeming ability for Elementals is described as &quot;As long as your character touches or is surrounded by his element, he may use it to take mundane actions at a distance of up to three yards (meters) away; these actions use his usual traits. This includes unarmed attacks, but not attacks with weapons.&quot; What exactly constitutes as a mundane action? Lock picking? Building a table? This ability is all well and good if I'm made of wood or water, but how am I touching lightning? I guess I could be carrying a zippo and use it to touch fire? As the quote above states: what defines my elemental affinity?<br /> <br /> - The Darkling Seeming ability goes like this &quot;If you spend a point of Willpower, your character may touch something insubstantial and become part of it for three consecutive turns, transubstantiating into smoke, shadow, a sunbeam \u2014 whatever\u2019s handy.&quot; What can I do for those nine seconds? Can I attack? Can I speak? Can I move?<br /> <br /> - I'd like to see a clear example of touchstones and clarity damage being used. I think I understand the basics of touchstones, but I'm having trouble visualizing the &quot;write your touchstone beside *composure + 1* box on the clarity track&quot; when the clarity track is like the healthbar, but the touchstone track is beneath it, not beside it. -_- Also, for clarity damage, it keeps referencing &quot;down to clarity 1, 2 or 3 from the right&quot;, but the track on the character sheet has a blank on the first box, then it starts 1, 2, 3 from the LEFTmost box. I think if I had to really do it, I guess I could make it work, but it just sucks that they couln't have an actual example in the book.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's what I've got for now, I just feel that with so many abilities left up to interpretation, it could cause lots of rule talk/arguments at the table, taking away from the core mood and gameplay. I love CoD, and want to make CtL 2e work, Maybe I'm trying to define things that are meant to be ambiguous for imagination or creativity's sake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3794-martmantzt","name":"MartManTZT","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:10:53-07:00","id":1339107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1339023#post1339023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With discrete summons ability to summon an object of up to availability 3, would it fit for this ability to be used to summon drugs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:16:48-07:00","id":1339723,"title":"","content":"I apologize if this question has already been asked, I couldn't find it by searching. What is the mechanical benefit of the Pathfinder contract (CtL 2e 144)?<br /> <br /> The source of my confusion is this: The rules for traveling in the Hedge imply that you don't need to know exactly the direction you're going, since space and direction do not exist in the same way in the Hedge as they do in the mundane world. In fact, on page 200, navigation is described the same way whether your declared intent is, &quot;I want to take a shortcut to San Francisco&quot; or &quot;I want to find the nearest Goblin Market.&quot; (CtL 200) There's no mention of Pathfinder in either the success modifiers or the dice pool modifiers in the printed book. There's no explicit mention of the Navigation mechanics in Pathfinder's description, just the implication of known direction and distance. The standard chase modifiers (CtL 196) allows for a modifier of -1 to the success total if your character &quot;knows the territory somewhat&quot; or -3 if they &quot;know the territory intimately,&quot; but it's not clear if Pathfinder qualifies as one of these.<br /> <br /> My table talked it over and we thought that being immune to the Lost condition when navigating to the target declared by the Pathfinder contract was fair, but I wanted to see what everyone else thought, and if we were missing something in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13508-necrobotany","name":"necrobotany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T20:19:20-07:00","id":1339752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1339023#post1339023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With discrete summons ability to summon an object of up to availability 3, would it fit for this ability to be used to summon drugs?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Far as I can tell, nothing stops you from making drugs appear into your hands - but you can't really use them or sell them. Those drugs would only last until the end of the scene, or until they left your hand - the latter of which would be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T21:00:59-07:00","id":1339758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MartManTZT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1339105#post1339105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Seeming ability for Elementals is described as &quot;As long as your character touches or is surrounded by his element, he may use it to take mundane actions at a distance of up to three yards (meters) away; these actions use his usual traits. This includes unarmed attacks, but not attacks with weapons.&quot; What exactly constitutes as a mundane action?</div> </div> </div> </div>An action that is not the activation of a supernatural power, generally speaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Darkling Seeming ability goes like this &quot;If you spend a point of Willpower, your character may touch something insubstantial and become part of it for three consecutive turns, transubstantiating into smoke, shadow, a sunbeam \u2014 whatever\u2019s handy.&quot; What can I do for those nine seconds? Can I attack? Can I speak? Can I move? </div> </div> </div>You can definitely move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - I'd like to see a clear example of touchstones and clarity damage being used. I think I understand the basics of touchstones, but I'm having trouble visualizing the &quot;write your touchstone beside *composure + 1* box on the clarity track&quot; when the clarity track is like the healthbar, but the touchstone track is beneath it, not beside it. -_- Also, for clarity damage, it keeps referencing &quot;down to clarity 1, 2 or 3 from the right&quot;, but the track on the character sheet has a blank on the first box, then it starts 1, 2, 3 from the LEFTmost box. </div> </div> </div>Both of these problems are stemming from something you seem to have overlooked: those numbers underneath the Clarity track appear to be for marking where Touchstones are attached; normal characters are not going to have more than six Touchstones, but it's well within the realm of possibility for a character to have Composure 5 and five dots in the Touchstone Merit<br /> <br /> Presumably you record the Touchstones in the appropriately numbered lines for their attached ratings' boxes, and then the first box in excess of your Wits + Composure + Icons total gets marked in such a way to indicate that the preceding boxes constitute your Max Clarity (which matches the number underneath the leftmost unusable box, numerically).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T22:29:38-07:00","id":1339766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1339752#post1339752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Far as I can tell, nothing stops you from making drugs appear into your hands - but you can't really use them or sell them. Those drugs would only last until the end of the scene, or until they left your hand - the latter of which would be an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>so...i see one way to make this work if it works like that, though its admittedly pretty niche: pretending to be high to lower people's guard. i mean, if it disappears once it leaves your hand, then you can't even ingest any drugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T10:42:58-07:00","id":1339875,"title":"","content":"Would a darkling gristlegrinder who has eaten someone take them their victim with them when they turn into another substance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T19:19:15-07:00","id":1341037,"title":"","content":"Can Fetches have children? <br /> If yes, are those children normal Mortals or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24571-malachitedrake","name":"MalachiteDrake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T00:27:06-07:00","id":1341064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalachiteDrake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1341037#post1341037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Fetches have children?<br /> If yes, are those children normal Mortals or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, fetches are usually sterile... but even so, sometimes they still have children.<br /> <br /> Autumn Nightmares gives two options for such children:<br /> <br /> The fetch-children have a touch of the fey about them, giving them Unseen Sense for the fae, the ability to enter the Hedge under their own power (and take others along with them), and <i>possibly</i> blood that's poisonous to the Gentry.<br /> <br /> The fetch-spawn, on the other hand, are soulless horrors with no connection to the Wyrd. They don't have Morality ratings, they can't learn the Empathy skill, they can't learn or use fae magic, they temporarily negate tokens by touching them, they can't be targeted by Contracts or tokens, they can't enter pledges, they add three successes to any Stealth roll, they can't be tied up, bound, or restrained, and locked doors open for them with the slightest touch, they don't dream, and they drain all the Glamour from a changeling with a touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T19:26:44-07:00","id":1343322,"title":"","content":"I asked this in a separate thread, but it was suggested it might be better asked here: In the 2e book it says that Hedgespun Items can get a +1 to equipment bonus, armor rating, or weapon damage per dot. is this on top of what the item normally gives, or instead of? A longsword normally does 3 damage with -2 initiative. What stats would a Hedgespun sword get? 5 damage or 2? -2 init or no init modifier? What about size and min strength? Also, can Hedgespun Items be taken using the Token merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T19:39:41-07:00","id":1343323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1343322#post1343322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked this in a separate thread, but it was suggested it might be better asked here: In the 2e book it says that Hedgespun Items can get a +1 to equipment bonus, armor rating, or weapon damage per dot. is this on top of what the item normally gives, or instead of? A longsword normally does 3 damage with -2 initiative. What stats would a Hedgespun sword get? 5 damage or 2? -2 init or no init modifier? What about size and min strength? Also, can Hedgespun Items be taken using the Token merit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and cross-posting a related question i posted in that thread before i remembered this thread (which I created in the first place, derp) exists<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1343094-hedgespun-item-bonuses?p=1343160#post1343160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may add another question to the pile, does the armor bonus apply to general armor, ballistic armor, both or your choice of one or the other every time you buy a dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:22:40-07:00","id":1343506,"title":"","content":"Given that the modifiers are listed under 'Extraordinary Equipment&quot; and it states <i><b>+</b></i>1 per dot I'm confident that it's meant to be added to an item's normal values, not replace them. And yes, they have a dot value and are intended to be purchased as the merit.<br /> <br /> As for armor the only guideline I could find is that subtle hedge shaping shifts add 1 to general and ballistic per success; based on that I say 1 of each per dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T13:22:16-07:00","id":1343640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1343506#post1343506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the modifiers are listed under 'Extraordinary Equipment&quot; and it states <i><b>+</b></i>1 per dot I'm confident that it's meant to be added to an item's normal values, not replace them. And yes, they have a dot value and are intended to be purchased as the merit.<br /> <br /> As for armor the only guideline I could find is that subtle hedge shaping shifts add 1 to general and ballistic per success; based on that I say 1 of each per dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't seem to find anything about having to pay for the base item before adding the modifiers from Token dots. Does this mean a character can just get a tank with a +1 modifier to something for the cost of 1 Merit dot? That seems a bit broken. If this is actually how this works I think I'm going to have to re-wright the rules for Hedgespun Items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T15:15:12-07:00","id":1343666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1343640#post1343640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't seem to find anything about having to pay for the base item before adding the modifiers from Token dots. Does this mean a character can just get a tank with a +1 modifier to something for the cost of 1 Merit dot? That seems a bit broken. If this is actually how this works I think I'm going to have to re-wright the rules for Hedgespun Items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your one-dot super-tank is still a tank-sized tank <i>and also it will be destroyed by contact with iron.</i> Its existence implies a tank was made into a token through one of the three vectors for token-acquisition that exist in the setting, the vast majority of which require having a tank from the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T15:46:28-07:00","id":1343672,"title":"","content":"Sure. Are you planning on leaving a tank in the hedge to &quot;marinate&quot;, swear multiple oaths upon it, or steal it from the True Fae? If option one or two, how will you get the tank in the first place? To make a hedge-forged token, it needs to be something with personal meaning to your character. Is it the tank your mother gave you just before she died? If it's an oath-forged token, you still need to get your hands on a tank somehow, then you have to convince changelings to swear an oath it... a tank... three times. Will they even be willing to swear upon something so large and conspicuous, considering anyone that just puts a hand on it can use it to locate them? Hope you have summer court goodwill. Of course, you can always just sneak into Arcadia and steal a tank from the True Fae. Yeah, good luck with that. At the end of the day, this all sounds like a lot of time and effort for a tank that gets a +1 bonus to something and is completely destroyed if it touches iron. Which will probably happen as soon as anyone feels threatened by your new pimpmobile. Then again, they probably did you a favor by destroying it. Who knows what the local freehold would have to say about one of their members joyriding through town in a tank. Rather than re-write any rules, you should just have fun with any player that tries to pull this kind of tomfoolery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T15:55:07-07:00","id":1343673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1343640#post1343640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't seem to find anything about having to pay for the base item before adding the modifiers from Token dots. Does this mean a character can just get a tank with a +1 modifier to something for the cost of 1 Merit dot? That seems a bit broken. If this is actually how this works I think I'm going to have to re-wright the rules for Hedgespun Items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narrative matters. Table co-operation matters.<br /> <br /> How you ended up with a Hedgespun tank matters to the story you're telling.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I thought I had something to do with the 1-Dot Tank, particularly if it was relevant to the setting, Sure, Not a Fucking Problem, Glad Someone Did It. If I thought it was a waste of my fucking time, I'd tell you to pick something else, and would take a <i>very annoyed</i> tone with insistence perpetuated in continuity until you either convinced me or I told you to fuck off with the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T16:41:53-07:00","id":1343682,"title":"","content":"Even for less egregious examples if you're really worried about it just limit the possibilities by Availability. We already have a good abstracted mechanic for limiting access based on rarity/expense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T04:37:07-07:00","id":1343748,"title":"","content":"There's no way narrative should ever excuse horrendously unbalanced rules. A tank is an extreme example, but if the base item isn't taken into account with regards to the Token Merit and Hedgespun Items then that can lead to some absolutely game-breaking scenarios. By taking the Token Merit you get to skip all the messy rules for actually having to create the Token, you just have it already. The item never has to &quot;marinate in the hedge&quot; because the Merit skips that step. &quot;Oh yea, I have a Hedgespun nuke I like to carry around with me. I paid my 1 Merit dot, so I just already have it&quot;. I'd rather not simply remove the whole mess (even though I am sorely tempted considering how badly this combination can be abused), so I guess I'll just houserule it so that the Availability cost of the base item adds to the cost of the Token Merit. So a longsword that does +1 damage would be a 4 dot Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T04:46:58-07:00","id":1343750,"title":"","content":"Saying that you've got a Hedgespun tank for a Merit dot is just as unbalanced and unreasonable as saying you've got a mundane tank for no cost at all. Neither explains how you got a hold of a tank in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1343748#post1343748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By taking the Token Merit you get to skip all the messy rules for actually having to create the Token, you just have it already. The item never has to &quot;marinate in the hedge&quot; because the Merit skips that step.</div> </div> </div> </div>It skips going through all of that <i>in play</i>. It still has to happen because items gained through Merits doesn't just show up ex nihilo. Any Merits you buy are in some way or another acquired by the character, be it through actions in the game, during downtime, during the character's backstory, etc. If your character don't have a reason for having a Merit, they shouldn't have it. Just like everything else on the character sheet, from Attributes to Skills to Specialties to equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T07:34:18-07:00","id":1343764,"title":"","content":"The wording of the merit seems to definitely imply that this is an object that you can either wear on your body or carry in your hands. I'd rule vehicles are out of it's purview. As for powerful handheld weapons, if it really bothers you, say you have to have the Resource Rating or appropriate dice pool needed to obtain an item of that Availability rating. But really, unless you really want to play a guy who is always on the run from the mundane law as well as the Gentry, a Hedgespun elephant gun or even just a pistol is more trouble than it's worth in damage due to how magically flashy and noticable they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:57:17-07:00","id":1343857,"title":"","content":"and if you really want a magical tank, add an armament upgrade to your Mobile Hollow (only sorta sarcastic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T06:55:45-07:00","id":1344182,"title":"","content":"Really basic question, but I haven't seen the answer explicitly stated: A character's Glamour-per-turn limit is determined by their Wyrd. If I have a Contract whose cost is greater than my per-turn limit (say, a Contract that costs 2 Glamour when I have Wyrd 1), does that mean I cannot use the Contract at all (except through its loophole)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T07:01:55-07:00","id":1344183,"title":"","content":"If you can't spend all the Glamour in one turn, you do it over several turns, only activating the Contract once you've spent the entire cost. I don't have the book on me now but I'm sure it's stated in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T07:08:36-07:00","id":1344184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1344183#post1344183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can't spend all the Glamour in one turn, you do it over several turns, only activating the Contract once you've spent the entire cost. I don't have the book on me now but I'm sure it's stated in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you! If you do manage to find a page reference, that would be really helpful-- I haven't found it in the Wyrd section, the Glamour section or the Contracts section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T07:12:02-07:00","id":1344186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1344184#post1344184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thank you! If you do manage to find a page reference, that would be really helpful-- I haven't found it in the Wyrd section, the Glamour section or the Contracts section.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL2e p126, Contracts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Contract costs more Glamour than the character can spend per turn based on her Wyrd, she may spend Glamour over multiple turns and invoke the Contract when the last required Glamour is spent.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimi</span></span><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">t</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T19:47:02-07:00","id":1344809,"title":"","content":"Is the 2e Hedge Duelist merit strictly for use in a formal Hedge duel? Or can it be employed in any kind of combat in the Hedge?<br /> <br /> I only ask because the first edition Hedge Duelist merit specified that the merit only applied to formal duels. But the 2e version of the merit conspicuously leaves that requirement out. Was that a mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:37:23-07:00","id":1345101,"title":"","content":"It's time for my silly question!<br /> <br /> When a runaway changeling escapes from his keeper and step into the Hedge, he can go back to the human world through an hedge gateways opened by others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 10-31-2019, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T15:23:39-08:00","id":1345654,"title":"","content":"When making an elemental character/npc are you supposed to pick one type of element? What if someone picks air, does that mean they can act anywhere that isn't a vacuum? What if they pick something that typically isn't found in large quantities, like crystal? What exactly counts as &quot;elements&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T16:30:14-08:00","id":1345661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1345654#post1345654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When making an elemental character/npc are you supposed to pick one type of element?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how &quot;elementals&quot; tend to work in fiction, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if someone picks air, does that mean they can act anywhere that isn't a vacuum? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Air&quot; typically refers to concrete phenomena in any case that isn't Awakened Matter magic, where the fact that most games take place on a planet with an atmosphere is accounted for in the difficulty of using &quot;transmutation&quot; as the explanation for how thirty cubic feet of poison gas effectively just manifested into empty space.<br /> <br /> Your Keeper didn't take you away to be empty space, no matter how esoteric their tastes were. You were a gust of wind or a cloud or a storm or any of the other manifestations of &quot;air&quot; that were actually interesting enough to put a character in the role for the type of purposes Elementals were kept for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if they pick something that typically isn't found in large quantities, like crystal? </div> </div> </div>Then you make do without that part of the blessing or you find a way to surround yourself with a rare element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exactly counts as &quot;elements&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Concrete physical phenomena that are not animals but could conceivably be encountered as a major part of the environment within some manner of legendary scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T16:52:18-08:00","id":1345663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1345661#post1345661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concrete physical phenomena that are not animals but could conceivably be encountered as a major part of the environment within some manner of legendary scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Keeper's domain is a ocean of teddy bears, it is not inconceivable that an you return as a Teddy Bear Elemental, as an extremely weird example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T17:01:45-08:00","id":1345664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1345663#post1345663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Keeper's domain is a ocean of teddy bears, it is not inconceivable that an you return as a Teddy Bear Elemental, as an extremely weird example.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to avoid confusing the issue:<br /> <br /> Primal/primordial forces and phenomena is the key here \u2014 there's a reason most of the literature's examples of elementals focus on relatively simple things. Elementals were blunt instruments and power sources, and their blessing typically reflects that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T17:13:31-08:00","id":1345668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1345664#post1345664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to avoid confusing the issue:<br /> <br /> Primal/primordial forces and phenomena is the key here \u2014 there's a reason most of the literature's examples of elementals focus on relatively simple things. Elementals were blunt instruments and power sources, and their blessing typically reflects that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, extremely important here, thank you.<br /> <br /> And curtailing some of the odd ends, Primal/Primordial forces and phenomenon that a Stranger would define. Passive attention or lack of attention don't quite make up the sorts of things a Stranger will make Elementals of. If a Keeper envisions a rocky-and lava-strewn world and creates their domain to the purview of their Title, and Gravity isn't a thing they mention, that doesn't mean that there's no gravity there, but it also doesn't mean you of course have Gravity Elementals on occasion.<br /> <br /> The fundamentals of the aesthetic, the formative elements that is then detailed upon-that's the Elementals. The True Fae do not paint worlds with color but with fire and shadow and teddy bears, and it is those &quot;paints&quot; that make up the Elemental Cast.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Taking this out of theory though, what counts as an element? Whatever the Storyteller and play group think will be engaging without being highly obnoxious in execution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T19:56:45-08:00","id":1345690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1345668#post1345668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And curtailing some of the odd ends, Primal/Primordial forces and phenomenon that a Stranger would define. Passive attention or lack of attention don't quite make up the sorts of things a Stranger will make Elementals of. If a Keeper envisions a rocky-and lava-strewn world and creates their domain to the purview of their Title, and Gravity isn't a thing they mention, that doesn't mean that there's no gravity there, but it also doesn't mean you of course have Gravity Elementals on occasion.<br /> <br /> The fundamentals of the aesthetic, the formative elements that is then detailed upon-that's the Elementals. The True Fae do not paint worlds with color but with fire and shadow and teddy bears, and it is those &quot;paints&quot; that make up the Elemental Cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do feel it's important to remember that all available evidence suggests that Faerie being less like a myth than an acid trip is more a function of changelings struggling with Clarity in the same way that mages having Inferior Arcana doesn't actually limit the abilities of Supernal beings from a given Realm \u2014 the Law of Patterns is more than just &quot;you can figure the pattern of a domain out,&quot; it's &quot;you can figure the pattern of a domain out <i>because there are rules, signs, and metaphors that govern that pattern</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The most abstract and esoteric gameline in the Chronicles of Darkness concerns itself with the changeover point between the abstract and the concrete, and the fae do not quite inhabit that extreme of the scale. Elementals draw upon elements informed by the Regalia of the Sword and the examples suggested by various Elemental seeming boons for other Contracts, and weirder manifestations are less certain for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T20:39:03-08:00","id":1345695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1345690#post1345690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do feel it's important to remember that all available evidence suggests that Faerie being less like a myth than an acid trip is more a function of changelings struggling with Clarity in the same way that mages having Inferior Arcana doesn't actually limit the abilities of Supernal beings from a given Realm \u2014 the Law of Patterns is more than just &quot;you can figure the pattern of a domain out,&quot; it's &quot;you can figure the pattern of a domain out <i>because there are rules, signs, and metaphors that govern that pattern</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The most abstract and esoteric gameline in the Chronicles of Darkness concerns itself with the changeover point between the abstract and the concrete, and the fae do not quite inhabit that extreme of the scale. Elementals draw upon elements informed by the Regalia of the Sword and the examples suggested by various Elemental seeming boons for other Contracts, and weirder manifestations are less certain for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair and correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:57:51-08:00","id":1345969,"title":"","content":"Should we revive the Kith Conversion (2e) thread or make a new thread for homebrew kiths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://