,"name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T21:56:29-08:00","id":1355763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1355762#post1355762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does Hedgespinning (and, by extension, Dreamweaving) work? Can you directly manipulate the Hedge, or does it all have to be done while you're doing other actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>You take actions in the environment that are literally or metaphorically related to your desired outcome and allocate excess successes toward your desired effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you take an Extended Action to build up greater changes, or does everything have o be generated at once? </div> </div> </div>You can shunt successes from a successful roll in an extended action, but unless you manage a paradigm shift and stock extra successes, your results come from singular rolls.<br /> <br /> Teamwork, tools, and dice tricks are your friends in this sort of endeavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:05:17-08:00","id":1355765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1355763#post1355763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You take actions in the environment that are literally or metaphorically related to your desired outcome and allocate excess successes toward your desired effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind sharing some examples?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:55:48-08:00","id":1355777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1355765#post1355765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind sharing some examples?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedgespinning section's text on Subtle Shifts provides the examples of bridging a chasm by convincing people to work together or wrestling physically with something that represents something you want to mentally move past, or creating a door to an unknown Hollow by convincing those present that a picture of a door is real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T03:01:02-08:00","id":1356267,"title":"","content":"I am having some difficulty appreciating the change that occurs in an object when it becomes permanently animated as a one dot Retainer via Dance Of The Toys. Does it no longer require an activation roll for accepting commands? Will it follow commands (or a single command) if it leaves the normal control area? Would it still benefit from any Seeming bonuses such as the ability to float at walking speed if a Wizened animated it?<br /> <br /> Basically I want to appreciate the benefit of spending an experience on something as opposed to evoking the contract over and over again to almost certainly get a better benefit than a Retainer\u2019s 2 dice to fulfill a task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-21-2019, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T09:43:40-08:00","id":1356311,"title":"","content":"Do Fetch using the Mimic Contract Echo get the benefit of the Seeming Blessing their Changeling counterpart gets? For example, would the Fetch of an Elemental get a bonus to Initiative and Speed when mimicking Fae Cunning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T13:43:34-08:00","id":1357098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1356267#post1356267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having some difficulty appreciating the change that occurs in an object when it becomes permanently animated as a one dot Retainer via Dance Of The Toys. Does it no longer require an activation roll for accepting commands? Will it follow commands (or a single command) if it leaves the normal control area? Would it still benefit from any Seeming bonuses such as the ability to float at walking speed if a Wizened animated it?<br /> <br /> Basically I want to appreciate the benefit of spending an experience on something as opposed to evoking the contract over and over again to almost certainly get a better benefit than a Retainer\u2019s 2 dice to fulfill a task.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct--it no longer requires an invocation roll (or Glamour/Loophole), and the animated device can go wherever. It functions just like any other Retainer, except it's not a person. You still retain the Seeming benefits. The main benefit to spending the Experience to buy it as a Merit is that it won't cost you any Glamour and it will stay animated even if it gets out of range; it'll just keep doing the last thing you told it to do until it can't anymore or you give it another command. And Changeling players are always coming up with creative ways to use what they've got, so I'm sure there are other ones I'm not thinking of right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T14:24:39-08:00","id":1357107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1356311#post1356311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Fetch using the Mimic Contract Echo get the benefit of the Seeming Blessing their Changeling counterpart gets? For example, would the Fetch of an Elemental get a bonus to Initiative and Speed when mimicking Fae Cunning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; they in fact get all the seeming benefits their changeling counterpart knows, even if the changeling learned them from a changeling of another seeming. They're mimicking the Contract exactly as their counterpart knows it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T15:58:11-08:00","id":1357261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1357098#post1357098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct--it no longer requires an invocation roll (or Glamour/Loophole), and the animated device can go wherever. It functions just like any other Retainer, except it's not a person. You still retain the Seeming benefits. The main benefit to spending the Experience to buy it as a Merit is that it won't cost you any Glamour and it will stay animated even if it gets out of range; it'll just keep doing the last thing you told it to do until it can't anymore or you give it another command. And Changeling players are always coming up with creative ways to use what they've got, so I'm sure there are other ones I'm not thinking of right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As someone making a Wizened Chatelaine character who will be rebuilding a mostly wrecked Volkswagen beetle that belonged to his grandparents, and someone who loves the Love Bug movies (both character and I), I cannot overstate my joy at this post. Thank you Meghan~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T21:08:50-08:00","id":1357304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1357107#post1357107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes; they in fact get all the seeming benefits their changeling counterpart knows, even if the changeling learned them from a changeling of another seeming. They're mimicking the Contract exactly as their counterpart knows it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> I have more questions.<br /> <br /> Do Fetch get Frailties as their Wyrd goes up?<br /> <br /> When a True Fae marks a Huntsman with a Title, do they lose access to the persona that Title represented while it's bound? Or is it more like The Title is just imbuing some of their essence in the Huntsman, but still keeps existing and doing other stuff while the Huntsman hunts?<br /> <br /> Does a Title get the Seeming benefits for their Contracts? Can they gain other Seeming benefits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T07:07:38-08:00","id":1357359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1357304#post1357304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Fetch get Frailties as their Wyrd goes up?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no reason to assume that they do, all other fae that develop frailties explicitly state that they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a True Fae marks a Huntsman with a Title, do they lose access to the persona that Title represented while it's bound? Or is it more like The Title is just imbuing some of their essence in the Huntsman, but still keeps existing and doing other stuff while the Huntsman hunts? </div> </div> </div>IIRC, that question was answered by one of the writers before, and the True Fae does not lose access to the Title themselves. They are imbued with a representation of the Title/part of it, rather than with the whole thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a Title get the Seeming benefits for their Contracts? Can they gain other Seeming benefits? </div> </div> </div>P. 270:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True Fae don\u2019t have kiths, courts,<br /> or anchors. They don\u2019t truly have seemings either,<br /> but each Title can use one seeming\u2019s blessing and<br /> bears something of that seeming\u2019s trappings regardless<br /> of the form it takes. </div> </div> </div>It does not spell it out, but it seems logical that the Seeming benefits of the associated Seeming are also part of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T22:40:17-08:00","id":1362583,"title":"","content":"Is it supposed to be super easy to heal Clarity damage? The rules make it seem like all one has to do is spend a couple scenes with a Touchstone and you can eliminate all Clarity damage. There isn't even a &quot;once per Chapter&quot; limitation or anything. What's the point of Contracts like Fortifying Presence (which is a Royal Contract that costs 2 Glamour just to heal 2 mild or 1 severe Clarity damage) if Clarity damage is so easy to get rid of by mundane means? I was expecting Clarity damage to require something like weeks of intense therapy. Am I missing something, or is Clarity really that much of a non-issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T23:33:09-08:00","id":1362587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1362583#post1362583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it supposed to be super easy to heal Clarity damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>At first, sure. Easy maintenance is still maintenance, and raising Wyrd and picking up Icons increases the frequency with which you are liable to suffer minor Clarity attacks even without Clarity attacks coming from things as simple as getting lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules make it seem like all one has to do is spend a couple scenes with a Touchstone and you can eliminate all Clarity damage. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Those are scenes you're spending not dealing with other problems and also scenes you're spending in the presence of one of the things it badly hurts you to lose access to or lose outright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the point of Contracts like Fortifying Presence (which is a Royal Contract that costs 2 Glamour just to heal 2 mild or 1 severe Clarity damage) if Clarity damage is so easy to get rid of by mundane means? </div> </div> </div>Because Fortifying Presence works with <i>anybody anywhere</i>. You can be miles into the Hedge and far away from the target's fetch or ex or pet occultist and Fortifying Presence still does the thing that it does as long as you hit its very broad trigger criteria.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was expecting Clarity damage to require something like weeks of intense therapy. Am I missing something, or is Clarity really that much of a non-issue? </div> </div> </div>Clarity <i>damage</i> is relatively simple to resolve. Clarity <i>Conditions</i>, meanwhile? Well, go check the Appendix to see what it takes to get rid of some of the Persistent Clarity Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T04:30:38-08:00","id":1362617,"title":"","content":"I'm starting up a new changeling chronicle soon, my first one actually, and I'm just wondering, considering how difficult it is to even give Wyrd 1 characters Clarity damage, and how easy it is to get rid of it, how can you even get characters to the point where they gain Clarity Conditions. Hopefully during the campaign it'll be different than I think, but currently unless I trap the characters in the Hedge for extended periods, I just can't see Clarity ever becoming a real issue. Is it supposed to be that Clarity is a non-issue for low Wyrd Changelings and is only supposed to be a problem for higher Wyrd Changelings? <br /> <br /> I was also wondering: do successes on the Clarity attack roll carry add dice to the damage roll? Or is it really the same amount of damage no matter how bad the trigger was? For a Wyrd 1 character is it only one damage die regardless if it's killing your touchstone or meeting your fetch for the first time? I know you get different amounts of dice for the attack roll, but the fact they all do the same damage just doesn't seem right. Why even have separate attack and damage rolls for this? Why not just have it something like Breaking Point value + Wyrd +/- Touchstone modifier +/- misc modifiers and have the result be the Clarity damage done. Seems a lot quicker and less complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 01-22-2020, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T04:50:18-08:00","id":1362619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1362617#post1362617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was also wondering: do successes on the Clarity attack roll carry add dice to the damage roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1362617#post1362617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why even have separate attack and damage rolls for this? Why not just have it something like Breaking Point value + Wyrd +/- Touchstone modifier +/- misc modifiers and have the result be the Clarity damage done. Seems a lot quicker and less complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that would mean high Wyrd characters would start failing their rolls a lot more often than low Wyrd characters for no proper reason. The devs wanted to divorce how often you fail and take damage with how much damage you take when failing.<br /> It works in combat because a success is a hit, and a better hit (more successes) means it should deal more damage. For Clarity attacks, what determines how likely you are to succeed or fail isn't supposed to determine how badly you fail. A high Wits+Composure individual with multiple Icons and Touchstones is likely to stave off the breaking point, but if they're high Wyrd it means that when they fail it's going to hit them a lot harder. You can't have that if you combine those two factors into one roll. (Unless you add a &quot;weapon modifier&quot; to the Clarity attack roll, but then you lose out on how variable the damage might be, and also more prone to take more damage if you're more prone to fail the roll, and vice versa.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T11:39:39-08:00","id":1362693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1362617#post1362617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting up a new changeling chronicle soon, my first one actually, and I'm just wondering, considering how difficult it is to even give Wyrd 1 characters Clarity damage, and how easy it is to get rid of it, how can you even get characters to the point where they gain Clarity Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower Max Clarity means it takes less damage to start applying Clarity Conditions in addition to there being less wiggle room between &quot;you have a bonus to Perception rolls&quot; and &quot;you have a penalty to Perception rolls and also may start hallucinating on a dramatic failure.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a Wyrd 1 character is it only one damage die regardless if it's killing your touchstone or meeting your fetch for the first time? </div> </div> </div>It's a <i>base</i> of one damage die. Conditions and Touchstone detachment add damage dice.<br /> <br /> This is how the Hedge's relation to Clarity gets tricky: The Clarity <i>attack</i> rolls from things that aren't part of the Hedge lose a die, but the Clarity <i>damage</i> rolls remain as normal, and the Hedge is prone to giving Conditions of the sort that add damage dice, so breaking points become that much more of a gamble.<br /> <br /> Gaining any non-Clarity Condition that spooks you or confuses your senses (which can include the Conditions on the Clarity Condition list coming from sources other than marking your last three Clarity boxes) is a Clarity attack with a base roll of two dice. In addition, the following Conditions add dice to Clarity damage rolls:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022 Amnesia (+2)<br /> \u2022 Awestruck (+2)<br /> \u2022 Berserk (+1)<br /> \u2022 Cowed (+1)<br /> \u2022 Demoralized (+1)<br /> \u2022 Disoriented (+1)<br /> \u2022 Frightened (+1)<br /> \u2022 Glamour Addicted (+1)<br /> \u2022 Goblin Queen (+2)<br /> \u2022 Hedge Denizen (+1)<br /> \u2022 Hunted (+1)<br /> \u2022 Lost (+1)<br /> \u2022 Oathbreaker (+1)<br /> \u2022 Paranoid (+1)<br /> \u2022 Ravaged (+1)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nothing directly in the system apart from the effects of the Hedge and the table of modifiers on page 104 affects the Clarity attack roll; attached Touchstones subtract dice from the damage roll, and having severe damage in the related boxes detaches Touchstones until they're all detached, at which point you add two more dice to Clarity damage rolls instead.<br /> <br /> What this means for a starting character is that mild damage is more likely than severe damage and less extreme in calm circumstances, but with a shorter Clarity track (average Attributes give you a maximum of 5 or 6 boxes), you're more likely to be dealing with normal Clarity Conditions and hallucinations while you adjust to life back on Earth; lower Glamour maximums means you're more likely to spend all of it in one day if you're spending it with any frequency, having your promises broken or being lied to or getting confused is a commonplace thing in an newly-unfamiliar place, and so on \u2014 you'll be getting minor pings regularly, including from your seeming-specific breaking point.<br /> <br /> Confused, Dissociation, Distracted, Shaken, Spooked, and Withdrawn are all relatively straightforward to resolve (and heal some Clarity by doing so), but the ones that aren't &quot;discharge this Condition by causing a problem&quot; apply moderate penalties that make it harder for a character to act gregariously and with their wits about them.<br /> <br /> When things are going well for a new changeling, they can get by well enough on account of having a chance die on Clarity damage rolls and no extra frailties, but depending on your Touchstones for Clarity when there's things after you and the world is a weird and scary place is a good way to have those Touchstones endangered unless you escalate in kind; taking charge and otherwise pursuing the negative modifiers for Clarity attack rolls is the main way you push back against mounting bonus dice to the damage roll from Conditions.<br /> <br /> It takes some cooperation from the players, but that's true for all the ChroD games \u2014 their responsibilities include highlighting their characters' weaknesses, making decisions that create drama, and confronting the problems you introduce as the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixed Awestruck damage bonus. 05-22-2020, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T01:26:28-08:00","id":1364492,"title":"","content":"Are there rules for forcing a Hedge Gate closed? One that someone else opened or one that is typically permanently open? I know Changelings can force open a Gate by spending Glamour, but can the same be done to force them closed again, or should it be harder to close a Gate than to open one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T08:33:32-08:00","id":1364545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1364492#post1364492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules for forcing a Hedge Gate closed? One that someone else opened or one that is typically permanently open? I know Changelings can force open a Gate by spending Glamour, but can the same be done to force them closed again, or should it be harder to close a Gate than to open one?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are not, because the normal state of affairs is that they're open for less than a minute at a time \u2014 usually if one's open for longer than that it's because something is holding it open, which needs to be stopped from doing so for it to close again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T21:14:11-08:00","id":1366230,"title":"","content":"Hello! I've started a new game recently and I'm having a little trouble wrapping my brain around how True Fae are supposed to work in 2E, specifically the relationship between their Titles, Regalia, and Tells<br /> <br /> The Title of a Fae gets a Tell for that Title, but does it have tells for each of the Regalia that Title can use? Or does the physical manifestation of the Regalia not have to be on the Title's person, like if it left it back in its territory in Arcadia while traipsing about in the real world? Also, does each Title need a separate manifestation for a Regalia, or can two of a True Fae's Titles have the same Regalia Token, i.e. does the Token belong to the Title, or does it belong to the Name and all the Titles can use whatever the Name owns?<br /> <br /> Mostly, I just need to know if I need to put a Crown on a cat when my Keeper is trying to be innocuous in the real world.<br /> <br /> Also, when a Keeper places its Title within a Huntsman, can that Title still manifest independently of the Huntsman, or is that Title effectively possessing the Huntsman and unable to act separately? So, can my Keeper dispatch a Huntsman and still go visit her neighbor for tea, or is the Keeper with/inside the Huntsman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25923-fidchel","user":"Fidchel","date":". 02-08-2020, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25923-fidchel","name":"Fidchel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T01:09:22-08:00","id":1366257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fidchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1366230#post1366230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! I've started a new game recently and I'm having a little trouble wrapping my brain around how True Fae are supposed to work in 2E, specifically the relationship between their Titles, Regalia, and Tells<br /> <br /> The Title of a Fae gets a Tell for that Title, but does it have tells for each of the Regalia that Title can use? Or does the physical manifestation of the Regalia not have to be on the Title's person, like if it left it back in its territory in Arcadia while traipsing about in the real world? Also, does each Title need a separate manifestation for a Regalia, or can two of a True Fae's Titles have the same Regalia Token, i.e. does the Token belong to the Title, or does it belong to the Name and all the Titles can use whatever the Name owns?<br /> <br /> Mostly, I just need to know if I need to put a Crown on a cat when my Keeper is trying to be innocuous in the real world.<br /> <br /> Also, when a Keeper places its Title within a Huntsman, can that Title still manifest independently of the Huntsman, or is that Title effectively possessing the Huntsman and unable to act separately? So, can my Keeper dispatch a Huntsman and still go visit her neighbor for tea, or is the Keeper with/inside the Huntsman?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I understand it (and someone better versed can correct me if I'm wrong), the True Fae has a number of Pact items, each one representing one Regalia that the True Fae can use in any of its forms. The Regalia do not need to accompany the Fae when it goes traipsing around...unless carrying said Regalia item with one of its Titles is part of whatever pact the True Fae made. The &quot;items&quot; don't have to be objects -- they can apparently incarnate as anything that resonates with whatever the Regalia is about -- they mention a cliffside representing Sword because it symbolizes strength and forthrightness. The Regalia have Tells that can be identified, so if one can learn the details of the pact that ties the Regalia to the name, they could mess with it. It seems that Regalia items are tied to the Name, not the Title.<br /> <br /> Also, I asked before about Huntsmen and Titles, and apparently the Title is still usable by the Gentry in question while it has a Huntsman out tied to it...I think it was said that the bit that's imbued in the Huntsman is whatever Aspiration lead to a particular Title being a Keeper in the first place. A Title can only imbue one Huntsman at a time, but it's still its own separate entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T08:39:52-08:00","id":1366784,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've got a simple one. Do video cameras (or camera functions on Smart Phones) work in the Hedge. I think I remember somewhere that they don't, but I can't see to find the proper passage in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24245-ruggedrock","name":"ruggedrock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:07:28-08:00","id":1366815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ruggedrock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1366784#post1366784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I've got a simple one. Do video cameras (or camera functions on Smart Phones) work in the Hedge. I think I remember somewhere that they don't, but I can't see to find the proper passage in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any complex technology, there's more things that can go weird even before getting into conceptual messes like what a camera reveals about its subjects.<br /> <br /> A video camera might work normally, but it's also possible that its screen or battery or lens might fail to work, or that the camera might show the scene around where you entered the Hedge or the inner turmoil of you-the-cameraperson or a speech a hobgoblin general gave in the area a month ago.<br /> <br /> Technology in general isn't reliable in the Hedge, and the more things it needs to work properly, the less likely that it will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-10-2020, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T06:51:20-08:00","id":1366963,"title":"","content":"After reading some things about Arthur's Brittania (Changeling, Vampire, Hunter) I was wondering:<br /> <br /> Is it possible for Vampires or Hunters to join a court? Specifically, is it possible for them to obtain Mantle or Court Goodwill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:38:07-08:00","id":1366973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1366963#post1366963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading some things about Arthur's Brittania (Changeling, Vampire, Hunter) I was wondering:<br /> <br /> Is it possible for Vampires or Hunters to join a court? Specifically, is it possible for them to obtain Mantle or Court Goodwill?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetches and fae-touched can't get a Mantle and the terms of Hedge Denizen and Goblin Queen specifically make your Mantle less effective, so I'm inclined to believe nothing that's not a changeling can have a Mantle.<br /> <br /> Court Goodwill, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:05:10-08:00","id":1367616,"title":"","content":"Should there be a -5 penalty to all rolls to act against a source of Cold Iron, in the same manner as other Major Frailties","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T19:19:20-08:00","id":1370484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1367616#post1367616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should there be a -5 penalty to all rolls to act against a source of Cold Iron, in the same manner as other Major Frailties</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so, since the specific wording says that cold iron acts as a Frailty Bane.<br /> <br /> A question of my own: The text for Thief of Reason says that the player rolls the successes on the Contract activation as a dice pool to attack a changeling's Clarity. Is this direct damage, or is it treated as a normal Clarity attack (ie, if the second roll is successful, the target's Wyrd is then rolled for damage)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T19:28:04-08:00","id":1370486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1370484#post1370484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question of my own: The text for Thief of Reason says that the player rolls the successes on the Contract activation as a dice pool to attack a changeling's Clarity. Is this direct damage, or is it treated as a normal Clarity attack (ie, if the second roll is successful, the target's Wyrd is then rolled for damage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the Elemental bonus specifically adds to the Wyrd of the target for the purposes of Clarity damage and both that bonus and the exceptional success result more directly use the term &quot;Clarity attack,&quot; I'd say it's not direct damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T19:38:19-08:00","id":1370487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1370486#post1370486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Elemental bonus specifically adds to the Wyrd of the target for the purposes of Clarity damage and both that bonus and the exceptional success result more directly use the term &quot;Clarity attack,&quot; I'd say it's not direct damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it seems that is right. Hmm, three rolls in a row? Yeesh. . . That said, the Contract does make for a good follow-up to Tumult. . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T16:31:39-07:00","id":1374652,"title":"","content":"Does a Changeling gain the Obliged Condition when the person they swore a bargain with is some other supernatural creature, like a werewolf or mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T17:04:52-07:00","id":1374659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1374652#post1374652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Changeling gain the Obliged Condition when the person they swore a bargain with is some other supernatural creature, like a werewolf or mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Weird side-effects may occur as well, but vampires et al aren't fae-touched and therefore don't have a connection to the Wyrd screwing up the deal.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, thank you for helping me cotton to why the capital-B Bargains of Courts also have to be done with non-fae entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T17:35:22-07:00","id":1374663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1374659#post1374659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Weird side-effects may occur as well, but vampires et al aren't fae-touched and therefore don't have a connection to the Wyrd screwing up the deal.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, thank you for helping me cotton to why the capital-B Bargains of Courts also have to be done with non-fae entities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I read that about Bargains... I told my Beast player that he could probably have his character found a new Court for Changelings, likely when his character became Incarnate. Then paused, and added this would probably not be a good thing. Nor a desirable thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T17:17:48-07:00","id":1374991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1374663#post1374663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When I read that about Bargains... I told my Beast player that he could probably have his character found a new Court for Changelings, likely when his character became Incarnate. Then paused, and added this would probably not be a good thing. Nor a desirable thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing they would feed on fear like the court of Autumn? And yeah, depending on how the court helps changelings stay safe from the Fae in terms of how members act, it could be a very bad thing indeed<br /> <br /> Though, considering the beast be an incarnate for this to happen, and the effects on the Hedge that Beasts have on it (damn, I hope the theroretical storyteller supplement discusses things like that), the court should offer very powerful benefits at whatever costs its have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T19:11:07-07:00","id":1376641,"title":"","content":"So if it's not infeasible for a changeling to make a tool out of shadows, and the Strix are at least nominally shadows, does it then compute that you could make fae items out of a Strix?<br /> <br /> Like, obviously there's a lot between Have Crazy Idea and actually Execute Crazy Idea that makes it unlikely, but in concept.<br /> <br /> (This idea hit me randomly and doesn't want to leave. This is more to get it out of my head than any serious questioning.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T00:07:57-07:00","id":1376677,"title":"","content":"Probably, but you may find the items are sympathetic for Strix possession since... well, it\u2019s of them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively it works and there are no issues from it since it is a weapon bound to your service, not theirs. It may even be more potent than normal, or alive... or even a legitimate way to make a Token dark sword with hunger, or a particularly dangerous Eldritch Entitlement. There are interesting things to do with it.<br /> <br /> ...dangit, now I have to make a Blackthorne entitlement...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T00:02:45-07:00","id":1378482,"title":"","content":"In regard to the Fae Mount merit, do its attacks do Lethal or Bashing damage? The stats don\u2019t indicate one or the other...<br /> <br /> And I assume a ramming attack/running body block would do Bashing damage, is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T00:43:33-07:00","id":1380046,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has been asked before, but if a Gentry puts their Title into a Huntsman and sends it out, do they lose access to that Title for the duration of the Huntsman\u2019s.... well, hunt? Does their domain lose its ruling figure, with no manifestations of them present? Or is it more like an aspect of their Title inhabits the Huntsman and not the whole dang thing? This point really confuses me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:46:56-07:00","id":1380137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1380046#post1380046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been asked before, but if a Gentry puts their Title into a Huntsman and sends it out, do they lose access to that Title for the duration of the Huntsman\u2019s.... well, hunt? Does their domain lose its ruling figure, with no manifestations of them present? Or is it more like an aspect of their Title inhabits the Huntsman and not the whole dang thing? This point really confuses me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assume analogy to ghouls rather than possession until proven otherwise. DE2 has &quot;distinguishing between a True Fae and her Huntsman doppelganger&quot; mentioned as a challenge and the metaphysics don't make it impossible for a physical representation of deep magic pactwork to be in two places at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:40:18-07:00","id":1381591,"title":"","content":"Just a very quick question: a changeling at wyrd 1 and with attached touchstone, must roll a chance die on his clarity damage rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T07:04:15-07:00","id":1381638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1381591#post1381591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a very quick question: a changeling at wyrd 1 and with attached touchstone, must roll a chance die on his clarity damage rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1362693#post1362693\">In the absence of Conditions that add Clarity damage dice, yes</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T05:42:15-07:00","id":1383131,"title":"","content":"Do hobgoblin have a morality trait?<br /> Do Goblin queens keep their morality trait after the transformation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T08:38:00-07:00","id":1383146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1383131#post1383131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do hobgoblin have a morality trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not natural ones, no.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Goblin queens keep their morality trait after the transformation? </div> </div> </div>Yes, given that the Condition applies a bonus to Clarity damage rolls and its two resolution criteria involve either a Clarity attack/breaking point or dropping back down to Hedge Denizen, whose non-&quot;become a Goblin Queen&quot; resolution specifically requires healing Clarity or gaining dots in an equivalent Trait.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T05:52:57-07:00","id":1383945,"title":"","content":"So I'm unclear about how magical abilities interact with Attributes in 2e. Might of the Terrible Brute specifically says it can let you get more Strength than your normal Wyrd limit. Does that mean that Red Revenge's +3 to all Physical Attributes only lifts you to the normal limit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T15:14:41-07:00","id":1384278,"title":"","content":"I'm really sorry if this has been asked before, but...<br /> Are Goblin Vows and Talecrafting getting updated to 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T21:44:54-07:00","id":1384353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1383945#post1383945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm unclear about how magical abilities interact with Attributes in 2e. Might of the Terrible Brute specifically says it can let you get more Strength than your normal Wyrd limit. Does that mean that Red Revenge's +3 to all Physical Attributes only lifts you to the normal limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might of the Terrible Brute gives you access to a move that increases your Strength by a variable amount, which is limited in terms of net bonus because a Common Contract allowing you to arm-wrestle your way to Strength 20 is a bit excessive. This in no way suggests that Red Revenge, a Royal Contract with a fixed bonus that inflicts a negative Condition on its user, can't break the cap.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, if a power boosts a character's actual Trait ratings it will specify if it <i>doesn't</i>\u200b adhere to the caps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1384278#post1384278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really sorry if this has been asked before, but...<br /> Are Goblin Vows and Talecrafting getting updated to 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been no indication that this is the case and the basis for Talecrafting working as it did is no longer the assumed framework of Changeling in 2e. The breadth of Goblin Contracts and the greater ease with which a character can strike a Bargain fills some of the niche of Goblin Vows, but I also wouldn't put money on the prospect of a game element so firmly based in 1e's model of pledgecraft returning without heavily reimagining the execution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T21:03:57-07:00","id":1384770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1384278#post1384278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really sorry if this has been asked before, but...<br /> Are Goblin Vows and Talecrafting getting updated to 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Satchel said it about Goblin Vows, but I'm not so sure about Talecrafting. There's something similar called dramaturgy coming in Kith and Kin, which sounds like updated Talecrafting, one that depends more on sympathetic magic. I'd wait for that before writing any updates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T21:23:40-07:00","id":1384771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1384770#post1384770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something similar called dramaturgy coming in Kith and Kin, which sounds like updated Talecrafting, one that depends more on sympathetic magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one mention of dramaturgy in OA&amp;T describes it as the way that a bauble is connected to the character whose dreams it was taken from (granting multiple bonuses to using the bauble against that character in particular), and the fact that it immediately equates that to sympathetic magic and effigies suggests that's more likely about things with a strong connection to a subject in general than anything really similar to talecrafting.<br /> <br /> That being said, K&amp;K is still in second drafts, so it'll be some time yet before we can say for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:05:57-07:00","id":1384800,"title":"","content":"Good day, does the core book says if<br /> Kenning rolls requires a reflexive or instant action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:15:10-07:00","id":1384829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1384800#post1384800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good day, does the core book says if<br /> Kenning rolls requires a reflexive or instant action?</div> </div> </div> </div>No in both editions, but kenning is also specifically a roll the Storyteller does and spending Willpower is a reflexive action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T08:06:35-07:00","id":1384845,"title":"","content":"wait, Kenning is a storyteller roll in 2e too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T11:55:26-07:00","id":1384882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1384845#post1384845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait, Kenning is a storyteller roll in 2e too?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to page 107, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:39:30-07:00","id":1385143,"title":"","content":"About the Darkling blessing of 2ed.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to become a part of a laser beam? If the answer is yes, them, if I point the laser 1km away and them shut it down, where do I reappear? At the end, middle or beginning of the beam? Also, can I meld my gear(backpack) with me when I use this ability or my clothes just fall into the ground?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:34:10-07:00","id":1385174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1385143#post1385143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Darkling blessing of 2ed.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to become a part of a laser beam?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Touch something insubstantial [\u2026] transubstantiating into smoke, shadow, a sunbeam \u2014 whatever's handy.&quot;<br /> <br /> As a storytelling tool this is pretty clearly keyed to things that an imaginary viewing audience could perceive through narration. Laser beams in fiction are generally either substantial enough to harm you or invisible outside of a medium that would itself be a valid subject for the seeming blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the answer is yes, them, if I point the laser 1km away and them shut it down, where do I reappear? At the end, middle or beginning of the beam? </div> </div> </div>Where you started or at whatever point along the length you moved to at your normal Speed in the intervening time. It's a power that lets you move unseen and somewhat unfettered by gravity, not a means of turning a high-powered flashlight into a makeshift bullet train.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, can I meld my gear(backpack) with me when I use this ability or my clothes just fall into the ground? </div> </div> </div>What literature have you read where the latter would be the way magic powers used by fairies works?<br /> <br /> If you're wearing it or carrying it and it's not substantially larger than a person, it can probably be assumed to go with you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T06:25:15-07:00","id":1385597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1385174#post1385174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What literature have you read where the latter would be the way magic powers used by fairies works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some sources that I cannot list here, because that would made me blush.<br /> <br /> But thank you for the explanation, sadly, my laser pointer transporter will not work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:04:09-07:00","id":1386056,"title":"","content":"Does any book set a minimum age for a changeling character?<br /> I understand that a newborn would lack the actual skills to escape, but if his mother is able to rescue him would him return as aa changeling?<br /> In 1ed i remember that the captive were required to accept contracts for being able to eat and drink, are there similar references in 2ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:40:15-07:00","id":1386614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386056#post1386056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does any book set a minimum age for a changeling character?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Old enough to be a person&quot; would seem self-evident. Clarity has certain needs as a narrative tool.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand that a newborn would lack the actual skills to escape, but if his mother is able to rescue him would him return as aa changeling? </div> </div> </div>Had the Fae put him to any role or purpose yet? Has he meaningfully experienced anything substantial in Faerie? If not, probably not.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1ed i remember that the captive were required to accept contracts for being able to eat and drink, are there similar references in 2ed? </div> </div> </div>2e does not currently have new material on how Arcadia works relative to the rest of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:37:01-07:00","id":1386631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386614#post1386614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Old enough to be a person&amp;quot; would seem self-evident. Clarity has certain needs as a narrative tool.<br /> Had the Fae put him to any role or purpose yet? Has he meaningfully experienced anything substantial in Faerie? If not, probably not.<br /> 2e does not currently have new material on how Arcadia works relative to the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for example, if a fae captures a newborn and turns him into a crying &quot;teddy bear&quot; for his fae &quot;children&quot;, then if the real mother rescues the newborn he could return as a Bestial Playmate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:00:40-07:00","id":1386639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386631#post1386631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for example, if a fae captures a newborn and turns him into a crying &quot;teddy bear&quot; for his fae &quot;children&quot;, then if the real mother rescues the newborn he could return as a Bestial Playmate?</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;old enough to be a person&quot; and &quot;meaningfully experienced anything.&quot; Infantile amnesia and an unengaging task are going to make developing the Clarity of this character challenging in a pretty dull fashion.<br /> <br /> The literature tends to indicate that the Fae are more likely to kidnap a mortal for a proportionally superficial or obsolete reason (pretty eyes on a plain assistant librarian, left in an attic after the untimely demise of the Lord they were to be gifted to, etc.) than they are to send for a transdimensional acquisition to make easily-replaceable qualities, which means your hypothetical changeling newborn is special enough that he probably doesn't secure escape or rescue until he's old enough to understand that being a noisemaking comfort object for monsters is more screwed up than normal.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the market is for literal infants as far as playable characters go, and there's ample room to argue that recovering a mortal newborn from Faerie is always &quot;early&quot; enough in the process that their fetch disintegrates and the child can grow up as normal as any other character with a supernatural encounter of that intensity in their background does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:19:09-07:00","id":1386641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386639#post1386639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See &amp;quot;old enough to be a person&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;meaningfully experienced anything.&amp;quot; Infantile amnesia and an unengaging task are going to make developing the Clarity of this character challenging in a pretty dull fashion.<br /> <br /> The literature tends to indicate that the Fae are more likely to kidnap a mortal for a proportionally superficial or obsolete reason (pretty eyes on a plain assistant librarian, left in an attic after the untimely demise of the Lord they were to be gifted to, etc.) than they are to send for a transdimensional acquisition to make easily-replaceable qualities, which means your hypothetical changeling newborn is special enough that he probably doesn't secure escape or rescue until he's old enough to understand that being a noisemaking comfort object for monsters is more screwed up than normal.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the market is for literal infants as far as playable characters go, and there's ample room to argue that recovering a mortal newborn from Faerie is always &amp;quot;early&amp;quot; enough in the process that their fetch disintegrates and the child can grow up as normal as any other character with a supernatural encounter of that intensity in their background does.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are saying that if the newborn is rescued early he would return as a normal human, but if the wyrd decide that he is special the time of the rescue would be posponed until the child would be self aware of his situation?<br /> I m asking because i m interested in a possible background for a pg or png who grew up as a changeling in the mortal world, without clear memories of his durance and rescue (his mother keept the secret)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:52:35-07:00","id":1386708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386641#post1386641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are saying that if the newborn is rescued early he would return as a normal human, but if the wyrd decide that he is special the time of the rescue would be posponed until the child would be self aware of his situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that if a character is important enough for a god to invest the resources and effort to take a human from Earth and that human is not grown enough to be an actor in their magical-political situation, then either they are effectively an object for the duration of their time in Faerie and can shrug it off as a bad dream like any other or they have to stay in Faerie for long enough to experientially retain such a wholesale change to their being in order for that wholesale change to be retained outside of Faerie.<br /> <br /> Remember that the Wyrd does not work in pure abstraction \u2014 it weights things as important because they're important in some way (possibly a way that has more to do with the past or the future than the present, but still some sort of way), not just because Destiny Says So.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I m asking because i m interested in a possible background for a pg or png who grew up as a changeling in the mortal world, without clear memories of his durance and rescue (his mother keept the secret) </div> </div> </div>As the Storyteller for a game where one of the PCs grew up in Faerie, I will say that this is difficult enough without removing an entire childhood's worth of memories of Arcadia from your toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T09:14:50-07:00","id":1386714,"title":"","content":"Could you use Changeling Hours contract on an object that is being held/worn by another person?<br /> <br /> To immobilize him by freezing his clothes in place for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T09:50:24-07:00","id":1386723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386714#post1386714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use Changeling Hours contract on an object that is being held/worn by another person?<br /> <br /> To immobilize him by freezing his clothes in place for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> It's an unrolled Contract, the described use-action would be indistinguishable from directing it at a person, and I can think of little to no precedent for this to be how, again, <i>a magical power used by fairies</i> would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T10:04:29-07:00","id":1386730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386723#post1386723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> It's an unrolled Contract, the described use-action would be indistinguishable from directing it at a person, and I can think of little to no precedent for this to be how, again, <i>a magical power used by fairies</i> would work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, ok, you could say that, but them, there's no instance of a Fairy tale of someone halting a plane in place by freezing only the plane in time, but you can do this if you spend enough glamour.<br /> <br /> I know that this contract is not rolled, but what defines &quot;Object&quot; in game system terms? My question is: As Written, what prohibits me of freezing someones gun or shirt in place?<br /> <br /> Also, if the only precedent needed for this is a written history saying that a fairy did it, nothing is stopping anyone from creating something like Artemis Foul fanfic saying that it happenned because a fairy did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T10:40:33-07:00","id":1386736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386730#post1386730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that this contract is not rolled, but what defines &quot;Object&quot; in game system terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The section in the book with the header &quot;Objects,&quot; Horodrigo. Page 191. It has an entry in the Table of Contents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My question is: As Written, what prohibits me of freezing someones gun or shirt in place? </div> </div> </div>The fact that people's clothes are not usually treated as separate elements in storytelling. This is not a simulation game \u2014 you are <i>telling a story</i> with characters using these powers that they got from magic bargains between reality and fairy-tale-resonant supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> In serious discussion, &quot;nothing says&quot; is a terrible justification for applying effects in ways that clearly aren't the things they're meant to evoke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if the only precedent needed for this is a written history saying that a fairy did it </div> </div> </div>This is intellectually dishonest and unproductive and you know it.<br /> <br /> The body of work that Changeling: the Lost draws upon has established trends that exist in aggregate. Much like 1e's Talecrafting sidebar providing a URL for TVTropes doesn't make everything written on that publicly-edittable wiki fair game for pattern-enforcement, &quot;someone could write fanfiction of a sci-fi story with fairies in it&quot; does not invalidate the fact that there is a cultural basis for What Fairies Do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:16:08-07:00","id":1386807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386736#post1386736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The body of work that Changeling: the Lost draws upon has established trends that exist in aggregate. Much like 1e's Talecrafting sidebar providing a URL for TVTropes doesn't make everything written on that publicly-edittable wiki fair game for pattern-enforcement, &quot;someone could write fanfiction of a sci-fi story with fairies in it&quot; does not invalidate the fact that there is a cultural basis for What Fairies Do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I'm not trying to be intellectually dishonest or things like that. But &quot;cultural basis for What Fairies Do&quot; is not a thing that helps here. Before Changeling, I've never had histories that tell me that you can leave a glass of milk in your window and a little elf would come to clean your house. Some cultures don't have those kind of histories. Many contracts don't do things that I learned on my stories that a Fairy would do, but do things that I would read on Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> Coming from d20 systems, sometimes is hard to catch up with some rules(or lack of rules) for Storytelling, I read a lot, but some things are really not clear and simply saying &quot;stuff works how fairy stuff works&quot; does not help much. There are movies and histories where a werewolf will rip his clothes when he transforms and others where the clothes will meld with him.<br /> <br /> Going for Object on pg 191, its things that have Durability, Size and Structure.<br /> <br /> Like, If I'm falling from a building and try to freeze my shirt in place to stop my fall. In some tables, that would be a neat trick, specially for a Royal contract, but if I can do that to my shirt, what would stop me from using it on someone else, to save, trap, etc, the other person?<br /> <br /> I understand that this would be blatantly overpower in some fights, like, if you could freeze an armored person in place for an entire chapter this would be a win button, and I'm not looking for that, but by reading things, what's stopping me from doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:21:43-07:00","id":1386868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1386807#post1386807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I'm not trying to be intellectually dishonest or things like that. But &quot;cultural basis for What Fairies Do&quot; is not a thing that helps here. Before Changeling, I've never had histories that tell me that you can leave a glass of milk in your window and a little elf would come to clean your house. Some cultures don't have those kind of histories. Many contracts don't do things that I learned on my stories that a Fairy would do, but do things that I would read on Harry Potter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <i>You can find many of those things on Google or a library search</i>. There are trends that you can observe that certain results deviate blatantly from.<br /> <br /> It would be one thing if we were talking about a gameline like Geist or Beast, where the archetypes of the monster you're playing are less directly represented in media, but this is Changeling. You don't have to struggle to find the fairy equivalent of &quot;stories about people who are half ghost that aren't Bleach or Danny Phantom.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coming from d20 systems, sometimes is hard to catch up with some rules(or lack of rules) for Storytelling, I read a lot, but some things are really not clear and simply saying &quot;stuff works how fairy stuff works&quot; does not help much. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Stuff works how fairy stuff works&quot; is not the starting metric, but it sure as hell helps as a general sanity-check for &quot;can this fairy magic typically produce a result that would be absurd to see in a normal story as a thing that a fairy does?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, If I'm falling from a building and try to freeze my shirt in place to stop my fall. In some tables, that would be a neat trick, specially for a Royal contract, but if I can do that to my shirt, what would stop me from using it on someone else, to save, trap, etc, the other person? </div> </div> </div>I would like you to read the text of the Contract again \u2014 more than the dice results and the seeming bonuses, because that descriptive text is not an elided-over optional part of this supernatural deal with the passage of time \u2014 as well as the definition of a turn on page 17 and the systems for Falling on page 190 (which ostensibly do not provide a per-turn drop-rate because most stories do not handle falls from heights greater than the napkin-math <i>144 feet</i> the average character will drop in that length of time).<br /> <br /> You're not going to draw a clock in the air between yourself and <i>the clothes you are wearing</i> in the time it takes you to fall farther than the height of most non-skyscrapers, and even if you did the result of <i>freezing your clothes in midair</i> as a means of arresting your descent is not going to be a terribly effective tool for avoiding the effects of terminal velocity on the living body you have that isn't a valid subject for the Contract.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand that this would be blatantly overpower in some fights, like, if you could freeze an armored person in place for an entire chapter this would be a win button, and I'm not looking for that, but by reading things, what's stopping me from doing that? </div> </div> </div>The books are not written in technical language and the fact that wordcount limits exist make forestalling every possible misapplication based on &quot;there isn't an explicit statement against it&quot; a fool's errand. If you are looking for me to produce a magic-bullet citation for why the Peasant Railgun and the Locate City Nuke are obviously not intended then you are out of luck, because my interpretive lenses are broad &quot;does this make sense for what the book says it's supposed to be?&quot; and &quot;does this seem obviously goofy for what the book says it's supposed to be?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T23:29:48-07:00","id":1387422,"title":"","content":"Re: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a><br /> So the flavour text of some of these contracts kinda mess with the mechanics of the game. Drawing a clock in the air is one of the examples on which I ask myself 'how do you do that if you fulfill the loophole to cast the spell reflexively?'<br /> <br /> Or Tumult, where you have to know someone's <i>true </i>name. What is a true name? The book doesn't help to clarify. Is it their full name they go by in day-to-day business? Is it their birth name? It's just one of those magics where 'o, there's this additional requirement where a situationally useful contract now can't be useful at all'. I would love to be able to use Tumult to neatly escape a couple of backalley muggers without having to sword them in the face, but since I don't know their true names I guess I won't.<br /> <br /> I guess I just dislike how the flavour is written to imply a certain method of casting a spell for some Contracts and in others it is just 'o you did the magic thing and now there is fire here'. &quot;You can't cast this magic when falling because making a clock with your hands take too long&quot; is a poor argument in my opinion since it is listed as an instant action, and there's a method in the book which makes any Contract a reflexive action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:29:38-07:00","id":1387485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387422#post1387422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the flavour text of some of these contracts kinda mess with the mechanics of the game. Drawing a clock in the air is one of the examples on which I ask myself 'how do you do that if you fulfill the loophole to cast the spell reflexively?'</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not spells. This isn't Mage, where the sole requirement for the effect is an exertion of will, this is you calling in a favor from the world by doing a thing in exchange for something else to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or Tumult, where you have to know someone's <i>true </i>name. What is a true name? The book doesn't help to clarify. Is it their full name they go by in day-to-day business? Is it their birth name? </div> </div> </div>The True Fae's mechanics make reference to the same thing. Pending clarification in a later book it's probably wise to operate under similar principles as found in folklore, e.g. the name you grew up with or the first name you were ever called or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\">the name that descriptively identifies you and in a way <i>is</i> you</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just one of those magics where 'o, there's this additional requirement where a situationally useful contract now can't be useful at all'. I would love to be able to use Tumult to neatly escape a couple of backalley muggers without having to sword them in the face, but since I don't know their true names I guess I won't. </div> </div> </div>It's almost like there's a completely different Common Crown Contract on the same page that would be more useful for this purpose than the one whose basic effect is to tell you what Conditions the target is under and explicitly links its further effects to subsequent action, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess I just dislike how the flavour is written to imply a certain method of casting a spell for some Contracts and in others it is just 'o you did the magic thing and now there is fire here'. &quot;You can't cast this magic when falling because making a clock with your hands take too long&quot; is a poor argument in my opinion since it is listed as an instant action, and there's a method in the book which makes any Contract a reflexive action. </div> </div> </div>Reflexive actions don't take up your ability to use an action in a turn, which is not the same thing as them taking absolutely no time at all universally, and that method requires you to pay the cost anyway.<br /> <br /> Further, in the specific example under discussion the issue is more the cluster of issues that also includes expecting someone to draw a circle <i>between themselves and the clothes they are wearing</i> to apply a Contract for affecting objects to &quot;objects&quot; that most stories don't differentiate from the person wearing them <i>in the span of time it takes for them to fall less than a hundred and fifty feet.</i> This is a deal with the passage of time through Arcadian pledgecraft to make things younger or older or unchanging for a bit, not a short-fall physics exploit in a video game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:36:12-07:00","id":1387487,"title":"","content":"Your nitpicking sure makes you come across as pretentious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:37:31-07:00","id":1387569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387487#post1387487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your nitpicking sure makes you come across as pretentious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't make personal attacks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T16:07:42-07:00","id":1387612,"title":"","content":"This may not be a terrible simple question, but I\u2019m making a Court whose patron entity is a Spirit named White Noise, and whose Mantle offers a variant of High Speech known as... white noise, which is like very heavily accented High Speech, allowing the Courtiers to speak with spirits but with confusion if both sides aren\u2019t used to the other\u2019s differences. How high up should it be for a Mantle benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T16:59:26-07:00","id":1387616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387612#post1387612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not be a terrible simple question, but I\u2019m making a Court whose patron entity is a Spirit named White Noise, and whose Mantle offers a variant of High Speech known as... white noise, which is like very heavily accented High Speech, allowing the Courtiers to speak with spirits but with confusion if both sides aren\u2019t used to the other\u2019s differences. How high up should it be for a Mantle benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you mean High Speech or First Tongue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T17:24:35-07:00","id":1387619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387616#post1387616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean High Speech or First Tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit language in general - apologies, I'm getting my terminology mixed up. I suppose First Tongue is the more accurate term for what I'm going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T18:08:04-07:00","id":1387624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387619#post1387619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirit language in general - apologies, I'm getting my terminology mixed up. I suppose First Tongue is the more accurate term for what I'm going for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, you're thinking of First Tongue. High Speech is the Mage Language that's metaphysically broken. <br /> <br /> I'd say the rating depends on three things<br /> <br /> 1) How hard is it for these courtiers to see and interact with spirits at all, much less in their language?<br /> <br /> 2) How often are you going to have a spirit that knows White Noise language but not the native human language in the area that this Freehold occupies?<br /> <br /> 3) Can courtiers use it for other purposes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T18:43:13-07:00","id":1387628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387612#post1387612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not be a terrible simple question, but I\u2019m making a Court whose patron entity is a Spirit named White Noise, and whose Mantle offers a variant of [strike]High Speech[/strike] First Tongue known as... white noise, which is like very heavily accented [strike]High Speech[/strike] First Tongue, allowing the Courtiers to speak with spirits but with confusion if both sides aren\u2019t used to the other\u2019s differences. How high up should it be for a Mantle benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of power level for that effect alone? One dot. In terms of placement based on where certain varieties of effect tend to wind up? Three dots.<br /> <br /> Important questions, given the power requirements for Courtly patrons:<br /> 1. What is White Noise's deal, as a Rank 6+ spirit?<br /> 2. What's the nature of the Bargain with White Noise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T19:41:04-07:00","id":1387631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387624#post1387624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yep, you're thinking of First Tongue. High Speech is the Mage Language that's metaphysically broken. <br /> <br /> I'd say the rating depends on three things<br /> <br /> 1) How hard is it for these courtiers to see and interact with spirits at all, much less in their language?<br /> <br /> 2) How often are you going to have a spirit that knows White Noise language but not the native human language in the area that this Freehold occupies?<br /> <br /> 3) Can courtiers use it for other purposes?</div> </div> </div> </div>For your questions;<br /> <br /> 1) As of now I haven't got most of their contracts and Mantle planned. However, a contract that allows them to see spirits and or their influences (that's Influence and their meddling) would definitely be in the cards. Therefore interaction with other spirits wouldn't be too hard to do.<br /> <br /> 2) The language of White Noise is limited to the entity of White Noise itself and the court based on it. The only others that could have it may be radio spirits around the area. I openly admit that I am not terribly well versed in spirits or ephemerals in general.<br /> <br /> 3) Courtiers can use the language for a number of means. Talking to their patron entity is one, as well as each other without others overhearing. A third is leaving other courtiers messages without others realizing it is a message. Another person on discord noted that a Changeling could run a radio channel using the language for covert dispersal of language. The whole &quot;talk to spirits and or werewolves with accent issues between them&quot; is just a hedge case scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387628#post1387628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of power level for that effect alone? One dot. In terms of placement based on where certain varieties of effect tend to wind up? Three dots.<br /> <br /> Important questions, given the power requirements for Courtly patrons:<br /> 1. What is White Noise's deal, as a Rank 6+ spirit?<br /> 2. What's the nature of the Bargain with White Noise?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) White Noise started as a relatively minor radio spirit who grew attached to the Ogre Helldiver who would go on to found the court. White Noise grew stronger and larger, eventually inhabiting a broadcasting radio tower (and resembling one). Becoming an official court patron was the act that helped push it into Rank 6, which helped push the court into being. It feeds off frustration (the courts emotion) and, well, static, and the freehold in general has a reception issue outside of wired connections. It's also territorial in regards to ephemeral activity, which plays into the fact that the court comes into power when the freehold feels that things are dangerous and everyone need to be ready to fight.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, all the patrons of the courts in the Freehold are beings who built themselves up as a partial result of their courts' founders. Bit of a theme of the freehold.<br /> <br /> 2) If you mean what happens when the court of White Noise comes into power, it's a bargain I am still pondering. The current idea is that no fae not part of the freehold can hear the words of courtiers unless specifically spoken to - they only hear static. However, that doesn't quite feel right for a court that comes into power at the height of tension/danger. In terms of bargain to being a patron for the court, that is something I am also pondering. Part of it does require that the radio tower White Noise is attached to remains active and powered, constantly broadcasting no matter the circumstances. Courtiers are to also have some form of electronic device making noise with them or in their homes. Most of my attention has gone to the train-based court that is part of the freehold (and the one that is active when things are calm/normal).<br /> <br /> From your points, Mantle 3 sounds appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T20:07:54-07:00","id":1387635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387631#post1387631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) White Noise started as a relatively minor radio spirit who grew attached to the Ogre Helldiver who would go on to found the court. White Noise grew stronger and larger, eventually inhabiting a broadcasting radio tower (and resembling one). Becoming an official court patron was the act that helped push it into Rank 6, which helped push the court into being. It feeds off frustration (the courts emotion) and, well, static, and the freehold in general has a reception issue outside of wired connections. It's also territorial in regards to ephemeral activity, which plays into the fact that the court comes into power when the freehold feels that things are dangerous and everyone need to be ready to fight.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, all the patrons of the courts in the Freehold are beings who built themselves up as a partial result of their courts' founders. Bit of a theme of the freehold.<br /> <br /> 2) If you mean what happens when the court of White Noise comes into power, it's a bargain I am still pondering. The current idea is that no fae not part of the freehold can hear the words of courtiers unless specifically spoken to - they only hear static. However, that doesn't quite feel right for a court that comes into power at the height of tension/danger. In terms of bargain to being a patron for the court, that is something I am also pondering. Part of it does require that the radio tower White Noise is attached to remains active and powered, constantly broadcasting no matter the circumstances. Courtiers are to also have some form of electronic device making noise with them or in their homes. Most of my attention has gone to the train-based court that is part of the freehold (and the one that is active when things are calm/normal).<br /> <br /> From your points, Mantle 3 sounds appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the big follow-up question that springs to mind now is what that Helldiver did to cement the Bargain (or if the founder did anything more than act as the channel for White Noise, which presents its own complications but feels germane to &quot;this thing became powerful enough to back a Court by backing a Court&quot; motif of the freehold). Presumably the Ogre in question did enough that they're not at the point of risking being consumed by their Mantle, but how did they enable White Noise to inhabit the broadcast tower, for example?<br /> <br /> I'm getting a sense that spiritual warfare is one angle White Noise is pushing; can the Court meddle directly in the Shadow in any way, or is this pure proxies-at-a-remove managed through the material-world activities of the Court?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T04:47:18-07:00","id":1387682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387612#post1387612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not be a terrible simple question, but I\u2019m making a Court whose patron entity is a Spirit named White Noise, and whose Mantle offers a variant of High Speech known as... white noise, which is like very heavily accented High Speech, allowing the Courtiers to speak with spirits but with confusion if both sides aren\u2019t used to the other\u2019s differences. How high up should it be for a Mantle benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, most Mantle up to 3 points only help with bonuses on skills, and give abilities at 4 and 5 points. So, 4 or 5 probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T04:51:04-07:00","id":1387683,"title":"","content":"About the Tatterdemalion\u2019s Workshop contract. A Wizened can build equipment at any size, let's build a Zepellin. I will use a Boat, an Oven, some blankets and ropes. Does the object gains a Mask to not draw attention or unnatural things just works and normal people can see them that way?<br /> <br /> Using the book examples, a normal person would see bathroom supplies and a fountain pen working as a Xerox Machine and would not question how that can work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T05:37:46-07:00","id":1387689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387683#post1387683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Tatterdemalion\u2019s Workshop contract. A Wizened can build equipment at any size, let's build a Zepellin. I will use a Boat, an Oven, some blankets and ropes. Does the object gains a Mask to not draw attention or unnatural things just works and normal people can see them that way?<br /> <br /> Using the book examples, a normal person would see bathroom supplies and a fountain pen working as a Xerox Machine and would not question how that can work?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The crafting process should look vaguely possible to the layman.&quot; Tatterdemalion's Workshop is the MacGuyver Contract and the results look like it.<br /> <br /> They are also, as per the normal rules for jury-rigging equipment, extremely likely to be Fragile or Volatile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:15:03-07:00","id":1387707,"title":"","content":"So, the object does not have a Mask and looks strange to normal people. But &quot;vaguely&quot; possible to function, unless close inspection by people of that particular area of work.<br /> Something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T10:03:40-07:00","id":1387751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387635#post1387635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the big follow-up question that springs to mind now is what that Helldiver did to cement the Bargain (or if the founder did anything more than act as the channel for White Noise, which presents its own complications but feels germane to &quot;this thing became powerful enough to back a Court by backing a Court&quot; motif of the freehold). Presumably the Ogre in question did enough that they're not at the point of risking being consumed by their Mantle, but how did they enable White Noise to inhabit the broadcast tower, for example?<br /> <br /> I'm getting a sense that spiritual warfare is one angle White Noise is pushing; can the Court meddle directly in the Shadow in any way, or is this pure proxies-at-a-remove managed through the material-world activities of the Court?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the proxies-at-a-remove angle was what I had initially envisioned, with just the courtiers gaining abilities similar to White Noise\u2019s potential numina and such. The ability to mark other things as targets for spirits or to make them more resonant with spirits is starting to work its way into my head though, and is already providing ideas for contracts. Certainly works well for a court who is meant to be the one who steps in when aggression is needed.<br /> <br /> As for what the founder did to secure the spirit for the bargain? I\u2019m not sure. One possibility is that she helped weaken other spirits native to the radio station to allow the one-to-become White Noise to devour them, allowing it to get bigger and stronger far faster than it could have otherwise. White Noise didn\u2019t start out as, well, a spirit of white noise initially, so devouring spirits native to the radio station would have gotten it to that state. Perhaps even outright purchasing the radio tower/station so she could ensure it would stay working without White Noise needing to step in and waste energy. I\u2019ll need to look into spirits (and radio towers) more to have a better idea.<br /> <br /> Also, funny you should mention risking being consumed by their Mantle, since that\u2019s actually a plot idea I\u2019ve got for the train based court. The founder is a hydra composed of trains that can split into a hive-like entity, which lives so long as at least one survives and can rebuild, and the founder allowed one into his own bastion to ensure it would live for months. This has had side effects like not regaining willpower via sleep, clarity attacks from the prolonged exposure, and the unprecedented effect of putting him at risk of gaining the Court Avatar condition even though he had no issues in establishing the court itself. (Sorry, couldn\u2019t resist blabbing about that)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387682#post1387682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, most Mantle up to 3 points only help with bonuses on skills, and give abilities at 4 and 5 points. So, 4 or 5 probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that other Mantles (such as Spring from the Seasonal Loeg) have 1 dot merits for their first Mantle dot, and it outright notes for making your own Mantles that dots three and four can do things like regaining willpower under different circumstances, rerolls of non-combat dice pools, or even spending a willpower to get temporary dots of other merits, or other comparable benefits. Even the main seasonal courts have things at Mantle 3 like getting armor based on Mantle dots or reducing contract costs by 1 when working against the fae. In either case a merit granting the ability to speak an off-brand spirit language would have fit in either spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:17:58-07:00","id":1388040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387707#post1387707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the object does not have a Mask and looks strange to normal people. But &quot;vaguely&quot; possible to function, unless close inspection by people of that particular area of work.<br /> Something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The object is constructed plausibly-enough by a Contract whose effect is &quot;you can jury-rig equipment without necessarily having the right tools or components slightly better than a normal attempt to do so.&quot; The Mask is functionally an extension of the mortal tendency in the ChroD to deliberately ignore and forget uncomfortable things like &quot;this guy is seven feet tall and has antlers&quot; or &quot;that camera winked at me with a human eye.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since the products of the Contract are not blatantly supernatural and the Contract does not make reference to the Mask in either its printed form or the 1e Contract that it shares a name with, I think it's safe to say that cobbling together a hovercraft out of an air mattress, a motorcycle engine, and some connective supplies is going to produce a hovercraft that looks like it was made with an air mattress and a motorcycle engine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1387751#post1387751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what the founder did to secure the spirit for the bargain? I\u2019m not sure. One possibility is that she helped weaken other spirits native to the radio station to allow the one-to-become White Noise to devour them, allowing it to get bigger and stronger far faster than it could have otherwise. White Noise didn\u2019t start out as, well, a spirit of white noise initially, so devouring spirits native to the radio station would have gotten it to that state. Perhaps even outright purchasing the radio tower/station so she could ensure it would stay working without White Noise needing to step in and waste energy. I\u2019ll need to look into spirits (and radio towers) more to have a better idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>One important thing to remember is that spirits get more complex and less conceptually pure as they grow in Rank; another thing is that Rank is not usually easy to raise, so White Noise would have to have been a fairly big deal already or this radio station acquisition (and/or whatever else was done) would have to have been huge enough to elevate a spirit to god-level from not-even-barely-a-god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-13-2020, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T23:56:11-07:00","id":1388251,"title":"","content":"So...slight rules debate happened elsewhere regarding Hedgespinning and how the whole excess successes thing works.<br /> <br /> In the game I was in, we had it so that if you rolled excess successes when you were in the Hedge, you would declare that you're banking them for Hedgespinning. And at a later time, the character would spend the successes to enact a Hedgespinning action.<br /> <br /> ...then I was pointed out how that's not how excess successes for Hedgespinning works. That there is no banking successes involved, that once the PC gets their excess successes, they must spend Glamour and use them immediately after they've seen what they rolled. And while not stated explicitly, that means the only realistic chance that a changeling has to pull off a Paradigm Shift is if they do an Extended Test or a Teamwork Test. This correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:29:32-07:00","id":1388257,"title":"","content":"It's all on page 205 in the Changeling book:<br /> <br /> &quot;Any mundane action a character takes in the Hedge may help pave the way toward Hedgespinning, although since the shifts reflect the emotions and general mental state of everyone involved, the results can have unpredictable side effects on exceptional successes and dramatic failures. Before each action, the player decides whether she wants it to generate shaping successes or not. If she does, the action takes a dice penalty depending on where she is: \u22123 on a trod, \u22122 in the Thorns, or \u22121 elsewhere. If she generates successes in excess of what\u2019s necessary to succeed at the action, she may immediately spend one Glamour and allocate those extra successes to Hedgespinning.&quot;<br /> <br /> So let's say you are using Brawl + Strength to punch a Hobgoblin in the face. You announce 'I am Hedgespinning' before making the roll, roll it with -1 because you are neither in the Thorns nor on a Trod, and get 6 successes. You can allocate any number of them to a shift and keep the rest (if any are left) to the actual punching.<br /> <br /> Now, if you do a Paradigm shift, there is an option that lets you bank successes for future Hedgespinning attempts:<br /> 2+: Bank a number of successes to add to a later shift within this scene (subtle or paradigm) equal to successes spent minus one, to a maximum of five banked successes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T01:55:23-07:00","id":1388273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1388257#post1388257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you do a Paradigm shift, there is an option that lets you bank successes for future Hedgespinning attempts:<br /> 2+: Bank a number of successes to add to a later shift within this scene (subtle or paradigm) equal to successes spent minus one, to a maximum of five banked successes</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I think THAT was the rule that my ST was using. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T02:25:10-07:00","id":1388277,"title":"","content":"So how does Hedgewise work? The merit grants a 2 dice bonus to Kenning a Hedge Portal. So let's say you experience some supernatural phenomena and spend the WP so the storyteller rolls your clarity. Do they add 2 dices to the roll if there's an unknown Hedge Portal nearby? What if you only get one success? Do you detect the Hedge Portal? Or the Mage?<br /> <br /> Or do you have to specifically ask your storyteller to roll for discovering Hedge Gates to get the dice bonus? Maybe I am a little bit dense here but a 2-dice bonus to a specific Kenning just didn't make a lot sense to me with how Kenning is described and rolled in the changeling book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T06:04:03-07:00","id":1388310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1388273#post1388273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I think THAT was the rule that my ST was using. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth pointing out that extended actions don't give you any better odds of achieving a paradigm shift; excess successes specifically don't accumulate between rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T11:47:59-07:00","id":1388375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1388310#post1388310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth pointing out that extended actions don't give you any better odds of achieving a paradigm shift; excess successes specifically don't accumulate between rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because I was initially going to say how as is, only being able to call on Hedgespinning (and by extension Oneiromancy) immediately after completing an action with any excess successes you happen to roll seems to make it less reliable and random. That a changeling could only realistically pull off Subtle Shifts on their own.<br /> <br /> And that if you ignored the &quot;banking successes&quot; bit then that means changelings would be completely reliant on teamwork actions in order to get the successes need to do the higher end Paradigm Shifts and that seemed...inelegant, since that would mean unless if the ST hands the players a scenario on a silver platter where a teamwork action, the players would have to force a teamwork action themselves just to get the successes to enact a Paradigm Shift...even if it means doing something that's not congruent with the story happening in those particular scene(s).<br /> <br /> Well, at least that doesn't seem to entirely be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 05-14-2020, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:29:12-07:00","id":1388389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1388375#post1388375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, at least that doesn't seem to entirely be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that kiths, entitlements, and Conditions all make it a lot easier to hit the threshold of exceptional success, and that paradigm shifts are a Big Deal that one would more likely have set out to do than squeeze into an ongoing scene; only changelings, Huntsmen, the True Fae, and the Hedge itself can enact paradigm shifts, and of those last three, Huntsmen manage it through the Fae Title imbued in them, Fae automatically succeed at Hedgespinning in general most of the time, and the Hedge doesn't even need to roll an exceptional success to impose them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Roll Athletics/Crafts/Expression/Occult/Persuasion/Subterfuge/Survival as a teamwork action to create goblin fruits/upgrade a Hollow/clear the Thorns/drastically alter the terrain, and it'll probably help if you were made for this/this is your job/someone involved is in the right mood for it&quot; feels within spec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T07:32:12-07:00","id":1388675,"title":"","content":"By what i can read on the core book it doesn t seem that to perform a reaping the target must be experiencing an emotion.<br /> Am i reading it correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T08:09:30-07:00","id":1388683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1388675#post1388675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By what i can read on the core book it doesn t seem that to perform a reaping the target must be experiencing an emotion.<br /> Am i reading it correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need an emotion to Harvest because the expression of feeling means they are exuding Glamour into their surroundings. Reaping, you're taking all the glamour straight out of their system, taking away their capacity to feel until they can build some spoons back up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:54:41-07:00","id":1389091,"title":"","content":"One of the possible options listed on hedgespinning paradigm shift is to learn the direction to a specific bastion.<br /> Now, if you are in the hedge the shift points you to the nearest gate of horn, but once you enter the dreaming roads..... no more hedgespinning allowed.<br /> Am i missing something?<br /> Does the shift impart you knowledge of the whole path to the desired bastion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:34:13-07:00","id":1389417,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to Hedgespin inside a Hollow for Goblin Fruits? The Merit Workshop seems to indicate that you can grow Goblin Fruits in a Garden inside your hollow, but I didn't find rules for growing them inside your hollow without other merit, Goblin Bounty, but this merit simply gives you the fruits, no rolls needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:20:07-07:00","id":1389434,"title":"","content":"Just how vast are the Hedge and Arcadia? Are they bigger than Earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:57:19-07:00","id":1389448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389434#post1389434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how vast are the Hedge and Arcadia? Are they bigger than Earth?</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume physical distance has any meaning in their realms? You travel at the speed of plot. The lands are as vast as the horizons of opportunity and as claustrophobic as your doubts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:02:13-07:00","id":1389503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389417#post1389417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to Hedgespin inside a Hollow for Goblin Fruits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The paradigm shift &quot;Add one enhancement to a Hollow you're currently inside&quot; wouldn't make much sense otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389434#post1389434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how vast are the Hedge and Arcadia? Are they bigger than Earth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bigger than the known geography of Earth, almost certainly, but in the Chronicles of Darkness the <i>actual</i> geography of Earth can also make that claim. The Hedge contains spaces that exist behind every mirror and reflect every dreaming mind as <i>side areas</i>, and Arcadia is arbitrarily large by virtue of being the claimed property of a numberless quantity of gods.<br /> <br /> Supernatural metaphysics in the setting being what they are, they probably aren't concretely infinite, but for the purposes of exploration within a chronicle they're big enough that you can reasonably assume there's more than you've seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T20:30:38-07:00","id":1389551,"title":"","content":"Can hobgoblins/fetches see past masks? Can they join courts and gain mantles?<br /> And for the second dot in winter mantles, you gain &quot;bonus dice equal to your character\u2019s Mantle dots when obscuring the truth.&quot;. What does that mean? Does that apply to stealth rolls, as you're obscuring your presence? Or does it just apply to things like covering up crimes and spreading misinformation and lies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26158-rhyzvanic","name":"Rhyzvanic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T21:17:45-07:00","id":1389558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhyzvanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389551#post1389551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can hobgoblins/fetches see past masks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They're fae beings, which are at the start of the list of things that can see through the Mask.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they join courts and gain mantles? </div> </div> </div>No. They're not changelings and can't swear oaths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for the second dot in winter mantles, you gain &quot;bonus dice equal to your character\u2019s Mantle dots when obscuring the truth.&quot;. What does that mean? Does that apply to stealth rolls, as you're obscuring your presence? Or does it just apply to things like covering up crimes and spreading misinformation and lies? </div> </div> </div>Things like covering up crimes and spreading misinformation and lies. This is a bonus from the same level of Mantle as &quot;mundane actions that encourage or bring about over-indulgence,&quot; &quot;mundane attack rolls when actively defending [your] freehold against a fae threat,&quot; and &quot;mundane rolls to intimidate or otherwise instill fear in someone.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T22:43:37-07:00","id":1389570,"title":"","content":"I'm reading the hedge navigation rules and they seem...very heavy and demand a significantly large amount of rolls. Have I missed something critical, or is the RAW/RAI that you conduct a chase mechanic roll every time the hedge needs to be traversed in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T00:07:46-07:00","id":1389580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389570#post1389570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading the hedge navigation rules and they seem...very heavy and demand a significantly large amount of rolls. Have I missed something critical, or is the RAW/RAI that you conduct a chase mechanic roll every time the hedge needs to be traversed in any way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Chase mechanics every time you want to travel anywhere into the Hedge.<br /> <br /> The only time you don't is if you're traveling down a trod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:34:42-07:00","id":1389628,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to bargain for a memory that a mortal has? So you can sell it later on the Goblin Market.<br /> Ex.: I can do your paperwork, in exchange you will give me the memory of your first kiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:18:44-07:00","id":1389656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389628#post1389628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to bargain for a memory that a mortal has? So you can sell it later on the Goblin Market.<br /> Ex.: I can do your paperwork, in exchange you will give me the memory of your first kiss.</div> </div> </div> </div>With an appropriate Goblin Contract or Dread Power, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:05:48-07:00","id":1389960,"title":"","content":"Did the Autumn Court contract &quot;Riding the Falling Leaves&quot; from Page 160 of the first edition corebook make it to second edition?<br /> <br /> It's the one that allows the character to transform into a cloud of flying leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:43:58-07:00","id":1389971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tomewilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389960#post1389960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Autumn Court contract &amp;quot;Riding the Falling Leaves&amp;quot; from Page 160 of the first edition corebook make it to second edition?<br /> <br /> It's the one that allows the character to transform into a cloud of flying leaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it s on page 158 of the second edition core, same name","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:56:32-07:00","id":1389977,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I don't have new edition yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:37:27-07:00","id":1390119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389503#post1389503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The paradigm shift &quot;Add one enhancement to a Hollow you're currently inside&quot; wouldn't make much sense otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bringing this back real quick:<br /> <br /> You can hedgespin inside your hollow to make some goblin fruits. Outside of the Paradigm Shift to produce any goblin fruit, is there any subtle shift that can let you find a random goblin fruit? Or the only option is to spend 2 glamour on a paradigm shift to create 1 goblin fruit?<br /> <br /> Also, how a &quot;farm of goblin fruits&quot; work on your hollow? Outside of the Goblin Bounty merit, because the Workshop provides you with bonus to roll and make a Goblin Farm, but I did not found any rules on making that farm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T18:27:10-07:00","id":1390143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390119#post1390119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can hedgespin inside your hollow to make some goblin fruits. Outside of the Paradigm Shift to produce any goblin fruit, is there any subtle shift that can let you find a random goblin fruit? Or the only option is to spend 2 glamour on a paradigm shift to create 1 goblin fruit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on your table, &quot;Introduce a minor beneficial twist of luck&quot; can probably be read to include &quot;come across a common goblin fruit of the sort that restores 1 Glamour when consumed.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how a &quot;farm of goblin fruits&quot; work on your hollow? Outside of the Goblin Bounty merit, because the Workshop provides you with bonus to roll and make a Goblin Farm, but I did not found any rules on making that farm. </div> </div> </div>Do farming. In the Hedge, anything that grows there is bound to be at least goblinesque.<br /> <br /> Remember that the bigger a Workshop's bonus is, the more Crafts Specialties it applies to, and that it applies that bonus to Building Equipment and other appropriate Crafts rolls. Depending on your setup, this could mean constructing frames for vines to grow along, tilling the soil so the shoots can take root, applying the right fertilizer, pruning branches, or otherwise creating an appropriate environment for your cultivars to flourish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T22:50:43-07:00","id":1390204,"title":"","content":"So the Loophole for Field of Regret (p. 161) is &quot;The changeling sings a melancholic song and lets a ghost possess her for at least 10 seconds.&quot; Now, do they mean as in the usual way as outlined in CofD's systems of &quot;place the Open Condition on yourself and have a ghost Possess you via the namesake Condition&quot;, or a more narrative &quot;whatever the ST and players deem is appropriate for the chronicle&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because if the former...well, there's a small issue that if you go by just the CtL2e corebook, changelings don't really have the means of creating the Open condition on their own. And that, while yes the general guidelines for Hedge ghosts are a bit on regular ghosts, they are different in a lot of key ways. And especially since there's pointedly no Manifestation chart, and the Manifestation section in the corebook seems to suggest most Hedge ghosts have little reason to take the other Manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T01:55:00-07:00","id":1390734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390204#post1390204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Loophole for Field of Regret (p. 161) is &amp;quot;The changeling sings a melancholic song and lets a ghost possess her for at least 10 seconds.&amp;quot; Now, do they mean as in the usual way as outlined in CofD's systems of &amp;quot;place the Open Condition on yourself and have a ghost Possess you via the namesake Condition&amp;quot;, or a more narrative &amp;quot;whatever the ST and players deem is appropriate for the chronicle&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> Because if the former...well, there's a small issue that if you go by just the CtL2e corebook, changelings don't really have the means of creating the Open condition on their own. And that, while yes the general guidelines for Hedge ghosts are a bit on regular ghosts, they are different in a lot of key ways. And especially since there's pointedly no Manifestation chart, and the Manifestation section in the corebook seems to suggest most Hedge ghosts have little reason to take the other Manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ll go for the narrative option, a sort of &quot;the wyrd possess the character&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T01:58:35-07:00","id":1390735,"title":"","content":"Does a changeling has a way to determine her current clarity damage level?<br /> I m asking because i m thinking about the fun factor of keeping it secret, adding a layer of doubt to the player perceptions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T09:52:32-07:00","id":1390799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390735#post1390735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a changeling has a way to determine her current clarity damage level?<br /> I m asking because i m thinking about the fun factor of keeping it secret, adding a layer of doubt to the player perceptions</div> </div> </div> </div>There are indicators for when it's full, when it's below half its maximum, when it's at any individual level below 5. Some of those indicators are specifically built around the character not knowing that something's amiss, but in general when a Trait directly impacts your Perception rolls as much as Clarity does it's hard not to be at least vaguely aware of what sort of place you're in with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T10:42:39-07:00","id":1390808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390799#post1390799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are indicators for when it's full, when it's below half its maximum, when it's at any individual level below 5. Some of those indicators are specifically built around the character not knowing that something's amiss, but in general when a Trait directly impacts your Perception rolls as much as Clarity does it's hard not to be at least vaguely aware of what sort of place you're in with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but by definition a mad man doesn t realize that what he sees could not be real.<br /> If a player knows that he reached clarity 1 he would start to suspect about hallucination, and to me it s more funny to keep that eventuality a secret.<br /> And by rules the changeling cannot realize by himself when he reach clarity 0.<br /> To solve the issue the storyteller could roll in secret every player perception roll, and he could declare as &quot;nothing magical registered&quot; every kenning roll performed with low clarity.<br /> What do you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T11:11:13-07:00","id":1390813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390808#post1390808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but by definition a mad man doesn t realize that what he sees could not be real.<br /> If a player knows that he reached clarity 1 he would start to suspect about hallucination, and to me it s more funny to keep that eventuality a secret.<br /> And by rules the changeling cannot realize by himself when he reach clarity 0.<br /> To solve the issue the storyteller could roll in secret every player perception roll, and he could declare as &quot;nothing magical registered&quot; every kenning roll performed with low clarity.<br /> What do you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a terrible idea, not least because Kenning explicitly can't be done at low Clarity, most dramatic failures in this system are going to be elective, and the game is typically played with multiple characters who do not necessarily share the perceptual limitations of a low-Clarity character.<br /> <br /> Unless you're doing some goofy shit where the entire motley shares a Clarity track, you're going to have to engage with the fact that the players need to know when what one of them sees is different from what the others see, and that's way less of a hassle when they can be informed participants in that process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T11:48:15-07:00","id":1390818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390813#post1390813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a terrible idea, not least because Kenning explicitly can't be done at low Clarity, most dramatic failures in this system are going to be elective, and the game is typically played with multiple characters who do not necessarily share the perceptual limitations of a low-Clarity character.<br /> <br /> Unless you're doing some goofy shit where the entire motley shares a Clarity track, you're going to have to engage with the fact that the players need to know when what one of them sees is different from what the others see, and that's way less of a hassle when they can be informed participants in that process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, imagine a session with four player.<br /> One of them sees a walking rock on the streets, the other three sees nothing at all.<br /> The first player tells them what he has seen, and the others are puzzled.<br /> Is he hallucinating?<br /> Probably yes.<br /> Or maybe all of the three are.<br /> Or maybe all of them.<br /> Or maybe it s a huntsman trap.<br /> What is real?<br /> The ones who doubt would face a clarity attack and start investigating.<br /> The ones who are sure of their point of view doesn t roll, but could face some nasty surprises.<br /> Wouldn t be a situation fun to play?<br /> Knowing the clarity levels would negate all the doubts in this case.<br /> Of course maybe this would require some homebrew rule modification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:27:38-07:00","id":1390840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1390818#post1390818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn t be a situation fun to play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who's run more games than he's played and had to execute on homebrewed mechanics without playtesting? <b>No.</b><br /> <br /> There are better ways to fuck with characters' perceptions than requiring you to <i>separate every character's sensory input channels,</i> a thing which is only remotely practical in online play through text.<br /> <br /> Doing this sort of thing requires both player buy-in and extra prep for very little benefit. The existing mechanics assume your players are bought in to respect the fiction and play along with their characters having bad information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:15:56-07:00","id":1391259,"title":"","content":"With an exceptional success, you can buy a mechanical device as a animated one-dot Retainer, using Dance of the Toys. Can the changeling upgrade the device to more than one dot retainer later, like, modifying his sentient car to be better at driving, instead of only having 2 dices to drive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 05-24-2020, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:10:58-07:00","id":1391276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391259#post1391259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With an exceptional success, you can buy a mechanical device as a animated one-dot Retainer, using Dance of the Toys. Can the changeling upgrade the device to more than one dot retainer later, like, modifying his sentient car to be better at driving, instead of only having 2 dices to drive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I lean no, for reasons discussed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1169452-fae-retainers-merit?p=1171369#post1171369\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T02:24:26-07:00","id":1391448,"title":"","content":"I m going to run a chronicle where players starts as humans for 3/4 sessions and then are turned into changelings.<br /> After they escape, when do you think they would manifest the first contract?<br /> How many contract they would manifest before they starts to use exp for buying them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T08:31:14-07:00","id":1391486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391448#post1391448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m going to run a chronicle where players starts as humans for 3/4 sessions and then are turned into changelings.<br /> After they escape, when do you think they would manifest the first contract?<br /> How many contract they would manifest before they starts to use exp for buying them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would already have contracts from their time in Arcadia, as they would being Hedge-fresh at character creation. Becoming a Changeling isn't like becoming a Deviant, where the changes reveal themselves gradually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:57:34-07:00","id":1391513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391486#post1391486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They would already have contracts from their time in Arcadia, as they would being Hedge-fresh at character creation. Becoming a Changeling isn't like becoming a Deviant, where the changes reveal themselves gradually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you think that all the starting template abilities, including pledges and portaling, are learned during the durance?<br /> I don t think so, because the template gives you the option to choose court contracts, and during the durance you coul not learn those type of contracts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 05-25-2020, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:07:18-07:00","id":1391546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391513#post1391513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you think that all the starting template abilities, including pledges and portaling, are learned during the durance?<br /> I don t think so, because the template gives you the option to choose court contracts, and during the durance you coul not learn those type of contracts</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you do gain all the inherent template abilities. You can't get any Court or Goblin Contracts, though, leaving only Arcadian Contracts. The least amount of Arcadian Contracts you can start with is two Common Contracts in your favoured Regalia. I would grant that to a character fresh out of their Durance.<br /> I would also grant an additional Common Court Contract free of charge when buying their first Mantle dot just to jump start them a bit. The first dot of Mantle is quite underwhelming and would practically be an XP cost increase to their first Court Contract otherwise. (Alternatively just make the first Mantle dot free. It's not what the book says about joining a Court after character creation, but I despise uneven starting distribution so I would grant any player not starting in a Court an extra XP to compensate anyway.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-25-2020, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:17:45-07:00","id":1391549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391546#post1391546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you do gain all the inherent template abilities. You can't get any Court or Goblin Contracts, though, leaving only Arcadian Contracts. The least amount of Arcadian Contracts you can start with is two Common Contracts in your favoured Regalia. I would grant that to a character fresh out of their Durance.<br /> I would also grant an additional Common Court Contract free of charge when buying their first Mantle dot just to jump start them a bit. The first dot of Mantle is quite underwhelming and would practically be an XP cost increase to their first Court Contract otherwise. (Alternatively just make the first Mantle dot free. It's not what the book says about joining a Court after character creation, but I despise uneven starting distribution so I would grant any player not starting in a Court an extra XP to compensate anyway.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems a good way to start, thanks.<br /> By the way how do you think that a changeling learns the basics of pledges and portaling in arcadia?<br /> Exposure to the wyrd energies?<br /> Watching their keeper using it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:43:22-07:00","id":1391554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391549#post1391549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems a good way to start, thanks.<br /> By the way how do you think that a changeling learns the basics of pledges and portaling in arcadia?<br /> Exposure to the wyrd energies?<br /> Watching their keeper using it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something that is inherent to changelings so those abilities are <i>gained</i> (as opposed to learned) sometime during the Durance and the transformation into a changeling. Exactly when is less important unless you want to play through the Durance (which I personally don't recommend, but you do you). When they figure out they have those abilities is a different question. Most Freeholds probably explain most of that stuff to newly escaped changelings they come across, while other changelings might figure those things out on their own. To a certain degree it's quite possibly instinctual; a changeling might figure out they can seal the words of another when they hear a promise made to them, or that they can escape bindings if tied up. As an ST, I would point out such opportunities to the players the first time or times it happens to represent the changeling PC figuring out that they can do stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:59:56-07:00","id":1391601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391546#post1391546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first dot of Mantle is quite underwhelming and would practically be an XP cost increase to their first Court Contract otherwise. (Alternatively just make the first Mantle dot free. It's not what the book says about joining a Court after character creation, but I despise uneven starting distribution so I would grant any player not starting in a Court an extra XP to compensate anyway.)</div> </div> </div> </div>First dot of Mantle is in fact free. That's how the societal oath to join a Court works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:29:58-07:00","id":1391778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1389570#post1389570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading the hedge navigation rules and they seem...very heavy and demand a significantly large amount of rolls. Have I missed something critical, or is the RAW/RAI that you conduct a chase mechanic roll every time the hedge needs to be traversed in any way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't like that aspect very much either, myself. I essentially dislike most systems that just require that many rolls in quick succession to function.<br /> For Oneiromancy it also seems like even a 2-3 Composure dreamer would make most skills a character with realistic/reasonable skills would have (ie. not min-maxed or overly skewed to a single specialization) veeery low in dice. Which then makes breaking into a Bastion without the key, essentially impossible.<br /> Perhaps Oneiromancy isn't something &quot;starting characters&quot; are really supposed to be doing?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T00:45:22-07:00","id":1391880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391778#post1391778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't like that aspect very much either, myself. I essentially dislike most systems that just require that many rolls in quick succession to function.<br /> For Oneiromancy it also seems like even a 2-3 Composure dreamer would make most skills a character with realistic/reasonable skills would have (ie. not min-maxed or overly skewed to a single specialization) veeery low in dice. Which then makes breaking into a Bastion without the key, essentially impossible.<br /> Perhaps Oneiromancy isn't something &amp;quot;starting characters&amp;quot; are really supposed to be doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book says &quot;An intruder can win her way into a Bas-tion with a paradigm shift, but the successes spent on the shift must exceed the Bastion\u2019s Fortification rating, which may require TEAMWORK to pull off&quot;<br /> But considering that a paradigm shift requires only an exeptional success in any kind of action, entering a human dream is not that hard, assuming a normal pool of six dice of presence+persuasion, increased to nine with willpower, you could persuade the bastion to open with 3 or 5 attempt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:47:37-07:00","id":1391914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391778#post1391778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which then makes breaking into a Bastion without the key, essentially impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I implore you, go back and look how oneiromancy worked in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:53:02-07:00","id":1391916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391880#post1391880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the book says &quot;An intruder can win her way into a Bas-tion with a paradigm shift, but the successes spent on the shift must exceed the Bastion\u2019s Fortification rating, which may require TEAMWORK to pull off&quot;<br /> But considering that a paradigm shift requires only an exeptional success in any kind of action, entering a human dream is not that hard, assuming a normal pool of six dice of presence+persuasion, increased to nine with willpower, you could persuade the bastion to open with 3 or 5 attempt</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really want my players to simply roll 3-5 times in a row for the same thing. It plays a bit silly. I'm a very &quot;fail forward&quot; sort of person, so I'm more likely to do something like let them choose to break in even on a fail, but make the dream more alert/more dangerous if they do, so they might choose not to then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391914#post1391914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I implore you, go back and look how oneiromancy worked in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't play the game back then, so I don't own the book. ;o<br /> I might be able to borrow it from a friend... Could you mention what you think I'd find if I did so? Is it better than 2e for my purposes/might I be able to borrow from it, or do you mean it in a &quot;Well, it used to be even more rolls!&quot;, which wouldn't be much solace I have to say. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-27-2020, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:36:26-07:00","id":1391925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391916#post1391916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be able to borrow it from a friend... Could you mention what you think I'd find if I did so? Is it better than 2e for my purposes/might I be able to borrow from it, or do you mean it in a &quot;Well, it used to be even more rolls!&quot;, which wouldn't be much solace I have to say. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to be that you literally <i>couldn't</i> enter the dreams of anyone who hadn't given you permission with a pledge (besides your fetch) and getting there was an extended meditation roll (Wits + Composure + Wyrd, each roll takes half an hour) that required a point of Glamour and <i>sixteen successes</i> (dropping to twelve successes and a point of Willpower for your fetch).<br /> <br /> You had to alter the dream before you could act in it as more than an observer, rolling more successes on a dream-riding attempt (the least intrusive form of oneiromancy) than the dream's Intensity (successes on a Wits + Resolve roll, subject to dice tricks if it was a recurring dream or a dream of a memory) cost you Willpower to keep the dream from unraveling altogether, and most of the things you could do with dream-riding had activity timers measured in <i>nights</i>. More involved oneiromancy cost Glamour and required you to hard-reboot any dream that was going on already.<br /> <br /> Oneiromachy (dream combat) was effectively resisted by two Attributes (since Dream Defense was equal to your highest Finesse Attribute and Dream Armor was equal to your highest Resistance Attribute; regular attacks used your highest Power Attribute and an appropriate Skill along with a bonus equal to your Wyrd, while Wits + Empathy + Wyrd could be used to attack by manipulating the environment). Since this was in an edition without Dream Health systems, damage was dealt to your Willpower and taking too much more than your remaining Willpower risked giving you temporary derangements.<br /> <br /> Getting into dreams that you don't have a pledge for didn't show up as an option until the Skein was introduced Dancers in the Dusk \u2014 two books past the game's initially projected limited run \u2014 and the only ways to start getting anywhere involve giving nightmares to your entry-point dreamer, getting help from an appropriate dream-creature (who usually needs payment in Glamour or dire threats), or making an extended action with a required obscure Skill Specialty to learn <i>who would be having a suitable dream in as much as a month's time</i>.<br /> <br /> Even then, unless you're using a guide, you still need to <i>find</i> the gate into the wider net of dreams, you have to make your way through a number of intervening dreams dependent upon how closely related your starting point and your target dreamer are, you can't use oneiromancy more involved than dream-riding and dream combat (both of which suffer penalties), and you can't just wake up like you can with dreams you have permission to (it takes hours of laying low to drift back to your own dreams, and if you ever run out of Willpower you're stuck in whatever dream you're in until you recover a Willpower point).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'll take the soft wall of &quot;you can get into anyone's dream, technically, but it will probably be difficult and expensive without a Key.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-27-2020, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T10:05:30-07:00","id":1391982,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the detailed write-up, Satchel! I must say it sounds <i>horrendous</i>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But it was a very interesting read. ^^<br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't mind so much the part about totally blocking off dreams unless you have a Pledge or something. That's a setting/power level decision. But if it's possible to get into a dream, I must be prepared for my PCs to potentially wish to try it. And after doing many rolls to resolve a chase scene through the Hedge (a part of the game that feels similarly over-systematized to me right now), arriving at the Bastion and then working up to some sort of semi-convoluted teamwork roll (you're basically doing teamwork just to do teamwork, in a way :P) rolling a failure on that roll is... quite boring! It doesn't move the plot, any plot, forward at all. It's just &quot;Well... you fail.&quot; and then blankly staring at one another across the table. :P<br /> <br /> I had one Oneiromancy session so far, where my players were infiltrating the dream of a neo-nazi. I had his Bastion basically be a sort of guarded entrance to a WWII camp. They got past it by knocking some of the &quot;guards&quot; nearby and taking their clothes, changing them a bit and pretending to be officers. I ruled it all as one &quot;attempt&quot; to get in, so one player rolled Stealth for the teamwork test (sneaking and taking out some of the guards), one rolled to socialize to read the overall mood/observe the functioning of the guards and give some tips for them all to fit in better, the third was the primary actor and rolled Subterfuge. They barely succeeded in &quot;convincing the gate guards&quot; (so, getting a paradigm shift) and got in. The moment they got in they were in D-Day among the americans, while the dreamer was a nazi general and pretty determined to win D-Day for the nazi party in his dreams at least. Getting to him was... challenging. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It was an awesome roleplaying scene! But what if they had failed the roll to enter in the first place? It'd have been a pretty anticlimactic &quot;You may not pass&quot; moment.<br /> <br /> I got a pretty neat idea from this brainstorming!<br /> I'm thinking that if you fail, you should wake up the next morning (or &quot;several hours later&quot; in case this isn't happening at night) with a slamming headache, vague memories of having been sucked into the dream in a helpless state, and a Condition that blocks you from trying again for some time. However, if you Resolve the condition, you find out the Key to the Bastion. Resolving it likely involves helping the Dreamer in some way, perhaps helping resolve one of their aspirations or doing another big service to them.<br /> That evokes the &quot;enter Dream with a Pledge&quot; feeling of 1e a <i>bit</i>, is very fey, but most importantly: keeps the story moving and <i>adds </i>to it.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's suitable for anyone else's table, but I'm going to try it out at mine at least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Once we can actually play together again. xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-27-2020, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T10:24:14-07:00","id":1391988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391982#post1391982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They got past it by knocking out one of the &quot;guards&quot; nearby and pretending to be officers. I ruled it all as one &quot;attempt&quot; to get in, so one player rolled Stealth for the teamwork test (sneaking and taking out some of the guards), one rolled to socialize to read the overall mood/observe the functioning of the guards and give some tips for them all to fit in better, the third was the primary actor and rolled Subterfuge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Teamwork rolls work. That's how Tactics from Hunter work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was an awesome roleplaying scene! But what if they had failed the roll to enter in the first place? It'd have been a pretty anticlimactic &quot;You may not pass&quot; moment. </div> </div> </div>&quot;When the dice hit the table, the Storyteller should have some idea of what will happen if the roll fails, as well as if it succeeds. Sometimes that\u2019s coded in the rules. If you fail on an attack roll, for example, you don\u2019t deal any damage. Other times, it\u2019s up to the Storyteller. If you fail a roll to jump between buildings to catch a group of hobgoblins, do you make it but fall on the other side, grab the next building by your fingertips, or plummet to the alley below?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That evokes the &quot;enter Dream with a Pledge&quot; feeling of 1e a <i>bit</i>, </div> </div> </div>2e's evocation of &quot;enter the dream with a pledge&quot; is &quot;A Bastion always allows an oneiropomp in if she has an active invitation, which takes the form of a pledge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Keys are vulnerabilities in mortal Bastions that change based in part on what the dream is currently about, so finding it out the next day isn't going to be much help. Mortals' lack of a Supernatural Tolerance Trait to contribute to their Fortification rating means getting in without spending Glamour just requires you to deal with having your rolls to do so normally contested by a single Attribute, barring the involvement of an important eidolon. You can literally just get into the Bastion by getting into the Bastion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:24:15-07:00","id":1392004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1391988#post1391988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how Teamwork rolls work. That's how Tactics from Hunter work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I let them teamwork with different skills rather than all using the same skill. It just makes sense sometimes! That's why I say I &quot;ruled&quot; it like that, using my prerogative as the Storyteller.<br /> No Hunter book is going to tell me I can't do something that just <i>makes sense</i> and makes the game better for everyone. ^^<br /> Especially not from way over there in the &quot;splat not included in this campaign&quot; corner where it can't do anything about it. :P<br /> <br /> People using skills simultaneously to work together to one roll =&gt; Teamwork! It makes (entering) the dream work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Using different skills to tackle different aspects of the same roll makes more sense than using the same one in many situations, I think. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;When the dice hit the table, the Storyteller should have some idea of what will happen if the roll fails, as well as if it succeeds. Sometimes that\u2019s coded in the rules. If you fail on an attack roll, for example, you don\u2019t deal any damage. Other times, it\u2019s up to the Storyteller. If you fail a roll to jump between buildings to catch a group of hobgoblins, do you make it but fall on the other side, grab the next building by your fingertips, or plummet to the alley below?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Obviously! That's one of the most interesting things we can discuss, ideas for how we might handle that! (The book is wrong about one thing though: It's not up to the Storyteller 'other times', but 'all times'. A storyteller should always wonder what's the best way to handle something for the good of the game and the enjoyment of all around the table, and shouldn't stop adjudicating simply because The Book Says! ^^)<br /> I've played plenty of Fate where there's essentially no hard rules for any failures, and you even have to decide if a fail is actually a fail or a very costly success to begin with (something I do for all my games anyway), so I don't have any problems with that in a general sense.<br /> But thanks for digging up the quote for me all the same. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2e's evocation of &quot;enter the dream with a pledge&quot; is &quot;A Bastion always allows an oneiropomp in if she has an active invitation, which takes the form of a pledge.&quot; </div> </div> </div>There's no reason there should only be one. ^^ Besides, there's many stories of fey creatures doing someone a favour and there being some weird price for it you didn't know of before, so I maintain: it's perfectly fey-y. ^^<br /> If it doesn't work for you, no beef!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keys are vulnerabilities in mortal Bastions that change based in part on what the dream is currently about, so finding it out the next day isn't going to be much help. </div> </div> </div>Then perhaps the Condition is simply a lingering dream-connection which can blossom into a temporary key under certain conditions, such as granting the dreamer their heart's desire.<br /> Don't hit me with the rulebook! I know nothing like this is in there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But it keeps the story moving, sets clear goals, still has a cost of failure (lost time in the dream, having to figure out what the target might want and actually getting it), and sets new emergent goals to be laced into the current story. I don't see any downsides. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortals' lack of a Supernatural Tolerance Trait to contribute to their Fortification rating means getting in without spending Glamour just requires you to deal with having your rolls to do so normally contested by a single Attribute, barring the involvement of an important eidolon. You can literally just get into the Bastion by getting into the Bastion. </div> </div> </div>Wait, so you don't need a Paradigm Shift? *Grabs the rulebook, opens to the relevant page and turns the book upside down.*<br /> <br /> Wow... Yeah, I guess you can read it like that! I thought you had to roll a paradigm shift achieved with a skill, always contested by at least the Fortification rating, and that was the only way to do it. As did my players who also read it. ^^<br /> <br /> That makes that way easier then and <i>much</i> less likely to come up as a binary &quot;succeed or fail&quot; roll. :P<br /> <br /> I can still see a use for the above described method should they be repulsed and wake up after a dream-thrashing, though. ^^ Far more fun that way. Players get a little something out of at least having found the Bastion and having their ass kicked. &quot;A little something&quot; here mostly being... more stuff to deal with. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:09:12-07:00","id":1392014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392004#post1392004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I let them teamwork with different skills rather than all using the same skill. It just makes sense sometimes! That's why I say I &quot;ruled&quot; it like that, using my prerogative as the Storyteller.<br /> No Hunter book is going to tell me I can't do something that just <i>makes sense</i> and makes the game better for everyone. ^^<br /> Especially not from way over there in the &quot;splat not included in this campaign&quot; corner where it can't do anything about it. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The Teamwork rules are quoted in the book that we're both referencing. Hunter is just the only game that has codified &quot;work together&quot; mechanics besides &quot;All the secondary actors compose and roll a dicepool with the same traits, then the primary actor rolls that pool with bonus dice equal to their successes.&quot; Teamwork is &quot;two or more characters work together on a single action.&quot;<br /> <br /> The way Hedgespinning and oneiromancy work mean you can easily leverage these kind of setup rolls to provide equipment bonuses and other boosts, and even without dreamweaving you can still leverage kiths, entitlements, Contracts Conditions, and so on to aim for an easier exceptional success; the average mortal has a default Fortification rating of 2, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T13:57:55-07:00","id":1392042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392014#post1392014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Teamwork rules are quoted in the book that we're both referencing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I have been saying, it's <i>my </i>ruling. :P I've never claimed the RAW says otherwise! Like I said &quot;<b>I </b><i>let</i> them&quot;. Not the rulebook. Me. I mentioned the Hunter book since you seemed to imply I couldn't/shouldn't use that house rule simply because there's a hunter mechanic that works in a similar way. But I don't care, I don't play Hunter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You are 100% correct about the RAW, no contest!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way Hedgespinning and oneiromancy work mean you can easily leverage these kind of setup rolls to provide equipment bonuses and other boosts, and even without dreamweaving you can still leverage kiths, entitlements, Contracts Conditions, and so on to aim for an easier exceptional success; the average mortal has a default Fortification rating of 2, after all. </div> </div> </div>It's not like teamwork doesn't exist outside of dreamweaving. Honestly, letting people teamwork with any skill that makes narrative sense, while NOT RAW, is no big deal. :P<br /> Many games do it, works great, feels good, thoroughly recommend. If you prefer pure RAW, don't do it! No problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But staying on my case about it after I point out that, yes, it's a house rule, and yes, I know it is, seems silly. :P Agree to disagree, I think. ^^<br /> <br /> If I failed to make it clear enough that I know it's a house rule and confused you, then my bad. D:<br /> <br /> Thanks for pointing out paradigm shifts are not the only way to break into a Bastion though, that is nifty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-27-2020, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T15:12:59-07:00","id":1392062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392042#post1392042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like teamwork doesn't exist outside of dreamweaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but the thing I'm describing there is not the Teamwork rules so much as using dreamweaving collaboratively and making use of the fact that you can take actions that aren't dreamweaving in a Bastion.<br /> <br /> Using Bedlam to daisy chain an eidolon's Competitive condition into an Inspired Condition for yourself so you can crack the Bastion more easily, or collaboratively doing a Streetwise roll to drum up an Organization to support your next roll, or otherwise making use of the resources multiple changelings can bring to bear is very definitely the sort of thing that the dreamweaving systems are built to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> Breaking into somebody's dreams is a big deal \u2014 this is a part of the game where the entire place you're operating in can cease to exist and scatter you to the far corners of the cosmology if things break badly enough; you're doing a heist on somebody's subconscious mind, and there's a whole sidebar about how a lot of the outcomes you'd be aiming for are more easily accomplished with other tools.<br /> <br /> My priority in general is understanding how the game is designed to be played, and if there's an opportunity to elaborate on that understanding in either direction, I'm generally going to take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T02:19:05-07:00","id":1392454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392062#post1392062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but the thing I'm describing there is not the Teamwork rules so much as using dreamweaving collaboratively and making use of the fact that you can take actions that aren't dreamweaving in a Bastion.<br /> <br /> Using Bedlam to daisy chain an eidolon's Competitive condition into an Inspired Condition for yourself so you can crack the Bastion more easily, or collaboratively doing a Streetwise roll to drum up an Organization to support your next roll, or otherwise making use of the resources multiple changelings can bring to bear is very definitely the sort of thing that the dreamweaving systems are built to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> Breaking into somebody's dreams is a big deal \u2014 this is a part of the game where the entire place you're operating in can cease to exist and scatter you to the far corners of the cosmology if things break badly enough; you're doing a heist on somebody's subconscious mind, and there's a whole sidebar about how a lot of the outcomes you'd be aiming for are more easily accomplished with other tools.<br /> <br /> My priority in general is understanding how the game is designed to be played, and if there's an opportunity to elaborate on that understanding in either direction, I'm generally going to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair! Those are some good options, too, will have to remind my players about them.<br /> Honestly, my biggest problem was percieving it as a pretty binary success/failure absed upon one roll. Knowing there's also just the option to &quot;go nuclear&quot;, beat up the guards, kick in the door and break in &quot;the old fashioned way&quot; on a failure helps a <i>lot</i> with that. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T03:33:34-07:00","id":1392469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392454#post1392454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair! Those are some good options, too, will have to remind my players about them.<br /> Honestly, my biggest problem was percieving it as a pretty binary success/failure absed upon one roll. Knowing there's also just the option to &quot;go nuclear&quot;, beat up the guards, kick in the door and break in &quot;the old fashioned way&quot; on a failure helps a <i>lot</i> with that. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if chances of success/failure depends on a roll it s not the end of the day.<br /> Sometimes a failure could give even better result, as the players must elaborate a new plan for reaching their goal.<br /> The important thing is that the failure itself must not be taken by the player as a frustrating NO, but as a better &quot;no, but maybe in another way...&quot;<br /> Oh, and remember that if the narrator needs an action to succed he could declare a failed roll as a &quot;success with narrative complications&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 05-29-2020, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:10:20-07:00","id":1392509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392469#post1392469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if chances of success/failure depends on a roll it s not the end of the day.<br /> Sometimes a failure could give even better result, as the players must elaborate a new plan for reaching their goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that, and talked about it a bit in one of the posts above, too. However, my problem <i>in this case</i> was that a dream takes a long time to reach already. There's an entire part before it where you're navigating the dreaming roads/hedge to even get to the Bastion (barring very specific contracts). And, RAW, that is a pretty &quot;heavy&quot; system with a lot of rolls already. At that point, one binary roll at the end of all that to determine success/failure after so much time/work has gone before it <i>would </i>be a problem I think.<br /> <br /> However, it turns out it's not a binary roll, so that problem does not exist! ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The important thing is that the failure itself must not be taken by the player as a frustrating NO, but as a better &quot;no, but maybe in another way...&quot;<br /> Oh, and remember that if the narrator needs an action to succed he could declare a failed roll as a &quot;success with narrative complications&quot; </div> </div> </div>I talked about this above as well. As stated, I consider myself a &quot;fail forward&quot; GM, so most failures in my game are &quot;No, however...&quot; by default. ^^<br /> I just don't think that adopting a fail forward mentality necessarily means that all failure mechanics get an automatic free pass because &quot;the GM can handle it&quot;. The GM is all-powerful, and can always handle it, that's never really in question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the thread is slowly starting to become more about my prsonal GM'ing style than my simple, answered, question, so I'll refrain from elaborating more on the topic. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:32:29-07:00","id":1392546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392509#post1392509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an entire part before it where you're navigating the dreaming roads/hedge to even get to the Bastion (barring very specific contracts).</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth remembering that there's relatively few incentives to use the Gate of Horn over the Gate of Ivory (chief among them being access to non-Social Attributes, immunity to the complications of high Dream Health damage, freedom from one form of time constraint, and no need to roll to leave a Bastion through the exit) and that navigating the Dreaming Roads works the same as navigating the regular Hedge (except the only &quot;normal&quot; territory is made of Bastions, so the wrinkles for trods and Thorns come into play more easily).<br /> <br /> From the exit of your own dreams, &quot;I want to reach X's Bastion&quot; is one Chase, and it isn't even that if the target's current dreams are linked to your own in some way and you're not in a hurry or working against something on the way there. The most basic aspects of this Chase, assuming average Traits and no existing Clarity damage or outstanding Conditions, are approximately as follows:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Hedge needs to get eight successes before you hit your required total, which starts at eight and is adjusted based on your Wyrd, Speed, Clarity, and Initiative modifier.<br /> \u2022 At Wyrd 1 with no incorporated Icons, a character with 2s in all Attributes (except their free dot from seeming) and no special bonuses has Clarity 4 (or 5, depending on seeming), Speed 9 (or 10, depending on seeming), and Initiative mod 4 (or 5, depending on seeming). They roll their choice of Attribute + Skill, which works less well if they don't have the Edge.<br /> \u2022 In normal circumstances, the Hedge has Speed 10, Initiative mod 6 (or 5, depending on seeming) against this character, and rolls five dice for everything (gaining an extra die each turn of the chase).<br /> \u2022 At this level, slight differences in Attributes will adjust your required success total by up to one die in either direction, but the bigger impact is that every dot of Wyrd you have reduces your required total by one success.<br /> \u2022 Since most player characters have substantially better Attributes than 2s in everything and your Wyrd and maximum Clarity can only go up, this is a fairly unoptimistic look at the odds even before the ability to take Goblin Debt to shorten the trip (and there <i>are</i> hobgoblins among the Roads).<br /> <br /> Most groups who aren't totally out of their depth will have better chances than this just from their existing stats; if you're Wyrd 6+, Composure 4+, and have a couple Icons under your belt, for example, you effectively only need to roll once on any Hedge navigation attempt where things aren't completely borked.<br /> <br /> All this represents the scene's worth of activity involved in getting from one dream to another, which can be shortcut past if you make use of a single Common Arcadian Contract and touch the dreamer in question. Circumventing it altogether is otherwise a matter of the stars being right and/or fortune favoring the prepared \u2014 which, again, tracks with an activity best compared to some sort of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QpR4p41F8G4\" target=\"_blank\">mind heist</a>.<br /> <br /> (Sorry for the ramble, but somehow I hadn't fully put together all the implications of Dreaming Road navigation working like regular Hedge navigation until today and I wanted to run through it given the opportunity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T12:15:58-07:00","id":1392622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and it isn't even that if the target's current dreams are linked to your own in some way </div> </div> </div>Is that explicitly stated somewhere? I mean, I just do it like that anyway because it is cool and makes sense, but I haven't read about it I think and I'm curious. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392546#post1392546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most groups who aren't totally out of their depth will have better chances than this just from their existing stats; if you're Wyrd 6+, Composure 4+, and have a couple Icons under your belt, for example, you effectively only need to roll once on any Hedge navigation attempt where things aren't completely borked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tend to play at splat power 1-3 most of the time (in things like Vampire anyway, haven't played Changeling too long yet), so most of the time it'll be far from this scenario. Though less dire than the one you paint, obviously. Then again, there can be time limits in play, negative clarity conditions, etc... so for Wyrd 1-2 characters it certainly can be quite close to that scenario.<br /> <br /> An opponent with 5 dice is pretty decent when it's only their starting off point. If the Hedge gets the Edge, it'll shoot up to 7 right away. This is <i>around</i> the value I'd expect my player's highest skills to start at, 7-8 (4 attribute + 4 skill is pretty damn competent, though they could reach numbers like this with a specialization here or there too). Now, assuming about average rolls, they'd need about 4 rolls. But if the Hedge has the Edge, it also picks what skill everyone should use that turn, and they either follow that or get stacking <i>penalties, </i>while the hedge gets that stacking <i>bonus</i> you mentioned. If you have the Edge, you also roll first and end the chase when you get your number. By the time 3 turns have passed, if the Hedge happens to have the Edge and picks skills that didn't suit one of the players, you might be looking at the Hedge rolling at least 10 dice, and that player either rolling a skill they might be bad it or choosing to roll a higher one with a potential penalty up to -3. :P<br /> The PCs will pretty much never all have the same skill high, so one or several of their members will be forced to roll a bad skill or take stacking penalties each turn even if one of the PCs has the Edge, since only one character has the Edge at a time and you only set 1 skill per round. You also lose 10-Again if you use the wrong skill and don't have the Edge.<br /> Being forced to use a &quot;bad skill&quot; even one turn can be bad, since if you fail a roll you incur the consequence of failure as set for that round, which might lower your chances even further.<br /> <br /> Both sides are sounding <i>reeaallly</i> tightly matched here, even when we consider Willpower. (&quot;use Willpower&quot; also tends to be the answer people give when you point out how close offensive/defensive numbers tend to be in combat, so we might be wanting to keep WP for that dream combat against eidolons we might need to do to break in ^^) It could really go both ways depending on specific conditions and so in play. Assuming WP use, let's call it 50% chance for each character to win (without WP I really doubt 50%, due to how the Edge works even when your team has it). But each character has to roll for themselves. So 50% chance for each character (average) to fail individually, means a party of 4 trying this would pretty much only have a 6.125% chance of getting through this without one person getting lost in the Hedge. And then we probably should spend time on the consequence of that. Otherwise, why are we rolling all this if we're not prepared to deal with the consequences of failure?<br /> <br /> So for 4 players, assuming 4-5 rounds of chase (which somewhat assume you'll get to use your higher skills most of the time, but the Hedge will end the chase around this time even if you don't), that's already going to be 20-25 rolls to resolve this Scene going purely by RAW, assuming nobody tries anything that might add more rolls in-between or something. And then there's a roughly 94% chance we'll first have to deal with someone failing before potentially moving on (I wouldn't let someone sit out the next several scenes to &quot;get back to them later&quot;, that'd likely be boring for them ^^ Slapping a quick condition or some other harm on them and then having them show up with the rest of the party anyway would be the fast approach, but it really doesn't seem worth 25 dice rolls to find that out :P).<br /> <br /> It seems quite over-designed to me, requiring too much overall rolls, especially the &quot;everyone rolls only for themselves&quot; approach really slows the action to a crawl if the entire Motley gets involved, which honestly sounds like a good idea most of the time considering several scenes will likely be devoted to this and you don't want people sitting out too long.<br /> <br /> All in all the math seems to point to 1 or several Motley members failing the Chase every time you do it (for non-Dreamweaving Hedge trips also, it's more of a general criticism) until everyone gets so advanced in skills/Wyrd that there is no chance of failing anymore.<br /> Even a 10% chance for each character to fail would lead to 35% chance per Hedge trip of failure, and I feel starting characters are <i>very</i> far off from reaching a 90% success rate on this. Very far.<br /> <br /> So it's a &quot;someone got lost in the Hedge!&quot; scenario nearly every time you try to just play it by the rules.<br /> <br /> Which is all essentially to say that:<br /> 1) There's just too many rolls in general in a single scene like this, to me, when we're only trying to accomplish one thing.<br /> 2) Due to the likelihood of failure <i>and</i> the amount of rolls, it's likely we'll spend a decent amount of time on this.<br /> 3) Therefore, the fear that much time might be invested in something that in the end would hinge on one roll, seems justified. (Though like we've said, it doesn't actually hinge on one roll, we've covered that. Just mentioning why I was worried about it in the first place.)<br /> <br /> I like the extra granularity of CofD over something like Fate, but for Hedgespinning/Dreamweaving in general, it feels waaaay over-engineered. Even if it's <i>less</i> over-engineered than previously over-engineered versions. :P<br /> <br /> I also don't feel extreme system knowledge should be required to just interact with an integral part of the setting. So even if you can sum up several ways in which players could stack the balance to their side a bit, I honestly don't want all my players to have to get degrees in gaming the mechanics to cope with the Hedge. :P<br /> <br /> (As an aside, since it's not really relevant to the kind of system this is:<br /> In Fate this would be:<br /> &quot;Hey guys, since you're in the Hedge now, you can use Create the Advantage in ways that wouldn't make sense in the real world, provided you do it in some Hedge-appropriate way.&quot;<br /> &quot;Ok, cool, cool!&quot;<br /> &quot;I'm going to treat the Hedge itself as a character, so it can oppose you when you try to navigate through it, and occassionally mess with you in other ways. Its skill level will depend on whether you're in the Thorns or not, and so on.&quot;<br /> &quot;Simple enough!&quot;<br /> &quot;Ok, that's... really all the rules we need, I guess!&quot;<br /> <br /> I love CtL but the Hedge rules really explore the limits of my tolerance for its tendency to systematize everything. :P Which is why I'll prooobably very often wave the chase rules and have them explain it with other means.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-29-2020, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T15:37:02-07:00","id":1392687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392622#post1392622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that explicitly stated somewhere? I mean, I just do it like that anyway because it is cool and makes sense, but I haven't read about it I think and I'm curious. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting it all together:<br /> <br /> &quot;In truth, Bastions are the only reliable hiding spots when trumpets sound and laughter like ashes and rust echoes beneath the never-changing sky. Even the weakest mortal Bastion provides some sanctuary, or at least a shortcut to elsewhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Bastions have more than one exit, opening out onto different Roads depending on how their dreams harmonize with the snatches of nightmare or reverie that lie along each.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Each Bastion\u2019s dream spills out into the surrounding area, so a traveler has some idea of what she\u2019s getting into as she approaches such a stretch: a dreamer stuck in a glass coffin in the woods imposes a dark forest filled with the baleful yellow eyes of hidden predators, while a dreamer flying among skyscrapers creates a shining metropolis where the sun glints from infinitely tall steel beams.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All Dreaming Roads are trods with ratings between 3 and 5, and characters navigate them as normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The scenery around a trod always maintains some semblance of similarity, but can change its nature \u2014 a wall of thorny brambles might turn into a mess of barbed wire, or a forest of razor-sharp ice crystals, or a wall of flame, but will never be open terrain. Certain landmarks remain constant, and the higher the trod\u2019s rating, the less mutable its terrain.&quot;<br /> <br /> tl;dr Dreaming Roads contain relatively consistent forms of terrain based on the dreams in the Bastions along them (which change and can link up to different Dreaming Roads from dream to dream), and you don't need to roll to navigate to places along their path. If you can steer the contents of your own dreams to be in line with the probable contents of their dream (whether through manipulation of or insight into their psyche via other channels), you have decent odds of not needing to look too far to find their Bastion relative to yours, because they're in the same motific/thematic neck of the woods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tend to play at splat power 1-3 most of the time (in things like Vampire anyway, haven't played Changeling too long yet), so most of the time it'll be far from this scenario. Though less dire than the one you paint, obviously. Then again, there can be time limits in play, negative clarity conditions, etc... so for Wyrd 1-2 characters it certainly can be quite close to that scenario. </div> </div> </div>My point was more that basic character creation outfits PCs with dramatically better stats than a 2 in every Attribute, which tends to knock off the &quot;Opponent's Speed is higher than yours&quot; disadvantage and increase the ease of beating its Initiative modifier. (To say nothing of how, if you're in Dream Form, you're calculating Advantages using just your Social Attributes.)<br /> <br /> Like, if you're playing at low Wyrd, that's expressly the point in the game's design where messing around in the Hedge and dreams outside of strongly controlled circumstances is a nightmare to deal with in exchange for fewer frailties, less frequent Clarity damage, and a generally easier time avoiding fae attention. Of <i>course</i> the prospect of breaking into someone's dreams nearly fresh out of Arcadia is daunting.<br /> <br /> We're out of the particular quicksand pit presented by 1e's mechanics, where being lost in the Hedge for long enough could increase the difficulty of finding your way out even if you spent the whole time looking for a way out, but Changeling's otherworlds always have been (and still are) threatening chiefly by how easy they are to get stuck in them without help from something that wants to extort you.<br /> <br /> (Speaking of which: again, Goblin Debt for a changeling character means you can trivially cut your required successes down to half of what the Hedge needs to hit. The practical difference between editions remains a shift from hard walls to soft ones.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An opponent with 5 dice is pretty decent when it's only their starting off point. If the Hedge gets the Edge, it'll shoot up to 7 right away. </div> </div> </div>The Edge is not universally determined by rolls, particularly not in situations where \u2014 again \u2014 everything has not already started out gone to shit, and the usual Skills for Chase rolls (Athletics, Survival, Streetwise) are all the sorts of things changelings of an exploratory bent are liable to have highly-rated. (Also, for regular Hedge navigation, remember that belonging to a freehold makes it slightly easier to navigate its territory.)<br /> <br /> Hell, there's a Royal Arcadian Contract that lasts for as long as you're in the Hedge whose effects specifically include &quot;until the sun next crosses the horizon, [you] always [have] the Edge in a chase.&quot; It's in the same Regalia as &quot;enter someone else's dreams through the Gate of Ivory&quot; and &quot;know the distance and direction of your choice of Hedge feature.&quot; This is loosely a specialist venue, but it's by no means impossible to prepare for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So for 4 players, assuming 4-5 rounds of chase (which somewhat assume you'll get to use your higher skills most of the time, but the Hedge will end the chase around this time even if you don't), that's already going to be 20-25 rolls to resolve this Scene going purely by RAW, assuming nobody tries anything that might add more rolls in-between or something.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> It seems quite over-designed to me, requiring too much overall rolls, especially the &quot;everyone rolls only for themselves&quot; approach really slows the action to a crawl if the entire Motley gets involved, which honestly sounds like a good idea most of the time considering several scenes will likely be devoted to this and you don't want people sitting out too long. </div> </div> </div>Why are you assuming multiple characters with the same goal and no circumstantial duress are necessarily going to be rolling separately, much less that those characters can't engage in Teamwork to make multiple rolls actually improve their odds of success?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's a &quot;someone got lost in the Hedge!&quot; scenario nearly every time you try to just play it by the rules. </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a reading that you came up with under the expectation that you should dislike the mechanic, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1104161-why-do-you-think-beast-is-good-bad?p=1104738#post1104738\">which I have an established opinion on</a>. The book is not perfectly clear on everything it presents, but there's a difference between imperfect presentation on a gameline with a troubled development history and the rules demanding you beat impossible odds because something is hard for a starting character to do.<br /> <br /> Also, I should point out that you said you were going to refrain from making this discussion yet more about your own GMing style and then launched into a ten-paragraph spiel reiterating how the mechanics don't mesh with your own GMing style, including a specific example of how you'd run it in a different game system, and your value judgment of these systems' predecessors has consistently just been some variant on &quot;that's horrible&quot; rather than &quot;that's harder than I'd like to make getting into other people's dreams.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's\u2026 some sort of something. :\\ I'm trying to unpack the ludonarrative toolbox, here, not beat my head against the rhetorical wall of &quot;why can't I do this hazardous thing that's modeled to take up a sizeable chunk of a chapter in very few rolls?&quot; Your opinion has been heard, and I'd be happy to answer more simple questions about this part of the game, but repetition of this sort is kind of exhausting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-29-2020, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T18:23:48-07:00","id":1392715,"title":"","content":"For the Seven League Leap contract\u2019s Ogre seeming bonus, it notes you can use the jump to make an unarmed attack against someone. Would this attack subtract the target\u2019s defence from the dice pool, or would it be considered an attack that doesn\u2019t take defence into account owing to it being a jump attack? I\u2019m not entirely clear on the mechanics of attacking like this.<br /> <br /> That said, I openly admit that I\u2019ve got <i>Rider <b>Kick!</b></i> stuck in my head conceptually, so I want to make sure it\u2019s a relatively accurate one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 05-29-2020, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T19:23:12-07:00","id":1392723,"title":"","content":"I don't see why the target would be denied their defense unless they were completely unaware of the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T19:49:02-07:00","id":1392730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392715#post1392715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Seven League Leap contract\u2019s Ogre seeming bonus, it notes you can use the jump to make an unarmed attack against someone. Would this attack subtract the target\u2019s defence from the dice pool, or would it be considered an attack that doesn\u2019t take defence into account owing to it being a jump attack? I\u2019m not entirely clear on the mechanics of attacking like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the benefit is just that you roll Strength + Athletics + 2 on a target in range and inflict the Tilt; in normal circumstances, the only type of attack that doesn't subtract Defense involves shooting at the target or them forgoing their Defense to Dodge, neither of which is baked into the Contract.<br /> <br /> \u2026It's not exactly Kamen Rider, but rereading it <i>does</i> now give me Chess Ogre vibes, which is. something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T20:57:25-07:00","id":1392742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392723#post1392723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why the target would be denied their defense unless they were completely unaware of the attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s fair. I\u2019ve never been big into Chronicles of Darkness games for the combat, so having this new option confused me a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392730#post1392730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the benefit is just that you roll Strength + Athletics + 2 on a target in range and inflict the Tilt; in normal circumstances, the only type of attack that doesn't subtract Defense involves shooting at the target or them forgoing their Defense to Dodge, neither of which is baked into the Contract.<br /> <br /> \u2026It's not exactly Kamen Rider, but rereading it <i>does</i> now give me Chess Ogre vibes, which is. something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the breakdown there. It makes a lot more sense to me now. No less Kamen Rider in my mind, but the idea for it working for a chess themed Changeling has some appeal...and makes me ponder on turning this Changeling from an Elemental to an Ogre. Doesn\u2019t help I can\u2019t think of a good element for him beyond darkness or somesuch, which interacts oddly with various contracts. How does one avoid harm from darkness being the primary one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T05:07:49-07:00","id":1392784,"title":"","content":"It says it's an unarmed attack, in which case Defense always applies unless something explicitly removes it. What I'm unsure of is whether the jumping roll is the same as the attack roll.<br /> If it is, you'd roll Strength(+2) + Athletics - Defense, dealing successes bashing damage and the Knocked Down Tilt on hit.<br /> If it's not, you'd first roll a Strength + Athletics jumping roll, and then a Strength(+2) + Brawl - Defense attack roll, dealing successes bashing damage and the Knocked Down Tilt on hit. (Small note: In this case you could apply Fighting Finesse to use Dexterity instead, but you'd forgo the +2 bonus since it only applies to Strength.)<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards the latter despite it being an additional roll because the regular text says jumping roll while the Seeming Benefit talks about an attack roll, and because the +2 bonus only applies to attacks, making it easier to jump if you're targeting an unaware enemy than if you just jump normally. Also, if it's a combined roll and you fail, you'd either fail to jump the distance at all (quite probably because of the enemy's Defense that they'd have no reason to apply on someone who failed to jump 20 meters away, causing a -1 penalty to their Defense for the rest of the turn) or you'd make the distance but miss the enemy, making it impossible to fail to jump as long as you target someone with an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:03:11-07:00","id":1393051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1392687#post1392687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting it all together:<br /> <br /> &quot;In truth, Bastions are the only reliable hiding spots when trumpets sound and laughter like ashes and rust echoes beneath the never-changing sky. Even the weakest mortal Bastion provides some sanctuary, or at least a shortcut to elsewhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Bastions have more than one exit, opening out onto different Roads depending on how their dreams harmonize with the snatches of nightmare or reverie that lie along each.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Each Bastion\u2019s dream spills out into the surrounding area, so a traveler has some idea of what she\u2019s getting into as she approaches such a stretch: a dreamer stuck in a glass coffin in the woods imposes a dark forest filled with the baleful yellow eyes of hidden predators, while a dreamer flying among skyscrapers creates a shining metropolis where the sun glints from infinitely tall steel beams.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All Dreaming Roads are trods with ratings between 3 and 5, and characters navigate them as normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The scenery around a trod always maintains some semblance of similarity, but can change its nature \u2014 a wall of thorny brambles might turn into a mess of barbed wire, or a forest of razor-sharp ice crystals, or a wall of flame, but will never be open terrain. Certain landmarks remain constant, and the higher the trod\u2019s rating, the less mutable its terrain.&quot;<br /> <br /> tl;dr Dreaming Roads contain relatively consistent forms of terrain based on the dreams in the Bastions along them (which change and can link up to different Dreaming Roads from dream to dream), and you don't need to roll to navigate to places along their path. If you can steer the contents of your own dreams to be in line with the probable contents of their dream (whether through manipulation of or insight into their psyche via other channels), you have decent odds of not needing to look too far to find their Bastion relative to yours, because they're in the same motific/thematic neck of the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice breakdown. ^^<br /> I agree with the conclusions drawn! It does play cleaner like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why are you assuming multiple characters with the same goal and no circumstantial duress are necessarily going to be rolling separately, much less that those characters can't engage in Teamwork to make multiple rolls actually improve their odds of success? </div> </div> </div>Because that's what the rules say to do. ^^ Chases are on the level of individual character by default. Each character even has their own amount of successes to shoot for, even in a group, and makes their own roll.<br /> <br /> The book calls out specifically that even companions roll separately:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s possible for some characters to succeed and some<br /> to fail, though, so sometimes changelings give up their<br /> victories to help out companions left behind or whisked<br /> away. </div> </div> </div>So everyone rolls on their own. it's a bit weird for everyone to get a turn and roll for themselves, but also roll Teamwork. Maybe if someone succeeds early, they can &quot;stay&quot; and Teamwork for the others, in exchange for suffering the same fate if the other person fails. That's a good <i>ruling</i> which I'd probably adopt, but it does nothing to counter the waterfall of rolls involved in such a scene, in fact potentially adding more rolls to it. But a good idea on the whole.<br /> <br /> I agree that 1 success/failure track per party would be cleaner, and probably how I'll house rule it in some fashion.<br /> <br /> There also <i>is</i> circumstantial duress, the Hedge itself provides it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This sounds like a reading that you came up with under the expectation that you should dislike the mechanic, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1104161-why-do-you-think-beast-is-good-bad?p=1104738#post1104738\">which I have an established opinion on</a>. </div> </div> </div>That's pretty unfair considering this rulebook is my first contact with Changeling, which my husband has always been raving on about and I thus definitely read with the intent to love it. ^^ And I do! Despite not liking <i>this</i> rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It's also pretty ad hominem, you're targetting me and my &quot;perceived&quot; intent rather than the arguments themselves. Which many, many people have an established opinion on, and not a positive one. :P<br /> When people have so many misunderstandings even in real-life where we have vocal and non-vocal cues to support our reading of intent, this seems a very risky conversation topic. The chance you're wrong is enormously high, and it leaves a bad aftertaste.<br /> <br /> But anyway: You're wrong, that is not the intent I read it with, I'd love to love it as it is written but currently simply cannot, please accept that going forward. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book is not perfectly clear on everything it presents, but there's a difference between imperfect presentation on a gameline with a troubled development history and the rules demanding you beat impossible odds because something is hard for a starting character to do. </div> </div> </div>Isn't the fact that I'm here asking questions proof that I'm trying to work through the &quot;unclear&quot; elements? ^^<br /> If I thought the book demanded impossible things from me at every turn, I'd chuck it rather than spend more time. My time is limited each day (which is why this reply took some time to get to, for instance) so if I spend time on it, it can only be out of love and a sincere desire to love it more. &lt;3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I should point out that you said you were going to refrain from making this discussion yet more about your own GMing style and then launched into a ten-paragraph spiel reiterating how the mechanics don't mesh with your own GMing style, </div> </div> </div>I said in one post that I was going to refrain from elaborating more <i>on the topic of the question</i> as it was <i>already answered</i> yet discussion wasn't winding down since there were remarks being made back and forth that I percieved as being only about GM'ing style, and wouldn't ever end if I didn't just stop replying to them. And I did not elaborate on that topic anymore. I didn't make some solemn life-long promise never to talk about my GM'ing style. :P<br /> You continued to reply, as is your right, and your answers picked out <i>new topics</i> that I wanted to respond to, as is <i>my</i> right. This isn't about my original question for Oneiromancy anymore, but rather the hedge navigation rules. And so I replied again. ^^<br /> <br /> But even if I had said I didn't want to talk about my GM'ing style anymore, I don't see that anyone'd have any right to use that as an argument against me. Even in that hypothetical situation I could change my mind, surely. I find mentioning how I play things helps understand where I'm coming from, and it also helps people see that I don't necessarily think a rule is <i>bad</i> or <i>incompetently written</i>, simply because it doesn't mesh with how <i>I</i> do things.<br /> It's more nuanced, a positive thing all around I think.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't quite get what you're trying to say, it feels like I'm being told off, but I don't see that any wrongdoing has occurred. ;o<br /> Likely, I simply misread you. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> including a specific example of how you'd run it in a different game system, and your value judgment of these systems' predecessors has consistently just been some variant on &quot;that's horrible&quot; rather than &quot;that's harder than I'd like to make getting into other people's dreams.&quot; </div> </div> </div>This is a good example of how it can be hard to read other's intent. Because you <i>think </i>I meant &quot;that's harder than I'd like to make getting into other people's dreams&quot; when I said &quot;that's horrible&quot;, while what I meant was: &quot;those rules seem heavy to process and complex&quot;. If it sounds like you need a flowchart to figure out the next bit, it sounds pretty horrible to me. But others might be really into it.<br /> <br /> This has <i>nothing</i> to do with how hard it is. I don't mind if it's so hard that starting characters just <i>can't</i> do it. See this post:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition/page23\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edition/page23</a><br /> &quot;Perhaps Oneiromancy isn't something &quot;starting characters&quot; are really supposed to be doing?&quot;<br /> =&gt; Was still about only Oneiromancy then, but you can just apply it to the Hedge in general as well. And this was me suggesting that perhaps my problems with it come from thinking that it should be something starting characters routinely do. A &quot;Yes, indeed, starting characters generally should shy away from this.&quot; answer to this is <i>acceptable</i>.<br /> <br /> And then there's this post:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition/page24\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edition/page24</a><br /> Like I said there, I don't even mind if it's so hard as to be <i>totally impossible</i> unless you meet a specific criterium (here: having a pledge).<br /> <br /> My problem is <i>only</i> with how <i>heavy</i> the rules for this feel to me, not with how difficult they are.<br /> <br /> If the rule simply was &quot;Roll this one dice pool, if you succeed, you get there.&quot; I'd have <i>less</i> problems with it, even if it asked for a ludicrous 15 successes or something. I'd still have an issue because that'd be <i>too</i> light, but then at least it wouldn't be a lot of mechanics to have to remember/teach/whatever for this specific task.<br /> The fact that it'd be totally impossible for starting characters would not be my concern; I can still give access through plot and specific circumstances where desired, <i>as I can too now, yes, I know.</i> ^^<br /> My problem isn't that &quot;the Storyteller can't handle it&quot;, because like I've said &quot;the Storyteller can <i>always</i> handle it&quot;, but that if a group suddenly unexpectedly decides to want to go for it and we default back to the RAW rules... Well, they still appear very heavy and we'll have a ton of rolling to do.<br /> <br /> Even the comment about at 50% chance for success the party only having a 6.125% to not lose at least one person is not a concern with difficulty. If they only had a 6.125% to <i>succeed</i> at starting power level, then fair enough. The point was about the situation that results from that other ~94%. Which we might be able to avoid by having the successful people opt to stay behind and provide Teamwork. It won't help the amount of rolls, but it helps a bit with the other of my personal issues with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the ludonarrative toolbox, here </div> </div> </div>This is very disrespectful, I have never shown you disrespect in this way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your opinion has been heard, and I'd be happy to answer more simple questions about this part of the game, but repetition of this sort is kind of exhausting. </div> </div> </div>I tried several times to exit stage right by thanking you/others and saying my question was resolved now. ^^ I even just blanket said that you were right, you solved my problem with Oneiromancy, I was and am grateful. ^^<br /> You kept it going for yourself by responding again to replies I made to Neos01 and bringing up new elements. You can't blame me for that, honestly. :P<br /> <br /> But you put a lot of time into it and I am grateful for the suggestions offered, as my understand HAS expanded and I took away several pieces of advice that will help me, so if you're exhausted I will give you this solemn promise (an actual promise this time, not just a sentence taken out of context :P): If you choose to reply to this comment, I shall read it, post a &quot;thank you&quot;, and we will let it end there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But don't feel forced, I'm not telling that you absolutely must reply, obviously. I'm grateful for your thoughts up to this point, truly, even if I can't like the Hedge navigation rules. They don't have to be to everyone's tastes, that's impossible anyway. But I tried to like them, and love the system overall. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-31-2020, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T18:54:51-07:00","id":1393287,"title":"","content":"Talking of the Dreaming Roads, a notionally simple question with little in the way of textual answers that I can recall: Bastions being how they are, they're probably not landmarks along the trods that make up the Roads (or subject to such a limitation in quantity); what sort of milestones might be found on the Wayward Paths?<br /> <br /> I assume they're not instances of the Gate of Horn, since that would kind of render the &quot;they're 3-5-dot trods&quot; distinction pointless when taken in combination with Hedgespinning not working and the points they bridge being completely outside the mortal world (the distance between points in which is otherwise presented as the starting factor for a trod's rating).<br /> <br /> Separately, I'm not sure how to read the Hedge navigation target number modifier for traveling a trod; since separate goals require separate chases, what does &quot;per milestone desired&quot; mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T02:45:13-07:00","id":1393379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1393287#post1393287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separately, I'm not sure how to read the Hedge navigation target number modifier for traveling a trod; since separate goals require separate chases, what does &amp;quot;per milestone desired&amp;quot; mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Trod is made up of two end points and a number of milestones equal to its rating. Each end point and milestone is its own location. When the characters declare which location they want to reach upon having a chase on a Trod (if their task is time sensitive; otherwise no need to roll), each milestone that needs to be reached adds to the target number.<br /> On a four dot Trod where each end point is a different Freehold: If the characters start at one end point and wants to reach the goblin market at the first milestone, they start a chase don't add anything to the target number. If they then want to reach the bank of treasured memories at the third milestone, they start another chase and add one to the target number. If they've picked up all their supplies on this apparently time sensitive errand run and want to reach a Freehold, they could choose to continue, passing the fourth and last milestone, adding one to the target number, or they could turn back to the Freehold where they once came and add two to the target number.<br /> The language is a bit unclear whether it's about each milestone you desire <i>to reach</i> or <i>to pass</i> but I assume the latter because otherwise you'd always end up adding to the target number unless you're at the milestone closest to an end point and go to it. Also, reaching the last milestone would add just as much to the target number as reaching the end point beyond it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T03:00:41-07:00","id":1393381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1393287#post1393287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking of the Dreaming Roads, a notionally simple question with little in the way of textual answers that I can recall: Bastions being how they are, they're probably not landmarks along the trods that make up the Roads (or subject to such a limitation in quantity); what sort of milestones might be found on the Wayward Paths?<br /> <br /> I assume they're not instances of the Gate of Horn, since that would kind of render the &amp;quot;they're 3-5-dot trods&amp;quot; distinction pointless when taken in combination with Hedgespinning not working and the points they bridge being completely outside the mortal world (the distance between points in which is otherwise presented as the starting factor for a trod's rating).<br /> <br /> Separately, I'm not sure how to read the Hedge navigation target number modifier for traveling a trod; since separate goals require separate chases, what does &amp;quot;per milestone desired&amp;quot; mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I m inclined to say that:<br /> -dreaming roads/trods has a gate of horn as an entry point<br /> -intersection with other roads AND/OR the outskirts of Bastions as Milestones<br /> -Another Gate of horn, crossroad or outskirt as an end point<br /> <br /> Because even if the outskirts of a Bastion changes every night it could remain on the same relative position on a dreaming road.<br /> <br /> In this way Bastion with different exits could exist between two roads, and hedgespinning in the hedge could point you to the gate of horn of a road wich has the desired bastion as a milestone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T10:18:47-07:00","id":1393791,"title":"","content":"With Changeling Hours, while the \u201cFreeze the clock\u201d effect is pretty evidently meant to only last a scene, are \u201cRewind the clock\u201d and \u201cSpeed the clock\u201d also meant to only last the scene? That is, will damage return/be undone after the scene is over (barring any other Seeming benefits made by a group)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T10:33:35-07:00","id":1393798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1393791#post1393791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Changeling Hours, while the \u201cFreeze the clock\u201d effect is pretty evidently meant to only last a scene, are \u201cRewind the clock\u201d and \u201cSpeed the clock\u201d also meant to only last the scene? That is, will damage return/be undone after the scene is over (barring any other Seeming benefits made by a group)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Duration says &quot;One chapter,&quot; but also I don't think anything particularly breaks for Speed/Rewind to be persistent effects, given that Changeling Hours is a Royal Contract and they're literally just affecting a limited amount of Structure damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T12:29:41-07:00","id":1393821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1393798#post1393798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Duration says &quot;One chapter,&quot; but also I don't think anything particularly breaks for Speed/Rewind to be persistent effects, given that Changeling Hours is a Royal Contract and they're literally just affecting a limited amount of Structure damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad read, though it feels a bit cheap to be able to just fix things for free/a discount (like a house or a car) if you know the name of the previous owner. I have a Wizened Changeling who has an initial character thrust of fixing up a classic Volkswagen beetle his grandparents had promised him, only for him to discover upon escaping Arcadia his Fetch had gotten the car and wrecked it, leaving it in the scrapyard for his Changeling self to find (though not intentionally of course). The Changeling manages to (barely) drive it out through Dance Of The Toys and Blessing Of Perfection, at least for my intended backstory; it feels kind of token if I could have him just take Changeling Hours, fix it up while chanting his grandparents\u2019 names and then literally drive it out like it\u2019s fresh off the production line.<br /> <br /> Granted, players are more likely to enjoy having smaller items fixed easily without having to go to the trouble of getting a replacement or specialty tools, rather than for the missed RP and story benefits of having to do the actions themselves to make something lasting. I suppose it\u2019s something that could work differently on individual tables, with different Seemings allowing for permanence to fill in for working in perpetuity rather than just a single scene.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the swift reply Satchel!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:38:15-07:00","id":1393845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1393821#post1393821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a bad read, though it feels a bit cheap to be able to just fix things for free/a discount (like a house or a car) if you know the name of the previous owner.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one to five points of Structure damage, rising as high as ten points if you're an extremely good and extremely magical craftsman, carried out at a rate of one point per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it feels kind of token if I could have him just take Changeling Hours, fix it up while chanting his grandparents\u2019 names and then literally drive it out like it\u2019s fresh off the production line. </div> </div> </div>The reading I have where these are lasting effects is also the reading where your Crafts rating is the limit of the Contract's ability to alter the object's Structure; a temporary effect would see the two clauses essentially reverse themselves at the end of the chapter.<br /> <br /> The same investment of resources in Royal Jewels lets you jury-rig a rocket launcher out of vaguely appropriate materials for free as long as you're wearing old glasses and using old tools. I'm not too worried about Powerful Faerie Magic making it trivial to fix completely mundane damage to precious family heirlooms; you have to learn that Contract <i>somehow</i>, and that knowledge affects the story by where you got it and who knows you have it, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-03-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:27:49-07:00","id":1394215,"title":"","content":"On a metaphysical level, what is the hedge? I'm not expecting an answer that's solid, just &quot;well, from what we know/how we understand it&quot;.<br /> <br /> All I can get is that is the imagination and wonder of humanity, which I assume due to how some Bridge Burners want to rid humanity of the True Fae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:58:39-07:00","id":1394221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394215#post1394215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a metaphysical level, what is the hedge? I'm not expecting an answer that's solid, just &quot;well, from what we know/how we understand it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A manifestation of the Gentry's greedy vow to possess the world entire, interposed between their homes in Arcadia and the rest of the world (having subsumed a few other places like the Dreaming Roads and the Hall of Mirrors along the way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T21:30:38-07:00","id":1394232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394221#post1394221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A manifestation of the Gentry's greedy vow to possess the world entire, interposed between their homes in Arcadia and the rest of the world (having subsumed a few other places like the Dreaming Roads and the Hall of Mirrors along the way).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so I completely messed up with my interpretation. And the Hall of Mirrors, the same from VASCU?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:54:44-07:00","id":1394251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394215#post1394215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a metaphysical level, what is the hedge? I'm not expecting an answer that's solid, just &amp;quot;well, from what we know/how we understand it&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> All I can get is that is the imagination and wonder of humanity, which I assume due to how some Bridge Burners want to rid humanity of the True Fae</div> </div> </div> </div>If i remember right,<br /> Dave Brookshaw once said that in his head (not canon) the hedge was the barrier between the human mind and the soul.<br /> Mages pass it spending mana during meditation and don t notice the world between in the same way as werewolf skips the world inside the gauntlet.<br /> So in some way it could be defined as the barrier between individualism and the shared soul of everything, this would also nicely explain the mindset of the fae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:34:51-07:00","id":1394320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394232#post1394232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Hall of Mirrors, the same from VASCU?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, considering it's the &quot;mirror space&quot; that Contracts like Glimpse of a Distant Mirror, Stealing the Solid Reflection, and Mirror Walk truck with. The Halls of Mirrors are mazes where mirror-people live and watch the real world play out rather than a chamber where the probable future can be observed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394251#post1394251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave Brookshaw once said that in his head (not canon) the hedge was the barrier between the human mind and the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1282958-2e-changeling-and-mage-arcadia?p=1283118#post1283118\">Since canonized, albeit we haven't seen it yet</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T11:29:49-07:00","id":1394400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394320#post1394320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, considering it's the &amp;quot;mirror space&amp;quot; that Contracts like Glimpse of a Distant Mirror, Stealing the Solid Reflection, and Mirror Walk truck with. The Halls of Mirrors are mazes where mirror-people live and watch the real world play out rather than a chamber where the probable future can be observed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1282958-2e-changeling-and-mage-arcadia?p=1283118#post1283118&amp;quot;]Since</a> canonized, albeit we haven't seen it yet[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, good to know.<br /> The unpublished book mentioned could be player guide to contagion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:12:41-07:00","id":1394415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394400#post1394400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, good to know.<br /> The unpublished book mentioned could be player guide to contagion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it may actually be the supplement called &quot;The Hedge&quot;. Though, it will a long time for that. And thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> for clarifying the hall of mirrors, I forgot about that section.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry if I already asked this everyone, but what's the reasoning for Ogres favoring the Contract of Shield? I have no issue with it, but it confuses me considering how Ogres make their way out of Arcadia by brutal violence (as far as I understand, the Seemings, and kiths, are decided just as much by how they lived in/escaped Arcadia as it is by the Gentry themselves)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:15:50-07:00","id":1394416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394415#post1394415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sorry if I already asked this everyone, but what's the reasoning for Ogres favoring the Contract of Shield? I have no issue with it, but it confuses me considering how Ogres make their way out of Arcadia by brutal violence (as far as I understand, the Seemings, and kiths, are decided just as much by how they lived in/escaped Arcadia as it is by the Gentry themselves)</div> </div> </div> </div>As a whole, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1311862-honest-question-not-a-complaint?p=1311875#post1311875\">the seeming is more pitiless enforcers and stalwart guardians than engines of destruction and ruinous force</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:32:18-07:00","id":1394421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394415#post1394415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it may actually be the supplement called &quot;The Hedge&quot;. Though, it will a long time for that. And thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> for clarifying the hall of mirrors, I forgot about that section.</div> </div> </div> </div>More likely is the proposed Fallen Worlds supplement. Unfortunately I can't find it on the projects page or in the Monday notes so it might not be worked on anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394415#post1394415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sorry if I already asked this everyone, but what's the reasoning for Ogres favoring the Contract of Shield? I have no issue with it, but it confuses me considering how Ogres make their way out of Arcadia by brutal violence (as far as I understand, the Seemings, and kiths, are decided just as much by how they lived in/escaped Arcadia as it is by the Gentry themselves)</div> </div> </div> </div>Focus less on the strength required to break free through violence, and more on the sturdiness and toughness required for a violent escape without falling to violence yourself. Being able to beat one of the gate guards to a pulp doesn't help if another guard beats you to a pulp in response. The Ogre Seeming is more of a &quot;tough guy&quot; archetype than a straight &quot;fighter&quot; archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T14:48:00-07:00","id":1394439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1394416#post1394416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a whole, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1311862-honest-question-not-a-complaint?p=1311875#post1311875&amp;quot;]the</a> seeming is more pitiless enforcers and stalwart guardians than engines of destruction and ruinous force[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I thought I asked it before, couldn't find it though. And thank you too <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>. I do hope Fallen Worlds isnt completely cancelled","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T01:02:11-07:00","id":1395034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1282958-2e-changeling-and-mage-arcadia?p=1283118#post1283118\">Since canonized, albeit we haven't seen it yet</a>. </div> </div> </div>In fact, I canonized it in Dark Eras 2, in the Mage/Changeling crossover Wild West era! But yes, Fallen Worlds is where that sort of thing will be expanded upon, if we get the green light from White Wolf to do that one after Tome of the Pentacle. (Neither I nor Onyx Path has any control over that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:01:46-07:00","id":1395056,"title":"","content":"Also, it was Meghan's idea to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 06-08-2020, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T10:06:39-07:00","id":1395098,"title":"","content":"I dont know how to properly term this, but what would be the umbrella Seeming effects have for contracts?<br /> <br /> Like for Ogres, the effects they add to contracts are very direct defensively (trapdoor spider's trick, chrysalis) and offensively (Vow of no Compromise, Fortifying Presence)<br /> <br /> I guess what I mean is, what should I be looking for when making a seeming effect for contracts? I also tend to struggle with Elementals as I can only think in terms of stuff like &quot;the Hedgewall takes on properties of the Sprite's element&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T11:57:38-07:00","id":1395123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395098#post1395098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know how to properly term this, but what would be the umbrella Seeming effects have for contracts?<br /> <br /> Like for Ogres, the effects they add to contracts are very direct defensively (trapdoor spider's trick, chrysalis) and offensively (Vow of no Compromise, Fortifying Presence)<br /> <br /> I guess what I mean is, what should I be looking for when making a seeming effect for contracts? I also tend to struggle with Elementals as I can only think in terms of stuff like &quot;the Hedgewall takes on properties of the Sprite's element&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been systematically going through all the contracts on-and-off and adding in Seeming benefits for those that don't have them yet (because it's fun to do and my players never mind it either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and I know your struggle! It's very, very easy to get in the trap of &quot;Well, beast should do something with animals... I guess?&quot; or &quot;Well, elemental should do something with some element...&quot; but after a certain point those very specific ideas are too confining and we need to open it up a bit.<br /> When looking at the official Seeming bonuses, you'll see that no matter what &quot;umbrella&quot; you come up for any particular Seeming, one Contract or the other will assign a Seeming benefit that you would give to Seeming X under a rigid adherence to theme to Seeming Y instead. This tells me that there is a lot of leeway in assigning these bonuses, and a perfect fit is impossible to achieve.<br /> <br /> There's also various Contracts that have similar uses with some pros/cons, so when you start giving Seeming bonuses to all of those it's really hard to not homogenize them, but that's another story. ^^<br /> <br /> Some suggested themes for each Seeming:<br /> <br /> - <b>Beasts: </b>Instinct, pack dynamics in a broad sense (benefiting members of your &quot;pack&quot;, or bonuses related to taking out/challenging the &quot;alpha dog&quot; of a group), senses, tracking, animals (both actual animals as traits and behaviours linked to animals), mobility, the Hedge. Tenacity (in a &quot;won't let go once I got the scent&quot;, sort of fashion.)<br /> <br /> - <b>Darklings: </b>Shadows, misdirection, fear, etherealness, visions, mysticism, the sinister, knowledge (&quot;secrets&quot;). Corrossion, rot, etc... Sinister things.<br /> <br /> - <b>Elementals: </b>Malleable, fluid, elemental. Objects and scenery want to help, even the air will help carry sounds you wish to hear to your ears, sort of stuff. <i>Powerful:</i> if I want a Seeming to just be able to pump more juice into a Contract and get a more explosive result than anyone else, Elemental is going to be a strong contended for where that bonus should go. Unrelenting, unstoppable, energetic. Plants. Timeless. Seldom subtle, but lots of bang means lots of buck.<br /> <br /> - <b>Fairest: </b>Beauty, charisma, inspiring. Emotions, particularly positive ones, but it's seldom hard to justify a Fairest bonus for a wide range of emotions. Command, you decree, he/she/it/the world obeys. Sentimentality. Shoe-in for many bonuses that help dominate social situations.<br /> <br /> - <b>Ogres: </b>Toughness. Protection. Taking one for the team. Brutality. Intimidation (shared with Beast, though it manifests a bit differently. Also different from the &quot;fear&quot; of Darklings). Mental health. Healing. Strength. Straightforward: sometimes it just <i>is </i>that simple, even if a non-Ogre has to try and make it all complicated. Brute force. Bodyguard. Largesse and largeness.<br /> <br /> - <b>Wizened: </b>Creativity, ingenuity, cunning. Knowledge, of all sorts. Surprisingly (to some people) manipulative, and much more active on a social level than you'd think, often a power-behind-the-throne type, chessmastering from behind the curtains while others are seen as the &quot;face&quot;. Changing one thing into another, which can be literal &quot;things&quot; (objects) or much more vague concepts. A special connection to the things they made themselves. Complexity. Analysis.<br /> <br /> Some Contracts are harder than others for this or that Seeming, but I find Beast the overall hardest, and you really need to let go of &quot;animal&quot; as the core idea often to make it work, which is good! Elementals can be tough on some Contracts (especially if you hold too tightly to the &quot;elements&quot; idea), but write themselves on others. Ogres can sometimes be tough if already written examples (often for Beasts) muscle (hehe) into their territory a lot, but often not too bad. Darklings, Fairest and Wizened tend to go quite smoothly.<br /> <br /> I find that once you add more bonuses, you'll at some point need to add a little bit of clarification of how different bonuses work together, too. I see it as good practice to ensure that a member of a certain Seeming might be very interested in learning 2-3 of the other bonuses due to synergy with the bonus they already have. If members of all Seemings would love to get their hands on almost all of the Seeming bonuses other Seemings get for a certain Contract, then you've generally got a winner. ;D<br /> It's often not possible though, so just making sure at least some of them synergise is a good start. ^^<br /> <br /> I shared what I had for Crown a bit less than ten months ago, but I've devoted a lot of time to other gamelines so haven't been able to finish it since then (though I have Jewels and Mirror too now, but I have to go over them again sometime to see how ready-for-critique they are). Here's the thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1331269-homebrew-contract-seeming-bonuses\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...eeming-bonuses</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-08-2020, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T12:35:13-07:00","id":1395129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395123#post1395123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue a