","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T23:07:25-07:00","id":1395768,"title":"","content":"Core books says that making a bargain with another splat not of the wyrd can have strange side effects.<br /> What effect could have a bargain with, for example, a geist?<br /> The ability to see and speak with ghosts would be too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T03:28:33-07:00","id":1395801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395768#post1395768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core books says that making a bargain with another splat not of the wyrd can have strange side effects.<br /> What effect could have a bargain with, for example, a geist?<br /> The ability to see and speak with ghosts would be too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would be too much, but in that case I would also have ghosts take special notice of the Changeling. Which could be quite problematic as I don't think Changelings have <i>that</i> many ways to really deal with/interact with ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T06:59:24-07:00","id":1395833,"title":"","content":"This might have been asked before, but what would be a good benchmark for number of contracts a changeling would need to know in order to be considered a decent sorcerer? What about a powerful sorcerer? I know, I know, some contracts are more powerful than others and simply knowing some of the stronger ones would get the changeling a reputation for knowing powerful magic, but still, number of contracts known still has to count for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T07:42:39-07:00","id":1395841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395833#post1395833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been asked before, but what would be a good benchmark for number of contracts a changeling would need to know in order to be considered a decent sorcerer? What about a powerful sorcerer? I know, I know, some contracts are more powerful than others and simply knowing some of the stronger ones would get the changeling a reputation for knowing powerful magic, but still, number of contracts known still has to count for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the cost of a contract in experience is similar to a level of discipline/arcana ecc,<br /> And that if you reach a level 5 with those powers you are considered a &quot;master&quot;,<br /> I would say that once you have 7 common or 5 royal ( or any similar combo) in one regalia you would be considered a master of it, but it is surely an imperfect way to handle the matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:07:40-07:00","id":1395879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395833#post1395833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been asked before, but what would be a good benchmark for number of contracts a changeling would need to know in order to be considered a decent sorcerer? What about a powerful sorcerer? I know, I know, some contracts are more powerful than others and simply knowing some of the stronger ones would get the changeling a reputation for knowing powerful magic, but still, number of contracts known still has to count for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure that a Sorcerer in Changeling terms is more someone who knows of magic outside of contracts, or at least contracts outside of the main regalia, since sorcerers in general are only referenced to in terms of the Autumn court from what I can see and Autumn takes the mind to investigate outside supernaturals. At the very least, I haven\u2019t seen the term used in a more general context, which you would expect for the Gentry given they master entire regalia through their Titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:18:50-07:00","id":1395885,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> Yes, it's true that the term has been used that way, but really it shouldn't be. The problem with it is that normal humans that do the same thing are called occultists. If the reason you're called a sorcerer is because you know a lot about the supernatural then you need to get your title fixed. If you're called a sorcerer because you can DO magic, well then, now your title makes sense, especially if you can do lots of it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, your reply is ignoring the main thrust of my question: how many contracts must a changeling know before they are considered magically powerful and wise in the ways of Fae magic? Neos has his take of 7 common or 5 royal, but that's only concerning a single regalia. How many regalia must a changeling &quot;master&quot; by that definition to be considered magically gifted/strong/informed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:32:32-07:00","id":1395886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395833#post1395833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been asked before, but what would be a good benchmark for number of contracts a changeling would need to know in order to be considered a decent sorcerer? What about a powerful sorcerer? I know, I know, some contracts are more powerful than others and simply knowing some of the stronger ones would get the changeling a reputation for knowing powerful magic, but still, number of contracts known still has to count for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an Entitlement in first edition, the Office of Vizierial Council, that requires a member to know at least 12 dots' worth of Contracts, so that might be a decent starting point. I think &quot;sorcerors&quot; in a Changeling context would also be those Lost who are particularly skilled at Hedgespinning, Dreamweaving, and/or Tokencrafting as well (and probably have some Bargains with various other supernatural entities on the side).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:58:03-07:00","id":1395891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395886#post1395886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think &quot;sorcerors&quot; in a Changeling context would also be those Lost who are particularly skilled at Hedgespinning, Dreamweaving, and/or Tokencrafting as well (and probably have some Bargains with various other supernatural entities on the side).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with that! There might not be any hard rules for it, but nothing prevents you from letting Changelings make powerful deals with powerful entities, or letting them gain sorcerous knowledge they can put to use with rituals using the Occult skill.<br /> <br /> In one of my games, the local Freehold had a rule about nobody opening Hedge gates anywhere inside of this small domain they operated from, but had one permanent Hedge-gate at the centre of a maze, which befuddled and slowed down anyone with hostile intentions.<br /> How? I don't know, Autumn Court were the ones who arranged all of that, and I never saw the need to explain it beyond &quot;sorcery&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T02:45:58-07:00","id":1395982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1395885#post1395885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> Yes, it's true that the term has been used that way, but really it shouldn't be. The problem with it is that normal humans that do the same thing are called occultists. If the reason you're called a sorcerer is because you know a lot about the supernatural then you need to get your title fixed. If you're called a sorcerer because you can DO magic, well then, now your title makes sense, especially if you can do lots of it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, your reply is ignoring the main thrust of my question: how many contracts must a changeling know before they are considered magically powerful and wise in the ways of Fae magic? Neos has his take of 7 common or 5 royal, but that's only concerning a single regalia. How many regalia must a changeling &quot;master&quot; by that definition to be considered magically gifted/strong/informed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your question was how many contracts a Changeling needed to be a \u201cdecent sorcerer\u201d. That is not the same as being magically powerful and wise in the way of Fae magic - sorcerers would require a good grasp on it, yes, but the point of the Autumn court sorcerers is that they are knowledgeable <i>outside</i> of contracts, of things like abjuration, making an environment more habitable for a spirit or ghost to manifest or to banish them. The difference between a mere human occultist and a Changeling sorcerer is that a human is for the most part in the dark on what a supernatural being is actually like, stuck with a human perspective and resources. Changelings innately have an advantage because they not only know of the supernatural pretty intimately, but they have the means and tools to disconcert truth from fiction. Clarity and Kenning both grant large advantages on their own for ferreting out details about the supernatural, hob goblins often have loads of things that a Changeling would want including tomes of lore from other beings and their Kiths can easily grant them advantages in themselves (Helldivers by themselves can access different realms and speak to spirits/ghosts through their Trickery). Autumn in general has this lovely habit of documenting things so that others in their court (and those with Goodwill) can research it and become knowledgeable in these things, hence why Autumn courtiers tend to be the sorcerers. Both occultists and sorcerers dabble in the occult beyond their natural reality, but the difference is that Changeling sorcerers have the context to actually <i>know</i> what they\u2019re looking into - if your definition of Sorcerer is simply \u201ccan do magic\u201d, you\u2019re including pretty much an entire freehold and thus losing distinction.<br /> <br /> And even if you\u2019re looking to ignore all of that, contracts are still a bad benchmark to go off of. Being wise to the ways of fae magic doesn\u2019t result in having lots of contracts, nor does having lots of contracts mean you\u2019re wise to the fae - it just means you\u2019ve spent lots of experiences and have made a bunch of deals with the entities that empower your contracts just as others are. Being wise to the ways of the fae means that you\u2019re knowledgeable about how the Hedge functions, about Arcadia and the nature of Gentry Titles and Names, about Bastions, dreams and Goblin debt. Contracts help, but how many someone has doesn\u2019t denote their experience and wisdom. You could have an expert in searching the Hedge who never went past having the initial six contracts you start out with simply because those six contracts are <i>exactly</i> what they needed to become an expert in that field. Having tons of contracts may make you powerful (depending on the selection), but wise/knowledgeable?<br /> <br /> To put it simpler, you\u2019re asking about how many cars someone needs to own to be wise and knowledgeable about automobiles, which ignores what experience they\u2019ve had, how long that experience is in and what they specialize in. Having different cars helps in that, but you could have had the same beat up truck for most of your life and still be a better master at maintaining vehicles than some rich yahoo with a dozen sports cars because you\u2019ve worked in several different garages with a half dozen tutors and hours upon hours of experience under the hood.<br /> <br /> What you\u2019re looking for is what contracts would serve to exemplify what the Changeling is wise and powerful in. As has been noted, Changelings have rather a lot in their world to know and learn about and become wise in, and no matter how much time and what durance they\u2019ve had they\u2019re going to have to specialize in what they know. The number of contracts merely denotes how much experience they\u2019ve devoted to the deals that make them able to do various things that relate to that wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 06-12-2020, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T13:45:40-07:00","id":1396066,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the double-post, but the Wizened Blessing has me confused. It notes that if you\u2019re using the proper tools to turn one object into another \u201c This counts as a five-die bonus for purposes of determining the required successes.\u201d Does this mean that the player gets +5 to the roll for making the transmutation, or that they take a -5 penalty to it... or that they simply have to get 5 more successes to succeed on the build action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T13:56:19-07:00","id":1396069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1396066#post1396066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the double-post, but the Wizened Blessing has me confused. It notes that if you\u2019re using the proper tools to turn one object into another \u201c This counts as a five-die bonus for purposes of determining the required successes.\u201d Does this mean that the player gets +5 to the roll for making the transmutation, or that they take a -5 penalty to it... or that they simply have to get 5 more successes to succeed on the build action?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they messed that up a little, since the Build Equipment rules just use an Instant Action lasting up to a few hours, not extended rolls, so you don't need multiple successes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I believe this is what they're referring to:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Built-In Penalty: <b>The roll always suffers a penalty<br /> equal to the intended equipment bonus.</b> Each other<br /> intended benefit, like a new function, an increased<br /> trait, or access to a resource, counts as a one-die bonus<br /> for this purpose, as well as to determine whether<br /> to roll in the first place. Weapons impose a penalty<br /> equal to their weapon modifier; armor imposes a<br /> penalty equal to its highest armor rating (general<br /> or ballistic). Penalties can\u2019t exceed \u22125. </div> </div> </div>So using the Blessing counts as trying to make a piece of equipment with a five-dice bonus (which doesn't mean the end product gives an actual five-dice bonus, it's just a unit of budgeting in the Build Equipment rules) and therefore you take a -5 penalty to your Build Equipment roll. On a simple success you transmute the material. Actually even on a failure you still do, but it'll be Fragile or Volatile.<br /> <br /> Note that with the blessing you can only turn one material into another material (straw into gold) not one object into another object (fridge into microwave). Just pointing it out due to your phrasing. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T14:38:39-07:00","id":1396074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1396069#post1396069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they messed that up a little, since the Build Equipment rules just use an Instant Action lasting up to a few hours, not extended rolls, so you don't need multiple successes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I believe this is what they're referring to:<br /> <br /> <br /> So using the Blessing counts as trying to make a piece of equipment with a five-dice bonus (which doesn't mean the end product gives an actual five-dice bonus, it's just a unit of budgeting in the Build Equipment rules) and therefore you take a -5 penalty to your Build Equipment roll. On a simple success you transmute the material. Actually even on a failure you still do, but it'll be Fragile or Volatile.<br /> <br /> Note that with the blessing you can only turn one material into another material (straw into gold) not one object into another object (fridge into microwave). Just pointing it out due to your phrasing. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Between my posting that and your reply, someone did note to me that the Taking Your Time option actually lines up with the write-up for the Wizened a bit more neatly than I had initially read, where the end result simply takes 5 more successes to get to. It\u2019s more trying to do it quickly via instant action that would have the penalty (though oi vey it\u2019s a bit confusing trying to apply it there). Still, thank you for the swift reply to take out the confusion, it\u2019s appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T12:47:40-07:00","id":1396202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1396074#post1396074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between my posting that and your reply, someone did note to me that the Taking Your Time option actually lines up with the write-up for the Wizened a bit more neatly than I had initially read, where the end result simply takes 5 more successes to get to. It\u2019s more trying to do it quickly via instant action that would have the penalty (though oi vey it\u2019s a bit confusing trying to apply it there). Still, thank you for the swift reply to take out the confusion, it\u2019s appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, I forgot about Taking Your Time. ^^<br /> So basically the Blessing should say &quot;This counts as building Equipment with a five-dice bonus.&quot; That way it works with both normal Build Equipment rules, as well as Taking Your Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T14:31:49-07:00","id":1396214,"title":"","content":"Two potentially not-so-simple questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What happens to a Huntsman if the mortal guarding its heart dies? Does the verderer die as well? Is it banished back to Arcadia? Is it now suddenly a free (albeit heartless) agent?<br /> <br /> 2. Can the Hedge ghost of a former changeling still swear oaths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:40:53-07:00","id":1396242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1396214#post1396214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two potentially not-so-simple questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What happens to a Huntsman if the mortal guarding its heart dies? Does the verderer die as well? Is it banished back to Arcadia? Is it now suddenly a free (albeit heartless) agent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gooooood question. Or, like, you know... what happens every morning when the mortal wakes? :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Bastion only exists for the span of a single dream.<br /> When the dreamer wakes, whether naturally or because a<br /> paradigm shift jarred them awake, the Bastion crumbles<br /> and disappears, its territory relinquished back to the surrounding<br /> dreamscape. </div> </div> </div>I have no answer to this, and would also like to know. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can the Hedge ghost of a former changeling still swear oaths? </div> </div> </div>No, hedge ghosts all have the same abilities, regardless of whether they're based off of a dead human or dead Changeling, and swearing Oaths is not part of their skillset.<br /> As an aside, if Hedge Ghosts really function similarly to ghosts then they might not really <i>be</i> to the individual that spawned them, like we would normally assume. One weird thing about CoFD ghosts is that it's actually possible that a ghost of you is created while you're still alive (I think it's in Mage where some examples of this are found?), so whatever they are they're more an imprint of you caused by specific events that leave echoes in the fabric of the world (<i>usually</i> this event is your death), and not really you-after-death.<br /> But that's deep in the itty-bitty-gritty details of the lore, which I usually tend to ignore whenever it suits me, so others here are probably WAY better informed about this than I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:26:31-07:00","id":1396279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1396242#post1396242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gooooood question. Or, like, you know... what happens every morning when the mortal wakes? :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no answer to this, and would also like to know. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I had assumed that while awake, the heart lies in like the mortal's subconscious (which could maybe be represented by a Persistent Condition or even a Supernatural Merit), but I suppose that's certainly a mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, hedge ghosts all have the same abilities, regardless of whether they're based off of a dead human or dead Changeling, and swearing Oaths is not part of their skillset.<br /> As an aside, if Hedge Ghosts really function similarly to ghosts then they might not really <i>be</i> to the individual that spawned them, like we would normally assume. One weird thing about CoFD ghosts is that it's actually possible that a ghost of you is created while you're still alive (I think it's in Mage where some examples of this are found?), so whatever they are they're more an imprint of you caused by specific events that leave echoes in the fabric of the world (<i>usually</i> this event is your death), and not really you-after-death.<br /> But that's deep in the itty-bitty-gritty details of the lore, which I usually tend to ignore whenever it suits me, so others here are probably WAY better informed about this than I am. </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I figured Hedge ghosts weren't the same as Avernian ghosts, but Mage does give us ghosts that already break established rules, and I thought it might make for some interesting stories if an oath could theoretically carry on beyond death in the right circumstances. The create-ghosts-from-living-trauma phenom is in Geist (and is one of my personal favorite additions to 2e).<br /> <br /> Hedge ghosts are pretty interesting for encompassing pretty much all other kinds of ephemeral entity, but while at the same time not actually being ephemeral entities. Hopefully they'll get further examination in <i>Kith &amp; Kin</i>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:29:27-07:00","id":1396281,"title":"","content":"Just have a couple questions about a contract <br /> For chrysalis do you also gain the skills with the animals, and the attacks, and special skills?<br /> Like in dark eras 2 the crocodile has the special abilities of river predator and terrible jaws, so I\u2019m wondering if a changeling would get that too, along with its skills and attack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25619-chronicle","name":"Chronicle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T15:20:03-07:00","id":1396502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1396279#post1396279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it might make for some interesting stories if an oath could theoretically carry on beyond death in the right circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, why not? If Wyrd thinks it should, Wyrd certainly could. ^^ I don't think Hedge Ghosts being unable to form new Oaths on their own necessarily prevents this scenario for an existing Oath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hedge ghosts are pretty interesting for encompassing pretty much all other kinds of ephemeral entity, but while at the same time not actually being ephemeral entities. Hopefully they'll get further examination in <i>Kith &amp; Kin</i>? </div> </div> </div>They are indeed pretty neat. ^^ You can give them the demanifestation power to make them more like &quot;regular&quot; ephemeral entities, but they do stay pretty different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:45:01-07:00","id":1396882,"title":"","content":"If i understand it rightly, there are two type of situation in which a changeling drops his mask:<br /> -automatic, in the hedge and dreams<br /> No bonus, fae get the changeling wyrd as a tracking bonus<br /> -voluntary, in the material world.<br /> Bonus on successes in contracts, but fae automatically track the changeling<br /> Is it correct?<br /> How does the obliged condition interact with the two different situations?<br /> And can a true fae drop her masl in, the material world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T07:42:12-07:00","id":1397506,"title":"","content":"Being that there seems to be no penalty for harvesting Glamour besides a rushed harvest, isn't it in effect possible for players to have unlimited glamour at all times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5284-sanaelar","name":"Sanaelar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5284_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:53:07-07:00","id":1397716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanaelar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1397506#post1397506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being that there seems to be no penalty for harvesting Glamour besides a rushed harvest, isn't it in effect possible for players to have unlimited glamour at all times?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rushed harvest and shallow/common emotion accounts for a lot, but also non-fae are not always going to be close at hand and harvesting often is going to have specific consequences for higher-Wyrd changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:20:53-07:00","id":1397725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1397716#post1397716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rushed harvest and shallow/common emotion accounts for a lot, but also non-fae are not always going to be close at hand and harvesting often is going to have specific consequences for higher-Wyrd changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to this, there's just the opportunity cost of time and effort. Gotta look up a concert to attend or a sad movie to watch and then actually go and be there for it. This is a small cost but it does mean you're topping your Glamour back up during downtime and it's not so convenient under time pressure.<br /> <br /> But yes, Glamour is one of the more easy-come-easy-go supernatural fuels. Changelings can be well stocked without having to hurt people or exert themselves too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T02:09:25-07:00","id":1398142,"title":"","content":"Dark eras 2, in the Arthurian setting, mentions &quot;natural occouring hedgeways&quot; located in forests.<br /> But for me it s hard to imagine the form of a natural closeable portals in a forest, can you think about some examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T02:46:21-07:00","id":1398144,"title":"","content":"Ditch them having to be closeable. The corebook technically doesn't say Hedgeways have to be closable; just that those created by changelings have to be. If they're naturally occurring, have them be whatever. Two trees with connecting branches that opens up when you walk around them three times, or a circle of mushrooms that you sink into if you lie horisontal in the middle and sing a song of passings. (Of course, changelings can still just will them open.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T04:06:01-07:00","id":1398155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398144#post1398144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ditch them having to be closeable. The corebook technically doesn't say Hedgeways have to be closable; just that those created by changelings have to be. If they're naturally occurring, have them be whatever. Two trees with connecting branches that opens up when you walk around them three times, or a circle of mushrooms that you sink into if you lie horisontal in the middle and sing a song of passings. (Of course, changelings can still just will them open.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the example on pag 311, the fae touched who reached the hedge passing under an oak branch arc, this actually make a lot of sense, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:27:36-07:00","id":1398205,"title":"","content":"Changeling has a lot of subsystems and minor rules for both the GM and his players to remember. do any of you know a good reference sheet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T02:06:53-07:00","id":1398311,"title":"","content":"Does frailty (and cold iron) bypass entirely even mundane (non magical) types of armor?<br /> I mean, it would seem a bit strange if a changeling transmits his vulnerability to the item he wears","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T02:15:38-07:00","id":1398312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398311#post1398311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does frailty (and cold iron) bypass entirely even mundane (non magical) types of armor?<br /> I mean, it would seem a bit strange if a changeling transmits his vulnerability to the item he wears</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any indication in the rules that it would, and can't think of any reason why it should either. So guess not. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T03:02:02-07:00","id":1398316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398312#post1398312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see any indication in the rules that it would, and can't think of any reason why it should either. So guess not. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Banes cut in-stantly through all forms of armor and protective magics&quot;<br /> This quote confuses me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T05:56:00-07:00","id":1398340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398311#post1398311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does frailty (and cold iron) bypass entirely even mundane (non magical) types of armor?<br /> I mean, it would seem a bit strange if a changeling transmits his vulnerability to the item he wears</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a ludonarrative thing.<br /> <br /> While a changeling is wearing a piece of armor, they're an armored changeling, not a changeling and a piece of armor that happens to be on them; the armor isn't having the changeling's vulnerability transmitted to it, the armor is refusing to protect the changeling from iron et al because something about the nature of reality as it relates to changelings (be it the mythic broken vow or some other explanation) allows that thing to harm the changeling per whatever esoteric law of the Wyrd gave them that frailty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T06:20:49-07:00","id":1398342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398340#post1398340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a ludonarrative thing.<br /> <br /> While a changeling is wearing a piece of armor, they're an armored changeling, not a changeling and a piece of armor that happens to be on them; the armor isn't having the changeling's vulnerability transmitted to it, the armor is refusing to protect the changeling from iron et al because something about the nature of reality as it relates to changelings (be it the mythic broken vow or some other explanation) allows that thing to harm the changeling per whatever esoteric law of the Wyrd gave them that frailty.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it works that way, the armor is simply pierced?<br /> Or the bane pass throug it as if it was insubstantial?<br /> And does clothes offer protection from the burning touch of those banes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T06:47:21-07:00","id":1398347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398342#post1398342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it works that way, the armor is simply pierced?<br /> Or the bane pass throug it as if it was insubstantial?</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction is sufficiently small-scale granular that I'm pretty comfortable saying &quot;whatever works for your game/that particular character.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And does clothes offer protection from the burning touch of those banes? </div> </div> </div>It would be very weird for that to be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T08:07:38-07:00","id":1398362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398347#post1398347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction is sufficiently small-scale granular that I'm pretty comfortable saying &amp;quot;whatever works for your game/that particular character.&amp;quot;<br /> It would be very weird for that to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It s important for me, cause i must decide if changeling can safely handle banes with protective gloves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T12:09:10-07:00","id":1398400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398362#post1398362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It s important for me, cause i must decide if changeling can safely handle banes with protective gloves</div> </div> </div> </div>Then that's extra weird, because if regular armor and protective magic don't work then I don't see how other protective equipment would fare any better.<br /> <br /> You have rolls penalized by the <i>presence</i> of a bane, and the universal frailty is generally put forth as a repellant. Picking up wolfsbane with tongs is one thing, but a method of avoiding contact that's visually identical to grasping it barehanded doesn't play to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T13:19:21-07:00","id":1398420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398400#post1398400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then that's extra weird, because if regular armor and protective magic don't work then I don't see how other protective equipment would fare any better.<br /> <br /> You have rolls penalized by the <i>presence</i> of a bane, and the universal frailty is generally put forth as a repellant. Picking up wolfsbane with tongs is one thing, but a method of avoiding contact that's visually identical to grasping it barehanded doesn't play to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok but protection from damage and protection are two different things.<br /> I am careful on this matter, because if leather gloves doesn t protect from cold iron handling then a changeling could not hold an iron sword, the hilt of the blade would at the same way offer no protection from the blade s metal.<br /> It seems to me that the book mentions changeling using iron melee weapon, so i m wondering on how much restrictive banes should be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T13:55:40-07:00","id":1398426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398420#post1398420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am careful on this matter, because if leather gloves doesn t protect from cold iron handling then a changeling could not hold an iron sword, the hilt of the blade would at the same way offer no protection from the blade s metal.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The hilt of a cold-iron sword is made of a different metal&quot; reads the same to me as &quot;the haft of a spear whose head is made of cold iron&quot; and thereby hits the same angle as handling the blade with tongs; with gloves you're not handling a thing that's attached to the metal, you're putting hands on the metal with protective gear.<br /> <br /> Also, it's only cold iron that functions as a bane that deals damage from exposure \u2014 just being made of iron only conveys the ability to pierce fae defenses. You don't need extra protection against something that doesn't hurt you by contact alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T00:40:25-07:00","id":1398542,"title":"","content":"Considering that the campaign will be setted in the Arthurian britannia of Dark eras 2 there will be only cold iron, and it would be a major threat, so sorry to everyone if i m trying to figuring out the fine details.<br /> On the same way i also need to know if frailty banes like &quot;church bell sound&quot; could be negated by wearing protective gear, like wax earplugs.<br /> And, most important, if the penalty of acting against your bane apply on every action targeted at an iron armored knight or a paesant holding an iron knife","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:48:23-07:00","id":1398549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398542#post1398542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the same way i also need to know if frailty banes like &quot;church bell sound&quot; could be negated by wearing protective gear, like wax earplugs.<br /> And, most important, if the penalty of acting against your bane apply on every action targeted at an iron armored knight or a paesant holding an iron knife</div> </div> </div> </div>Fae banes make you get away from the problem as quick as you can. Like the when-in-doubt-iron-wins rule of thumb for fae magic, you are going to be better served treating frailties as the hard weaknesses that they are \u2014 changeling banes are levers for your enemies to lean on to put themselves in a position of strength rather than the more manageable drawbacks of e.g. Bound and Forsaken constitutions.<br /> <br /> The splat incentivizes being hard to pin down for a reason. Assume methods of avoiding problems from your frailties default to &quot;don't trip over them in the first place.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:01:18-07:00","id":1398557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1398316#post1398316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Banes cut in-stantly through all forms of armor and protective magics&quot;<br /> This quote confuses me</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always read it as &quot;Banes cut instantly through all forms of armour magics and protective magics.&quot;<br /> I could be wrong in that, though! Just on a language level it is a correct reading, and I've always just assumed they wanted to call out the mechanical effect of gaining armour dots specifically, and then establish that it also applies to anything you might think of as &quot;protective&quot;.<br /> It also neatly and clearly draws a line in the sand, and avoids all the nitpicking about what level of abstraction, gloves VS hilts, etc... is sufficient 'protection'. :P I'd rather not have to make too many individual rulings on what will work when a valid reading exists that makes it all a lot easier. ^^<br /> <br /> I personally don't see a fae with a bane of 'grass pollen' being affected by it while walking through a field wearing a hazmat suit, but YMMV!<br /> <br /> The frailty rules also talk about &quot;exposure&quot; (and &quot;touching&quot; for major ones), while hazmat suits are essentially designed to prevent exposure. It all gets a bit too nitty-gritty for me.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also elements of the frailties that apply to proximity to a bane, and those continue to work even while you're in your little hazmat suit, obviously.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day I'd say both readings are valid, and with the rest of the text not taking a firm stance either way one should just decide what will play best at their particular table in this case. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T03:55:21-07:00","id":1398576,"title":"","content":"Well, both takes on the matter have pros and cons.<br /> I m still a little confused about what counts as acting against a source of bane, but probably the system takes inspiration by legend about putting an iron nail in your pocket to obtain protection from fae.<br /> Thanks for sharing your opinions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T07:09:55-07:00","id":1400305,"title":"","content":"What If a human falls in love with a changeling and promises to him that &quot;i ll follow you anywhere for the rest of my life&quot;, does the Human turns in a fae touched if he follows the changeling into the hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T07:58:31-07:00","id":1400313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1400305#post1400305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What If a human falls in love with a changeling and promises to him that &quot;i ll follow you anywhere for the rest of my life&quot;, does the Human turns in a fae touched if he follows the changeling into the hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Becoming fae-touched is contingent upon a mortal keeping a promise they made with a changeling from before they became a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T23:16:47-07:00","id":1400461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1400313#post1400313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming fae-touched is contingent upon a mortal keeping a promise they made with a changeling from before they became a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably it s true, but i don t understand clearly why the mechanism works that way.<br /> The future changeling has no connection to the wyrd at the time of the promise, why he cannot turn a mortal into an avowed now that he has a strong connection to the wyrd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T05:33:11-07:00","id":1400504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1400461#post1400461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably it s true, but i don t understand clearly why the mechanism works that way.<br /> The future changeling has no connection to the wyrd at the time of the promise, why he cannot turn a mortal into an avowed now that he has a strong connection to the wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the changeling is not the one turning the mortal into a fae-touched and the process involves the fae-touched entering the Hedge <i>to try and reach the changeling in Arcadia</i> through the bond of the promise the Avowed has upheld their end of. That circumstance becomes dramatically harder to replicate once a changeling is out of Faerie and <i>never going back there in my life, are you <u>kidding</u> me?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T03:50:24-07:00","id":1401454,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the extra side effect of a bargain with supernaturals.<br /> I will soon have a motley of 3 players working with a Promethean throng of 2 players, and probably they will strike a group bargain.<br /> Apart from the normal benefits i m considering the idea of adding this not foreseen extras (a smaller version of miasma rules):<br /> -Prometheans doesn t cause disquiet to the motley<br /> -changelings gains extra dice harvesting from the throng s milestones<br /> But the prices for this is:<br /> -all motley s fetches becomes part of the throng, and can start the pilgrimage under the promethean tutelage (with all the added rules from dark eras 2).<br /> True fae and huntsman pursuing the changelings become subjected to a modified version of the fetches extempore disquiet, they mistakes the fetches for the corresponding changelings and tries to capture or kill them instead.<br /> If Prometheans refuses to teach the fethes the bargain is broken from their side, and if the changeling fail to protect their fetches from capture or death they break their part of the pledge.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> Too much for a bargain power?<br /> Do you like the idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 07-07-2020, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T04:24:35-07:00","id":1402781,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, there's nothing that really stops a changeling from having titles from two Entitlements. Is that correct? Are there any conflicts (other than the obvious of having to juggle two separate sets of duties) that I might've overlooked?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T06:07:52-07:00","id":1402792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402781#post1402781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell, there's nothing that really stops a changeling from having titles from two Entitlements. Is that correct? Are there any conflicts (other than the obvious of having to juggle two separate sets of duties) that I might've overlooked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that titles define who you are, having multiple titles seems to me like multiple personality disorder, possible but unhealty.<br /> But yes, i see no mechanical rule against it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:25:41-07:00","id":1402803,"title":"","content":"I hardly think it's that dramatic. A title shapes the changeling but it doesn't redefine their personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T08:07:33-07:00","id":1402811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402803#post1402803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hardly think it's that dramatic. A title shapes the changeling but it doesn't redefine their personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, i did not meant that, but the changeling probably would end up living parallel lifes with different &quot;personas&quot;.<br /> On the long run, this may drive him crazy, developing the disorder as a consequence of clarity loss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T02:27:48-07:00","id":1402924,"title":"","content":"I think an Entitlement isn't just what you do, but what you are. It's like your role in a grand fairytale. And few if any characters in a fairytale ever have two roles. So I wouldn't do it, but YMMV. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:27:54-07:00","id":1402951,"title":"","content":"Lorewise, how do Changelings learn Contracts and Seeming Benefits from within their own favored categories? Do they need to be taught?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:37:58-07:00","id":1402955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402951#post1402951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lorewise, how do Changelings learn Contracts and Seeming Benefits from within their own favored categories? Do they need to be taught?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within their two favored regalia they can learn any contract without a teacher.<br /> They automatically unlock their seeming benefit on any contract they learn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T15:07:27-07:00","id":1402992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402951#post1402951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lorewise, how do Changelings learn Contracts and Seeming Benefits from within their own favored categories? Do they need to be taught?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always a bit vague in any splat, most of the time it seems to boil down to not needing a teacher if it's &quot;favoured&quot;. I'd see it as the Changeling looking into their own nature and communing with aspects of existence to figure out existing Contracts fashioned by the True Fae, and then figuring out how to tap into them. This might involve oneiromancy, travelling the hedge, maybe even meditating for some, but all of that could be done off-screen and the effort is represented by the xp spent I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T15:23:59-07:00","id":1402996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402951#post1402951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lorewise, how do Changelings learn Contracts and Seeming Benefits from within their own favored categories? Do they need to be taught?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Any citizen of Arcadia, including changelings, may claim these rights as Contracts. This claim requires conscious effort, like finding a teacher, reading a tome detailing the Contract, or meditating extensively upon the nature of the deal.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if the Contract is in a favoured Regalia or not. The only difference is that favoured Contracts are easier to learn (represented through cheaper XP costs) but the process can be the same for either.<br /> <br /> Seeming Benefits for your own Seeming are automatically unlocked. You learn them when you learn the Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T23:11:26-07:00","id":1403046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402996#post1402996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Any citizen of Arcadia, including changelings, may claim these rights as Contracts. This claim requires conscious effort, like finding a teacher, reading a tome detailing the Contract, or meditating extensively upon the nature of the deal.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if the Contract is in a favoured Regalia or not. The only difference is that favoured Contracts are easier to learn (represented through cheaper XP costs) but the process can be the same for either.<br /> <br /> Seeming Benefits for your own Seeming are automatically unlocked. You learn them when you learn the Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pag 95 of the core book says &quot;The Lost may learn favored Regalia Contracts and Court Contracts without a teacher. All other Contracts require someone, or something, to teach them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T23:16:45-07:00","id":1403048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1402992#post1402992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's always a bit vague in any splat, most of the time it seems to boil down to not needing a teacher if it's &amp;quot;favoured&amp;quot;. I'd see it as the Changeling looking into their own nature and communing with aspects of existence to figure out existing Contracts fashioned by the True Fae, and then figuring out how to tap into them. This might involve oneiromancy, travelling the hedge, maybe even meditating for some, but all of that could be done off-screen and the effort is represented by the xp spent I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only splats that i can find in which there are no indications are Demon and Beasts, and both adresses the problem in their player guide.<br /> Can you point me the splats where you found vague indications please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T14:11:54-07:00","id":1404087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1403048#post1403048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only splats that i can find in which there are no indications are Demon and Beasts, and both adresses the problem in their player guide.<br /> Can you point me the splats where you found vague indications please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for instance in Vampire:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred<br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences. </div> </div> </div>So it says that &quot;many spontaneously manifest new Disciplines&quot;, but it doesn't say what those others who aren't included in &quot;many&quot; do. Probably they need a teacher? Maybe they just need to practice? That's pretty vague! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And like I said: &quot;most of the time it seems to boil down to not needing a teacher if it's 'favoured'&quot; =&gt; Applies exactly here, as you yourself quoted, so I don't think we're in disagreement? ^^<br /> <br /> Perhaps I shouldn't have said it is &quot;always&quot; a bit vague, but it's clearly a pretty common theme, as it is true for Vampire and apparently, as you have found, Beast and Demon as well. And arguably in Changeling too, since the quote Tessie posted and the one you posted are somewhat at odds with one another, the one seeming to imply that &quot;finding a teacher&quot; is only <i>one </i>of the options and not implying it matters whether it is favoured or not, the other stating that it does matter and making it the only option in such a case. It is at the very least confusing, and I had similar questions in the past about it as a result. ^^<br /> <br /> I don't have knowledge of every other splat, but 4 splats where it's either not mentioned or there's a lack of clarity in the text seems like a pretty high number already. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T14:39:15-07:00","id":1404092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1404087#post1404087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well for instance in Vampire:<br /> <br /> <br /> So it says that &amp;quot;many spontaneously manifest new Disciplines&amp;quot;, but it doesn't say what those others who aren't included in &amp;quot;many&amp;quot; do. Probably they need a teacher? Maybe they just need to practice? That's pretty vague! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And like I said: &amp;quot;most of the time it seems to boil down to not needing a teacher if it's 'favoured'&amp;quot; =&gt; Applies exactly here, as you yourself quoted, so I don't think we're in disagreement? ^^<br /> <br /> Perhaps I shouldn't have said it is &amp;quot;always&amp;quot; a bit vague, but it's clearly a pretty common theme, as it is true for Vampire and apparently, as you have found, Beast and Demon as well. And arguably in Changeling too, since the quote Tessie posted and the one you posted are somewhat at odds with one another, the one seeming to imply that &amp;quot;finding a teacher&amp;quot; is only <i>one </i>of the options and not implying it matters whether it is favoured or not, the other stating that it does matter and making it the only option in such a case. It is at the very least confusing, and I had similar questions in the past about it as a result. ^^<br /> <br /> I don't have knowledge of every other splat, but 4 splats where it's either not mentioned or there's a lack of clarity in the text seems like a pretty high number already. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, lot of core books in the dedicated power section are a little vague yes.<br /> But if you search for the chapters named Experience, you always find the detailed conditions about learning powers.<br /> In Vampire corebook for example you ll find it on pag 83","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T11:56:06-07:00","id":1404270,"title":"","content":"For the Whispers Of Morning contract, are Changelings able to move while in their noncorporeal state? They\u2019re not affected by gravity, but they\u2019re also unable to interact with other things, so I don\u2019t know if they can move from the spot they evoke it in or if they need a Seeming bonus to do so. Just pondering for any Seeming Bonuses I was thinking of making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:04:50-07:00","id":1404273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1404270#post1404270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Whispers Of Morning contract, are Changelings able to move while in their noncorporeal state? They\u2019re not affected by gravity, but they\u2019re also unable to interact with other things, so I don\u2019t know if they can move from the spot they evoke it in or if they need a Seeming bonus to do so. Just pondering for any Seeming Bonuses I was thinking of making.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can specifically move through physical barriers and the Ogre blessing gives you the ability to extend it to people you're carrying, so I'm inclined to call that a hard &quot;Yes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T10:55:29-07:00","id":1404428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1404270#post1404270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Whispers Of Morning contract, are Changelings able to move while in their noncorporeal state? They\u2019re not affected by gravity, but they\u2019re also unable to interact with other things, so I don\u2019t know if they can move from the spot they evoke it in or if they need a Seeming bonus to do so. Just pondering for any Seeming Bonuses I was thinking of making.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what Satchel says, if you try to &quot;physics&quot; this contract too much, you'd &quot;logically&quot; end up with a Changeling hanging in empty space the very next moment as the planet instantly zips away from them. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T20:05:01-07:00","id":1407432,"title":"","content":"Is there anyway for Changelings to have a Safe Place in the Mortal World that is impervious to the Gentry and Huntsmen?<br /> <br /> My current idea is a community of Changelings inside a building, but I've been told that it would be an easy target since the Changelings never leave. My thought is that the building is protected in someway by the Seasonal Court Oaths such that when the Seasons change the True Fae don't see it as a stronghold of Changelings, because to them its a new territory that has appeared not a static structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T20:42:06-07:00","id":1407439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1407432#post1407432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anyway for Changelings to have a Safe Place in the Mortal World that is impervious to the Gentry and Huntsmen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without invoking unique or particular circumstances. Hollows are more secure than Safe Places for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T17:58:39-07:00","id":1407622,"title":"","content":"When a True Fae creates a Huntsman it gives it one of its Titles, correct? Does this mean the True Fae no longer has access to this Title? And is the Huntsman responsible for maintaining the True Fae\u2019s Oath?<br /> <br /> For instance can a Huntsman accidentally be made to break the Oath for their Keeper? Resulting in the loss of the title for the Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T18:39:54-07:00","id":1407640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1407622#post1407622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a True Fae creates a Huntsman it gives it one of its Titles, correct? Does this mean the True Fae no longer has access to this Title? And is the Huntsman responsible for maintaining the True Fae\u2019s Oath?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Dark Eras includes reference to a Fae and their Huntsman double, the practical reading seems to be that pouring their desire into the void where a Huntsman's heart would be is a particular exercise of the Title's power that it can only commit to a singular instance of at any given time \u2014 note the use of language like &quot;the Keeper's heart&quot; and &quot;the purest, powerless representation of their tormentor&quot; in the section on The End of the Chase.<br /> <br /> The Huntsman is a separate being that is driven mostly by its master's desires as long as the Title still commands it, rather than a direct manifestation of the Gentry's will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:10:36-07:00","id":1408156,"title":"","content":"Can Changelings have children? According to page 42 of the CTL 1st edition it seems like no, but I know sometimes supplements change things to add a new Mortal type. 2e seems to not address this.<br /> <br /> The main part of my question is do Changeling who have children together have a Mortal, Changeling, or other subtype kid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T14:52:09-07:00","id":1408412,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25291_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25291\" data-vbnamecard=\"25291\">DontEatRawHagis</a> it is called out in a few places as &quot;possible but difficult&quot; I know that there is a bit in goblin markets about a way hobgoblins might be able to help a changeling have a child. It's a 1e book but I feel that's still an appropriate method that just hasn't been covered by 2e yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T14:59:31-07:00","id":1408413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1408156#post1408156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main part of my question is do Changeling who have children together have a Mortal, Changeling, or other subtype kid?</div> </div> </div> </div> In 1e, at least, the children of changelings were regular mortals, albeit with a tendency for minor (and entirely mundane) quirks relating to their parents' nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:12:47-07:00","id":1408576,"title":"","content":"I have some trouble adjudicating what is and isn't an appropriate action for a hedgespinning shift, or indeed don't even know if this is something I should be concerned with to begin with.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I'm confused by how hedgespinning is at the same time described as something that happens <i>in addition</i> to the mundane action that generated the successes (albeit giving a penalty and moving some of the successes from the action's normal result to hedgespinning shifts), and in the examples as some specific actions taken for the express purpose of hedgespinning a certain result.<br /> <br /> Take the example on p. 204-205 concerning persuading the locals into building a bridge to proceed. I assume in this case you'd roll a persuasion roll (with penalty for hedgespinning) to convince them. But if you succeed, you might still not have enough successes to get the shift to build the bridge. Then what happens? It feels odd to succeed on a skill roll, but then the bridge doesn't get made so it isn't all that successful in the end. I must be missing something, but I need some help figuring out precisely what. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Possible resolution to this that I can think of: The local hobs agree to help, but some obstacle presents itself keeping them from finishing a bridge. You can thus bank the successes you've got already to add them to the next hedgespinning roll, which you'll likely do while helping them clear this obstacle, which might involve getting materials to build the bridge, or getting rid of hostile hobs trying to stop the building, etc... Does that sound right? =&gt; Problem: banking successes is only available with a Paradigm Shift, which they likely did not achieve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bit of a bummer since this really seems like a good answer otherwise!)<br /> <br /> On a similar note I find it difficult to adjudicate what skills are and aren't appropriate for a given goal (if indeed that is even a thing). One other possible way of building the bridge reads:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or physically wrestling<br /> with a foe who represents an internal struggle she wishes<br /> to move past </div> </div> </div>So if my player says &quot;I want to get this bridge built by wrestling with a physical representation of an internal struggle!&quot; is that always automatically an option or can I on occasion go &quot;Err... well, no such opponent seems to be present right now.&quot;?<br /> <br /> If an action must only be thematically related to the feelings and end result you're trying to achieve, can a Musician kith Changeling heavily specialized in music essentially whip up a thematically appropriate piece of music on the fly (perhaps with improvisation penalties if it's not a piece they've made/rehearsed before) to hedgespin essentially any desired end result on the strength of that one dicepool alone with few variations in approach?<br /> I think it sounds like more fun for all involved if the actions need to be a <i>bit</i> more directly linked to end result (like the examples of smashing rocks together and forcing them to become a hammer, or convincing people around you that a door you draw is real; those are fun and very scene-specific! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and the dicepools therefore more varied, but I can't find any strong textual support for that; singing all your problems away for the most part seems directly supported. :P (And Hedge-singing sounds cool and thematically appropriate so I want music to be a viable answer sometimes, but not every time. xD)<br /> The specific skill here is only a theoretical example, I'm sure there are other skills to that effect. ^^<br /> <br /> Then finally, when your goal isn't to hedgespin necessarily, like when you make an attack and decide to make it a hedgespinning one &quot;just in case&quot;, do you need to spend shifts in a way that aligns with your method of attacking/your intentions? How should I see this, exactly? ^^<br /> <br /> If anyone just outright can go &quot;Here, this is a PBP campaign I did and this is an outright transcription of a hedge-focused session we did with a bunch of hedgespinning examples,&quot; that would be so &lt;3.<br /> Any examples appreciated, essentially. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-16-2020, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:58:51-07:00","id":1408638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1408576#post1408576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the example on p. 204-205 concerning persuading the locals into building a bridge to proceed. I assume in this case you'd roll a persuasion roll (with penalty for hedgespinning) to convince them. But if you succeed, you might still not have enough successes to get the shift to build the bridge. Then what happens? It feels odd to succeed on a skill roll, but then the bridge doesn't get made so it isn't all that successful in the end. I must be missing something, but I need some help figuring out precisely what. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Possible resolution to this that I can think of: The local hobs agree to help, but some obstacle presents itself keeping them from finishing a bridge. You can thus bank the successes you've got already to add them to the next hedgespinning roll, which you'll likely do while helping them clear this obstacle, which might involve getting materials to build the bridge, or getting rid of hostile hobs trying to stop the building, etc... Does that sound right? =&gt; Problem: banking successes is only available with a Paradigm Shift, which they likely did not achieve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bit of a bummer since this really seems like a good answer otherwise!)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember that the &quot;softer&quot; version of banking successes is a regular subtle shift: securing an equipment bonus for a subsequent roll may not add successes directly, but it does add dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if my player says &quot;I want to get this bridge built by wrestling with a physical representation of an internal struggle!&quot; is that always automatically an option or can I on occasion go &quot;Err... well, no such opponent seems to be present right now.&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Context rules the day. If your player does the narrative legwork to paint a physical obstacle as representative of an internal struggle, then they can definitely use surmounting that obstacle to get over the chasm they're trying to tie a rope across.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If an action must only be thematically related to the feelings and end result you're trying to achieve, can a Musician kith Changeling heavily specialized in music essentially whip up a thematically appropriate piece of music on the fly (perhaps with improvisation penalties if it's not a piece they've made/rehearsed before) to hedgespin essentially any desired end result on the strength of that one dicepool alone with few variations in approach? </div> </div> </div>Filtering Hedgespinning efforts through your areas of specialty (particularly kiths, thanks to their effects on Skills) is a legitimate method to use, but as ever, context is important (and can shift rapidly in the Hedge \u2014 remember that the Hedge shapes itself in response to interactions with it). If you feel like the connective tissue between a given method and the desired outcome is too tenuous, I think it would be fine to necessitate some intervening steps and descriptive work to get from point A to point D.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then finally, when your goal isn't to hedgespin necessarily, like when you make an attack and decide to make it a hedgespinning one &quot;just in case&quot;, do you need to spend shifts in a way that aligns with your method of attacking/your intentions? How should I see this, exactly? ^^ </div> </div> </div>Could you give an example of how this wouldn't be the outcome anyway, given the context-sensitive nature of Hedgespinning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T10:54:20-07:00","id":1408745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1408638#post1408638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give an example of how this wouldn't be the outcome anyway, given the context-sensitive nature of Hedgespinning?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm fully understanding your question, but what I mean is: When I'm doing an action specifically to try to hedgespin a bridge, I sort of know what I'm going for, right? But if I make an attack and I hedgespin it, can I then decide to use the shifts to make armour for myself because that's &quot;related&quot; to fighting, or not because I was on the offense, not defense, or where abouts should one draw the line?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Filtering Hedgespinning efforts through your areas of specialty (particularly kiths, thanks to their effects on Skills) is a legitimate method to use, but as ever, context is important (and can shift rapidly in the Hedge \u2014 remember that the Hedge shapes itself in response to interactions with it). If you feel like the connective tissue between a given method and the desired outcome is too tenuous, I think it would be fine to necessitate some intervening steps and descriptive work to get from point A to point D. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my biggest concern is that the idea of &quot;shape the hedge according to my music&quot; sounds a bit repetitive, because you can essentially make music to fit any situation but it doesn't have much narrative &quot;weight&quot;, i.e. nothing much is &quot;happening&quot; in the story aside from you playing a lot of music. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T19:17:30-07:00","id":1408830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1408745#post1408745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'm fully understanding your question, but what I mean is: When I'm doing an action specifically to try to hedgespin a bridge, I sort of know what I'm going for, right? But if I make an attack and I hedgespin it, can I then decide to use the shifts to make armour for myself because that's &quot;related&quot; to fighting, or not because I was on the offense, not defense, or where abouts should one draw the line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Context and details will make or break particular instances, but if you're spending a shift you got by progressing a conflict to engage further with the conflict I don't think anyone would take much issue with that (hell, it's half the point of Hedge Brawler).<br /> <br /> (It should be noted that direct attacks are generally a less-than-ideal set of actions to Hedgespin from, since you need to roll multiple successes on a penalized roll and Defense makes that even harder, and by a similar token adding a penalty to an action on a whim is a massive gamble for most actions a character could conceivably take.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, my biggest concern is that the idea of &quot;shape the hedge according to my music&quot; sounds a bit repetitive, because you can essentially make music to fit any situation but it doesn't have much narrative &quot;weight&quot;, i.e. nothing much is &quot;happening&quot; in the story aside from you playing a lot of music. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I think the solution to that is to remember that e.g. &quot;shape the Hedge by physically crafting it&quot; is descriptively identical \u2014 you press for details in cases like this, because Hedgespinning effects don't just <i>happen</i> without any sort of process playing out to shift them into focus. Attracting wandering hobgoblins to supply you with an organization is one way to get musically-sourced Hedgespinning effects to work, while tugging at the heartstrings of the Hedge itself to make it rain is another, and replicating the howl of a bestial Hedge ghost with your instruments is yet a third.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the section exhorts players to describe shifts in terms of what's happening to the scenery, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T18:08:43-07:00","id":1410172,"title":"","content":"Can dream manipulation be used on animals? In particular if my players have a specific animal they need to manipulate the dreams of can they do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T05:21:00-07:00","id":1410270,"title":"","content":"Many types of animals do have dreams, but the Dreaming Roads are only described as linking up to human dreams. You might have to find another way to influence the dreams other than entering its Gate of Horn. Not that I really know what you might hope to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:06:01-07:00","id":1410294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1410270#post1410270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many types of animals do have dreams, but the Dreaming Roads are only described as linking up to human dreams. You might have to find another way to influence the dreams other than entering its Gate of Horn. Not that I really know what you might hope to achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im setting up a scenario where the Winter Court is trying to make the Groundhog for Groundhogs Day so scared that it doesn\u2019t come out of its burrow. And thus Winter secures 6 weeks more time to reign. <br /> <br /> Thought is that if they can get into an animal\u2019s dreams they can make it want to stay in its enclosure. Yes this is a very crazy plan, but it\u2019s Ocean\u2019s Eleven/Inception with a Groundhog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T09:21:54-07:00","id":1410312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1410294#post1410294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought is that if they can get into an animal\u2019s dreams they can make it want to stay in its enclosure. Yes this is a very crazy plan, but it\u2019s Ocean\u2019s Eleven/Inception with a Groundhog.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are less roundabout ways for changelings to do this, namely by turning into groundhogs and persuading or impersonating Phil.<br /> <br /> Of course, I should point out that the ceremony in question a) is centered on Phil seeing his shadow and going back into the burrow rather than never coming out in the first place, and 2) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punxsutawney_Phil\" target=\"_blank\">is a whole lot wackier than the basic description would indicate</a>, and you can have a lot of fun with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:02:23-07:00","id":1410319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1410312#post1410312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are less roundabout ways for changelings to do this, namely by turning into groundhogs and persuading or impersonating Phil.<br /> <br /> Of course, I should point out that the ceremony in question a) is centered on Phil seeing his shadow and going back into the burrow rather than never coming out in the first place, and 2) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punxsutawney_Phil\" target=\"_blank\">is a whole lot wackier than the basic description would indicate</a>, and you can have a lot of fun with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Punxsutawney Phil is the most famous Groundhog, but there are so many other Groundhogs out there. During Groundhog Day there is a website that aggregates all the different Groundhog predictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T11:15:34-07:00","id":1410341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1410319#post1410319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punxsutawney Phil is the most famous Groundhog, but there are so many other Groundhogs out there. During Groundhog Day there is a website that aggregates all the different Groundhog predictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> You understand that it's still a less involved process for characters who can turn into, speak with, and/or command animals to sabotage a yearly mortal-run event by using and/or developing those powers than by going through three or four layers of expensive brain-heist obstacles to ensure that Spring doesn't arrive early, right?<br /> <br /> Because I feel that that is the more important facet of my post than the fact that Buckeye Chuck and company also exist and I would like to be clear on that. 2e making the walls involved in oneiromancy softer doesn't change the textual statement that there are still easier ways to do a lot of the stuff oneiromancy lets you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T05:00:20-07:00","id":1411326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1408412#post1408412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25291_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25291\" data-vbnamecard=\"25291\">DontEatRawHagis</a> it is called out in a few places as &quot;possible but difficult&quot; I know that there is a bit in goblin markets about a way hobgoblins might be able to help a changeling have a child. It's a 1e book but I feel that's still an appropriate method that just hasn't been covered by 2e yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e, changelings can definitely have children and it's no harder than it is for mortals. As for exactly what happens, I haven't had the opportunity to put the details in a book yet, but I'm always on the lookout for one!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T08:06:09-07:00","id":1411352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1411326#post1411326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, changelings can definitely have children and it's no harder than it is for mortals. As for exactly what happens, I haven't had the opportunity to put the details in a book yet, but I'm always on the lookout for one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring logistical obstacles, I presume.<br /> <br /> &quot;The goblins at Market could get you what you need \u2014 the wax of azure bees \u2014 but they asked for your seventh-born son. You weren\u2019t even sure you could have a <i>first</i>-born, since your genitals are hot enough to melt plastic.&quot;<br /> p.245","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:19:48-07:00","id":1411370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1411326#post1411326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 2e, changelings can definitely have children and it's no harder than it is for mortals. As for exactly what happens, I haven't had the opportunity to put the details in a book yet, but I'm always on the lookout for one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a good way to justify a Mortal character with supernatural merits. &quot;Oh, my dad was a walking fireball, that's why I have pyrokinesis!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T22:07:27-07:00","id":1411746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1411352#post1411352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The goblins at Market could get you what you need \u2014 the wax of azure bees \u2014 but they asked for your seventh-born son. You weren\u2019t even sure you could have a <i>first</i>-born, since your genitals are hot enough to melt plastic.&quot;<br /> p.245</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, barring that! But that sort of thing is a decision a player would make deliberately, not something the game imposes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1411370#post1411370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like a good way to justify a Mortal character with supernatural merits. &quot;Oh, my dad was a walking fireball, that's why I have pyrokinesis!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T08:57:05-07:00","id":1411805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1411352#post1411352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\<br /> &quot;The goblins at Market could get you what you need \u2014 the wax of azure bees \u2014 but they asked for your seventh-born son. You weren\u2019t even sure you could have a <i>first</i>-born, since your genitals are hot enough to melt plastic.&quot;<br /> p.245</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lethal Mien sucks in ways some don't anticipate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:35:49-07:00","id":1411815,"title":"","content":"Hmm. So, some probably-but-not-necessarily Changeling-themed Supernatural Merits would be fitting, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T01:29:16-07:00","id":1412404,"title":"","content":"Hello guys and girls!<br /> <br /> Someone can tell me what exactly a Bastion is? It's the whole dream itself? Or it's a specific strucrute into the dream, instead (maybe something like a house or a castle)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T03:07:54-07:00","id":1412405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1412404#post1412404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys and girls!<br /> <br /> Someone can tell me what exactly a Bastion is? It's the whole dream itself? Or it's a specific strucrute into the dream, instead (maybe something like a house or a castle)?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what i ve understanded the Bastion fully contains the dream, it s not visible from inside the dream but reflect some of the characteristics of what is happening inside","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T12:52:19-07:00","id":1412632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1412404#post1412404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys and girls!<br /> <br /> Someone can tell me what exactly a Bastion is? It's the whole dream itself? Or it's a specific strucrute into the dream, instead (maybe something like a house or a castle)?</div> </div> </div> </div>An example I could see is a Bastion that contains someone's dream of being in a club. The Bastion itself might look like a nightclub with a bouncer at the door, representing the Bastion's defenses. The players either need the key or be on the list of those allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T13:28:33-07:00","id":1412636,"title":"","content":"Or to put it another way, the Bastion is the shell or the skin of the dream.<br /> <br /> When you are within a dream, &quot;the Bastion&quot; simply refers to the dream as a whole, and there aren't necessarily any visible walls that would indicate where &quot;the edge of the dream&quot; is. Everything perceived within a dream is on the inside of the Bastion. There is, however, at least one defined exit from the dream, whatever form it takes (a road leading over the horizon, leaping down a chasm, an Employees Only door). Finding the exit and passing through will put you somewhere in the Dreaming Roads stepping out of the Bastion's entrance, or if you are in dream form, you can instead choose to wake up and return to your body.<br /> <br /> When you are in the Dreaming Roads, a Bastion appears as a symbolic representation of the events and motifs of the dream it contains: a dream of a night on the town might manifest as a nightclub with a line and a bouncer, or a dream of being chased might appear as a dark thicket or a vast wall featureless except for doors that open into snaking hallways. Bastions have exterior defenses which an uninvited guest must circumnavigate to reach an entrance and enter the dream within, represented either by eidolons of the dream standing guard outside, or by hazards and obstacles represented by the dream's Fortification rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T14:25:02-07:00","id":1415236,"title":"","content":"Can Fae-Touched see through the Mein?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T14:45:42-07:00","id":1415237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415236#post1415236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Fae-Touched see through the Mein?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ja, they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:17:53-07:00","id":1415316,"title":"","content":"Next dumb question - so for Clarity damage, there's an attack pool formed by the type of Breaking Point, modifiers, etc... And then if that gets any successes, you roll the Wyrd for the actual damage, right?<br /> <br /> Are there any additions to that damage pool? It seems weird because a) it's a two-step attack and then damage roll, which feels very clunky and oWoD, and b) for low Wyrd changelings it seems like getting any Clarity damage is going to be pretty rare. You can roll a massive attack pool, and then they roll their 1 Wyrd or whatever and 2/3rds of the time...no damage.<br /> <br /> The Clarity damage system just seems very strange and clunky, which makes me wonder if I'm just doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:31:56-07:00","id":1415318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415316#post1415316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any additions to that damage pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having no attached Touchstones and having specific Conditions, which I ran through <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1362693#post1362693\">earlier in the thread</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems weird because a) it's a two-step attack and then damage roll, which feels very clunky and oWoD, and b) for low Wyrd changelings it seems like getting any Clarity damage is going to be pretty rare. You can roll a massive attack pool, and then they roll their 1 Wyrd or whatever and 2/3rds of the time...no damage.<br /> <br /> The Clarity damage system just seems very strange and clunky, which makes me wonder if I'm just doing it wrong. </div> </div> </div>It is functionally near-identical to rolling for glitches in Demon. Staying at Wyrd 1 to reduce the odds of taking Clarity damage is going to pay forward in having a completely different set of problems, chief among them being that you've got relatively little magical power backing you up and need to rely on bargains and other stealth measures in the mortal world instead of being able to more confidently confront fae pursuers or survive a bug-out session in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> (Which, fittingly enough, is also the dichotomy Demon presents between maintaining Cover and developing Primum \u2014 you can lay low and avoid compromise to better maintain your fake ID or you can develop your escape routes and holdout weapons at the cost of greater visibility and reduced metaphysical fidelity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:35:04-07:00","id":1415319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415316#post1415316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next dumb question - so for Clarity damage, there's an attack pool formed by the type of Breaking Point, modifiers, etc... And then if that gets any successes, you roll the Wyrd for the actual damage, right?<br /> <br /> Are there any additions to that damage pool? It seems weird because a) it's a two-step attack and then damage roll, which feels very clunky and oWoD, and b) for low Wyrd changelings it seems like getting any Clarity damage is going to be pretty rare. You can roll a massive attack pool, and then they roll their 1 Wyrd or whatever and 2/3rds of the time...no damage.<br /> <br /> The Clarity damage system just seems very strange and clunky, which makes me wonder if I'm just doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of Conditions that add dice to Clarity damage rolls, many of which can be inflicted on a changeling through fae magic, the Hedge, or taking Clarity damage.<br /> <br /> Clarity is meant to be a slippery slope. At low Wyrd, you don't have to worry a whole too much about taking damage, but most recently returned Lost are facing a lot of situations that'll provoke Clarity attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T23:20:44-07:00","id":1415367,"title":"","content":"Can Changelings with Eidetic Memory recall the Durance perfectly, by-passing the normal guidelines on how Wyrd determines how much you remember from your Durance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T01:40:29-07:00","id":1415374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415367#post1415367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Changelings with Eidetic Memory recall the Durance perfectly, by-passing the normal guidelines on how Wyrd determines how much you remember from your Durance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remembering the durance is taxing for your clarity.<br /> I think that any changeling could recall events of it with some concentration, but his mind would explode from thrauma.<br /> Wyrd rating in 2ed from what i can understand determine only the frequence of dream about durance, and how much they are detailed.<br /> Anyway i don t think that eidetic memory would change something, because it s a matter of &quot;i don t want remember&quot; rather than &quot;i can t remember&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T02:33:15-07:00","id":1415377,"title":"","content":"The Durance is heavily associated with memory loss (both in the way that trauma often can cause memory loss, and by memories literally ripped out of you in the form of Icons), so while a Changeling with Eidetic Memory could potentially remember large swathes of their Durance they would not remember all of it. It's even fully possible that the memory of the entire Durance is lost through Icons, meaning she wouldn't remember a thing even with Eidetic Memory.<br /> <br /> While remembering trauma can be traumatising in its own right (especially if it happens unexpectedly) it doesn't have to be, and there's no reason why a changeling's mind would &quot;explode&quot; from it unless the memory is unusually painful and previously repressed. Reenacting/reliving a memory from your Durance is a Clarity breaking point, but it's not one to just remember it.<br /> The Durance is universally described as traumatic, but it explicitly does not have to be (overtly) painful. Some changelings are stated to heavily regret their escape and want to get back to their Keeper, if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T03:01:15-07:00","id":1415381,"title":"","content":"Changelings with Eidetic Memory shouldn't remember more of the Durance, they should just remember the parts they do remember more clearly.<br /> <br /> The memory loss is chiefly associated with losing parts of yourself to the Thorns after all, and Eidetic Memory does ot protect you from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T03:14:25-07:00","id":1415385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415381#post1415381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings with Eidetic Memory shouldn't remember more of the Durance, they should just remember the parts they do remember more clearly.<br /> <br /> The memory loss is chiefly associated with losing parts of yourself to the Thorns after all, and Eidetic Memory does ot protect you from this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Icons are one way for memory loss to happen, but it's far from the only way. Icons doesn't even have to tear away any of the memories of the Durance; they could instead remove memories of things that happened before the changeling was whisked away on a magical adventure.<br /> If Icons were the chief way of losing the memories of your Durance, there'd be no point in having dreams unlocking new memories because they couldn't unlock memories that are literally torn out of you.<br /> I think the reason for these dreams is that the Durance is naturally very hazy once you leave Arcadia and finalise the transformation into a changeling, and that changelings may have a hard time understanding their experiences from their new perspective when they're both transformed and in a world (actually two worlds) that follow a different set of rules. As Wyrd increases the changeling's perspective starts changing once again, towards a better understanding of the Wyrd, and the nature of Fae, allowing them to better understand their dreams of their Durance despite the fact that more time should've passed between the Durance and for them to reach higher levels of Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T05:13:13-07:00","id":1415399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415377#post1415377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Durance is heavily associated with memory loss (both in the way that trauma often can cause memory loss, and by memories literally ripped out of you in the form of Icons), so while a Changeling with Eidetic Memory could potentially remember large swathes of their Durance they would not remember all of it. It's even fully possible that the memory of the entire Durance is lost through Icons, meaning she wouldn't remember a thing even with Eidetic Memory.<br /> <br /> While remembering trauma can be traumatising in its own right (especially if it happens unexpectedly) it doesn't have to be, and there's no reason why a changeling's mind would &quot;explode&quot; from it unless the memory is unusually painful and previously repressed. Reenacting/reliving a memory from your Durance is a Clarity breaking point, but it's not one to just remember it.<br /> The Durance is universally described as traumatic, but it explicitly does not have to be (overtly) painful. Some changelings are stated to heavily regret their escape and want to get back to their Keeper, if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sample breaking point list &quot;Actively searching out memories of your durance&quot; is a two dice breaking point<br /> I mean, memory is not always a coherent thing, thinking about a pleasant event could suddenly link to a torture for some common detail or reference, especially in dreams","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 09-25-2020, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T05:20:14-07:00","id":1415400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415385#post1415385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Icons are one way for memory loss to happen, but it's far from the only way. Icons doesn't even have to tear away any of the memories of the Durance; they could instead remove memories of things that happened before the changeling was whisked away on a magical adventure.<br /> If Icons were the chief way of losing the memories of your Durance, there'd be no point in having dreams unlocking new memories because they couldn't unlock memories that are literally torn out of you.<br /> I think the reason for these dreams is that the Durance is naturally very hazy once you leave Arcadia and finalise the transformation into a changeling, and that changelings may have a hard time understanding their experiences from their new perspective when they're both transformed and in a world (actually two worlds) that follow a different set of rules. As Wyrd increases the changeling's perspective starts changing once again, towards a better understanding of the Wyrd, and the nature of Fae, allowing them to better understand their dreams of their Durance despite the fact that more time should've passed between the Durance and for them to reach higher levels of Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the analogy with real life thrauma applies, dreams are a way for your mind to process bad memories, coping with them and fixing them in your long term memory in order to be a quick reference for similar future events (or something similar, i m not a psych).<br /> Given the supernatural nature of the durance, probably an higher Wyrd rating is necessary to manage the higer levels of magical thrauma<br /> The whole durance is too much thraumatic for a human mind to process, so it s normal for a changeling mind to divide the experience in clusters, and confront with the lesser intense first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 09-25-2020, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T10:39:03-07:00","id":1415439,"title":"","content":"Just gonna keep spouting off questions as I read and have them...<br /> <br /> Do Fetches have a Mask and Mein? Or does a Fetch just look like what it looks like?<br /> <br /> I can't tell from the book whether a Fetch actually looks like an obviously inhuman construct and is covered over by the magic of a Mask, or if it is constructed to look almost human without needing a magic veil, it just has some tells that might reveal its true nature...<br /> <br /> What I'm particularly wondering is if an average Changeling interacting with a Fetch will realize it is a Fetch just by looking at it by seeing through a Mask or the like? Does a Fetch need Normalcy to hide themselves from a Changeling just looking at it, or only to disguise themselves from Contracts and the like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T11:00:55-07:00","id":1415442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415439#post1415439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just gonna keep spouting off questions as I read and have them...<br /> <br /> Do Fetches have a Mask and Mein? Or does a Fetch just look like what it looks like?<br /> <br /> I can't tell from the book whether a Fetch actually looks like an obviously inhuman construct and is covered over by the magic of a Mask, or if it is constructed to look almost human without needing a magic veil, it just has some tells that might reveal its true nature...<br /> <br /> What I'm particularly wondering is if an average Changeling interacting with a Fetch will realize it is a Fetch just by looking at it by seeing through a Mask or the like? Does a Fetch need Normalcy to hide themselves from a Changeling just looking at it, or only to disguise themselves from Contracts and the like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the picture at pag 99 is a good clue on how it works, if we assume that the girl is looking at her fetch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T14:41:41-07:00","id":1415458,"title":"","content":"Sorry to ask what is a pretty obtuse question, but I'm about to fire up Session 0 of a Changeling game and could have SWORN there was a HUGE list of Kiths back during the Kickstarter days, but there's only a handful in the Corebook. Am I misremembering? Remembering fan conversions? Or am I about to luck out, and one of you will point to a preview that got cut and is part of the upcoming Kiths book? Can't wait to find out! Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T14:50:42-07:00","id":1415459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415458#post1415458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to ask what is a pretty obtuse question, but I'm about to fire up Session 0 of a Changeling game and could have SWORN there was a HUGE list of Kiths back during the Kickstarter days, but there's only a handful in the Corebook. Am I misremembering? Remembering fan conversions? Or am I about to luck out, and one of you will point to a preview that got cut and is part of the upcoming Kiths book? Can't wait to find out! Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>You are thinking of the playtest documents, which worked differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T02:26:30-07:00","id":1415789,"title":"","content":"Strange question.<br /> All changeling starts with wyrd 1, and this seems to imply that they develope the first dot after their escapes from durance.<br /> So what did they have/use DURING the Durance?<br /> The wyrd of their Keepers?<br /> It s important to define because i don t know if a keeper can send a captive changeling outside of arcadia for a mission (like an helldiver) or if it can use only huntsmans and returned Loyalist changelings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T02:56:26-07:00","id":1415793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415789#post1415789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange question.<br /> All changeling starts with wyrd 1, and this seems to imply that they develope the first dot after their escapes from durance.<br /> So what did they have/use DURING the Durance?<br /> The wyrd of their Keepers?<br /> It s important to define because i don t know if a keeper can send a captive changeling outside of arcadia for a mission (like an helldiver) or if it can use only huntsmans and returned Loyalist changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>Send out a captured changeling and it too should have to go through the Torns and finalise the transformation (or, rather, transform back into a more humanoid shape).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T06:07:10-07:00","id":1415808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415793#post1415793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Send out a captured changeling and it too should have to go through the Torns and finalise the transformation (or, rather, transform back into a more humanoid shape).</div> </div> </div> </div>This would make sense, as after passing through the Thorns the changeling should decide if he wants to complete the task and return as a Loyalist or if he prefer to escape and become a Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T06:47:25-07:00","id":1415817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415789#post1415789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange question.<br /> All changeling starts with wyrd 1, and this seems to imply that they develope the first dot after their escapes from durance.<br /> So what did they have/use DURING the Durance?<br /> The wyrd of their Keepers?<br /> It s important to define because i don t know if a keeper can send a captive changeling outside of arcadia for a mission (like an helldiver) or if it can use only huntsmans and returned Loyalist changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahm So.<br /> <br /> All <b>player</b><b> characters </b>start with Wyrd 1. I would assume there's people/changelings kept as playthings in Arcadia with 3 in Wyrd or 10 in Wyrd etc too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T07:38:35-07:00","id":1415825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415817#post1415817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahm So.<br /> <br /> All <b>player</b><b> characters </b>start with Wyrd 1. I would assume there's people/changelings kept as playthings in Arcadia with 3 in Wyrd or 10 in Wyrd etc too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno, i think that a wyrd rating is a personal thing, that require some measure of freedom.<br /> Before escaping arcadia changelings are as you say only playthings, puppets following the narration (and probably wyrd) of their keeper.<br /> I may be wrong, so if everyone knows of the matter were handled in 1st edition it could be a good reference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T10:49:03-07:00","id":1415852,"title":"","content":"Is the effect of the Mercurial Visage, the Mirrorskin's Kith Blessing, permanent? If not, how long does the transformation last?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T11:02:54-07:00","id":1415856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415852#post1415852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the effect of the Mercurial Visage, the Mirrorskin's Kith Blessing, permanent? If not, how long does the transformation last?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the text, the effect lasts &quot;indefinitely&quot; until the changeling spends a point of Glamour to change back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T15:39:29-07:00","id":1416037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1415439#post1415439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just gonna keep spouting off questions as I read and have them...<br /> <br /> Do Fetches have a Mask and Mein? Or does a Fetch just look like what it looks like?<br /> <br /> I can't tell from the book whether a Fetch actually looks like an obviously inhuman construct and is covered over by the magic of a Mask, or if it is constructed to look almost human without needing a magic veil, it just has some tells that might reveal its true nature...<br /> <br /> What I'm particularly wondering is if an average Changeling interacting with a Fetch will realize it is a Fetch just by looking at it by seeing through a Mask or the like? Does a Fetch need Normalcy to hide themselves from a Changeling just looking at it, or only to disguise themselves from Contracts and the like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's inconsistent. And it's been inconsistent since 1e. A lot of art for Changeling has fetches clearly represented by various types of constructs, but the text tends to imply that fetches don't look different from normal humans (even to those who can see the Mien, which every Fetch can thanks to Attuned to the Wyrd), and the Normalcy Echo says the Fetch with it can't be detected as anything other than human by <i>any</i> Fae detective magic.<br /> <br /> So it's up to the Storyteller how they want to portray them.<br /> <br /> If the ST wants to say that Fetches have a Mask and Mien like Changelings, and that Fetches can be seen for what they are if the Mask fails (for instance, if they go into the Hedge), then a lot fewer Fetches will know they aren't human -- only those with the Normalcy power would be completely human looking (unless you think that a Fetch is never going to catch a glimpse of themselves in a mirror or see themselves in a picture, which is unlikely). This take plays up the alien nature of the Fetch-as-Gentry-construct, and how they don't belong wherever they've been placed.<br /> <br /> If the ST wants to portray them as looking human and only being detectable by magic such as Kenning (and not even then if they have Normalcy), that plays up the &quot;you can't go home again&quot; nature of the Fetch and the potential unreliability of the Changeling's memories, making them question their own reality.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a game where the PCs themselves are Fetches, dealing with their Changelings returning from Arcadia, so I'm going with the second version in my own game, but I could easily run a game where the Fetch is meant to be more of an antagonist and look less consistently human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T15:53:48-07:00","id":1416039,"title":"","content":"Okay, clearing some nonsense up:<br /> <br /> Fetches don't have a Mask or a Mein.<br /> <br /> Fetches look like the person they replaced at any or all times until they are killed. Sometimes even months after that event.<br /> <br /> Art can get conflicting on that, because it's more fun to show a fetch as a stitchwork, but the absolute rule is that a Fetch looks more like You than You do most of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T23:34:34-07:00","id":1416060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416039#post1416039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, clearing some nonsense up:<br /> <br /> Fetches don't have a Mask or a Mein.<br /> <br /> Fetches look like the person they replaced at any or all times until they are killed. Sometimes even months after that event.<br /> <br /> Art can get conflicting on that, because it's more fun to show a fetch as a stitchwork, but the absolute rule is that a Fetch looks more like You than You do most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems a little odd to me.<br /> True fae doesn t have reality shaping powers in the material world (apart from contracts), so i always readed it as &quot;they animate a bunch of things with a shadow splinter and then <br /> the same mechanism that make changeling, goblin and other hedgy things project a mask cast a permanent glamorous illusion (a mask) to give it an human appearance.<br /> <br /> You seem very sure of what you have written, perhaps a developer has clarified it in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T23:39:07-07:00","id":1416061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416060#post1416060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems a little odd to me.<br /> True fae doesn t have reality shaping powers in the material world (apart from contracts), so i always readed it as &quot;they animate a bunch of things with a shadow splinter and then<br /> the same mechanism that make changeling, goblin and other hedgy things project a mask cast a permanent glamorous illusion (a mask) to give it an human appearance.<br /> <br /> You seem very sure of what you have written, perhaps a developer has clarified it in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure as the summer solstice's day is long. Sure as the fact that before being the girl who talks about Beast all the time, I was the Changeling Guy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Beyond textual evidence-read Autumn Nightmares, Winter Masques, Rites of Spring, Dancers in the Dusk, and both cores again-an underappreciated element of horror for Changeling is the possibility that they are <i>wrong</i> about their assumption of who they are. Changeling is fundamentally a game of mirrors with plenty of smoke in front of them, and part of the central point of all of that isn't just that all of these shards of people and enemies around you might contain a truth about you you're unwilling to commit to facing, but that they might <i>actually</i> have a better claim to your name than you do. While, honestly, a whole host of people have stakes to that, the fundamental case is the Fetch itself, who, for all the ways they can be adversarially played against you, could honestly be just be some innocent your &quot;Forgot that I was a Mirrorskin the entire time&quot; self-because-that's-a-consequence-of-Arcadia could only <i>accept</i> as the thief of your life because that is the narrative you were <i>sold</i> on.<br /> <br /> I find that a lot of the bemoaning of disregard for the Charlatans is misplaced, but as it regards to this point, I get it-we could do with a whole <i>book</i> on the fact that changelings aren't always right about who they are. Names and identities can be traded, and who you are and who you were are strongly disassociated matters in the world of the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-30-2020, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T00:50:34-07:00","id":1416072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416061#post1416061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure as the summer solstice's day is long. Sure as the fact that before being the girl who talks about Beast all the time, I was the Changeling Guy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Beyond textual evidence-read Autumn Nightmares, Winter Masques, Rites of Spring, Dancers in the Dusk, and both cores again-an underappreciated element of horror for Changeling is the possibility that they are <i>wrong</i> about their assumption of who they are. Changeling is fundamentally a game of mirrors with plenty of smoke in front of them, and part of the central point of all of that isn't just that all of these shards of people and enemies around you might contain a truth about you you're unwilling to commit to facing, but that they might <i>actually</i> have a better claim to your name than you do. While, honestly, a whole host of people have stakes to that, the fundamental case is the Fetch itself, who, for all the ways they can be adversarially played against you, could honestly be just be some innocent your &amp;quot;Forgot that I was a Mirrorskin the entire time&amp;quot; self-because-that's-a-consequence-of-Arcadia could only <i>accept</i> as the thief of your life because that is the narrative you were <i>sold</i> on.<br /> <br /> I find that a lot of the bemoaning of disregard for the Charlatans is misplaced, but as it regards to this point, I get it-we could do with a whole <i>book</i> on the fact that changelings aren't always right about who they are. Names and identities can be traded, and who you are and who you were are strongly disassociated matters in the world of the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately i own only 2ed core.<br /> <br /> But i realized that fetches can see through the mask even before their changeling escapes, so looking in a mirror should reveal their true form to them.<br /> Since most fetches believe to be human before their changeling returns, they clearly cannot possess a regular mask.<br /> <br /> From what is written it seems to me that the nature of the fetches material component is not altered.<br /> So are you perhaps saying that they cast a more potent mask, similar to what Tokens do, that changeling cannot normally pierce?<br /> By the way, can changeling identify fetches and tokens using their Kenning sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:39:32-07:00","id":1416171,"title":"","content":"It's not just an art inconsistency. Page 45 of first edition corebook references Changelings &quot;Looking in a passing baby carriage and seeing a newly formed fetch waving its cornhusk legs and twig fingers&quot;.<br /> Lucy in It Happened To Me part V on pages 230 and 231 of the second edition core can see James' true cloth doll nature when she looks at his reflection, and the description is consistent with Aimee's.<br /> <br /> There are multiple textual examples in both editions of characters looking at a fetch and seeing a weird doll person instead of a flesh and blood human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T19:16:59-07:00","id":1416200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416171#post1416171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are multiple textual examples in both editions of characters looking at a fetch and seeing a weird doll person instead of a flesh and blood human.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also multiple textual examples in Werewolf confusing the powerful spirits the Firstborn with the original batch of werewolves the First Pack. This does not make the totems of the Pure and Forsaken tribes werewolves.<br /> <br /> There are multiple textual examples in Beast of Primordial Pathways being used in a fashion that Primordial Pathways explicitly do not work in. This does not make Primordial Pathways portals.<br /> <br /> There is a piece of chapter fiction in Mage that suggests a character can Awaken without being aware of it or even having any experience to associate the event with in spite of the way Awakenings are otherwise consistently described as a relatively lengthy process. This does not make Awakening instantaneous.<br /> <br /> The point of a fetch is that it fools the vast majority of the universe (sometimes including itself) into believing that it is the person it is modeled on. It can be flawed in various ways, its particular glamour can fail to work on a small handful of key people, it can even reveal itself to all as a weird scarecrow-person for some length of time if it's made in the particular way that allows for that to happen, but what it <i>can't</i> be is a-priori <i>that bad at its job</i> under normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> This is a particularly dense piece of faerie legerdemain that typically only wears off after the thing is dead and enough uncertainty exists for the body to be &quot;replaced&quot; with various garbage; it's got to be durable enough to placeholder someone's mortal destiny. Never say never, sure, but <i>the sort of fetches that we use as the measuring stick for &quot;normal&quot; </i>do not register as animate trashheaps to the average fae or mortal senses.<br /> <br /> They have Health and Integrity despite being made of nonliving materials. They're human persons, possibly with a weird quirk that the mortal-viewer-side escalation of we-don't-talk-about-it-so-it-can't-hurt-us that the Mask taps into papers over as easily as it ignores the Runnerswift's rack of antlers, but most fetch flaws are going to be situational or bear more of a resemblance to the marks of alien abduction than obvious inhumanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T04:44:58-07:00","id":1416464,"title":"","content":"Personally I rule that a Fetch's &quot;Mask&quot; is simply stronger before the Changeling escapes. When the Changeling comes back, there being two of them in Ironsides weakens the claim the Fetch has over that identity and allows anyone who can see past the Mask to see it for what it is. The Fetch only realises it is a fetch generally after the Changeling escapes, so this makes sense to me and smooths over all possible weird cases.<br /> <br /> At the very least it satisfies all the criteria Satchel listed as being integral to the Fetch myth.<br /> <br /> Aside from the &quot;Fetches as measuring sticks for normal&quot; thing... I mean, the book very clearly lays out that there's often something wrong with them in some way or the other, so not sure why we'd use them as a measuring stick for anything. But they'll <i>fool you</i> into believing they're normal enough, sure. That part is important, but that little feeling at the back of a loved one's neck that something is <i>wrong</i> here is an integral part of the mythos and important, too.<br /> <br /> Some 2nd Ed text:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is a fetch, a <b>flimsy simulacrum</b> made of sticks and<br /> string, meaty bits, or whatever other ephemera the True<br /> Fae chooses to bend to the task. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Flimsy simulacrum&quot;, not &quot;solid copy&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You \u2014 warped by your durance, changed<br /> by your experiences in ways even your Mask cannot hide<br /> \u2014 are likely to seem less \u201cyou\u201d than the being that has<br /> experienced your life in your absence. Your fetch knows<br /> things you missed during your durance, knows the joys<br /> and pain they\u2019ve shared with the people you once called<br /> friends over the years. Years that are, for you, filled with<br /> memories of an entirely different place, different lessons,<br /> a different life. </div> </div> </div>Note how it focuses a lot on actions and experiences. Those are more important than simply what the fetch looks like &quot;for real&quot;, so focusing so much on what it looks like is a bit of a sidetrack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see things now, know things, can<br /> do things that are frankly a danger to anyone around you.<br /> You\u2019re not \u201cyou\u201d anymore, not the you that you were before<br /> your durance. And while it may not have started as<br /> the real you, it\u2019s lived the life you couldn\u2019t. Raised your<br /> children. Worked your job. Paid your bills. Even now, it\u2019s<br /> willing to fight to protect the things and the people you<br /> couldn\u2019t. Even if that means fighting you. </div> </div> </div>More focus on actions, on role in the story, over looking like a human or not.<br /> <br /> So yeah, let humans be unable to see its true nature (aside from a little feeling of wrongness occassionally), sure, but letting fae see the truth once its changeling has returned is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T04:32:11-07:00","id":1416709,"title":"","content":"When using Spinning Wheel, can I keep rolling if I meet the target successes (let's say 2) and go all the way up to the +-5 cap of the contract? The usefulness of this contract kinda depends a lot on whether you stop once you hit wyrd/resolve, or can keep going with the extended action rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T04:20:15-07:00","id":1416965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416709#post1416709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Spinning Wheel, can I keep rolling if I meet the target successes (let's say 2) and go all the way up to the +-5 cap of the contract? The usefulness of this contract kinda depends a lot on whether you stop once you hit wyrd/resolve, or can keep going with the extended action rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually use the last roll in an extended action to determine the successes.<br /> If a player want to roll again to get better results i let him if he has not reached the maximum numbers of roll, but i don t let him accumulate successes with the previous roll, i only consider the last roll number of successes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T04:47:15-07:00","id":1416967,"title":"","content":"You don't get to roll again once you've reached the target number unless it's specified. Once you've reached the target number the roll has succeeded.<br /> The exact wording of the Contract implies you count all successes rolled, meaning a successful activation cannot score a modifier below the higher of the subject's Wyrd or Resolve, and is likely to score a high number of successes regardless provided the target doesn't have terrible stats.<br /> The more likely way it's intended to work is that you only count the successes on the final roll. Then you get a distribution that fits non-extended resisted activations.<br /> <br /> Extended actions with the number of successes determining the outcome is just a shit mechanism. It goes against the design philosophy of binary rolls being preferable, and fails to take advantage of the fact that extended actions have numerous Exceptional Success results to choose from to reward good rolls. Personally, I would just throw out it being an extended action and just have Spinning Wheel be an instant action that takes 10 minutes. That would trade out the reliability of the Contract (as failing a roll is much more likely than running out of number of rolls before achieving the target number) for a guarantee that it won't take more than 10 minutes to invoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-06-2020, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T05:40:08-07:00","id":1416972,"title":"","content":"I m a little confused by fae tracking ability and the bargains.<br /> In the bargain (with humans) description the book states that it works by concealing the changeling to the fae senses and this is applied with the Obliged condition.<br /> The problem is that in the book there are two versions of fae tracking systems.<br /> <br /> 1- the wyrd rating of the changeling ALWAYS applies as a bonus to the fae tracking rolls, dropping the mask results in automatic success on this roll.<br /> <br /> 2- the wyrd bonus only applies when the changeling drop the mask in the hedge, dropping the mask in the mundane world results in automatic success on the roll.<br /> OR<br /> the wyrd bonus only applies in each situation in which the changeling is without the mask<br /> <br /> In each cases i think that the Obliged condition negates the wyrd bonus and forces a clash of will with the Hunter senses power.<br /> <br /> If the scenario 1 is true bargains are very useful, but in scenario 2 the description in the bargain section becomes very confusing, as a changeling could simply avoid to drop the mask in the mundane world to avoid attention.<br /> <br /> Have i misunderstood something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T07:18:01-07:00","id":1416984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416972#post1416972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have i misunderstood something?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't drop the Mask in the Hedge, because the Mask doesn't exist in the Hedge. Scenario 2 is a nonsense scenario.<br /> <br /> The sole ambiguities (in the Huntsman section and the Obliged Condition) can be parsed out easily enough:<br /> <br /> 1. The Wyrd rating of a changeling is added as a dice bonus to rolls by fae creatures and Huntsmen to track them.<br /> 2. Scouring away the Mask opens Hedgeways and causes the above rolls to automatically succeed within a range determined by Wyrd, but does not affect the dice bonus outside that range.<br /> 3. The Obliged Condition removes the dice bonus for fae creatures and Huntsmen, forces a Clash of Wills for the Hunter's Senses Dread Power to provide its bonuses, and allows a changeling to hide from Wyrd-touched pursuers at the site of their obligation for a scene once per chapter; it does not affect the act of dropping the Mask (save that it presumably supersedes the automatic success if you are, in fact, hiding).<br /> <br /> Side routes:<br /> A. The Dull Beacon Merit reduces a changeling's effective Wyrd for the purposes of conveying automatic success to fae trackers and opening Hedgeways when dropping the Mask, but does not affect the tracking bonus.<br /> B. The Hollow Merit penalizes all mundane and supernatural attempts to track a changeling while they are in the Hollow, which functionally counteracts the bonus to fae tracking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T07:37:00-07:00","id":1416990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1416984#post1416984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't drop the Mask in the Hedge, because the Mask doesn't exist in the Hedge. Scenario 2 is a nonsense scenario.<br /> <br /> The sole ambiguities (in the Huntsman section and the Obliged Condition) can be parsed out easily enough:<br /> <br /> 1. The Wyrd rating of a changeling is added as a dice bonus to rolls by fae creatures and Huntsmen to track them.<br /> 2. Scouring away the Mask opens Hedgeways and causes the above rolls to automatically succeed within a range determined by Wyrd, but does not affect the dice bonus outside that range.<br /> 3. The Obliged Condition removes the dice bonus for fae creatures and Huntsmen, forces a Clash of Wills for the Hunter's Senses Dread Power to provide its bonuses, and allows a changeling to hide from Wyrd-touched pursuers at the site of their obligation for a scene once per chapter; it does not affect the act of dropping the Mask (save that it presumably supersedes the automatic success if you are, in fact, hiding).<br /> <br /> Side routes:<br /> A. The Dull Beacon Merit reduces a changeling's effective Wyrd for the purposes of conveying automatic success to fae trackers and opening Hedgeways when dropping the Mask, but does not affect the tracking bonus.<br /> B. The Hollow Merit penalizes all mundane and supernatural attempts to track a changeling while they are in the Hollow, which functionally counteracts the bonus to fae tracking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, this is in fact the most coherent interpretation to me, unfortunately the rules written on the oblige condition and the huntsman powers had confunded me.<br /> Also, i was wondering if the wyrd tracking bonus applies also on other creatures linked to arcadia (a changeling tracking a true fae, or another changeling).<br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T16:27:36-07:00","id":1417396,"title":"","content":"I asked this before but it never got answered. When you buy an enhancement dot on hedgespun equipment for armor, are you getting a +1/+1 to both general and ballistic for each dot, +1 to general armor only, or a +1 to either general or ballistic, your choice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T18:18:53-07:00","id":1417405,"title":"","content":"I would assume +1/+1, but that's based on the rather flimsy precedent of contracts that grant armor give equal amounts of general and ballistic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T21:42:38-07:00","id":1417411,"title":"","content":"There is an argument to be made it is +1 in either general or ballistic in order to balance the merit against itself. A hedhespun weapon gives +1 to damage per dot, meaning a hedgespun firearm, bow, or crossbow would have its damage considerably mitigated by an armour of the equivalent rating if the latter gives +1/+1. Essentially, the +1/+1 double ups on the gain per dot compared to the +1s of weapons/other hedgespun items, and I am not entirely sure why the armour would be more cost effective.<br /> <br /> It is a bit ambiguously written and I'd preferred if it had been more clear in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T03:11:18-07:00","id":1417426,"title":"","content":"I say +1 general armour. It's exactly as efficient as a +1 damage modifier. It's also how MtA handles it and it's the one game that has a fairly exhaustive system for improvising/comparing such bonuses.<br /> Technically it should be a choice between general and ballistics armour, but since the latter is always worse than the former when compared on a one to one basis it's not much of a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T06:41:10-07:00","id":1418038,"title":"","content":"The elemental fury contract talks about summoning &quot;raging fires&quot;, and i think that this means applying the Inferno tilt.<br /> Do you think that it would be possible to summon a variant thunderous tilt or it would be impossible, requiring a power that imposes extreme environment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T07:43:05-07:00","id":1418044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1418038#post1418038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The elemental fury contract talks about summoning &quot;raging fires&quot;, and i think that this means applying the Inferno tilt.<br /> Do you think that it would be possible to summon a variant thunderous tilt or it would be impossible, requiring a power that imposes extreme environment?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can summon literal earthquakes, supposedly even there where earthquakes don't generally occur. So I don't think there's necessarily a thematic problem. But rules-wise I can see two problems:<br /> - There is no &quot;Storm&quot; tilt. You need to combine Heavy Winds and Heavy Rain... and then you still don't have lightning. But maybe if it's only lightning, though you'll need to make a new tilt for it.<br /> - There's an Autumn contract that summons a storm that also zaps people with lightning. It would suck for them if you could just do the same with Elemental Fury. So make sure it's not just better than that Contract.<br /> <br /> I guess I'd allow it, but there'll be no controlling the effects of the lightning strikes, and once you unleash it it may destabilize local weather and lead to unforeseen effects (just like how an inferno, once unleashed, will spread by itself and possibly unpredictably).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T08:47:10-07:00","id":1418053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1418038#post1418038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The elemental fury contract talks about summoning &quot;raging fires&quot;, and i think that this means applying the Inferno tilt.<br /> Do you think that it would be possible to summon a variant thunderous tilt or it would be impossible, requiring a power that imposes extreme environment?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Contract applies any Environmental Tilt of your choice, and if one doesn't exist you're both free and encouraged to just make one up. Easiest way to do that is, as you suggest yourself, to just modify one of the sample Tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T03:45:02-07:00","id":1420103,"title":"","content":"A Huntsman's heart resides within a mortal Bastion.<br /> A Bastion exists only for the span of a single dream. When the dreamer awakes, the Bastion crumbles and disappears.<br /> When the heart is destroyed, the Huntsman is no more and its animating Title goes back to its Keeper whence it came.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that a Huntsman only exists for the span of a single dream?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T05:37:03-07:00","id":1420112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1420103#post1420103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Huntsman's heart resides within a mortal Bastion.<br /> A Bastion exists only for the span of a single dream. When the dreamer awakes, the Bastion crumbles and disappears.<br /> When the heart is destroyed, the Huntsman is no more and its animating Title goes back to its Keeper whence it came.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that a Huntsman only exists for the span of a single dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, for much the same reason that the rules for adding Empathy to kenning rolls to see if a character's Bastion has been dreamwoven within a week aren't unusable.<br /> <br /> The Huntsman's heart may be inaccessible during that time (barring tricky uses of things like the Oathbreaker's Punishment Contract), but being in a Bastion as it crumbles doesn't destroy it, particularly not when navigating a Bastion to find it already indicates it's treated more like a native of the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T07:05:30-07:00","id":1420119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1420103#post1420103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Huntsman's heart resides within a mortal Bastion.<br /> A Bastion exists only for the span of a single dream. When the dreamer awakes, the Bastion crumbles and disappears.<br /> When the heart is destroyed, the Huntsman is no more and its animating Title goes back to its Keeper whence it came.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that a Huntsman only exists for the span of a single dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some obvious problems with the hearts/bastions, but I'd resolve them by saying that the heart resides in the subconcious of the human, which becomes accessible when they dream through the Bastion, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:04:48-08:00","id":1423057,"title":"","content":"when I get a new Touchstone, do I attach it to the Clarity Box on the left or on the right of my existing attached Touchstone?<br /> <br /> also, I'm biased as the thread creator, but why isn't this pinned yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:34:08-08:00","id":1423064,"title":"","content":"As it says under the Touchstone Merit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Write each one beside the next available box to the right of the rightmost box with an associated Touchstone. If the last Clarity box already has a Touchstone, you cannot purchase this Merit again. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T11:55:57-08:00","id":1423090,"title":"","content":"So did the Muse Kith in Dark Eras 2 just get designed the wrong way, not getting a exceptional succes on 3 dices for a roll? Every other kith has that specific mechanics and it just seems odd to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T14:50:47-08:00","id":1423380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1423090#post1423090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So did the Muse Kith in Dark Eras 2 just get designed the wrong way, not getting a exceptional succes on 3 dices for a roll? Every other kith has that specific mechanics and it just seems odd to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> there was a period between editions where the development team had a shake up and a new leadership team took over 2e. during this inbetween period, some early rules from the previous developer's edition (we'll call it 1.5) made it to some pdf-only releases. a lot of the previous developer's work didn't make it into the final second edition of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T15:45:19-08:00","id":1423393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1423380#post1423380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there was a period between editions where the development team had a shake up and a new leadership team took over 2e. during this inbetween period, some early rules from the previous developer's edition (we'll call it 1.5) made it to some pdf-only releases. a lot of the previous developer's work didn't make it into the final second edition of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the entirety of Dark Eras 2 was written after 1.5e was scrapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T10:26:48-08:00","id":1424772,"title":"","content":"Is it reasonable to read the &quot;per milestone desired&quot; modifier for Hedge navigation as navigating <i>to</i> a trod from elsewhere in the Hedge, i.e. more powerful trods take longer to reach/find?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T10:40:49-08:00","id":1424777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1424772#post1424772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it reasonable to read the &quot;per milestone desired&quot; modifier for Hedge navigation as navigating <i>to</i> a trod from elsewhere in the Hedge, i.e. more powerful trods take longer to reach/find?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's for the number of milestones you wish to pass when travelling on a trod. The further you go, the more difficult it's going to be (provided you're already under pressure from something that makes you roll when on a trod).<br /> If you're asking if you can <i>also</i> apply that modifier that way, then that could make sense depending on how you interpret the Hedge. A more powerful trod is more static and concrete in a realm that is remarkable for how psychoactive and abstract it often is. That means, wherever you are in the Hedge, a finding a trod means you need to go from a highly mutable location to a highly static location, and it makes sense that a more static location is &quot;further away&quot; than a less static location.<br /> Edit: Actually, the dot rating of the trod would make more sense than just number of milestones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-18-2020, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T20:39:15-08:00","id":1424863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1424777#post1424777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it's for the number of milestones you wish to pass when travelling on a trod. The further you go, the more difficult it's going to be (provided you're already under pressure from something that makes you roll when on a trod).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the &quot;desired&quot; that's tripping me up on assuming that reading \u2014 if it was milestones between you and your destination, it'd be &quot;intervening milestones&quot; or a similar phrase, and if they're <i>not</i> just places you're passing through then the nature of Hedge navigation obviously precludes having multiple separate goals for the same navigation attempt by the same character.<br /> <br /> A trod with more milestones (or a higher dot rating) also effectively counts as a destination that is multiple destinations, which (in addition to the find-a-rock-in-a-stormy-sea challenge the Hedge's nature presents) provides a ready reason for this to be a common enough modifier to put on the core chart even for characters that aren't looking for a stable exit point or attempting a very particular recurring journey to Grandmother's house.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a>, could you shed some light on this point of confusion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T00:48:01-08:00","id":1424880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1423393#post1423393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the entirety of Dark Eras 2 was written after 1.5e was scrapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The Muse kith's mechanics aren't a &quot;mistake,&quot; they're just non-standard because they fit the kith better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1424863#post1424863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the &quot;desired&quot; that's tripping me up on assuming that reading \u2014 if it was milestones between you and your destination, it'd be &quot;intervening milestones&quot; or a similar phrase, and if they're <i>not</i> just places you're passing through then the nature of Hedge navigation obviously precludes having multiple separate goals for the same navigation attempt by the same character.<br /> <br /> A trod with more milestones (or a higher dot rating) also effectively counts as a destination that is multiple destinations, which (in addition to the find-a-rock-in-a-stormy-sea challenge the Hedge's nature presents) provides a ready reason for this to be a common enough modifier to put on the core chart even for characters that aren't looking for a stable exit point or attempting a very particular recurring journey to Grandmother's house.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2229_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2229\" data-vbnamecard=\"2229\">Meghan Fitzgerald</a>, could you shed some light on this point of confusion?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're traveling on a trod and you're under some kind of duress and thus need to actually make chase rolls, then you're looking to get somewhere on that trod; the number of milestones between you and the place you want to get to is the number of desired milestones. Even if you don't know what's on that trod or where it leads, or you don't have a specific destination in mind, you still need to choose a number of milestones (that's why it's &quot;desired&quot;); the ST has to know how far you intend to travel, and should tell you when you get to the trod what its rating is. (The characters don't necessarily know, but the <i>players</i> have to in order to make rolls.) If it's just &quot;go until we reach the endpoint,&quot; then the ST should tell you how many milestones that is. You're not always assumed to be at one end of a trod, either, especially when its endpoints are in the mundane world. You can step onto a trod somewhere in the middle just like any road.<br /> <br /> If you want to travel <i>to</i> a trod from somewhere else, milestones don't enter into it at all until you get there; it's not multiple destinations, it's just you moving from where you are to &quot;somewhere on that trod.&quot; Then if the chase has to continue once you're there, because someone's after you or whatnot, change the numbers to fit traveling on a trod instead of traveling elsewhere. You don't have to start a separate chase, you're just adding to the target number based on how far you want to go.<br /> <br /> I hope that makes sense!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T06:36:37-08:00","id":1424925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1424880#post1424880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're traveling on a trod and you're under some kind of duress and thus need to actually make chase rolls, then you're looking to get somewhere on that trod; the number of milestones between you and the place you want to get to is the number of desired milestones. Even if you don't know what's on that trod or where it leads, or you don't have a specific destination in mind, you still need to choose a number of milestones (that's why it's &quot;desired&quot;); the ST has to know how far you intend to travel, and should tell you when you get to the trod what its rating is. (The characters don't necessarily know, but the <i>players</i> have to in order to make rolls.) If it's just &quot;go until we reach the endpoint,&quot; then the ST should tell you how many milestones that is. You're not always assumed to be at one end of a trod, either, especially when its endpoints are in the mundane world. You can step onto a trod somewhere in the middle just like any road.<br /> <br /> If you want to travel <i>to</i> a trod from somewhere else, milestones don't enter into it at all until you get there; it's not multiple destinations, it's just you moving from where you are to &quot;somewhere on that trod.&quot; Then if the chase has to continue once you're there, because someone's after you or whatnot, change the numbers to fit traveling on a trod instead of traveling elsewhere. You don't have to start a separate chase, you're just adding to the target number based on how far you want to go.<br /> <br /> I hope that makes sense!</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Quick couple of follow-up questions:<br /> <br /> 1. So changing the target number mid-chase from changing circumstances (e.g. taking on Goblin Debt or suffering that Hedgespinning effect that decreases your Speed or Initiative) is definitely supposed to happen?<br /> <br /> 2. What kind of stuff serves as milestones on the Dreaming Roads?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T06:23:32-08:00","id":1426124,"title":"","content":"Beast player guide states that it s possible to watch and interact with a person s dream (or Bastion) while within his Oneiros, but it s like acting through a membrane.<br /> Do you think that there are some specific rules or that it s only a cosmetic thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T07:51:40-08:00","id":1426128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1426124#post1426124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast player guide states that it s possible to watch and interact with a person s dream (or Bastion) while within his Oneiros, but it s like acting through a membrane.<br /> Do you think that there are some specific rules or that it s only a cosmetic thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the statement of that possibility is filtered through the facts of:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The most common psychic inhabitants are animate scenery that variously ignores you, talks to you like you're the person you're walking around inside, or attacks you if you attract attention.<br /> \u2022 The individual soul shifts constantly when not in deep sleep or meditation.<br /> \u2022 The system for changing beliefs and opinions in the Bright Dream, while largely ported from Mage 1e's systems for changing public opinion through the Temenos, does not differentiate between sections of the Bright Dream, and the lowest target number for its extended action is inclusive of a single person.<br /> <br /> You can influence a person's thoughts and emotions from inside their Oneiros, but it'll take multiple rolls if you don't get an exceptional success and there'll be a penalty commensurate to the strength of the belief you're trying to alter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T10:15:17-08:00","id":1426144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1426128#post1426128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the statement of that possibility is filtered through the facts of:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The most common psychic inhabitants are animate scenery that variously ignores you, talks to you like you're the person you're walking around inside, or attacks you if you attract attention.<br /> \u2022 The individual soul shifts constantly when not in deep sleep or meditation.<br /> \u2022 The system for changing beliefs and opinions in the Bright Dream, while largely ported from Mage 1e's systems for changing public opinion through the Temenos, does not differentiate between sections of the Bright Dream, and the lowest target number for its extended action is inclusive of a single person.<br /> <br /> You can influence a person's thoughts and emotions from inside their Oneiros, but it'll take multiple rolls if you don't get an exceptional success and there'll be a penalty commensurate to the strength of the belief you're trying to alter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok<br /> So, considering that this membrane exist and it s tangible (and that from dark eras 2 we know that it is in fact the Hedge), do you think that it s possible to interact physically between the two &quot;realms&quot;?<br /> I would be inclined to say yes, because the dreams are a mechanism of interaction between conscious and subconscious mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T19:38:00-08:00","id":1426785,"title":"","content":"I recently noticed that the Hunterheart's Trickery only uses Attribute + Wyrd for its dice pool, despite being a contested roll. Is that intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T16:44:10-08:00","id":1427057,"title":"","content":"In first edition, I recall that it was common for Changelings to use an alias, either because they forgot their original name or because it provided some manner of protection (names have power). Does 2e cover this topic in any way? I see True Names for the Gentry having power in their section, but I couldn't find anything about Changelings hiding their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T18:01:04-08:00","id":1427073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427057#post1427057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first edition, I recall that it was common for Changelings to use an alias, either because they forgot their original name or because it provided some manner of protection (names have power). Does 2e cover this topic in any way? I see True Names for the Gentry having power in their section, but I couldn't find anything about Changelings hiding their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same section, first paragraph. It applies to everyone, but changelings knowing what they know incentivizes them to protect against that vulnerability in particular through assumed names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T06:09:39-08:00","id":1427131,"title":"","content":"I know the Tumult contract requires you to know someone's true name to use it against them. Apart from that, I can't find anything that suggests that someone knowing a changeling's true name gives them any power over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T06:43:44-08:00","id":1427136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427131#post1427131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the Tumult contract requires you to know someone's true name to use it against them. Apart from that, I can't find anything that suggests that someone knowing a changeling's true name gives them any power over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>See pag 270 of the 2ed core book, the names and pledges paragraph, for a very solid reason to using Aliases","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T09:04:23-08:00","id":1427146,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> I'm also having a very hard time finding a clean way to explain the difference between Seeming and Kith to my players. The various sections in the book where either are described seem to contradict and overlap, so I can't get a solid understanding.<br /> <br /> Kith is described as &quot;a refinement of Seeming&quot; but they are now completely detached from Seeming, as they say two sentences after calling it a refinement of one. They call Kith the result of being crafted to a purpose of coping a specific way, but these are both descriptions used for what a Seeming is, as well.<br /> <br /> Is there a simple and easy rule-of-thumb or method to explain to players what the difference is, narratively? The mechanical differences are pretty clear, but I need to explain what they mean for the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T09:49:06-08:00","id":1427155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427136#post1427136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See pag 270 of the 2ed core book, the names and pledges paragraph, for a very solid reason to using Aliases</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is a True Fae around then having the Obsessed condition is one of my least concerns. It's a very niche and (in my games at least) extremely rare situation. I think a Changeling not keeping their true name concealed isn't really all that much of a deal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:34:34-08:00","id":1427167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427146#post1427146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.<br /> <br /> I'm also having a very hard time finding a clean way to explain the difference between Seeming and Kith to my players. The various sections in the book where either are described seem to contradict and overlap, so I can't get a solid understanding.<br /> <br /> Kith is described as &quot;a refinement of Seeming&quot; but they are now completely detached from Seeming, as they say two sentences after calling it a refinement of one. They call Kith the result of being crafted to a purpose of coping a specific way, but these are both descriptions used for what a Seeming is, as well.<br /> <br /> Is there a simple and easy rule-of-thumb or method to explain to players what the difference is, narratively? The mechanical differences are pretty clear, but I need to explain what they mean for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeming is broad where Kith is specific. Any given Seeming can represent a wide swath of characters through a generalized fairy tale archetype, while a Kith serves to narrow that down. A Seeming continuously colors a changeling's experiences, whereas a Kith only comes up on certain occasions. You could also think of Kiths as the adjective to Seeming's noun: An Artist Ogre carries a different connotation from a Gristlegrinder Ogre, though an Ogre can also stand unqualified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:58:12-08:00","id":1427169,"title":"","content":"A seeming is a broad archetype or a kind of story from which you emerged from your durance in Faerie: the noble, the laborer, the brute. Many possible stories can be told within each seeming. A kith is like a flavoring or a coat of paint, aesthetics and defined expression: what kind of noble, what kind of laborer, what kind of brute, a story of dragons or flowers or thunder.<br /> <br /> Think of Urashima Taro and Rip van Winkle as examples of two characters with the same seeming but different kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T13:09:40-08:00","id":1427192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427155#post1427155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there is a True Fae around then having the Obsessed condition is one of my least concerns. It's a very niche and (in my games at least) extremely rare situation. I think a Changeling not keeping their true name concealed isn't really all that much of a deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a privateer or a goblin could learn your name and sell it to a true fae.<br /> With this advantage a true fae can make a changeling obsessed visiting his Bastion, and the hedge would react to it automatically pointing the changeling to the corresponding arcadian realm on the next hedge trip.<br /> If you consider how paranoid some changelings are, they would likely avoid this risky situation i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T13:19:02-08:00","id":1427195,"title":"","content":"As already stated by everyone else, one's the broad archetype while the other is the specialisation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427167#post1427167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeming is broad where Kith is specific. Any given Seeming can represent a wide swath of characters through a generalized fairy tale archetype, while a Kith serves to narrow that down. <b>A Seeming continuously colors a changeling's experiences, whereas a Kith only comes up on certain occasions.</b> You could also think of Kiths as the adjective to Seeming's noun: An Artist Ogre carries a different connotation from a Gristlegrinder Ogre, though an Ogre can also stand unqualified.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda disagree with the bolded part. I think it can vary a lot.<br /> Seemings are supposed to colour the whole changeling experience but they really don't do much after character creation aside from the Blessing/Curse (and even those might not show up much).<br /> How much Kiths matter really depends on how they're designed. In most cases they are probably quite situational (more like a profession than anything) but sometimes they can be absolutely defining for a character.<br /> Either can also affect the mien to very varying degrees. A Human Torch looking Elemental is definitely based on their Seeming and you might not be able to guess at their Kith at all, while a changeling that looks like Count Orlok might be from any Seeming (though probably not Elemental or Fairest) but their Kith is highly likely to relate to vampires (maybe a Leechfinger, or a variation of it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T14:01:06-08:00","id":1427199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427146#post1427146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a simple and easy rule-of-thumb or method to explain to players what the difference is, narratively? The mechanical differences are pretty clear, but I need to explain what they mean for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've struggled with this, especially since it has shifted from 1st edition.<br /> <br /> I <b>think</b> the best answer now is that your Seeming is the <i>role in the story</i> you played in Arcadia, while your Kith is how it <i>shaped</i> you (or you shaped yourself to it).<br /> <br /> Note how the Seeming descriptions don't really focus on cosmetics anymore. There's usually some flavour text that give an example, but that doesn't really seem to define anything. An Ogre could be a big hulking brute...or they could be a malicious needle-toothed little pixie...or a tall and slender sidhe warrior with cruel blades... what defines you as an Ogre isn't a particular archetypal appearance or shape, but the fact that your story was one of <i>Brutality</i>. You were an enforcer or an executioner or a torturer. Your story was one of hurting people.<br /> <br /> Kith is the <i>shape</i> that story made you take - whether it be hulking brute, wee pixie, or slender and pointy-eared sidhe. Not just cosmetic by any means, but it is your adaptations to the role you played.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's how I see it breaking down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T03:19:26-08:00","id":1427256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1427199#post1427199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Ogre could be a big hulking brute...or they could be a malicious needle-toothed little pixie...or a tall and slender sidhe warrior with cruel blades...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a wide eyed little girl... like my current character. (Also an example of how the Kith can be absolutely defining for a character, as I pointed out above, since the Kith I designed is what stopped her from ageing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T14:36:46-08:00","id":1428028,"title":"","content":"What is exactly the distinction between Mien and Mask? Does the Mask merely hides the supernatural parts of the changeling's appearance, or is it a completely different visage? For example, if a Changeling with Many Masks should change their facial features or sex, would their Mien be affected by those changes as well? or would the changeling's Mask and Mien have completely different features or sexes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T15:36:39-08:00","id":1428034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428028#post1428028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is exactly the distinction between Mien and Mask? Does the Mask merely hides the supernatural parts of the changeling's appearance, or is it a completely different visage? For example, if a Changeling with Many Masks should change their facial features or sex, would their Mien be affected by those changes as well? or would the changeling's Mask and Mien have completely different features or sexes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the description of Mask and Mien in the Chapter Two and the description of Manymask, your Mask conforms more or less to the height and build of your mien, which starts out mostly human with vestiges of your durance and adjustments based on court affiliation, Contract knowledge, and other history at low Wyrd; below Wyrd 5, a changeling with Manymask may gradually shift cosmetic details of their Mask (which, aside from facial structure, are mostly matters of color or pattern).<br /> <br /> The prominence of supernatural features in a changeling's mien grow with their Wyrd, and accordingly their Mask grows further apart from it or harder to be covered up by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T07:14:25-08:00","id":1428087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428028#post1428028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is exactly the distinction between Mien and Mask? Does the Mask merely hides the supernatural parts of the changeling's appearance, or is it a completely different visage? For example, if a Changeling with Many Masks should change their facial features or sex, would their Mien be affected by those changes as well? or would the changeling's Mask and Mien have completely different features or sexes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at it from the other direction. The Mask is how you used to look as a human, with some minor influences of your Mien.<br /> The Mien, on the other hand, is how you look like now, which can be completely independent from your old human form. I.e. it can be really similar to the Mask (maybe it's basically the same but with antlers and hooves), or it could be so altered that it's impossible to determine what the Mask would look like (a stylised mannekin with a blank face, for example, or a completely new face). Aside from having roughly the same height and build, it's up to the player's preferences how much the Mask and the Mien intersects.<br /> Manymasks is an exception to how the Mask usually works since it allows you to take on completely new features instead of being permanently roughly how you looked like before your Durance. If planning a character with the Manymasks Merit I'd simply not have the Mien be similar to the Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T12:44:21-08:00","id":1428385,"title":"","content":"I tend to be pretty direct when it comes to the relationship between Mask and Mein. Outside of Contracts or Merits, even big and small changelings are just Giant or Small Framed--bigger or smaller is a Contract, or an easy way to tell Hobgoblins from the Lost. I am part of the camp that says that the mask merely hides the supernatural elements of the Mein. For example, in my original time period of 1999, weirdly colored hair or eyes persisted in the Mask--(&quot;wow, you must spend a lot of money on hair dye&quot;, &quot;doesn't it hurt to wear contact lenses all the time like that?&quot;). Meanwhile, in the 1912 portion of the same universe, oddly colored hair or eyes are entirely mundanized. The Mask might allow for blue hair in modern times, but not back then. Similarly, in 1912, one of the characters has azure skin. In 1999, I might've had him look African, or perhaps even have that chemical imbalance to make him blue. But in 1912, he just looks tan. <br /> <br /> Aside from features from contracts or merits, I tend to go with the idea of describing it loosely, because the mask doesn't work too hard. &quot;Her youthful/ancient eyes stared upon you&quot; fits for both mask and Mein, and is thus appropriate. &quot;He ran his finger through his shaggy hair and scratched his furry chest&quot;. It's all about metaphors and similes. Most of what you see is what you get, even if the Mein makes it more Wyrd and can be extrapolated to supernatural levels. &quot;He pulled his fiery hair from his face&quot; works for both, even if the humans see bright red and the fae see actual fire. <br /> <br /> It also serves as a good character development trait when it comes to the features that CANT be translated, like a satyr always being barefoot (because shoes are uncomfortable on hooves, especially with such thick toenails if you don't file them down) or wings or extra arms. Having to explain to your lover why your bangs are always pointed upwards, even after sleeping, because you have antlers is a good story point. So is the weirdness you feel if your mask just makes your antlers Invisible and your lover can't even feel them. Having vestigal arms coming out of your back is scary and weird, but do is the fact that things move around you that humans couldn't see you touch, both because you have four arms.<br /> <br /> A big note, however, is that the Gentry don't much care about your face. They may want you to be prettier or uglier, they may have a certain look or theme in mind for their mutant offspring, but rarely would a Faerie even notice what you specifically look like to a human degree. That's why the mask and Mein rarely diverge too much. The facial structure you had to start with may be morphed, but the Gentry don't usually pay close enough attention to the majority of the details about you. Some will (&quot;I don't like that mole&quot;, &quot;your eyes need to be bigger to see with&quot;). But everything outside of those whims will be something the Gentry literally don't even see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:17:36-08:00","id":1428930,"title":"","content":"So there's a cap on bonuses/penalties of +5/-5... But that doesn't count things that are part of the die roll. Like if your Defense is 9, it doesn't cap the penalty on your attacker's attack roll at -5, because Defense is just part of the pool.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming when looking at Merits and such, if it uses the word &quot;bonus&quot;, it is affected by the cap. But if it says &quot;Add your rating to your rolls&quot;, then probably not affected by the cap. So for social rolls with your Court, you just add the rating to your die pool so not included in the cap. But for the bonus provided by Workshop, it says bonus so it *is* affected.<br /> <br /> Is that correct? Is there a better way to figure it than just &quot;did whoever wrote that particular section happen to use the word 'bonus'&quot;?<br /> <br /> And this is more of a general CoD, but what about things like specialities? Spending Willpower? Affected by cap or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:25:20-08:00","id":1428934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428930#post1428930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's a cap on bonuses/penalties of +5/-5... But that doesn't count things that are part of the die roll. Like if your Defense is 9, it doesn't cap the penalty on your attacker's attack roll at -5, because Defense is just part of the pool.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming when looking at Merits and such, if it uses the word &quot;bonus&quot;, it is affected by the cap. But if it says &quot;Add your rating to your rolls&quot;, then probably not affected by the cap. So for social rolls with your Court, you just add the rating to your die pool so not included in the cap. But for the bonus provided by Workshop, it says bonus so it *is* affected.<br /> <br /> Is that correct? Is there a better way to figure it than just &quot;did whoever wrote that particular section happen to use the word 'bonus'&quot;?<br /> <br /> And this is more of a general CoD, but what about things like specialities? Spending Willpower? Affected by cap or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be completely honest, I'm pretty sure the different writers didn't think about a lot of these individual cases. What's intended, if anything, is something we can only guess at. Your rule of thumb is one way to handle it, and probably far from the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T15:34:57-08:00","id":1428941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428930#post1428930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's a cap on bonuses/penalties of +5/-5... But that doesn't count things that are part of the die roll. Like if your Defense is 9, it doesn't cap the penalty on your attacker's attack roll at -5, because Defense is just part of the pool.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming when looking at Merits and such, if it uses the word &quot;bonus&quot;, it is affected by the cap. But if it says &quot;Add your rating to your rolls&quot;, then probably not affected by the cap. So for social rolls with your Court, you just add the rating to your die pool so not included in the cap. But for the bonus provided by Workshop, it says bonus so it *is* affected.<br /> <br /> Is that correct? Is there a better way to figure it than just &quot;did whoever wrote that particular section happen to use the word 'bonus'&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>My general understanding is that the net modifier doesn't go above or below +/-5 and if a roll doesn't specially define a Trait as part of the base pool then it's a modifier. Social rolls adding dice from Mantle is almost directly analogous to adding Status to rolls within an organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this is more of a general CoD, but what about things like specialities? Spending Willpower? Affected by cap or not? </div> </div> </div>Willpower isn't, but the way Specialties work means that while &quot;bonus&quot; is used in some of the language I don't think too much breaks from counting them as conditional extra Skill dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T20:44:59-08:00","id":1428977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428941#post1428941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower isn't, but the way Specialties work means that while &quot;bonus&quot; is used in some of the language I don't think too much breaks from counting them as conditional extra Skill dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't Willpower be affected by the cap? It is specifically phrased as &quot;a three-die bonus&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone got a cite on the <i>total</i> bonuses or penalties not exceeding +/-5? Reading over the sections I can find, it seems vague on whether it is any individual modifier or modifiers in total.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T21:34:21-08:00","id":1428983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428977#post1428977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't Willpower be affected by the cap? It is specifically phrased as &quot;a three-die bonus&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Misworded my statement while arranging the sentence. It's subject to the cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, anyone got a cite on the <i>total</i> bonuses or penalties not exceeding +/-5? Reading over the sections I can find, it seems vague on whether it is any individual modifier or modifiers in total. </div> </div> </div>Common-sense reading based on how the game works.<br /> <br /> If an average professional in a field has two to three dots in each of the Attributes and Skills necessary to do the thing they do, it is unlikely for anything but the absolute worst-case scenario to bring them down to a situation where a dramatic failure will happen without the player upgrading a normal failure.<br /> <br /> If a completely talentless novice in a field has no Skill dots and minimal Attribute ratings for the task to which those things apply, no amount of good gear and lucky happenstance is going to let them have better odds of success than the aforementioned average professional working under normal circumstances, because past a certain level of bonus it's stopped being <i>the character doing the thing.</i><br /> <br /> On a practical level, it also stops the number of dice on a single roll from reaching &quot;bring a bucket&quot; without a lot of luck and a specific physical approach to the X-Again, rote, and Advanced Action qualities. Most characters will not roll more than ten to fifteen dice on the thing they're good at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T06:48:39-08:00","id":1429018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1428977#post1428977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, anyone got a cite on the <i>total</i> bonuses or penalties not exceeding +/-5? Reading over the sections I can find, it seems vague on whether it is any individual modifier or modifiers in total.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> vague. That's why people have different interpretations. Satchel provides an in-depth analysis for why they believe it is (or should be) total, but the truth is there's no unifying intent behind it since different writers and devs have to reinterpret the exiwting books when writing new books.<br /> My group interpreted the cap as being per source of modifier. We think it's more fun that way since supernaturals often have the ability to break the dice pool ceiling that regular humans are subject to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T11:57:01-08:00","id":1429044,"title":"","content":"In 1e, there were explicit modifier caps. In CofD, each modifier &quot;usually&quot; ranges from -3 to +3 and is capped at -5 to +5. However, there is nothing about total modifiers being capped. Indeed, there are examples of situational modifiers being at 5 and equipment modifiers being at 5 and said example makes no mention that you are limited to +5 total between them.<br /> <br /> RAW, I see no support for a total modifier cap, only a per-modifier cap.<br /> <br /> The Changeling book makes this a bit fuzzier by rewording the standard text as it exists in core and the other books, but looking at the other books makes it pretty clear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":".  Clarifying Changeling Core vs other books 12-19-2020, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T13:47:24-08:00","id":1429665,"title":"","content":"Do Hobgoblins in the mortal world have Masks?<br /> <br /> I'd assume so since everything else seems to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T17:27:15-08:00","id":1429694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1429665#post1429665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Hobgoblins in the mortal world have Masks?<br /> <br /> I'd assume so since everything else seems to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do, but i don t remember where it is explained","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T00:59:25-08:00","id":1430056,"title":"","content":"I have a question about the Comatose Condition. From what I understand:<br /> - If your Clarity track is filled and you take mild damage, you gain the Comatose Condition.<br /> - If your Clarity track is filled and you take severe damage, you get the Persistent version instead.<br /> <br /> Does this imply that the non-Persistent version is temporary? Usually, non-Persistent Conditions are meant to be resolved within the session, and may be removed if no longer relevant (and the ST may choose do grant the beat or not). Does this apply to the mild Comatose as well? Can the Condition &quot;fade away&quot; after some time, without being resolved? What happens to the Clarity damage then?<br /> <br /> To put it in another way: why isn't the mild version Persistent as well?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T02:34:23-08:00","id":1430058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1430056#post1430056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the Comatose Condition. From what I understand:<br /> - If your Clarity track is filled and you take mild damage, you gain the Comatose Condition.<br /> - If your Clarity track is filled and you take severe damage, you get the Persistent version instead.<br /> <br /> Does this imply that the non-Persistent version is temporary? Usually, non-Persistent Conditions are meant to be resolved within the session, and may be removed if no longer relevant (and the ST may choose do grant the beat or not). Does this apply to the mild Comatose as well? Can the Condition &amp;quot;fade away&amp;quot; after some time, without being resolved? What happens to the Clarity damage then?<br /> <br /> To put it in another way: why isn't the mild version Persistent as well?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The changeling itself can resolve the non persistent condition, the persistent one can be resolved only with external intervention","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T03:05:43-08:00","id":1430059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1430056#post1430056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the Comatose Condition. From what I understand:<br /> - If your Clarity track is filled and you take mild damage, you gain the Comatose Condition.<br /> - If your Clarity track is filled and you take severe damage, you get the Persistent version instead.<br /> <br /> Does this imply that the non-Persistent version is temporary? Usually, non-Persistent Conditions are meant to be resolved within the session, and may be removed if no longer relevant (and the ST may choose do grant the beat or not). Does this apply to the mild Comatose as well? Can the Condition &quot;fade away&quot; after some time, without being resolved? What happens to the Clarity damage then?<br /> <br /> To put it in another way: why isn't the mild version Persistent as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Persistent Conditions are supposed to be lasting, in terms of rules they only differ from regular Conditions in two ways: They take more effort to resolve, and they grant one beat per session if they impact the character's life.<br /> The regular version of Comatose can be resolved the very same scene with no external input. The Persistent version requires external help, thus requiring more effort than the regular version.<br /> <br /> Conditions can fade because of two reasons: They have a timer, or they stop being relevant to the character. Technically both regular and Persistent Conditions can fade, but Persistent Conditions will rarely, if ever, do so because they're supposed to represent lasting issues or circumstances.<br /> In practice, however, neither version of Comatose will ever fade because being comatose should never stop being relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T06:02:29-08:00","id":1430070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1430059#post1430059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While Persistent Conditions are supposed to be lasting, in terms of rules they only differ from regular Conditions in two ways: They take more effort to resolve, and they grant one beat per session if they impact the character's life.<br /> The regular version of Comatose can be resolved the very same scene with no external input. The Persistent version requires external help, thus requiring more effort than the regular version.<br /> <br /> Conditions can fade because of two reasons: They have a timer, or they stop being relevant to the character. Technically both regular and Persistent Conditions can fade, but Persistent Conditions will rarely, if ever, do so because they're supposed to represent lasting issues or circumstances.<br /> In practice, however, neither version of Comatose will ever fade because being comatose should never stop being relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I guess the name Persistent Condition is a bit misleading, at least to me. As you put it, the difference with regular Conditions is less about fading or lasting, and more about the effort required to resolve it. The two concepts usually coincide most of the time, but not always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T23:21:57-08:00","id":1430185,"title":"","content":"Are entitlements all one of a kind? Like is there only ever one Baron of the lesser ones? Or could there theoretically be more than one active at a time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T02:33:36-08:00","id":1430195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1430185#post1430185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are entitlements all one of a kind? Like is there only ever one Baron of the lesser ones? Or could there theoretically be more than one active at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Every entitlement is unique, although a few contain several roles and titles within them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The titles in legion entitlements are also implied to be unique, if still related to one another (like the Dauphines of Wayward Children).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T10:50:02-08:00","id":1430246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1430195#post1430195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Every entitlement is unique, although a few contain several roles and titles within them.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The titles in legion entitlements are also implied to be unique, if still related to one another (like the Dauphines of Wayward Children).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I was little confused due to how it explained interactions with huntsmen and the true fae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T11:19:22-08:00","id":1430350,"title":"","content":"I didn't get the read at all that legion Entitlements had to be unique in their roles. If that's the case, this should have been written out a lot more clearly in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T13:44:20-08:00","id":1430368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every entitlement is unique, although a few contain several roles and titles within them.<br /> <br /> Most entitlements are singular, but a few hold multiple, related titles. Such a legion entitlement contains five or six roles at most </div> </div> </div>They hold related roles and titles, but it does seem to be that they are unique, not copies of the same role or title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T05:24:31-08:00","id":1430561,"title":"","content":"So the book mentions that a changeling can create goblin fruit under paradigm shifts by hedgespinning. Considering that this requires the changeling to not only acquire at minimum 5 successes but also spend 2 glamour, creating any goblin fruit that can do things other than just give glamour seems reasonable, no? Including creating amaranthine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T10:03:04-08:00","id":1430585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1430561#post1430561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the book mentions that a changeling can create goblin fruit under paradigm shifts by hedgespinning. Considering that this requires the changeling to not only acquire at minimum 5 successes but also spend 2 glamour, creating any goblin fruit that can do things other than just give glamour seems reasonable, no? Including creating amaranthine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Remember, though, that regardless of what fruit you produce this produces only one goblin fruit, gives you an emotional Condition at the end of the scene based on how you got there, attracts attention from the locals, and will probably cost more than 2 Glamour unless you weren't leveraging a lowered exceptional success threshold on a penalized roll. As with many things in the Hedge, going carefully tends to go best.<br /> <br /> (Not for nothing is Goblin Fruit Farming a sample Specialty for Workshops.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T09:37:59-08:00","id":1431294,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for another supernatural, like a Mage or Werewolf, take possession of a Fae's Tittle, becoming Entitled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T10:56:22-08:00","id":1431299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1431294#post1431294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for another supernatural, like a Mage or Werewolf, take possession of a Fae's Tittle, becoming Entitled?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that an entitlement requires a wyrd score to work properly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T11:34:47-08:00","id":1431304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1431294#post1431294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for another supernatural, like a Mage or Werewolf, take possession of a Fae's Tittle, becoming Entitled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring Weird Crossover Shit I don't think so, given that the entitlement is represented as a Merit with &quot;changeling&quot; in its prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T18:14:04-08:00","id":1432271,"title":"","content":"Does the destruction of a Comatose changeling's Bastion or the depletion of their Dream Health cause them to realize they are dreaming and resolve the Condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T23:09:52-08:00","id":1432283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1432271#post1432271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the destruction of a Comatose changeling's Bastion or the depletion of their Dream Health cause them to realize they are dreaming and resolve the Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don t know, probably it depends on how do you do it.<br /> By the way, is it possible to destroy a bastion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T07:08:11-08:00","id":1432312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1432283#post1432283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, is it possible to destroy a bastion?</div> </div> </div> </div>A character who attempts a paradigm shift while they have the Dream Assailant Shift Condition and loses the contested Clarity + Composure vs Willpower + Resolve roll against the dreamer causes the dreamer to wake and the Bastion to begin to crumble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T08:10:04-08:00","id":1432316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1432271#post1432271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the destruction of a Comatose changeling's Bastion or the depletion of their Dream Health cause them to realize they are dreaming and resolve the Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that you destroy their Bastion to wake them up; it's that you wake them and the Bastion is destroyed as a result. And yes, if you successfully wake them (in accordance to the specifics of the Comatose Condition) then they wake up. I'm personally of the mind that jarring paradigm shifts and being killed automatically makes the dreamer realise it's a dream; the former because of the natural dissonance between the Bastion as it was and the effects of the shift, and the latter because that's also quite jarring and it gets rid of the situation where the dreamer (potentially a PC) no longer has any agency at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T22:58:51-08:00","id":1435050,"title":"","content":"Are there any examples of eldritch titles? I have an idea for an entitlement but I don't know if it'd qualify or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T06:06:25-08:00","id":1435181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435050#post1435050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any examples of eldritch titles? I have an idea for an entitlement but I don't know if it'd qualify or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>None yet in Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T07:17:13-08:00","id":1435188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435050#post1435050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any examples of eldritch titles? I have an idea for an entitlement but I don't know if it'd qualify or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to follow the sidebar, the only things you need are a high Wyrd prereq (Wyrd 6 or higher seems fitting since the step from Wyrd 5 to 6 is the biggest in terms of becoming less human and becoming more fairy, and powerstat 6+ generally feels weightier) and privileges &amp; duties that can fit a True Fae's Title. I'd suggest things that seem bizarre and/or antagonistic towards other changelings.<br /> However, the step from merely having an Entitlement to becoming a True Fae isn't detailed at all. Somehow the Entitlement probably transforms into the new Gentry's first Title, which I imagine requires Wyrd 10 when the character has access to all Blessings. You could model it after Wild Titles, with the final step to Fae-hood being a trial as if trying to tame an <i>eleventh</i> rank. The question then becomes whether it's by succeeding or by failing that you become a True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T08:02:22-08:00","id":1435198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435188#post1435188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're going to follow the sidebar, the only things you need are a high Wyrd prereq (Wyrd 6 or higher seems fitting since the step from Wyrd 5 to 6 is the biggest in terms of becoming less human and becoming more fairy, and powerstat 6+ generally feels weightier) and privileges &amp; duties that can fit a True Fae's Title. I'd suggest things that seem bizarre and/or antagonistic towards other changelings.<br /> However, the step from merely having an Entitlement to becoming a True Fae isn't detailed at all. Somehow the Entitlement probably transforms into the new Gentry's first Title, which I imagine requires Wyrd 10 when the character has access to all Blessings. You could model it after Wild Titles, with the final step to Fae-hood being a trial as if trying to tame an <i>eleventh</i> rank. The question then becomes whether it's by succeeding or by failing that you become a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly ask because the entitlement I'm making is probably more powerful then the written ones that currently exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T08:27:08-08:00","id":1435201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435198#post1435198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly ask because the entitlement I'm making is probably more powerful then the written ones that currently exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fitting, considering the high prereq and the fact that it's a stepping stone to become a True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T09:33:13-08:00","id":1435212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435201#post1435201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems fitting, considering the high prereq and the fact that it's a stepping stone to become a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't seem to 100% lead to becoming a true fae though. The entitlement for it's own part deals with working on trods an hallows. Shaping the hedge into something that's livable. The token is supposed to grant the ability to add more enhancements]to a hollow with each dot granting a special enhancements or adding a feature to trods. The merits are the problem, I have a general idea of them and what I want them to do but I'm unsure of the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-11-2021, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T22:12:04-08:00","id":1435272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1308379#post1308379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Seizing The Edge, Greyhound or Relentless merits affect chases through the Hedge in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for reposting this, but I\u2019ve not seen anyone answer this question (unless I am very blind) and I really am curious if it would work outside a mundane chase. It\u2019s for a character who was the ex-companion of a Doctor Who-like Gentry (and as we all know, there\u2019s <i>always</i> running in Doctor Who).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T23:11:15-08:00","id":1435274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435272#post1435272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies for reposting this, but I\u2019ve not seen anyone answer this question (unless I am very blind) and I really am curious if it would work outside a mundane chase. It\u2019s for a character who was the ex-companion of a Doctor Who-like Gentry (and as we all know, there\u2019s <i>always</i> running in Doctor Who).</div> </div> </div> </div>I ve found this quote:<br /> &quot;Navigation inside the Hedge works just like a chase, using the rules on p. 195. Even if the characters are unopposed, the Hedge itself works as an \u201copponent,\u201d representing the myriad dangers and temptations that face all travelers there.&quot;<br /> <br /> So i think that all chase specific merits apply even in the hedge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T01:17:44-08:00","id":1435277,"title":"","content":"I have a stupid question maybe. Spin the Wheel. The Crown Royal Contract. The writing does not specify that it cannot be the player to target themselves. Just want to make sure I'm interpreting that correctly...because theoretically a passive -5 to all enemies and a+5 to all personal rolls in pursuit of an action can be fairly powerful...especially since the catch requires only a drop of blood that does no damage from a willing target, mitigating the 3 glamour and 1 willpower every time this contract is cast on oneself. The writing sorta presents like it's primarily meant to target others rather than the self but doesn't specify it does not target the self. So If I'm reading right, a Changeling could prick their own finger and say something like &quot;We will defeat our enemy.&quot; And for they and their allies gain +5 while penalizing their enemy at -5 for all future encounters through the lunar month. As long as you have some time to prepare for the extended action, you could dictate your own aspirations (if ruled general enough) and gain that bonus for theoretically the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> Making sure I'm reading it right and reading 'event' right. Is there a difference between event and goal? Like 'Find our enemy' vs 'Defeat our enemy'? What's ya'lls read on it?<br /> <br /> Again, I feel a little silly asking in case it's abundantly clear or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7452-tulpa-theory","name":"Tulpa Theory","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T01:52:58-08:00","id":1435281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tulpa Theory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1435277#post1435277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a stupid question maybe. Spin the Wheel. The Crown Royal Contract. The writing does not specify that it cannot be the player to target themselves. Just want to make sure I'm interpreting that correctly...because theoretically a passive -5 to all enemies and a+5 to all personal rolls in pursuit of an action can be fairly powerful...especially since the catch requires only a drop of blood that does no damage from a willing target, mitigating the 3 glamour and 1 willpower every time this contract is cast on oneself. The writing sorta presents like it's primarily meant to target others rather than the self but doesn't specify it does not target the self. So If I'm reading right, a Changeling could prick their own finger and say something like &amp;quot;We will defeat our enemy.&amp;quot; And for they and their allies gain +5 while penalizing their enemy at -5 for all future encounters through the lunar month. As long as you have some time to prepare for the extended action, you could dictate your own aspirations (if ruled general enough) and gain that bonus for theoretically the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> Making sure I'm reading it right and reading 'event' right. Is there a difference between event and goal? Like 'Find our enemy' vs 'Defeat our enemy'? What's ya'lls read on it?<br /> <br /> Again, I feel a little silly asking in case it's abundantly clear or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me he can target himself, but:<br /> <br /> Loopholes doesn t mitigate willpower costs<br /> <br /> The bonus/malus equals the number of successes gained on the last roll probably, and it s not easy to obtain 5 successes on a single roll even with large pools","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T12:01:31-08:00","id":1436055,"title":"","content":"What is the BriarNet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25340-pennyforatale","name":"pennyforatale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T22:46:34-08:00","id":1436154,"title":"","content":"I have two questions, are trods made via hedgespinning or are their other rules? Similarly would making a hallow also be a hedgespinning action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-20-2021, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T04:30:38-08:00","id":1436177,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book on me right now so I might be completely wrong, but I think that Hedgespinning is the primary way to create both. Trods most often just naturally generate within the Hedge without active interference from changelings (possibly by the Hedge using its usual Hedgespinning rolls when people interact with it) but Hollows are probably primarily created through intentional Hedgespinning. I don't know of any other rules to create either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T08:18:56-08:00","id":1436207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pennyforatale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1436055#post1436055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the BriarNet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The digital Hedge. It's discussed in <i>Oak, Ash, and Thorn</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T12:13:05-08:00","id":1436255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1436177#post1436177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the book on me right now so I might be completely wrong, but I think that Hedgespinning is the primary way to create both. Trods most often just naturally generate within the Hedge without active interference from changelings (possibly by the Hedge using its usual Hedgespinning rolls when people interact with it) but Hollows are probably primarily created through intentional Hedgespinning. I don't know of any other rules to create either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building a hollow actually isn't in the book so I just wanted to make sure there wasn't a rule I was missing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T11:44:01-08:00","id":1437020,"title":"","content":"Is there anything stopping a changeling from sealing <i>their own</i> words? And if so, is there any detectable sign that a changeling has done so? I'm imagining a changeling who wants to make it clear that they truly mean what they say putting a seal on their words to underline their intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26379-aeshdan","name":"Aeshdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26379_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T13:37:28-08:00","id":1437144,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not clear to me how resolving the Lost Condition in the Hedge works. Suppose I lose the chase to the goblin market and am now Lost. Do I try again to get to the market and resolve Lost if I win, or do I have to do a chase with the goal of \u201cResolve the Lost Condition\u201d first and if I win that one <i>then</i> I can try again to get to the market?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T15:17:08-08:00","id":1437151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437144#post1437144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not clear to me how resolving the Lost Condition in the Hedge works. Suppose I lose the chase to the goblin market and am now Lost. Do I try again to get to the market and resolve Lost if I win, or do I have to do a chase with the goal of \u201cResolve the Lost Condition\u201d first and if I win that one <i>then</i> I can try again to get to the market?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, much as you can't get to a mundane location before successfully navigating to know where you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T15:40:35-08:00","id":1437398,"title":"","content":"Do fetches have any weakness, like Cold Iron?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T16:32:33-08:00","id":1437403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437398#post1437398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do fetches have any weakness, like Cold Iron?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They are functionally nearly-human and many of the limited powers at their disposal only work in the presence of one changeling. The weakness appropriate to the part of the story they're antagonists for is that they're just a person and you're a monster, which tends to tilt the balance in your favor in a straight fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T10:11:55-08:00","id":1437500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437020#post1437020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything stopping a changeling from sealing <i>their own</i> words? And if so, is there any detectable sign that a changeling has done so? I'm imagining a changeling who wants to make it clear that they truly mean what they say putting a seal on their words to underline their intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIU no, they can't.<br /> A changeling can allow another fae creature to seal their words. I don't think they can do so by themselves. If you want to underline your intent, you'd need to find someone and request them to seal you, as a witness to your promise.<br /> <br /> Oaths seem to be thematically more suited for pledges made by yourself. For instance, while it does affect an enemy, you don't need anyone to swear an hostile oath: the Wyrd is the only witness you need. (If you can't swear vengeance on your nemesis by yourself, while holding the body of a murdered loved one, possibly while it's raining, then something's wrong with these rules).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","user":"moonwhisper","date":". 03-01-2021, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T10:22:37-08:00","id":1437502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437500#post1437500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(If you can't swear vengeance on your nemesis by yourself, while holding the body of a murdered loved one, possibly while it's raining, then something's wrong with these rules).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, something's wrong with these rules. All oaths needs to be sworn by all participants. This includes Hostile oaths. The very last sentence in the section mentions that it can be difficult to get someone to agree with Hostile oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T10:25:25-08:00","id":1437503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437500#post1437500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> AFAIU no, they can't.<br /> A changeling can allow another fae creature to seal their words. I don't think they can do so by themselves. If you want to underline your intent, you'd need to find someone and request them to seal you, as a witness to your promise.<br /> <br /> Oaths seem to be thematically more suited for pledges made by yourself. For instance, while it does affect an enemy, you don't need anyone to swear an hostile oath: the Wyrd is the only witness you need. (If you can't swear vengeance on your nemesis by yourself, while holding the body of a murdered loved one, possibly while it's raining, then something's wrong with these rules).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oaths require a physical gesture and are mutual affairs; it doesn't matter that you've sworn enmity toward the one who killed your beloved if you aren't establishing a shared relationship of some kind, because one-sided pledges are sealings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:02:32-08:00","id":1437507,"title":"","content":"Oh, crap. I apologize. I figured it was a mutual agreement for personal and societal oaths, but I missed that was also the case for hostile oaths.<br /> <br /> Am I confusing with the 1st ed. Pledge system?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437502#post1437502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, something's wrong with these rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still stand by my opinion. This is such a classic and dramatic trope, it <i>definitely</i> needs some way to fit in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:19:04-08:00","id":1437510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437507#post1437507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, crap. I apologize. I figured it was a mutual agreement for personal and societal oaths, but I missed that was also the case for hostile oaths.<br /> <br /> Am I confusing with the 1st ed. Pledge system?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are. 1e had one-sided pledges as a system introduced in Rites of Spring, where they still required a witness and pledgecraft granted bonuses beyond the scope of your own holdings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:21:25-08:00","id":1437511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1437507#post1437507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, crap. I apologize. I figured it was a mutual agreement for personal and societal oaths, but I missed that was also the case for hostile oaths.<br /> <br /> Am I confusing with the 1st ed. Pledge system?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I still stand by my opinion. This is such a classic and dramatic trope, it <i>definitely</i> needs some way to fit in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Red Revenge contract could be what you are searching for!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T13:53:53-08:00","id":1438494,"title":"","content":"Can a Changeling harvest Glamour from their own dreams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T13:59:56-08:00","id":1438495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1438494#post1438494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Changeling harvest Glamour from their own dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You can't harvest Glamour from any fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T09:15:30-08:00","id":1439463,"title":"","content":"Just want to double check something I'm pretty sure I already know the answer to<br /> <br /> 2e did away with the Title categories that were introduced in Equinox Road, such as Actors for single entities, Wisps for Titles represented as large, singleminded groups, etc<br /> <br /> In 2e; Gentry can, within the themes of their Title, manifest as a location, group, singular monster or pretty much anything. Except the big important magicsl objects that would have been Prop Tiles in 1e are the manifestations of their Regalia.<br /> <br /> Is this the interpretation of the text everyone else has?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T01:14:37-07:00","id":1440336,"title":"","content":"Elemental Weapon: When you create a weapon that uses ammunition such as a crossbow or a longbow, do you need mundane ammunition for it or does it just generate the ammunition on its own?<br /> <br /> Also, are there stats for a basic bow and arrow, not just a crossbow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T03:42:12-07:00","id":1440351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1440336#post1440336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Weapon: When you create a weapon that uses ammunition such as a crossbow or a longbow, do you need mundane ammunition for it or does it just generate the ammunition on its own?<br /> <br /> Also, are there stats for a basic bow and arrow, not just a crossbow?</div> </div> </div> </div>The<br /> Hurt locker and Dark eras companions<br /> Have normal bows stats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T07:39:34-07:00","id":1440597,"title":"","content":"Can a changeling work iron in a mundane way? One of my players wants to play a wizened smith who forges iron weapons to use against the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T16:03:25-07:00","id":1440657,"title":"","content":"Sure, that\u2019s specifically a common practice for obvious reasons, just remember to wear gloves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T01:36:25-07:00","id":1441038,"title":"","content":"Probably asked before even though my searches didn't turn up anything: What elements can be chosen for the Elemental Seeming? Are you just supposed to stick to the classic 4 (air, earth, fire, water), or do you have to be more specific (metal, crystal, etc), or do you have to be super specific (gold, silver, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T05:58:15-07:00","id":1441066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441038#post1441038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably asked before even though my searches didn't turn up anything: What elements can be chosen for the Elemental Seeming? Are you just supposed to stick to the classic 4 (air, earth, fire, water), or do you have to be more specific (metal, crystal, etc), or do you have to be super specific (gold, silver, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Middle ground. If it's a palpable natural phenomenon with clear visuals, you should be good, but there's no need to stick to any set of classics or subdivision thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T06:15:01-07:00","id":1441068,"title":"","content":"Could one Kidnap an Eidolon/steal a prop from a Bastion? Like could a Hobgoblin, Changeling, or Huntsman walk into a dream and snatch up an item or an eidolon and take it into the hedge or even to Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T06:19:46-07:00","id":1441070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441068#post1441068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could one Kidnap an Eidolon/steal a prop from a Bastion? Like could a Hobgoblin, Changeling, or Huntsman walk into a dream and snatch up an item or an eidolon and take it into the hedge or even to Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending future information, not without special abilities like Goblin Contracts or the Fae's power to forge baubles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T13:53:17-07:00","id":1441123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441066#post1441066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Middle ground. If it's a palpable natural phenomenon with clear visuals, you should be good, but there's no need to stick to any set of classics or subdivision thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm, that really does make certain elements significantly more powerful than others when it comes to the Elemental's Blessing. Air just seems hands down better than anything else. Water would be amazing in a chronicle set at sea, but not as good in a landlocked city. Going with anything more specific, like crystal, just seems pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T14:03:17-07:00","id":1441125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441123#post1441123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hm, that really does make certain elements significantly more powerful than others when it comes to the Elemental's Blessing. Air just seems hands down better than anything else. Water would be amazing in a chronicle set at sea, but not as good in a landlocked city. Going with anything more specific, like crystal, just seems pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d ban Air as an element for precisely that reason. The Blessing is meant to be selectively situational, not so ubiquitous the only situation it isn\u2019t active is by drowning or being in outer space. Wind still is open but requires air currents rather than just standing air.<br /> <br /> As for crystal, it honestly depends on the situation and your creativity. If you\u2019re in an affluent area, jewelry may be a common thing and by doing something as simple as wearing a necklace with a piece of quartz you now can see, hear and touch anyone wearing a piece of jewelry with a gemstone within three yards/meters of you. Water could also work well in a dining situation (how rare is it for someone to have a glass of water near them when they eat a meal), or as a means to overhear things through the plumbing or other drinks that are standing around (or even standing water in the trays under house plants). And, of course, that\u2019s all before you account for supernatural means of affecting the scene\u2019s elemental balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T14:57:47-07:00","id":1441134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441123#post1441123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, that really does make certain elements significantly more powerful than others when it comes to the Elemental's Blessing. Air just seems hands down better than anything else. Water would be amazing in a chronicle set at sea, but not as good in a landlocked city. Going with anything more specific, like crystal, just seems pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441125#post1441125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d ban Air as an element for precisely that reason. The Blessing is meant to be selectively situational, not so ubiquitous the only situation it isn\u2019t active is by drowning or being in outer space. Wind still is open but requires air currents rather than just standing air.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou choose what element you use every time you invoke Elemental Weapon. There are exceedingly few circumstances where you couldn't come up with any other element so banning air only means you're fucking over air elementals from using their Seeming Benefit. If the goal is to force more variety or an effort to use the same element over and over again, just ask the player to try to be a little creative. The player is already incentivised to be more creative because air's going to be hella difficult to combine with the loophole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T15:07:43-07:00","id":1441136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441134#post1441134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bYou choose what element you use every time you invoke Elemental Weapon. There are exceedingly few circumstances where you couldn't come up with any other element so banning air only means you're fucking over air elementals from using their Seeming Benefit. If the goal is to force more variety or an effort to use the same element over and over again, just ask the player to try to be a little creative. The player is already incentivised to be more creative because air's going to be hella difficult to combine with the loophole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except we weren\u2019t discussing Elemental Weapon. We were discussing the Elemental Seeming\u2019s Blessing, the one where if they\u2019re surrounded by or touching their element then they can take mundane actions through that element up to three yards/meters away from them. The reason I would ban Air is because there\u2019s nothing situational about it - unless you\u2019re under water, buried alive or in outer space, you\u2019re always going to be touched/surrounded by air. That\u2019s severely unbalanced compared to other elements, even something like Earth/Stone, Water or Wood/Plants, because these ones are more situational in when they\u2019d be viable/accessible. Notably, the situations I mentioned beforehand are ones where unless you have provisions where you still have air, you\u2019d <i>die</i>, so having Air as your element simply has no recourse to balance it without a life or death situation. Wind, meanwhile, requires setup or weather conditions to be productive.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t see where having Air makes Elemental Weapon difficult when you can still throw it around with fans, clothes or somesuch to catch it and move it around like Wind would allow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441038#post1441038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably asked before even though my searches didn't turn up anything: What elements can be chosen for the Elemental Seeming? Are you just supposed to stick to the classic 4 (air, earth, fire, water), or do you have to be more specific (metal, crystal, etc), or do you have to be super specific (gold, silver, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T15:20:26-07:00","id":1441138,"title":"","content":"My bad. (characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T16:03:20-07:00","id":1441146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441038#post1441038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably asked before even though my searches didn't turn up anything: What elements can be chosen for the Elemental Seeming? Are you just supposed to stick to the classic 4 (air, earth, fire, water), or do you have to be more specific (metal, crystal, etc), or do you have to be super specific (gold, silver, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can choose anything that makes sense for your character have been turned into as long as it's not iron. Music, cold, light, fire, wood, gold, all are fair game.<br /> <br /> You could probably even choose something more abstract like &quot;love&quot; or &quot;hunger,&quot; but those are going to be more difficult to get benefit from as an Elemental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T08:32:05-07:00","id":1441249,"title":"","content":"Air on its own can't be felt by beings without special senses, but Heavy Wind can be felt pushing and pulling at you. It is a noticable force.<br /> <br /> Another possibility: Scents.<br /> <br /> A grody, slimy Elemental that can manipulate air only when its suffused with the smell of rot and noxious chemicals<br /> <br /> A melting Ambergris woman who can manipulate through perfumed air<br /> <br /> Etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-24-2021, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T09:02:44-07:00","id":1441252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441249#post1441249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air on its own can't be felt by beings without special senses,</div> </div> </div> </div>Inhale through your nose. You don't feel the smell of the air? Inhale through your mouth over your tongue. You don't taste the air? Wave your arm back and forth. You don't feel the drag of air against your skin? Technically you also feel the pressure of air on you as well as the air's temperature. You can even see air (through optical mechanisms that differ from almost everything else we can see but still) though only over long distances so not as relevant in this context. Submerge one hand in water and keep one hand in the air, and you can feel the difference in the textures.<br /> <br /> While both your senses and your brain are calibrated to ignore most sensory input from air, you can absolutely sense it, and focusing properly on those senses does allow you to experience that stimuli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T21:18:44-07:00","id":1441853,"title":"","content":"What means do Changelings have to see through supernatural concealment like Light-Shy(or Obfuscate from Vampire or whatever else)?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Solstice Revelation and Goblin's Eye, but am I missing anything?<br /> <br /> Are there any additional means available to Hobs, Huntsmen, or True Fae?<br /> <br /> Half my group has Light-Shy and I want them to get good use out of it, so I'm making people who know Goblin's Eye very rare, but I'm wondering if there are any other obvious means of triggering a Clash of Wills over it that I'm missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T21:39:50-07:00","id":1441854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441853#post1441853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What means do Changelings have to see through supernatural concealment like Light-Shy(or Obfuscate from Vampire or whatever else)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending new Arcadian Contracts in a later supplement, Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts that do that. Also, iron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there any additional means available to Hobs, Huntsmen, or True Fae? </div> </div> </div>Same deal, with especial note for Huntsmen using iron often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Half my group has Light-Shy and I want them to get good use out of it, so I'm making people who know Goblin's Eye very rare, but I'm wondering if there are any other obvious means of triggering a Clash of Wills over it that I'm missing. </div> </div> </div>Not in a game where most of the playable characters have good reason to be paranoid about otherworldly spies and the entire metaphysic they deal with is assumed to get at problems sideways most of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T22:18:08-07:00","id":1441857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441854#post1441854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pending new Arcadian Contracts in a later supplement, Court Contracts and Goblin Contracts that do that. Also, iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm real curious how you'd use iron to pierce invisibility powers - sure, I get that if you secure a piece of iron to someone they might not be able to hide with a Contract (or maybe they can hide, but the iron will still be visible...), but if they're already hidden...how would you tag them with the iron in the first place?<br /> <br /> It <i>does</i> make me wonder if carrying iron would prevent you from using Light-Shy at all, or if like you'd turn invisible but those shotgun shells loaded with iron in your pocket would still be visible floating in mid-air...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T23:23:16-07:00","id":1441862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441857#post1441857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm real curious how you'd use iron to pierce invisibility powers - sure, I get that if you secure a piece of iron to someone they might not be able to hide with a Contract (or maybe they can hide, but the iron will still be visible...), but if they're already hidden...how would you tag them with the iron in the first place?<br /> <br /> It <i>does</i> make me wonder if carrying iron would prevent you from using Light-Shy at all, or if like you'd turn invisible but those shotgun shells loaded with iron in your pocket would still be visible floating in mid-air...</div> </div> </div> </div>You can toss iron powder in a room.<br /> If there is someone concealed, the iron that comes in contact with him would still be visible and you would see a standing man shaped iron cloud","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T16:26:29-07:00","id":1442442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441857#post1441857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm real curious how you'd use iron to pierce invisibility powers - sure, I get that if you secure a piece of iron to someone they might not be able to hide with a Contract (or maybe they can hide, but the iron will still be visible...), but if they're already hidden...how would you tag them with the iron in the first place?<br /> <br /> It <i>does</i> make me wonder if carrying iron would prevent you from using Light-Shy at all, or if like you'd turn invisible but those shotgun shells loaded with iron in your pocket would still be visible floating in mid-air...</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as the iron you carry is covered by something else, I guess it'd work, since there would be no way for its presence to reach your senses in the first place (Light-Shy edits the Changeling out from everyone else's senses, it doesn't make the Changeling see-through). But if the iron is on the outside, it wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> Tossing iron powder seems like a good tactic. Depending on how &quot;fairy tale logic&quot; you want to go, perhaps looking through a loop of (cold?) iron might also do the trick. Depends on the level of buy in at your table, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 04-02-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T17:25:33-07:00","id":1442445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1441857#post1441857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm real curious how you'd use iron to pierce invisibility powers [\u2026] if they're already hidden...how would you tag them with the iron in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frames for glasses or windows. Horseshoes over doorways and other thresholds. Daubed in a paste under or over your eyes. Placed as sheeting in front of something you'd expect to see a shadow cross.<br /> <br /> The book specifically says to favor iron piercing fae magic or otherwise being immune to it. There's a wealth of literature to draw from for methodology here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T21:52:41-07:00","id":1442582,"title":"","content":"Do other Fae creatures with Glamour - for example Hobgoblins, Huntsmen, and True Fae - have the ability to escape bonds and grapples by spending Glamour the way Changelings do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T04:12:03-07:00","id":1442596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1442582#post1442582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do other Fae creatures with Glamour - for example Hobgoblins, Huntsmen, and True Fae - have the ability to escape bonds and grapples by spending Glamour the way Changelings do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's a changeling specific ability. Some people even house rule that loyalists who didn't escape Arcadia don't have that ability (or, at least, there's rumours about it in their settings).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T10:47:27-07:00","id":1442620,"title":"","content":"I've never seen it explictily stated they can't do that but it just makes sense that only Changelings. Honestly, since it's all part of the same ability, I would rule at my table that only escapee Changelings can turn any doorway into a Hedge Gate. Everyone else has to find natural ones, even True Fae.<br /> <br /> That said, do you think a Huntsman could shapeshift out of a grapple by taking on bigger or smaller forms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T11:21:36-07:00","id":1442623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1442620#post1442620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, do you think a Huntsman could shapeshift out of a grapple by taking on bigger or smaller forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's a grapple rather than just restrains, then spending an action on shapeshifting means you don't spend an action grappling, making it child's play for the opponent to just do their next grappling move (which could be reapplying Hold or Restrain if the ST thinks the new shape requires new holds to pin down). The exception being if the resulting form is too large or too small to grapple with, in which case the grapple would end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T07:43:03-07:00","id":1442970,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifting isn\u2019t a grapple move in the first place, you do it reflexively or you don\u2019t do it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T19:41:16-07:00","id":1443075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1442970#post1442970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting isn\u2019t a grapple move in the first place, you do it reflexively or you don\u2019t do it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know that's how grappling works RAW but it seems odd to disallow shape changing because someone is holding you. Like, Tam Lin is a pretty famous fairy tale with a signficant part of the story being about holding onto a shape changer. See also, Proteus, literal namesake of Protean. More generally I don't think grappling was written to account for magic abilities that don't require freedom of movement to enact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T20:52:47-07:00","id":1443080,"title":"","content":"You\u2019d think that but this is the very gameline that <i>re</i>wrote grappling to be <i>more</i> explicit that that\u2019s how it works. I don\u2019t entirely get it either but there it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T01:04:43-07:00","id":1443095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443080#post1443080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019d think that but this is the very gameline that <i>re</i>wrote grappling to be <i>more</i> explicit that that\u2019s how it works. I don\u2019t entirely get it either but there it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what they were going for with Changeling's more explicit grapple rules, but RAW it's very silly. There are tonnes of cases in Changeling and other gamelines where it makes sense for characters to be able to take instant actions even though they're grappled. My houserule is that you can take any instant actions while grappled that logically make sense (shapeshifting and various powers that don't require the use of your arms) however doing so happens on your initiative and deprives you of your roll to contest the grapple that turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T14:16:04-07:00","id":1443803,"title":"","content":"How do the alternative Courts work? When does a Monarch reign?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s pretty easy for the Seasonal Courts, right? Three month cycle, reigns end. But when does the Queen of Coin from the Traders Courts reign?<br /> <br /> Does the Dragon Court (Morning, Day, Night Courts) cycle through monarchs three times during the course of a day? I don\u2019t see any indication but perhaps I\u2019m missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T15:30:49-07:00","id":1443806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443803#post1443803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the alternative Courts work? When does a Monarch reign?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s pretty easy for the Seasonal Courts, right? Three month cycle, reigns end. But when does the Queen of Coin from the Traders Courts reign?<br /> <br /> Does the Dragon Court (Morning, Day, Night Courts) cycle through monarchs three times during the course of a day? I don\u2019t see any indication but perhaps I\u2019m missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Freehold has its own system for how to transition between Courts. Seasonal Courts have a pretty self-explanatory cycle for determining which Court should be the next, but exactly when the transition happens is still up for the Freehold to decide. It could be at specific dates, or it could be decided by committee or by an election to allow for choosing the time that works best for such a transition.<br /> Freeholds without cyclical transitions also have to decide in which order the Courts take power, but it's the same thing there; it can be by committee, by general election (either for the Courts at large or for individual candidates for the Crown), through a tournament or other type of contest, by drawing straws or other ways of using random chance, by consulting an oracle (or maybe just whoever is the next to walk through that doorway), etc.<br /> Edit: Even cyclical Court structures could have some leeway in how they run things. For example, if the rules of a Freehold with the four Seasonal Courts allow it, they could potentially skip a season if that particular Court doesn't have a candidate for being monarch or if the actual season isn't particularly prominent (meteorologically speaking) in that region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-13-2021, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:47:06-07:00","id":1443841,"title":"","content":"Searching here too; is there any mention of some fae creature that embodies a City, Town, etc, be it canon or homebrew, 1E or 2E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:55:17-07:00","id":1443842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443841#post1443841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Searching here too; is there any mention of some fae creature that embodies a City, Town, etc, be it canon or homebrew, 1E or 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e? Only in the generalized sense that True Fae can be locations courtesy of Realms being a type of Manifestation.<br /> <br /> In 2e? The Deep Caves is a hobgoblin that is either a cave system or a hobgoblin so massive it can convincingly masquerade as one, and otherwise there's just a few snippets here and there about Goblin Queens.<br /> <br /> It's kind of outside Changeling's usual wheelhouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:58:04-07:00","id":1443843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443842#post1443842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e? Only in the generalized sense that True Fae can be locations courtesy of Realms being a type of Manifestation.<br /> <br /> In 2e? The Deep Caves is a hobgoblin that is either a cave system or a hobgoblin so massive it can convincingly masquerade as one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So nothing about urbane environments in particular, outside of weirder Gentries and possible Court patrons? Anyways, I'll go and read about Deep Caves. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T22:33:20-07:00","id":1443845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443843#post1443843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So nothing about urbane environments in particular, outside of weirder Gentries and possible Court patrons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble there is that Court patrons are specifically not fae \u2014 a Bargain works on more or less the same principles as a bargain \u2014 so the most probable source of fae things &quot;embodying&quot; that sort of phenomenon is going to be the knock-on effects of a changeling striking a Bargain with such a thing and prompting mythic backsplash into the local Hedge, which are chiefly going to be Hedge ghosts or changeling Court Avatars who've hit Clarity 0.<br /> <br /> The general capricious/pastoralist vibe of a lot of Changeling's material tends to mesh poorly with the concept outside of the more general the-king-and-the-land-are-one stuff common to many territorial freeholds or the particular cases of Courts sworn to a regional phenomenon \u2014 most conventional fae stuff limits its &quot;civilized&quot; interaction to grand balls and manor estates at the upper end and more typically houses and dens.<br /> <br /> Is this for a particular purpose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T22:42:12-07:00","id":1443846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443845#post1443845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trouble there is that Court patrons are specifically not fae \u2014 a Bargain works on more or less the same principles as a bargain \u2014 so the most probable source of fae things &quot;embodying&quot; that sort of phenomenon is going to be the knock-on effects of a changeling striking a Bargain with such a thing and prompting mythic backsplash into the local Hedge, which are chiefly going to be Hedge ghosts or changeling Court Avatars who've hit Clarity 0.<br /> <br /> The general capricious/pastoralist vibe of a lot of Changeling's material tends to mesh poorly with the concept outside of the more general the-king-and-the-land-are-one stuff common to many territorial freeholds or the particular cases of Courts sworn to a regional phenomenon \u2014 most conventional fae stuff limits its &quot;civilized&quot; interaction to grand balls and manor estates at the upper end and more typically houses and dens.<br /> <br /> Is this for a particular purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the 1E writeup for the House of Ariadne from Mage has this mentions of city-gods. They\u2019re Time- and Fate-mages, so I was wondering...<br /> <br /> EDIT: And looks I need to really get down and read Changeling 2E stuff <i>thoroughly</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T01:52:47-07:00","id":1443858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443841#post1443841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Searching here too; is there any mention of some fae creature that embodies a City, Town, etc, be it canon or homebrew, 1E or 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e: True Fae can manifest in the form of locations. Two examples given is a &quot;sky citadel&quot; and a &quot;filthy high rise&quot;. The literal meaning of citadel is small city, i.e. the small part of a city that's protected by fortifications. As such, a small town is definitely possible, and there's really nothing that says a Name or a Title can't take the form of an even larger location like a full city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T01:58:14-07:00","id":1443859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443858#post1443858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e: True Fae can manifest in the form of locations. Two examples given is a &quot;sky citadel&quot; and a &quot;filthy high rise&quot;. The literal meaning of citadel is small city, i.e. the small part of a city that's protected by fortifications. As such, a small town is definitely possible, and there's really nothing that says a Name or a Title can't take the form of an even larger location like a full city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gotcha. Hmm... looks like a True Fae can masquerade as the &quot;will of the city&quot; after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T07:12:58-07:00","id":1443874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443859#post1443859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha. Hmm... looks like a True Fae can masquerade as the &quot;will of the city&quot; after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that:<br /> <br /> 1) The filthy high-rise is reproduced verbatim from the True Fae material in 1e's Equinox Road, where Realm forms are limited to Arcadia and are considered by Fae to be a dull but necessary use of their resources, much like they don't enjoy taking the Prop forms whose 2e equivalent is imprisonment in their Regalia (the Actor is the most commonly-encountered Manifestation for a reason)<br /> 2) True Fae in the mortal world suffer Glamour addiction, have frailties and sensory cues that accompany each Title, which makes Realm-equivalent shapeshifting a bit of a poor fit for a mortal city, and<br /> 3) the entire deal with the &quot;City Gods&quot; sidebar in Legacies: the Sublime concerns a phenomenon so subtle that many mages doubt it even exists.<br /> <br /> If anything, I'd look to Mummy's Lifeweb or Demon's Infrastructure for that particular facet of the House of Ariadne's metaphysics; Changeling's extended cast trends a lot more specifically otherworldly than can be found rooted to a metropolis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T16:35:10-07:00","id":1443949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1443874#post1443874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that:<br /> <br /> 1) The filthy high-rise is reproduced verbatim from the True Fae material in 1e's Equinox Road, where Realm forms are limited to Arcadia and are considered by Fae to be a dull but necessary use of their resources, much like they don't enjoy taking the Prop forms whose 2e equivalent is imprisonment in their Regalia (the Actor is the most commonly-encountered Manifestation for a reason)<br /> 2) True Fae in the mortal world suffer Glamour addiction, have frailties and sensory cues that accompany each Title, which makes Realm-equivalent shapeshifting a bit of a poor fit for a mortal city, and<br /> 3) the entire deal with the &quot;City Gods&quot; sidebar in Legacies: the Sublime concerns a phenomenon so subtle that many mages doubt it even exists.<br /> <br /> If anything, I'd look to Mummy's Lifeweb or Demon's Infrastructure for that particular facet of the House of Ariadne's metaphysics; Changeling's extended cast trends a lot more specifically otherworldly than can be found rooted to a metropolis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T21:03:35-07:00","id":1444436,"title":"","content":"I was reading about Empty changelings. They return when they die from damage. But do they die from old age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T21:39:13-07:00","id":1444441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1444436#post1444436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading about Empty changelings. They return when they die from damage. But do they die from old age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling life being what it is I'd say that the priority there rates about the same as it does for werewolves (old age is the <i>last</i> thing you have to worry about when the Wild Hunt is part of your life), but incentive structure being what it is for raising Wyrd I'd say yes \u2014 stretching out your number for another two decades is a simple matter of diving deeper into fae magic and maybe tracking down a blazon for a suitably ageless entitlement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:22:36-07:00","id":1444446,"title":"","content":"The real problem was not to die from old age, but to become ageless. Even if little by little, age weakens the body and makes you suceptible to be captured again. But I know that not aging is a double edge sword, because you will be forever hunted by the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:42:59-07:00","id":1444448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1444446#post1444446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real problem was not to die from old age, but to become ageless. Even if little by little, age weakens the body and makes you suceptible to be captured again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings have always specifically had reductions to the weakening of old age as a scaling benefit of their Wyrd rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T13:57:50-07:00","id":1444543,"title":"","content":"Question on fetches: do they have bodily fluids? --I mean, specifically the important ones that would enable procreation on one hand and blood specifically on the other?<br /> <br /> My initial answer to this is &quot;it depends on what the fetch is made of&quot;, but there may be another. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> (Addendum: if they lack such fluids, then concealing their existence as made-up things seems like it could get... challenging.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:53:20-07:00","id":1444553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1444543#post1444543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on fetches: do they have bodily fluids? --I mean, specifically the important ones that would enable procreation on one hand and blood specifically on the other?<br /> <br /> My initial answer to this is &quot;it depends on what the fetch is made of&quot;, but there may be another. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> (Addendum: if they lack such fluids, then concealing their existence as made-up things seems like it could get... challenging.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption has always been that fetches look and work exactly like a human right up until the point that they die. People would notice pretty quickly if they stopped eating or stopped using the bathroom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T15:31:26-07:00","id":1444556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1444553#post1444553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My assumption has always been that fetches look and work exactly like a human right up until the point that they die. People would notice pretty quickly if they stopped eating or stopped using the bathroom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mask is the normal mortal tendency to brush weird shit under the rug turned up to eleven. The Mask is real for mortals. The go-to example of a fetch &quot;putting on their glasses&quot; in the morning actually sewing on their button-eyes illustrates the phenomenon pretty cleanly.<br /> <br /> As far as ninety-nine percent of the world is concerned, a fetch operates like a normal human being. The times where it doesn't (and supernatural senses aren't involved) tend to be a wrinkle with individual people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T01:23:12-07:00","id":1444609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1444543#post1444543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on fetches: do they have bodily fluids? --I mean, specifically the important ones that would enable procreation on one hand and blood specifically on the other?<br /> <br /> My initial answer to this is &quot;it depends on what the fetch is made of&quot;, but there may be another. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> (Addendum: if they lack such fluids, then concealing their existence as made-up things seems like it could get... challenging.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetches have a specific flaw as per their five questions. I'd just assume that they're otherwise functionally human as their disguise is so good even the fetch tends to be fooled by it. That's way more powerful than the Mask of changelings that changelings themselves can't percieve without making an effort. Which is fitting since they were specifically created by some of the setting's most powerful creatures to blend in with humans.<br /> What a fetch is made of is stated to factor into their personalities, but it doesn't inform anything about their bodies. A scaled up doll can still chew and swallow food even though their mouth is literally sewn or painted on their face, and a dead wolf stuffed with rocks still only deals -1B if they were to bite anyone with their fanged jaws (unless they have something like Lethal Mien to represent their jaws as an advantage). Just look at the fetch on page 232 (whose human guise really looks like John Noble to me even though it's barely visible); there's no way he could fake <i>any</i> biological functions if taken at face value. It's obvious that his disguise is majorly backed up because even he should be possible to be fooled (and you're not tricked into thinking you're a human if you're incapable of ingesting any non-liquid food, and having liquids mostly just soaking your cloth skin).<br /> <br /> You can always add more flaws in their disguise than the one question if you want, but it's not necessary or assumed by the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-19-2021, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T11:38:13-07:00","id":1444693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1444609#post1444609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetches have a specific flaw as per their five questions. I'd just assume that they're otherwise functionally human as their disguise is so good even the fetch tends to be fooled by it. That's way more powerful than the Mask of changelings that changelings themselves can't percieve without making an effort. Which is fitting since they were specifically created by some of the setting's most powerful creatures to blend in with humans.<br /> What a fetch is made of is stated to factor into their personalities, but it doesn't inform anything about their bodies. A scaled up doll can still chew and swallow food even though their mouth is literally sewn or painted on their face, and a dead wolf stuffed with rocks still only deals -1B if they were to bite anyone with their fanged jaws (unless they have something like Lethal Mien to represent their jaws as an advantage). Just look at the fetch on page 232 (whose human guise really looks like John Noble to me even though it's barely visible); there's no way he could fake <i>any</i> biological functions if taken at face value. It's obvious that his disguise is majorly backed up because even he should be possible to be fooled (and you're not tricked into thinking you're a human if you're incapable of ingesting any non-liquid food, and having liquids mostly just soaking your cloth skin).<br /> <br /> You can always add more flaws in their disguise than the one question if you want, but it's not necessary or assumed by the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Tessie--appreciate the point back to their flaw per the questions. I just skimmed that and will re-read.<br /> <br /> It all &quot;makes sense&quot; I suppose if you consider reality as less actuality and more a conduit for cause (will to action) and effect (result). In that sense the Wyrd acts as the bridge between want and fulfillment, and whatever passes for the spirits of observers can see that which makes them comfortable.<br /> <br /> Thus, fetches (and changelings, with perhaps more trouble) can bear children more or less normally, &quot;bleed&quot;, eat, etc. Right up to the point that they &quot;die&quot; and the Wyrd contract that sustains their illusion is satisfied.<br /> <br /> <b>Addendum: </b>Oh ok, now I know where some of my confusion came from--the section in <i>Seven Wonders</i> on the fetch, in which the author emphasized their inhumanity with phrases such as &quot;Did a hunter see you cut yourself and not bleed?&quot; and the entire &quot;What are you made of&quot; paragraph. In fact it appears the author is very fixed on the physical nature of the fetch as a created being--which is fine when they are held up as similar enough to Promethians to partake of their journey, but perhaps not entirely accurate to all fetches.... Obviously if your 5 question flaw is &quot;I bleed sand&quot;, then said sand is not going to serve the same purpose as blood for anyone else. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  Seven Wonders addendum 04-20-2021, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:16:41-07:00","id":1445878,"title":"","content":"How does the Flickering Hours contract actually work? What does it do exactly? What does it look like to other characters when they run into someone under the effect of the Contract? Does it have any effect on chases outside of the Fleet of Foot merit and the edge? If so, what effect does it have? If not, why not, it specifically points out being able to use it on people chasing you so it feels like it should? Yet there is no listed chase effect for having your time slowed, only one for having it sped up.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that speeding yourself up by a factor of 2 while slowing someone else down by a factor of 2 doesn't mean you get four times the actions they do should you somehow get into contact with them. But it's very unclear what the Contract actually does. It seems to try to limit itself to chases without clearly explaining what it actually accomplishes, but I'm having a hard time seeing how being quickened (if it's really related to time and not pathfinding) wouldn't have diverse other benefits.<br /> <br /> &quot;anyone quickened also gains...&quot; =&gt; are the quickened people those for whom time passes twice as fast, or those for whom time has been slowed by half? Assuming the Contract has no effect on what you can accomplish in a &quot;turn&quot;, having time go half as fast for you means you can get twice as many things done right? So then you are &quot;quickened&quot;? That sounds like it makes sense to me, but it's hard to read the author's intent since they used &quot;twice as quickly&quot; in the preceding sentence, which evokes a sort of link with the word &quot;quickened&quot;, casting doubt on my conclusion.<br /> <br /> If you had several people in a group, and you chose to speed up time for some of them and slow it down for others, could they continue to travel together normally without noticing anything, or is one part of the group speeding away at 4 times the speed of the other part then? If so, that is not sufficiently covered mechanically with just the rather weak fleet of foot merit and the edge right? If not, why not, what does having your time sped up actually <i>do</i> then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 04-25-2021, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T23:35:17-07:00","id":1445936,"title":"","content":"I'd assume that Speed gets doubled or halved, but then it wouldn't make sense to apply Fleet of Foot which also modifies Speed. And since Speed is likely not directly affected, it's really weird that there are zero mechanical effects for those who are slowed.<br /> Other than Fleet of Foot and always having the Edge, the only thing I can think of is having timed stuff (such as intervals between rolls in extended actions) take twice as long or be half as short, and having any worn clocks be desynchronised. That's really underwhelming for a Royal Contract. At least the mechanical benefits for quickened characters also apply in Hedge navigation, but unless I was Wyrd 3+ I'd prefer spending 3 XP on Fleet of Foot than 3-4 XP on this Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T07:35:45-07:00","id":1445967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1445878#post1445878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what does having your time sped up actually <i>do</i> then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effects that scale over time scale faster. This includes healing, fatigue, and poison, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T08:14:35-07:00","id":1445972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1445967#post1445967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Effects that scale over time scale faster. This includes healing, fatigue, and poison, among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's only personal time, and unlinked from &quot;world time&quot;? If you're travelling somewhere and use it on yourself, you can't use it to get there faster than you normally would?<br /> <br /> (As an aside, it'd be ironic if it turns out the main use for/most potent use of a Contract that keeps speaking of journeys is to be staying in place to heal faster. xD)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T09:40:39-07:00","id":1445981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1445972#post1445972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's only personal time, and unlinked from &amp;quot;world time&amp;quot;? If you're travelling somewhere and use it on yourself, you can't use it to get there faster than you normally would?</div> </div> </div> </div>It only works in the Hedge, where navigating to macro-scale destinations within an intended time window is accomplished by beating the Hedge and other competition in a Chase in which one to three extra pips of Speed can make it marginally easier for you to succeed, especially with the Edge. That <i>is</i> getting there faster than you normally would, as long as getting there fast is your intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T15:29:06-07:00","id":1445996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1445981#post1445981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only works in the Hedge, where navigating to macro-scale destinations within an intended time window is accomplished by beating the Hedge and other competition in a Chase in which one to three extra pips of Speed can make it marginally easier for you to succeed, especially with the Edge. That <i>is</i> getting there faster than you normally would, as long as getting there fast is your intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it sounds like those mechanics are pretty detached from the explanation of &quot;speeding up or slowing down time&quot;, doesn't it? It just doesn't mesh very well. By that explanation, slowing the group down has no effect on how fast you get there, since the Edge/amount of successes required stays the same, and you're hanging the entire &quot;speed of travel&quot; part off of that mechanical aspect.<br /> <br /> Considering the fact that there's rules written for how to break free of the Contract if you're unwilling, it sounds like there should be a significant detrimental aspect to it when used against you, but so far we haven't really been able to identify what that is, exactly.<br /> <br /> What happens when a group of Changelings travel together, and we apply the Contract only to a few of them? Or we apply opposing sides of the Contract within the same group? Can they still travel together, or not? What does it look like to the Changelings involved in these various different cases? What does it feel like to be one of the Changelings affected by the Contract or not, in that scenario? How would you describe it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T18:42:40-07:00","id":1446013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1445996#post1445996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it sounds like those mechanics are pretty detached from the explanation of &quot;speeding up or slowing down time&quot;, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Slow or speed the passage of time [\u2026] for any of the targets individually.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the 2e version of a Contract specifically built for its effects on the speed at which time passes.* Travel buffs are a bonus; the main distinctions 2e's version of Flickering Hours has are that you can apply speeding and slowing effects to different people (though the rate change is limited to a factor of two) and it no longer ends as soon as any target leaves the Hedge.<br /> <br /> * &quot;This Contract is an excellent way to pass time quickly or to retreat to the Hedge to sleep, heal, or find time to finish an important project in an unnaturally short amount of time.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens when a group of Changelings travel together, and we apply the Contract only to a few of them? Or we apply opposing sides of the Contract within the same group? Can they still travel together, or not? What does it look like to the Changelings involved in these various different cases? What does it feel like to be one of the Changelings affected by the Contract or not, in that scenario? How would you describe it? </div> </div> </div>The passage of time on those characters changes the way it does for the duration of the Contract, which lasts until sundown or sunup or until they leave the Hedge. It is a long-term effect that is there to make scheduling weirdness happen on purpose through the environment of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-26-2021, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:52:06-07:00","id":1446075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446013#post1446013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Slow or speed the passage of time [\u2026] for any of the targets individually.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the 2e version of a Contract specifically built for its effects on the speed at which time passes.* Travel buffs are a bonus; the main distinctions 2e's version of Flickering Hours has are that you can apply speeding and slowing effects to different people (though the rate change is limited to a factor of two) and it no longer ends as soon as any target leaves the Hedge.<br /> <br /> * &quot;This Contract is an excellent way to pass time quickly or to retreat to the Hedge to sleep, heal, or find time to finish an important project in an unnaturally short amount of time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how this is an answer to the question of whether or not the &quot;flavour&quot; actually fits the mechanical repercussions?<br /> <br /> I guess the main question that remains with that is whether or not that is underwhelming for a Royal Contract, and I might agree with Tessie that it is.<br /> <br /> If it cuts in half extended actions, it should cut in half the time it takes to navigate to somewhere, too. As that is nothing but essentially a contest of extended actions in the Hedge. Yet, it doesn't for some odd reason. And if you let it do it, there's also a lot of oddities there, what with people chasing you having any chance to catch you at all when you're essentially arriving twice as fast. It's a pretty confusing Contract overall, and &quot;Well, Hedge weird!&quot; only goes so far. The ways through which the Hedge does things don't need to be explained, but what effect it has on our end state kinda does, as does the way our characters experience that change... since we'll be moving our characters through that change towards the end state. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The passage of time on those characters changes the way it does for the duration of the Contract, which lasts until sundown or sunup or until they leave the Hedge. It is a long-term effect that is there to make scheduling weirdness happen on purpose through the environment of the Hedge. </div> </div> </div>This answer is a very abbreviated statement of Contract intent (which I had caught already; the generics are clear, the <i>specifics</i> aren't), but it doesn't answer any of the detailed questions I have... It certainly doesn't answer the questions it is quoting.<br /> <br /> Which is fine, of course, you're not forced to answer any questions or anything, but we'll just end up at &quot;Ok, thanks, but I'll wait for someone to answer the questions asked&quot; at this rate. ^^<br /> <br /> Specifically, out of those quoted, these have not been answered:<br /> - What happens when a group of Changelings travel together, and we apply the Contract only to a few of them? Or we apply opposing sides of the Contract within the same group?<br /> - Can they still travel together, or not?<br /> - New question: in case they <i>can't</i> for some reason, does that answer change if we tie them together with rope? What if we tie them together with chains of iron running between them?<br /> - What does it <i>look</i> like to the Changelings involved in these various different cases? What does it <i>feel</i> like to be one of the Changelings affected by the Contract or not, in that scenario? How would you <i>describe</i> it?<br /> <br /> It's all fine to decide it finishes Extended Actions twice as fast as normal, but in my head I need a reason why that wouldn't also be speeding you up in cases of combat or chases (more than it is now, since Edge and Fleet of Foot are not going to be an x2 modifier...) that can be explained and described from a character-facing perspective.<br /> <br /> So not pure mechanics or actual wording, but how would it feel to characters, look to them... if a few Autumn courtiers study the terms of the Contract and its precise effects, how do <i>they</i> word what it can and can't do, etc... ?<br /> That sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 04-27-2021, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T06:21:30-07:00","id":1446096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446075#post1446075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- What happens when a group of Changelings travel together, and we apply the Contract only to a few of them? Or we apply opposing sides of the Contract within the same group?<br /> - Can they still travel together, or not?<br /> - New question: in case they <i>can't</i> for some reason, does that answer change if we tie them together with rope? What if we tie them together with chains of iron running between them?<br /> - What does it <i>look</i> like to the Changelings involved in these various different cases? What does it <i>feel</i> like to be one of the Changelings affected by the Contract or not, in that scenario? How would you <i>describe</i> it?<br /> <br /> It's all fine to decide it finishes Extended Actions twice as fast as normal, but in my head I need a reason why that wouldn't also be speeding you up in cases of combat or chases (more than it is now, since Edge and Fleet of Foot are not going to be an x2 modifier...) that can be explained and described from a character-facing perspective.<br /> <br /> So not pure mechanics or actual wording, but how would it feel to characters, look to them... if a few Autumn courtiers study the terms of the Contract and its precise effects, how do <i>they</i> word what it can and can't do, etc... ?<br /> That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>About chases, I can see the people on normal speed or halved speed catching up to the people with double speed, because of shortcuts or things like that. Since the people with double speed will have the Edge on chases, it probably will be difficult at best to catch them, but not outright impossible.<br /> <br /> The problem arrives when the &quot;blue hedgehog&quot; ones get caught in the chase. Because even when they lose the chase, they are still fast. Powers that give more actions are way too strong on a system like this, but since they always have the Edge, after being ambushed(per chase rules), I would say that at least they'll always act first in combat. If their enemies are also slowed, I would say that they can't apply defense against the ones that are with double speed. But all of that are houserules.<br /> <br /> For me, your question raised valid points that should have a little more mechanical bulk. The flavor text in the mechanical setup does not deliver. The major problem being this phrase:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Until the sun next crosses the horizon, anyone quickened <u><b>also</b></u> gains the Fleet of Foot Merit, with effective dots equal to the changeling\u2019s Wyrd up to three, and always has the Edge in a chase. </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Since it says also, the quickened status should be a Condition or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-27-2021, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T08:27:23-07:00","id":1446102,"title":"","content":"The Autumn's Fury Contract (p.156) inflicts the Heavy Rain and Heavy Winds Tilts. What rating should the Heavy Winds Tilt have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T09:37:54-07:00","id":1446112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446102#post1446102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Autumn's Fury Contract (p.156) inflicts the Heavy Rain and Heavy Winds Tilts. What rating should the Heavy Winds Tilt have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since there's no activation roll, I'd go with Mantle rating","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T18:41:46-07:00","id":1446208,"title":"","content":"Re: Flickering Hours, it may not say that it <i>does</i> double or halve Speed but it also doesn\u2019t say that it <i>doesn\u2019t</i> and I\u2019d expect that it does unless told otherwise. And if it does then that\u2019s a better chance than not of giving both the Hedge and everyone you don\u2019t like +3 required successes to catch you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T21:34:47-07:00","id":1446218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446075#post1446075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it cuts in half extended actions, it should cut in half the time it takes to navigate to somewhere, too. As that is nothing but essentially a contest of extended actions in the Hedge. Yet, it doesn't for some odd reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will repeat: Hedge travel takes an arbitrary length of time. Making it go faster is accomplished by making it easier to accomplish your intent of getting somewhere fast by increasing your Speed a bit and giving you the Edge in the chase. There is no actual way to make it go faster otherwise, because there is no base speed to increase for a Hedge chase. You get somewhere quicker by being more likely to succeed at trying to get somewhere quickly, and if that means running down a trod at what hindsight will clock at thirty miles an hour then nobody will notice it in the moment unless they've got some sort of sense for temporal weirdness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you let it do it, there's also a lot of oddities there, what with people chasing you having any chance to catch you at all when you're essentially arriving twice as fast. It's a pretty confusing Contract overall, and &quot;Well, Hedge weird!&quot; only goes so far. The ways through which the Hedge does things don't need to be explained, but what effect it has on our end state kinda does, as does the way our characters experience that change... since we'll be moving our characters through that change towards the end state. :P </div> </div> </div>It changes the passage of time. The primary effect of the Contract is its effect on the passage of time. Your ability to walk faster is negligible because it is affecting your personal time and that interacts with the Hedge in the way that interacts with any psychoactive space. This isn't Celerity, it's being able to spend what felt like ten minutes talking at the Goblin Market and come back to find that a whole night has passed. It's Arcadian Metabolism as a generalized toggle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is fine, of course, you're not forced to answer any questions or anything, but we'll just end up at &quot;Ok, thanks, but I'll wait for someone to answer the questions asked&quot; at this rate. ^^ </div> </div> </div>You're asking questions that don't have textual answers, which amounts to an opinion check. Nobody in this thread can help you find answers that don't exist; this is all interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Specifically, out of those quoted, these have not been answered:<br /> - What happens when a group of Changelings travel together, and we apply the Contract only to a few of them? Or we apply opposing sides of the Contract within the same group?<br /> - Can they still travel together, or not?<br /> - What does it <i>look</i> like to the Changelings involved in these various different cases? What does it <i>feel</i> like to be one of the Changelings affected by the Contract or not, in that scenario? How would you <i>describe</i> it? </div> </div> </div>They can certainly travel together. Nothing unusual happens, unless you're keeping track over a long enough time to see changes like fatigue or healing come into play, at which point you have an incongruity to observe but not much else. If they split up they may find that more happens to one set of them than the other before they regroup, but again, that's a long-term oddity. Maybe some characters feel ill \u2014 that sort of flavoring is part of what the book is getting at when it tells you to personalize the feel of your character's Contracts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So not pure mechanics or actual wording, but how would it feel to characters, look to them... if a few Autumn courtiers study the terms of the Contract and its precise effects, how do <i>they</i> word what it can and can't do, etc... ?<br /> That sort of thing. </div> </div> </div>Shorter equivalents of Rip Van Winkle's infamous outing. Skewed day/night cycles. People getting tired from a relatively small amount of running or failing to notice that the seconds take longer to pass. It is easy to overlook if you're not paying attention to it, because it happens in reality in smaller chunks throughout a normal day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446096#post1446096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it says also, the quickened status should be a Condition or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been rightly observed before that not everything with mechanics has to be or should be a Condition \u2014 &quot;any effect that progresses over time does so at half or twice the rate, ending when the target leaves the Hedge or the sun goes down or comes up, and they don't get a Beat for either of those things&quot; firmly shifts Flickering Hours onto the &quot;not&quot; end of the scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T12:25:19-07:00","id":1446314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446218#post1446218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're asking questions that don't have textual answers, which amounts to an opinion check. Nobody in this thread can help you find answers that don't exist; this is all interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like I knew there would be no answers when I asked, though! ;D<br /> <br /> I like to approach things like this from the perspective of writing clear rules that are easily understood by new players, and will make smooth transitions between different tables and groups easy. In the end I can always rule things however I like for my table. That's a foregone conclusion. I just wasn't sure if this Contract was really as wildly unclear and confusing as I thought, or if it was just me.<br /> <br /> Considering the responses, I think it's fair to say it's not me. ^^ People can't even say for sure what it does to <i>Speed</i>, a simple, hard mechanics question. :P<br /> <br /> I don't agree with your conclusions, but it's essentially clear that if I want a better defined Contract I'll just have to rewrite it myself, so that is Question Answered as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has been rightly observed before that not everything with mechanics has to be or should be a Condition \u2014 &quot;any effect that progresses over time does so at half or twice the rate, ending when the target leaves the Hedge or the sun goes down or comes up, and they don't get a Beat for either of those things&quot; firmly shifts Flickering Hours onto the &quot;not&quot; end of the scale. </div> </div> </div>It could be a Tilt, though. They say tilts &quot;can&quot; easily causes Conditions outside of action scenes, but not that they must. They also say: &quot;Personal Tilts only apply to one character and include ways in which that character can overcome the effect.&quot; Well, the Contract includes a way for individual characters to overcome the effect placed upon them, and the effect is placed on individuals, not on a location or anything. So it could easily be a Tilt.<br /> They suggest not using Tilts outside of action scenes, but to use Conditions instead... but people use Tilts like Heavy Winds in scenes where we're not going by turn order (so, not an action scene) all the time, so that's a pretty arbitrary thing.<br /> <br /> In the end Tilts are really just shorthand for a collection of different rules effects that you want to be able to easily reference with just a few lines of text without having to type it all out again.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it makes sense to make this a Tilt thus basically comes down to whether you're going to use this same Tilt in other places or not. If you'll only use it once, might as well be in the Contract. As soon as it's two or more times... sure, make it a Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 04-28-2021, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T13:51:30-07:00","id":1446491,"title":"","content":"Hi to all!<br /> Hobgoblins and the Gentry can visit the human world? And they also have a mask just like the changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T14:39:38-07:00","id":1446494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446491#post1446491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi to all!<br /> Hobgoblins and the Gentry can visit the human world? And they also have a mask just like the changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can enter the world, yes. This usually imposes Conditions on them that make it unpleasant for them to stay for very long, but they can indeed do so. Huntsmen in particular frequently head Ironsides to capture their quarries.<br /> <br /> They generally have Masks, too, but those Masks usually have a Tell -- some strange feature that marks them as &quot;off,&quot; if not downright supernatural. (I personally like use Demon Glitches as Tells, but that's just a personal thing). The Masks may or may not be humanoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T15:00:17-07:00","id":1446500,"title":"","content":"So... maybe a hobgoblin pixie can mask herself as a little sparrow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T23:16:05-07:00","id":1446564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446500#post1446500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... maybe a hobgoblin pixie can mask herself as a little sparrow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a weird little sparrow with very expressive bright green eyes and long curled feathers.<br /> He likes to sit on a tree behind the window when you are watching your favourite TV show.<br /> You could swear that sometimes he laugh at the jokes, with a very human pitch, but that s impossible, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T03:17:08-07:00","id":1446578,"title":"","content":"The helldiver kith states:<br /> &quot;Once she completely fades, she acts like a dematerialized Hedge ghost (p. 249), unable to physically interact with anything except other immate-rial beings and objects, such as Hedge ghosts, other Helldivers, changelings using the Whis-pers of Morning Contract (p. 143), the unquiet dead, and spirits of all stripes. She can see and interact with all of these, no matter their current state.&quot;<br /> It s safe to assume that the last statement could be translated with &quot;no matter their current manifestation conditions?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T06:19:37-07:00","id":1446591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446578#post1446578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The helldiver kith states:<br /> &quot;Once she completely fades, she acts like a dematerialized Hedge ghost (p. 249), unable to physically interact with anything except other immate-rial beings and objects, such as Hedge ghosts, other Helldivers, changelings using the Whis-pers of Morning Contract (p. 143), the unquiet dead, and spirits of all stripes. She can see and interact with all of these, no matter their current state.&quot;<br /> It s safe to assume that the last statement could be translated with &quot;no matter their current manifestation conditions?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Manifestation Conditions start from &quot;the being is in the immaterial state of Twilight,&quot; yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T07:54:08-07:00","id":1446600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446591#post1446591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Manifestation Conditions start from &amp;quot;the being is in the immaterial state of Twilight,&amp;quot; yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that s very important, because it would imply that helldivers could interact even with materialized or claimed entity while diving, is it correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T08:32:08-07:00","id":1446607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446600#post1446600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that s very important, because it would imply that helldivers could interact even with materialized or claimed entity while diving, is it correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T08:38:43-07:00","id":1446609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446607#post1446607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except everything that's in an immaterial state like Twilight or Dematerialised Hedge Ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T09:08:48-07:00","id":1446613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446607#post1446607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But an Helldiver is immaterial while diving, so it s strange to think that he could interact with a materialized ephemeral being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:06:44-07:00","id":1446622,"title":"","content":"The phrase does begin with &quot;other immaterial beings and objects, such as,&quot; implying the assumption that the list that follow describes beings that are immaterial. A materialized being isn't immaterial.<br /> <br /> It's clumsily written, though. (And reminds me of my personal bugbear that the whole thing would be both clearer and simpler if hedge ghosts and helldivers were just described as occupying their own fae &quot;frequency&quot; of Twilight, with a stripped-down barebones treatment of manifestations, rather than defining a new state of immateriality that behaves <i>almost</i> the same. Grumpo grump shakes fist at cloud)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:31:52-07:00","id":1446697,"title":"","content":"<i>Everything</i> to do with Hedge ghosts and eidolons is I Can\u2019t Believe It\u2019s Not An Ephemeral Entity and it drives me nuts just wondering <i>why</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:30:57-07:00","id":1446762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446622#post1446622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's clumsily written, though. (And reminds me of my personal bugbear that the whole thing would be both clearer and simpler if hedge ghosts and helldivers were just described as occupying their own fae &amp;quot;frequency&amp;quot; of Twilight, with a stripped-down barebones treatment of manifestations, rather than defining a new state of immateriality that behaves <i>almost</i> the same. Grumpo grump shakes fist at cloud)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446697#post1446697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Everything</i> to do with Hedge ghosts and eidolons is I Can\u2019t Believe It\u2019s Not An Ephemeral Entity and it drives me nuts just wondering <i>why</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's enough text spent on explaining their new non-Twilight intangible/invisible state <i>and</i> that it is different from actual Twilight that there's no way they could've saved wordcount compared to just saying that they're in Twilight, have no other Manifestations (like Goetia/Dreamborn in MtA/BPG) and have an incorporality Numen that replicates the effects of Twilight in the Hedge, and then have Helldivers and Whispers of Morning just referencing this.<br /> <br /> And even if it's for some reason important that they're not ephemeral entities, it still doesn't explain why they would have to invent a new type of intangible/invisible state that doesn't interact with Twilight when 1.) different &quot;frequencies&quot; of Twilight already doesn't interact with each other so it's literally identical in all but name (and the extremely rare effects that affect all Twilight frequencies*), and 2.) already established that even non-ephemeral beings can naturally be in a state of Twilight: See Quashmallim from PtC.<br /> <br /> *And out of the three examples I know of that affect all Twilight frequencies, there's only one of them (Ephemeral Enchantment from MtA) that also wouldn't work on Hedge Ghosts as they are right now because Pseshkf from VtR deals damage to everything that is noncorporeal (which naturally includes Hedge Ghosts) and Helldivers who also interact with everything that is immaterial with Hedge Ghosts being specifically mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T04:29:34-07:00","id":1446774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446762#post1446762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And there's enough text spent on explaining their new non-Twilight intangible/invisible state <i>and</i> that it is different from actual Twilight that there's no way they could've saved wordcount compared to just saying that they're in Twilight, have no other Manifestations (like Goetia/Dreamborn in MtA/BPG) and have an incorporality Numen that replicates the effects of Twilight in the Hedge, and then have Helldivers and Whispers of Morning just referencing this.<br /> <br /> And even if it's for some reason important that they're not ephemeral entities, it still doesn't explain why they would have to invent a new type of intangible/invisible state that doesn't interact with Twilight when 1.) different &amp;quot;frequencies&amp;quot; of Twilight already doesn't interact with each other so it's literally identical in all but name (and the extremely rare effects that affect all Twilight frequencies*), and 2.) already established that even non-ephemeral beings can naturally be in a state of Twilight: See Quashmallim from PtC.<br /> <br /> *And out of the three examples I know of that affect all Twilight frequencies, there's only one of them (Ephemeral Enchantment from MtA) that also wouldn't work on Hedge Ghosts as they are right now because Pseshkf from VtR deals damage to everything that is noncorporeal (which naturally includes Hedge Ghosts) and Helldivers who also interact with everything that is immaterial with Hedge Ghosts being specifically mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then... who thinks that diving Helldivers are able to interact with Materialized ephemeral being?<br /> If yes, how it is supposed to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:02:31-07:00","id":1446780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446774#post1446774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then... who thinks that diving Helldivers are able to interact with Materialized ephemeral being?<br /> If yes, how it is supposed to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text isn't great. It clearly says that Helldivers can interact with Hedge Ghosts and ephemeral entities regardless of whether they're using Dematerialize, are in Twilight, are physically present in the Hedge or uses Materialize, but I think it's much more likely that the writer intended that Helldivers can interact with all other intangible beings <i>regardless of why they are intangible</i>. (Much like how Pseshkf doesn't care why you're incorporeal; it's gonna hurt regardless if you're in Twilight or a physically present Strix made of shadowy smoke.)<br /> <br /> Basically, the Helldiver can interact with all Twilight frequencies and the non-Twilight frequency of Dematerialized Hedge Ghosts and Whispers of Morning users, but not Hedge Ghosts that <i>aren't</i> Dematerialized or ephemeral entities that aren't in Twilight (i.e. if they're Materialized, or in the Hedge or other realm where there is no Twilight).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446762#post1446762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if it's for some reason important that they're not ephemeral entities, it still doesn't explain why they would have to invent a new type of intangible/invisible state that doesn't interact with Twilight when 1.) different &quot;frequencies&quot; of Twilight already doesn't interact with each other so it's literally identical in all but name (and the extremely rare effects that affect all Twilight frequencies*), and 2.) already established that even non-ephemeral beings can naturally be in a state of Twilight: See Quashmallim from PtC.</div> </div> </div> </div>A small correction: Changelings using the Whispers of Morning Contract act identical to how beings in Twilight act; they can interact with each other and other incorporeal fae beings and objects, but not anything physical or anything in other frequencies of Twilight. The text even outright says that users of Whispers of Morning &quot;<b>exists on a different frequency than creatures in Twilight</b>&quot;, which is how the fandom has described Twilight <i>for years</i>.<br /> <br /> But Hedge Ghosts using Dematerialize can't even interact with other Hedge Ghosts. That is indeed different from how Twilight works, but between Helldivers, Whispers of Morning and Hedge Ghosts, we've got <i>three types of intangibility that each works differently from the rest and interacts differently from the rest</i>.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Dematerialized Hedge Ghosts can't interact with anything physical, anything in Twilight, or anything that is incorporeal for other reasons including other Dematerialized Hedge Ghosts, except for Whispers of Morning users and Diving Helldivers.<br /> \u2022 Whispers of Morning users can't interact with anything physical, anything in Twilight, but can interact with every fae being and object that is incorporeal including other Whispers of Morning users, except for Diving Helldivers if they wish to not be visible and interactive.<br /> \u2022 Diving Helldivers can't interact with anything physical, but they can interact with everything in Twilight and everything that is incorporeal for other reasons including other Diving Helldivers, and can freely choose not to be visible and interactive specifically to Whispers of Morning users.<br /> <br /> It's a clusterfuck that didn't need to exist if they just used the game-agnostic framework for incorporeal beings that specifically exists to easily model incorporeal beings rather than coming up with unique rules that are specific only to this game for seemingly no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:45:14-07:00","id":1446830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446780#post1446780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a clusterfuck that didn't need to exist if they just used the game-agnostic framework for incorporeal beings that specifically exists to easily model incorporeal beings rather than coming up with unique rules that are specific only to this game for seemingly no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I keep running into places in Changeling 2nd edition where it felt like the book was a battleground between contributers who were maybe immersed in Changeling lore but only kinda skimmed the Chronicles of Darkness rules and didn't care for the unified mechanics much, vs others who were very invested in updating Changeling to use CofD rules.<br /> <br /> Lots of things I love about Changeling 2nd edition, but it does feel like it needed another draft to iron out some of this stuff that feels less like really smart intentional design choices and more like &quot;eh, this is what our freelancer gave us, I don't have time to integrate it as well as I'd like.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:12:23-07:00","id":1446860,"title":"","content":"Shuffling all of the incorporeal fae to Dream/Astral/Mind Twilight sounds like a reasonable houserule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:39:46-07:00","id":1446863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446860#post1446860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shuffling all of the incorporeal fae to Dream/Astral/Mind Twilight sounds like a reasonable houserule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a Faerie Twilight would be more consistent with how things work now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:01:45-07:00","id":1446866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446863#post1446863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having a Faerie Twilight would be more consistent with how things work now.</div> </div> </div> </div>On second thought, that\u2019s better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:48:44-07:00","id":1446978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446830#post1446830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I keep running into places in Changeling 2nd edition where it felt like the book was a battleground between contributers who were maybe immersed in Changeling lore but only kinda skimmed the Chronicles of Darkness rules and didn't care for the unified mechanics much, vs others who were very invested in updating Changeling to use CofD rules.<br /> <br /> Lots of things I love about Changeling 2nd edition, but it does feel like it needed another draft to iron out some of this stuff that feels less like really smart intentional design choices and more like &quot;eh, this is what our freelancer gave us, I don't have time to integrate it as well as I'd like.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the rather infamous development issues of C:tL 2e, this doesn't surprise me in the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:09:22-07:00","id":1447041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1446978#post1446978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the rather infamous development issues of C:tL 2e, this doesn't surprise me in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now I'm curious - what were the infamous development issues? I was kind of out of the fandom when it was coming out, so wasn't paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:21:17-07:00","id":1447044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1447041#post1447041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm curious - what were the infamous development issues? I was kind of out of the fandom when it was coming out, so wasn't paying attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the former lead dev of CtL left in protest after White Wolf/Paradox (don't quite remember how it was all structured back then, but anyway it's the owner of the Chronicles of Darkness license) hired someone who had harassed people online, including the former lead dev. Because she quit, the entire manuscript (which had already been sent out in previews to Kickstarter backers) was scrapped and CtL 2e rebuilt from scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:23:28-07:00","id":1447059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1447044#post1447044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, the former lead dev of CtL left in protest after White Wolf/Paradox (don't quite remember how it was all structured back then, but anyway it's the owner of the Chronicles of Darkness license) hired someone who had harassed people online, including the former lead dev. Because she quit, the entire manuscript (which had already been sent out in previews to Kickstarter backers) was scrapped and CtL 2e rebuilt from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was before the Kickstarter even started; Liv just put out pieces of the mechanics for playtest on the forums in the process of open development. Bits that weren't previewed definitely existed (I know this because I had to sign NDAs to read them), but all of the changes between those playtest documents and the compiled manuscript were made by the time the Kickstarter had previews ready. By Kelly's estimate, about a third of the content from the Underhill version carried forward into the final product.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah, this is the gist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T11:55:47-07:00","id":1447610,"title":"","content":"The Chatelaine Kith blessing, does it just automatically give you knowledge of all a character's social merits? Or do you choose based on what you assume (or know) they have? Just curious about that unmentioned part of the mechanic.<br /> <br /> For Reference<br /> <br /> *<b>Will That Be All?:</b>* Spend a point of Glamour to activate this blessing for the scene. With a successful Manipulation + Socialize roll, a Chatelaine may use the Social Merits of one other character in the scene as though they were her own. When the effect ends, characters act as though the target had used the Merits himself<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T18:15:21-07:00","id":1447676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1447610#post1447610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chatelaine Kith blessing, does it just automatically give you knowledge of all a character's social merits? Or do you choose based on what you assume (or know) they have? Just curious about that unmentioned part of the mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T10:35:00-07:00","id":1448143,"title":"","content":"Perhaps not a simple question, but how much do you think your average group of Changelings know about how the Huntsmen work?<br /> <br /> Like if you find out you're being hunted by a Huntsman and ask around the Freehold, do you think you're gonna be able to find out &quot;oh yeah, they're pretty nasty - not affected by iron, come back from the dead, etc - but they have a missing heart so if you can somehow find the bastion it is hidden in and go in you might be able to get an oath out of them&quot;?<br /> <br /> It seems like such information is intended to be a kind of &quot;mysterious secret about the setting&quot; thing, but I imagine your average Freehold has dealt with a <i>lot</i> of Huntsmen over the years. Many of those Huntsmen probably were successful and whisked away their targets, but if any of them were stopped it is probably because someone figured out the hidden heart thing. And I'd think, upon finding out that information, they'd probably want to pass that toe very Changeling who'd listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T23:09:05-07:00","id":1448200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448143#post1448143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps not a simple question, but how much do you think your average group of Changelings know about how the Huntsmen work?<br /> <br /> Like if you find out you're being hunted by a Huntsman and ask around the Freehold, do you think you're gonna be able to find out &amp;quot;oh yeah, they're pretty nasty - not affected by iron, come back from the dead, etc - but they have a missing heart so if you can somehow find the bastion it is hidden in and go in you might be able to get an oath out of them&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> It seems like such information is intended to be a kind of &amp;quot;mysterious secret about the setting&amp;quot; thing, but I imagine your average Freehold has dealt with a <i>lot</i> of Huntsmen over the years. Many of those Huntsmen probably were successful and whisked away their targets, but if any of them were stopped it is probably because someone figured out the hidden heart thing. And I'd think, upon finding out that information, they'd probably want to pass that toe very Changeling who'd listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably depends on how much old a freehold is.<br /> Also, even if changeling are supposed to share such kind of informations, nothing says that they must be free of charge....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T10:43:18-07:00","id":1448239,"title":"","content":"Might be just me, but I'm pretty sure I wouldn't trust any info I ever got for free from anyone if I became a Changeling. Only stuff I traded fairly for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T11:28:36-07:00","id":1448244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448239#post1448239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be just me, but I'm pretty sure I wouldn't trust any info I ever got for free from anyone if I became a Changeling. Only stuff I traded fairly for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, you re probably right!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T12:07:39-07:00","id":1448250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448239#post1448239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be just me, but I'm pretty sure I wouldn't trust any info I ever got for free from anyone if I became a Changeling. Only stuff I traded fairly for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always tend to presume within a Freehold that there's a fair bit of mutual assistance going on, at least when it comes to threats coming from the Gentry. But I guess not everyone plays it that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T18:32:32-07:00","id":1448278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448250#post1448250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always tend to presume within a Freehold that there's a fair bit of mutual assistance going on, at least when it comes to threats coming from the Gentry. But I guess not everyone plays it that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh there's plenty of mutual assistance. But it has to be mutual. You never let someone do something for you without working out an explicit repayment. But it's all part of the Freehold Pledges. You get the protection so long as you play your part. Part of it is just me irl seeing everything as being transactional on some level. If I became a Changeling, I would just stop trusting &quot;I get endorphins from feeling like I did good&quot; as a reason for people to do stuff for me. I'd be terrified of being in non-specific debt to anyone for too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-11-2021, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T06:37:12-07:00","id":1448499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448278#post1448278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh there's plenty of mutual assistance. But it has to be mutual. You never let someone do something for you without working out an explicit repayment. But it's all part of the Freehold Pledges. You get the protection so long as you play your part. Part of it is just me irl seeing everything as being transactional on some level. If I became a Changeling, I would just stop trusting &quot;I get endorphins from feeling like I did good&quot; as a reason for people to do stuff for me. I'd be terrified of being in non-specific debt to anyone for too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense, as it is explicitly spelled out that if you don't put a correct &quot;price&quot; on things, Wyrd may settle the debt, usually in a way nobody likes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T01:43:45-07:00","id":1448571,"title":"","content":"While I'm asking about Huntsmen - anyone want to Explain To Me Like I'm Five how the returning the Heart thing works? I find this section in the rule book very confusing:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is their secret: to anchor them and allow them to manifest fully in the mortal world as creatures of Wyrd and flesh, the True Fae must hide the heart of a Huntsman within a Bastion. For months, even years, alien emotions plague some mortal\u2019s sleep, thoughts of hunting in some dark and deep wood. A Huntsman can borrow some of the Gentry\u2019s talent for oneiromancy and Hedge shaping, but they are forever blind to the Bastion that holds their heart \u2014 the one thing they cannot track down even with all their cunning, no matter how earnest their hidden longing.<br /> <br /> Only in the Hedge can a changeling sway the Huntsman from their mission, if temporarily. The Huntsman\u2019s natural inclination for order clashes with the obsessive excitement of the changeling\u2019s proximity to Arcadia and the fulfillment of the Keeper\u2019s heart that beats within. The Lost can see, and feel, this tension \u2014 it crackles like fatigue, electricity behind their eyes, from a dark cloud above the Hedge\u2019s canopy. If the changeling can convince or trick the Huntsman into letting her find the Bastion where their heart waits, escape becomes possible. Within the Bastion, a changeling may swear an oath (p. 212) with the Huntsman, heart to heart, if they\u2019re willing; but the changeling must overcome the Fae\u2019s desires that spill out from within in a battle of wits or will. As a Wyrd-witnessed declaration of true feeling, the oath allows the Huntsman to express their own desires once more, asserting their own needs and wants over the Keeper\u2019s and wresting back control of their fate for a short while \u2014 for the scene, no longer. Once that time is over, the Fae\u2019s desires return to the fore, but the oath remains.<br /> <br /> Finally returned, the Huntsman\u2019s heart can expunge the Keeper\u2019s Title, though even then the oath is still intact \u2014 presuming the heart can found within the tempestuous mortal Bastion. What a motley will do with the purest, powerless representation of their tormentor is anyone\u2019s guess. Letting the verderer live is dangerous, of course, because an oath broken hurts the changeling just as much as it does the Huntsman, and an oath is forever. The sworn are irreversibly connected, for good or for ill. But killing them alerts the True Fae as surely as a road flare, and paves the way for a<br /> new, unknown adversary to take the Huntsman\u2019s place. </div> </div> </div>So, the Changeling first has to find the Heart - presumably by either tricking or persuading the Huntsman somehow into leading them to it but in the paragraph above it says Huntsmen can never ever find the Bastion their heart is in so.... I guess they somehow have to find it completely on their own? Okay, good luck with that, but I guess that's straightforwardish...<br /> <br /> Once they find the heart, the Changeling can swear and oath with the Huntsman if they're both willing... Presumably the Changeling can communicate with the Huntsmen through their hearts or something, 'cause the Huntsman isn't going to be in the Bastion they can never find, right? Or do you gotta lead the Huntsman <i>to</i> their heart?<br /> <br /> I don't know what you might do to convince the Huntsman to swear, but presumably you leverage their remaining Aspiration in some fashion. I guess that's simple enough, even if often difficult.<br /> <br /> But then must they &quot;overcome the Fae's desires that spill out from within in a battle of wits or will&quot; - what the hell does <i>that</i> mean? Does it mean the Title emerges from the Huntsman and must be battled? Or does it just mean the Title tries to assert itself over the Huntsman and the Changeling has to somehow convince the Huntsman to resist or something?<br /> <br /> Okay, but if you manage all that then swearing an Oath the Huntsman gets a scene free of the Keeper's control. That's straightforward.<br /> <br /> Does &quot;finally returned&quot; in the last paragraph... I do not know the role of that phrase in this paragraph. I initially read it as a continuation of the above paragraph in a &quot;Now that the heart has been finally returned...&quot; way. But maybe it actually is more &quot;Finally, if return the Huntsman's heart can expunge the Keeper's Title?&quot; It just makes things more confusing.<br /> <br /> Presumably since it is an <i>Oath</i>, not a Pledge, the Oath must indeed be like either a personal oath of friendship or the like, or a hostile oath of emnity. &quot;I give you your heart back, you stop hunting me&quot; is a Pledge, not an Oath. So that's why swearing the Oath is dangerous because it sticks around...<br /> <br /> I dunno, I feel I almost understand what's being expressed in this package but the language around it keeps spinning me in circles when I go back and re-read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T17:55:45-07:00","id":1448733,"title":"","content":"Swearing the oath gives the huntsman one scene of free will with which to help you search the bastion for its heart. Finding and handing over the heart frees it for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T07:07:19-07:00","id":1448774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448733#post1448733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swearing the oath gives the huntsman one scene of free will with which to help you search the bastion for its heart. Finding and handing over the heart frees it for good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought in order to swear the oath, they had to be within the Bastion and swear the oath &quot;heart to heart&quot; - presumably in front of the Huntsman's heart - in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T07:40:26-07:00","id":1448777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448774#post1448774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought in order to swear the oath, they had to be within the Bastion and swear the oath &quot;heart to heart&quot; - presumably in front of the Huntsman's heart - in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space is weird in the Hedge and especially in dreams. The heart is in the Bastion \u2014 and its presence there is enough to have a persistent effect on its owner's dreams. If the changeling and the Huntsman are both in the Bastion as well, then they are close enough for an agreement to be come to \u2014 the Huntsman is still its own being even without its heart, as evidenced by the fact that it can swear oaths in other contexts with consequences less onerous than the Fae would face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T08:09:05-07:00","id":1448780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448777#post1448777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space is weird in the Hedge and especially in dreams. The heart is in the Bastion \u2014 and its presence there is enough to have a persistent effect on its owner's dreams. If the changeling and the Huntsman are both in the Bastion as well, then they are close enough for an agreement to be come to \u2014 the Huntsman is still its own being even without its heart, as evidenced by the fact that it can swear oaths in other contexts with consequences less onerous than the Fae would face.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would seem, though, that the most common scenario would be to end up in the Bastion without the Huntsman present - since the Huntsman <i>cannot</i> find the Bastion, pretty much the only way they're getting in that Bastion is if you're leading them in there.<br /> <br /> So why would any bother leading a Huntsman into the Bastion just so you could swear the Oath with them? When, instead, you could just head into the Bastion yourself in order to find the Heart so you can return it? That's part of what I'm not getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T23:35:56-07:00","id":1448835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448780#post1448780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It would seem, though, that the most common scenario would be to end up in the Bastion without the Huntsman present - since the Huntsman <i>cannot</i> find the Bastion, pretty much the only way they're getting in that Bastion is if you're leading them in there.<br /> <br /> So why would any bother leading a Huntsman into the Bastion just so you could swear the Oath with them? When, instead, you could just head into the Bastion yourself in order to find the Heart so you can return it? That's part of what I'm not getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because in most cases the changeling has been captured by the huntsman.<br /> I think that the typical scenario is:<br /> The changeling is dragged in the hedges.<br /> Huntsman sighs.<br /> &quot;What z up man?&quot;<br /> &quot;I miss my heart&quot;<br /> &quot;I ll find it for you if you release me&quot;<br /> &quot;You think i m a moron?&quot;<br /> &quot;Let s go toghether then, if i fail you can still bring me to the evil queen&quot;<br /> &quot;Seems legit&quot;<br /> The changeling finds the Bastion and leads the Huntsman there<br /> &quot;Passing the f...ing DRAGONS watching the heart could be a little troublesome with my hands cuffed, could you release me now, PLEASE?&quot;<br /> &quot;OK but only if we swear an oath&quot;<br /> &quot;Seems legit&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 05-18-2021, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T07:20:15-07:00","id":1448856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1448835#post1448835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because in most cases the changeling has been captured by the huntsman.<br /> I think that the typical scenario is:<br /> The changeling is dragged in the hedges.<br /> Huntsman sighs.<br /> &quot;What z up man?&quot;<br /> &quot;I miss my heart&quot;<br /> &quot;I ll find it for you if you release me&quot;<br /> &quot;You think i m a moron?&quot;<br /> &quot;Let s go toghether then, if i fail you can still bring me to the evil queen&quot;<br /> &quot;Seems legit&quot;<br /> The changeling finds the Bastion and leads the Huntsman there<br /> &quot;Passing the f...ing DRAGONS watching the heart could be a little troublesome with my hands cuffed, could you release me now, PLEASE?&quot;<br /> &quot;OK but only if we swear an oath&quot;<br /> &quot;Seems legit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahhhhh! That is a scenario that finally makes things seem plausible to me. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T01:17:27-07:00","id":1449174,"title":"","content":"Do Fetches have Touchstones?<br /> <br /> By looking at the Fetch creation process it would seem so, since it's the same as the Changeling one &quot;unless otherwise noted&quot; and for Touchstones I couldn't find it noted otherwise.<br /> <br /> However, rules-wise Touchstones interact with Clarity, which the Fetches don't have since they have Integrity.<br /> From a narrative point of view, it wouldn't make much sense for those Fetches who don't know (yet) what they are and see themselves as human.<br /> <br /> For Storyteller controlled characters it may not matter much, but it may be relevant if you want to play one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T03:26:40-07:00","id":1449179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1449174#post1449174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Fetches have Touchstones?<br /> <br /> By looking at the Fetch creation process it would seem so, since it's the same as the Changeling one &quot;unless otherwise noted&quot; and for Touchstones I couldn't find it noted otherwise.<br /> <br /> However, rules-wise Touchstones interact with Clarity, which the Fetches don't have since they have Integrity.<br /> From a narrative point of view, it wouldn't make much sense for those Fetches who don't know (yet) what they are and see themselves as human.<br /> <br /> For Storyteller controlled characters it may not matter much, but it may be relevant if you want to play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones interact with a Changeling's Clarity, they are inherently a part of the Clarity system. Since Fetches have Integrity, I'd take that to mean Fetches do not have Touchstones since those are not part of the Integrity system and would play no role for them. In essence, saying &quot;Fetches have Integrity, not Clarity.&quot; already includes &quot;and therefore, do not have those things associated with Clarity, either&quot;. They don't get Perception bonuses/penalties based on Clarity either, nor can they use Kenning.<br /> <br /> Fetches also do not need to to touch base with their human side since... they don't really have one, they are and have always been what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 05-21-2021, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T09:29:38-07:00","id":1452004,"title":"","content":"What is the power of the Tilt generated by Elemental Fury?<br /> Like, Heavy winds 1 is very different from Heavy winds 5. If there is any offical ruling on this I would like to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T08:30:07-07:00","id":1452167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1452004#post1452004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the power of the Tilt generated by Elemental Fury?<br /> Like, Heavy winds 1 is very different from Heavy winds 5. If there is any offical ruling on this I would like to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know of any official ruling, but given the wording of Elemental Fury and the effects of most of the other Tilts in CtL, I would rule that the Tilts are either only at the lowest level, or that they increase in power as you spend Glamour to increase the Tilt's size","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T07:55:26-07:00","id":1452629,"title":"","content":"On the contract &quot;Glimpse of a Distant Mirror&quot;, &quot;the changeling looks into any reflective surface, which becomes a window that looks out through another such surface that has reflected his face before.&quot;<br /> <br /> What is the limitations for this contract? Like, If I have a viral TikTok video and thousands of people use their cellphones to see my image, thus, having my image reflected into their Eyeballs, does those count as &quot;reflective surface&quot;? Even if this is a huge stretch, let's say someone watched me close to a mirror, does this mirror count? Do I need to know the surface that reflected me, or can I just ask the mirror to show me all the places where I was reflected last night?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:57:56-07:00","id":1452639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1452629#post1452629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the contract &quot;Glimpse of a Distant Mirror&quot;, &quot;the changeling looks into any reflective surface, which becomes a window that looks out through another such surface that has reflected his face before.&quot;<br /> <br /> What is the limitations for this contract? Like, If I have a viral TikTok video and thousands of people use their cellphones to see my image, thus, having my image reflected into their Eyeballs, does those count as &quot;reflective surface&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, screens <i>project</i> images and video. Only in a metaphorical sense can they be said to reflect what happened by playing a recording.<br /> Since a literal reading is also the simplest, I think it's most likely also the intended reading: The Contract should be limited to literally reflective surfaces, such as mirrors, polished metal objects, objects made of glass, and pools of reflective liquids (though should the liquid be sufficiently disturbed as to stop being reflective, I would count that as a new surface rather than the same).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if this is a huge stretch, let's say someone watched me close to a mirror, does this mirror count? </div> </div> </div>If a mirror has reflected your face, then your face has been reflected in the mirror. Whether someone saw you reflected or close to a mirror is pretty irrelevant in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do I need to know the surface that reflected me, or can I just ask the mirror to show me all the places where I was reflected last night? </div> </div> </div>The Contract doesn't actually state anything about how the end point is chosen, so I'm assuming the changeling chooses one. Since you can only choose one end point per activation of the Contract, you can't do the second part of your question.<br /> However, the Beast Seeming Benefit highly implies you don't need to identify a specific mirror. Choosing a mirror &quot;close to me when I was at XXX last night&quot; should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:09:58-07:00","id":1453156,"title":"","content":"Can non-fae things have Court Goodwill. I know changelings, fetches, fae-touched, and presumably, hobs can have Court Goodwill. But can for example Demons, Minor Templates, Sin-Eaters, and so on get the merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T10:46:05-07:00","id":1453658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1453156#post1453156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can non-fae things have Court Goodwill. I know changelings, fetches, fae-touched, and presumably, hobs can have Court Goodwill. But can for example Demons, Minor Templates, Sin-Eaters, and so on get the merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but they wouldn't be able to get anything related to it like Mantle, Contracts, etc... That being the case, just give them Status instead, since it'll end up being the exact same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T11:21:37-07:00","id":1453660,"title":"","content":"The advanced Beast merits are Beast exclusively, or a Changeling could pick Advanced Striking Looks and things like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T20:53:58-07:00","id":1453680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1453660#post1453660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advanced Beast merits are Beast exclusively, or a Changeling could pick Advanced Striking Looks and things like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think there was official wording on them\u2026 but I\u2019d allow them, and not just for changelings too. But the ones whose lore mentions Beast-specific stuff will need to be altered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T22:51:17-07:00","id":1453683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1453660#post1453660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advanced Beast merits are Beast exclusively, or a Changeling could pick Advanced Striking Looks and things like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the Merit section in Beast:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the prerequisites list \u201cBeast,\u201d it\u2019s only available to Beast characters. A Hero could not have that Merit, for example. At Storyteller discretion, other supernatural characters in your game may purchase some of these Merits to reflect their kinship with the Primordial.<br /> <br /> If a Merit lists being \u201cAdvanced\u201d or \u201cEpic,\u201d it\u2019s a supernatural extension of a mundane Merit. This requires the mundane version of the Merit to be purchased first. Most such Merits require your character to be a Beast, but that\u2019s noted in their prerequisites. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T04:43:24-07:00","id":1453915,"title":"","content":"I'm a it confused by how seeing the Mask/Mien of other Changelings works all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> The attuned to the Wyrd echo for fetches says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fetches see changelings\u2019 miens as well as their mortal guises, in much the same way that other changelings do </div> </div> </div>Implying they see both at once?<br /> <br /> But the section on Mask/Mien says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A changeling can spend a Glamour to see another changeling\u2019s Mask instead of her mien for a few seconds. </div> </div> </div>So... is the Fetch part just implying the rules are the same for both (so both need to spend a glamour to see the Mask of a changeling), or are Fetches supposed to see both at once and is there an inconsistency in here somehow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T05:42:21-07:00","id":1453923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1453915#post1453915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... is the Fetch part just implying the rules are the same for both (so both need to spend a glamour to see the Mask of a changeling), or are Fetches supposed to see both at once and is there an inconsistency in here somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetches recognize other changelings the same way changelings recognize each other, meaning that if a changeling strenghted her mask, she would not be discovered by appearance, but the fetch would still have the general feeling that something is odd. This is in regards to the Attuned to the Wyrd that all fetches have. Some fetches also have Normalcy, wich makes almost impossible for changelings to perceive a fetch for what it trully is. Making non-fae supernatural beings better at spotting fetches than changelings, wich is a little strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T13:30:18-07:00","id":1454232,"title":"","content":"i remember something about Changelings being sterile in first ed, I haven't seen anything about this in second ed so I will assume it is not....but anyone knows if that's the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T14:21:22-07:00","id":1454239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1454232#post1454232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i remember something about Changelings being sterile in first ed, I haven't seen anything about this in second ed so I will assume it is not....but anyone knows if that's the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't, as dev commentary has clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T17:26:53-07:00","id":1454313,"title":"","content":"The inability to escape from bounds or to not let your words be Sealed, would be a minor or major frailty for a Changeling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:21:34-07:00","id":1454359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1454313#post1454313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inability to escape from bounds or to not let your words be Sealed, would be a minor or major frailty for a Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those are too broad, all the examples in the book are of the form of &quot;inability to do X when Y&quot;, and it's how common the &quot;Y&quot; is that decides whether it is minor or major.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T09:49:47-07:00","id":1454751,"title":"","content":"A Elemental seeming changeling can be hurted be mundane versions of his own element? For example a Fire elemental can walk safelly on a vulcano or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T10:49:35-07:00","id":1454753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1454751#post1454751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Elemental seeming changeling can be hurted be mundane versions of his own element? For example a Fire elemental can walk safelly on a vulcano or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW being an elemental confers no immunity, but you're free to rule it how you like of course. There's also no rules on a Fire Elemental burning people on touch either, but one of the fluff texts describes an Elemental with genitals hot enough to melt your junk, so clearly it's more literal for some Elementals than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T11:28:10-07:00","id":1454757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1454751#post1454751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Elemental seeming changeling can be hurted be mundane versions of his own element? For example a Fire elemental can walk safelly on a vulcano or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what the Primal Glory Contract is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T01:14:51-07:00","id":1461312,"title":"","content":"Does the Mask covers things like Contracts and Kith benefits? Like if I swoop from the sky on someone using my Windwing Kith benefit, swinging a flaming sword conjured with Elemental Weapon, do normal people see a perfectly mundane human sailing through the sky with a flaming sword? Or do they somehow rationalize it into something mundane?<br /> <br /> What about physical changes summoned with magic but that aren't actually part of your Mien, like surrounding yourself with fire with Primal Glory or gaining claws with Wing and Talon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T02:02:37-07:00","id":1461317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1461312#post1461312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Mask covers things like Contracts and Kith benefits? Like if I swoop from the sky on someone using my Windwing Kith benefit, swinging a flaming sword conjured with Elemental Weapon, do normal people see a perfectly mundane human sailing through the sky with a flaming sword? Or do they somehow rationalize it into something mundane?<br /> <br /> What about physical changes summoned with magic but that aren't actually part of your Mien, like surrounding yourself with fire with Primal Glory or gaining claws with Wing and Talon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless otherwise specified (which some Kiths do), any activated powers are not protected by the Mask. It only covers your Mien.<br /> Actions are also fully visible; if you use Lethal Mien to eviscerate someone, anyone looking will see how your nails or teeth dig much deeper than what they would expect.<br /> The Mask is powerful in how it's always active, but unlike Quiescence and Lunacy, it does not affect anyone's mental state or cause people to rationalise away anything they see. (Many people still do, but that's the perfectly mundane psychological effect of the shock and the inability to make sense of what they experienced.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-25-2021, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T21:00:52-07:00","id":1463053,"title":"","content":"Props and Scenery<br /> <br /> Does this contract's exceptional success result mean you learn the form with all the extra success benefits saved and only need a single success when using it reflexively to use the form exactly as it was when you earned the exceptional success?<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Does it mean you assume a form as if you used it normally and only got 1 success?<br /> <br /> The first concept seems like you save the awesome form you took before and the second option is that it is a alternate but weaker way of using the contract but you have to exceptionally succeed to purchase the alternate use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T22:20:16-07:00","id":1463058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1463053#post1463053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Props and Scenery<br /> <br /> Does this contract's exceptional success result mean you learn the form with all the extra success benefits saved and only need a single success when using it reflexively to use the form exactly as it was when you earned the exceptional success?<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Does it mean you assume a form as if you used it normally and only got 1 success?<br /> <br /> The first concept seems like you save the awesome form you took before and the second option is that it is a alternate but weaker way of using the contract but you have to exceptionally succeed to purchase the alternate use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the latter. You save a Willpower and an instant action on the form you've purchased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T22:22:22-07:00","id":1463059,"title":"","content":"But is the form you purchased essentially the same strength as a normal 1 success usage of the contract or as it was when you crit and applied all the upgrades?<br /> <br /> Feels weird that it takes about it like its a specific form but it doesnt resemble the strength or effect of the original. Like if your crit was a walking chair then id hope the form u buy is a walking chair and 1 success just means u cant buy more stuff to it. Actually, that does seem right now that i think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T07:02:56-07:00","id":1463090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1463059#post1463059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is the form you purchased essentially the same strength as a normal 1 success usage of the contract or as it was when you crit and applied all the upgrades?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the former, which was the latter when you first asked the question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Feels weird that it takes about it like its a specific form but it doesnt resemble the strength or effect of the original. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The strength or effect of the original,&quot; barring the mobility enhancement and any ST-approved other extra, is either bigger/smaller or more durable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like if your crit was a walking chair then id hope the form u buy is a walking chair and 1 success just means u cant buy more stuff to it. Actually, that does seem right now that i think about it. </div> </div> </div>Remember that any successfully rolled Contract counts as an exceptional success that's rolled [higher of Wyrd and Mantle] successes when you've scoured your Mask away. &quot;A crit&quot; is not very hard to get for this effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T07:11:12-07:00","id":1463092,"title":"","content":"There's a blink-and-you'll-miss-it mention of Centaurs in the Changeling section of Dark Eras concerning Greece. Just out of interest...has there ever been a Kith, 1e or 2e, like that? Or is it more a Hobgoblin thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T08:23:43-07:00","id":1463100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1463092#post1463092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a blink-and-you'll-miss-it mention of Centaurs in the Changeling section of Dark Eras concerning Greece. Just out of interest...has there ever been a Kith, 1e or 2e, like that? Or is it more a Hobgoblin thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings revert to a humanoid body-shape when they escape from Arcadia, so a pure centaur is a little outside the scope of possibility. They'd probably be best represented with the 1e Broadback Kith, in my opinion, and you could choose a centaur shape for Chrysalis as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T15:12:13-07:00","id":1464222,"title":"","content":"How generous are folks with interperting the contitions for the Summer Mantle stuff?<br /> <br /> Like, 2 dot is &quot;when actively defending her freehold against a fae threat&quot; - does that mean she has to be defending the freehold as a whole from a Keeper? Or like, would it apply if a member of the Freehold was getting attacked by Briarwolves or something?<br /> <br /> Some of the other stuff like &quot;when acting as a protector, bodyguard, or champion for someone else&quot; also seem a bit loose on how to interpret - like do they need to be in a formal role like that, or is it fine to just be like &quot;yeah I'm trying to draw the attention of the monster so it doesn't go after my Motley-mate&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T13:56:19-07:00","id":1464277,"title":"","content":"Fae, as in lowercase 'fae', usually mean any fae creature (Gentry, changelings, Hedge Ghosts, Fae-Touched, hobgoblins, et cetera). I would count defending members of the Freehold from harm as 'defending the Freehold', but to me acting as a protector, bodyguard, or champion is a formal role. Just showing up at a scene and joining a fight wouldn't fulfill that condition, unless there are people present that you have already sworn to protect. This is just my take, and generally I assume every group finds their own definitions (these were pretty vaguely defined).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","user":"Vintervalpen","date":". 10-21-2021, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T08:01:59-07:00","id":1464587,"title":"","content":"For the Beast seeming. It mentions if they are feared they cannot use their benefit for more than 3 consecutive turns. I have two questions regarding this. Does that mean I can use lethal, use lethal, use bashing, use lethal, use lethal, use bashing etc... every turn and never need to pay the glamor? Also, does the fear aspect also suppress the bonus to initiative and speed or just the lethal damage? I lean towards it effecting the damage and the two bonuses but not the favored attribute so people feel more compelled to upkeep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:03:38-07:00","id":1464915,"title":"","content":"If you are not suffering some form of fear, you just get +3 Initiative and Speed and can deal lethal damage unarmed, period. Use lethal, use lethal, use lethal, use lethal, use lethal, no Glamour cost.<br /> <br /> If you are afraid of something to the extent that it inflicts a Condition, you can spend a Glamour to get +3 Initiative and Speed and deal lethal damage unarmed for three turns. Use bashing, (glamour) use lethal, use lethal, use lethal, (glamour) use lethal, use lethal, use lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:59:03-07:00","id":1465040,"title":"","content":"So is there no way to get the 'Court' Contracts from non Traditional Mantles, since you can't get Court Goodwill with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T22:47:05-07:00","id":1465243,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Beasts and them doing Lethal... Is a Beast doing Lethal (or other fae monsters with natural weaponry) still considered to be &quot;unarmed&quot; for the purposes of things like the Unarmed Defense style (which gives you a big bonus to defense when fighting &quot;unarmed opponent[s]&quot;)?<br /> <br /> And I guess on the flip side of that, if you've got natural weaponry do you still get to use Fighting Styles or the like that depend on you being &quot;unarmed&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T23:41:00-07:00","id":1465245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1465243#post1465243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Beasts and them doing Lethal... Is a Beast doing Lethal (or other fae monsters with natural weaponry) still considered to be &quot;unarmed&quot; for the purposes of things like the Unarmed Defense style (which gives you a big bonus to defense when fighting &quot;unarmed opponent[s]&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unarmed Defense gives you up to two extra Defense unless you're rocking superhuman ratings in Brawl and the language of the Style suggests it's meant for fighting humans fighting like things that don't have claws and fangs (speaking of which, it's likewise not printed in Vampire or Werewolf, where that's a much more widespread ability), so probably not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I guess on the flip side of that, if you've got natural weaponry do you still get to use Fighting Styles or the like that depend on you being &quot;unarmed&quot;? </div> </div> </div>The fact that none of the Style Merits printed in Changeling 2e have this stipulation indicates to me that this is going to have to be decided on a case-by-case basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:15:52-07:00","id":1465248,"title":"","content":"Perhaps im reading this wrong, but the way the beasts glamor cost is written it says you spend it for every 3 consecutive turns. Which means one after the other. It's written as if you spend it after the three turns. Which ultimately means you could do it for two turns, skip a turn, then do it for two turns and it not cost glamour even when feared. If the goal was to spend it and then get 3 turns of benefit it is not written very clear. I see how you could interpret the other way though, given every other blessing is a pay first setup. Just wish it was clearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-25-2021, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T19:11:06-07:00","id":1465594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1465248#post1465248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps im reading this wrong, but the way the beasts glamor cost is written it says you spend it for every 3 consecutive turns. Which means one after the other. It's written as if you spend it after the three turns. Which ultimately means you could do it for two turns, skip a turn, then do it for two turns and it not cost glamour even when feared. If the goal was to spend it and then get 3 turns of benefit it is not written very clear. I see how you could interpret the other way though, given every other blessing is a pay first setup. Just wish it was clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should always assume the Wyrd takes its payment upfront. Anything that would cheat it gets defenestrated. This is axiomatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:21:38-07:00","id":1465655,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that puts it into perspective more than any response could have. lol Sometimes I read this stuff too mechanically. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T01:08:46-07:00","id":1465875,"title":"","content":"Hello, i ve made a first draft on another thread of a true fae, who is going to be the main villain of my chronicle.<br /> I m not sure if i ve done it rightly, 2ed rules confunds me a little, so i would gladly hear the opinion of experts.<br /> Also i really need some advice for frailties, as i cannot find any source for them.<br /> Thank you in advance ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403971-lugh-the-irish-god\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403971-lugh-the-irish-god\"> Lugh, the Irish God - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403971-lugh-the-irish-god\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1403971-lugh-the-irish-god </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Good day, I m going to start GMing a chronicle set in arthurian britannia. The main antagonist and Keeper of the three changeling player should be modeled after the god Lugh, and without a published example of a 2 ed true fae &amp;quot;sheet&amp;quot; i m encountering some difficulties in creating it, and also i m not an expert of celtic mythology. So i m asking for help to anyone who wish to collaborate. The project will be multi staged. In stage 1 i need to define the true name and the 3 associated titles, including the seeming more in tune with them. In stage 2 i need to define each title tells and </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T22:05:29-07:00","id":1466224,"title":"","content":"Okay, killing the true Fae...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A True Fae never takes bashing damage from anything other than its banes (including iron), and takes lethal damage only from banes unless an attacker speaks its true Name or it breaks an oath, as above. Only cold-iron weapons can deal aggravated damage to the Gentry. </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure how the first and second sentences interact. Do the Gentry take aggravated damage from cold-iron weapons even if you haven't spoken its name or it has broken an oath? Or is it instead that it only ever takes lethal, even from cold iron, unless you speak its Name or it has broken an oath?<br /> <br /> Also - does lethal damage wrap around and inflict aggravated like normal? That'd make it too easy to kill the True Fae I'd think. But if it doesn't wrap around - what happens to the Gentry when you fill up its track with lethal and keep doing damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T23:20:57-07:00","id":1466227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466224#post1466224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, killing the true Fae...</div> </div> </div> </div>Once damage starts rolling it isn't meant to be that hard to kill something. The key is to make it start rolling.<br /> <br /> But about the sentences, it works as that:<br /> <br /> If a source of damage causes Bashing damage, it can damage a True Fae only if it is also a Bane;<br /> <br /> If a source of damage causes Lethal damage, it can damage the True Fae if it is a Bane, <u><b>or</b></u> if the attacker speaks the True Fae's name, <b><u>or</u></b> if the True Fae broke its oaths;<br /> <br /> If a source of damage is Cold-Iron, it causes Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Now, Iron isn't the same as Cold-Iron, that's the catch on the second part. Iron is a Bane in any form, but only Cold-Iron causes aggravated damage on them.<br /> <br /> A weapon made of Iron that isn't Cold-Iron, then, will cause its normal type of damage on a True Fae. A weapon that causes Bashing damage but isn't a Bane, though, will never cause them damage under no circumstance.<br /> <br /> Don't focus too much on this part, though. What makes a True Fae terrifying is its powers, not its resilience. You'll have enough problem to touch it to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:02:59-07:00","id":1466340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466227#post1466227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't focus too much on this part, though. What makes a True Fae terrifying is its powers, not its resilience. You'll have enough problem to touch it to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I hadn't thought the True Fae would be so relatively fragile. I imagine they must be extremely cautious when venturing outside of Arcadia - I know in Arcadia they'll be Hedgespinning like mad, but outside they seem not much more potent than just Changelings with high stats and lots of Contracts - Contracts which cold iron will ignore. Obviously most normal mortals won't have cold iron just sitting around, but motivated player characters can certainly arm themselves with cold iron if they're trying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:12:22-07:00","id":1466344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466340#post1466340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously most normal mortals won't have cold iron just sitting around, but motivated player characters can certainly arm themselves with cold iron if they're trying.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's their point.<br /> <br /> Fae are <b>really</b> weak against Cold-Iron, but not because it causes Aggravated damage, mostly because it ignores their magical defenses. And that really is the whole point. They're not supposed to be nearly unkillable beasts past that.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, though, that Cold-Iron <b>sucks</b>. It is a crappy metal for weapons. It isn't rare, actually it is fairly common to make things that only need to be hard, like gates and candlesticks, or as ingredient for steel making.<br /> <br /> So don't have high-hopes for fancy Cold-Iron weapons. They tend to break because they're too brittle for weapon-grade metal. Even a dagger won't live much, so most Cold-Iron weapons are likely to be badly improvised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:54:20-07:00","id":1466350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466344#post1466344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So don't have high-hopes for fancy Cold-Iron weapons. They tend to break because they're too brittle for weapon-grade metal. Even a dagger won't live much, so most Cold-Iron weapons are likely to be badly improvised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine my players would be most likely to just chop the iron up into bits and load shotgun shells with it. Doing +3A damage and ignoring defense (because it is a firearms attack) will rip anything to pieces really fast.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, it is unlikely to be something they'd carry around on a daily basis - probably only something they'd do if they were going out with the mission of killing one of the True Fae. I guess that just switches the hard part from the confrontation to <i>finding</i> them on the Motley's terms. If you can find them, you can kill them - but can you find them instead of them finding you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T23:41:43-07:00","id":1466420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466340#post1466340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, I hadn't thought the True Fae would be so relatively fragile. I imagine they must be extremely cautious when venturing outside of Arcadia - I know in Arcadia they'll be Hedgespinning like mad, but outside they seem not much more potent than just Changelings with high stats and lots of Contracts - Contracts which cold iron will ignore. Obviously most normal mortals won't have cold iron just sitting around, but motivated player characters can certainly arm themselves with cold iron if they're trying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if i read it rightly, killing a fae even with cold iron only get rid of it for A Time, sfter which the Title reforms.<br /> The only way to eliminate it permanently is by oaths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T04:22:48-07:00","id":1466435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466420#post1466420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if i read it rightly, killing a fae even with cold iron only get rid of it for A Time, sfter which the Title reforms.<br /> The only way to eliminate it permanently is by oaths</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with a caveat.<br /> <br /> What is said is that the Title will be reformed from &quot;another piece&quot; of the True Fae. While it hardly means it will run thin on pieces to do this, what stays in the air is how much it changes the entity from the perspective of the Changeling.<br /> <br /> Is this new incarnation just a copy/past of the previous one? Does it stays as Keeper to its previous charges? Is it even recognizable for Changelings as the same entity? Does it keep the same personality and/or interests? It takes how <b>much</b> time to reform? What it means for practical purposes?<br /> <br /> Being True Fae as they are, the answers to those questions shouldn't be consistent, being governed by their unique and arcane oaths as everything else in them. So it is up to the ST what death by Cold-Iron entails in a given story. It may mean nothing, it may equate to banishment for thousand years or even a new &quot;reformed&quot; Fae that helps Changelings instead of kidnapping new ones. Or it may result in a new form that is even worse springing to action in the first opportunity or even immediately.<br /> <br /> Also, pay attention to what it means for the Changeling. The player know from the book how a True Fae works, but the characters not necessarily. The inner workings of Titles, Names and their manifestations are arcane and mysterious from an IC standpoint, and it is possible that not a single member of a given court knows anything about it. So what it means from the perspective of the characters?<br /> <br /> You killed your Keeper. Other True Fae are still a menace, but you got your vengeance. Even if a disturbingly similar Fae later appears to oppose the Court and try to claim the character, why use semantics to rob the character of its closure? If it does adds to the story, ok, especially if the PC doesn't feel really a closure in how it &quot;ended&quot;. But if there's a strong enough sense of closing that arc in the PC's life and the battle was fulfilling, there's no need to mess with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:36:25-07:00","id":1466586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466420#post1466420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, if i read it rightly, killing a fae even with cold iron only get rid of it for A Time, sfter which the Title reforms.<br /> The only way to eliminate it permanently is by oaths</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahhh, see I could have sworn I read something like that but I'm finding a real hard time finding it in the text?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:53:30-07:00","id":1466592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466586#post1466586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahhh, see I could have sworn I read something like that but I'm finding a real hard time finding it in the text?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 268, second paragraph:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The True Fae are the lords and ladies in their palaces<br /> of crystal and moonlight, but they are also the palace and<br /> the masked servants and the forest in which the castle<br /> sits. <b>What the courts call the \u201cKeeper\u201d is just one Title\u2019s<br /> manifestation, and even if a changeling kills it, the oaths<br /> it made would simply cast a new piece of itself in that role<br /> eventually and pick up the Wild Hunt where it left off.</b><br /> Only breaking the deals that created a Title in the first<br /> place can permanently unravel it, although another Fae<br /> may devour it and claim it for itself. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T07:21:36-07:00","id":1466770,"title":"","content":"About tokens, let s suppose a freehold has a token sword.<br /> They need to do something about it in order to make the token able to withstand the touch of iron without shattering.<br /> Considering that no fae magic can possibly do the trick, what do you think the changelings could come up with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T22:45:50-07:00","id":1466902,"title":"","content":"Is there a defult duration for Contracts that don't have a duration listed? At first I thought they lasted for a scene, but some contracts seem exceptionally broken if they last an entire scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T23:46:23-07:00","id":1466909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466770#post1466770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About tokens, let s suppose a freehold has a token sword.<br /> They need to do something about it in order to make the token able to withstand the touch of iron without shattering.<br /> Considering that no fae magic can possibly do the trick, what do you think the changelings could come up with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like something that would require either an out-of-context solution or a Huntsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T06:31:32-07:00","id":1466932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466902#post1466902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a defult duration for Contracts that don't have a duration listed? At first I thought they lasted for a scene, but some contracts seem exceptionally broken if they last an entire scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per the overview at the start of the Contracts section, it's a scene unless otherwise noted. Which Contracts were giving you pause?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:27:56-07:00","id":1466971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466932#post1466932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per the overview at the start of the Contracts section, it's a scene unless otherwise noted. Which Contracts were giving you pause?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all of them. I mean Primal Glory makes the character immune to damage from a particular element, auto inflicts damage to everyone within reach, and gives the character armour, all for a common Contract with a really easy to gain loophole, and it lasts an entire scene? Or Ice Queen's Call, another common Contract, that lets you create a huge blizzard that lasts for an entire scene, with a loophole that is so laughable the contract might as well just cost 0 glamour. Nearly all Contracts seem like they should only last a single round, or maybe one round per dot of Wyrd, or maybe one round base with the option of extending it by spending an extra point of glamour each round. Or all Conracts should have their costs increased a point or two and have significantly harder to gain loopholes. Currently it just sems like Contracts are too powerful, last too long, and are too cheap. A lot of Contracts also have loopholes that are WAY too easy to gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:57:28-07:00","id":1466977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466971#post1466971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently it just sems like Contracts are too powerful, last too long, and are too cheap. A lot of Contracts also have loopholes that are WAY too easy to gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all contracts are consistently powerful, have you considered that this may be by design? Why do you think they should be weaker?<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that every splat is considerably powerful, but AFAIK (it has been a time since I've read CtL, I have to do so again) Changelings don't have as much innate advantages if you don't consider the Contracts are just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T11:43:39-08:00","id":1467080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1466909#post1466909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like something that would require either an out-of-context solution or a Huntsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, until now i thought about a mage solution, but an Huntsman solution would be really better.<br /> About this what do you think would happen to an huntsman panoply after his death?<br /> Do you think it s possible for an huntsman to own a panoply with extra powers?<br /> Are changelings able to use hunter s panoplies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:45:37-08:00","id":1467093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1467080#post1467080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting idea, until now i thought about a mage solution, but an Huntsman solution would be really better.<br /> About this what do you think would happen to an huntsman panoply after his death?<br /> Do you think it s possible for an huntsman to own a panoply with extra powers?<br /> Are changelings able to use hunter s panoplies?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Probably the same as whatever happens to the Huntsman at death. For some reason I thought the corebook addressed this, but it seems not.<br /> <br /> 2) I'd design it as a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> 3) Don't see why not, with the caveats that all Huntsmen can recall their favored tools with Glamour, and plenty are made of cold iron. (Where they're getting the cold iron for their Panoply is another question entirely.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:00:57-08:00","id":1467465,"title":"","content":"Do the stats gained from Hedgespun Item add onto the stats of the base item, or do they determin the stats of the Hedgespu Item. For example, does a 3 dot Hedgespun fire axe do +3 lethal, or +6?<br /> <br /> If a character wears leather armour (+2 general armour), has heavy weapons 4 (with a hedgespun greatsword that has a +5 damage bonus, although see above question) and summer mantle 4, do all the armour bonuses stack? If the character spends a point of willpower and simply says &quot;yea, I'm that guy's bodyguard, or whatever&quot; he can get a general armour value of 11 against all attacks for an entire turn? That seems completely insane. <br /> <br /> For summer mantle 3, what counts as acting as &quot;a protector, bodyguard, or champion for someone else.&quot; Can the character simply state &quot;I'm that's guys protector&quot; and essentially gain a permanent bonus to armour?<br /> <br /> For summer mantle 4, what counts as a &quot;mundane barrier or inanimate impediment&quot;? Can the character just coolaid man through any wall he wants? Or is this meant to only count on things like breaking down doors and escaping traps like snares and nets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T16:10:08-08:00","id":1467497,"title":"","content":"Hedgespun Tokens give +1 to the base item; you could have a +6 fashion dress or a +6L axe.<br /> <br /> Heavy Weapons doesn't give armor against all attacks, only melee.<br /> <br /> I don't see why the armor bonuses wouldn't stack. Just saying 'lol I am his bodyguard' doesn't make it so in my opinion; it has to be agreed upon between the characters involved. Also armor is very useful, just remember that any Frailty bane (including cold iron) ignores -all- armor your character has. That 11 becomes 0, and that is completely insane.<br /> <br /> A wall is a barrier. It is meant to keep things out (or in).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T16:39:34-08:00","id":1467610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1467497#post1467497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedgespun Tokens give +1 to the base item; you could have a +6 fashion dress or a +6L axe.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people seem to think it stacks, but I'm wondering why? Was this given as an official response somewhere? The Merit doesn't say you take a base item and add bonuses to it. Enhanced Item from Mage specifically says you take an item and increase its existing stats. Hedgespun Item seems more like you create an item from scratch that just mimics a regular item, or may have been a mundane item once but gets transformed into something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T20:45:09-08:00","id":1467636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1467610#post1467610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedgespun Item seems more like you create an item from scratch that just mimics a regular item, or may have been a mundane item once but gets transformed into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read the name of the Hedgespun Item benefit that adds to equipment bonuses, note that the other two benefits are similarly plainly named, and remember that, as a token, any Hedgespun item is attention-grabbing while in use and is completely destroyed by contact with iron. (Not even cold iron, just iron.)<br /> <br /> There's a hard cap on how much you can exceed the base stats of the item by and most equipment is not going to be better than a +3 on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T01:13:50-08:00","id":1467662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1467610#post1467610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of people seem to think it stacks, but I'm wondering why? Was this given as an official response somewhere? The Merit doesn't say you take a base item and add bonuses to it. Enhanced Item from Mage specifically says you take an item and increase its existing stats. Hedgespun Item seems more like you create an item from scratch that just mimics a regular item, or may have been a mundane item once but gets transformed into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The descriptions for Tokens mentions three ways to create them: Two of them uses a base item, and the third is that the True Fae creates them and someone manages to steal it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T06:06:59-08:00","id":1467675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1467610#post1467610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of people seem to think it stacks, but I'm wondering why? Was this given as an official response somewhere? The Merit doesn't say you take a base item and add bonuses to it. Enhanced Item from Mage specifically says you take an item and increase its existing stats. Hedgespun Item seems more like you create an item from scratch that just mimics a regular item, or may have been a mundane item once but gets transformed into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does: &quot;Extraordinary Equipment: an appropriate +1equipment bonus, armor rating, or weapon damage modifier.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you have a 2L sword, an extraordinary equipment sword would go up to 3L, 4L, or 5L depending on your merit rating. It's kind of how 'Improved Alacricy' gives you +2 to speed, without assuming your speed is zero and now you have 2 or 4 or 6 speed if you are wearing the item.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> As a counterpoint: why would anyone pay 3 xp for a +3 equipment bonus Hedgespun dress, when you can just get mundane equipment that does exactly the same without any xp investment? If it doesn't add on top, there's a lot of cases where you either pay XP to get a worse version of a mundane item or one that's the same.<br /> <br /> Now, what I would have liked the merit to say is whether +1 to armor rating is +1/+1, or +1 in either general or ballistic armor. I've seen people arguing both cases (because of the Hedgespinning shift armor), but also, getting +3 to general armor is just really useful. Iron making it evaporate isn't really a big deterrant from getting it, since Banes ignore all armor anyway, so wearing a kevlar vest or fullplate doesn't even matter anyway if someone comes at you with Cold Iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","user":"Vintervalpen","date":". 11-13-2021, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T11:22:05-08:00","id":1468286,"title":"","content":"Just to be sure, if a human makes a deal with an hobgoblin, and he exchanges a chocolate bar for a potion of sweet dreams, he ALSO accrues a point of Goblin debt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T14:24:06-08:00","id":1468301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468286#post1468286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be sure, if a human makes a deal with an hobgoblin, and he exchanges a chocolate bar for a potion of sweet dreams, he ALSO accrues a point of Goblin debt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Accepting Goblin Debt <i>is</i> the payment. No need to bring chocolate unless you wish to improve your impression or relationship with that particular hobgoblin. Or maybe the hobgoblin isn't willing to make deals in the first place unless placated with chocolate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T22:00:52-08:00","id":1468330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468301#post1468301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Accepting Goblin Debt <i>is</i> the payment. No need to bring chocolate unless you wish to improve your impression or relationship with that particular hobgoblin. Or maybe the hobgoblin isn't willing to make deals in the first place unless placated with chocolate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, then i m a little confused.<br /> The book says that changeling can trade services for shedding goblin debt points, in this case &quot;hey Stinky Joe if i give you this candy bar we are even for the potion of the last week?&quot; &quot;Oh oh, yup!&quot;<br /> But mortals can shed them only by sacrificing important things or by doing specific very difficult task.<br /> I don t understand, the goblin will offer his services and state that the mortal will owe him an unspecified favor in the future?<br /> He will wait until the mortal accrues enough debt to turn into a Hedge denizen or at some point he will say &quot;give me your wedding ring and we are even?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T23:37:56-08:00","id":1468332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468330#post1468330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, then i m a little confused.<br /> The book says that changeling can trade services for shedding goblin debt points, in this case &amp;quot;hey Stinky Joe if i give you this candy bar we are even for the potion of the last week?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Oh oh, yup!&amp;quot;<br /> But mortals can shed them only by sacrificing important things or by doing specific very difficult task.<br /> I don t understand, the goblin will offer his services and state that the mortal will owe him an unspecified favor in the future?<br /> He will wait until the mortal accrues enough debt to turn into a Hedge denizen or at some point he will say &amp;quot;give me your wedding ring and we are even?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The book doesn't specify, but I believe the service a changeling can perform should be on par with the task a mortal has to complete. Mortals also have the option to lose something important (which, imo, should also be available for changelings) while changelings also have the list of ways the ST can spend Goblin Debt to mess with them.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the actual negotiation, you could either have the goblin be vague about an unspecified future favour, or have them be more like &quot;now that I've given you this, it's time to discuss your payment&quot; but unfortunately the lack of immediacy for Goblin Debt does create a disconnect between the concept of being indebted to weird supernatural creatures/forces and the pressure you'd expect to feel while indebted to them.<br /> In short, hobgoblins who makes trades are basically loansharks who are more interested in putting people into debt than actually collecting that debt. Given the lack of drawbacks (especially for mortals, but there are multiple Merits for changelings to get rid of it for free, allowing their players to just say no to the ST if it's too inconvenient), just having Goblin Debt is largely trivial as long as you don't rack up too much of it.<br /> <br /> One way to make payment actually feel important (like how it works in most of the source material) is to just skip the middle step and have the hobgoblin request the payment for Goblin Debt immediately as part of the transaction, meaning you technically gain the point of Goblin Debt and resolve it instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T08:11:10-08:00","id":1468345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468286#post1468286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be sure, if a human makes a deal with an hobgoblin, and he exchanges a chocolate bar for a potion of sweet dreams, he ALSO accrues a point of Goblin debt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The Goblin Debt isn't the payment so much as the representation of the goblin (or its backer) having a foot in the door \u2014 remember, none of these deals are one-and-done unless you actually need a single temporary fix. There's a reason Market Sense's effect is &quot;you can reduce your Goblin Debt by one&quot; and not &quot;you can ignore one point of Goblin Debt.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a story in Hunter's Horror Recognition Guide, &quot;The Market,&quot; that makes a pretty solid distinction about why you can't pay for things with regular money at a Goblin Market: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The chipped mug, how much? I held 10 bucks out as I asked.<br /> \u201cWhat? What for?\u201d<br /> \u201cThese.\u201d I waved the bills, feeling too conspicuous for my own good.<br /> \u201cPah! No. They\u2019ve got no worth, only value. You want something with worth, you offer something with worth. What use do I have for value?\u201d<br /> I backed away before I caused more offense. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The people walking the floor all had something in their eyes, a burning need. After a while, I saw the pattern. They each fixated on one thing. Maybe it was a piece of trash or a bite to eat. A few wanted in to the strange, enclosed tents on the outskirts. One lusted after something I couldn\u2019t quite see to start with, but when I looked, I saw a man\u2019s arm, wrapped in old newspaper. Everyone there had something they needed. Watching for longer, I could see nobody got what they went in for. People traded for things, then traded them away, but the market\u2019s not running a fair game. Like a casino, the house always keeps its cut. Apparently, I\u2019ve become part of the market. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;But how can that work? I mean, without money, how do they profit?&quot;<br /> &quot;You\u2019re still new. They\u2019re not in it for profit. They\u2019ve got a need, same as everyone else. They need our desperation, same as I need another lung. That little sinking feeling in your gut when you realize they\u2019ve got you over a barrel? That\u2019s what they\u2019re really after.&quot; </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see other people walking around and they trade as best they can, but they don\u2019t understand their situation \u2014 they\u2019re working toward an ever-changing goal. It\u2019s not like I could haggle on a price for my marriage then work my way back along the chain. Value isn\u2019t a constant here, so there\u2019s no way of mapping out a path to your goal. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Market\u2019s prices, the acceptable trades, vary according to need. If you really need something, you need to trade more for it. If it\u2019s just another step on your journey of transaction, then you get a better deal than if it\u2019s your end goal. It\u2019s the Market making sure it always has plenty of need to feast upon. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T23:47:21-08:00","id":1468387,"title":"","content":"Can Wizened via Dance of the Toys Contract animate spring switchblade (for it is even being a knife still a simple mechanicle device) to attack his foes? If yes, will it attack separately from him, or should he make an instant action to attack by the flying knife? And what if he animates two or three knives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 11-20-2021, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T12:28:18-08:00","id":1468620,"title":"","content":"When evoking the Loophole for Dance of the Toys, do you need to inscribe a name on an object every time you use it on the same object, or do you just need to do it once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T16:09:36-08:00","id":1468637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468620#post1468620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When evoking the Loophole for Dance of the Toys, do you need to inscribe a name on an object every time you use it on the same object, or do you just need to do it once?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just do it once. You don't have to keep renaming the gun from Jack to Ace to Bandit, you just have to make sure that if you have multiple guns, none of them share the same name.<br /> <br /> Still have to invoke it out loud every time, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T18:01:25-08:00","id":1468642,"title":"","content":"Has there ever been a kith that deals with having multiple arms? I\u2019m trying to make a NPC, and I like the visual for them, but I can\u2019t find anything. If there is none, does the multiple limbs demonic form seem able to be refitted for Changeling? Those bonuses seem a bit much for a trickery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T20:46:57-08:00","id":1468654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468642#post1468642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there ever been a kith that deals with having multiple arms? I\u2019m trying to make a NPC, and I like the visual for them, but I can\u2019t find anything. If there is none, does the multiple limbs demonic form seem able to be refitted for Changeling? Those bonuses seem a bit much for a trickery.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, for much the same reason there hasn't been a kith for having a tail and the Cyclopean kith isn't actually about having one eye. Arc breaks down why demonic forms and kiths aren't interchangeable concepts (the latter being whole-body affairs and the former being more compartmentalized) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> It's important not to get too hung up on the visual when coming up with mechanics, especially for elements that can appear in lots of different visuals. Think about what the character actually <i>is</i>, folklorically speaking. For example, are they evoking the six-armed three-faced <i>asura</i> of Buddhist mythology or the kraken of Scandanavian folklore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T21:51:40-08:00","id":1468659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468654#post1468654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, for much the same reason there hasn't been a kith for having a tail and the Cyclopean kith isn't actually about having one eye. Arc breaks down why demonic forms and kiths aren't interchangeable concepts (the latter being whole-body affairs and the former being more compartmentalized) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div> A interesting read. And rather relevant since I was thinking of having one unchained involved in a plot line with my Autumn Court. But I probably shouldn\u2019t since I don\u2019t feel confident in my ability to weld Changeling\u2019s and Demon\u2019s themes together into something coherent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468654#post1468654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important not to get too hung up on the visual when coming up with mechanics, especially for elements that can appear in lots of different visuals. Think about what the character actually <i>is</i>, folklorically speaking. For example, are they evoking the six-armed three-faced <i>asura</i> of Buddhist mythology or the kraken of Scandanavian folklore?</div> </div> </div> </div> So, this might be a good time to mention I\u2019m not basing them on any particular folklore. My own whimsy and imagination are all I have, for better or worse. I started making this character after reading about the Family of Silent Nights, at the thought of a master of the oneiromantic arts, being a bringer sweet dreams, inverse of a Nightmare. Of course, oneiromancy doesn\u2019t require a particular skill, so I can\u2019t play on that as kith/seeming shaper, to reinforce or subvert. So I must use my mind to fill out the gaps. I think of them as a gentle, caring, weaver of dreams. That\u2019s where the arms come in, for some reason, I associate multiple arms and dreams with weaving. Perhaps it\u2019s some connection with spiders webs and dream catchers. Or maybe a Tv Tropes article. Anyways the theme is being a positive, constructive force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 11-23-2021, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T14:40:12-08:00","id":1468703,"title":"","content":"Ok different question: do those dream creatures from 1e, incubi I think, still exist in 2e? Do they have bans and banes? Or I guess frailties in 2e. Are they Goetic entries or something else? Should I use the hedge ghost stats if I want to use them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T15:10:40-08:00","id":1468706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468703#post1468703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok different question: do those dream creatures from 1e, incubi I think, still exist in 2e? Do they have bans and banes? Or I guess frailties in 2e. Are they Goetic entries or something else? Should I use the hedge ghost stats if I want to use them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you read the 2E book you'd see which creatures still exist in 2e.<br /> <br /> There's no such creatures described in the book, but you can make your own, using whatever system you feel is the most appropriate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T15:59:48-08:00","id":1468711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468706#post1468706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think if you read the 2E book you'd see which creatures still exist in 2e.<br /> <br /> There's no such creatures described in the book, but you can make your own, using whatever system you feel is the most appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I have read the 2e core rulebook, Eidolons are the closest thing, but are fundamentally different. I have not, however, read a single 1e book. I only know about these creatures from the white wolf wiki. That would why I\u2019m asking about mechanics, so as to better be able to covert them to 2e.<br /> <br /> Secondly, not every Changeling relevant creature\u2019s mechanics in 2e are detailed in the Changeling core rule book. For example the mirror people are canon to 2e but are in the chronicles of darkness core rulebook instead, despite having a named place in the hedge, mirror-space or the halls of mirrors. I do not have every book. Maybe one of the night horrors, or contagion chronicle has something. I wouldn\u2019t know since I don\u2019t own those books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 11-23-2021, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T18:19:05-08:00","id":1468717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468642#post1468642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there ever been a kith that deals with having multiple arms? I\u2019m trying to make a NPC, and I like the visual for them, but I can\u2019t find anything. If there is none, does the multiple limbs demonic form seem able to be refitted for Changeling? Those bonuses seem a bit much for a trickery.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the past, I tried to write up a multi-limbed kith, but ran into the same problems that I think every crunchy RPG with combat elements does when it comes to that sort of thing. As Satchel mentions and Arc elaborates, focusing on the overall theme of the kith will lead to more fruitful results than the outward form (it's what's inside that counts, after all). That said, I think a multi-limbed changeling could be designed with either a Merit or a feature of the Talon &amp; Wing Contract, depending on what exactly you want those arms to do.<br /> <br /> Some Incubi work as Eidolons, others as hobgoblins, others will require a bit more conversion-work depending on the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T20:25:14-08:00","id":1468725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468717#post1468717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the past, I tried to write up a multi-limbed kith, but ran into the same problems that I think every crunchy RPG with combat elements does when it comes to that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, duel wielding and it\u2019s variants never seem to be quite balanced. Frankly, I\u2019m not looking for combat applications for this character, sure they fight nightmares, but I\u2019m not seeing their kith playing into it. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468717#post1468717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As Satchel mentions and Arc elaborates, focusing on the overall theme of the kith will lead to more fruitful results than the outward form (it's what's inside that counts, after all).</div> </div> </div> </div> This is sound advice. Unfortunately that\u2019s where I\u2019m stuck. I have some personality done and a clear purpose, but kith eludes me, because the main concept doesn\u2019t need it it. I\u2019m currently bouncing between perhaps stereotypical kiths, (Di-Cang, or Weisse Frau) or something quite different that still makes some sense. (Artist as a weaver) I actually started delving into my seemingly random connection between spiders and dream catchers to try and come up with something. So I researched, and found dream catchers are: a) a protective charm for more than just dreams, b) actually are supposed to look like webs (I was always told they were nets), and c) has a mythological figure behind them in the form of spider woman or spider grandmother. I had no idea. Cool stuff. Also I found a big cultural appropriation debate. So now I\u2019m sad.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468717#post1468717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That said, I think a multi-limbed changeling could be designed with either a Merit or a feature of the Talon &amp; Wing Contract, depending on what exactly you want those arms to do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly, I\u2019m probably going to have it take up some merit points. I\u2019m not looking for much, being able to hold some extra stuff in hands is really all I want. Maybe help them do certain tasks\u2026faster. <br /> *facepalms* Oh I\u2019m dumb sometimes. Think a Drudge would be appropriate? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468717#post1468717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Incubi work as Eidolons, others as hobgoblins, others will require a bit more conversion-work depending on the specifics.</div> </div> </div> </div> Judging by this, there is nothing made for 2e yet. I had figured from Vintervalpen\u2019s post, but was kinda hoped there would be something elsewhere. Oh well. I\u2019ll look more into the types. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T21:05:17-08:00","id":1468726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468659#post1468659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I probably shouldn\u2019t since I don\u2019t feel confident in my ability to weld Changeling\u2019s and Demon\u2019s themes together into something coherent.</div> </div> </div> </div>[aside glance at the state of the Grey City Freehold] i feel your pain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, this might be a good time to mention I\u2019m not basing them on any particular folklore. My own whimsy and imagination are all I have, for better or worse. I started making this character after reading about the Family of Silent Nights, at the thought of a master of the oneiromantic arts, being a bringer sweet dreams, inverse of a Nightmare. Of course, oneiromancy doesn\u2019t require a particular skill, so I can\u2019t play on that as kith/seeming shaper, to reinforce or subvert. So I must use my mind to fill out the gaps. </div> </div> </div>Empathy has historically been a useful Skill for oneiromancy and remains only slightly less so in 2e, where it's still used to spot tampering in a Bastion through Kenning, gauge its Fortification rating, and add to deeper subliminal cues for bonus dice on Manipulation rolls with Shift Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think of them as a gentle, caring, weaver of dreams. That\u2019s where the arms come in, for some reason, I associate multiple arms and dreams with weaving. Perhaps it\u2019s some connection with spiders webs and dream catchers. Or maybe a Tv Tropes article. Anyways the theme is being a positive, constructive force. </div> </div> </div>Something to do with mitigating the hostility of eidolons and/or triggering paradigm shifts might be a thing to go for. Possibly take cues from Playmate, as an alternative?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468703#post1468703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok different question: do those dream creatures from 1e, incubi I think, still exist in 2e? Do they have bans and banes? Or I guess frailties in 2e. Are they Goetic entries or something else? Should I use the hedge ghost stats if I want to use them?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the book the term premiers in:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dancers in the Dusk, p24-5, &quot;Incubi&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings use the term \u201cIncubi\u201d to mean any being that has intruded into a dreamscape without the permission granted by a pledge. An Incubus can be anything capable of entering the dreamscape, though the term is not usually applied to beings that mean to aid the dreamer. Some fae who solved the problem of their fetch peacefully even call those fae who inflict nightmares on their doubles Incubi, claiming they are no different from anything else deliberately torturing a dreamer in their sleep.<br /> <br /> <b>Origins</b><br /> The origins of Incubi are as ephemeral as the dreams they inhabit, and fae that fight them are often forced to admit they have no idea as to the precise nature of their opponent. Some are recognizable as True Fae, entering dreams by Dream Poison for their own inscrutable purposes. Some are fetches, striking back at the fae they replaced through their linked dreams. Others, oneiropomps are forced to reluctantly conclude, are changelings pursuing vendettas.<br /> <br /> The \u201cknown\u201d Incubi, the ones that can be described as one familiar group or another, are only a very slim majority. Stranger things are found in dreams; beings that do not appear to fit with the changelings\u2019 sketchy knowledge of the world. Self-aware dreams that pass from dreamer to dreamer, archetypes that resemble famous individuals warping the dreams of their fans, strangely powerful versions of the dreamer that shape the dreamscape through oneiromancy and attack intruding fae, creatures that may be hobgoblins, blurring the edges of the dream and the Hedge, bizarre effects that might indicate the birthing of a new member of the Gentry, beings that may be ghosts, manifesting in the sleep of their former loved ones rather than in the physical world, vampires, mages and werewolves \u2014 and odder things \u2014 using their own powers to enter the sleeping mind and still more intruders beyond recognizable form.<br /> <br /> Some Incubi seem determined to prevent others (such as the fae) from altering the dream they\u2019re in. Others shape the dreams they are part of themselves and attack those that attempt to interfere. Many Incubi blend so well into the dreamscape, camouflaging themselves as native dreams (if indeed they aren\u2019t), that they go unnoticed until they strike. Some engage in direct dream combat while others shape the dreamscape to be hostile to travelers. Some might even <u>be</u> the dreamscape in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underhill draft of 2e had incubi as a mostly-consistent phenomenon that the final version has done up as eidolons, but in the line's published history &quot;incubus&quot; is a catch-all for &quot;thing in someone's dreams that's not supposed to be there,&quot; of which Dancers' list includes a great many things that are goetia that have misplaced themselves or are being reflected up through the Astral shallows into dreams.<br /> <br /> Non-fae intruders in dreams that aren't an existing stattable monster should probably have frailties appropriate to the bans and banes of equally powerful goetia, modeled as eidolons but distinct from them just as Hedge ghosts are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T22:10:29-08:00","id":1468731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468726#post1468726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[aside glance at the state of the Grey City Freehold] i feel your pain.</div> </div> </div> </div> *smiles* Thanks for this, and the rest of the post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468726#post1468726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empathy has historically been a useful Skill for oneiromancy and remains only slightly less so in 2e, where it's still used to spot tampering in a Bastion through Kenning, gauge its Fortification rating, and add to deeper subliminal cues for bonus dice on Manipulation rolls with Shift Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had planed on having a high empathy for them, it just fits the concept. But this is a useful point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468726#post1468726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to do with mitigating the hostility of eidolons and/or triggering paradigm shifts might be a thing to go for. Possibly take cues from Playmate, as an alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div> I will keep this in mind. I believe that it is more fitting in character for the eidolons to recognize them as a benevolent influence. It won\u2019t keep them form getting kicked out, but forestalling anger is useful enough. And I can have both with a Empathy blessing. Actually, looking at the rules, the dreamer\u2019s composure penalty is something that I could mess with. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468726#post1468726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the book the term premiers in:<br /> <br /> The Underhill draft of 2e had incubi as a mostly-consistent phenomenon that the final version has done up as eidolons, but in the line's published history &quot;incubus&quot; is a catch-all for &quot;thing in someone's dreams that's not supposed to be there,&quot; of which Dancers' list includes a great many things that are goetia that have misplaced themselves or are being reflected up through the Astral shallows into dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh. I was under the assumption that they were all a certain type of creature, just very obscure. This actually works better. Also the provided quote is great. Lots of ideas there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468726#post1468726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-fae intruders in dreams that aren't an existing stattable monster should probably have frailties appropriate to the bans and banes of equally powerful goetia, modeled as eidolons but distinct from them just as Hedge ghosts are.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perfect. A great starting point. <br /> <br /> Alright, thank you everyone! I believe I have a solid character, and direction now. I really do appreciate my questions being answered so fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T07:09:09-08:00","id":1468754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468717#post1468717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the past, I tried to write up a multi-limbed kith, but ran into the same problems that I think every crunchy RPG with combat elements does when it comes to that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem comes from wrong (but common) assumptions about how multi-limbs should play out. And from our tendency to simulate physics instead of abstracting situations.<br /> <br /> IRL few if any animals regularly engage on multiple <u><i>focused</i></u> tasks despite number of limbs. Even wielding two weapons in combat is far harder than it seems and most actual techniques will reduce the complexity of the task instead of trying to achieve two distinct sets of actions.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, multiple limbs have just as much effect as the <b>brain</b> of the entity is equipped to use them. That means they can give a bonus to whatever task you want, nothing more. In fact, you can reasonably have multi-limbs as a disadvantage (Persistent Condition in our case), as the Changeling isn't actually adapted to use them and they keep getting in the way all the time instead of coordinating. A neutral stance of having more hands just to hold things and doing nothing is already pretty good in comparison.<br /> <br /> So instead of assuming that multiple hands have to give you multiple actions of some kind, stop to think what effect you want for this specific character, and this effect is what will define the best path to rule them. Different characters with the same number of arms beyond two may have them through distinct rules as they get distinct effects from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T15:19:16-08:00","id":1468786,"title":"","content":"Damn, this makes me want to do another re-write of my hecatoncheir kith. Maybe split it up into two kiths, one for the entrapment and one for the overworked multitasking. There hasn't been a post in the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1404858-fan-made-kiths-updating-the-test-material-kiths\"> Fan-Made Kiths thread</a> since Nov 18 2020. Should I revive it or make a new &quot;Post Your Kiths&quot; thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T21:58:46-08:00","id":1468813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468786#post1468786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, this makes me want to do another re-write of my hecatoncheir kith. Maybe split it up into two kiths, one for the entrapment and one for the overworked multitasking. There hasn't been a post in the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1404858-fan-made-kiths-updating-the-test-material-kiths\"> Fan-Made Kiths thread</a> since Nov 18 2020. Should I revive it or make a new &quot;Post Your Kiths&quot; thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would have answered earlier, but I had assumed someone else would answer. I personally believe you should make a new post, unless you get permission from the original poster on the Fan made kiths thread. Normally I\u2019d be against having multiple threads, but the fan made kiths for 2e are spread out over several threads already. The damage has already been done. This way we won\u2019t fill Strictura\u2019s notification box, or commit necromancy. Also I will probably put in my dream weaver kith in whatever you decide (if I ever come up with good name).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 11-25-2021, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1