a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:38:07-08:00","id":1468835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468833#post1468833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. Anyone else want an @ notification when it's up?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can add me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T12:20:06-08:00","id":1469008,"title":"","content":"Is Whispers of Morning useful in the Hedge? I have a Hedge Navigator Changeling, with a favored regalia in Shields (I love the contracts there too much, and I want him to start with Fortifying Presence) who is part of the Autumn court, and I am struggling to find a good Royal contract to fit him. Whispers of Morning is a favorite of mine, but I don\u2019t know how useful it would be in the Hedge given everything there is magical and thus get around the usefulness of going intangible. Plus I am not sure if anything there would let a Changeling using it pass through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T13:03:35-08:00","id":1469011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469008#post1469008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Whispers of Morning useful in the Hedge? I have a Hedge Navigator Changeling, with a favored regalia in Shields (I love the contracts there too much, and I want him to start with Fortifying Presence) who is part of the Autumn court, and I am struggling to find a good Royal contract to fit him. Whispers of Morning is a favorite of mine, but I don\u2019t know how useful it would be in the Hedge given everything there is magical and thus get around the usefulness of going intangible. Plus I am not sure if anything there would let a Changeling using it pass through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it works in the Hedge. Even though Twilight doesn\u2019t exist in the Hedge, Hedge Ghosts can still go invisible and incorporeal with dematerialize. I don\u2019t see why Whispers of Morning wouldn\u2019t be similar. Otherwise, it would be mentioned that it doesn\u2019t work in the Hedge. To not put such a disclaimer if it wasn\u2019t intended to work in the Hedge seems a bit weird since the Hedge is kinda a big deal in Changeling. At most, the bit about not being able to see other dematerialized creatures will need to be accounted for. At least from my reading of the rules. We shall see if someone disagrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T13:37:29-08:00","id":1469013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469008#post1469008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[..] but I don\u2019t know how useful it would be in the Hedge given everything there is magical and thus get around the usefulness of going intangible. Plus I am not sure if anything there would let a Changeling using it pass through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite understand this part. Being part of the Hedge doesn't mean it automatically blocks intangible beings, if that's what you mean. You still need pretty specific supernatural effects/powers to block someone using Whispers of Morning. They're probably more common in the Hedge, but it should still be quite rare to see anything except Hedge Ghosts being able to interact with WoM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:22:58-08:00","id":1469027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469013#post1469013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't quite understand this part. Being part of the Hedge doesn't mean it automatically blocks intangible beings, if that's what you mean. You still need pretty specific supernatural effects/powers to block someone using Whispers of Morning. They're probably more common in the Hedge, but it should still be quite rare to see anything except Hedge Ghosts being able to interact with WoM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed they were referring to the lack of Twilight in the Hedge. The contract doesn\u2019t explicitly say that it works using Fae Twilight, but it rather strongly implicitly does, because it talks about what you can see that happens to be in Twilight. It also highlights the difference between it and the Helldiver kith, which goes into every form of Twilight at once. (Helldiver is awesome)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:39:11-08:00","id":1469030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469027#post1469027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed they were referring to the lack of Twilight in the Hedge. The contract doesn\u2019t explicitly say that it works using Fae Twilight, but it rather strongly implicitly does, because it talks about what you can see that happens to be in Twilight. It also highlights the difference between it and the Helldiver kith, which goes into every form of Twilight at once. (Helldiver is awesome)</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the opposite. Morning of Whispers, Hedge Ghosts and Helldivers explicitly <b>don't</b> use Twilight. Instead, they can all become intangible in the Hedge.<br /> What you've likely misread is the part where Morning of Whispers says it's on a frequency different from Twilight; not that it's on a different Twilight frequency.<br /> Edit: It's a terrible phrasing since different types of Twilight are almost exclusively referred to as different &quot;frequencies&quot; in these forums, even if it's just fan terminology.<br /> <br /> <b>Why</b> there isn't a Fae/Hedge based Twilight is far beyond my understanding, since Twilight from a Doylist perspective is just shorthand for being invisible &amp; intangible, but that's how it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-27-2021, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:57:14-08:00","id":1469032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469030#post1469030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite the opposite. Morning of Whispers, Hedge Ghosts and Helldivers explicitly <b>don't</b> use Twilight. Instead, they can all become intangible in the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why go through all the trouble of saying \u201cHowever, she exists on a different frequency than creatures in Twilight\u201d if they aren\u2019t in Twilight? That seems really misleading. I think we both agree, though, the contract just makes you intangible and invisible in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469030#post1469030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why</b> there isn't a Fae/Hedge based Twilight is far beyond my understanding, since Twilight from a Doylist perspective is just shorthand for being invisible &amp; intangible, but that's how it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* blame Mage and Werewolf I guess. Or word count.<br /> <br /> Semi related new question: which Twilight do you think a oneiropomp in dream form that gets hurled back into the mortal world is in? Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:10:15-08:00","id":1469035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469030#post1469030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why</b> there isn't a Fae/Hedge based Twilight is far beyond my understanding, since Twilight from a Doylist perspective is just shorthand for being invisible &amp; intangible, but that's how it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that it's because Twilight has descriptive qualities for how you interact with the world that aren't appropriate to a Glamour-fueled state of intangibility \u2014 washed out colors and muffled sounds don't really track for things that aren't ghosts and spirits with conceptual blinders over everything that isn't their Manifestation Conditions, especially for a power used by a splat that already has a way to muddle their senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:31:49-08:00","id":1469038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469013#post1469013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't quite understand this part. Being part of the Hedge doesn't mean it automatically blocks intangible beings, if that's what you mean. You still need pretty specific supernatural effects/powers to block someone using Whispers of Morning. They're probably more common in the Hedge, but it should still be quite rare to see anything except Hedge Ghosts being able to interact with WoM.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not being blocked, it\u2019s the thought that things like the thorns and other supernatural effects could still affect a Changeling using WoM. This character doesn\u2019t have many if any combat abilities, and social strategies won\u2019t work every time either. Having something he can semi-reliably use is kind of paramount in that sense.<br /> <br /> Still, it seems the general consensus is that WoM should be able to function in these circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:52:21-08:00","id":1469042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469038#post1469038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not being blocked, it\u2019s the thought that things like the thorns and other supernatural effects could still affect a Changeling using WoM. This character doesn\u2019t have many if any combat abilities, and social strategies won\u2019t work every time either. Having something he can semi-reliably use is kind of paramount in that sense.<br /> <br /> Still, it seems the general consensus is that WoM should be able to function in these circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Hedge will probably still find a way to mess with you, even if you are semi-permanently invisible and intangible. Probably by giving you a scene you can\u2019t ignore. Or Clarity damage stuff. Preferably both at the same time. That said, for physical threats, this contract should get you away from most problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T03:18:38-08:00","id":1469080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469032#post1469032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why go through all the trouble of saying \u201cHowever, she exists on a different frequency than creatures in Twilight\u201d if they aren\u2019t in Twilight? That seems really misleading. I think we both agree, though, the contract just makes you intangible and invisible in the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;different frequency <i>than</i> creatures in Twilight&quot;<br /> That phrasing means the former are distinct from the latter. The latter are defined by existing in Twilight. The former, from inference, don't exist in Twilight.<br /> It's a very subtle change from &quot;different frequency <i>of</i> Twilight than ghosts and spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *shrug* blame Mage and Werewolf I guess. Or word count. </div> </div> </div>I don't see what either game has to do with it.<br /> As for word count, that benefit surely went out the door with the word count spent for each individual Twilight-like ability that explains how it's different from Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Semi related new question: which Twilight do you think a oneiropomp in dream form that gets hurled back into the mortal world is in? Astral? </div> </div> </div>Dream forms are definitely in Astral Twilight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469035#post1469035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is that it's because Twilight has descriptive qualities for how you interact with the world that aren't appropriate to a Glamour-fueled state of intangibility \u2014 washed out colors and muffled sounds don't really track for things that aren't ghosts and spirits with conceptual blinders over everything that isn't their Manifestation Conditions, especially for a power used by a splat that already has a way to muddle their senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>An easily changed description that'd naturally only affect beings in Changeling who uses that system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T02:09:31-08:00","id":1469633,"title":"","content":"So, here\u2019s a question that came up in a discussion with another; are the Court Bargains effectively Oaths that a Gentry and their forces can break by accident? That is, could you trick a Gentry to retreat from a battle by pretending to be dead during Summer, or disguise yourself as their target in Spring so they strike you even though you are not truly the one they want to harm?<br /> <br /> My default is no, but this is for clarity\u2019s sake. Besides, I have been wrong about bigger things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T04:05:15-08:00","id":1469638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469633#post1469633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here\u2019s a question that came up in a discussion with another; are the Court Bargains effectively Oaths that a Gentry and their forces can break by accident? That is, could you trick a Gentry to retreat from a battle by pretending to be dead during Summer, or disguise yourself as their target in Spring so they strike you even though you are not truly the one they want to harm?<br /> <br /> My default is no, but this is for clarity\u2019s sake. Besides, I have been wrong about bigger things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Court bargains are not Oath sworn by the Gentry, so they cannot broke them.<br /> The court Patron simply impose behavioral restriction on the True Fae using its powers.<br /> About breaking those impositions, i don t know, if it s possible to break Taboos by accident the answer is probably yes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T07:06:04-08:00","id":1469725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468345#post1468345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. The Goblin Debt isn't the payment so much as the representation of the goblin (or its backer) having a foot in the door \u2014 remember, none of these deals are one-and-done unless you actually need a single temporary fix. There's a reason Market Sense's effect is &amp;quot;you can reduce your Goblin Debt by one&amp;quot; and not &amp;quot;you can ignore one point of Goblin Debt.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There's a story in Hunter's Horror Recognition Guide, &amp;quot;The Market,&amp;quot; that makes a pretty solid distinction about why you can't pay for things with regular money at a Goblin Market: <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mmh, if this is the way it goes i m still a little confused.<br /> Let s take the aforementioned example.<br /> Bob the human has nightmares every night (he has an Huntsmen heart in his bastion)<br /> One evening Stinky joe the goblin pops out from a trash can in an alley, appearing as a tramp.<br /> He sells a dose of a drug called Sweet dreams, he is hungry so he accept a chocolate bar as a payment.<br /> Bob is hungry too, but out of curiosity (and joes manipulation+subterfuge 8 dices) he accepts.<br /> Unknow to him Sweet dreams has a little side effect: if he stops taking it the nightmares intensity increases.<br /> At first Bob buys one pill, but it starts craving for more.<br /> But more pills means an higher price.<br /> Bob sells his clothes, his car, his apartment, everything.<br /> After the ninth deal, one year later, Bob starts having nightmares that hurts, a lot, when he doesn t take Sweet dreams.<br /> He meets joe in his apartment, and joe offers him a definitive deal.<br /> An experimental super dose of Sweet dreams, that would let him stay perpetually awake.<br /> The cost is his name (and identity).<br /> Bob accepts, and after ingesting the pill, he transform in an hobgoblin and finally sees the true mien of joe.<br /> Joe now owns every part of Bob, who is his slave.<br /> Their lifestyle switched, and now Bob the Hedge denizen is a tramp who makes deals in a dark alley, while joe can buy back from his master his freedom and humanity by selling Bob ownership to it.<br /> He can now start to live his new comfortable life... until ha starts having bad dreams...<br /> <br /> In this case Bobs debt represents his increasing desire and dependency of what joe has to offer, am i right?<br /> But in the case of a changeling, especially one who accrues debt point only with contracts, how does this differ?<br /> Does their knowledge of the laws of wyrd help them better understands those deals ramifications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T11:06:12-08:00","id":1469751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469638#post1469638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Court bargains are not Oath sworn by the Gentry, so they cannot broke them.<br /> The court Patron simply impose behavioral restriction on the True Fae using its powers.<br /> About breaking those impositions, i don t know, if it s possible to break Taboos by accident the answer is probably yes</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the examples provided feel like a better way to frustrate the entity making the bargain, since you\u2019re clearly not acting in the spirit of it. If you pretend to be dead instead of fighting, you aren\u2019t following Summer\u2019s teachings. If you pretend to be a Gentry\u2019s Changeling specifically to get them to harm you, the you must really want to be that Gentry\u2019s Changeling.<br /> <br /> In either case, I would let the Bargains effects falter as the entity deliberately doesn\u2019t follow through. Play stupid games, win stupid prizes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T14:59:27-08:00","id":1469768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469725#post1469725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case Bobs debt represents his increasing desire and dependency of what joe has to offer, am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case Bob has fallen for the &quot;first hit is free&quot; scam and probably been paying a lot longer than nine deals' worth \u2014 the section on Hobgoblin Deals isn't explicit about how much Goblin Debt a major sacrifice pays off, but given that the very first example aligns with the escape clause for being a Goblin Queen I don't imagine it's too much of a stretch for it to be a full payment. The Goblin Debt is the promise of &quot;you still owe that guy&quot; \u2014 it's the Wyrd having a red line in your ledger because agreed-upon payment is contextual and just because you gave someone something doesn't mean what they give you was an exchange. Attention to wording is key when dealing with the fae.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in the case of a changeling, especially one who accrues debt point only with contracts, how does this differ?<br /> Does their knowledge of the laws of wyrd help them better understands those deals ramifications? </div> </div> </div>Remember that the Lost have big raggedy tears in their souls that their Icons came out of and a marked tendency to burst contagious emotion onto all observers through Bedlam, and the same bargain they struck with Faerie by escaping that lets them slip any bonds or wriggle out of a giant's grasp can easily be pointed to as a thematic neighbor to &quot;the Hedge's bill collectors won't have something on you forever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T06:55:31-08:00","id":1469831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469768#post1469768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Goblin Debt is the promise of &amp;quot;you still owe that guy&amp;quot; \u2014 it's the Wyrd having a red line in your ledger because agreed-upon payment is contextual and just because you gave someone something doesn't mean what they give you was an exchange. Attention to wording is key when dealing with the fae.;</div> </div> </div> </div>I m not sure to understand this part of the reply (mainly for meaning lost in translation).<br /> Do you mean that even if the Goblin says &quot;i give you X if you give me Y&quot; there is a difference in value between X and Y that accrues as a debt?<br /> Or that there is a clause in the deal in which the Goblin imply that you must give him Y and D ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T14:55:46-08:00","id":1469874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469831#post1469831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I m not sure to understand this part of the reply (mainly for meaning lost in translation).<br /> Do you mean that even if the Goblin says &quot;i give you X if you give me Y&quot; there is a difference in value between X and Y that accrues as a debt?<br /> Or that there is a clause in the deal in which the Goblin imply that you must give him Y and D ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I mean that hobgoblin deals tend not to be material trades \u2014 the relevant section gives two examples where the exchange is service-for-agreement. Following the second example in that section, Bob's trade of chocolate for Sweet Dreams didn't incur Debt because the train starts rolling on him when he comes back for the follow-up fix, just like the goblin cobbler's agreement to repair the worker's shoes. The sample court system built around a Goblin Market runs through a short list of valid &quot;currencies,&quot; and material exchange is only one item on that list for a reason.<br /> <br /> Remember: hobgoblin deals accrue Debt slower than Goblin Contracts, but Goblin Debt eventually turns someone into a goblin with Goblin Contracts that they can use &quot;for free&quot; while they're in a state that allows them to make hobgoblin deals and freely change their goblin toolkit every morning. The advice for designing Goblin Contracts begins: &quot;Imagine a problem. Now imagine a goblin. How does he solve it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe The Hedge will say differently as far as how Goblin Markets work with regard to Goblin Debt, but by my reckoning the point of the system is not to cover every possible act of exchange a goblin partakes in.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblin deals are made to <i>keep people coming back</i>. If that means neglecting to mention that there's unlisted side-effects to that night of pleasant dreams that you've got the cure for, fine. If that means offering a customer's first visit at a cutthroat price, so be it. The point is to get your hooks in them and <i>extract worth</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-07-2021, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T10:36:52-08:00","id":1469931,"title":"","content":"I am making NPCs and I have questions.<br /> 1) So Changelings get turned back into a human form when they first emerge from the Hedge, described as \u201croughly humanoid\u201d, but what are the limits of that? If I wanted, let\u2019s say a Centaur, is that roughly within the limits?<br /> 1.5) if so, how does the Mask handle the horse bits, since they should take up more space?<br /> 2) Can someone trade their memories for a services in a Goblin Market or to pay Goblin debt?<br /> 2.5) If someone has some memories they would rather be rid of, can they try to be clever and trade those memories and get something else, or is memory removal it\u2019s own service?<br /> 2.75) Is it conceivable that a Mirrorskin might trade enough of their memories away, in order to help them cope, that they no longer remember anything of who they were?<br /> 3) While looking though homebrew and conversions of kiths, I found one of Chimera that uses the basic Skin Deep Atavism from Beast to represent mutations. While Chimera now has a (cool) official kith for 2e, I think the idea of a constantly mutating kith might not be a horrible idea. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:02:30-08:00","id":1469934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469931#post1469931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am making NPCs and I have questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) If you put a blanket over it, can it pass as a human under a blanket? A centaur is clearly off limits. Otherwise the Mask can make weird stuff or just render uncommon bit invisible, like horns or extra appendages.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, I guess. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> will know better.<br /> <br /> 2.5) Do not try to be overly clever. The value of something at the Market is based on its worth for you. If you want to get rid of your memories, then this will be a service. But memories that you cherish serve as payment.<br /> <br /> 2.75) Yes.<br /> <br /> 3) Maybe under another name. My only gripes with it is that the concept of a Chimera is of a mixture, not a flux. You have other legends across the world about creatures that change shape into myriad other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:22:40-08:00","id":1469961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469931#post1469931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) So Changelings get turned back into a human form when they first emerge from the Hedge, described as \u201croughly humanoid\u201d, but what are the limits of that? If I wanted, let\u2019s say a Centaur, is that roughly within the limits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The general trend is that the further from an ordinary human body plan you go, the higher your Wyrd tends to be; if you want to hew closely to that trend and/or lean into gradual body horror, I'd start with just having horse legs and progress to the extra feet from there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1.5) if so, how does the Mask handle the horse bits, since they should take up more space? </div> </div> </div>Same way it handles the giant rack of antlers on the Hunterheart \u2014 people might notice that you have to take extra care not to bump into things while turning around or bump your head on doorframes a lot, but to a casual observer the inhuman bits will be interpreted in a way attributable to mundane (if notable) proportions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Can someone trade their memories for a services in a Goblin Market or to pay Goblin debt? </div> </div> </div>Memories of your grandmother (as an example of &quot;something dear to [you]&quot; is specifically given as an example for what you would have to part with to pay down Goblin Debt, so yes, almost certainly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.5) If someone has some memories they would rather be rid of, can they try to be clever and trade those memories and get something else, or is memory removal it\u2019s own service? </div> </div> </div>See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468345#post1468345\">the quotes from &quot;The Market&quot;</a> \u2014 you can try to play the system by getting something for someone else through the Market, but price is a matter of need, so if you don't need the thing you're giving up, it's going to trade for lower worth than something you don't want to get rid of.<br /> <br /> There might be a deal with unpleasant fine print to it that would accept seemingly-unwanted memories as a valid payment for something substantial, but as I mentioned earlier, that's Step 1 of a hustle that ends with you losing the shirt off your back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.75) Is it conceivable that a Mirrorskin might trade enough of their memories away, in order to help them cope, that they no longer remember anything of who they were? </div> </div> </div>Sure is, to the point where it's adjacent to at least two offhand-mentioned example characters in 1e. Remember also, though, that the Thorns can offer this &quot;service&quot; as an incidental effect of taking a wrong turn towards a different goal; it's definitely ironic enough as a bad end to a journey to be comfortable with oneself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) While looking though homebrew and conversions of kiths, I found one of Chimera that uses the basic Skin Deep Atavism from Beast to represent mutations. While Chimera now has a (cool) official kith for 2e, I think the idea of a constantly mutating kith might not be a horrible idea. What do you think? </div> </div> </div>Run through the design process on p304-6 and figure out what you want the kith to be mutating <i>for</i>. Note also that the first piece of kith design advice in Winter Masques (which is from 1e, but still reasonably applicable in 2e) is as follows:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A blessing isn\u2019t a Contract. A blessing is a neat trick or a particular affinity, not a showy supernatural power or a dramatic full-body modification. There are exceptions to the rule, of course, but a blessing should mirror the fact that the kith is for a changeling, not a True Fae. Changelings haven\u2019t been fully changed into the stuff of Faerie. A particularly dramatic change such as a Gargantuan\u2019s ability to grow should probably have a tradeoff as dramatic. </div> </div> </div>2e's version of Chimera gives you a limited version of one of the benefits of being a Hedge Denizen without the tradeoff of losing access to the benefits of your Mantle, and the cost is that you have to cycle through all the Goblin Contracts you know on a chapter-by-chapter basis before you can benefit from the same Contract Debt-free for another chapter. Replicating a highly visible and variable power from another gameline is going to be iffy without a suitably interesting counterbalance, particularly since most of Skin Deep's sample listing encompasses Athletics, Brawl, or Perception rolls or just having the right Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T18:31:42-08:00","id":1469985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469961#post1469961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general trend is that the further from an ordinary human body plan you go, the higher your Wyrd tends to be; if you want to hew closely to that trend and/or lean into gradual body horror, I'd start with just having horse legs and progress to the extra feet from there.<br /> <br /> Same way it handles the giant rack of antlers on the Hunterheart \u2014 people might notice that you have to take extra care not to bump into things while turning around or bump your head on doorframes a lot, but to a casual observer the inhuman bits will be interpreted in a way attributable to mundane (if notable) proportions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Got it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469961#post1469961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Memories of your grandmother (as an example of &quot;something dear to [you]&quot; is specifically given as an example for what you would have to part with to pay down Goblin Debt, so yes, almost certainly.</div> </div> </div> </div> How did I miss that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469961#post1469961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468345#post1468345\">the quotes from &quot;The Market&quot;</a> \u2014 you can try to play the system by getting something for someone else through the Market, but price is a matter of need, so if you don't need the thing you're giving up, it's going to trade for lower worth than something you don't want to get rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense. At least you can get something out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469961#post1469961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There might be a deal with unpleasant fine print to it that would accept seemingly-unwanted memories as a valid payment for something substantial, but as I mentioned earlier, that's Step 1 of a hustle that ends with you losing the shirt off your back.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a interesting point. Deals with goblins never really end, if the goblin can help it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469961#post1469961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure is, to the point where it's adjacent to at least two offhand-mentioned example characters in 1e. Remember also, though, that the Thorns can offer this &quot;service&quot; as an incidental effect of taking a wrong turn towards a different goal; it's definitely ironic enough as a bad end to a journey to be comfortable with oneself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do those characters happen to also be Spring Court characters trying to start completely fresh?<br /> <br /> Do the Thorns still steal pieces of the souls of Changelings, even after their return? Or is the memory loss from the dramatic failures inflicting a condition part? Or were you referring to Icons, and that went straight over my head?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469961#post1469961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Run through the design process on p304-6 and figure out what you want the kith to be mutating <i>for</i>. Note also that the first piece of kith design advice in Winter Masques (which is from 1e, but still reasonably applicable in 2e) is as follows:<br /> <br /> 2e's version of Chimera gives you a limited version of one of the benefits of being a Hedge Denizen without the tradeoff of losing access to the benefits of your Mantle, and the cost is that you have to cycle through all the Goblin Contracts you know on a chapter-by-chapter basis before you can benefit from the same Contract Debt-free for another chapter. Replicating a highly visible and variable power from another gameline is going to be iffy without a suitably interesting counterbalance, particularly since most of Skin Deep's sample listing encompasses Athletics, Brawl, or Perception rolls or just having the right Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. My concept for this kith would adaptability or fluidity of form. This shouldn\u2019t be a disguise, or otherwise it would be a Mirrorskin. So I think the idea should be having major flexibility in the trickery, but being extremely limited in power in exchange. Which ends up being roughly the same thing as Skin Deep anyway. *sigh*<br /> <br /> Beast\u2019s Skin Deep allows Lair/2 modifications that cause breaking points when witnessed, and the Beast may retract these as a Instant action. In exchange these modifications are minor (somewhat, Beasts\u2019s power scale is weird) and limited to extremely physical things. Beast\u2019s basic version can make these without any cost, but require a instant action. Changeling\u2019s powers are on the whole weaker than Beasts, or have a cost when roughly identical. So I think Changeling\u2019s version needs a glamour cost and a roll, Stamina + Survival probably. But I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s enough to distinguish the two. I decided to compare Ravenous Maw and the Gristlegrinder\u2019s trickery, since I thought they did roughly the same thing. Now I\u2019m even more confused, because Ravenous Maw doesn\u2019t include any effects after you swallow someone with the low satiety option. I guess the target just dies? Or is in the stomach of the Beast? Otherwise the two are identical except the Gristlegrinder\u2019s roll isn\u2019t a grapple, just a normal roll. And inflicts lethal acid damage while someone is in the stomach. And the Gristlegrinder has a lethal bite for free. Actually, looking at the two, Changeling\u2019s trickery is more powerful, but with a glamour cost. I don\u2019t really know what to make of this. So instead I compared Enemy Within and Mirrorskin. Enemy Within is the same as the Mirrorskin, except other Fae things can see though it by default, and it doesn\u2019t have a cost.<br /> <br /> After looking at the Homebrew, it seems they solved it by having the modifications being unable to be retracted and stay around forever, and once you reach to cap of modifications you must start exchanging the older modification for a new ones. It\u2019s not directly stated in the Homebrew, but these modifications don\u2019t cause breaking points, since the author chose to copy the text of the Atavism except that part. I guess the Mask covers it up the majority of the modifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-08-2021, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T19:47:13-08:00","id":1469991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469985#post1469985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do those characters happen to also be Spring Court characters trying to start completely fresh?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are incidental examples of Mirrorskin changelings and that is the most I can tell you from memory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the Thorns still steal pieces of the souls of Changelings, even after their return? Or is the memory loss from the dramatic failures inflicting a condition part? Or were you referring to Icons, and that went straight over my head? </div> </div> </div>The second one, with a more temporary side of &quot;the Hedge can more easily get a paradigm shift in the Thorns and one of the listed paradigm shifts for Hedgespinning is applying a Persistent Condition (of which Amnesia is one) that lasts until you leave the Hedge or get your memory back.&quot;<br /> <br /> Less temporarily and more prosaically, a goblin taking your memories doesn't have to be doing so as part of an exchange (although that's still a good racket it you can get it going, too). Nasty stuff hangs out in the Thorns by definition, and not for nothing is one of the sample Dread Powers for hobgoblins &quot;the goblin siphons off your memories, which you might be able to get back depending on how the specific instance of the power works vis-a-vis storage and disposal.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm. My concept for this kith would adaptability or fluidity of form. This shouldn\u2019t be a disguise, or otherwise it would be a Mirrorskin. So I think the idea should be having major flexibility in the trickery, but being extremely limited in power in exchange. Which ends up being roughly the same thing as Skin Deep anyway. *sigh*<br /> <br /> Beast\u2019s Skin Deep allows Lair/2 modifications that cause breaking points when witnessed, and the Beast may retract these as a Instant action. In exchange these modifications are minor (somewhat, Beasts\u2019s power scale is weird) and limited to extremely physical things. Beast\u2019s basic version can make these without any cost, but require a instant action. Changeling\u2019s powers are on the whole weaker than Beasts, or have a cost when roughly identical. So I think Changeling\u2019s version needs a glamour cost and a roll, Stamina + Survival probably. But I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s enough to distinguish the two. </div> </div> </div>You could have it modify the act of dropping the Mask, if that helps sync things up, but I should point out from experience that trying to make a Swiss Army Character tends to run into either the Bland Everyman problem or the Chase Two Rabbits Catch Neither problem. Having a concrete concept works dramatically better.<br /> <br /> I would guess, to route this back to the design process, that this is a Physically-oriented kith whose Skill blessing relates to one of the non-tool-oriented Physical Skills, or possibly Medicine. A thing that may help narrow this decision: what is any character with this kith best-suited to use as their go-to approach for Hedgespinning or oneiromancy or in-a-pinch Willpower recovery (through the Inspired Condition) due to a lowered threshold for exceptional success?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I decided to compare Ravenous Maw and the Gristlegrinder\u2019s trickery, since I thought they did roughly the same thing. Now I\u2019m even more confused, because Ravenous Maw doesn\u2019t include any effects after you swallow someone with the low satiety option. I guess the target just dies? Or is in the stomach of the Beast? Otherwise the two are identical except the Gristlegrinder\u2019s roll isn\u2019t a grapple, just a normal roll. And inflicts lethal acid damage while someone is in the stomach. And the Gristlegrinder has a lethal bite for free. Actually, looking at the two, Changeling\u2019s trickery is more powerful, but with a glamour cost. I don\u2019t really know what to make of this. </div> </div> </div>The Gristlegrinder kith blessing only works on things with a lower Size than you, apart from the ability to make bite attacks without a grapple, and even without a lucky roll a target who can survive long enough to knock the Gristlegrinder out from inside (with attacks ignoring Defense and Armor and Changeling being a game where setting yourself on fire or having claws are commonplace abilities) can allow you to use a Killing Blow to break free.<br /> <br /> Ravenous Maw's equivalent to To Serve Man is the Satiety Expenditure effect as a prelude to using the Low Satiety effect for body-disposal. The Low Satiety effect alone in this context establishes that if you eat something, its presence is not going to be causing you problems later, given that its precondition for using it on living creatures involves subduing them and &quot;success&quot; in an ongoing grapple to consume them means one of you stops grappling the other; if they're able to grapple with you, they're consumed when they're dead or unconscious, which you can help along by using the Damage move on each successful grapple roll.<br /> <br /> The takeaway, though, is that a kith Trickery about being able to swallow stuff that's smaller than the character but gives no special resistance to the complications of eating nasty stuff shouldn't be looking to an Atavism whose core basis is in being able to safely eat stuff that would otherwise really hurt to eat (including stuff much larger than them) as a mechanical comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T21:18:35-08:00","id":1470004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469991#post1469991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second one, with a more temporary side of &quot;the Hedge can more easily get a paradigm shift in the Thorns and one of the listed paradigm shifts for Hedgespinning is applying a Persistent Condition (of which Amnesia is one) that lasts until you leave the Hedge or get your memory back.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I didn\u2019t think about Hedgespinning. That\u2019s evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469991#post1469991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less temporarily and more prosaically, a goblin taking your memories doesn't have to be doing so as part of an exchange (although that's still a good racket it you can get it going, too). Nasty stuff hangs out in the Thorns by definition, and not for nothing is one of the sample Dread Powers for hobgoblins &quot;the goblin siphons off your memories, which you might be able to get back depending on how the specific instance of the power works vis-a-vis storage and disposal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that power is actually what lead me on this line of thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469991#post1469991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have it modify the act of dropping the Mask, if that helps sync things up, but I should point out from experience that trying to make a Swiss Army Character tends to run into either the Bland Everyman problem or the Chase Two Rabbits Catch Neither problem. Having a concrete concept works dramatically better.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s an interesting idea. Maybe three glamor and dropping the mask causes some less than subtle physical changes. Hmm\u2026Everything I\u2019m thinking of is either lame, or basically just what another kith would do. I will work on it. I still want some small subtle changes though, eyes opening in places they just weren\u2019t there before is just a fun image. My main image for this is a lumpy thing in robes, with eyes in unusual places, and maybe a tentacle or two. Later, they are trying to catch a desert creature and give up the eyes and tentacles for being cold blooded and scales. Maybe they later hide from their Huntsman by hiding underwater in a swamp and growing gills in exchange for their cold blood. I\u2019m personally ok with a slightly terrible Jay of all Traits, as long as they have interesting options and choices available. I just want them to be able to have the means to survive any environment, and maybe have some fun body horror with benefits. I\u2019ll work on it.<br /> <br /> On a side note, do you think an update to Polychromatics could feasibly modify Bedlam? Maybe spend extra Glamour for more conditions, like the exceptional success?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469991#post1469991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would guess, to route this back to the design process, that this is a Physically-oriented kith whose Skill blessing relates to one of the non-tool-oriented Physical Skills, or possibly Medicine. A thing that may help narrow this decision: what is any character with this kith best-suited to use as their go-to approach for Hedgespinning or oneiromancy or in-a-pinch Willpower recovery (through the Inspired Condition) due to a lowered threshold for exceptional success?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the best option is one that leverages their body as a tool, closely followed by trying to adapt to or tough out a hostile environment. So Survival rolls to endure tilts caused by extreme environments is probably my go to. I guess could see intimidation as a possibility, they probably should be pretty good that that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469991#post1469991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gristlegrinder kith blessing only works on things with a lower Size than you, apart from the ability to make bite attacks without a grapple, and even without a lucky roll a target who can survive long enough to knock the Gristlegrinder out from inside (with attacks ignoring Defense and Armor and Changeling being a game where setting yourself on fire or having claws are commonplace abilities) can allow you to use a Killing Blow to break free.<br /> <br /> Ravenous Maw's equivalent to To Serve Man is the Satiety Expenditure effect as a prelude to using the Low Satiety effect for body-disposal. The Low Satiety effect alone in this context establishes that if you eat something, its presence is not going to be causing you problems later, given that its precondition for using it on living creatures involves subduing them and &quot;success&quot; in an ongoing grapple to consume them means one of you stops grappling the other; if they're able to grapple with you, they're consumed when they're dead or unconscious, which you can help along by using the Damage move on each successful grapple roll.<br /> <br /> The takeaway, though, is that a kith Trickery about being able to swallow stuff that's smaller than the character but gives no special resistance to the complications of eating nasty stuff shouldn't be looking to an Atavism whose core basis is in being able to safely eat stuff that would otherwise really hurt to eat (including stuff much larger than them) as a mechanical comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for this analysis. I agree completely with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-09-2021, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T19:18:34-08:00","id":1470100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470004#post1470004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s an interesting idea. Maybe three glamor and dropping the mask causes some less than subtle physical changes. Hmm\u2026Everything I\u2019m thinking of is either lame, or basically just what another kith would do. I will work on it. I still want some small subtle changes though, eyes opening in places they just weren\u2019t there before is just a fun image. My main image for this is a lumpy thing in robes, with eyes in unusual places, and maybe a tentacle or two. Later, they are trying to catch a desert creature and give up the eyes and tentacles for being cold blooded and scales. Maybe they later hide from their Huntsman by hiding underwater in a swamp and growing gills in exchange for their cold blood. I\u2019m personally ok with a slightly terrible Jay of all Traits, as long as they have interesting options and choices available. I just want them to be able to have the means to survive any environment, and maybe have some fun body horror with benefits. I\u2019ll work on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To put some context on this:<br /> <br /> In Deviant: the Renegades, a lot of the Clade Variations for Invasives are specifically built as Swiss-Army Powers \u2014 the core list is five items that include the &quot;gain your pick from this subset of Merits&quot; power, the &quot;gain dots in your choice of Skill&quot; power, the &quot;gain specialized forms of perception/perception filters on the fly&quot; power, and the &quot;you can produce useful equipment at will&quot; power.<br /> <br /> This works for a couple reasons, chief among them being 1) Deviant powers manifest through the basic concept of their highly-individualized supernatural state and almost universally come with attached drawbacks for all but the weakest Variations, and 2) even without an attached drawback, the driving impetus of a deviant's Touchstones gives a very clear direction to bend that versatility towards.<br /> <br /> The Invasives are also often one of the more consistently gross/blunt/mundane Clades in their manifestation. Their powers come from bodily merging with nonliving material in a way that lets them shrug off a substantial amount of harm by &quot;damaging&quot; their Variations instead, which, while a striking concept, is somewhat unglamorous compared to their counterparts' ability to ratchet up the strength of their powers, drop the intensity of their Scars down to the &quot;take a Beat for roleplaying it&quot; level,&quot; or temporarily trade out their Variations for a weaker pick from the Universal list.<br /> <br /> Notably, that last one is the signature trick of the Mutants, who 1) as the &quot;biology is fucking weird&quot; Clade, are the other archetypically &quot;ugly&quot; category of deviant, 2) basically flip the Invasives' shtick by having a Swiss-Army Power in their innate kit and a set of Clade Variations built chiefly mostly around survivability (the &quot;regenerate&quot; and &quot;eat anything&quot; powers are on their list, as are &quot;bleed acid&quot; and &quot;don't need to breathe/eat/sleep&quot;).<br /> <br /> There's kind of an inverted &quot;form follows function&quot; thing going on there, with versatility coming at the price of visual refinement. (Not to say the other three Clades can't be right messes, but psychics, half-human hybrids, and people infused with mundane or otherworldly energies are a lot easier to romanticize next to the more hard sci-fi-adjacent categories of cyborgs and mutants.)<br /> <br /> In Changeling, the closest thing on the books to a kith that's constantly shifting for myriad small bonuses is the mechanics for Actors being able to switch kiths at will and even gin up unique pseudo-kiths representing a particular shape or attitude of that Actor, such that they get a persistent bonus of a die or two to represent those minor talents.<br /> <br /> Actors are True Fae as they're most recognizably encountered, and Equinox Road, where these mechanics are presented, is the endgame book for Changeling 1e, covering high-Wyrd changelings, journeys into Arcadia, and the nature and mechanics of Faerie beyond the feverish blotted-out recollections available through the haze of Clarity and beginning Wyrd. I would not use them as a basis for a kith, specifically because their mechanics represent something more and less than a kith.<br /> <br /> Also, in Changeling, the Mask specifically covers up or glosses over overt supernatural qualities, which is the main reason why my suggestion involved modifying dropping the Mask; Changeling's take on body horror lines up with its take on alienation through the fact that, maddeningly enough, most people cannot see the evidence (as clear as day to your Wyrded eyes) that you are no longer entirely human unless you shred their comforting illusions in a burst of Glamour or let them see you in their dreams or in the hungry thicket that wants to enslave you and them and everyone.<br /> <br /> Gamelines like Deviant (and to a lesser extent Demon) play with body horror that is persistently visible under certain circumstances, and hiding your inhuman state is a recurrent aspect of those games. Oftentimes, if a changeling's supernatural state has left them with odd needs or hungers, the ease with which they can turn to the Hedge to help them get patched up or keep them in rare goblin methodone means their physiological problems aren't what directly drives them into conflict with people.<br /> <br /> A deviant who can't survive more than three hours out of the water has to steal, borrow, or improvise an environment suit or an aquatic route to make a major trip inland, and even if he wasn't incentivized to stay in the material world where there are more people to hate and/or protect, he doesn't have a near-native's access to a dreamlike dimension where anything and everything is up for sale for the right price. Demons inhabit a world where they can exploit a great many shortcuts but their pursuers are that much closer, and breaking into secure facilities is necessary for a few major forms of damage control from people knowing more about you than they should.<br /> <br /> Changeling is a game of Beautiful Madness, and while it was established early on that &quot;beauty&quot; means a lot of things, there should still be some sense of elegance in how a piece of fae magic manifests \u2014 &quot;ugly&quot; things are off-putting on purpose or in a way where someone could theoretically admire the &quot;craft&quot; put into making something repellent, and the lens's takes on the Uncanny Valley tend to be the result of &quot;looking natural&quot; not being the artistic goal of those specimens' maker's view of perfection (when they aren't just deliberately made to be creepy in that particular way).<br /> <br /> Applications of fae talent can be appreciated through the senses. Generalizing this to whole-body affairs like kiths, the thing that makes it <i>compelling</i> should probably factor into the thing that it's good at \u2014 form follows function, and the form is appealing at least in the sense that the design is coherent and does what it's set out to do (which, as changelings' miens tend to factor in some of their inner lives in their development over time, makes that Dolly Parton quote about finding out who you are and doing it on purpose extra useful advice).<br /> <br /> This kind of got away from me in the composition, but hopefully you can see what I'm getting at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a side note, do you think an update to Polychromatics could feasibly modify Bedlam? Maybe spend extra Glamour for more conditions, like the exceptional success? </div> </div> </div>That's the direct contrapositive of how the old Polychromatic blessing worked, but it's certainly in the same neck of the woods. For their Blessing, were you thinking of something like Persuasion rolls to manipulate characters who are under the effects of Bedlam?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the best option is one that leverages their body as a tool, closely followed by trying to adapt to or tough out a hostile environment. So Survival rolls to endure tilts caused by extreme environments is probably my go to. I guess could see intimidation as a possibility, they probably should be pretty good that that. </div> </div> </div>Definitely keep pinning down the core idea, for the reasons outlined previously.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, an offhand suggestion for the Trickery:<br /> <br /> When dropping the Mask or entering the Hedge, the [tktk kith name goes here] may roll Stamina + Survival to gain up to their Wyrd in Merit dots to divide between the Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes, Fleet of Foot, Giant, Iron Stamina, Lethal Mien, Small-Framed, Striking Looks, or Trained Observer Merits until her Mask reasserts itself. She may reassign these Merit dots with an instant action and a point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T22:53:31-08:00","id":1470111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put some context on this:<br /> <br /> In Deviant: the Renegades, a lot of the Clade Variations for Invasives are specifically built as Swiss-Army Powers \u2014 the core list is five items that include the &quot;gain your pick from this subset of Merits&quot; power, the &quot;gain dots in your choice of Skill&quot; power, the &quot;gain specialized forms of perception/perception filters on the fly&quot; power, and the &quot;you can produce useful equipment at will&quot; power.<br /> <br /> This works for a couple reasons, chief among them being 1) Deviant powers manifest through the basic concept of their highly-individualized supernatural state and almost universally come with attached drawbacks for all but the weakest Variations, and 2) even without an attached drawback, the driving impetus of a deviant's Touchstones gives a very clear direction to bend that versatility towards.<br /> <br /> The Invasives are also often one of the more consistently gross/blunt/mundane Clades in their manifestation. Their powers come from bodily merging with nonliving material in a way that lets them shrug off a substantial amount of harm by &quot;damaging&quot; their Variations instead, which, while a striking concept, is somewhat unglamorous compared to their counterparts' ability to ratchet up the strength of their powers, drop the intensity of their Scars down to the &quot;take a Beat for roleplaying it&quot; level,&quot; or temporarily trade out their Variations for a weaker pick from the Universal list.<br /> <br /> Notably, that last one is the signature trick of the Mutants, who 1) as the &quot;biology is fucking weird&quot; Clade, are the other archetypically &quot;ugly&quot; category of deviant, 2) basically flip the Invasives' shtick by having a Swiss-Army Power in their innate kit and a set of Clade Variations built chiefly mostly around survivability (the &quot;regenerate&quot; and &quot;eat anything&quot; powers are on their list, as are &quot;bleed acid&quot; and &quot;don't need to breathe/eat/sleep&quot;).<br /> <br /> There's kind of an inverted &quot;form follows function&quot; thing going on there, with versatility coming at the price of visual refinement. (Not to say the other three Clades can't be right messes, but psychics, half-human hybrids, and people infused with mundane or otherworldly energies are a lot easier to romanticize next to the more hard sci-fi-adjacent categories of cyborgs and mutants.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I think my part of my problem then, is that I\u2019m trying take some of the thematics around Mutants by using the Invasive Claude variations. I\u2019m not sure if I should attach something like a scar to the power to direct it, technically Changelings get frailties much like scars already. Oooh, what if you could take a temporary frailty in exchange for more power? Oh wait, Cleverquick kinda already did this. And anyway that leaves the choice of frailty in the hands of the player would be difficult to balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Changeling, the closest thing on the books to a kith that's constantly shifting for myriad small bonuses is the mechanics for Actors being able to switch kiths at will and even gin up unique pseudo-kiths representing a particular shape or attitude of that Actor, such that they get a persistent bonus of a die or two to represent those minor talents.<br /> <br /> Actors are True Fae as they're most recognizably encountered, and Equinox Road, where these mechanics are presented, is the endgame book for Changeling 1e, covering high-Wyrd changelings, journeys into Arcadia, and the nature and mechanics of Faerie beyond the feverish blotted-out recollections available through the haze of Clarity and beginning Wyrd. I would not use them as a basis for a kith, specifically because their mechanics represent something more and less than a kith.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um. Well I knew that being able to change kiths constantly around was a bad idea, even if it was linked to dropping the Mask, but wow. I didn\u2019t realize that was a feature of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in Changeling, the Mask specifically covers up or glosses over overt supernatural qualities, which is the main reason why my suggestion involved modifying dropping the Mask; Changeling's take on body horror lines up with its take on alienation through the fact that, maddeningly enough, most people cannot see the evidence (as clear as day to your Wyrded eyes) that you are no longer entirely human unless you shred their comforting illusions in a burst of Glamour or let them see you in their dreams or in the hungry thicket that wants to enslave you and them and everyone.<br /> <br /> Gamelines like Deviant (and to a lesser extent Demon) play with body horror that is persistently visible under certain circumstances, and hiding your inhuman state is a recurrent aspect of those games. Oftentimes, if a changeling's supernatural state has left them with odd needs or hungers, the ease with which they can turn to the Hedge to help them get patched up or keep them in rare goblin methodone means their physiological problems aren't what directly drives them into conflict with people.<br /> <br /> A deviant who can't survive more than three hours out of the water has to steal, borrow, or improvise an environment suit or an aquatic route to make a major trip inland, and even if he wasn't incentivized to stay in the material world where there are more people to hate and/or protect, he doesn't have a near-native's access to a dreamlike dimension where anything and everything is up for sale for the right price. Demons inhabit a world where they can exploit a great many shortcuts but their pursuers are that much closer, and breaking into secure facilities is necessary for a few major forms of damage control from people knowing more about you than they should.<br /> <br /> Changeling is a game of Beautiful Madness, and while it was established early on that &quot;beauty&quot; means a lot of things, there should still be some sense of elegance in how a piece of fae magic manifests \u2014 &quot;ugly&quot; things are off-putting on purpose or in a way where someone could theoretically admire the &quot;craft&quot; put into making something repellent, and the lens's takes on the Uncanny Valley tend to be the result of &quot;looking natural&quot; not being the artistic goal of those specimens' maker's view of perfection (when they aren't just deliberately made to be creepy in that particular way).<br /> <br /> Applications of fae talent can be appreciated through the senses. Generalizing this to whole-body affairs like kiths, the thing that makes it <i>compelling</i> should probably factor into the thing that it's good at \u2014 form follows function, and the form is appealing at least in the sense that the design is coherent and does what it's set out to do (which, as changelings' miens tend to factor in some of their inner lives in their development over time, makes that Dolly Parton quote about finding out who you are and doing it on purpose extra useful advice).</div> </div> </div> </div> Shredding comforting illusions is actually a good theme on how this kith should work with it\u2019s horror based off of it\u2019s inspiration. When put that way, I see why you suggested it. That\u2019s pretty clever.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I worry that this particular kith is too close to Deviant in theme. As mentioned above I\u2019m basically going for exactly the Mutants themes. As you mentioned, making the modifications tied to the dropping of the Mask is a good way to keep them separate. Another is that I think the kith on the whole would be more comfortable in their own skin than any Deviant would be. Changelings for better or worse don\u2019t have to deal with Instability, they get Clarity instead. (I guess Mental Instability can take a form similar to Clarity.)<br /> <br /> This kith is supposed to made when a keeper doesn\u2019t want to be bothered with continually changing a Changeling to fit a inconsistent realm and role. Why not make them into something that can just transform into whatever you need at that moment? Kinda like Shoggoths (as I understand them). Personally, I can see the elegance in making a fluid all purpose servant if you are too lazy to just remake it each time you need something new, and don\u2019t have enough pieces to work with. I also see that fluidity being extremely unsettling from a human perspective. It\u2019s not for nothing that the Beast version causes breaking points when seen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of got away from me in the composition, but hopefully you can see what I'm getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div> It was a lot, but I think I do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the direct contrapositive of how the old Polychromatic blessing worked, but it's certainly in the same neck of the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know, but I\u2019m having problems with how their blessing should work. The old Blessing was purely passive, but every new Trickery is a active power, that doesn\u2019t rely on outside conditions. Besides Notary, now that I think about it. So I tried to retool the concept to fit. My first concept was one where the Polychromatic was so full of emotion that it spread to others, and and realized that that effect was Bedlam. It makes sense that Polychromatics would be great at handling Bedlam, and my immediate thought was that a better Bedlam would have more emotions and conditions. If I continued down that line of thinking, maybe it would be better to have it specified, like projecting fear onto enemies and hope onto allies? Multiple contradictory emotional conditions on a single person might or might not make sense. If instead I wanted to be more in line with the old version, maybe I should have the Polychromatic be passively be aware of emotional manipulation, and be able to transform a emotional condition into another for a significant cost, much like the five dot spring mantle does for clarity conditions?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For their Blessing, were you thinking of something like Persuasion rolls to manipulate characters who are under the effects of Bedlam?</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much. I was thinking either Empathy to determine the source of a emotional condition, or Persuasion rolls to manipulate people with a condition matching the Polychromatic\u2019s current emotions. Both feel a bit broad, though? I haven\u2019t actually played a game of Changeling, so I\u2019m unsure of how often Bedlam comes up. If it\u2019s pretty common, or their Trickery encourages Bedlam to be more common, then the Blessing specifically requiring it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely keep pinning down the core idea, for the reasons outlined previously.</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470100#post1470100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, an offhand suggestion for the Trickery:<br /> <br /> When dropping the Mask or entering the Hedge, the [tktk kith name goes here] may roll Stamina + Survival to gain up to their Wyrd in Merit dots to divide between the Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes, Fleet of Foot, Giant, Iron Stamina, Lethal Mien, Small-Framed, Striking Looks, or Trained Observer Merits until her Mask reasserts itself. She may reassign these Merit dots with an instant action and a point of Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is just having a list of merits available a good idea for a kith? (Genuine question) I had come up with something similar when you suggested linking the transformation to the Mask, but I didn\u2019t think it was good, because a gain x dots of a merit didn\u2019t seem like it would be something you would see in a official kith. But I\u2019m rethinking it now you suggested it.<br /> <br /> The suggestion works pretty well mechanically I think, but I\u2019d like to expand the list with some inhuman merits that represent gills and tentacles. Do you think the physical Changeling only merits would be out of bounds, like Arcadian Body and Lethal Mien?<br /> <br /> Edit: Now that I have slept, and am not writing this right before I must sleep, I\u2019m hoping I\u2019m more coherent.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of naming the Kith Fluxform or maybe Strangeskin. I don\u2019t know, I\u2019m bad with names.<br /> <br /> Dropping the Mask and gain a pool of merits is a good idea. I\u2019m certain now. Apparently, I can\u2019t read because you do have Lethal Mien on the list. Looking at the general list of merits, I think Hardy, Freediving, and Double Jointed should be added. Survivalist should be added as well. Portaling is a thing, and serves a similar purpose, but Double Jointed is a logical extension of the Trickery. Of course, this brings up the question of whether you can escape from iron bindings using this trickery. I\u2019m inclined to say no, but one could make the argument that the Trickery technically doesn\u2019t effect the iron, just the Changeling. I\u2019d say that\u2019s the equivalent of saying a Changeling could use Whispers of Morning to get out. Another question is whether or not to use some of the Advanced Merits found in Beast. I think Advanced Double Jointed is fine for example, but not Advanced Giant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-10-2021, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T00:58:23-08:00","id":1470117,"title":"","content":"I m gonna use the Avalon freehold from Dark eras 2, and i was thinking about the Nanannan character (a changeling Darkling who is faking to be a Mekhet vampire).<br /> I think that he should at least be able to exude the Predatory aura, what is the easiest way for him to do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T08:26:01-08:00","id":1470136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470117#post1470117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m gonna use the Avalon freehold from Dark eras 2, and i was thinking about the Nanannan character (a changeling Darkling who is faking to be a Mekhet vampire).<br /> I think that he should at least be able to exude the Predatory aura, what is the easiest way for him to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>First thought is a variation of the Mantle Mask Goblin Contract (a Strix Contract, perhaps?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T09:19:13-08:00","id":1470143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470136#post1470136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First thought is a variation of the Mantle Mask Goblin Contract (a Strix Contract, perhaps?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhh, good idea !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T19:00:37-08:00","id":1470179,"title":"","content":"New question: How might a Hobgoblin show affection for a Changeling if they genuinely like them? I was thinking of a NPC that creates dolls, that may or may not be alive and semi-autonomous. Think Dance of the Toys and Hedgespun Automatons. I was thinking of one of the Dolls actually being a Hob, but they still like their \u201ccreator/parent\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T19:03:59-08:00","id":1470180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470179#post1470179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: How might a Hobgoblin show affection for a Changeling if they genuinely like them? I was thinking of a NPC that creates dolls, that may or may not be alive and semi-autonomous. Think Dance of the Toys and Hedgespun Automatons. I was thinking of one of the Dolls actually being a Hob, but they still like their \u201ccreator/parent\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing concrete, but cats gifting half-dead mice, roaches, birds etc. to humans immediately come to mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T19:51:54-08:00","id":1470182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470180#post1470180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing concrete, but cats gifting half-dead mice, roaches, birds etc. to humans immediately come to mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A fun note as an alternative direction to steer this in, especially given the Wyrd's reciprocal bent (or e.g. what Hob Kin opens up for Hollows):<br /> <br /> Cats do this because <a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/637681114186727424/rockyjonez-prokopetz-that-thing-about-how\" target=\"_blank\">housecats derive from African wildcats, who are social creatures that live in colonies</a>; when they bring you dead things, it's for the community food stash since as far as they can see you're a non-hunting member of the group and you're a creature that needs to eat just like they are.<br /> <br /> How that might translate for hobgoblins is, of course, a question of individuals, but there <i>is</i> that fun bit in Oak, Ash &amp; Thorn about not all hobgoblins understanding the transferral of a blazon's identity equally well\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T20:28:07-08:00","id":1470184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470182#post1470182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fun note as an alternative direction to steer this in, especially given the Wyrd's reciprocal bent (or e.g. what Hob Kin opens up for Hollows):</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s going get weird, because the Changeling is taking care of the Hob (badly), and the Hob is trying to take care of the Changeling (badly). This isn\u2019t helped by the Hob being nearly completely new, and having a hard time with humans, and the Changeling having a hard time with Clarity in general. (I\u2019m leaving it ambiguous as to what actually made the Hob.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470182#post1470182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cats do this because <a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/637681114186727424/rockyjonez-prokopetz-that-thing-about-how\" target=\"_blank\">housecats derive from African wildcats, who are social creatures that live in colonies</a>; when they bring you dead things, it's for the community food stash since as far as they can see you're a non-hunting member of the group and you're a creature that needs to eat just like they are.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I never knew that. That\u2019s just so adorable. Using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470182#post1470182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How that might translate for hobgoblins is, of course, a question of individuals, but there <i>is</i> that fun bit in Oak, Ash &amp; Thorn about not all hobgoblins understanding the transferral of a blazon's identity equally well\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yeah\u2026 that\u2019s going to be fun. The Changeling is definitely in their own weird personal Entitlement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T21:02:25-08:00","id":1470188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470111#post1470111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kith is supposed to made when a keeper doesn\u2019t want to be bothered with continually changing a Changeling to fit a inconsistent realm and role. Why not make them into something that can just transform into whatever you need at that moment? Kinda like Shoggoths (as I understand them). Personally, I can see the elegance in making a fluid all purpose servant if you are too lazy to just remake it each time you need something new, and don\u2019t have enough pieces to work with. I also see that fluidity being extremely unsettling from a human perspective. It\u2019s not for nothing that the Beast version causes breaking points when seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to draw another comparison that should hopefully illustrate why this doesn't quite sit right with me:<br /> <br /> In the initial drafts of Changeling 2e, Chimeras were mechanically fairly similar to their 1e incarnation \u2014 their kith blessing gave them bonus dice on Social rolls to interact with stuff from the Hedge, and they could spend Glamour to gain the rote quality on a roll to resist or avoid targeted supernatural effects. That's fine and good.<br /> <br /> The draft also said that some Chimeras were made by the Fae's attempts to develop new kiths by deliberately combining random bits of other kiths, but that most of them were the result of changelings being accidentally infused with too much of the stuff of Faerie and altering their bodies in an uncontrolled fashion. This\u2026 doesn't really work for a couple reasons, chief among them being that the initial drafts were still leaning very much into the Wyrd as a narrative force and the result is that there's a bunch of characters with a mechanically identical Special Quality whose sorting category that hobgoblins at the market chat about is basically &quot;none of the above&quot; (as distinct from &quot;none&quot;).<br /> <br /> Arc's big post elucidating the differences between Changeling and Demon comes to mind here, because the anthropomorphic tendencies of faerie stories feels at least adjacent to the fact that if something is distinct enough to have a name, it has definite qualities that can be attributed to it. (There are gamelines in the Chronicles of Darkness for which this is not a metaphysical truism, but Changeling is not one of those games at the player toolkit level.)<br /> <br /> <br /> On the Other end of things, if one of the Gentry is being characterized as &quot;too lazy&quot; to remake their servant for a bunch of different tasks, there are a number of less intensive processes they can go through instead of crafting a wildly variable kith that needs to be able to do any given one of the tasks they're set \u2014 they could enlist the aid of another Stranger, retain the services of a Darkling with Riddle-Kith, or just <i>get more slaves</i>. (Or swallow your pride and employ hobgoblins. The Hedge provides!)<br /> <br /> Remember, in their own domains the Gentry are functionally gods as far as their servants are concerned, and their sense of attachment can be weird, but the changes they wreak on the Lost are generally related to what they were taken for. If a Keeper decides, quite regularly, that they want to remodel their entire realm, they'll probably just get new people that suit the new d\u00e9cor rather than try to alter all of the existing help; if the old staff are lucky and the Keeper's sensibilities shift in cycles, they may still be alive when their job comes back around. If you don't have the resources to retain multiple specialists, the solution is typically to have a good generalist rather than try to create an omni-specialist.<br /> <br /> I guess, going back to the design process again, two operative questions come to mind for moving forward:<br /> 1. How available is this kith supposed to be in the game it is being developed for? (Prolific, Unique, or somewhere in-between?)<br /> 2. What is the seeming of the character this kith is being written for? (My first guesses are Beast or Wizened.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know, but I\u2019m having problems with how their blessing should work. The old Blessing was purely passive, but every new Trickery is a active power, that doesn\u2019t rely on outside conditions. [\u2026] If instead I wanted to be more in line with the old version, maybe I should have the Polychromatic be passively be aware of emotional manipulation, and be able to transform a emotional condition into another for a significant cost, much like the five dot spring mantle does for clarity conditions? </div> </div> </div>\u2026Know what other mechanic would probably be relevant to Polychromatics? Threads. A back-of-the-napkin draft:<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Polychromatic rolls Persuasion to influence somebody whose emotions currently align with her Thread, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>With Kaleidoscope Eyes:</i> By spending a point of Glamour, a Polychromatic can roll Composure + Empathy to shed a single emotional Condition, changing her Thread to a different one of her choice until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is just having a list of merits available a good idea for a kith? (Genuine question) I had come up with something similar when you suggested linking the transformation to the Mask, but I didn\u2019t think it was good, because a gain x dots of a merit didn\u2019t seem like it would be something you would see in a official kith. But I\u2019m rethinking it now you suggested it. </div> </div> </div>Lacking a more elegant phrasing for it, that was what I went with.<br /> <br /> Something that may be more mechanically elegant would be to take cues from Artist and build bonus dice and &quot;equipment&quot; off of the character's Specialties in (an) appropriate Physical Skill(s) and then just build a custom Merit that modifies how dropping the Mask works to fill the niche of being Visibly Weird in a way the necessitates cloaks and such to hide.<br /> <br /> (Always worth remembering: In the absence of specific mechanical widgets, Merits are the default part of the system to turn to for messing with the normal functioning of some part of the game in a way that's tied to character advancement.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T23:16:29-08:00","id":1470193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to draw another comparison that should hopefully illustrate why this doesn't quite sit right with me:<br /> <br /> In the initial drafts of Changeling 2e, Chimeras were mechanically fairly similar to their 1e incarnation \u2014 their kith blessing gave them bonus dice on Social rolls to interact with stuff from the Hedge, and they could spend Glamour to gain the rote quality on a roll to resist or avoid targeted supernatural effects. That's fine and good.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I like our current version of Chimera, I wonder why it was changed from this version?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The draft also said that some Chimeras were made by the Fae's attempts to develop new kiths by deliberately combining random bits of other kiths, but that most of them were the result of changelings being accidentally infused with too much of the stuff of Faerie and altering their bodies in an uncontrolled fashion. This\u2026 doesn't really work for a couple reasons, chief among them being that the initial drafts were still leaning very much into the Wyrd as a narrative force and the result is that there's a bunch of characters with a mechanically identical Special Quality whose sorting category that hobgoblins at the market chat about is basically &quot;none of the above&quot; (as distinct from &quot;none&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I understand that. Because they all are Unique it doesn\u2019t make sense for them for them to have a strict definition as a type of thing. It\u2019s kinda like Deviant is really a bunch of completely unique monster that are mostly unrelated to each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc's big post elucidating the differences between Changeling and Demon comes to mind here, because the anthropomorphic tendencies of faerie stories feels at least adjacent to the fact that if something is distinct enough to have a name, it has definite qualities that can be attributed to it. (There are gamelines in the Chronicles of Darkness for which this is not a metaphysical truism, but Changeling is not one of those games at the player toolkit level.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess this is a disconnect then, because I was under the impression that being mutable was a definite and defining quality in and of itself. Are you saying that\u2019s not the case?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Other end of things, if one of the Gentry is being characterized as &quot;too lazy&quot; to remake their servant for a bunch of different tasks, there are a number of less intensive processes they can go through instead of crafting a wildly variable kith that needs to be able to do any given one of the tasks they're set \u2014 they could enlist the aid of another Stranger, retain the services of a Darkling with Riddle-Kith, or just <i>get more slaves</i>. (Or swallow your pride and employ hobgoblins. The Hedge provides!)</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean this is fair, but I guess I don\u2019t understand the Others mind set at all. I chose that background because of Shoggoths being a vaguely similar creature to what I was doing, and they were created and enslaved to basically serve a role. That role being whatever the Elder Things wanted at the time. (They are basically robots as I understand) I figured that worked well enough to port over to Changeling. (I don\u2019t read Lovecraft, really but I browse wikis sometimes) Employing Hobgoblins would make much more sense, but I get the impression asking one of the Kindly Ones to swallow their pride just won\u2019t happen unless they are forced to. As for the Darkling with Riddle-Kith, that\u2019s a fair point. It would be better to be able to rapidly change specialties than be just being super adaptable. I don\u2019t think this invalidates the Kith though, unless Skinmask invalidates Mirrorskin. On the subject of contacts, this Kith really isn\u2019t that different from Talon and Wing. Talon and Wing doesn\u2019t explicitly say you can\u2019t get a creatures ability to survive in certain environments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, in their own domains the Gentry are functionally gods as far as their servants are concerned, and their sense of attachment can be weird, but the changes they wreak on the Lost are generally related to what they were taken for. If a Keeper decides, quite regularly, that they want to remodel their entire realm, they'll probably just get new people that suit the new d\u00e9cor rather than try to alter all of the existing help; if the old staff are lucky and the Keeper's sensibilities shift in cycles, they may still be alive when their job comes back around. If you don't have the resources to retain multiple specialists, the solution is typically to have a good generalist rather than try to create an omni-specialist.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that a Keeper who\u2019s whims continuously remold themselves and their realm are the only way this kith results. Regularly enough that getting new real people might actually be consistent problem. I don\u2019t know about you, but eventually I\u2019d get tired of all my toys breaking down, and if I was a powerful enough I\u2019d just make one that wouldn\u2019t. Maybe I\u2019m weird, but I like my stuff to last a while, even if I\u2019m rough with it. Or forget it exists. Getting new stuff is just so exhausting. (That just might be a me thing though) (The only way I can kinda approach the Others mindset is assuming my desires are the only thing that matters, and nothing else is really\u2026real.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, going back to the design process again, two operative questions come to mind for moving forward:<br /> 1. How available is this kith supposed to be in the game it is being developed for? (Prolific, Unique, or somewhere in-between?)<br /> 2. What is the seeming of the character this kith is being written for? (My first guesses are Beast or Wizened.)</div> </div> </div> </div> In-between, on the far end of rare, but not rare enough that someone devoted to documenting kiths wouldn\u2019t have heard of it. The Seeming this is designed for is definitely Beast. They are just supposed to fit whatever situation they wind up in, without needing input from their keeper, or needing to think about it. Their instincts will allow them to survive. That says Beast to me, where as a Wizened has some task they specialize in by performing it until it is perfect. (I might be using 1e sensibilities, though)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Know what other mechanic would probably be relevant to Polychromatics? Threads. A back-of-the-napkin draft:</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, yeah. You are really good at this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Polychromatic rolls Persuasion to influence somebody whose emotions currently align with her Thread, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>With Kaleidoscope Eyes:</i> By spending a point of Glamour, a Polychromatic can roll Composure + Empathy to shed a single emotional Condition, changing her Thread to a different one of her choice until the end of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div> *nods enthusiastically* I think this even ties in to their description of how their blessing worked in 1e. Let\u2019s see: \u201c<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Changeling can change her mood as if moving from color to color.</span></span></span>\u201d which translates easily into changing Threads. (Threads are a bit more than just a mood but it still works. Heck, it even plays into them being hard to read since I\u2019m pretty sure it would be confusing if you think you know someone\u2019s thread only for them to suddenly being radically different. I believe we have a winner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lacking a more elegant phrasing for it, that was what I went with.<br /> <br /> Something that may be more mechanically elegant would be to take cues from Artist and build bonus dice and &quot;equipment&quot; off of the character's Specialties in (an) appropriate Physical Skill(s) and then just build a custom Merit that modifies how dropping the Mask works to fill the niche of being Visibly Weird in a way the necessitates cloaks and such to hide.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is certainly more elegant. I\u2019m not sure I like it more than the list of merits though. Unless the specialities can move it\u2019s not really adaptable unless you really stretch the equipment bonuses. Might work as a Athlete Kith. Actually that sounds pretty cool. I bet the Fae Olympics is pretty interesting. The merit to modify dropping the mask is interesting. I don\u2019t think we have a merit for modifies the Mien when dropping the mask for benefits. It actually really suits a number of character archetypes like a berserker Beast or Ogre who want to drop the mask for a physical power boost even if they don\u2019t really use contracts. Do you think I should drop the kith in exchange for the merit? The kith could just be something like a Broadback or Cleverquick that really invests in that merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470188#post1470188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Always worth remembering: In the absence of specific mechanical widgets, Merits are the default part of the system to turn to for messing with the normal functioning of some part of the game in a way that's tied to character advancement.)</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s fair. I think I\u2019ve heard it said that Changeling powers are designed off of supernatural merits and given a fairy tale twist.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to say I do like the pool of merits. I edited one of my previous posts, but I don\u2019t think you saw that. To reiterate, I had few extra merits I thought could be added, and asked about Beast\u2019s advanced merits. I looked to see if any conversation had emerged about using the Advanced Merits, and I saw a previous conversation on this very thread about them. Now I\u2019d like to ask if there is any reason not to port the Advanced Merits that don\u2019t use Beast specific mechanics over if I thought it could fit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T05:52:37-08:00","id":1470216,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The simple question is now a large discussion. Probably good to make it its own thread now if you wish to continue.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T07:56:55-08:00","id":1470221,"title":"","content":"Very well. I am afraid that I will be very occupied with life events for today and the next few days, so I won\u2019t be able to create it immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T15:36:28-08:00","id":1471561,"title":"","content":"Does the Mask persist in the Astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T16:05:34-08:00","id":1471564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1471561#post1471561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Mask persist in the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in dreams, a part of Astral space, masks drops, i would say no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T01:17:15-08:00","id":1471582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1471561#post1471561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Mask persist in the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>Navigating the Astral uses a Dream Form (which is specifically unMasked), and physical entry into dreams is treated as being physically present in the Hedge (ditto), but sufficiently low Clarity might swing a changeling's internal context enough that their self-image presents as something other than their mien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T16:11:33-08:00","id":1472031,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m working on some npc characters in the freehold, so I have some questions:<br /> 1) Is sound a appropriate element for a Elemental? (Made a concept for a Elemental Whisperwhisp without thinking about it.)<br /> 1.5) If so, how much sound is enough so be surrounded for their blessing to work?<br /> 2) Would using red capsaicin from ogre peppers instead of normal capsaicin in pepper spray have a mechanical difference?<br /> 2.5) Would spray paint count as a improvised version of pepper spray? <br /> 2.75) if one had hedgespun \u201cpepper spray\u201d, could it do damage?<br /> 3) does the Parkour merit effect hedge navigation successes needed?<br /> 4) Is it possible to add hollow merits to a wagon? Or have a mobile hollow?<br /> 4.5) or have a token wagon that\u2019s bigger on the inside?<br /> 5) Does the Ogre blessing work Hedgewall and the Field of Thorns from Thorns and Brambles?<br /> 6) How powerful is the Notary blessing?<br /> 7) How does extended actions work with hedgespinning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T17:58:27-08:00","id":1472039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1472031#post1472031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is sound a appropriate element for a Elemental? (Made a concept for a Elemental Whisperwhisp without thinking about it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as I wouldn't make an earthquake elemental whose element was &quot;quaking,&quot; I'd recommend using the expected medium of the sound instead (most likely air, barring a particular sort of undersea durance).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Would using red capsaicin from ogre peppers instead of normal capsaicin in pepper spray have a mechanical difference? </div> </div> </div>ST's call. Maybe it takes twice as many turns to reduce the penalty, maybe it only needs one success to Stun a target, maybe it isn't meaningfully different in that use-case; goblin stuff is weird about the particulars of its application sometimes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.5) Would spray paint count as a improvised version of pepper spray? </div> </div> </div>Possibly, though I'd require a targeted attack to the eyes or reduce the penalty or both, given that spray paint does not have the particular chemical qualities that make pepper spray effective at what it does.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.75) if one had hedgespun \u201cpepper spray\u201d, could it do damage? </div> </div> </div>Its classification as a weapon notwithstanding, I feel like the specific quality of &quot;does no damage&quot; means it'd either get a dice bonus to the attack roll instead.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) does the Parkour merit effect hedge navigation successes needed? </div> </div> </div>The tricky thing about this is that the Parkour Merit pre-dates the Chase system, let alone the Hedge Navigation mechanics, and is largely ported over from the 1e version, which modeled chases as a contested Stamina + Athletics action; meanwhile, several forms of Hedge Navigation simply don't operate on principles for which Parkour is applicable. Make the call for your game and be consistent about it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Is it possible to add hollow merits to a wagon? Or have a mobile hollow? </div> </div> </div>1e had Mobile Hollow as a scaled Hollow add-on Merit from Swords at Dawn (p92-3) with prerequisites in Wyrd and Hollow Size; considering that Hollow is now capped at five dots, you could certainly try and gin up a scaled (maybe 1-3 dot) Hollow enhancement following a similar progression (though I'd recommend modeling it using variable stats to plug into the Hedge Navigation mechanics instead of porting the 1e version, which doesn't have a terribly smooth gradation on account of it juggling three or four different metrics of what one would find desirable in &quot;mobility.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4.5) or have a token wagon that\u2019s bigger on the inside? </div> </div> </div>This is much less hassle, yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) Does the Ogre blessing work Hedgewall and the Field of Thorns from Thorns and Brambles? </div> </div> </div>It's not the Ogre dealing the damage, so probably not.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) How powerful is the Notary blessing? </div> </div> </div>That's a bit of an open-ended question, but: they can prevent characters from having to spend the fuel they need at least one point of to keep from starving to make the sort of agreements their society runs on, get perfect memory of its wording for as long as those agreements last, and can more easily get Conditions (including the likes of Informed, Inspired, and Steadfast) from negotiating, reading, or interpreting those agreements. It's by no means game-breaking, but it definitely gives them a niche to exploit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7) How does extended actions work with hedgespinning? </div> </div> </div>This is spelled out on page 205 of the corebook: &quot;Extended actions in the Hedge can allocate successes to Hedgespinning as well, but each roll must immediately apply its excess successes to shaping during that interval; they don\u2019t accumulate over the course of the action.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T20:33:34-08:00","id":1475286,"title":"","content":"If a changeling transfers a Shift Condition to another oneiropomp through a Paradigm Shift, does the instigating changeling then gain a new Shift Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T05:54:24-08:00","id":1475311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1475286#post1475286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a changeling transfers a Shift Condition to another oneiropomp through a Paradigm Shift, does the instigating changeling then gain a new Shift Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that you would pick up Dream Infiltrator while the target got whichever Shift Condition you had previously, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T11:16:38-07:00","id":1478503,"title":"","content":"When a Changeling enters the Hedge, does she look as she did when she was created by the True Fae in Arcadia, or does she still appear as a half-human, half-thing when she escaped from Arcadia? How does the Mask/Mien actually work in the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T13:06:43-07:00","id":1478512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1478503#post1478503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Changeling enters the Hedge, does she look as she did when she was created by the True Fae in Arcadia, or does she still appear as a half-human, half-thing when she escaped from Arcadia? How does the Mask/Mien actually work in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mask is gone when you enter the Hedge. You look the way other fae would see you in the mortal world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T19:08:50-07:00","id":1478538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1478503#post1478503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Changeling enters the Hedge, does she look as she did when she was created by the True Fae in Arcadia, or does she still appear as a half-human, half-thing when she escaped from Arcadia? How does the Mask/Mien actually work in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mien is the true appearance of a Changeling. It is somewhat malleable, but real. It may happen that your Mien once you reach Earth again isn't the same as it was under your True Fae, but that would be the exception, not the rule. Most of the time what the True Fae manage to make with the Changeling <b>is</b> a half-human, half-thing, not something completely inhuman. Mantles, Entitlements and stuff may affect your Mien, as it is still malleable, and those changes are still all real changes to your true form.<br /> <br /> Now, the Mask is mostly an illusion. It <i><u>tends</u></i> to conform to the human appearance you would have if never taken by the True Fae, with a bunch of adaptations as needed, but ultimately the Mask isn't real in any way. Non-fae see the Mask when looking at you most of the time, unless something drops the illusion. But your Mien is still the real you and is physically there even if not perceived. Changeling on Earth will see a superposition of sorts of Mask and Mien when looking at you, but that's not what you are, you are still the Mien, solely.<br /> <br /> What happens in the Hedge is that the Hedge <b>is</b> one of the things that drop the illusion. There's no Mask at all in there, so neither fae see you as a superposition nor non-fae see you as human anymore, they only see your Mien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T00:30:56-07:00","id":1478551,"title":"","content":"The changeling is basically putty in the hands of their Keeper, and can be forced into any type of form during their Durance. This includes forms that strictly speaking are impossible or lack actual physical presence. You could be stuck in a painting, have non-euclidian geometries, or be a song propagating through the air.<br /> <br /> When the changeling escapes, they become humanoid again, but with traits from the form they were forced into by their Keeper. This is their Mien and it's their actual form. <br /> <br /> Outside the Hedge, changelings automatically put on their Mask, which makes them look mostly like their pre-Durance selves. But the Mask is only an illusion that can be seen through by any kind of supernatural sense.<br /> The changeling can drop the Mask to reveal themselves to those who can't see through it, which has a truckload of various effects no one could reasonably remember during a game.<br /> <br /> Note that changelings don't see the Mask of other changelings by default. A changeling can make an effort to temporarily see the Mask of other changelings or to fortify their own Mask so other changelings can see it, but otherwise changelings have no idea what other changelings' Masks look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T14:47:12-07:00","id":1478711,"title":"","content":"The book was not clear about it, so I decided to ask.<br /> I know that Huntsman have their own dread powers and can use the ones on the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook, but can they use Hobgoblins dread powers too?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T14:52:33-07:00","id":1478712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LunaLupa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1478711#post1478711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book was not clear about it, so I decided to ask.<br /> I know that Huntsman have their own dread powers and can use the ones on the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook, but can they use Hobgoblins dread powers too?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that some of the Dread Powers provided for hobgoblins are more appropriate for them than Huntsmen, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T15:33:19-07:00","id":1478715,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> Similar to what I was planning to use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T18:58:32-07:00","id":1478725,"title":"","content":"Do mortals who see a changeling without their Mask suffer a Breaking Point? (Asking because of the built-in Spooked Condition.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T19:14:15-07:00","id":1478729,"title":"","content":"I'd take that one depending on context, same as any other supernatural shock. Is the changeling being violent? Did the changeling suddenly burst in or were they talking and trying to prepare the person for what she was about to see? Does the changeling's mien appear threatening, grotesque or dangerous? How did the mortal answer the five Integrity questions that illuminate her worldview and context for trauma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T19:17:01-07:00","id":1478730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1478725#post1478725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mortals who see a changeling without their Mask suffer a Breaking Point? (Asking because of the built-in Spooked Condition.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My take from another thread:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility?p=1470577#post1470577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's reasonable to say that witnessing an unMasked changeling is not consistently a breaking point against Integrity, given ChroD Core's guidelines of &quot;witness[ing] something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles [your] understanding of the world&quot; or &quot;[being] the victim of a supernatural attack, whether physical, emotional, or mental.&quot;<br /> <br /> (The encounter might <i>go on</i> to induce breaking points from those things, and seeing the actual act of burning away the Mask might itself be distressing, but just seeing a person with pointy ears and bug-eyes walking around less so.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T23:33:58-07:00","id":1478740,"title":"","content":"I don't know how Changeling describes Integrity, but other games straight up says that merely witnessing the supernatural is a breaking point. And I think it should be for anyone who isn't already aware that the supernatural exists.<br /> <br /> If the changeling appears biologically impossible in ways that can't be explained away with advanced make up, then anyone who sees the changeling will have their understanding of the world broken (unless their understanding of the world already includes the supernatural, which it should for most Fae-Touched and humans with Supernatural Merits). Dropping the mask in front of humans also makes them accutely aware of the transformation of someone they thought human, making it impossible to explain it away as make up or other special effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T10:11:36-07:00","id":1478770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1478740#post1478740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how Changeling describes Integrity, but other games straight up says that merely witnessing the supernatural is a breaking point. And I think it should be for anyone who isn't already aware that the supernatural exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ended up scouring the book to double-check, and although Integrity is mentioned multiple times in Changeling, the rules for Breaking Points aren't reprinted. In fact, different books say different things about them, reframed for the context of their gamelines (such as through the lens of Lunacy for Werewolf or Quiescence for Mage). According to Beast, mortals experience breaking points from &quot;witnessing something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles understanding of the world,&quot; or are &quot;the victim of a supernatural attack,&quot; while Mummy truncates this to &quot;exposure to supernatural forces.&quot; Because mortals automatically gain Spooked (a possible Condition to suffer when encountering a Breaking Point) when exposed to a fae Mien, I was wondering if that was meant to replicate the situation. (Uh oh, is this another &quot;invisible and intangible&quot; problem?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T14:41:32-07:00","id":1479098,"title":"","content":"Am i wrong or does Entitlement s token slightly deviates from normal Tokens rules?<br /> They all have multiple effects, and if i m reading it rightly some of the effects can be activated without a Glamour cost.<br /> It is correct to assume that Glamour free effects could be activated by a mortal without using the Catch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T17:31:29-07:00","id":1479106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1479098#post1479098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i wrong or does Entitlement s token slightly deviates from normal Tokens rules?<br /> They all have multiple effects,</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of those effects are Conditional upon the changeling keeping up with their duties \u2014 they're more things the changeling can do with the token as part of their role than abilities of the token in general.<br /> <br /> It would be prudent not to take &quot;a token does one thing and does it well&quot; to mean &quot;tokens can only have one effect&quot; when the rules for tokens combining more than one simple effect on the chart are on the same page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if i m reading it rightly some of the effects can be activated without a Glamour cost.<br /> It is correct to assume that Glamour free effects could be activated by a mortal without using the Catch? </div> </div> </div>The Last Key's passive once-per-day detection of people that mean its bearer deadly harm is the only one I can see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T21:46:16-07:00","id":1479112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1479106#post1479106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those effects are Conditional upon the changeling keeping up with their duties \u2014 they're more things the changeling can do with the token as part of their role than abilities of the token in general.<br /> <br /> It would be prudent not to take &amp;quot;a token does one thing and does it well&amp;quot; to mean &amp;quot;tokens can only have one effect&amp;quot; when the rules for tokens combining more than one simple effect on the chart are on the same page.<br /> <br /> The Last Key's passive once-per-day detection of people that mean its bearer deadly harm is the only one I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The baron seal<br /> &quot;Upon activation in the mundane world, the Baron automatically learns where the closest existing Hedge gate is, active or dormant.&quot;<br /> For example, doesn t lista a Glamour cost and isn t conditional.<br /> I m reading it correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T07:07:54-07:00","id":1479129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1479112#post1479112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The baron seal<br /> &amp;quot;Upon activation in the mundane world, the Baron automatically learns where the closest existing Hedge gate is, active or dormant.&amp;quot;<br /> For example, doesn t lista a Glamour cost and isn t conditional.<br /> I m reading it correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Upon activation&quot; means it costs Glamour if you don't use the Catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T09:12:54-07:00","id":1479134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1479129#post1479129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Upon activation&amp;quot; means it costs Glamour if you don't use the Catch.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are probably right, my confusion springs by the interchangable use of the words &quot;upon activation&quot; and &quot;he may spend 1 Glamour to&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T02:47:41-07:00","id":1479683,"title":"","content":"Not sure of where to post this...<br /> Do you think fetches are able to &quot;produce&quot; a regular ghost at death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T05:01:09-07:00","id":1479685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1479683#post1479683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure of where to post this...<br /> Do you think fetches are able to &amp;quot;produce&amp;quot; a regular ghost at death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno if we had official wording somewhere in a book, but we already have ghosts of animals, objects, still-living persons, and whatever Chthonians and Shades are, so I\u2019d say yes.<br /> <br /> Now, how would they differ from \u2018normal\u2019 ghosts is another matter\u2026 maybe they resemble Hedge Ghosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe, in contrast with the above, they <i>can\u2019t</i> leave ghosts, because they\u2019re already a type of ghost, shed from the changeling. That\u2019d make them a strange type of a doppelg\u00e4nger, the \u2018ghosts of still-living persons\u2019 mentioned above.<br /> <br /> And isn\u2019t \u201cfetch\u201d used as another word for \u201cdoppelganger\u201d somewhere? Hmm\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T19:17:27-07:00","id":1481331,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\">When I use a contract such as Riddle-kith on my own character instead of using it on another character, do I still need to roll? What about using Discreet Summons to summon an object rather than a Hobgoblin?</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T22:03:54-07:00","id":1481341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1481331#post1481331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I use a contract such as Riddle-kith on my own character instead of using it on another character, do I still need to roll? What about using Discreet Summons to summon an object rather than a Hobgoblin?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that Riddle-Kith lists its action-type as &quot;instant or contested&quot; would seem to indicate that you don't roll Composure + Wyrd against the Contract, but you do still roll for the Contract. Ditto for Discreet Summons, which contrasts the action-type for summoning an object and summoning a hobgoblin (and provides a means of waiving the hobgoblin's Composure roll as well).<br /> <br /> One of the benefits of dropping the Mask is that any successfully-rolled Contract counts as an exceptional success, and for that to work, you need to make the roll; unrolled Contracts get a different benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T00:35:30-07:00","id":1481345,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T08:29:19-07:00","id":1481535,"title":"","content":"Can changelings using Whispers of Mornin and Helldiving float or fly or can they only walk? They're described as weightless and immaterial, but it's a bit vague to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T12:16:40-07:00","id":1481855,"title":"","content":"Does a changeling need to be touching an oath-forged token to regain Glamour from fulfilling a bound pledge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T15:03:03-07:00","id":1481867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1481855#post1481855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a changeling need to be touching an oath-forged token to regain Glamour from fulfilling a bound pledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem to be the case, given the lack of language indicating the benefit applies to the bearer of the token; recall that court monarchs can turn their Crown into an oath-forged token, as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T02:10:13-07:00","id":1482354,"title":"","content":"Do Huntsmen have Frailties? I mean, aside from Iron, which we know they're not affected by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T06:36:21-07:00","id":1482368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1482354#post1482354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Huntsmen have Frailties? I mean, aside from Iron, which we know they're not affected by.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Huntsmen do not suffer the frailties of other fae creatures, which is one reason the Gentry risk sending their Titles into the world this way.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're also specifically created using the rules for creating hobgoblins except where specified, and the section on creating hobgoblins notes frailties that aren't iron as optional (albeit helpful as ludonarrative handles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T13:54:47-07:00","id":1482403,"title":"","content":"Okay thank you^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T14:38:10-07:00","id":1483517,"title":"","content":"What happens to Changeling bodies when they die? Do they look human, or do they show their true form? Do the bodies disintegrate, or turn into crass or leaves? <br /> <br /> Apologies if this was answered, but I tried searching with the keywords &quot;Death,&quot; &quot;Bodies,&quot; &quot;Corpses,&quot; and &quot;Die,&quot; with no results. I also looked in the 2E rulebook, but in the Injury section, it went straight from Injury to Healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:26:55-07:00","id":1483528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1483517#post1483517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to Changeling bodies when they die? Do they look human, or do they show their true form? Do the bodies disintegrate, or turn into crass or leaves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consistently nothing, unlike fetches, which can break down into their component parts an unspecified amount of time after death when nobody's looking.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 1e Core Rulebook, p172, &quot;Mien and the Mask&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mask is not a choice. <b>It protects and disguises the Lost even when they would have it otherwise, even beyond death.</b> The Mask seems to be another expression of the ancient pacts struck by the Fae to protect them and theirs from the eyes of common men and women.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e Core Rulebook, p83, &quot;Mask&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sight is not the only sense the Mask affects. While your human paramour may believe that her flower-bearing fae lover smells delightful, she will not recognize your scent as the lilacs and lilies growing in your beard. Hoof clicks will sound like normal footsteps to non-fae ears, and even claws or horns will seem like normal nails or an unmarred forehead if touched by human skin. <b>This power is so great that it holds even after you die; no matter how grotesquely unnatural your living form might be, you will leave behind a mundane-looking corpse.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:32:11-07:00","id":1483529,"title":"","content":"Well, that's a little awkward. Thank You, Satchel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T22:38:50-07:00","id":1483557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1483529#post1483529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's a little awkward. Thank You, Satchel.</div> </div> </div> </div>One notable exception to the above is if a changeling is killed by a major bane, in which case:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e Core Rulebook, p 102, &quot;Frailties&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">her entire body unravels in spectacular fashion, exploding into thorns and leaves or hundreds of torn gossamer wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T23:03:49-07:00","id":1484478,"title":"","content":"What's the latest news on Kith and Kin? I thought there used to be a page telling the current progress on all the books, but I can't seem to find it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T23:22:03-07:00","id":1484480,"title":"","content":"Kith and Kin's in layout, per last month's update.<br /> <br /> As for the other thing... Current Projects currently only lists what projects are on the go, not where they are; for that, you have to check each month's Release Roundup.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T18:50:36-07:00","id":1487671,"title":"","content":"Can someone be born into Arcadia? That is, can two Changelings in the midst of their durance conceive a child? And if so, is the kid a Changeling by default, but lacking a Fetch?<br /> <br /> Obviously whether or not the hypothetical child could survive once born would depend on the Keeper and their realm, my main concern is if it's a plausible scenario in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T21:55:49-07:00","id":1487689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487671#post1487671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone be born into Arcadia? That is, can two Changelings in the midst of their durance conceive a child? And if so, is the kid a Changeling by default, but lacking a Fetch?<br /> <br /> Obviously whether or not the hypothetical child could survive once born would depend on the Keeper and their realm, my main concern is if it's a plausible scenario in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, 2e has loosely done away with the consistent idea that the fae are sterile (though the physical-mechanical complications of a given mien may still make the prospect unlikely \u2014 as the bit in the sidebar notes, producing children is a little tricky when your child-producing anatomy Does Things that interfere with that process), and the Fae have sufficient mastery over their domains that it's not inconceivable* for them to be able to facilitate (or deny) the production of children by their once-human slaves. The offhand mention in Chapter Two's short fiction-snippets of a Keeper's son could be interpreted in multiple different ways, at least one of which is that the Gentry are not barred from reproducing in a way that bears resemblance to the biological method.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, faeries stealing babies out of cribs is a genre trope that bears retention as part of the greater constellation of reasons for the Lost to be concerned with children in the mortal world beyond abstract symmetry with Peter Pan (harvesting Glamour working better with new emotions being another of these), the durance is a place and time where the mien is even less human-adjacent than usual, Werewolf 2e has largely moved away from the elements that supported &quot;group of people kept as breeding stock&quot; as a regularly-enough-encountered thing for a reason, and speaking personally as a Changeling ST who encountered issues running the game for a PC whose durance included &quot;grew up in Faerie from young enough to have no recollection of the mortal world at all&quot; I cannot recommend the supposition that a character born in Arcadia has the ludonarrative tools to possess Clarity without serious tweaks to the system to accommodate it.<br /> <br /> More likely the result of changeling unions that produce viable offspring during the durance is a hobgoblin, animal, or other strangeness that can't be traded as &quot;your firstborn/seventhborn/etc child&quot; to any but the most flexible goblin merchant/by any but the most open-hearted changeling lucky enough to keep their spawn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* [your exasperated groan here]</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:07:49-07:00","id":1487690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487689#post1487689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More likely the result of changeling unions that produce viable offspring during the durance is a hobgoblin, animal, or other strangeness that can't be traded as &quot;your firstborn/seventhborn/etc child&quot; to any but the most flexible goblin merchant/by any but the most open-hearted changeling lucky enough to keep their spawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since my biggest concern was whether the thing would even have a soul, that about makes sense. A hobgoblin or some eldritch abomination is most likely. Maybe a modification on the Nativity from MtAw.<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no plans to make this a PC, just to clarify. It was just something I was wondering about while reading up on Fetches, and got to thinking about what circumstances would lead to a Changling having <i>no</i> Fetch. At best it would be a plot device.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487689#post1487689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* [your exasperated groan here]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I chuckled. Nothing like a good pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-24-2022, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T23:40:01-07:00","id":1487699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487671#post1487671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone be born into Arcadia? That is, can two Changelings in the midst of their durance conceive a child? And if so, is the kid a Changeling by default, but lacking a Fetch?<br /> <br /> Obviously whether or not the hypothetical child could survive once born would depend on the Keeper and their realm, my main concern is if it's a plausible scenario in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what i understand EVERYTHING that happens in Arcadia is part of the keepers Title and wholly controlled by it.<br /> Changelings are clearly an exception during their Durance, but their autonomy is badly compromised on all levels, and in any case it s limited only in regard of themselves.<br /> My take is that if two changelings conceives &quot;something&quot; in Arcadia, it s possible only if the Keeper allows and controls the whole process, and the resulting being would simply become a part of the Title manifestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T10:48:53-07:00","id":1487743,"title":"","content":"How does teamwork works for hedgespinning?<br /> Does everyone need to spend glamour?<br /> Does every one in fact need to be able to hedgespin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:04:27-07:00","id":1487748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487743#post1487743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does teamwork works for hedgespinning?<br /> Does everyone need to spend glamour?<br /> Does every one in fact need to be able to hedgespin?</div> </div> </div> </div>The one doing the Hedgespinning needs to spend Glamour. Unless the secondary actors are also Hedgespinning with their own actions, they don't need to spend Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:20:13-07:00","id":1487796,"title":"","content":"Both Hedgespinning and Dreamweaving list their banking successes effect as a Paradigm Shift. Should it be treated as one in all cases? (Ie, you can only do so on an exceptional success, doing so imposes an emotional/Shift Condition, etc.) It seems like something of a special case, not altering the environment drastically but merely building up momentum for greater shifts down the line, and so I'm left wondering if they're placed where they are simply for the sake of reference in relation to the effects for which it will most likely be the most relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:39:22-07:00","id":1487801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487796#post1487796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Hedgespinning and Dreamweaving list their banking successes effect as a Paradigm Shift. Should it be treated as one in all cases? (Ie, you can only do so on an exceptional success, doing so imposes an emotional/Shift Condition, etc.) It seems like something of a special case, not altering the environment drastically but merely building up momentum for greater shifts down the line, and so I'm left wondering if they're placed where they are simply for the sake of reference in relation to the effects for which it will most likely be the most relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The cost of banking successes is based on the fact that paradigm shifts allow you to use all of the successes on the roll, dreamweaving is a delicate balancing act for which Shift Conditions have their own benefits, emotional Conditions come into play only once per scene regardless of how many Hedgespinning shifts you make, and the most likely things for a character to roll an exceptional success at concern things like kith blessings, entitlement boons, Inspiration, and the exploitation of other emotional Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T21:16:32-07:00","id":1487971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487748#post1487748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one doing the Hedgespinning needs to spend Glamour. Unless the secondary actors are also Hedgespinning with their own actions, they don't need to spend Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if for example a changeling is in the hedge with 5 humans, thay can all add teamwork dices to the changeling hedgespinning action?<br /> Do they need to apply the hedgespinning penalty to their rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T21:23:56-07:00","id":1487973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1487971#post1487971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if for example a changeling is in the hedge with 5 humans, thay can all add teamwork dices to the changeling hedgespinning action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Subject to the usual caveats for teamwork rolls, yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they need to apply the hedgespinning penalty to their rolls? </div> </div> </div>No, because they're not Hedgespinning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T16:59:52-07:00","id":1489278,"title":"","content":"Since Dreams are connected to the Hedge and Arcadia with the Dreaming Roads, is it possible for Eidolons and Props to be taken out of one's Dreams and become materialized as normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T17:17:54-07:00","id":1489281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1489278#post1489278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Dreams are connected to the Hedge and Arcadia with the Dreaming Roads, is it possible for Eidolons and Props to be taken out of one's Dreams and become materialized as normal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eidolons and props can be encountered in the spaces along the Dreaming Roads around Bastions, where oneiromancy works, and the True Fae (and hobgoblins with particular Goblin Contracts and/or Dread Powers) can take them out of that context (the True Fae doing so being the sole source of baubles), but by default it can be safely assumed that dream-things won't leave the place they come from in a useful manner otherwise without Plot Devices being brought to bear.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's as possible as anything is in the Chronicles, but there's a trick to it and without such a trick you'll have as much luck actually stealing abstractions and intangibles in the mortal world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T17:42:32-07:00","id":1489284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1489281#post1489281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eidolons and props can be encountered in the spaces along the Dreaming Roads around Bastions, where oneiromancy works, and the True Fae (and hobgoblins with particular Goblin Contracts and/or Dread Powers) can take them out of that context (the True Fae doing so being the sole source of baubles), but by default it can be safely assumed that dream-things won't leave the place they come from in a useful manner otherwise without Plot Devices being brought to bear.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's as possible as anything is in the Chronicles, but there's a trick to it and without such a trick you'll have as much luck actually stealing abstractions and intangibles in the mortal world.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's possible to get the Goblin Contract? What could it be called? And I can pick it up from the Goblin Market, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T18:17:21-07:00","id":1489288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1489284#post1489284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's possible to get the Goblin Contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a goblin will sell it to you, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What could it be called? </div> </div> </div>Whatever that particular Goblin Contract is called. It is not a published power, but it is a described power of some types of goblin in both editions of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I can pick it up from the Goblin Market, right? </div> </div> </div>Again, yes, if somebody's selling it.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that, as the design tips in the corebook state, Goblin Contracts tend to be more specific than Court or Arcadian Contracts, so you're more likely to find a Goblin Contract for mining bits of a person's self-confidence out of their dreams as glittering ores or harnessing a nightmare into a terrifying steed than you are to come across a general-purpose &quot;take things out of dreams and keep them for real&quot; power without a lot of legwork and/or big trades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T18:10:59-07:00","id":1490570,"title":"","content":"Just seeking some clarification on the Spring Court Contract Gift of Warm Breath. The description is listed as &quot;The target instantly sheds all fatigue penalties, tilts relating to fatigue and temporary illnesses (such as Sick or Poisoned), and bashing wounds. Is this penalties due to bashing wounds or is it actually healing bashing wounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T18:39:43-07:00","id":1490572,"title":"","content":"It's healing bashing wounds. Comma placement groups it like this:<br /> <br /> The target sheds:<ul><li>fatigue penalties,</li> <li>Tilts relating to fatigue and temporary illnesses (such as the Sick or Poisoned Tilt), and</li> <li>bashing wounds.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> When the game is talking about penalties caused by damage it uses the term &quot;wound penalties,&quot; and effects that ignore them specify how long before the penalty applies again if the wound is not healed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 08-17-2022, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T16:08:46-07:00","id":1491053,"title":"","content":"Have another Contract question, this one Whispers of Morning. Just curious about the limits of the Contract. So does weightless mean floating/flying for the duration? And I assume that the regular/material world can still be seen clearly but can you still use other Contracts, like Paralyzing Presence for instance, while ethereal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T18:55:50-07:00","id":1491067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1491053#post1491053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have another Contract question, this one Whispers of Morning. Just curious about the limits of the Contract. So does weightless mean floating/flying for the duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e clause Whispers of Morning most directly emulates (down to having the same catch/Loophole and Glamour cost), Phantom Glory, specifies that the character can't walk on air but can walk on water; Tread Lightly, the first clause in the same Contracts of Separation as Phantom Glory comes from, explicitly doesn't allow the character to fly or even jump higher than normal, but <i>does</i> allow them to (as specific examples) run across snow without breaking through the surface, negate the terminal velocity upgrade to lethal damage from long falls, and climb surfaces that would otherwise be too fragile to support their weight, due to the clause allowing them to move across any surface as though they weighed only a few ounces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I assume that the regular/material world can still be seen clearly but can you still use other Contracts, like Paralyzing Presence for instance, while ethereal? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Can't be touched or attacked (or touch or attack others) save by magical means&quot; suggests to me that the answer is &quot;yes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T00:10:55-07:00","id":1492788,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know why the Center Court wasn't included in the Directional Cort update in Oak, Ash, and Thorn? I totally understand if it was just a space constraint, but wasn't sure if I was ignorant of something else having precluded it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T09:07:07-07:00","id":1492807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1492788#post1492788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know why the Center Court wasn't included in the Directional Cort update in Oak, Ash, and Thorn? I totally understand if it was just a space constraint, but wasn't sure if I was ignorant of something else having precluded it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Center Courts were designed for a version of the game that never came out and weren't part of the original presentation of the Directional Courts in 1e; considering that the wholesale replacement of Southern Mantle brings it back in line with Winter Masques' association of the Court with Ecstasy instead of Rebellion and the Center Court being tied to a position privileged as neutral territory in 1e's version of the Directional Courts, I think it's a safe guess that the Jakarta writeup referencing there being five courts instead of four and its freehold having a Bargain (when it's courts that have Bargains now and freeholds had Bulwarks in the version of 2e Three Kingdoms of Darkness was written for) is an artifact that slipped through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T05:23:34-07:00","id":1493321,"title":"","content":"How much time can a Huntsmen stay on the living world before deteriorating and need to kill again to become another person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T13:08:52-07:00","id":1493352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1493321#post1493321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much time can a Huntsmen stay on the living world before deteriorating and need to kill again to become another person?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume this question is about the unpublished second edition of Changeling developed by Olivia Hill. Note that the Changeling 2e book ultimately published by Onyx Path is a different manuscript with different developers and different mechanics, and while it retains a concept of Huntsmen, the published book's Huntsmen do not need to kill to acclimate to the material realm.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking of the Olivia Hill manuscript, a Huntsman can remain in the material realm indefinitely as long as they have unspent Yearning. Killing has nothing to do with becoming another person; rather, a Huntsman between hunts forgets in its formless rest the nature of the material realm, and when a new hunt begins it enters the material realm alien and unfamiliar with basic reality until it glimpses the fear in a pair of dying eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T15:33:27-07:00","id":1493360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1493352#post1493352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume this question is about the unpublished second edition of Changeling developed by Olivia Hill. Note that the Changeling 2e book ultimately published by Onyx Path is a different manuscript with different developers and different mechanics, and while it retains a concept of Huntsmen, the published book's Huntsmen do not need to kill to acclimate to the material realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I may have read the manuscript and after my reading of Broken Things by Lawerence Hawkins on the Anthology I screambled the information. But strictly speaking about the 2nd edition:<br /> If they use the same rules as Hobgoblins, they get the deprived condition, or just no condition at all?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T16:07:37-07:00","id":1493361,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen in the published book also can remain in the material realm indefinitely.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: the Lost Second Edition, p. 265</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Huntsman can stay in the mortal world as long as they like and suffer no ill effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T06:46:25-07:00","id":1493407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1493361#post1493361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen in the published book also can remain in the material realm indefinitely.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As long as their heart is in a mortal Bastion, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T20:29:25-07:00","id":1493450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1493407#post1493407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as their heart is in a mortal Bastion, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any time. Their heart being squirreled away in a mortal Bastion means it's in a place that vanishes and reappears in a different place every night on top of being the one thing their tracking prowess can't help them find, which is the main thing keeping their priorities firmly aligned with the Keeper's, which in turn are usually priorities located in the mortal world. They pre-date Faerie and the Hedge, and are not bound to either in the way that the fae are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T21:25:39-07:00","id":1493451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1493450#post1493450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time. Their heart being squirreled away in a mortal Bastion means it's in a place that vanishes and reappears in a different place every night on top of being the one thing their tracking prowess can't help them find, which is the main thing keeping their priorities firmly aligned with the Keeper's, which in turn are usually priorities located in the mortal world. They pre-date Faerie and the Hedge, and are not bound to either in the way that the fae are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, &quot;This is their secret: to anchor them and allow them to manifest fully in the mortal world as creatures of Wyrd and flesh, the True Fae must hide the heart of a Huntsman within a Bastion. &quot;<br /> What does mean exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T05:37:51-07:00","id":1493470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1493451#post1493451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, &quot;This is their secret: to anchor them and allow them to manifest fully in the mortal world as creatures of Wyrd and flesh, the True Fae must hide the heart of a Huntsman within a Bastion. &quot;<br /> What does mean exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>What it sounds like: the Huntsman can manifest <i>fully</i> in the mortal world as a creature of Wyrd <i>and flesh</i>.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming Roads are older than the Hedge, and the things normally found there are not material beings. A Huntsman who has not been made an instrument of one of the Fae is an inhabitant of a seemingly empty stage from before the Gentry's arrival \u2014 &quot;air and darkness assuming thought and form by will or whim.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Strangers make the verderers into the things that pursue changelings by twisting the rules that they keep to; they're creatures of the primeval principles of pursuit, which means they could <i>notionally</i> show up anywhere, but in the material world there is a separation between solidity and imagination that the Fae need to bridge if they want their elite agent to be able to physically bring their quarry all the way home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T05:11:51-07:00","id":1496103,"title":"","content":"Does Changeling have any way to deal with Blood Bonds from Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T07:56:47-07:00","id":1496107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1496103#post1496103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Changeling have any way to deal with Blood Bonds from Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that they can use Wyrd instead of Blood potency to resistit.<br /> Once full bonded, probably a Goblin deal or a complex Hedgespinning could remove it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T09:26:12-08:00","id":1497371,"title":"","content":"Is anything stopping a Huntsman from transforming and then covering up their tell naturally? Like one who always has a &quot;red right hand&quot; transforming into a human with a bloody right hand, then covering it in a thick cast and saying they broke their arm. Would the Wyrd make their Tell manifest in another way?<br /> <br /> And now that we have the Moon Freehold, am I missing something in the book or would they have fragile Clarity from the difficulty of interacting with mortals? Is that not as core to Clarity as I think it is anymore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T13:41:45-08:00","id":1497406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1497371#post1497371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now that we have the Moon Freehold, am I missing something in the book or would they have fragile Clarity from the difficulty of interacting with mortals? Is that not as core to Clarity as I think it is anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike vampires and Humanity, changelings count as mortals for the purposes of maintaining Clarity through social contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T11:07:35-08:00","id":1497923,"title":"","content":"How is it determined which Seeming Benefits Hobgoblins recieve? Is it just whatever the ST deems appropriate, since they 100% NPC material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T12:10:40-08:00","id":1497930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1497923#post1497923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it determined which Seeming Benefits Hobgoblins recieve? Is it just whatever the ST deems appropriate, since they 100% NPC material?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd default to not giving them any, using ST discretion to allow them benefits that specifically feel very appropriate for that hobgoblin's nature.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T14:13:22-08:00","id":1497946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1497923#post1497923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it determined which Seeming Benefits Hobgoblins recieve? Is it just whatever the ST deems appropriate, since they 100% NPC material?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As far as I know, it's completely up to the ST. When I make hobgoblins, I give them the Seeming benefits for Contracts that most fit my conception of the Hobgoblin -- If I'm building a Hedge Beast, I might use a mix of Ogre and Beast Contract benefits, rather than sticking to a single Seeming. If I want to give them the overall Seeming benefit (the Ogre's ability to inflict Beat Down with any damage it deals, for instance), I'll use a Dread Power for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-24T00:06:34-08:00","id":1497969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1497923#post1497923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it determined which Seeming Benefits Hobgoblins recieve? Is it just whatever the ST deems appropriate, since they 100% NPC material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they supposed to have Seeming benefits? Can't find any mention of it on pages 252-253 so I'd just assume they wouldn't have any. Unless, of course, they've somehow managed to bargain for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-24T11:23:17-08:00","id":1498007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1497969#post1497969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are they supposed to have Seeming benefits? Can't find any mention of it on pages 252-253 so I'd just assume they wouldn't have any. Unless, of course, they've somehow managed to bargain for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That us possible. I assumed that was one possibility but wasn't very good at expressing it in my initial question","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T15:04:25-08:00","id":1498236,"title":"","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Hollow questions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assuming that a non-changeling can access the Hedge, can anyone get the Hollow merit? In the mage forum, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498156#post1498156\">two</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498157#post1498157\">different</a> posters agree but I wanted the opinion from the Changeling folks.</li> <li>Do I understand correctly that the Hollow does not need to reflect the Thorn / Hedge theme? For example I want my Hollow to look like a comfortable mid sized manor on a fortified island in the middle of the sea (Luxury Goods, Size Matters 2, Hidden Entry)</li> <li>If the answer to the previous question is YES, what stops me from making the Hollow larger and larger by developing more of the sea?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-28-2022, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T15:18:07-08:00","id":1498238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1498236#post1498236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Hollow questions:<ul><li>Do I understand correctly that the Hollow does not need to reflect the Thorn / Hedge theme? For example I want my Hollow to look like a comfortable mid sized manor on a fortified island in the middle of the sea (Luxury Goods, Size Matters 2, Hidden Entry)</li> <li>If the answer to the previous answer is YES, what stops me from making the Hollow larger and larger by developing more of the sea?</li> </ul>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I answered one as the former Changeling Guy and otherwise as some person who checks out Mage,<br /> <br /> 2. The Hedge need not strictly look like a traditional thorn bush and greenery, but the idea of thorns is omnipresent. The oceans of the Hedge are cramped with raised coral, ice-flow strewn wall waves, and constantly dancing lightning, while the cities of the Hedge are littered with reams of sharp glasssed neon lights, jagged steel-like protrusions, and broken concrete. The Thorns need not be plants, but all the Hedge is Thornsome all the same.<br /> 3. Your ability to keep the Hedge tame. Hollows can sometimes form and gain mild staying power for wahtever reason, but any hollow of size is a thing that needs presence of power, and often active application of said power to keep in place, else the Hedge begin to eat it up. Eventually, any Hollow too large for a motley(/-adjacent) to maintain will shrink to the limits of their upkeep.<br /> <br /> For more information, please consult Rites of Spring, and WInter Masques and Dancers in the Dark as asides.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, a note on 1-anyone who can assert power and influence over the Hedge can take and expand a Hollow. Someone who doesn't have that might claim a Hollow as it exists, but without that power and influence, the Hedge could shape itself into dissolving that some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-28-2022, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T17:34:12-08:00","id":1498249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1498238#post1498238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I answered one as the former Changeling Guy and otherwise as some person who checks out Mage,<br /> <br /> 2. The Hedge need not strictly look like a traditional thorn bush and greenery, but the idea of thorns is omnipresent. The oceans of the Hedge are cramped with raised coral, ice-flow strewn wall waves, and constantly dancing lightning, while the cities of the Hedge are littered with reams of sharp glasssed neon lights, jagged steel-like protrusions, and broken concrete. The Thorns need not be plants, but all the Hedge is Thornsome all the same.<br /> 3. Your ability to keep the Hedge tame. Hollows can sometimes form and gain mild staying power for wahtever reason, but any hollow of size is a thing that needs presence of power, and often active application of said power to keep in place, else the Hedge begin to eat it up. Eventually, any Hollow too large for a motley(/-adjacent) to maintain will shrink to the limits of their upkeep.<br /> <br /> For more information, please consult Rites of Spring, and WInter Masques and Dancers in the Dark as asides.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, a note on 1-anyone who can assert power and influence over the Hedge can take and expand a Hollow. Someone who doesn't have that might claim a Hollow as it exists, but without that power and influence, the Hedge could shape itself into dissolving that some day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. How would a non-changeling assert power over the Hedge? I could envision a mage (specially someone with Fate and Mind) doing it, but seems hard for other supers, and even more for humans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T18:19:08-08:00","id":1498255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1498249#post1498249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer. How would a non-changeling assert power over the Hedge? I could envision a mage (specially someone with Fate and Mind) doing it, but seems hard for other supers, and even more for humans.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, a human <i>wouldn't</i>. Most other supernaturals* <i>wouldn't</i>. The Hedge is not as amiable as the Shadow or Astral, with only the Underworld being more seemingly pernicious (and even that just <i>eats you</i> rather than writhes about)<br /> <br /> That said, if you really wanted to do the most you could for the matter, you might argue you can....<i>bait</i> the Hedge certain ways. Since the Hedge is psychoactive, you might try manipulating the emotional and mental states of others to try and chase it into a certain direction-powers that do that sort of thing might get you somewhere, and at a minimum maintaining a meditative state might keep things stable. Of course, given that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1495540-storytelling-the-hedge?p=1495544#post1495544\">the Hedge is prone to challenging your perceptions of yourself,</a> that's gambling a lot, and none of it is actually control.<br /> <br /> I'd have to have my books (ie not be at work) to dig up any of the exceptions beyond Mage's open explanation on how they might(hedgeshaping wasn't a really thing in ie, but Equinox Road should at least be instructive in a &quot;pointing the way&quot; sort of way), but it's worth noting that I <i>think</i> there might be some situations where the other monsters are able to grasp some of the Hedge*. That said, there's been limited discussion so far on that subject (I imagine The Hedge will cover more of the notion), so if there any, I expect it to be scant. The changelings get it because it's their neck of the woods, and mages needed their way to be a submarine to the fairies fish eventually.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is not a fanciful backyard to have jaunty adventures in. It's a barrier between worlds that is so active as assumed to be alive above and beyond it's peers in regular otherworlds, a thing that wriggles, writhes, and challenges. Things that should not be there will very quickly realize that temptation is not the same thing as welcome, and what was true yesterday has no worth today. <br /> <br /> And most importantly, the Hedge was not exactly a place designed with crossover in mind.<br /> <br /> *obligatory &quot;I suppose it should be mentioned it's not infeasible that Beast could develop a Kinship Merit that allows for limited hedgeshaping&quot; because of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T13:54:05-08:00","id":1500522,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ed Core Page 84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings see their own mien when they look<br /> at themselves, and (barring the use of magic) see other<br /> changelings\u2019 miens when they look at their fellows.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ed Core Page 108</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A changeling can spend<br /> a Glamour to see another changeling\u2019s Mask instead of<br /> her mien for a few seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does or does not a changeling need Glamour to see the Miens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T14:20:52-08:00","id":1500527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1500522#post1500522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does or does not a changeling need Glamour to see the Miens?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not for the mien. That is the default view a Changeling gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T14:41:50-08:00","id":1500529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1500527#post1500527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do not for the mien. That is the default view a Changeling gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, after posting I just realized the difference between mien and mask, my bad. And thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}